// Auto-generated for the Unit Board — TOEIC Themed Vocabulary
window.TC_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"Accident 意外事故","cards":[{"w":"collision","p":"n.","d":"a crash in which two things hit each other","c":"碰撞；相撞","s":"A: Why are all the delivery trucks so late this morning, and why hasn't the warehouse manager answered any of my calls yet? B: There was a collision between two buses on the highway near the factory, so traffic is blocked for miles, and the manager is busy calling customers to explain the delay.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上所有的送貨卡車都這麼晚，而且倉庫經理到現在都還沒接我的電話？ B：工廠附近的高速公路上兩輛公車發生了【碰撞】，所以車流堵塞了好幾英里，經理正忙著打電話向客戶解釋延誤的原因。"},{"w":"crash","p":"n.","d":"an accident in which a vehicle hits something hard","c":"撞車；車禍；墜毀","s":"A: Did the sales manager make it to the conference in Chicago on time, or did someone else have to give his presentation to the clients? B: No, he missed the morning session because a car crash closed the main road to the airport, so he had to take a longer route and catch a later flight.","t":"A：業務經理有準時趕到芝加哥的研討會嗎？還是有別人必須代替他向客戶做簡報？ B：沒有，他錯過了上午的場次，因為一場【車禍】封閉了通往機場的主要道路，所以他只好繞遠路並改搭較晚的班機。"},{"w":"incident","p":"n.","d":"something unusual or bad that happens","c":"事件；事故","s":"A: Should I tell the supervisor that a heavy box fell from the top shelf in the warehouse this afternoon, even though it didn't hit anyone? B: Yes, you should, because every incident must be written down in the safety log, and the supervisor uses those notes to decide which shelves need to be repaired or replaced.","t":"A：今天下午倉庫最上層的架子掉下一個很重的箱子，雖然沒有砸到任何人，我還是應該告訴主管嗎？ B：對，你應該說，因為每一起【事件】都必須記錄在安全日誌裡，主管會根據這些紀錄決定哪些架子需要修理或更換。"},{"w":"mishap","p":"n.","d":"a small accident or piece of bad luck","c":"小意外；小差錯","s":"A: How did the product launch go yesterday, and were the new customers happy with the demonstration of our latest software? B: It went well overall, and most guests were impressed, but there was a small mishap when the projector suddenly stopped working, so we had to present the last part without any slides.","t":"A：昨天的產品發表會進行得如何？新客戶對我們最新軟體的展示滿意嗎？ B：整體很順利，大部分來賓都印象深刻，但投影機突然故障時出了個小【意外】，所以最後一部分我們只好在沒有投影片的情況下報告。"},{"w":"injury","p":"n.","d":"harm done to a person's body","c":"傷害；受傷","s":"A: Why is Tom working from home this week, and will he still be able to join the client meeting on Thursday afternoon? B: He got a back injury while he was lifting heavy boxes in the storeroom, so his doctor told him to rest for a few days, but he can still join the meeting by video call.","t":"A：湯姆這週為什麼在家工作？他還能參加星期四下午的客戶會議嗎？ B：他在儲藏室搬重箱子時背部【受傷】了，所以醫生要他休息幾天，不過他還是可以透過視訊參加會議。"},{"w":"damage","p":"n.","d":"harm done to a thing so it is broken or worth less","c":"損壞；損害","s":"A: Has the insurance company checked the delivery van yet, and do they know how much the repairs are going to cost us? B: Yes, an agent came this morning to take photos, and he said the damage to the front door and the side mirror will cost about two thousand dollars, which our policy should cover.","t":"A：保險公司檢查過那輛送貨車了嗎？他們知道修理費用大概要花我們多少錢嗎？ B：檢查過了，今天早上有位專員來拍照，他說前門和側後照鏡的【損壞】大約要花兩千元修理，我們的保單應該會理賠。"},{"w":"wound","p":"n.","d":"a cut or hurt place on the body","c":"傷口","s":"A: The new worker on the night shift cut his hand on a sharp metal sheet at the factory. Was it serious, and did anyone help him? B: The company nurse cleaned the wound carefully and covered it with a clean bandage, and then she reminded him to wear protective gloves every time he handles metal parts.","t":"A：夜班的新員工在工廠被一片鋒利的金屬板割傷了手。嚴重嗎？有人幫他處理嗎？ B：公司護士仔細清潔了【傷口】，並用乾淨的繃帶包紮，然後提醒他每次處理金屬零件時都要戴上防護手套。"},{"w":"emergency","p":"n.","d":"a sudden, dangerous situation that needs fast action","c":"緊急情況","s":"A: What should all the visitors and staff do if the fire alarm rings during the board meeting on the twelfth floor this afternoon? B: In an emergency, everyone should stay calm, leave the building by the nearest stairway, and meet in the parking lot, but please do not use the elevators under any circumstances.","t":"A：如果今天下午十二樓開董事會時火災警報響了，所有訪客和員工應該怎麼做？ B：遇到【緊急情況】時，每個人都應該保持冷靜，從最近的樓梯離開大樓，並到停車場集合，但無論如何都請不要搭電梯。"},{"w":"ambulance","p":"n.","d":"a vehicle that takes sick or hurt people to hospital","c":"救護車","s":"A: One of the visitors at the front desk suddenly fainted in the lobby, and she still isn't waking up. What should we do right now? B: Call an ambulance right away, and then ask the security guard to keep the area clear and open the main entrance so the medical team can get in quickly when they arrive.","t":"A：櫃台有位訪客突然在大廳昏倒了，到現在還沒有醒來。我們現在該怎麼辦？ B：馬上叫【救護車】，然後請警衛淨空該區域並打開正門，這樣醫療團隊抵達時就能快速進來。"},{"w":"rescue","p":"v.","d":"to save someone from danger","c":"救援；營救","s":"A: Was anyone trapped inside when the old storage building near the train station caught fire late last night? B: Two security workers were still inside checking the doors, but the firefighters arrived within ten minutes and managed to rescue them before the roof fell down, so both of them are safe now.","t":"A：昨天深夜火車站附近的舊倉庫失火時，有人被困在裡面嗎？ B：有兩名保全人員還在裡面檢查門窗，但消防員在十分鐘內趕到，並在屋頂塌下來之前成功把他們【救出】，所以兩人現在都很安全。"},{"w":"survive","p":"v.","d":"to stay alive or keep going after something bad","c":"倖存；存活；撐過","s":"A: I read in the news about the passenger plane that made an emergency landing near the coast during the storm. Was anyone badly hurt? B: It was a frightening experience for everyone on board, but thanks to the pilot's skill, all the passengers managed to survive, and only a few of them needed to stay in the hospital overnight.","t":"A：我在新聞上看到那架客機在暴風雨中於海岸附近緊急降落。有人受重傷嗎？ B：對機上每個人來說都是很可怕的經歷，但多虧了機長的技術，所有乘客都【倖存】了，只有少數幾人需要在醫院住一晚。"},{"w":"collapse","p":"v.","d":"to fall down suddenly","c":"倒塌；崩塌","s":"A: Why is the parking garage behind our office closed to all employees today, and where are we supposed to park our cars? B: Engineers are worried that part of the second floor could collapse after the heavy rain last weekend, so they are checking the structure today, and staff can use the public parking lot across the street.","t":"A：我們辦公室後面的停車場今天為什麼不開放給所有員工？我們應該把車停在哪裡？ B：工程師擔心上週末大雨過後二樓有一部分可能會【倒塌】，所以他們今天正在檢查結構，員工可以使用對街的公共停車場。"},{"w":"slip","p":"v.","d":"to slide by accident and lose your balance","c":"滑倒；滑跤","s":"A: Why is there a large yellow warning sign in front of the restroom on the third floor, right next to the meeting rooms? B: The cleaner just mopped the floor, and it is still very wet, so the sign warns people that they might slip and fall if they walk too quickly or carry heavy things past the area.","t":"A：三樓洗手間前面、就在會議室旁邊，為什麼放了一個大大的黃色警告標誌？ B：清潔人員剛拖完地，地板還很濕，所以這個標誌是提醒大家，如果走太快或搬重物經過這裡，可能會【滑倒】摔跤。"},{"w":"fall","p":"v.","d":"to drop down to the ground by accident","c":"跌落；掉落；跌倒","s":"A: Why do all the visitors and workers need to wear hard hats as soon as they enter the construction site, even for a short tour? B: Workers on the upper floors sometimes drop small tools, and these tools can fall from a great height, so a helmet protects your head from serious harm, even if you only stay for a few minutes.","t":"A：為什麼所有訪客和工人一進入工地就必須戴安全帽，即使只是短暫參觀也一樣？ B：上層樓的工人有時會掉落小工具，這些工具可能從很高的地方【掉落】，所以即使你只待幾分鐘，安全帽也能保護你的頭部免受嚴重傷害。"},{"w":"trip","p":"v.","d":"to hit your foot on something and almost fall","c":"絆倒；絆到","s":"A: Could you please move these long computer cables away from the walkway before the visitors from the head office arrive this afternoon? B: Sure, I'll do it right now, because someone could easily trip over them and get hurt, and the safety inspector is also coming at three o'clock to check every department on this floor.","t":"A：總公司的訪客今天下午抵達之前，能請你把這些長長的電腦線從走道移開嗎？ B：當然，我馬上處理，因為很容易有人被它們【絆倒】而受傷，而且安全檢查員三點也會來檢查這層樓的每個部門。"},{"w":"careless","p":"adj.","d":"not paying enough attention; not careful","c":"粗心的；不小心的","s":"A: How did the forklift hit the metal shelf in the warehouse, and were any of the boxes of new phones damaged? B: The driver was careless and kept looking at his phone while he was driving, so he hit the shelf and broke six boxes, and the manager gave him a written warning this morning.","t":"A：堆高機怎麼會撞上倉庫的金屬貨架？有任何一箱新手機受損嗎？ B：司機很【粗心】，開車時一直看手機，所以撞上了貨架並弄壞了六箱貨，經理今天早上給了他書面警告。"},{"w":"dangerous","p":"adj.","d":"likely to hurt someone or cause harm","c":"危險的","s":"A: Is it okay to store these boxes of cleaning chemicals next to the heater in the back room until the supplier picks them up next week? B: No, that is very dangerous because those chemicals can catch fire easily when they get hot, so please move them to the cool storage room downstairs and keep the door locked.","t":"A：在供應商下週來取貨之前，可以把這幾箱清潔化學藥品放在後面房間的暖氣旁邊嗎？ B：不行，那非常【危險】，因為那些化學藥品變熱時很容易起火，所以請把它們移到樓下陰涼的儲藏室，並把門鎖好。"},{"w":"serious","p":"adj.","d":"very bad and worrying","c":"嚴重的","s":"A: I heard there was an accident at the factory last week. Was it serious, and will production be stopped for a long time? B: Fortunately not, because the two workers only had small cuts on their hands, but the machine was badly damaged, so the production line will be closed until a new one arrives next Monday.","t":"A：我聽說上週工廠發生了事故。情況【嚴重】嗎？生產線會停工很久嗎？ B：幸好不嚴重，那兩名員工手上只有小割傷，但機器嚴重損壞，所以生產線會關閉，直到下週一新機器送達為止。"},{"w":"minor","p":"adj.","d":"small and not very serious","c":"輕微的；次要的","s":"A: Do we need to cancel the company trip to the mountains because of the bus accident this morning, or can we still go? B: No, it was only a minor accident in the parking lot and nobody was hurt, and the bus company is sending another vehicle, so we can still leave on time after lunch.","t":"A：因為今天早上遊覽車發生事故，我們需要取消公司的山區旅遊嗎？還是仍然可以去？ B：不用，那只是停車場裡一起【輕微的】事故，沒有人受傷，而且客運公司會另派一輛車，所以我們午餐後還是可以準時出發。"},{"w":"unexpected","p":"adj.","d":"not expected; surprising","c":"意外的；出乎意料的","s":"A: Why did the shipment of electronic parts from Japan arrive three days late, and did our customers complain about the delay? B: There was an unexpected storm along the coast, so the ship had to wait in the port until the weather improved, and we sent an email to every customer to explain the situation.","t":"A：從日本來的那批電子零件為什麼晚了三天才到？我們的客戶有抱怨延誤嗎？ B：沿海出現了一場【出乎意料的】暴風雨，所以船只好在港口等到天氣好轉，我們也寄了電子郵件給每位客戶說明情況。"},{"w":"suddenly","p":"adv.","d":"quickly and without any warning","c":"突然地","s":"A: What happened during the sales presentation this morning? Some people said the meeting room became very dark. B: The lights suddenly went out in the whole building because of a power problem, so we had to finish the meeting with only the light from our laptops, and the clients thought it was quite funny.","t":"A：今天早上的業務簡報發生了什麼事？有些人說會議室變得很暗。 B：因為電力問題，整棟大樓的燈【突然】熄滅了，所以我們只好靠筆電的光把會議開完，客戶們覺得還蠻好笑的。"},{"w":"fortunately","p":"adv.","d":"luckily; used before good news","c":"幸運地；幸好","s":"A: I heard that a delivery truck hit the front gate of our office building early this morning. Was anyone hurt in the accident? B: Yes, the gate was badly damaged, but fortunately, nobody was standing near it at that time, and the driver was not hurt either, so we only need to call a repair company today.","t":"A：我聽說今天一大早有輛送貨卡車撞上了我們辦公大樓的大門。有人在事故中受傷嗎？ B：有，大門嚴重損壞，但【幸好】當時沒有人站在附近，司機也沒有受傷，所以我們今天只需要打電話找維修公司就好。"},{"w":"unfortunately","p":"adv.","d":"sadly; used before bad news","c":"不幸地；遺憾地","s":"A: Will Ms. Lin still be able to give her speech at the marketing conference tomorrow morning, or should we change the schedule? B: unfortunately, she hurt her ankle while she was jogging in the park last night, so her assistant will speak in her place, and we don't need to change the schedule at all.","t":"A：林小姐明天早上還能在行銷研討會上演講嗎？還是我們應該更改議程？ B：【很遺憾】，她昨晚在公園慢跑時扭傷了腳踝，所以會由她的助理代替她發言，我們完全不需要更改議程。"},{"w":"carefully","p":"adv.","d":"with close attention so you don't make mistakes or get hurt","c":"小心地；仔細地","s":"A: Is there anything important I should know before I start using the new cutting machine in the workshop for the first time? B: Yes, read the instructions carefully before you turn it on, and always wear safety glasses and gloves, because small pieces of metal can fly out and hurt your eyes or hands.","t":"A：我第一次使用工作坊裡那台新的切割機之前，有什麼重要的事情是我應該知道的嗎？ B：有，開機前要【仔細地】閱讀說明書，而且一定要戴上護目鏡和手套，因為小金屬碎片可能會飛出來傷到你的眼睛或手。"},{"w":"witness","p":"n.","d":"a person who sees something happen","c":"目擊者；證人","s":"A: Did anyone see the car hit the bicycle outside our store this afternoon? The police officer wants to speak to someone who was there. B: Yes, one of our cashiers was a witness because she was standing by the window, and she has already told the police officer exactly what she saw before the ambulance came.","t":"A：今天下午有人看到那輛車在我們店外撞上腳踏車嗎？警察想找當時在場的人談一談。 B：有，我們的一位收銀員是【目擊者】，因為她當時站在窗邊，她已經在救護車來之前把看到的情況詳細告訴警察了。"},{"w":"report","p":"v.","d":"to tell a person in charge about something that happened","c":"報告；通報","s":"A: What should I do if I see broken equipment in the laboratory, especially if other people are planning to use it later in the day? B: You should report the problem to the safety officer immediately, and you should also put a \"Do Not Use\" sign on the equipment so that nobody touches it before it is repaired.","t":"A：如果我在實驗室看到損壞的設備，尤其是其他人當天稍後還打算使用時，我該怎麼做？ B：你應該立刻向安全負責人【通報】這個問題，並在設備上貼上「請勿使用」的標示，這樣在修好之前就不會有人碰它。"},{"w":"investigate","p":"v.","d":"to try to find out the facts about something","c":"調查","s":"A: Does anyone know why the machine on Line 3 caught fire yesterday, and is it safe for the workers to go back to that area? B: Not yet, but the safety team will investigate the problem this week, and they will share their findings with all staff, so please keep Line 3 closed until they finish their report.","t":"A：有人知道昨天三號生產線的機器為什麼起火嗎？工人回到那個區域安全嗎？ B：還不知道，但安全小組本週會【調查】這個問題，並將結果告知全體員工，所以在他們完成報告之前，請讓三號生產線保持關閉。"},{"w":"cause","p":"n.","d":"the reason why something happens","c":"原因；起因","s":"A: Have the engineers found out why the elevator stopped between the fifth and sixth floors yesterday with six people inside? B: Yes, they said the cause was an electrical problem in the control box, and the elevator will be fixed by Friday, so please use the stairs or the other elevator until then.","t":"A：工程師查出昨天電梯為什麼載著六個人卡在五樓和六樓之間了嗎？ B：查出來了，他們說【原因】是控制箱的電力問題，電梯會在星期五前修好，所以在那之前請走樓梯或使用另一部電梯。"},{"w":"prevent","p":"v.","d":"to stop something from happening","c":"預防；防止","s":"A: Why are we putting new rubber mats at the main entrance and in front of the elevators on the first floor this week? B: The mats will help prevent accidents on rainy days, because the floor near the doors gets very wet and slippery, and last month two customers almost fell while they were walking in.","t":"A：我們這週為什麼要在一樓正門和電梯前面鋪新的橡膠地墊？ B：這些地墊有助於【預防】雨天發生意外，因為門口附近的地板會變得又濕又滑，上個月就有兩位客戶走進來時差點跌倒。"},{"w":"safety","p":"n.","d":"the state of being safe from danger or harm","c":"安全","s":"A: Do new employees have to attend any training before they start working on the production floor, or can they begin right away? B: Everyone must attend a safety workshop on the first day, where they learn how to use the fire extinguishers, where the emergency exits are, and what to do if someone gets hurt.","t":"A：新進員工在生產線開始工作之前必須參加任何訓練嗎？還是可以馬上開始？ B：每個人第一天都必須參加【安全】研習，學習如何使用滅火器、緊急出口在哪裡，以及有人受傷時該怎麼做。"},{"w":"recover","p":"v.","d":"to get well again after being sick or hurt","c":"康復；恢復","s":"A: When will Mr. Chen come back to the office after his car accident, and who is taking care of his projects right now? B: His doctor says he needs about two weeks to recover, so the three of us on his team will share his projects until he returns, and he will answer emails from home when he feels better.","t":"A：陳先生出車禍後什麼時候會回辦公室？現在由誰負責他的專案？ B：他的醫生說他大約需要兩週時間【康復】，所以在他回來之前，我們團隊三個人會分擔他的專案，等他感覺好一點時會在家回覆電子郵件。"},{"w":"shock","p":"n.","d":"a sudden, strong feeling of surprise or fear after something bad","c":"震驚；驚嚇","s":"A: How is the delivery driver who was in the accident on Main Street this morning? I heard his truck was badly damaged. B: He was not badly hurt, but he was in shock for a while and could not answer questions clearly, so the paramedics kept him in the ambulance until he felt calm enough to talk.","t":"A：今天早上在緬因街出車禍的那位送貨司機還好嗎？我聽說他的卡車嚴重損壞。 B：他沒有受重傷，但有一段時間處於【驚嚇】狀態，無法清楚回答問題，所以急救人員讓他待在救護車上，直到他冷靜到可以說話為止。"},{"w":"treatment","p":"n.","d":"medical care for an illness or injury","c":"治療","s":"A: Does our company insurance pay for hospital costs if an employee gets hurt in an accident while working at the factory? B: Yes, it covers all medical treatment for injuries at work, including doctor visits and medicine, but you must fill out the claim forms and submit them to the HR office within thirty days.","t":"A：如果員工在工廠工作時發生意外受傷，公司的保險會支付醫療費用嗎？ B：會，它涵蓋所有工作傷害的醫療【治療】費用，包括看診和藥品，但你必須填寫理賠表格，並在三十天內交給人資辦公室。"},{"w":"traffic","p":"n.","d":"the cars and other vehicles on a road","c":"交通；車流","s":"A: Should we leave for the airport now to meet the clients from Singapore, or can we finish this report first? B: We should leave right away, because there was an accident on the bridge an hour ago, so the traffic will be heavy all the way to the airport, and we don't want the clients to wait for us.","t":"A：我們現在該出發去機場接新加坡來的客戶了嗎？還是可以先把這份報告完成？ B：我們應該馬上出發，因為一小時前橋上發生了事故，所以到機場一路上【交通】都會很擁擠，我們可不想讓客戶等我們。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"Accommodation 住宿","cards":[{"w":"currently","p":"adv.","d":"at the present time","c":"目前；現在","s":"A: Is the company still looking for a new office in the city center, or has the manager decided to stay in this old building for another year? B: We are currently renting a small floor near the train station while the agents search for a larger space with better parking for our staff and visitors.","t":"A：公司還在市中心找新辦公室嗎？還是經理已經決定在這棟舊大樓再待一年？ B：我們【目前】在火車站附近租了一個小樓層，同時仲介正在幫我們找一個更大、讓員工和訪客停車更方便的空間。"},{"w":"afford","p":"v.","d":"to have enough money to pay for something","c":"負擔得起；買得起","s":"A: Are you going to buy that two-bedroom flat near your office, since you said last month that the rent you pay now is far too high? B: I would love to, but I can't afford such a large down payment this year, so I plan to save more money and look again next spring.","t":"A：你要買你辦公室附近那間兩房公寓嗎？你上個月說現在付的房租太高了。 B：我很想買，但今年我無法【負擔】這麼高的頭期款，所以我打算多存點錢，明年春天再看看。"},{"w":"yard","p":"n.","d":"an area of land next to a house, often with grass","c":"院子；庭院","s":"A: Why did your family choose the older house on Maple Street instead of the new apartment downtown, even though the drive to work is much longer? B: The house has a large yard where our children can play safely after school, and there is enough room for a small vegetable garden and our dog.","t":"A：為什麼你們家選擇楓樹街那間比較舊的房子，而不是市中心的新公寓，即使開車上班要久得多？ B：那間房子有一個大【院子】，孩子們放學後可以在那裡安全地玩耍，而且還有足夠的空間弄一個小菜園和養我們的狗。"},{"w":"veranda","p":"n.","d":"a covered area with a roof along the outside of a house","c":"有頂的走廊；陽台","s":"A: Where should we serve coffee to the guests after the hotel tour this afternoon, since the weather report says it might rain a little later? B: Let's use the veranda at the front of the main building, because it has a roof to keep everyone dry, comfortable chairs, and a lovely view of the lake.","t":"A：今天下午飯店導覽結束後，我們應該在哪裡請客人喝咖啡？氣象報告說晚一點可能會下點雨。 B：我們就用主建築前面的【有頂走廊】吧，因為它有屋頂可以讓大家不被淋濕，有舒服的椅子，還能看到湖的美景。"},{"w":"spot","p":"n.","d":"a particular place","c":"地點；場所","s":"A: Have you found a good place to stay for the sales conference next month, or are all the hotels near the convention center already fully booked? B: I found a quiet spot just ten minutes away by subway, and it has a free breakfast, fast internet, and a small meeting room we can use.","t":"A：你找到下個月業務會議期間的好住處了嗎？還是會展中心附近的飯店都已經訂滿了？ B：我找到一個安靜的【地點】，搭地鐵只要十分鐘，而且有免費早餐、快速網路，還有一間我們可以使用的小會議室。"},{"w":"outskirts","p":"n.","d":"the outer areas of a town or city","c":"郊區；市郊","s":"A: Why is the new factory so far from the city center, when most of the workers live downtown and have to take two buses every morning? B: Land on the outskirts of town is much cheaper, so the company could build a bigger site, and it will run a free shuttle bus for staff starting next month.","t":"A：為什麼新工廠離市中心這麼遠？大部分工人都住在市區，每天早上得搭兩班公車。 B：城鎮【郊區】的土地便宜很多，所以公司能蓋更大的廠區，而且從下個月開始會為員工提供免費接駁車。"},{"w":"uniquely","p":"adv.","d":"in a special way that is unlike any other","c":"獨特地；獨一無二地","s":"A: What makes this boutique hotel so popular with business travelers, even though its room prices are higher than the chain hotels nearby? B: Each room is uniquely designed by a local artist, and guests also enjoy free laundry service, a quiet work area, and a personal welcome from the friendly owner.","t":"A：為什麼這間精品飯店這麼受商務旅客歡迎，雖然它的房價比附近的連鎖飯店還貴？ B：每間房間都是由當地藝術家【獨特地】設計的，而且客人還能享受免費洗衣服務、安靜的工作區，以及友善老闆的親自歡迎。"},{"w":"patio","p":"n.","d":"a flat paved area outside a building for sitting or eating","c":"露台；戶外平台","s":"A: Where are we having the team lunch on Friday, since the cafeteria is closed for repairs and the conference room is too small for everyone? B: The manager booked a restaurant with a large patio behind the building, so we can eat outdoors under umbrellas and enjoy the warm weather together.","t":"A：星期五的團隊午餐我們要在哪裡吃？員工餐廳因為維修關閉，會議室又太小，容納不下所有人。 B：經理訂了一家餐廳，建築後面有一個大【露台】，所以我們可以在陽傘下戶外用餐，一起享受溫暖的天氣。"},{"w":"port","p":"n.","d":"a town or place with a harbor where ships load and unload","c":"港口；港市","s":"A: Why did the shipping company move its main office out of the capital last year, when most of its clients are still based there? B: The managers wanted to be close to the busy port where our cargo ships arrive, so they can check deliveries quickly and solve problems with customs officers in person.","t":"A：為什麼那家航運公司去年把總部搬出首都？它大部分的客戶都還在那裡。 B：經理們想靠近我們貨船抵達的繁忙【港口】，這樣他們就能快速檢查貨物，並親自和海關人員解決問題。"},{"w":"barbeque","p":"n.","d":"an outdoor meal where food is cooked over a fire","c":"烤肉；烤肉聚會","s":"A: How are we going to welcome the new employees who joined the sales department this month, since many of them have not met the rest of the staff yet? B: We are planning a barbeque in the park next Saturday afternoon, and the company will pay for the meat, drinks, and games for everyone's families.","t":"A：我們要怎麼歡迎這個月加入業務部的新員工？他們很多人都還沒見過其他同事。 B：我們計劃下星期六下午在公園辦一場【烤肉聚會】，公司會出錢買肉、飲料，還會為大家的家人準備遊戲。"},{"w":"apartment block","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large building divided into many flats","c":"公寓大樓","s":"A: Where will the new engineers from overseas live when they arrive next month, since the hotels near the office are very expensive for long stays? B: The company rented ten units in a new apartment block across the street, so they can walk to work, share a gym, and get help from the building manager.","t":"A：海外來的新工程師下個月抵達後要住在哪裡？辦公室附近的飯店長期住宿非常貴。 B：公司在對街一棟新的【公寓大樓】租了十個單位，這樣他們可以走路上班、共用健身房，還能得到大樓管理員的協助。"},{"w":"back garden","p":"n.phr.","d":"the garden behind a house","c":"後花園；後院","s":"A: Why are you working from home every Friday now, when you used to come into the office five days a week without any problems? B: My manager agreed that I could use the quiet office I built in my back garden, so I can focus on reports without noise and save two hours of driving.","t":"A：為什麼你現在每個星期五都在家工作？你以前一週五天進辦公室都沒問題啊。 B：我的主管同意我使用我在【後花園】蓋的安靜辦公室，這樣我可以在沒有噪音的情況下專心寫報告，還能省下兩小時的開車時間。"},{"w":"detached house","p":"n.phr.","d":"a house that stands alone and is not joined to another","c":"獨棟房屋","s":"A: Are you and your wife still looking at small flats in the city, or have you changed your plans since the baby was born last spring? B: We now want a detached house with three bedrooms, because we need more space and privacy, and we don't want to share walls with noisy neighbors anymore.","t":"A：你和太太還在看城裡的小公寓嗎？還是去年春天寶寶出生後你們改變計畫了？ B：我們現在想要一間有三個房間的【獨棟房屋】，因為我們需要更多空間和隱私，也不想再和吵鬧的鄰居共用牆壁了。"},{"w":"suburb","p":"n.","d":"an area where people live outside the center of a city","c":"郊區；近郊住宅區","s":"A: Why does Ms. Chen take the early train every morning, even though our meetings usually don't start until ten o'clock? B: She lives in a quiet suburb about forty minutes from the city, so she leaves early to avoid crowded trains and uses the extra time to answer her emails.","t":"A：為什麼陳小姐每天早上都搭早班火車？我們的會議通常十點才開始。 B：她住在離城市大約四十分鐘車程的安靜【郊區】，所以她提早出門以避開擁擠的列車，並利用多出來的時間回覆電子郵件。"},{"w":"terraced house","p":"n.phr.","d":"one of a row of houses that are joined together","c":"連棟房屋；排屋","s":"A: What kind of home did you finally choose when you moved to London for your new job at the bank last autumn? B: I rented a small terraced house in a row of old brick homes, and although the walls are shared, it is cheaper than a flat and close to the underground station.","t":"A：你去年秋天為了銀行的新工作搬到倫敦時，最後選了什麼樣的住處？ B：我在一排老舊的磚造房子中租了一間小【連棟房屋】，雖然牆壁是共用的，但比公寓便宜，而且離地鐵站很近。"},{"w":"dream home","p":"n.phr.","d":"the perfect house that someone has always wanted","c":"夢想中的家","s":"A: Why have you been working so much overtime and saving almost all of your salary since the beginning of the year? B: My husband and I found our dream home near the beach, with big windows and a sunny kitchen, and we need a larger down payment before the bank will approve our loan.","t":"A：為什麼你從年初開始就一直加班，還把幾乎所有薪水都存起來？ B：我先生和我在海邊附近找到了我們【夢想中的家】，有大窗戶和陽光充足的廚房，在銀行核准貸款前我們需要更多頭期款。"},{"w":"layout","p":"n.","d":"the way the parts of a place are arranged","c":"格局；佈局；配置","s":"A: Did the clients like the new office building they visited yesterday, or do they still want to look at other places before signing the lease? B: They loved the open layout, because the desks, meeting rooms, and kitchen are arranged so that teams can easily talk, share ideas, and work together.","t":"A：客戶喜歡他們昨天參觀的新辦公大樓嗎？還是他們在簽租約前還想看看其他地方？ B：他們很喜歡那個開放式的【格局】，因為辦公桌、會議室和廚房的配置讓各團隊可以輕鬆交談、分享想法並一起工作。"},{"w":"troublesome","p":"adj.","d":"causing problems or worry","c":"麻煩的；棘手的","s":"A: Why did you decide to move out of your old flat downtown before your lease ended, even though the rent was very reasonable? B: The heating system was troublesome all winter, and the landlord took weeks to send someone to fix it, so I often had to work at home in my coat.","t":"A：為什麼你在租約到期前就決定搬離市區的舊公寓？雖然房租很合理。 B：暖氣系統整個冬天都很【麻煩】，房東要好幾週才派人來修，所以我在家工作時常常得穿著外套。"},{"w":"fully-furnished","p":"adj.","d":"having all the furniture that is needed","c":"家具齊全的","s":"A: What should I bring when I move to Singapore for the six-month project, since I don't want to ship too many heavy boxes? B: Don't worry, the company has booked you a fully-furnished apartment with a bed, sofa, desk, and kitchen tools, so you only need your clothes and your laptop.","t":"A：我搬去新加坡做六個月的專案時該帶什麼？我不想運太多很重的箱子。 B：別擔心，公司已經幫你訂了一間【家具齊全的】公寓，有床、沙發、書桌和廚房用具，所以你只需要帶衣服和筆電。"},{"w":"hall of residence","p":"n.phr.","d":"a building where university students live","c":"大學宿舍；學生宿舍","s":"A: Where did the summer interns from the local university stay while they worked at our head office for eight weeks this year? B: They lived in a hall of residence on campus, which was cheap and near the bus line, and they shared meals there with students working at other companies too.","t":"A：今年在我們總公司工作八週的當地大學暑期實習生住在哪裡？ B：他們住在校園內的【學生宿舍】，價格便宜又靠近公車路線，而且他們也在那裡和在其他公司工作的學生一起吃飯。"},{"w":"home comforts","p":"n.phr.","d":"things that make life at home easy and pleasant","c":"居家的舒適；家中的便利","s":"A: Do you enjoy staying in hotels during your long business trips, or do you get tired of living out of a suitcase for weeks? B: I usually miss my home comforts, like my own soft pillow, my coffee machine, and cooking my own dinner, so I try to book serviced apartments instead.","t":"A：你長期出差時喜歡住飯店嗎？還是連續好幾週靠一只行李箱過活會讓你感到疲倦？ B：我通常會想念【居家的舒適】，像是我自己的軟枕頭、咖啡機，還有自己煮晚餐，所以我會盡量改訂服務式公寓。"},{"w":"house-warming party","p":"n.phr.","d":"a party to celebrate moving into a new home","c":"喬遷派對；暖屋派對","s":"A: What are you doing this Saturday evening, since several of us from the marketing team are going out for dinner after the trade show? B: I can't join you because Kevin from accounting just bought a new flat, and he invited the whole department to his house-warming party to see the place.","t":"A：你這個星期六晚上要做什麼？我們行銷團隊幾個人在商展結束後要出去吃晚餐。 B：我沒辦法跟你們去，因為會計部的凱文剛買了新公寓，他邀請整個部門去參加他的【喬遷派對】看看新家。"},{"w":"exhausting","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel very tired","c":"令人筋疲力盡的","s":"A: How was your move to the new office building last weekend, and did the moving company arrive on time with enough workers? B: It was exhausting, because the elevator broke in the morning, so we had to carry dozens of boxes up five floors, and I slept for twelve hours afterward.","t":"A：你們上週末搬到新辦公大樓的情況如何？搬家公司有準時帶足夠的工人來嗎？ B：真是【令人筋疲力盡】，因為電梯早上壞了，我們只好把幾十個箱子搬上五樓，之後我睡了十二個小時。"},{"w":"move into","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start living or working in a new place","c":"搬進；遷入","s":"A: When can the accounting team start using the new office space on the third floor, since they are working in the crowded meeting room right now? B: The painters will finish on Thursday, so the team can move into the new space next Monday, after the IT staff set up the phones and computers.","t":"A：會計團隊什麼時候可以開始使用三樓的新辦公空間？他們現在正在擁擠的會議室裡工作。 B：油漆工星期四會完工，所以在資訊人員裝好電話和電腦之後，團隊下星期一就可以【搬進】新空間。"},{"w":"chill out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to relax and rest","c":"放鬆；休息","s":"A: What do you usually do after a long week of meetings and deadlines, since you always look so calm and fresh on Monday mornings? B: I like to chill out on my balcony with a good book and some music, and I turn off my work phone so nobody can bother me all weekend.","t":"A：在經歷了一整週的會議和截止期限後，你通常會做什麼？你每個星期一早上看起來總是很冷靜又有精神。 B：我喜歡在陽台上看本好書、聽點音樂來【放鬆】，而且我會關掉工作手機，這樣整個週末就沒人能打擾我。"},{"w":"permanent address","p":"n.phr.","d":"the place where you live long-term, used on official forms","c":"永久地址；戶籍地址","s":"A: Which address should I write on this job application form, since I am staying in a hotel until I find a flat in the city? B: Please give your permanent address, such as your family home, so the human resources office can send your contract and tax documents to a place that won't change.","t":"A：在這張求職申請表上我應該寫哪個地址？我在城裡找到公寓之前都住在飯店。 B：請填寫你的【永久地址】，例如你的老家，這樣人資部才能把你的合約和稅務文件寄到一個不會變動的地方。"},{"w":"ideal home","p":"n.phr.","d":"the best possible home for someone","c":"理想的家","s":"A: What is the main goal of the new housing project that our construction company is building near the river next year? B: We want to create the ideal home for young families, with safe parks, good schools nearby, energy-saving windows, and prices that most local workers can really pay each month.","t":"A：我們建設公司明年要在河邊蓋的新住宅案，主要目標是什麼？ B：我們想為年輕家庭打造【理想的家】，有安全的公園、附近有好學校、節能窗戶，而且價格是大部分當地上班族每個月真的付得起的。"},{"w":"single room","p":"n.phr.","d":"a room for one person","c":"單人房","s":"A: Should I book a double room for the training course in Tokyo, or will I be sharing with someone else from our branch office? B: The company only pays for a single room for each employee, so you will have your own space, but it is quite small and has just one bed and a desk.","t":"A：東京的培訓課程我該訂雙人房嗎？還是我會和分公司的其他人同住？ B：公司只為每位員工支付一間【單人房】的費用，所以你會有自己的空間，但房間很小，只有一張床和一張書桌。"},{"w":"spacious room","p":"n.phr.","d":"a room with a lot of space","c":"寬敞的房間","s":"A: Why did the managers choose this hotel for the annual training workshop instead of the cheaper one near the airport? B: This hotel offered a spacious room that can hold eighty people with tables, a large screen, and good lighting, while the other one only had small meeting areas for groups of ten.","t":"A：為什麼主管們選這間飯店舉辦年度培訓工作坊，而不是機場附近比較便宜的那間？ B：這間飯店提供了一間能容納八十人、配有桌子、大螢幕和良好照明的【寬敞房間】，而另一間只有供十人小組使用的小型會議區。"},{"w":"cozy","p":"adj.","d":"warm, comfortable, and pleasant","c":"舒適溫暖的；溫馨的","s":"A: How do you like the small café the company opened on the ground floor for staff who want a break from their desks? B: It feels very cozy, with soft chairs, warm lights, and a small bookshelf, so many of us go there to relax or have quiet meetings in the afternoon.","t":"A：你覺得公司在一樓為想離開辦公桌休息的員工開的小咖啡館怎麼樣？ B：感覺非常【溫馨舒適】，有柔軟的椅子、溫暖的燈光和一個小書架，所以我們很多人下午都會去那裡放鬆或開安靜的會議。"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"Achievement 成就","cards":[{"w":"success","p":"n.","d":"the good result of doing what you planned to do","c":"成功","s":"A: Why did the director invite the whole sales team to a dinner at the hotel restaurant last Friday evening? B: She wanted to celebrate the success of our new product launch, because we sold twice as many units as we expected in the first month, and she believed everyone deserved a reward for their hard work.","t":"A：主管為什麼上週五晚上邀請整個業務團隊到飯店餐廳吃晚餐？ B：她想慶祝我們新產品上市的【成功】，因為第一個月的銷量是我們預期的兩倍，而且她認為每個人的努力都值得獎勵。"},{"w":"accomplish","p":"v.","d":"to finish something successfully","c":"完成；達成","s":"A: Do you think our small team can finish the whole website redesign before the client meeting next Thursday afternoon? B: If we divide the work carefully, stay focused, and avoid long meetings this week, I believe we can accomplish the task on time, even though two designers are still on vacation until Monday.","t":"A：你覺得我們這個小團隊能在下週四下午的客戶會議前完成整個網站改版嗎？ B：如果我們仔細分工、保持專注，並且這週避免開冗長的會議，我相信我們能準時【完成】這項任務，雖然有兩位設計師休假到星期一。"},{"w":"attain","p":"v.","d":"to reach a goal or level after a lot of effort","c":"達到；獲得","s":"A: Why is the factory manager asking every worker to attend extra safety training on Saturday mornings this month? B: The company wants to attain an international quality certificate by the end of the year, and the inspectors will check whether every employee understands the new safety rules before they visit the factory.","t":"A：為什麼工廠經理這個月要求每位工人星期六早上參加額外的安全訓練？ B：公司想在年底前【取得】一張國際品質認證，而檢查人員來工廠前會確認每位員工是否了解新的安全規定。"},{"w":"milestone","p":"n.","d":"an important event or stage in the development of something","c":"里程碑；重要階段","s":"A: Why is everyone in the office wearing party hats and eating cake in the meeting room this afternoon? B: Our online store just reached one million customers, which is an important milestone for a company that started in a tiny garage only five years ago, so the boss ordered snacks for everyone.","t":"A：為什麼今天下午辦公室裡每個人都戴著派對帽、在會議室吃蛋糕？ B：我們的網路商店剛達到一百萬名顧客，對一家五年前才在小車庫創立的公司來說，這是一個重要的【里程碑】，所以老闆幫大家訂了點心。"},{"w":"fulfillment","p":"n.","d":"a happy feeling that comes from doing something useful or important","c":"成就感；滿足感","s":"A: Why did you leave your well-paid job at the bank to become a teacher at a small community center last year? B: The salary was great, but I never felt any real fulfillment there, and now I feel happy every day because I can see my students improving and using English confidently at work.","t":"A：你去年為什麼辭掉銀行的高薪工作，去一間小社區中心當老師？ B：那裡薪水很好，但我從沒感到真正的【成就感】，現在我每天都很快樂，因為我能看到學生進步，並在工作上自信地使用英文。"},{"w":"triumph","p":"n.","d":"a great success or victory","c":"勝利；巨大成功","s":"A: How did the new marketing manager react when she heard that the company had signed the contract with the Japanese buyer? B: She called it a real triumph for the whole department, because three other companies had also wanted the deal, and our team worked late every night for two months to prepare the proposal.","t":"A：新任行銷經理聽到公司和日本買家簽約時有什麼反應？ B：她說這是整個部門的一大【勝利】，因為另外三家公司也想拿到這筆生意，而我們團隊連續兩個月每晚加班準備提案。"},{"w":"excel","p":"v.","d":"to be very good at something","c":"擅長；表現出色","s":"A: Why did the human resources department choose Kevin to lead the customer service training program for new employees this year? B: He has always been able to excel at solving difficult problems with angry customers, and he explains things in a calm, friendly way that helps new staff feel relaxed and confident.","t":"A：人資部門今年為什麼選凱文來負責新進員工的客服訓練課程？ B：他一向【擅長】處理憤怒顧客的棘手問題，而且他會用冷靜友善的方式解釋事情，讓新員工感到放鬆又有自信。"},{"w":"progress","p":"n.","d":"movement toward finishing or improving something","c":"進展；進步","s":"A: The construction company promised that the new office building would be ready in March, so why are we still working from the old one? B: Heavy rain stopped the workers for several weeks, so progress has been slower than planned, but the manager says we should be able to move in by early summer.","t":"A：建設公司承諾新辦公大樓三月就會完工，為什麼我們還在舊大樓上班？ B：大雨讓工人停工好幾週，所以【進度】比計畫慢，不過經理說我們應該能在初夏前搬進去。"},{"w":"mastery","p":"n.","d":"great skill or knowledge in a subject or activity","c":"精通；熟練","s":"A: Why did the company hire a young engineer from Germany instead of choosing someone from the local office for the new project? B: Her mastery of the latest design software is impressive, and the project needs someone who can solve technical problems quickly and also train our local team to use the same programs.","t":"A：公司為什麼從德國聘請一位年輕工程師，而不是從本地辦公室挑人負責新專案？ B：她對最新設計軟體的【精通】令人佩服，而這個專案需要一個能快速解決技術問題、又能訓練本地團隊使用同樣程式的人。"},{"w":"distinction","p":"n.","d":"a special honor given for excellent work or results","c":"優異成績；殊榮；卓越","s":"A: Have you heard anything about the new accountant who is joining our finance team next Monday morning? B: Yes, she graduated with distinction from a famous business school in London, and after that she worked for an international bank for six years, so I think she will bring a lot of useful experience.","t":"A：你有聽說下週一早上要加入我們財務團隊的新會計嗎？ B：有，她以【優異成績】從倫敦一所知名商學院畢業，之後在一家國際銀行工作了六年，所以我想她會帶來很多有用的經驗。"},{"w":"recognition","p":"n.","d":"public praise or thanks for something good someone has done","c":"認可；表揚","s":"A: Why does the company hold a special lunch for staff members at the end of every quarter? B: The managers want to give public recognition to employees who worked hard or helped customers in special ways, because they believe that thanking people in front of their coworkers makes everyone feel more motivated.","t":"A：為什麼公司每季末都會為員工舉辦特別午餐？ B：主管們想公開【表揚】那些努力工作或用特別方式幫助顧客的員工，因為他們相信在同事面前感謝別人，會讓大家更有動力。"},{"w":"realize","p":"v.","d":"to make a hope or plan really happen","c":"實現（夢想、計畫）","s":"A: Why did your sister quit her office job and open a small bakery near the train station last spring? B: She had always dreamed of running her own business, and after saving money for ten years, she finally decided it was time to realize that dream before she got too busy with other responsibilities.","t":"A：你姊姊去年春天為什麼辭掉辦公室工作，在火車站附近開了一家小麵包店？ B：她一直夢想經營自己的事業，存了十年的錢之後，她終於決定是時候【實現】這個夢想了，免得之後被其他責任綁住而太忙。"},{"w":"victory","p":"n.","d":"success in a game, competition, or fight","c":"勝利","s":"A: Why is the sports shop on Main Street offering a thirty percent discount on all football shirts this weekend? B: The local team won the national championship last night, and the owner wants to celebrate the victory with the fans, so he expects the store to be very crowded until Sunday evening.","t":"A：為什麼大街上的運動用品店這個週末所有足球衫都打七折？ B：當地球隊昨晚贏得全國冠軍，老闆想和球迷一起慶祝這場【勝利】，所以他預計店裡到星期日晚上都會很擁擠。"},{"w":"breakthrough","p":"n.","d":"an important new discovery or development","c":"突破；重大進展","s":"A: Why are the scientists in the research lab so excited, and why did the company cancel this afternoon's regular meeting? B: They finally made a major breakthrough in developing a cheaper battery for electric cars, so the director called an urgent meeting with the investors to discuss how quickly the product can reach the market.","t":"A：研究實驗室的科學家為什麼這麼興奮？公司又為什麼取消今天下午的例行會議？ B：他們終於在開發更便宜的電動車電池上有了重大【突破】，所以主管召開緊急會議，和投資人討論產品能多快上市。"},{"w":"accolade","p":"n.","d":"praise or an award given for excellent work","c":"讚揚；榮譽；獎項","s":"A: Have you seen the article in this morning's newspaper about the small Italian restaurant across the street from our office? B: Yes, a famous food critic gave it the highest accolade of the year, so now it is almost impossible to book a table there for our team lunch next Friday.","t":"A：你看了今天早報上那篇關於我們辦公室對面那家小義大利餐廳的報導嗎？ B：看了，一位知名美食評論家給了它今年最高的【讚譽】，所以現在要訂那裡的位子給我們下週五的團隊午餐幾乎不可能了。"},{"w":"honor","p":"n.","d":"something that makes you feel proud and respected","c":"榮幸；榮譽","s":"A: How did you feel when the president of the company asked you to give the opening speech at the annual conference in Singapore? B: It was a great honor for me, because I have only worked here for two years, but I was also very nervous about speaking in front of five hundred people.","t":"A：公司總裁請你在新加坡年會上致開幕詞時，你有什麼感覺？ B：這對我來說是莫大的【榮幸】，因為我在這裡才工作兩年，但要在五百人面前演講也讓我非常緊張。"},{"w":"advance","p":"v.","d":"to move forward or get a higher position at work","c":"晉升；前進","s":"A: Why are so many junior staff members signing up for the evening management courses that the company offers this semester? B: They know that employees who complete the courses usually advance to senior positions more quickly, and the company also pays for the classes, so it is a great opportunity for everyone.","t":"A：為什麼這學期有這麼多基層員工報名公司開設的晚間管理課程？ B：他們知道完成課程的員工通常能更快【晉升】到高階職位，而且公司也負擔學費，所以對大家來說是很好的機會。"},{"w":"gain","p":"v.","d":"to get something useful, such as skills or experience","c":"獲得；增加","s":"A: Why did you accept a summer internship at a small trading company instead of taking a longer vacation with your family? B: I wanted to gain some practical experience before I graduate, and the manager there promised that I could work directly with overseas clients, which will look great on my resume.","t":"A：你為什麼接受一家小貿易公司的暑期實習，而不是和家人去度個較長的假？ B：我想在畢業前【獲得】一些實務經驗，而且那裡的經理承諾我可以直接和海外客戶合作，這會讓我的履歷很加分。"},{"w":"prosperity","p":"n.","d":"a situation of having money and success","c":"繁榮；興旺","s":"A: Why has the city government spent so much money on building a new port and highway near the coast? B: The mayor believes that better transportation will attract foreign companies and bring long-term prosperity to the region, creating thousands of new jobs for young people who usually move away to find work.","t":"A：市政府為什麼花那麼多錢在海岸附近興建新港口和高速公路？ B：市長相信更好的交通能吸引外國企業，為這個地區帶來長期的【繁榮】，替那些通常得外移找工作的年輕人創造數千個新工作機會。"},{"w":"completion","p":"n.","d":"the act of finishing something","c":"完成；結束","s":"A: When will the contractor receive the final payment for renovating our office on the third floor? B: According to the contract, we will pay the last part of the money after the completion of all the work, including painting the walls, installing the new lights, and cleaning the whole area.","t":"A：承包商什麼時候會收到我們三樓辦公室翻修的尾款？ B：根據合約，我們會在所有工程【完成】後支付最後一筆款項，包括粉刷牆壁、安裝新燈具以及清潔整個區域。"},{"w":"reward","p":"n.","d":"something given to thank someone for good work or effort","c":"獎勵；報酬","s":"A: Why did the store manager give each cashier a gift card and an extra day off at the end of the holiday season? B: It was a reward for their hard work during the busiest weeks of the year, when they served long lines of customers and stayed late almost every night without complaining.","t":"A：店經理為什麼在假期旺季結束時給每位收銀員一張禮物卡和一天額外的假？ B：那是對他們在一年中最忙碌幾週辛勤工作的【獎勵】，當時他們服務大排長龍的顧客，幾乎每晚都留下來加班卻毫無怨言。"},{"w":"ambition","p":"n.","d":"a strong wish to be successful or to do something","c":"抱負；雄心","s":"A: What did the young sales assistant say during her interview when the manager asked about her plans for the future? B: She said her biggest ambition is to open her own fashion company one day, and she wants to learn everything about buying, marketing, and managing a store while she works with us.","t":"A：主管在面試時問那位年輕的銷售助理對未來的規劃，她怎麼回答？ B：她說她最大的【抱負】是有一天開自己的服裝公司，所以她想在跟我們工作時，學習所有關於採購、行銷和管理商店的知識。"},{"w":"merit","p":"n.","d":"good quality or ability that deserves praise or reward","c":"優點；功績；實力","s":"A: How does the company decide which employees receive a pay raise at the end of each year? B: Raises are based on merit, not on how long people have worked here, so managers look carefully at each person's results, teamwork, and customer feedback before they make any final decisions.","t":"A：公司每年年底如何決定哪些員工可以加薪？ B：加薪是根據【實力與表現】，而不是看在這裡工作多久，所以主管在做最後決定前，會仔細檢視每個人的成果、團隊合作和顧客回饋。"},{"w":"earn","p":"v.","d":"to get money or respect because of your work","c":"賺取；贏得","s":"A: Why does Daniel work as a tour guide on weekends even though he already has a full-time job at the bank? B: He wants to earn some extra money to pay for his master's degree next year, and he also enjoys meeting tourists from different countries and practicing his foreign languages.","t":"A：丹尼爾已經在銀行有全職工作，為什麼週末還要當導遊？ B：他想【賺】一些外快來支付明年的碩士學費，而且他也喜歡認識來自不同國家的觀光客並練習外語。"},{"w":"win","p":"v.","d":"to be the best in a competition or to get a prize or contract","c":"贏得；獲勝","s":"A: Why is the design team working so late every evening this week, even though their normal projects are almost finished? B: They are preparing a special presentation because they really hope to win the contract for the new airport terminal, which would be the biggest project in the company's history.","t":"A：設計團隊這週為什麼每晚都加班到很晚，即使他們的一般專案都快完成了？ B：他們正在準備一份特別簡報，因為他們非常希望【贏得】新機場航廈的合約，那將是公司史上最大的專案。"},{"w":"outcome","p":"n.","d":"the final result of an action or event","c":"結果；成果","s":"A: Have the managers decided whether we will move our main office to the new business park outside the city? B: Not yet, they are still discussing the costs with the landlord, and they said they will tell all the staff about the final outcome of the negotiations at the meeting next Wednesday.","t":"A：主管們決定好是否要把總公司搬到市郊新的商業園區了嗎？ B：還沒，他們還在和房東討論費用，並說會在下週三的會議上告訴所有員工談判的最終【結果】。"},{"w":"acquire","p":"v.","d":"to get or learn something, such as a skill or a company","c":"習得；取得；收購","s":"A: Why does the company send new engineers to work in the Tokyo office for six months during their first year? B: It helps them acquire useful skills and learn how our partners in Japan work, so they can communicate better with overseas clients when they return to the head office.","t":"A：公司為什麼在新工程師的第一年派他們到東京辦公室工作六個月？ B：這能幫助他們【習得】實用的技能，並了解我們日本夥伴的工作方式，讓他們回到總公司後能和海外客戶更順利地溝通。"},{"w":"status","p":"n.","d":"a person's position or importance compared with others","c":"地位；身分","s":"A: Why do so many of our clients insist on staying at the expensive five-star hotel downtown when they visit for business meetings? B: For many of them, staying there shows their high status in the company, and they also like the quiet meeting rooms and the excellent restaurant on the top floor.","t":"A：為什麼我們很多客戶來開商務會議時，堅持要住市中心那家昂貴的五星級飯店？ B：對他們很多人來說，住在那裡能彰顯他們在公司裡的崇高【地位】，而且他們也喜歡那裡安靜的會議室和頂樓的高級餐廳。"},{"w":"self-made","p":"adj.","d":"successful or rich because of your own hard work, not help from others","c":"白手起家的","s":"A: What do you know about the woman who will give the main speech at the small business conference next month? B: She is a self-made businesswoman who started selling handmade bags at a night market twenty years ago, and today her company has more than fifty shops across Asia and Europe.","t":"A：你對下個月在小企業研討會上發表主題演講的那位女士了解多少？ B：她是一位【白手起家的】女企業家，二十年前從夜市賣手工包包起家，如今她的公司在亞洲和歐洲擁有超過五十家店。"}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"Activity 活動","cards":[{"w":"event","p":"n.","d":"something important or special that happens, often planned","c":"活動；大型活動；事件","s":"A: Why is the hotel lobby so crowded today, and why are there so many people in suits carrying name badges and brochures? B: A large technology company has rented the main hall for a special event to celebrate its twentieth anniversary, so hundreds of guests, partners, and reporters have arrived from different cities this morning.","t":"A：為什麼今天飯店大廳這麼擁擠，而且有這麼多穿西裝的人拿著名牌和手冊？ B：一家大型科技公司租下了主廳舉辦一場特別的【活動】來慶祝二十週年，所以今天早上有數百位賓客、合作夥伴和記者從不同城市來到這裡。"},{"w":"occasion","p":"n.","d":"a special time or event","c":"場合；特殊時刻","s":"A: Should I wear my usual work clothes to the retirement dinner for Mr. Lin on Friday night, or do you think something more formal would be better? B: Since it is an important occasion and the president will give a speech, most of the staff are planning to wear suits or nice dresses, so I would dress up a little.","t":"A：週五晚上林先生的退休晚宴，我應該穿平常的上班服裝，還是你覺得穿正式一點比較好？ B：因為這是一個重要的【場合】，而且總裁會致詞，大部分員工都打算穿西裝或漂亮的洋裝，所以我會稍微打扮一下。"},{"w":"gathering","p":"n.","d":"a meeting of people for a social or work purpose","c":"聚會；集會","s":"A: Are you going to the small gathering in the staff lounge after work today, or do you have to leave early to pick up your children from school? B: I will stay for about an hour because the team wants to say goodbye to Emma, who is moving to our Tokyo office next week, and I helped buy her gift.","t":"A：你今天下班後會去員工休息室的小型【聚會】嗎？還是你得早點離開去學校接小孩？ B：我會待大約一個小時，因為團隊想跟下週要調到東京辦公室的艾瑪道別，而且我有幫忙買她的禮物。"},{"w":"celebration","p":"n.","d":"a party or special event to show you are happy about something","c":"慶祝；慶祝活動","s":"A: Why did the manager order so many cakes and balloons for the office this afternoon, and is it someone's birthday today? B: No, it is a celebration for our sales team, because they reached their yearly target two months early, and the director wants to thank everyone for working so hard during the busy season.","t":"A：為什麼經理今天下午幫辦公室訂了這麼多蛋糕和氣球？今天是誰生日嗎？ B：不是，這是為我們業務團隊舉辦的【慶祝活動】，因為他們提早兩個月達成年度目標，主管想感謝大家在旺季這麼努力工作。"},{"w":"festival","p":"n.","d":"a special time when people enjoy music, food, or culture, often for several days","c":"節慶；（藝術、音樂等）節","s":"A: Why are all the hotels near the river fully booked next weekend, and where should our visiting clients stay during their trip? B: The city is holding its yearly food and music festival by the river, so thousands of tourists are coming, and we should book rooms in a business hotel near the train station instead.","t":"A：為什麼下週末河邊附近的飯店都客滿了？來訪的客戶出差期間應該住在哪裡？ B：市政府要在河邊舉辦一年一度的美食音樂【節】，所以會有數千名遊客湧入，我們應該改訂火車站附近的商務旅館。"},{"w":"ceremony","p":"n.","d":"a formal public event with special traditions or actions","c":"典禮；儀式","s":"A: What time should the guests arrive at the new factory on Monday morning, and will there be enough chairs for the local reporters? B: The opening ceremony starts at ten o'clock, when the mayor will cut the ribbon, so guests should arrive by nine-thirty, and I have already asked the staff to set up fifty extra seats.","t":"A：週一早上賓客應該幾點到達新工廠？給當地記者的椅子夠嗎？ B：開幕【典禮】十點開始，屆時市長會剪綵，所以賓客應該在九點半前抵達，而且我已經請員工多擺五十個座位。"},{"w":"function","p":"n.","d":"a formal social event, such as a party or dinner","c":"宴會；正式聚會","s":"A: Is the large dining room on the top floor of the hotel available on Saturday evening, or has another company already reserved it? B: I'm sorry, but a bank is holding a private function for its most important customers that night, so the room is closed to the public, but our garden restaurant still has space.","t":"A：飯店頂樓的大型餐廳週六晚上可以使用嗎？還是已經被其他公司預訂了？ B：很抱歉，那天晚上一家銀行要為最重要的客戶舉辦私人【宴會】，所以那個廳不對外開放，不過我們的花園餐廳還有位子。"},{"w":"program","p":"n.","d":"a planned series of activities or events","c":"計畫；課程方案；節目","s":"A: How can new employees learn about the company's products and safety rules before they start working in the warehouse next month? B: The human resources department has created a two-week training program with short classes, factory tours, and practice tests, so every new worker will understand the main rules before their first real shift.","t":"A：新進員工下個月開始在倉庫工作前，要怎麼了解公司的產品和安全規定？ B：人資部門設計了一個為期兩週的訓練【計畫】，包括短期課程、工廠參觀和練習測驗，所以每位新員工在第一次正式上班前都會了解主要規定。"},{"w":"session","p":"n.","d":"a period of time used for a particular activity","c":"（活動的）一段時間；場次；講習","s":"A: I couldn't get to the conference until lunchtime because my flight was delayed, so did I miss anything really important this morning? B: You missed the first session about online marketing, but the speaker uploaded her slides to the website, and the afternoon talks about customer service are probably more useful for your team anyway.","t":"A：我的班機延誤，所以到中午才趕到研討會，我今天早上有錯過什麼很重要的內容嗎？ B：你錯過了第一【場】關於網路行銷的講座，不過講者已經把投影片上傳到網站，而且下午關於客服的演講對你的團隊可能反而更有用。"},{"w":"meeting","p":"n.","d":"an event when people come together to discuss something","c":"會議","s":"A: Why isn't Mr. Chen answering his phone this morning, when the client from Singapore has called him three times already? B: He is in a long meeting with the board of directors to discuss next year's budget, and he asked his assistant not to disturb him until it finishes at about eleven-thirty.","t":"A：為什麼陳先生今天早上都不接電話？新加坡的客戶已經打給他三次了。 B：他正在和董事會開一場很長的【會議】討論明年的預算，他請助理在大約十一點半結束前不要打擾他。"},{"w":"workshop","p":"n.","d":"a meeting where people learn a skill by doing practical activities","c":"研習會；工作坊","s":"A: Do you know any good way for our sales staff to improve their speaking skills before they meet the overseas buyers next month? B: Yes, a local business school is offering a one-day workshop on presentation skills, where each person practices speaking in small groups and gets helpful feedback from an experienced trainer.","t":"A：你知道有什麼好方法可以讓我們的業務人員在下個月見國外買家之前提升口說能力嗎？ B：有，當地一所商學院開設了為期一天的簡報技巧【工作坊】，每個人都會在小組中練習說話，並得到經驗豐富的講師給予的實用回饋。"},{"w":"seminar","p":"n.","d":"a class or meeting where a small group discusses a subject with an expert","c":"研討會；專題討論會","s":"A: Why are so many accountants from our department leaving the office early this Thursday afternoon, and who will answer client calls? B: They are going to a seminar at the city hall about the new tax laws, which will start next year, and two staff members from the front desk will answer the phones while they are away.","t":"A：為什麼我們部門這週四下午有這麼多會計師提早離開辦公室？誰來接客戶的電話？ B：他們要去市政廳參加一場關於明年開始實施的新稅法的【研討會】，他們不在時，櫃台的兩位員工會負責接電話。"},{"w":"conference","p":"n.","d":"a large formal meeting where many people discuss a subject, often for several days","c":"（大型）會議；大會","s":"A: Have you booked your flight to Singapore for next month yet, and are you going to give a speech there this year? B: Yes, I booked it yesterday, because I'm speaking at the international conference on green energy, where about two thousand engineers and business leaders will share ideas for three days.","t":"A：你訂好下個月飛新加坡的機票了嗎？你今年會在那裡演講嗎？ B：訂好了，我昨天訂的，因為我要在國際綠能【大會】上演講，屆時大約兩千名工程師和企業領袖會在三天內交流想法。"},{"w":"competition","p":"n.","d":"an event in which people try to win a prize by being the best","c":"比賽；競賽","s":"A: Why is everyone in the design department working so late every night this week, even though our big project is already finished? B: They entered a national competition for the best new product packaging, and the winning team will receive a large cash prize, so they want their design to be perfect before Friday's deadline.","t":"A：為什麼設計部的每個人這週每天晚上都工作到這麼晚？我們的大案子明明已經完成了。 B：他們報名了一場全國最佳新產品包裝【比賽】，獲勝的團隊會得到一大筆獎金，所以他們希望在週五截止前讓設計完美無缺。"},{"w":"tournament","p":"n.","d":"a sports or game competition with many players or teams and several rounds","c":"錦標賽；聯賽","s":"A: Why is the company gym booked every evening this month, when I usually go there after work to exercise? B: Our office is holding a basketball tournament between eight departments, and teams practice there every night, but the games will end next Friday, so you can use the gym again after that.","t":"A：為什麼公司健身房這個月每天晚上都被預約滿了？我平常下班後都會去那裡運動。 B：我們辦公室正在舉辦一場八個部門之間的籃球【錦標賽】，各隊每天晚上都在那裡練習，不過比賽下週五就會結束，之後你就可以再使用健身房了。"},{"w":"performance","p":"n.","d":"the act of playing music, dancing, or acting in front of people","c":"演出；表演","s":"A: Did you enjoy the company's year-end party at the hotel last night, or did you leave early because you were so tired? B: I stayed until the end, because the most exciting part was a live performance by a famous jazz band, and the guests kept dancing and clapping until almost midnight.","t":"A：你昨晚喜歡公司在飯店舉辦的尾牙嗎？還是因為太累提早離開了？ B：我待到最後，因為最精彩的部分是一個知名爵士樂團的現場【演出】，賓客一直跳舞拍手到快午夜。"},{"w":"show","p":"n.","d":"an event where people look at products or watch entertainment","c":"展覽；表演；節目","s":"A: Why did the marketing team pack so many boxes of brochures and product samples into the van this morning? B: They are driving to the convention center for a three-day trade show, where hundreds of companies display their newest products, and they hope to meet many new buyers from Japan and Korea there.","t":"A：為什麼行銷團隊今天早上把這麼多箱手冊和產品樣品搬上廂型車？ B：他們要開車到會展中心參加為期三天的貿易【展】，數百家公司會在那裡展示最新產品，他們希望能在那裡認識許多來自日本和韓國的新買家。"},{"w":"exhibition","p":"n.","d":"a public event where art or products are shown to people","c":"展覽；展覽會","s":"A: What are you planning to do with the visiting clients on Saturday afternoon after the factory tour is over? B: I'm going to take them to the city museum, because there is a special exhibition of old Taiwanese photographs and paintings, and they told me they are very interested in local history and art.","t":"A：週六下午工廠參觀結束後，你打算帶來訪的客戶做什麼？ B：我要帶他們去市立博物館，因為那裡有一個台灣老照片和畫作的特別【展覽】，他們跟我說對當地歷史和藝術很有興趣。"},{"w":"presentation","p":"n.","d":"a talk that gives information about something to a group of people","c":"簡報；報告","s":"A: You look very nervous this morning, so is something wrong with the new project, or did you not sleep well last night? B: I have to give a presentation to the senior managers about our sales results at ten o'clock, and I'm worried that the projector might not work, so I printed copies of every slide.","t":"A：你今天早上看起來很緊張，是新專案出了什麼問題，還是昨晚沒睡好？ B：我十點要向高階主管做一場關於業績結果的【簡報】，我擔心投影機可能會故障，所以把每張投影片都印出來了。"},{"w":"demonstration","p":"n.","d":"an act of showing how something works or how to do something","c":"示範；展示","s":"A: How will the store staff learn to use the new coffee machines before the café opens to customers next Monday? B: A technician from the supplier is coming on Friday afternoon to give a demonstration, so she will show everyone step by step how to clean the machine and make each type of drink.","t":"A：門市員工要怎麼在下週一咖啡廳開幕前學會使用新的咖啡機？ B：供應商的技術人員週五下午會來做【示範】，她會一步一步教大家如何清潔機器以及製作每一種飲料。"},{"w":"activity-based","p":"adj.","d":"using practical activities to help people learn or work","c":"以活動為主的；活動式的","s":"A: The new employees seemed bored during last month's training, so how can we make the lessons more interesting for the next group? B: We should try an activity-based approach, where trainees solve real problems in small teams and play short role-play games instead of listening to long lectures all day.","t":"A：新進員工在上個月的訓練中似乎很無聊，我們要怎麼讓下一梯次的課程更有趣？ B：我們應該試試【以活動為主的】方式，讓學員以小組解決真實問題並玩簡短的角色扮演遊戲，而不是整天聽冗長的講課。"},{"w":"interactive","p":"adj.","d":"allowing people to take part and communicate, not just watch or listen","c":"互動的；互動式的","s":"A: Why do so many children and parents visit the science museum downtown on weekends, even though the tickets are quite expensive? B: The museum has many interactive displays, where visitors can touch screens, build simple machines, and try small experiments, so families have fun and learn something at the same time.","t":"A：為什麼週末有這麼多孩子和家長去市中心的科學博物館，即使門票相當貴？ B：博物館有很多【互動式的】展示，參觀者可以觸碰螢幕、組裝簡單的機器並嘗試小實驗，所以家庭可以同時玩得開心又學到東西。"},{"w":"recreational","p":"adj.","d":"relating to activities that people do for fun when they are not working","c":"娛樂的；休閒的","s":"A: What kind of benefits does the new company offer its staff, apart from a good salary and health insurance? B: It has a large recreational center next to the office with a swimming pool, a game room, and tennis courts, so employees can relax and exercise after work without paying any extra fees.","t":"A：除了優渥的薪水和健康保險，新公司還提供員工哪些福利？ B：公司在辦公室旁邊有一座大型【休閒】中心，裡面有游泳池、遊戲室和網球場，所以員工下班後可以放鬆和運動，不需要另外付費。"},{"w":"scheduled","p":"adj.","d":"planned for a particular time","c":"預定的；排定的","s":"A: Is the shipment of new office furniture still going to arrive on Tuesday, or has the delivery company changed the date again? B: The scheduled delivery time is still Tuesday at two o'clock, but the driver said heavy rain might cause a short delay, so someone should wait at the loading area that afternoon.","t":"A：新辦公家具還是會在週二送到嗎？還是貨運公司又改日期了？ B：【預定的】送貨時間還是週二下午兩點，不過司機說大雨可能會造成短暫延誤，所以那天下午應該要有人在卸貨區等。"},{"w":"organized","p":"adj.","d":"planned carefully and arranged well","c":"有組織的；安排好的","s":"A: Are you going on the weekend trip to the mountains with the rest of the accounting team, or do you prefer to rest at home? B: I'm going, because it's an organized tour with a bus, a local guide, and all the meals included, so I don't need to plan anything or worry about getting lost.","t":"A：你會跟會計團隊的其他人一起去山上的週末旅行嗎？還是你比較想在家休息？ B：我會去，因為那是一個【安排好的】團體行程，包含巴士、當地導遊和所有餐點，所以我不需要計畫任何事情，也不用擔心迷路。"},{"w":"participate","p":"v.","d":"to take part in an activity or event","c":"參加；參與","s":"A: Do all employees have to join the company's charity run in the park next Sunday morning, even if they are not very good at running? B: No, nobody is required to participate, but the manager hopes many people will join, because the money we raise will help buy books for children at a local school.","t":"A：所有員工都必須參加下週日早上在公園舉辦的公司慈善路跑嗎？即使不太擅長跑步也一樣？ B：不，沒有人被要求一定要【參加】，但經理希望很多人會加入，因為我們募到的錢會用來幫當地一所學校的孩子買書。"},{"w":"host","p":"v.","d":"to organize an event and invite people to it","c":"主辦；舉辦","s":"A: Which city did the board of directors finally choose for next year's sales meeting, and when will they tell the regional managers? B: They decided that our Taichung office will host the meeting, because it has a large new conference room and is close to the high-speed rail station, and they will announce it on Monday.","t":"A：董事會最後選了哪個城市辦明年的業務會議？他們什麼時候會告知各區經理？ B：他們決定由我們台中辦公室【主辦】這場會議，因為那裡有一間新的大型會議室，而且離高鐵站很近，他們會在週一宣布。"},{"w":"attend","p":"v.","d":"to go to an event, such as a meeting or class","c":"出席；參加","s":"A: Will you be able to attend the training workshop on customer service tomorrow afternoon, or are you still busy preparing the monthly report? B: I'll be there, because my supervisor said it is very important for everyone who works at the front desk, and I finished most of the report last night anyway.","t":"A：你明天下午能【出席】客服訓練工作坊嗎？還是你還在忙著準備月報？ B：我會到，因為主管說這對所有在櫃台工作的人都非常重要，而且反正我昨晚已經把報告大部分完成了。"},{"w":"conduct","p":"v.","d":"to organize and do a particular activity","c":"進行；實施","s":"A: How will the company find out whether customers are happy with the new mobile app that we released last month? B: The marketing department plans to conduct an online survey next week, asking about five hundred users to answer ten short questions, and the results will help the designers decide what to improve.","t":"A：公司要怎麼了解顧客是否滿意我們上個月推出的新手機應用程式？ B：行銷部打算下週【進行】一項線上調查，請大約五百位使用者回答十個簡短的問題，結果會幫助設計師決定要改善哪些地方。"},{"w":"launch","p":"v.","d":"to start something new, or to make a new product available","c":"推出；發起","s":"A: Why has the marketing team been working so hard on weekends recently, and when will they finally get some rest? B: The company is going to launch its new line of energy drinks at a big event next month, so they are busy preparing the advertisements, the website, and the free samples for customers.","t":"A：為什麼行銷團隊最近週末都這麼努力工作？他們什麼時候才能休息？ B：公司下個月要在一場大型活動中【推出】新系列的能量飲料，所以他們正忙著準備廣告、網站和給顧客的免費樣品。"},{"w":"engage","p":"v.","d":"to take part in an activity, or to get someone interested","c":"參與；吸引（注意）","s":"A: Why does the new manager always ask so many questions and give small prizes during her training classes for the sales staff? B: She wants everyone to engage in the discussion instead of just sitting quietly, because she believes people remember more information when they share their own ideas and experiences with the group.","t":"A：為什麼新經理在業務人員訓練課上總是問很多問題又發小獎品？ B：她希望大家都能【參與】討論，而不是只是安靜地坐著，因為她相信當人們和團隊分享自己的想法和經驗時，會記得更多資訊。"},{"w":"occur","p":"v.","d":"to happen","c":"發生","s":"A: Why did the factory manager suddenly call an emergency meeting this afternoon, and should the office staff join it too? B: He wants to explain the new safety rules, because two small accidents happened in the warehouse last week, and he wants to make sure that problems like that never occur again in any part of the building.","t":"A：為什麼工廠經理今天下午突然召開緊急會議？辦公室員工也要參加嗎？ B：他想說明新的安全規定，因為上週倉庫發生了兩起小意外，他要確保這類問題不會在大樓的任何地方再次【發生】。"},{"w":"wrap-up","p":"n.","d":"the final part of an event that sums up what happened","c":"總結；收尾","s":"A: Do I need to stay until the very end of the three-day conference on Friday, or can I leave after the last afternoon talk? B: Please stay for the wrap-up at four o'clock, because the organizers will summarize the main ideas from every session, give out certificates, and explain how to download all of the speakers' slides.","t":"A：週五這場為期三天的研討會，我需要待到最後嗎？還是可以在下午最後一場演講後離開？ B：請留下來參加四點的【總結】，因為主辦單位會歸納每一場的重點、頒發證書，並說明如何下載所有講者的投影片。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"Actor 演員","cards":[{"w":"actress","p":"n.","d":"a woman whose job is acting in plays, films, or TV shows","c":"女演員","s":"A: Who is going to appear in the new television commercial for our skin care products, and has the marketing team already signed the contract with her agent? B: We hired a young actress from Taipei who has starred in two popular dramas, and her agent signed the contract yesterday, so filming will start next Monday at the studio downtown.","t":"A：誰要出演我們護膚產品的新電視廣告？行銷團隊已經和她的經紀人簽約了嗎？ B：我們聘請了一位來自台北、主演過兩部熱門連續劇的年輕【女演員】，她的經紀人昨天已經簽約了，所以下週一將在市中心的攝影棚開始拍攝。"},{"w":"perform","p":"v.","d":"to act, sing, or dance in front of an audience","c":"表演；演出","s":"A: What kind of entertainment have you planned for the company's annual dinner, and will it be finished before the awards ceremony begins? B: A local theater group will perform a short comedy about office life for about twenty minutes, and then the managers will hand out the awards right after the actors leave the stage.","t":"A：你為公司年度晚宴安排了什麼樣的娛樂節目？會在頒獎典禮開始前結束嗎？ B：一個當地劇團將【表演】一齣大約二十分鐘、關於辦公室生活的短篇喜劇，演員們一離開舞台，經理們就會立刻頒發獎項。"},{"w":"performance","p":"n.","d":"an event when people act, sing, or dance for an audience","c":"演出；表演","s":"A: Did you enjoy the play that the sales department took our overseas clients to see at the National Theater last Friday evening? B: Yes, the performance was excellent, and the clients were so impressed by the actors and the music that they asked our manager to book tickets for another show before they fly home.","t":"A：上週五晚上業務部帶海外客戶去國家戲劇院看的那齣戲，你喜歡嗎？ B：喜歡，那場【演出】非常精彩，客戶們對演員和音樂印象深刻，還請我們經理在他們回國前再訂另一場表演的票。"},{"w":"role","p":"n.","d":"the part that an actor plays in a film or play","c":"角色","s":"A: Why has the famous actor agreed to appear in such a small training video for our bank, even though he usually only makes big movies? B: His sister works in our customer service department, and he liked the role of a friendly bank teller who helps an elderly customer, so he agreed to take a much lower fee than usual.","t":"A：為什麼那位知名演員願意出演我們銀行這麼小的培訓影片，他平常不是只拍大型電影嗎？ B：他的妹妹在我們客服部工作，而且他喜歡那個幫助年長顧客的親切銀行櫃員【角色】，所以他同意收取比平常低很多的酬勞。"},{"w":"character","p":"n.","d":"a person or animal in a story, film, or play","c":"角色；人物","s":"A: What do you think about the new animated advertisement that the design team created for our online shopping app last week? B: I really like the main character, a cheerful delivery cat who brings packages to customers' doors, because it is cute and easy to remember, and many young shoppers have already shared the video on social media.","t":"A：你覺得設計團隊上週為我們的網購應用程式製作的新動畫廣告怎麼樣？ B：我很喜歡那個主要【角色】，一隻把包裹送到顧客家門口的開心送貨貓，因為牠很可愛又好記，許多年輕購物者已經在社群媒體上分享這支影片了。"},{"w":"cast","p":"n.","d":"all the actors in a film, play, or show","c":"全體演員；演員陣容","s":"A: How many people will be in the short film that the human resources department is making about workplace safety this spring? B: The whole cast includes eight employees from different departments, and they will practice their parts together every Wednesday afternoon in the meeting room until filming begins at the factory in April.","t":"A：人資部今年春天要拍的職場安全短片會有多少人參與演出？ B：【全體演員】包括來自不同部門的八名員工，他們每週三下午會在會議室一起排練各自的部分，直到四月在工廠開拍為止。"},{"w":"script","p":"n.","d":"the written words that actors say in a film, play, or ad","c":"劇本；腳本","s":"A: Have you finished writing the words for the product video, or do you still need more time to check the technical details with the engineers? B: I finished the script last night and emailed it to the engineers this morning, so once they confirm the information is correct, the actors can start learning their parts tomorrow.","t":"A：你寫完產品影片的台詞了嗎？還是你還需要更多時間跟工程師確認技術細節？ B：我昨晚完成了【劇本】，今天早上已經寄給工程師了，所以只要他們確認資訊正確，演員明天就能開始背自己的部分。"},{"w":"rehearse","p":"v.","d":"to practice a play, speech, or show before the real event","c":"排練；預演","s":"A: Why are the sales team members staying so late in the conference room every evening this week, even though their reports are already finished? B: They want to rehearse the short play they are presenting at the trade show on Saturday, because they will perform in front of hundreds of visitors and don't want to forget anything.","t":"A：為什麼業務團隊成員這週每天晚上都在會議室待到這麼晚，他們的報告不是已經完成了嗎？ B：他們想【排練】週六要在商展上演出的短劇，因為他們將在數百名參觀者面前表演，不想忘記任何東西。"},{"w":"dialogue","p":"n.","d":"the words that characters say to each other in a film or play","c":"對話；對白","s":"A: Why did the director stop filming the scene in the hotel lobby so many times this afternoon, and is there a problem with the actors? B: The dialogue between the receptionist and the guest sounded too formal and unnatural, so the writer is changing some of the words to make the conversation sound more like real people talking.","t":"A：為什麼導演今天下午在飯店大廳拍那場戲時喊停了那麼多次？演員有什麼問題嗎？ B：櫃台人員和客人之間的【對白】聽起來太正式、不自然，所以編劇正在修改一些用字，讓這段對話聽起來更像真人在交談。"},{"w":"monologue","p":"n.","d":"a long speech by one actor alone","c":"獨白","s":"A: What will the actor do at the start of our product launch event, before the CEO walks out to introduce the new smartphone? B: He will deliver a two-minute monologue alone on the stage about how much a phone changes our daily lives, and then the lights will go down and the CEO will appear.","t":"A：在執行長走出來介紹新智慧型手機之前，那位演員會在我們產品發表會一開始做什麼？ B：他會獨自在舞台上發表一段兩分鐘的【獨白】，講述手機如何改變我們的日常生活，然後燈光會暗下來，執行長就會登場。"},{"w":"stage","p":"n.","d":"the raised area in a theater or hall where people perform","c":"舞台","s":"A: Is the main hall ready for tomorrow's awards ceremony, or are the workers still setting up the lights and the sound system? B: The workers finished building the stage this afternoon, but they are still testing the microphones and the lights, so I think everything will be ready by about ten o'clock tonight.","t":"A：大廳已經準備好明天的頒獎典禮了嗎？還是工作人員還在架設燈光和音響系統？ B：工作人員今天下午已經搭好【舞台】，但他們還在測試麥克風和燈光，所以我想今晚十點左右一切都會準備就緒。"},{"w":"screen","p":"n.","d":"the surface where films or TV shows are seen; films and TV in general","c":"螢幕；銀幕","s":"A: Why did the company choose that young actor for our new coffee commercial when there are so many experienced people available? B: He looks very warm and friendly on screen, and when we tested his video with customers in three cities, most of them said they trusted him more than the other actors.","t":"A：為什麼公司選了那位年輕演員拍我們新的咖啡廣告，明明有那麼多有經驗的人可以選？ B：他在【螢幕】上看起來非常溫暖親切，而且我們在三個城市拿他的影片給顧客測試時，大多數人都說比起其他演員更信任他。"},{"w":"audition","p":"n.","d":"a short test where an actor shows if they are right for a part","c":"試鏡","s":"A: How did you choose the actors for the training videos, and how many people came to try out for the parts last weekend? B: We held an audition at our office on Saturday morning, and more than forty people came to read the script, so it took us the whole day to choose the final six actors.","t":"A：你們是怎麼挑選培訓影片的演員的？上週末有多少人來爭取角色？ B：我們週六早上在辦公室舉辦了一場【試鏡】，有四十多人來讀劇本，所以我們花了一整天才選出最後的六位演員。"},{"w":"director","p":"n.","d":"the person who tells the actors and crew what to do when making a film or play","c":"導演","s":"A: Who is in charge of telling the actors where to stand and how to say their words during the filming of our new advertisement? B: The director we hired from a film company will guide the actors and the camera crew, and she will also decide which scenes we keep after filming is finished next week.","t":"A：在拍攝我們的新廣告時，誰負責告訴演員站在哪裡以及如何說台詞？ B：我們從一家電影公司請來的【導演】會指導演員和攝影團隊，下週拍攝結束後，她也會決定保留哪些場景。"},{"w":"producer","p":"n.","d":"the person who controls the money and plans for a film, show, or play","c":"製作人","s":"A: Who is responsible for the budget of the company documentary, and who should I talk to if we need to rent more equipment? B: You should speak to the producer, because he controls the money, hires the staff, and makes sure the project finishes on time, so he will decide whether we can rent more equipment.","t":"A：誰負責公司紀錄片的預算？如果我們需要租更多設備，我應該找誰談？ B：你應該和【製作人】談，因為他掌控資金、聘請工作人員，並確保專案準時完成，所以要不要多租設備由他決定。"},{"w":"talent","p":"n.","d":"a natural ability to do something well","c":"天賦；才能","s":"A: Why did the manager ask Lisa from accounting to speak in the new recruiting video instead of hiring a professional actor? B: Lisa has a natural talent for speaking in front of a camera, and she is relaxed and friendly, so the manager believes job seekers will find her more honest than a paid actor.","t":"A：為什麼經理請會計部的Lisa在新的招募影片中說話，而不是聘請專業演員？ B：Lisa天生有面對鏡頭說話的【天賦】，而且她輕鬆又親切，所以經理認為求職者會覺得她比付費請來的演員更真誠。"},{"w":"expressive","p":"adj.","d":"showing feelings clearly, often with the face or voice","c":"富有表情的；善於表達的","s":"A: Why did the advertising agency choose that actor for our silent video, which has no words, only music and pictures? B: He has a very expressive face, so he can show surprise, joy, and worry clearly without saying anything, which is perfect for a video that will play on screens in busy train stations.","t":"A：為什麼廣告公司為我們那支沒有台詞、只有音樂和畫面的無聲影片挑選了那位演員？ B：他的臉非常【富有表情】，不用說話就能清楚地表現驚訝、喜悅和擔憂，非常適合在繁忙火車站的螢幕上播放的影片。"},{"w":"dramatic","p":"adj.","d":"exciting, sudden, or full of strong feeling","c":"戲劇性的；激動人心的","s":"A: How did the audience react at the end of the play that our company sponsored at the city theater last weekend? B: The ending was very dramatic, with loud music and the main character running into the rain, so many people in the audience stood up and clapped for several minutes after the lights came back on.","t":"A：我們公司上週末在市立劇院贊助的那齣戲，結尾時觀眾有什麼反應？ B：結局非常【戲劇性】，配上響亮的音樂和主角衝進雨中的畫面，所以燈光重新亮起後，許多觀眾起立鼓掌了好幾分鐘。"},{"w":"convincing","p":"adj.","d":"making people believe that something is true or real","c":"令人信服的；逼真的","s":"A: Did the customers believe the actor in our new advertisement was a real doctor, or did they think he was just reading a script? B: His acting was so convincing that many viewers called our office to ask which hospital he worked at, so we had to add a small note saying that he is an actor.","t":"A：顧客相信我們新廣告裡的演員是真正的醫生嗎？還是他們覺得他只是在念劇本？ B：他的演技非常【逼真】，許多觀眾打電話到我們辦公室詢問他在哪家醫院工作，所以我們只好加上一個小註記，說明他是演員。"},{"w":"versatile","p":"adj.","d":"able to do many different things well","c":"多才多藝的；多用途的","s":"A: Why do you want to hire the same actor for all three of our commercials, when each one is so different in style and mood? B: She is very versatile, so she can play a serious business owner in one commercial, a funny mother in another, and a sporty student in the third without any problem.","t":"A：我們的三支廣告風格和氛圍都很不一樣，為什麼你想讓同一位演員拍全部三支？ B：她非常【多才多藝】，所以她可以在一支廣告中飾演嚴肅的企業主，在另一支中飾演風趣的媽媽，在第三支中飾演愛運動的學生，完全沒問題。"},{"w":"famous","p":"adj.","d":"known by many people","c":"有名的；著名的","s":"A: Why are there so many reporters and photographers waiting outside the hotel entrance this morning, blocking the guests' cars? B: A famous movie star is staying here while she films a new action movie in the city, and the reporters are hoping to take her picture when she leaves for the studio.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上有那麼多記者和攝影師在飯店門口等候，還擋住了客人的車？ B：一位【有名的】電影明星在本市拍攝新動作片期間住在這裡，記者們希望在她出發去攝影棚時拍到她的照片。"},{"w":"celebrity","p":"n.","d":"a famous person, especially in entertainment","c":"名人","s":"A: How can we attract more visitors to the opening of our new shopping mall next month, since the advertising budget is limited? B: We could invite a local celebrity, such as a popular TV host or singer, to cut the ribbon, because fans will come to see them and then stay to shop in the stores.","t":"A：既然廣告預算有限，我們下個月新購物中心開幕時要怎麼吸引更多遊客？ B：我們可以邀請一位當地【名人】，例如受歡迎的電視主持人或歌手來剪綵，因為粉絲會來看他們，然後留下來在店裡購物。"},{"w":"spotlight","p":"n.","d":"a strong light on a performer; public attention","c":"聚光燈；眾人注目的焦點","s":"A: Why did the new manager look so nervous at the award ceremony, even though she won the prize for the best sales results? B: She is a quiet person who doesn't enjoy being in the spotlight, so standing on the stage in front of five hundred coworkers with everyone looking at her made her very uncomfortable.","t":"A：為什麼新經理在頒獎典禮上看起來那麼緊張，她明明拿到了最佳業績獎？ B：她是個安靜的人，不喜歡成為【眾人注目的焦點】，所以站在五百名同事面前的舞台上、被大家盯著看，讓她非常不自在。"},{"w":"emotion","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling, such as love, fear, or sadness","c":"情感；情緒","s":"A: Why did so many people at the charity event start crying while they were watching the short film about the children's hospital? B: The young actors showed real emotion when they played sick children waiting for help, and the story was so touching that the guests donated twice as much money as we expected.","t":"A：為什麼慈善活動上那麼多人在看那部關於兒童醫院的短片時哭了？ B：年輕演員們在飾演等待幫助的生病孩子時流露出真實的【情感】，故事非常感人，所以賓客捐出的錢是我們預期的兩倍。"},{"w":"improvise","p":"v.","d":"to act or speak without planning or practicing first","c":"即興表演；即興發揮","s":"A: What happened during the live product show yesterday when the projector suddenly stopped working in the middle of the presentation? B: The host had to improvise for about five minutes, so he told funny stories and asked the audience questions until the technicians fixed the problem, and nobody even noticed that anything was wrong.","t":"A：昨天的現場產品展示會上，投影機在簡報進行到一半時突然故障，發生了什麼事？ B：主持人只好【即興發揮】了大約五分鐘，他講了好笑的故事並向觀眾提問，直到技術人員解決問題，根本沒有人察覺出了狀況。"},{"w":"line","p":"n.","d":"words that an actor says in a play or film","c":"台詞","s":"A: Why did the filming of the bank commercial take so much longer than planned yesterday afternoon? B: The actor kept forgetting his last line, \"Your money is safe with us,\" because he was nervous, so the director had to film the same short scene about fifteen times before it was perfect.","t":"A：為什麼昨天下午銀行廣告的拍攝時間比計畫中長那麼多？ B：那位演員因為緊張，一直忘記他的最後一句【台詞】「您的錢交給我們很安全」，所以導演只好把同一個短場景拍了大約十五次才完美。"},{"w":"backstage","p":"adv.","d":"in the area behind the stage that the audience cannot see","c":"在後台","s":"A: Where should the speakers wait before they give their presentations at the conference, and can they bring their own laptops? B: They should wait backstage in the small room behind the main hall, where there are chairs, water, and power outlets, so they can check their slides on their laptops before they go on.","t":"A：講者在研討會上簡報之前應該在哪裡等候？他們可以帶自己的筆電嗎？ B：他們應該在【後台】、也就是大廳後方的小房間等候，那裡有椅子、水和電源插座，所以他們上台前可以先用筆電檢查投影片。"},{"w":"costume","p":"n.","d":"special clothes an actor wears to look like a character","c":"戲服；服裝","s":"A: Why is the marketing team spending so much money on clothes for the history video about our company's first factory? B: Each actor needs a costume that looks like the clothes workers wore in the 1960s, because the video should look real, and the old photos show exactly what everyone was wearing back then.","t":"A：為什麼行銷團隊為了那支關於我們公司第一間工廠的歷史影片，花那麼多錢在服裝上？ B：每位演員都需要一套看起來像1960年代工人穿著的【戲服】，因為影片要看起來真實，而舊照片清楚顯示了當時每個人穿的衣服。"},{"w":"makeup","p":"n.","d":"colors and creams put on the face to change how it looks","c":"化妝；彩妝","s":"A: Why do the managers have to arrive at the studio an hour before the filming of the company interview video starts? B: The makeup artist needs time to prepare their faces, because the bright studio lights can make people look pale or shiny on camera, and she wants everyone to look healthy and natural.","t":"A：為什麼經理們必須在公司訪談影片開拍前一小時抵達攝影棚？ B：【化妝】師需要時間幫他們的臉做準備，因為攝影棚明亮的燈光會讓人在鏡頭前看起來蒼白或油亮，她希望每個人看起來都健康自然。"},{"w":"scene","p":"n.","d":"one part of a film or play that happens in one place","c":"場景；一場戲","s":"A: Which part of the new commercial do you think the customers will remember most after they see it on television? B: I think they will remember the final scene, where the whole family sits around the table and shares our frozen dumplings, because it is warm, simple, and shows the product clearly.","t":"A：你覺得顧客在電視上看到新廣告後，會對哪個部分印象最深？ B：我想他們會記得最後一【場戲】，全家人圍坐在餐桌旁分享我們的冷凍水餃，因為那一幕溫馨、簡單，又能清楚呈現產品。"},{"w":"lead","p":"n.","d":"the main part in a play or film, or the actor who plays it","c":"主角","s":"A: Who is going to play the main part in the musical that our company is sponsoring at the arts festival this summer? B: A young singer from Kaohsiung got the lead after a long competition with many other performers, and the director says her strong voice will help the show sell lots of tickets.","t":"A：誰要在我們公司今年夏天於藝術節贊助的音樂劇中擔任主要角色？ B：一位來自高雄的年輕歌手在和許多其他表演者激烈競爭後拿到了【主角】，導演說她渾厚的嗓音將幫助這齣戲賣出很多票。"},{"w":"supporting","p":"adj.","d":"(of an actor or part) less important than the main part","c":"配角的；輔助的","s":"A: Did the actor from our company's training video win any prizes at the short film festival last month? B: Yes, he won the award for best supporting actor, because even though he only appeared in a few scenes as the helpful coworker, his acting made the whole story feel more real.","t":"A：我們公司培訓影片中的那位演員，上個月在短片影展有得到任何獎項嗎？ B：有，他獲得了最佳【男配角】獎，因為雖然他只在幾場戲中飾演樂於助人的同事，但他的演技讓整個故事感覺更真實。"},{"w":"career","p":"n.","d":"the job or series of jobs a person does for a long time","c":"職業生涯；事業","s":"A: Why did the well-known TV actor agree to teach a public speaking workshop for our sales staff next month? B: He started his career as a salesperson before he became an actor, so he understands how hard it is to talk to customers, and he wants to share his speaking skills with young employees.","t":"A：為什麼那位知名電視演員同意下個月為我們的業務人員教授公眾演說工作坊？ B：他在成為演員之前，是以業務員開始他的【職業生涯】的，所以他了解和顧客交談有多難，也想和年輕員工分享他的說話技巧。"},{"w":"applause","p":"n.","d":"the sound of people clapping their hands to show they liked something","c":"掌聲","s":"A: How did the employees respond when the CEO announced the year-end bonuses at the end of the company party last night? B: There was loud applause that lasted for almost a minute, and some people even stood on their chairs and cheered, because the bonuses were much bigger than everyone had expected this year.","t":"A：昨晚公司派對結束時執行長宣布年終獎金，員工們有什麼反應？ B：現場響起了幾乎持續一分鐘的熱烈【掌聲】，有些人甚至站到椅子上歡呼，因為今年的獎金比大家預期的多很多。"}]},{"unit":6,"theme":"Ad 廣告","cards":[{"w":"advertise","p":"v.","d":"to tell people about a product, service, or job in public so they will want it","c":"做廣告；刊登廣告","s":"A: Our new bakery opened last week, but very few customers have come in, so what do you think we should do to bring in more people from the neighborhood? B: I think we should advertise on the local radio station and in the community newspaper, because many older residents still listen and read them every morning before work.","t":"A：我們的新麵包店上週開幕了，但很少有客人上門，你覺得我們該怎麼做才能吸引更多附近的居民？ B：我認為我們應該在地方廣播電台和社區報紙上【刊登廣告】，因為許多年長的居民每天早上上班前仍然會收聽和閱讀它們。"},{"w":"advertising","p":"n.","d":"the business or activity of making and showing ads","c":"廣告業；廣告活動","s":"A: Why did the marketing director ask for a much larger budget at yesterday's meeting with the finance team? B: She explained that our competitors spend twice as much on advertising as we do, and if we don't increase our spending on television and online ads, we will lose customers to them this year.","t":"A：為什麼行銷總監在昨天和財務團隊的會議上要求大幅增加預算？ B：她解釋說，我們的競爭對手在【廣告】上的花費是我們的兩倍，如果我們不增加電視和網路廣告的支出，今年就會把客戶輸給他們。"},{"w":"promotion","p":"n.","d":"an activity, such as a special price, that helps sell a product","c":"促銷；宣傳活動","s":"A: Have you seen all the customers waiting outside the electronics store this morning, even before the doors opened? B: Yes, the store is running a special promotion this weekend, so anyone who buys a new laptop gets a free printer and a two-year warranty, and many people want to take advantage of it.","t":"A：你有看到今天早上電子產品店外面等候的那些客人嗎？甚至在開門之前就在排了。 B：有啊，這家店這個週末在舉辦特別【促銷活動】，任何購買新筆電的人都能獲得一台免費印表機和兩年保固，所以很多人想好好把握。"},{"w":"promote","p":"v.","d":"to help sell something by telling people about it","c":"推廣；促銷；宣傳","s":"A: The company is launching a new line of healthy snacks next month, so how are we going to tell people about them? B: We plan to promote the snacks at gyms and sports events, where we will hand out free samples and discount coupons to customers who care about eating well.","t":"A：公司下個月要推出新的健康零食系列，我們要怎麼讓大家知道呢？ B：我們打算在健身房和運動賽事上【推廣】這些零食，在那裡發送免費試吃品和折價券給重視飲食健康的顧客。"},{"w":"campaign","p":"n.","d":"a planned series of activities to sell a product or reach a goal","c":"（廣告）宣傳活動","s":"A: Why is everyone in the marketing department staying late at the office every evening this week? B: They are preparing a big campaign for our new phone, which includes TV ads, posters in train stations, and online videos, and everything has to be ready before the product goes on sale next Monday.","t":"A：為什麼行銷部的每個人這週每天晚上都在辦公室待到很晚？ B：他們正在為我們的新手機準備一個大型【宣傳活動】，包括電視廣告、火車站的海報和網路影片，而且一切都必須在產品下週一開賣前準備好。"},{"w":"brand","p":"n.","d":"the name of a product made by a particular company","c":"品牌；商標","s":"A: Why do so many shoppers pay more for this coffee when the supermarket's own coffee looks almost the same? B: Most people trust this brand because it has been popular for over fifty years, and they believe the quality is always good, so they are happy to spend a little extra money for it.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多購物者願意花更多錢買這款咖啡，而超市自有的咖啡看起來幾乎一樣？ B：大多數人信任這個【品牌】，因為它已經流行了五十多年，而且他們相信品質一直都很好，所以他們很樂意為它多花一點錢。"},{"w":"branding","p":"n.","d":"the design, name, and image a company uses so people recognize it","c":"品牌形象；品牌塑造","s":"A: Our small tea shop has good products, so why did the owner hire a design company to change our logo and cups? B: She thinks our branding looks old-fashioned, and a fresh logo, modern colors, and matching packaging will help young customers remember us and recognize our shop from across the street.","t":"A：我們的小茶店產品很好，為什麼老闆要請設計公司更換我們的標誌和杯子？ B：她認為我們的【品牌形象】看起來很過時，而新的標誌、現代的顏色和搭配的包裝能幫助年輕顧客記住我們，並且從對街就認出我們的店。"},{"w":"commercial","p":"n.","d":"an ad on television or radio","c":"（電視或廣播）廣告","s":"A: How did you first hear about the new sports drink that everyone in the office is talking about? B: I saw a funny thirty-second commercial on TV during the basketball game last night, and it showed famous players drinking it after a hard practice, so I bought a bottle on my way to work.","t":"A：你最初是怎麼聽說辦公室裡大家都在談論的那款新運動飲料的？ B：我昨晚看籃球比賽時在電視上看到一支有趣的三十秒【廣告】，畫面中知名球員在辛苦練習後喝它，所以我在上班途中買了一瓶。"},{"w":"slogan","p":"n.","d":"a short, easy-to-remember phrase used in ads","c":"標語；口號","s":"A: The design team has finished the new poster for our airline, but do you think the words at the bottom are good enough? B: I think the slogan is too long, because customers only look at a poster for a few seconds, so we need a short and simple phrase that people can remember easily.","t":"A：設計團隊已經完成了我們航空公司的新海報，但你覺得底部的文字夠好嗎？ B：我認為那句【標語】太長了，因為顧客只會看海報幾秒鐘，所以我們需要一句簡短又容易讓人記住的話。"},{"w":"headline","p":"n.","d":"the title in large letters at the top of an article or ad","c":"標題；大標","s":"A: Why did the editor ask us to rewrite the top of the advertisement for the newspaper before it goes to print tomorrow? B: She said the headline was not exciting enough, and since most readers only see the large words at the top of the page, they must be strong enough to make people stop and read more.","t":"A：為什麼編輯要求我們在明天付印前重寫報紙廣告的頂端部分？ B：她說那個【標題】不夠吸引人，而因為大部分讀者只會看到頁面頂端的大字，所以它們必須夠有力，才能讓人停下來繼續閱讀。"},{"w":"copy","p":"n.","d":"the written words used in an ad","c":"廣告文案；廣告文字","s":"A: The pictures for our new hotel brochure look beautiful, but who is going to write the text that goes next to them? B: We hired a freelance writer to prepare the copy, and she will describe the rooms, the pool, and the restaurant in a friendly way that makes families want to book a holiday with us.","t":"A：我們新飯店手冊的照片看起來很漂亮，但誰要撰寫旁邊的文字呢？ B：我們聘請了一位自由撰稿人來準備【廣告文案】，她會以親切的方式描述客房、游泳池和餐廳，讓家庭想要向我們預訂假期。"},{"w":"target","p":"v.","d":"to aim a product or ad at a particular group of people","c":"以…為目標；鎖定","s":"A: Our new video game is selling well in Japan, but why are sales so low in Europe and North America? B: The marketing team decided to target teenagers in those regions with ads on social media apps, but most of our real players are adults in their thirties who rarely use those apps at all.","t":"A：我們的新電玩遊戲在日本賣得很好，但為什麼在歐洲和北美的銷量這麼低？ B：行銷團隊決定在那些地區透過社群媒體應用程式的廣告來【鎖定】青少年，但我們真正的玩家大多是三十多歲的成年人，他們很少使用那些應用程式。"},{"w":"audience","p":"n.","d":"the people who watch, read, or listen to something","c":"觀眾；聽眾；受眾","s":"A: Should we show our new advertisement during the late-night news or during the morning cartoons on Saturday? B: Since our product is a toy for young children, the morning time is better, because the audience at that hour is mostly kids and their parents, who are exactly the people we want to sell to.","t":"A：我們應該在深夜新聞時段還是週六早上的卡通時段播放我們的新廣告？ B：既然我們的產品是給幼童的玩具，早上的時段比較好，因為那個時間的【觀眾】大多是孩子和他們的父母，正是我們想要銷售的對象。"},{"w":"reach","p":"v.","d":"to be seen or heard by a group of people","c":"觸及；接觸到（受眾）","s":"A: Why did the company decide to put its ads on a popular music app instead of in printed magazines this year? B: The manager believes we can reach millions of young listeners every day through the app, while magazine sales have fallen a lot, so fewer people would see our ads in print.","t":"A：為什麼公司今年決定把廣告放在熱門音樂應用程式上，而不是印刷雜誌上？ B：經理相信透過這個應用程式，我們每天可以【觸及】數百萬年輕聽眾，而雜誌銷量已經大幅下滑，所以在紙本上看到我們廣告的人會比較少。"},{"w":"impression","p":"n.","d":"one time that an online ad is shown to a person","c":"（廣告）曝光次數；印象","s":"A: The report says our online banner ad was shown two million times last month, but why are the managers still unhappy? B: Each impression only means the ad appeared on someone's screen, so although the number looks big, very few people actually opened it or bought anything from our website.","t":"A：報告說我們的網路橫幅廣告上個月被顯示了兩百萬次，但為什麼經理們還是不滿意？ B：每一次【曝光】只代表廣告出現在某人的螢幕上，所以雖然數字看起來很大，但實際上打開它或在我們網站上購買東西的人非常少。"},{"w":"engagement","p":"n.","d":"how much people react to and take part in content, such as liking or sharing","c":"互動；參與度","s":"A: Our posts on social media get thousands of views, so why does the marketing manager want to change our strategy? B: She is worried about low engagement, because people see the posts but rarely like, share, or comment on them, which means they are not really interested in our products or our company.","t":"A：我們在社群媒體上的貼文有數千次瀏覽，為什麼行銷經理想要改變我們的策略？ B：她擔心【互動】程度偏低，因為人們看到貼文，卻很少按讚、分享或留言，這表示他們對我們的產品或公司並不是真的感興趣。"},{"w":"click","p":"n.","d":"the act of pressing a mouse button or tapping a link on a screen","c":"點擊","s":"A: How do we know whether people are interested in the new online ad for our cooking classes? B: Every click on the ad takes a visitor to our sign-up page, so the system counts how many people want more information, and so far more than five hundred people have visited the page this week.","t":"A：我們怎麼知道大家是否對我們烹飪課的新網路廣告感興趣？ B：廣告上的每一次【點擊】都會把訪客帶到我們的報名頁面，所以系統會計算有多少人想要更多資訊，到目前為止，這週已經有超過五百人造訪了該頁面。"},{"w":"conversion","p":"n.","d":"the act of a visitor or viewer becoming a paying customer","c":"轉換（指訪客變成顧客）","s":"A: Thousands of people visited our online shoe store after the holiday ads started, so why are sales still disappointing? B: Our conversion rate is very low, which means most visitors look at the shoes but leave without buying, so we need to make the checkout page faster and offer free delivery to change their minds.","t":"A：假期廣告開始後，有數千人造訪我們的網路鞋店，為什麼銷量還是令人失望？ B：我們的【轉換】率非常低，這表示大部分訪客看了鞋子卻沒買就離開了，所以我們需要讓結帳頁面更快，並提供免運來改變他們的想法。"},{"w":"endorsement","p":"n.","d":"public support for a product by a famous person, often for money","c":"代言；背書","s":"A: Sales of our running shoes doubled in only two months, so what was the main reason for this sudden success? B: We got an endorsement from a famous Olympic runner, and after she said in interviews that she wears our shoes every day, many sports fans started trusting our products and buying them.","t":"A：我們的跑鞋銷量在短短兩個月內翻倍，這突然成功的主要原因是什麼？ B：我們獲得了一位知名奧運跑者的【代言】，在她於訪談中說她每天都穿我們的鞋之後，許多運動迷開始信任並購買我們的產品。"},{"w":"testimonial","p":"n.","d":"a statement from a customer saying a product or service is good","c":"推薦；（顧客）見證","s":"A: Our website explains all the features of the language software, but how can we make new visitors trust us more? B: We could add a testimonial from a happy customer, such as a nurse who passed her English test after using our program for three months, because people believe real users more than companies.","t":"A：我們的網站說明了這款語言軟體的所有功能，但我們要怎麼讓新訪客更信任我們？ B：我們可以加入一位滿意顧客的【推薦見證】，例如一位使用我們的程式三個月後就通過英文考試的護理師，因為人們比較相信真正的使用者，而不是公司。"},{"w":"influencer","p":"n.","d":"a person who affects what others buy, often through social media","c":"網紅；有影響力的人","s":"A: Why is our cosmetics company paying a young woman to post videos about our new lipstick on her social media account? B: She is a popular influencer with over a million followers, and when she shows a product in her videos, many of her fans go online and buy it within a few days.","t":"A：為什麼我們的化妝品公司要付錢給一位年輕女性，請她在社群媒體帳號上發布關於我們新口紅的影片？ B：她是一位擁有超過一百萬名追蹤者的熱門【網紅】，當她在影片中展示一項產品時，她的許多粉絲會在幾天內上網購買。"},{"w":"placement","p":"n.","d":"the position where a product or ad is put so people will see it","c":"（商品或廣告的）擺放位置；置入","s":"A: The supermarket has agreed to sell our new cereal, but why are we paying an extra fee to the store? B: The fee is for better placement, so our boxes will sit at eye level near the entrance instead of on the bottom shelf, where busy shoppers might walk past without noticing them.","t":"A：超市已經同意販售我們的新穀片，但為什麼我們還要付額外的費用給店家？ B：那筆費用是為了取得更好的【陳列位置】，這樣我們的盒子就會擺在入口附近、與視線同高的地方，而不是在最底層的架子上，因為忙碌的購物者可能會走過去而沒注意到。"},{"w":"display","p":"n.","d":"an arrangement of products for people to look at in a store","c":"陳列；展示","s":"A: The new perfume arrives at our department store on Friday, so how should we show it to customers in the busy holiday season? B: Let's set up a large display near the main entrance with bright lights, flowers, and free samples, so everyone who walks into the store will notice the perfume right away.","t":"A：新香水週五會到我們百貨公司，在繁忙的假期季節中，我們該如何展示給顧客看？ B：我們在主要入口附近布置一個大型【展示區】，搭配明亮的燈光、花卉和免費試用品，讓每個走進店裡的人都能馬上注意到這款香水。"},{"w":"broadcast","p":"v.","d":"to send out a program or ad on TV or radio","c":"播放；廣播","s":"A: Our company paid a lot of money for a two-minute ad, so when will people actually be able to watch it on television? B: The TV station will broadcast it during the final match of the football championship next Sunday evening, when millions of fans across the country will be sitting in front of their screens.","t":"A：我們公司為一支兩分鐘的廣告付了很多錢，那麼大家到底什麼時候能在電視上看到它？ B：電視台將在下週日晚上的足球錦標賽決賽期間【播放】它，屆時全國數百萬名球迷都會坐在螢幕前。"},{"w":"sponsor","p":"v.","d":"to pay for an event or team in return for advertising","c":"贊助","s":"A: Why does our bank's logo appear on the shirts of the local basketball team this season? B: Our bank decided to sponsor the team, which means we pay for their uniforms and travel costs, and in return our name is shown at every game, so thousands of local families see it each week.","t":"A：為什麼這一季我們銀行的標誌出現在本地籃球隊的球衣上？ B：我們銀行決定【贊助】這支球隊，也就是說我們支付他們的制服和交通費用，作為回報，我們的名字會在每場比賽中出現，所以每週都有數千個本地家庭看到它。"},{"w":"persuasive","p":"adj.","d":"able to make people believe or do something","c":"有說服力的","s":"A: Your sales presentation to the hotel group went very well, so how did you convince them to sign a three-year contract? B: I think my argument was persuasive because I showed them clear numbers proving that our cleaning service saves money, and I also shared positive comments from other hotels we work with.","t":"A：你對飯店集團的銷售簡報非常成功，你是怎麼說服他們簽下三年合約的？ B：我想我的論點很有【說服力】，因為我向他們展示了明確的數據，證明我們的清潔服務能省錢，而且我也分享了其他合作飯店的正面評價。"},{"w":"promotional","p":"adj.","d":"used to advertise a product or company","c":"促銷的；宣傳的","s":"A: We have a lot of extra pens, bags, and T-shirts with our company logo, so what should we do with them? B: Let's give them away at the trade fair next month as promotional gifts, because visitors love free items, and every time they use them, they will be reminded of our company and our services.","t":"A：我們有很多印有公司標誌的多餘筆、袋子和T恤，該怎麼處理它們？ B：我們下個月在商展上把它們當作【宣傳】贈品送出去吧，因為參觀者喜歡免費物品，而且每次使用時，都會讓他們想起我們公司和我們的服務。"},{"w":"viral","p":"adj.","d":"spreading very quickly to many people on the internet","c":"（網路上）迅速傳播的；爆紅的","s":"A: I heard that our small restaurant suddenly became busy last week, so what happened to bring in all those new customers? B: A customer filmed our chef making noodles by hand and posted it online, and the video went viral, so millions of people watched it in just three days and many came to try our food.","t":"A：我聽說我們的小餐廳上週突然變得很忙，到底發生什麼事，帶來了這麼多新客人？ B：一位顧客拍下我們的主廚手工製作麵條的影片並上傳到網路上，結果那支影片【爆紅】，短短三天內就有數百萬人觀看，很多人都來品嚐我們的食物。"},{"w":"catchy","p":"adj.","d":"easy to remember and pleasant to hear","c":"易記的；朗朗上口的","s":"A: Why do so many people in the office keep singing the same little song while they work this week? B: It's from the new ice cream ad on the radio, and the music is so catchy that once you hear it, you cannot stop humming it all day, which is exactly what the company wanted.","t":"A：為什麼這週辦公室裡這麼多人一邊工作一邊哼著同一首小歌？ B：那是電台新冰淇淋廣告裡的歌，旋律非常【朗朗上口】，你一聽到就會一整天停不下來地哼，這正是那家公司想要的效果。"},{"w":"compelling","p":"adj.","d":"so interesting or strong that you pay attention or are convinced","c":"引人入勝的；令人信服的","s":"A: Many companies made short films for the charity competition, so why did the judges choose our video as the winner? B: They said our story about the old fisherman and his daughter was very compelling, and it made viewers feel strong emotions, so they wanted to keep watching until the very end.","t":"A：很多公司都為慈善比賽拍攝了短片，為什麼評審選擇我們的影片為冠軍？ B：他們說我們關於老漁夫和他女兒的故事非常【引人入勝】，讓觀眾產生強烈的情感，所以他們想一直看到最後。"},{"w":"strategically","p":"adv.","d":"in a carefully planned way to reach a goal","c":"策略性地；戰略上","s":"A: Why did the coffee chain open its new branches next to train stations and large office buildings instead of in quiet neighborhoods? B: The company placed them strategically, because thousands of busy workers pass those places every morning, and many of them want a quick cup of coffee on their way to work.","t":"A：為什麼那家咖啡連鎖店把新分店開在火車站和大型辦公大樓旁邊，而不是安靜的住宅區？ B：公司是【策略性地】安排它們的位置，因為每天早上都有數千名忙碌的上班族經過那些地方，其中很多人在上班途中想要一杯快速取得的咖啡。"},{"w":"creatively","p":"adv.","d":"in a new and imaginative way","c":"有創意地；創造性地","s":"A: Our marketing budget is very small this year, so how can we compete with the big companies that spend millions on TV? B: We have to think creatively, for example by making funny short videos with our own staff, running online contests, and working with local shops to share customers at no extra cost.","t":"A：我們今年的行銷預算很少，要怎麼和那些在電視上花數百萬的大公司競爭？ B：我們必須【有創意地】思考，例如用自己的員工拍攝有趣的短片、舉辦網路競賽，並和本地商店合作互相分享顧客，而且不需額外費用。"}]},{"unit":7,"theme":"Adventure 冒險","cards":[{"w":"explore","p":"v.","d":"to travel around a place to learn about it","c":"探索；探險；考察","s":"A: We have a free afternoon after the sales conference in Lisbon, so what would you like to do before our flight leaves tomorrow morning? B: I'd love to explore the old part of the city on foot, because the hotel receptionist said there are small cafés, markets, and museums hidden in every narrow street.","t":"A：我們在里斯本的業務研討會結束後有一個空閒的下午，所以在明天早上班機起飛前你想做什麼？ B：我很想步行【探索】這座城市的舊城區，因為飯店櫃檯人員說每條窄巷裡都藏著小咖啡館、市場和博物館。"},{"w":"exploration","p":"n.","d":"the act of traveling through a place to find out about it","c":"探索；探勘；考察","s":"A: Why did the travel company decide to add a new tour to its catalog this year, even though most of its customers prefer beach holidays? B: More young professionals are asking for trips that include exploration of caves and mountain villages, so the managers believe this kind of tour will sell well next summer.","t":"A：為什麼這家旅行社今年決定在型錄裡增加新的行程，雖然大部分客人比較喜歡海灘度假？ B：越來越多年輕上班族要求包含洞穴和山村【探索】的旅程，所以經理們相信這類行程明年夏天會賣得很好。"},{"w":"journey","p":"n.","d":"a trip from one place to another, often a long one","c":"旅程；旅行","s":"A: How was your trip to the factory in the north last week, and did you manage to finish the safety inspection before the weekend? B: The journey took nearly nine hours by train and bus because of heavy snow, but I arrived in time and finished the inspection on Friday afternoon.","t":"A：你上週去北部工廠的行程怎麼樣，有在週末前完成安全檢查嗎？ B：因為大雪，這趟【旅程】搭火車和巴士花了將近九個小時，不過我及時抵達，並在週五下午完成了檢查。"},{"w":"expedition","p":"n.","d":"an organized trip made for a special purpose, such as science or exploring","c":"遠征；探險；考察旅行","s":"A: I heard our outdoor equipment company is sponsoring a group of climbers this spring, so where exactly are they planning to go? B: They are joining an expedition to the Himalayas for six weeks, and they will test our new tents and jackets in very cold and windy conditions.","t":"A：我聽說我們戶外用品公司今年春天要贊助一群登山客，他們究竟打算去哪裡？ B：他們要參加為期六週的喜馬拉雅山【遠征】，並會在非常寒冷且強風的環境中測試我們的新帳篷和外套。"},{"w":"quest","p":"n.","d":"a long search for something important or difficult to find","c":"追求；探索；尋找","s":"A: Why has the hotel group sent its chef to visit small farms in three different countries during the past two months? B: The chef is on a quest for the freshest local ingredients, because the company wants every restaurant menu to feature special dishes that guests cannot find anywhere else.","t":"A：為什麼這家飯店集團在過去兩個月內派主廚去拜訪三個不同國家的小農場？ B：主廚正在【尋找】最新鮮的在地食材，因為公司希望每間餐廳的菜單都能推出客人在其他地方吃不到的特色料理。"},{"w":"venture","p":"n.","d":"a new business or activity that involves some risk","c":"（有風險的）事業；冒險","s":"A: Is it true that Mr. Tanaka is leaving the bank next month after working there for more than fifteen years? B: Yes, he and his sister are starting a new business venture together, a small travel agency that plans hiking and camping trips for families who live in big cities.","t":"A：田中先生在銀行工作了十五年以上，下個月要離職是真的嗎？ B：是的，他和他姊姊要一起展開一項新的商業【冒險事業】，開一間小型旅行社，為住在大城市的家庭規劃健行和露營旅程。"},{"w":"discovery","p":"n.","d":"the act of finding something that was not known before","c":"發現；發現的事物","s":"A: Why are so many reporters waiting outside the museum this morning, and why has the director canceled all of her afternoon meetings? B: A team of researchers made an exciting discovery of ancient coins near the river last week, and the director will present them to the public at noon today.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上有這麼多記者在博物館外面等候，館長又為什麼取消了她下午所有的會議？ B：一組研究人員上週在河邊有了令人振奮的古錢幣【發現】，館長今天中午將向大眾展示這些錢幣。"},{"w":"trail","p":"n.","d":"a path through the countryside, forest, or mountains","c":"小徑；步道","s":"A: Our team-building weekend is next month, so do you know a good place where twenty employees can walk together safely? B: The national park has a wide forest trail that takes about three hours to complete, and there are rest areas, clean toilets, and a small café near the end.","t":"A：我們的團隊建立週末活動在下個月，你知道哪裡有適合二十名員工安全地一起健行的好地方嗎？ B：國家公園有一條寬敞的森林【步道】，大約三個小時可以走完，沿途有休息區、乾淨的廁所，終點附近還有一間小咖啡館。"},{"w":"voyage","p":"n.","d":"a long trip, especially by sea or in space","c":"航行；航程","s":"A: Why did the cruise company hire so many extra kitchen staff and entertainers for the trip that starts next Monday? B: It is a three-week voyage across the Pacific Ocean with more than two thousand passengers, so the ship needs extra workers to prepare meals and keep guests busy every evening.","t":"A：為什麼郵輪公司為下週一出發的旅程額外雇用了這麼多廚房人員和表演者？ B：那是一趟橫越太平洋、為期三週的【航行】，船上有兩千多名乘客，所以需要更多員工來準備餐點，並讓客人每晚都有活動可以參加。"},{"w":"escape","p":"n.","d":"a way of forgetting about daily problems or a stressful situation for a short time","c":"逃離；逃避；解脫","s":"A: You always look so relaxed when you come back to the office on Monday, so what do you usually do on weekends? B: My husband and I drive to a quiet cabin in the mountains, and it is the perfect escape from the noise of the city and the pressure of our busy jobs.","t":"A：你每週一回到辦公室時看起來總是很放鬆，你週末通常都做些什麼？ B：我和我先生會開車到山上一間安靜的小木屋，那是【逃離】城市喧囂和繁忙工作壓力的完美去處。"},{"w":"risk","p":"n.","d":"the possibility that something bad or dangerous may happen","c":"風險；危險","s":"A: Should we let our guests go kayaking on the lake tomorrow afternoon if the weather report says there might be strong winds? B: I don't think so, because there is a serious risk that the boats could turn over, and our insurance does not cover water activities in bad weather.","t":"A：如果氣象預報說明天下午可能有強風，我們還應該讓客人去湖上划獨木舟嗎？ B：我認為不應該，因為船有翻覆的嚴重【風險】，而且我們的保險不涵蓋惡劣天氣下的水上活動。"},{"w":"challenge","p":"n.","d":"something new and difficult that tests your skill or ability","c":"挑戰；難題","s":"A: Why did you accept the job in Singapore when you already had a good position and a comfortable life here in Taipei? B: I wanted a new challenge, and managing a team of people from five different countries will help me improve my leadership and communication skills much faster.","t":"A：你在台北已經有不錯的職位和舒適的生活，為什麼還接受新加坡的工作？ B：我想要一個新的【挑戰】，管理來自五個不同國家的團隊會幫助我更快提升領導和溝通能力。"},{"w":"thrill","p":"n.","d":"a sudden strong feeling of excitement and pleasure","c":"興奮；激動；刺激","s":"A: Why do you think the zip-line tour is the most popular activity at the resort, even though the ticket is quite expensive? B: Most guests love the thrill of flying over the jungle at high speed, and they also enjoy the beautiful view of the waterfalls and the ocean from above.","t":"A：雖然票價相當貴，你為什麼認為高空滑索行程是度假村最受歡迎的活動？ B：大部分客人都喜歡在叢林上空高速飛越的【刺激】感，也很享受從上方看到瀑布和海洋的美麗景色。"},{"w":"excitement","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of being very happy and eager about something","c":"興奮；激動","s":"A: Why is everyone in the marketing department talking so loudly and smiling so much this morning? B: There is a lot of excitement because the manager just told us that our team won the annual sales award, and the prize is a four-day trip to Bali for everyone in the department.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上行銷部的每個人都說話這麼大聲、笑得這麼開心？ B：大家都很【興奮】，因為經理剛告訴我們，我們團隊贏得了年度業績獎，獎品是全部門同仁四天的峇里島之旅。"},{"w":"wilderness","p":"n.","d":"a large natural area where nobody lives and nature has not been changed","c":"荒野；未開發地區","s":"A: Should I bring my laptop and phone charger on the company's survival training trip next week? B: You can bring them, but they won't be very useful, because we will spend three days in the wilderness, far from any towns, roads, or electricity, and there is no phone signal there.","t":"A：下週公司的野外求生訓練之旅，我應該帶筆電和手機充電器嗎？ B：你可以帶，但用處不大，因為我們會在【荒野】中待三天，遠離任何城鎮、道路和電力，那裡也沒有手機訊號。"},{"w":"survival","p":"n.","d":"the state of continuing to live or exist, especially after danger or difficulty","c":"生存；存活","s":"A: Why did the hiking club ask every new member to attend a two-day training course before joining the mountain trips? B: The course teaches basic survival skills, such as how to find clean water, build a simple shelter, and stay warm if someone gets lost in bad weather.","t":"A：為什麼登山社要求每位新成員在參加登山活動前，先上兩天的訓練課程？ B：這門課教基本的【求生】技巧，例如如何找到乾淨的水、搭建簡單的避難所，以及有人在惡劣天氣中迷路時如何保暖。"},{"w":"brave","p":"adj.","d":"willing to do things that are dangerous or difficult without showing fear","c":"勇敢的","s":"A: Did you hear what happened at the hotel pool yesterday afternoon when a small child fell into the deep water? B: Yes, a brave young lifeguard jumped in immediately and pulled the child out, and the hotel manager has decided to give him a special award at next week's staff meeting.","t":"A：你有聽說昨天下午飯店泳池發生的事嗎？有個小孩掉進了深水區。 B：有，一位【勇敢的】年輕救生員立刻跳下水把孩子救上來，飯店經理決定在下週的員工會議上頒給他特別獎。"},{"w":"daring","p":"adj.","d":"brave enough to do something dangerous, new, or unusual","c":"大膽的；勇於冒險的","s":"A: What did the investors think about the plan to open our first restaurant on a boat that travels along the river every evening? B: They said it was a daring idea that nobody in the city had tried before, but they agreed to fund it because tourists would probably love the experience.","t":"A：投資人對於我們把第一間餐廳開在每晚沿河航行的船上這個計畫有什麼看法？ B：他們說這是一個城裡從未有人嘗試過的【大膽的】構想，但他們同意出資，因為觀光客很可能會喜愛這種體驗。"},{"w":"fearless","p":"adj.","d":"not afraid of anything","c":"無畏的；大無畏的","s":"A: Who do you think should guide the group of guests on the rock-climbing tour this Saturday morning? B: Maria would be perfect, because she is fearless on steep cliffs, she has ten years of experience, and she always explains the safety rules clearly so that nervous beginners feel calm.","t":"A：你認為這週六早上應該由誰帶領客人參加攀岩行程？ B：瑪麗亞再適合不過了，因為她在陡峭的懸崖上【毫無畏懼】，有十年的經驗，而且總是把安全規則解釋得很清楚，讓緊張的初學者感到安心。"},{"w":"wild","p":"adj.","d":"living or growing in nature, not kept or controlled by people","c":"野生的；未經馴化的","s":"A: Is it safe for our tour group to leave food outside the tents at the campsite tonight after dinner? B: No, the park ranger warned us that wild animals such as bears and foxes often come close to the camp at night, so we must lock all the food in the cars.","t":"A：今晚晚餐後，我們旅行團把食物留在營地帳篷外面安全嗎？ B：不安全，公園管理員警告我們，熊和狐狸等【野生】動物晚上常會靠近營地，所以我們必須把所有食物鎖在車裡。"},{"w":"remote","p":"adj.","d":"far away from towns, cities, and other people","c":"偏遠的；遙遠的","s":"A: Why does it take so long to deliver our products to the new customer in the mountains, even when we use express shipping? B: The village is in a very remote area with only one narrow road, so the delivery trucks can go there just twice a week when the weather is good.","t":"A：為什麼即使用快遞，把產品送到山區的新客戶那裡還是要花這麼久？ B：那個村莊位於非常【偏遠的】地區，只有一條狹窄的道路，所以貨車只有在天氣好的時候，每週才能去兩次。"},{"w":"unpredictable","p":"adj.","d":"changing so often that you cannot know what will happen","c":"無法預測的；難以預料的","s":"A: Should we hold the company picnic by the sea in early October, or is it better to plan an indoor event this year? B: I prefer an indoor event, because the weather near the coast is very unpredictable in autumn, and a sudden storm could ruin all the food and games we prepare.","t":"A：我們應該在十月初到海邊辦公司野餐，還是今年最好規劃室內活動？ B：我比較喜歡室內活動，因為秋天海岸附近的天氣非常【難以預測】，一場突來的暴風雨可能會毀了我們準備的所有食物和遊戲。"},{"w":"dangerous","p":"adj.","d":"able to hurt or harm people","c":"危險的","s":"A: Why did the tour company cancel the boat trip to the small island this afternoon, even though most passengers had already paid? B: The captain said the waves were too high and it was dangerous to sail, so the company is offering everyone a full refund or a free ticket for another day.","t":"A：為什麼旅行社今天下午取消了去小島的船程，即使大部分乘客都已經付款了？ B：船長說浪太高，出航很【危險】，所以公司提供每個人全額退款，或改天使用的免費船票。"},{"w":"experience","p":"n.","d":"something that happens to you and affects how you feel","c":"經歷；體驗","s":"A: How was your weekend trip to the desert with the new clients from Dubai, and did they enjoy the activities you planned? B: It was an amazing experience for all of us, because we rode camels, watched the sunset from the sand dunes, and ate a traditional dinner under the stars.","t":"A：你和杜拜的新客戶去沙漠的週末之旅怎麼樣？他們喜歡你安排的活動嗎？ B：對我們所有人來說都是一次很棒的【經歷】，因為我們騎了駱駝、在沙丘上看日落，還在星空下吃了傳統晚餐。"},{"w":"wander","p":"v.","d":"to walk slowly around a place without a clear direction or purpose","c":"閒逛；漫步","s":"A: What did you do during the long break between your two meetings in Kyoto yesterday? B: I decided to wander through the quiet streets near the old temples for about two hours, and I found a lovely tea shop where I bought some gifts for my coworkers back home.","t":"A：昨天你在京都兩場會議之間的長時間空檔做了什麼？ B：我決定在古寺附近安靜的街道上【漫步】大約兩個小時，還發現了一間很棒的茶舖，在那裡幫家鄉的同事買了一些禮物。"},{"w":"roam","p":"v.","d":"to move or travel freely around a large area","c":"漫遊；閒逛；徜徉","s":"A: What makes the safari park different from an ordinary zoo, and why are the tickets so popular with families? B: In the safari park, the animals can roam across large open fields instead of living in small cages, and visitors watch them safely from special buses with big windows.","t":"A：野生動物園和一般動物園有什麼不同？為什麼門票這麼受家庭歡迎？ B：在野生動物園裡，動物可以在廣大的開放草原上自由【漫遊】，而不是住在小籠子裡，遊客則從有大窗戶的特殊巴士上安全地觀賞牠們。"},{"w":"navigate","p":"v.","d":"to find the right way to go from one place to another","c":"導航；找路；駕駛（船、飛機等）","s":"A: How will we find the hotel if our phones lose signal while we are driving through the mountains tonight? B: Don't worry, Ken brought a paper map and a compass, and he learned how to navigate without GPS when he worked as a tour guide in Canada for five years.","t":"A：如果今晚我們開車穿越山區時手機沒有訊號，要怎麼找到飯店？ B：別擔心，肯帶了紙本地圖和指南針，他在加拿大當了五年導遊，學會了如何在沒有衛星導航的情況下【找路】。"},{"w":"trek","p":"v.","d":"to make a long, difficult journey, usually on foot","c":"長途跋涉；徒步旅行","s":"A: Why are the new hiking boots selling so quickly in our store this month, even though they cost more than the old model? B: Many customers plan to trek across the mountains during the holiday season, and they want strong, waterproof boots that will keep their feet dry and comfortable.","t":"A：為什麼新款登山靴這個月在我們店裡賣得這麼快，雖然它比舊款貴？ B：許多顧客計畫在假期期間徒步【長途跋涉】穿越山區，他們想要堅固又防水的靴子，讓雙腳保持乾燥舒適。"},{"w":"boldly","p":"adv.","d":"in a brave and confident way, without fear","c":"大膽地；勇敢地","s":"A: How did our small company manage to win the contract when three much larger firms were also competing for it? B: Our director spoke boldly at the final meeting, promised a faster delivery schedule, and showed the clients a creative plan that none of the other companies had thought of.","t":"A：當另外三家大得多的公司也在競爭時，我們這家小公司是怎麼贏得合約的？ B：我們的總監在最後一次會議上【大膽地】發言，承諾更快的交貨時程，還向客戶展示了其他公司都沒想到的創意企畫。"},{"w":"freely","p":"adv.","d":"without being controlled or limited","c":"自由地；無拘束地","s":"A: Do the guests on the island tour have to stay with the guide all day, or can they choose their own activities? B: After lunch, they can move around the island freely, so some people go swimming, others visit the local market, and a few just relax on the beach until the boat leaves.","t":"A：參加島嶼行程的客人必須整天跟著導遊，還是可以自己選擇活動？ B：午餐後他們可以在島上【自由地】活動，所以有些人去游泳，有些人逛當地市場，還有幾個人就在沙灘上放鬆到船開為止。"},{"w":"unexpectedly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that surprises you because you did not think it would happen","c":"出乎意料地；意外地","s":"A: Why didn't the hiking group reach the top of the mountain on Saturday, when they had planned the trip for months? B: The weather changed unexpectedly in the early afternoon, and the guide decided to turn back because thick clouds and strong rain made the path too slippery to continue.","t":"A：為什麼登山隊週六沒有登上山頂？他們可是計畫了好幾個月。 B：天氣在午後【出乎意料地】變了，因為濃厚的雲層和大雨讓山路太滑無法繼續，嚮導決定折返。"}]},{"unit":8,"theme":"Advice 建議","cards":[{"w":"advise","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone what you think they should do","c":"建議；勸告；忠告","s":"A: I'm thinking about buying a used delivery van for my flower shop, but I don't know much about cars, so what should I do first? B: I would advise you to ask a trusted mechanic to check the engine and brakes carefully before you sign anything, because repairs on old vans can be very expensive.","t":"A：我在考慮為我的花店買一輛二手送貨車，但我不太懂車，我應該先做什麼？ B：我會【建議】你在簽任何文件之前，先請一位信得過的技師仔細檢查引擎和煞車，因為舊貨車的維修費用可能非常高。"},{"w":"guidance","p":"n.","d":"help and advice about how to do something","c":"指導；引導","s":"A: How are the new interns doing in their first month at the accounting firm, and have they made many mistakes with the reports? B: They are doing well, mostly because each intern works under the guidance of a senior accountant who checks their work every afternoon and answers their questions patiently.","t":"A：新來的實習生在會計師事務所的第一個月表現如何？他們的報告出了很多錯嗎？ B：他們表現得很好，主要是因為每位實習生都在一位資深會計師的【指導】下工作，那位會計師每天下午都會檢查他們的工作並耐心回答問題。"},{"w":"suggestion","p":"n.","d":"an idea or plan that you offer for someone to think about","c":"建議；提議","s":"A: The staff kitchen is always messy at the end of the day, and people keep complaining about it, so what can we do? B: I have a suggestion: let's make a simple weekly cleaning schedule and put it on the fridge, so each team takes care of the kitchen for one day.","t":"A：員工廚房每天下班時總是很亂，大家一直抱怨，我們能怎麼做？ B：我有一個【建議】：我們來做一張簡單的每週清潔值日表貼在冰箱上，讓每個小組各負責一天的廚房清潔。"},{"w":"recommendation","p":"n.","d":"advice about what is best to do or buy, often from an expert","c":"推薦；建議","s":"A: Why did the company suddenly change its supplier of office chairs after using the same one for almost ten years? B: The safety committee made a recommendation after many employees complained about back pain, so the managers chose a new supplier that sells chairs with much better support.","t":"A：為什麼公司在用了同一家辦公椅供應商將近十年後突然換掉？ B：在許多員工抱怨背痛之後，安全委員會提出了一項【建議】，所以主管們選擇了一家販售支撐性好得多的椅子的新供應商。"},{"w":"counsel","p":"n.","d":"advice, especially from an older or more experienced person or a professional","c":"忠告；勸告；法律顧問","s":"A: You seemed so calm during the difficult contract talks with the Japanese company last month, so how did you prepare for them? B: Before the talks, I asked for counsel from our former director, who has negotiated with many Asian firms, and her advice helped me stay patient and polite.","t":"A：上個月和那家日本公司進行艱難的合約談判時，你看起來很冷靜，你是怎麼準備的？ B：在談判前，我向我們的前任總監尋求【忠告】，她和許多亞洲公司談判過，她的建議幫助我保持耐心和禮貌。"},{"w":"instruction","p":"n.","d":"information that tells you how to do or use something","c":"指示；說明；用法說明","s":"A: The new printer in the meeting room keeps showing an error message, so do you know how to fix it before the clients arrive? B: Read the instruction printed on the inside of the front cover, because it explains step by step how to remove stuck paper and restart the machine safely.","t":"A：會議室的新印表機一直出現錯誤訊息，你知道在客戶到之前要怎麼修好嗎？ B：去看印在前蓋內側的【說明】，上面一步一步解釋如何取出卡紙並安全地重新啟動機器。"},{"w":"tip","p":"n.","d":"a small but useful piece of practical advice","c":"訣竅；小建議；提示","s":"A: I have to give a speech in English at the international sales meeting next week, and I'm already very nervous about it, so can you help? B: Here's a useful tip that always works for me: practice in front of a mirror every night, and speak a little more slowly than you normally do.","t":"A：下週我必須在國際業務會議上用英文演講，我已經非常緊張了，你能幫幫我嗎？ B：這是一個對我總是很有用的【訣竅】：每天晚上對著鏡子練習，並且說話比平常稍微慢一點。"},{"w":"warning","p":"n.","d":"a statement telling someone about a possible danger or problem","c":"警告；預告","s":"A: Why did all the ships stay in the harbor this morning, even though the sky looked clear and the sea was calm? B: The weather office issued a storm warning late last night, saying that strong winds and heavy rain would reach the coast by noon, so the captains decided not to sail.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上所有船隻都留在港口，即使天空看起來很晴朗、海面也很平靜？ B：氣象局昨晚深夜發布了暴風雨【警報】，說強風和大雨中午前會抵達沿岸，所以船長們決定不出航。"},{"w":"encouragement","p":"n.","d":"words or actions that give someone confidence or hope","c":"鼓勵；激勵","s":"A: How did Daniel manage to pass the difficult accounting exam on his third try, after failing it twice last year? B: His manager gave him a lot of encouragement, let him leave work early twice a week to study, and kept telling him that he had the skills to succeed.","t":"A：丹尼爾去年考了兩次都沒過，他是怎麼在第三次通過那個困難的會計考試的？ B：他的主管給了他很多【鼓勵】，讓他每週兩次提早下班去讀書，還不斷告訴他，他有成功的能力。"},{"w":"feedback","p":"n.","d":"comments about how well someone did something, given so they can improve","c":"回饋；意見","s":"A: How will we know whether guests are happy with the changes we made to the hotel restaurant last month? B: We can send them a short online survey after they check out, and their feedback will show us which dishes they liked and what we still need to improve.","t":"A：我們要怎麼知道客人對上個月飯店餐廳的改變是否滿意？ B：我們可以在他們退房後寄一份簡短的線上問卷，他們的【回饋】會讓我們知道他們喜歡哪些菜，以及我們還需要改進什麼。"},{"w":"consult","p":"v.","d":"to go to a person or a book for information or advice","c":"諮詢；請教；查閱","s":"A: The pain in my wrist has become much worse since I started typing for eight hours a day on the new project, so what should I do? B: You should consult a doctor this week, and you might also ask the office manager for a better keyboard and a soft wrist pad.","t":"A：自從我開始在新專案每天打字八個小時後，手腕就痛得更厲害了，我該怎麼辦？ B：你這週應該去【請教】醫生，也可以向辦公室經理要一個比較好的鍵盤和柔軟的護腕墊。"},{"w":"consultation","p":"n.","d":"a meeting with an expert to get advice","c":"諮詢；商議；會診","s":"A: I'd like to make my small restaurant more energy-efficient, but I have no idea where to start, so can you help me? B: The city offers a free consultation with an energy expert, who will visit your restaurant, check your kitchen equipment, and suggest simple ways to cut your electricity bills.","t":"A：我想讓我的小餐廳更節能，但完全不知道從何開始，你能幫我嗎？ B：市政府提供和能源專家的免費【諮詢】，專家會到你的餐廳檢查廚房設備，並建議簡單的方法來降低電費。"},{"w":"opinion","p":"n.","d":"what you think or believe about something","c":"意見；看法；見解","s":"A: The marketing team has prepared two different designs for the new product package, and we need to choose one by Friday. B: In my opinion, the blue design looks more modern and professional, but we should also show both designs to a few customers before we make the final decision.","t":"A：行銷團隊為新產品包裝準備了兩種不同的設計，我們必須在週五前選出一個。 B：依我的【看法】，藍色的設計看起來比較現代、專業，但在做最後決定前，我們也應該把兩種設計拿給幾位顧客看看。"},{"w":"perspective","p":"n.","d":"a particular way of thinking about something","c":"觀點；看法；角度","s":"A: Why did the director invite three young employees to join the planning meeting for next year's advertising campaign? B: She wanted a fresh perspective from people in their twenties, because the campaign is aimed at young customers, and the older managers may not understand what they really want.","t":"A：為什麼總監邀請三位年輕員工參加明年廣告活動的企畫會議？ B：她想要聽聽二十幾歲年輕人的新【觀點】，因為這次活動的對象是年輕顧客，而年長的主管們可能不了解他們真正想要什麼。"},{"w":"direction","p":"n.","d":"instructions or control that help someone know what to do","c":"指導；指揮；方向","s":"A: The new branch had very poor sales last year, so why are the numbers so much better this year? B: Under the direction of the new branch manager, the staff set clear monthly goals, improved their customer service, and started selling products online as well as in the store.","t":"A：新分店去年的業績很差，為什麼今年的數字好了這麼多？ B：在新分店經理的【指導】下，員工訂定了明確的每月目標、改善了顧客服務，並且除了店面之外也開始在網路上銷售產品。"},{"w":"input","p":"n.","d":"ideas, advice, or information that you give to help with a project","c":"意見；建議；投入","s":"A: Should we finish the budget plan ourselves this afternoon, or do we need to talk to anyone else in the company first? B: We need some input from the sales department before we finish, because they know which products will need more money for advertising during the holiday season.","t":"A：我們應該今天下午自己完成預算計畫，還是需要先和公司裡的其他人談談？ B：在完成之前，我們需要業務部的一些【意見】，因為他們知道哪些產品在假期期間需要更多的廣告經費。"},{"w":"recommend","p":"v.","d":"to say that someone or something is good and suitable","c":"推薦；建議","s":"A: Our Korean clients are arriving on Thursday evening, and I want to take them somewhere nice for dinner after their long flight. B: I recommend the seafood restaurant near the harbor, because it is quiet enough for conversation, the service is excellent, and it has a beautiful view of the city lights.","t":"A：我們的韓國客戶週四晚上抵達，他們長途飛行後，我想帶他們去不錯的地方吃晚餐。 B：我【推薦】港口附近的那間海鮮餐廳，因為那裡夠安靜可以聊天，服務很好，還能欣賞美麗的城市夜景。"},{"w":"urge","p":"v.","d":"to strongly advise or try hard to persuade someone to do something","c":"力勸；敦促；催促","s":"A: Why did the IT department send another email to all staff this morning, when we already received one yesterday? B: They want to urge everyone to change their passwords before Friday, because several employees received fake emails last week that tried to steal their account information.","t":"A：為什麼資訊部今天早上又寄了一封信給全體員工？我們昨天已經收到一封了。 B：他們想【敦促】大家在週五前更改密碼，因為上週有幾位員工收到企圖竊取帳號資料的假電子郵件。"},{"w":"proposal","p":"n.","d":"a plan or idea that is formally suggested for people to consider","c":"提案；建議；計畫書","s":"A: What happened at the board meeting this morning, and did the directors agree to open a new office in Vietnam? B: They read the proposal carefully and liked most of it, but they asked us to add more details about costs and local hiring before they make a final decision next month.","t":"A：今天早上的董事會發生了什麼事？董事們同意在越南設立新辦公室了嗎？ B：他們仔細閱讀了【提案】，大部分都很喜歡，但要求我們補充更多關於成本和當地招聘的細節，下個月才會做最後決定。"},{"w":"hint","p":"n.","d":"a small piece of advice or a clue that helps you do or guess something","c":"提示；暗示；小訣竅","s":"A: I've tried three times to set up the new video meeting software on my laptop, but it still won't connect to the camera. B: Here's a hint: close all your other programs first, then restart the software, because the camera often stops working when another app is already using it.","t":"A：我已經試了三次在筆電上安裝新的視訊會議軟體，但它還是連不上攝影機。 B：給你一個【提示】：先關掉其他所有程式，再重新啟動軟體，因為當其他應用程式正在使用攝影機時，它常常會無法運作。"},{"w":"lesson","p":"n.","d":"something you learn from a bad experience that helps you in the future","c":"教訓；課程","s":"A: Last year we lost a big order because we promised a delivery date that our factory could not meet, didn't we? B: Yes, and that was an important lesson for all of us, so now we always check with the factory before we promise any dates to customers.","t":"A：去年我們因為承諾了工廠無法達到的交貨日期而失去一筆大訂單，對吧？ B：對，那是給我們所有人的重要【教訓】，所以現在我們在向客戶承諾任何日期之前，一定會先和工廠確認。"},{"w":"reminder","p":"n.","d":"something that helps you remember something you must do","c":"提醒；提示通知","s":"A: How can we stop so many patients from missing their appointments at the dental clinic every week? B: We could send each patient a text message reminder the day before the visit, because most people forget appointments that they made several weeks earlier, especially when they are busy at work.","t":"A：我們要怎麼做，才能讓牙科診所每週不再有這麼多病人錯過預約？ B：我們可以在看診前一天傳簡訊【提醒】每位病人，因為大部分人會忘記幾週前預約的時間，尤其是工作忙碌的時候。"},{"w":"coaching","p":"n.","d":"the process of training and helping someone to improve a skill","c":"指導；訓練；輔導","s":"A: Our sales staff are friendly, but many of them find it hard to close deals with difficult customers, so what can we do? B: We could hire an expert to provide weekly coaching for the team, because practicing real situations with a professional usually builds confidence and improves results quickly.","t":"A：我們的業務人員很友善，但很多人都很難和難搞的顧客成交，我們能怎麼做？ B：我們可以聘請專家每週為團隊提供【指導訓練】，因為和專業人士一起演練真實情境，通常能很快建立信心並提升成果。"},{"w":"mentorship","p":"n.","d":"help and advice given over time by an experienced person to a less experienced one","c":"師徒指導；導師制度","s":"A: Why do so many young engineers want to work at your company, even though other firms offer slightly higher salaries? B: We have an excellent mentorship program, in which every new engineer is paired with a senior colleague who meets them each week and helps them plan their careers.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多年輕工程師想到你們公司工作，即使其他公司提供稍高的薪水？ B：我們有一個很棒的【導師指導】計畫，每位新進工程師都會和一位資深同事配對，對方每週和他們見面，並幫助他們規劃職涯。"},{"w":"directive","p":"n.","d":"an official order or instruction from someone in authority","c":"指令；命令；指示","s":"A: Why are all the managers working from the office again this week when they were allowed to work from home last month? B: The head office sent a new directive on Monday saying that all managers must be in the office at least four days a week to meet with their teams.","t":"A：為什麼這週所有經理又回辦公室上班了？上個月他們不是可以在家工作嗎？ B：總公司週一發布了一項新的【指令】，規定所有經理每週至少要有四天在辦公室與團隊開會。"},{"w":"guiding","p":"adj.","d":"giving direction or advice that helps someone decide what to do","c":"指導性的；引導的","s":"A: Our company is growing very fast, so how do you make sure that all the new branches treat customers in the same way? B: We have one guiding principle that every employee learns on the first day, which is that the customer's comfort and safety always come before quick profits.","t":"A：我們公司成長得很快，你們要怎麼確保所有新分店都用同樣的方式對待顧客？ B：我們有一個每位員工第一天就要學習的【指導】原則，就是顧客的舒適與安全永遠優先於快速獲利。"},{"w":"advisory","p":"adj.","d":"having the job of giving advice, usually without making the final decisions","c":"顧問的；諮詢的","s":"A: Will the university professors decide how the city spends the money for the new public transportation system? B: No, they only have an advisory role, so they will study the plans and share their ideas, but the city council will make the final decisions about the budget.","t":"A：大學教授們會決定市政府如何使用新大眾運輸系統的經費嗎？ B：不會，他們只擔任【顧問】角色，所以他們會研究計畫並提供想法，但預算的最後決定權在市議會。"},{"w":"wisdom","p":"n.","d":"the ability to make good decisions based on knowledge and experience","c":"智慧；明智","s":"A: Why does the young owner of the bakery still ask her grandfather for advice, even though he retired many years ago? B: He ran the shop successfully for forty years, and she values his wisdom about handling customers, choosing suppliers, and keeping costs low during difficult times.","t":"A：為什麼那間麵包店的年輕老闆仍然向祖父請教，即使他多年前就退休了？ B：他成功經營那家店四十年，她很重視他在應對顧客、挑選供應商，以及在困難時期控制成本方面的【智慧】。"}]},{"unit":9,"theme":"Age 年齡","cards":[{"w":"reality","p":"n.","d":"the true situation, not what you hope or imagine","c":"現實；真實情況","s":"A: When I was a student, I thought that working at a big company would be exciting every day, so how does it feel after five years? B: The reality is quite different, because most days are full of emails and meetings, but I've learned to enjoy the small successes and the friendly people around me.","t":"A：我當學生時，以為在大公司工作每天都會很刺激，你工作五年後感覺如何？ B：【現實】很不一樣，因為大部分的日子都塞滿了電子郵件和會議，但我已經學會享受小小的成就和身邊友善的人們。"},{"w":"quite","p":"adv.","d":"fairly or very, but not extremely","c":"相當；頗","s":"A: Your father retired from the bank last spring, so how is he spending his time now that he doesn't go to the office every day? B: He is quite busy, actually, because he volunteers at the library twice a week, takes cooking classes, and helps my sister look after her two young children.","t":"A：你爸爸去年春天從銀行退休了，他現在不用每天進辦公室，都怎麼打發時間？ B：其實他【相當】忙，因為他每週去圖書館當兩次志工、上烹飪課，還幫我姊姊照顧她的兩個小孩。"},{"w":"enjoy","p":"v.","d":"to get pleasure from something","c":"享受；喜愛","s":"A: Many of our older customers have stopped coming to the gym in the evenings, so do you know why they changed their routine? B: They told me they enjoy the morning yoga classes much more, because the gym is quieter, the music is softer, and they can have coffee together afterward.","t":"A：我們很多年長的顧客晚上不再來健身房了，你知道他們為什麼改變作息嗎？ B：他們告訴我，他們更【喜歡】早上的瑜伽課，因為健身房比較安靜、音樂比較柔和，而且課後他們可以一起喝咖啡。"},{"w":"relive","p":"v.","d":"to remember something so clearly that you feel you are experiencing it again","c":"重溫；再經歷","s":"A: Why did so many retired employees come to the company's fiftieth anniversary party last Saturday night? B: The organizers showed old photos and videos from the 1980s, so everyone had a chance to relive their younger days and meet colleagues they had not seen for many years.","t":"A：為什麼上週六晚上有這麼多退休員工來參加公司五十週年派對？ B：主辦單位播放了1980年代的老照片和影片，所以大家都有機會【重溫】年輕時光，並見到許多年沒見的同事。"},{"w":"appear","p":"v.","d":"to seem; to give a particular impression","c":"顯得；看起來；似乎","s":"A: Did you know that Mr. Wilson, the new head of the design team, is already sixty-two years old? B: Really? He doesn't appear to be that old at all, maybe because he exercises every morning, rides his bike to work, and is always full of new ideas in meetings.","t":"A：你知道設計團隊的新主管威爾森先生已經六十二歲了嗎？ B：真的嗎？他完全【看起來】不像那個年紀，可能是因為他每天早上運動、騎腳踏車上班，而且開會時總是充滿新點子。"},{"w":"near","p":"adj.","d":"close in time or distance","c":"接近的；不久的","s":"A: Our team is getting older, and three senior engineers will retire within two years, so what is the company planning to do? B: In the near future, the company will hire several young engineers and ask the senior staff to train them before they leave.","t":"A：我們團隊的年紀越來越大，有三位資深工程師兩年內就要退休，公司打算怎麼做？ B：在【不久的】將來，公司會雇用幾位年輕工程師，並請資深員工在離職前訓練他們。"},{"w":"adulthood","p":"n.","d":"the time of life when you are an adult","c":"成年；成年期","s":"A: Why does the bank run free money-management workshops for university students every summer? B: Many young people enter adulthood without knowing how to save money, pay bills, or avoid debt, so the bank wants to teach them these skills before they start their first full-time jobs.","t":"A：為什麼銀行每年夏天都為大學生舉辦免費的理財工作坊？ B：許多年輕人步入【成年】時還不知道如何存錢、繳帳單或避免負債，所以銀行想在他們開始第一份全職工作前教他們這些技能。"},{"w":"experienced","p":"adj.","d":"having knowledge or skill from doing something for a long time","c":"有經驗的；經驗豐富的","s":"A: The client wants the new shopping center designed in only six months, so who should we put in charge of the project? B: We need an experienced architect who has handled large projects before, because a tight schedule like this leaves no time for beginners to learn from their mistakes.","t":"A：客戶希望新購物中心在短短六個月內設計完成，我們應該讓誰負責這個專案？ B：我們需要一位以前處理過大型專案、【經驗豐富的】建築師，因為這麼緊湊的時程，沒有時間讓新手從錯誤中學習。"},{"w":"recognize","p":"v.","d":"to know who someone is because you have seen them before","c":"認出；認得","s":"A: Did you meet anyone interesting at the high school reunion dinner at the hotel last weekend? B: It was a bit funny, because after twenty-five years many of my classmates had gray hair, and I couldn't recognize some of them until they told me their names.","t":"A：上週末在飯店舉辦的高中同學會晚餐，你有遇到什麼有趣的人嗎？ B：有點好笑，因為過了二十五年，很多同學都有白頭髮了，有些人直到他們告訴我名字，我才【認出】他們來。"},{"w":"dynamic","p":"adj.","d":"full of energy and new ideas","c":"充滿活力的；有幹勁的","s":"A: Why do you think the new manager has become so popular with the staff in only three months? B: She is very dynamic, always full of energy and fresh ideas, and she encourages both younger and older employees to share their opinions in every meeting.","t":"A：你認為新經理為什麼在短短三個月內就這麼受員工歡迎？ B：她非常【有活力】，總是充滿幹勁和新點子，而且她在每次會議上都鼓勵年輕和年長的員工分享意見。"},{"w":"personality","p":"n.","d":"the kind of person someone is, shown by the way they behave and feel","c":"個性；性格","s":"A: Both candidates for the receptionist job have similar experience, so how will we choose the right person? B: I think we should choose the one with the warmer personality, because the receptionist is the first person every visitor meets, and a friendly attitude makes a strong first impression.","t":"A：兩位應徵接待員工作的人經驗差不多，我們要怎麼選出合適的人？ B：我認為我們應該選【個性】比較溫暖的那一位，因為接待員是每位訪客見到的第一個人，友善的態度能留下深刻的第一印象。"},{"w":"relaxed","p":"adj.","d":"calm and not worried","c":"放鬆的；輕鬆自在的","s":"A: You looked very tired and stressed last month, but you seem much happier now, so what changed? B: I started leaving work on time and walking in the park every evening, and now I feel much more relaxed, even when we have busy weeks with lots of deadlines.","t":"A：你上個月看起來很疲倦、壓力很大，但現在似乎開心多了，有什麼改變嗎？ B：我開始準時下班，每天傍晚去公園散步，現在即使遇到截止期限很多的忙碌週，我也覺得【放鬆】多了。"},{"w":"predict","p":"v.","d":"to say what will happen in the future","c":"預測；預言","s":"A: Why is the company building so many new apartments for older people in the suburbs this year? B: Experts predict that the number of residents over sixty-five will grow quickly in the next ten years, so the company expects strong demand for safe, comfortable homes near hospitals and parks.","t":"A：為什麼公司今年在郊區興建這麼多給年長者的新公寓？ B：專家【預測】未來十年六十五歲以上的居民人數會快速增加，所以公司預期靠近醫院和公園、安全又舒適的住宅會有強勁需求。"},{"w":"intriguing","p":"adj.","d":"very interesting because it is unusual or mysterious","c":"引人入勝的；耐人尋味的","s":"A: What did you think of the presentation about the island where many people live past one hundred years old? B: I found it very intriguing, especially the part about their simple diet and close family ties, and I'd like to read the full research report when it is published next month.","t":"A：你覺得那場關於許多人活過一百歲的島嶼的簡報怎麼樣？ B：我覺得非常【引人入勝】，尤其是關於他們簡單飲食和緊密家庭關係的部分，等下個月完整的研究報告出版時，我想讀一讀。"},{"w":"confident","p":"adj.","d":"sure that you can do something well","c":"有信心的；自信的","s":"A: How did your daughter feel about her first job interview at the travel agency yesterday afternoon? B: She felt quite confident, because she had practiced her answers with me several times, researched the company carefully, and prepared some good questions to ask the manager at the end.","t":"A：你女兒對她昨天下午在旅行社的第一次工作面試感覺如何？ B：她覺得很有【自信】，因為她跟我練習了好幾次回答、仔細研究了公司，還準備了幾個好問題在最後問經理。"},{"w":"vastly","p":"adv.","d":"very much; to a very great degree","c":"極大地；大大地","s":"A: Do you think the way young people shop today is similar to how your parents shopped thirty years ago? B: Not at all, it is vastly different, because most young people now compare prices on their phones and buy online, while my parents always went to local stores and paid in cash.","t":"A：你覺得現在年輕人購物的方式和你父母三十年前的方式相似嗎？ B：完全不同，是【大大地】不一樣，因為現在大部分年輕人都用手機比價並在網路上購買，而我父母總是去當地商店並用現金付款。"},{"w":"ponder","p":"v.","d":"to think carefully about something for a long time","c":"沉思；仔細考慮","s":"A: Is your uncle still planning to sell his restaurant and retire next year, or has he changed his mind? B: He is still trying to decide, so he will ponder the offer from the buyer over the holiday, because the restaurant has been his whole life for over thirty years.","t":"A：你叔叔還打算明年把餐廳賣掉然後退休嗎？還是他改變心意了？ B：他還在考慮，所以他會在假期期間【仔細思考】買家的出價，因為三十多年來，那間餐廳就是他的全部生活。"},{"w":"mature","p":"adj.","d":"behaving in a sensible way, like an adult","c":"成熟的；穩重的","s":"A: The new intern is only twenty years old, so are you sure we should let her speak with our most important client? B: Yes, she is very mature for her age, because she listens carefully, stays calm under pressure, and always asks for help when she isn't sure about something.","t":"A：新來的實習生才二十歲，你確定我們應該讓她和我們最重要的客戶談話嗎？ B：確定，以她的年紀來說她非常【成熟】，因為她會仔細聆聽、在壓力下保持冷靜，而且不確定的時候總會尋求協助。"},{"w":"independent","p":"adj.","d":"able to live or work without help from others","c":"獨立的；自主的","s":"A: Why did your grandmother decide to stay in her own apartment instead of moving in with your family? B: She wants to stay independent as long as possible, so she cooks for herself, takes the bus to the market, and only asks us for help with heavy cleaning once a month.","t":"A：你奶奶為什麼決定住在自己的公寓，而不搬去和你們家同住？ B：她想盡可能保持【獨立】，所以她自己煮飯、搭公車去市場，只有每個月一次的大掃除才會請我們幫忙。"},{"w":"insecure","p":"adj.","d":"not confident about yourself or your abilities","c":"沒有安全感的；缺乏自信的","s":"A: Why does Tom always stay quiet in meetings, even when he clearly knows the answer to the manager's questions? B: He feels insecure because he is the youngest person on the team, so he worries that the older engineers will laugh at his ideas or think they are too simple.","t":"A：為什麼湯姆開會時總是保持沉默，即使他顯然知道經理問題的答案？ B：他覺得【沒有自信】，因為他是團隊裡最年輕的人，所以擔心年長的工程師會嘲笑他的想法，或覺得太簡單。"},{"w":"embrace","p":"v.","d":"to accept new ideas, changes, or opportunities with enthusiasm","c":"欣然接受；擁抱","s":"A: Were the older staff members unhappy when the company replaced all the paper forms with a new computer system? B: Surprisingly, most of them were happy to embrace the change, because the training was clear and patient, and the new system saves them about an hour of work every day.","t":"A：公司用新的電腦系統取代所有紙本表格時，年長的員工不高興嗎？ B：令人驚訝的是，他們大多數人都樂於【接受】這項改變，因為訓練清楚又有耐心，而且新系統每天幫他們省下大約一個小時的工作。"},{"w":"ageless","p":"adj.","d":"never seeming to grow old; not affected by time","c":"永不顯老的；永恆的","s":"A: Why did the fashion company choose a famous sixty-year-old actress for its new advertising campaign this autumn? B: The company wanted to show that style is ageless, and its research found that many older women feel ignored by advertisements that only use very young models.","t":"A：為什麼這家時尚公司今年秋天的新廣告活動選了一位六十歲的知名女演員？ B：公司想表達時尚是【不受年齡限制的】，而且它的研究發現，許多年長女性覺得只用年輕模特兒的廣告忽略了她們。"},{"w":"mindset","p":"n.","d":"a way of thinking or set of attitudes","c":"心態；思維模式","s":"A: How has your sixty-five-year-old father managed to learn computer programming so quickly after he retired? B: He has a great mindset, because he believes people can learn new skills at any age, so he practices every day and isn't afraid of making mistakes.","t":"A：你六十五歲的父親退休後，是怎麼這麼快學會電腦程式設計的？ B：他有很棒的【心態】，因為他相信人在任何年紀都能學習新技能，所以他每天練習，而且不怕犯錯。"},{"w":"re-energize","p":"v.","d":"to give someone new energy and enthusiasm","c":"使恢復活力；重新振作","s":"A: Our sales team seems tired and bored after such a long and difficult year, so what can we do to help them? B: A short trip to the beach for team activities might re-energize everyone, and the managers could also announce some exciting new goals and rewards for next year.","t":"A：經過這麼漫長又艱難的一年，我們的業務團隊似乎又累又無精打采，我們能做些什麼來幫助他們？ B：去海邊進行短程的團隊活動或許能讓大家【重新振作】，主管們也可以宣布一些令人振奮的明年新目標和獎勵。"},{"w":"vibrant","p":"adj.","d":"full of life, energy, and color","c":"充滿活力的；鮮明的","s":"A: Why did the company choose this neighborhood for its new office, when the rent is higher than in other parts of the city? B: The area is very vibrant, with busy cafés, art galleries, and street markets, and the managers believe young employees will enjoy working in such a lively place.","t":"A：為什麼公司把新辦公室選在這個社區？這裡的租金比城裡其他地方都高。 B：這個地區非常【有活力】，有熱鬧的咖啡館、藝廊和街頭市集，主管們相信年輕員工會喜歡在這麼熱鬧的地方工作。"},{"w":"inevitable","p":"adj.","d":"certain to happen and impossible to avoid","c":"不可避免的；必然的","s":"A: Do you think our company will need to raise the price of our products next year because of higher costs? B: I'm afraid it's inevitable, because the price of raw materials and shipping has gone up by twenty percent, and we cannot keep paying for the difference ourselves.","t":"A：你認為我們公司明年會因為成本上升而需要調漲產品價格嗎？ B：恐怕這是【不可避免的】，因為原物料和運費已經上漲了百分之二十，我們沒辦法一直自己吸收差額。"},{"w":"priority","p":"n.","d":"something that is more important than other things and must be done first","c":"優先事項；優先考慮","s":"A: Now that your children are in elementary school, have you thought about going back to full-time work at the hospital? B: Yes, but my main priority is still my family, so I'm looking for a part-time job that lets me finish work before the children come home in the afternoon.","t":"A：既然你的孩子都上小學了，你有考慮回醫院做全職工作嗎？ B：有，但我的首要【優先事項】仍然是家庭，所以我在找一份兼職工作，讓我能在孩子下午回家前下班。"},{"w":"behave","p":"v.","d":"to act or do things in a particular way","c":"表現；舉止","s":"A: Why are we giving the new store staff a full day of customer service training before the shop opens next week? B: We want them to know how to behave politely with all customers, including elderly people who may need extra time and patience when they pay or ask questions.","t":"A：為什麼要在下週新店開幕前，給新店員一整天的顧客服務訓練？ B：我們希望他們知道如何對所有顧客禮貌地【應對】，包括在付款或詢問時可能需要更多時間和耐心的長者。"},{"w":"physically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way related to the body","c":"身體上；體力上","s":"A: Your father is eighty years old, but he still works in his garden every morning, so how does he stay so healthy? B: He stays physically active by walking for an hour every day, lifting light weights, and doing simple stretching exercises, and he also eats lots of fresh vegetables from his garden.","t":"A：你父親八十歲了，但每天早上還在花園裡工作，他是怎麼保持這麼健康的？ B：他每天走路一小時、舉輕量啞鈴、做簡單的伸展運動來保持【身體】活躍，還吃很多自家花園種的新鮮蔬菜。"},{"w":"mentally","p":"adv.","d":"in a way related to the mind","c":"心理上；精神上；智力上","s":"A: How does your grandmother keep her memory so sharp, even though she is now over ninety years old? B: She stays mentally active by doing crossword puzzles every morning, reading the newspaper, and playing card games with her friends at the community center three afternoons a week.","t":"A：你奶奶已經九十多歲了，她是怎麼讓記憶力保持這麼好的？ B：她每天早上玩填字遊戲、看報紙，每週有三個下午在社區中心和朋友玩紙牌，藉此保持【頭腦】活躍。"},{"w":"obsessed","p":"adj.","d":"thinking about something or someone all the time in a way that is not normal","c":"著迷的；執著的","s":"A: Why does our sales manager check the sales numbers on his phone every ten minutes, even during lunch? B: He is obsessed with reaching the yearly target before December, but I think he should relax a little, because the team is already doing better than last year.","t":"A：為什麼我們的業務經理連吃午餐時都每十分鐘就用手機查一次業績數字？ B：他對在十二月前達成年度目標很【執著】，但我覺得他應該稍微放鬆一點，因為團隊的表現已經比去年好了。"},{"w":"relevant","p":"adj.","d":"connected with what is being discussed or done","c":"相關的；切題的","s":"A: Should I include my summer job at the ice cream shop on my résumé when I apply for the marketing position? B: Only if it is relevant to the job, so you could mention that you designed the shop's social media posts, because that shows you already have some marketing experience.","t":"A：我應徵行銷職位時，應該在履歷上寫我暑假在冰淇淋店打工的經歷嗎？ B：只有在和這份工作【相關】時才寫，所以你可以提到你設計過店裡的社群媒體貼文，因為那顯示你已經有一些行銷經驗。"},{"w":"inclination","p":"n.","d":"a feeling that makes you want to do something","c":"傾向；意願；愛好","s":"A: Your father has worked as a lawyer for forty years, so does he plan to keep working, or will he retire soon? B: He has no inclination to stop working yet, because he still loves helping his clients, and he says that a busy schedule keeps him young and healthy.","t":"A：你父親當了四十年律師，他打算繼續工作，還是很快就會退休？ B：他目前還沒有停止工作的【意願】，因為他仍然很喜歡幫助客戶，而且他說忙碌的行程讓他保持年輕和健康。"},{"w":"interact","p":"v.","d":"to communicate with and spend time with other people","c":"互動；交流","s":"A: Why did the nursing home start inviting students from the nearby high school to visit every Friday afternoon? B: The staff want the elderly residents to interact with young people more often, because talking, playing games, and sharing stories helps everyone feel happier and less lonely.","t":"A：為什麼安養院開始邀請附近高中的學生每週五下午來拜訪？ B：工作人員希望長者住民能更常和年輕人【互動】，因為聊天、玩遊戲和分享故事能讓每個人更快樂、更不孤單。"}]},{"unit":10,"theme":"Airport 機場","cards":[{"w":"terminal","p":"n.","d":"a large building at an airport where passengers arrive and leave","c":"航廈；航站","s":"A: I'm picking up our clients from Seoul at the airport tomorrow afternoon, but I'm not sure where I should wait for them. B: Their airline uses terminal 2, so wait near the arrivals hall on the first floor, and send them a message so they know where to find you after they collect their bags.","t":"A：我明天下午要去機場接首爾來的客戶，但不確定該在哪裡等他們。 B：他們的航空公司使用第二【航廈】，所以在一樓入境大廳附近等，並傳訊息給他們，讓他們領完行李後知道去哪裡找你。"},{"w":"runway","p":"n.","d":"a long, flat road where airplanes take off and land","c":"跑道","s":"A: Why has our plane been waiting on the ground for forty minutes when it was supposed to leave at nine o'clock? B: The captain just announced that workers are clearing snow from the runway, and he thinks we will be able to take off in about fifteen minutes once they have finished.","t":"A：為什麼我們的飛機已經在地面等了四十分鐘？它原本應該九點起飛的。 B：機長剛剛廣播說，工作人員正在清除【跑道】上的積雪，他認為等他們清完，我們大約十五分鐘後就能起飛。"},{"w":"gate","p":"n.","d":"the place in an airport where passengers get on a plane","c":"登機門","s":"A: Excuse me, my flight to Bangkok leaves in thirty minutes, but the screen doesn't show where I should go to get on the plane. B: Your flight has just been moved to gate 15 because of a technical problem, so please walk quickly to the end of this hall and turn left.","t":"A：不好意思，我飛往曼谷的班機三十分鐘後起飛，但螢幕沒有顯示我該去哪裡登機。 B：因為技術問題，您的班機剛剛改到15號【登機門】，所以請快步走到這個大廳的盡頭再左轉。"},{"w":"check-in","p":"n.","d":"the place or process where you show your ticket and give your bags before a flight","c":"報到；登機手續；報到櫃台","s":"A: Our flight to Tokyo leaves at seven in the morning, so what time do you think we should leave the hotel? B: Let's leave at four thirty, because the check-in counter closes one hour before departure, and there are often long lines of tour groups at the airport early in the morning.","t":"A：我們飛往東京的班機早上七點起飛，你覺得我們應該幾點離開飯店？ B：我們四點半出發吧，因為【報到】櫃台在起飛前一小時就關閉了，而且清晨的機場常常有旅行團排長長的隊伍。"},{"w":"security","p":"n.","d":"the area at an airport where bags and passengers are checked for dangerous items","c":"安檢；安全檢查處；安全","s":"A: Why did it take you so long to get to the gate, when you arrived at the airport two hours before the flight? B: The line at security was huge, and then the officers opened my bag because I forgot to take my laptop out and put it in a separate tray.","t":"A：你在班機起飛前兩小時就到機場了，為什麼花了這麼久才到登機門？ B：【安檢】的隊伍超長，然後安檢人員打開了我的包包，因為我忘了把筆電拿出來放在另一個托盤裡。"},{"w":"customs","p":"n.","d":"the place at an airport where officers check what you bring into a country","c":"海關","s":"A: I bought some expensive watches during my business trip to Switzerland, so do I need to do anything special when I land? B: Yes, you need to go to the red line at customs and tell the officers what you bought, because you may have to pay tax on goods over a certain value.","t":"A：我在瑞士出差時買了幾支昂貴的手錶，降落時需要做什麼特別的事嗎？ B：需要，你必須到【海關】的紅線通道向關員申報你買的東西，因為超過一定金額的物品可能要繳稅。"},{"w":"immigration","p":"n.","d":"the place at an airport where officers check passports and visas","c":"入境檢查；移民局","s":"A: How long will it take us to leave the airport after we land in New York on Monday evening? B: It could take an hour or more, because the lines at immigration are usually very long in the evening, and the officers ask every visitor several questions before stamping their passports.","t":"A：我們週一晚上在紐約降落後，要花多久時間才能離開機場？ B：可能要一個小時以上，因為晚上【入境審查】的隊伍通常很長，而且官員在護照蓋章前會問每位訪客好幾個問題。"},{"w":"baggage","p":"n.","d":"the bags and suitcases you take with you when you travel","c":"行李","s":"A: I'm flying to Singapore for a two-week training course, and I need to bring a lot of documents and clothes. B: Check the airline's website before you pack, because your ticket only includes twenty kilograms of baggage, and the fee for extra weight at the airport is very expensive.","t":"A：我要飛去新加坡參加兩週的培訓課程，需要帶很多文件和衣服。 B：打包前先查一下航空公司的網站，因為你的機票只含二十公斤的【行李】，在機場付超重費非常貴。"},{"w":"luggage","p":"n.","d":"suitcases and bags used for carrying things when traveling","c":"行李","s":"A: Do you know where I can leave my bags for a few hours, because my hotel room won't be ready until three o'clock this afternoon? B: There is a luggage storage office on the ground floor of the train station, and it only costs about five dollars for each bag per day.","t":"A：你知道我可以把包包寄放在哪裡幾個小時嗎？因為我的飯店房間要到下午三點才準備好。 B：火車站一樓有一個【行李】寄放處，每件每天大約只要五美元。"},{"w":"carousel","p":"n.","d":"a moving belt at an airport from which passengers collect their bags","c":"行李轉盤","s":"A: We've been waiting for our suitcases for nearly thirty minutes, so are you sure we're standing in the right place? B: The screen says that bags from our flight will come out on carousel 4, but there was a problem with the machine, so the airport staff are fixing it now.","t":"A：我們已經等行李將近三十分鐘了，你確定我們站對地方了嗎？ B：螢幕顯示我們班機的行李會從4號【行李轉盤】出來，但機器出了問題，所以機場人員正在修理。"},{"w":"boarding","p":"n.","d":"the act of getting on a plane, ship, or train","c":"登機；上船；上車","s":"A: I still need to buy a gift for my client at the duty-free shop, so do I have enough time before our flight? B: You'll have to hurry, because boarding starts in fifteen minutes, and passengers with small children and business class tickets will get on the plane first.","t":"A：我還需要在免稅店買份禮物給客戶，我們班機起飛前我時間夠嗎？ B：你得快一點，因為十五分鐘後就開始【登機】了，帶小孩的乘客和商務艙旅客會先上飛機。"},{"w":"departure","p":"n.","d":"the act of leaving a place, especially at the start of a journey","c":"出發；離開；起飛","s":"A: Our flight to Hong Kong was supposed to leave at eleven, but it's already eleven thirty, so what's happening? B: The airline just sent a text saying that the departure has been moved to twelve fifteen because the plane arrived late from Manila after bad weather this morning.","t":"A：我們飛往香港的班機原定十一點起飛，但現在已經十一點半了，怎麼回事？ B：航空公司剛剛傳簡訊說，因為飛機今天早上遇到壞天氣從馬尼拉晚到，【起飛】時間改到十二點十五分。"},{"w":"arrival","p":"n.","d":"the act of reaching a place","c":"抵達；到達","s":"A: When should the hotel driver go to the airport to pick up our guest speaker from London? B: Her arrival is planned for six forty in the evening, but the driver should check the flight information online before he leaves, because flights from Europe are sometimes early or late.","t":"A：飯店司機應該什麼時候去機場接從倫敦來的演講嘉賓？ B：她預計晚上六點四十分【抵達】，但司機出發前應該先上網查航班資訊，因為來自歐洲的班機有時會提早或延誤。"},{"w":"delay","p":"n.","d":"a time when someone or something has to wait or is late","c":"延誤；耽擱","s":"A: Why didn't Mr. Lopez join the morning meeting at our office in Taipei as he had planned? B: His flight had a four-hour delay because of a typhoon near Hong Kong, so he landed after lunch and joined the afternoon session by video call from the airport.","t":"A：為什麼羅培茲先生沒有如原本計畫參加我們台北辦公室的早上會議？ B：他的班機因為香港附近的颱風【延誤】了四個小時，所以他午餐後才降落，並在機場用視訊參加了下午的會議。"},{"w":"cancellation","p":"n.","d":"a decision that something planned will not happen","c":"取消","s":"A: The airline just told us that our flight to Osaka won't leave tonight because of the snowstorm, so what should we do? B: Go to the service desk right away, because after a cancellation like this, the airline must offer you a seat on the next flight and a free hotel room.","t":"A：航空公司剛告訴我們，因為暴風雪，我們飛往大阪的班機今晚不會起飛，我們該怎麼辦？ B：馬上去服務櫃台，因為發生像這樣的【取消】後，航空公司必須提供你下一班飛機的座位和免費的飯店房間。"},{"w":"passport","p":"n.","d":"an official document that shows who you are and allows you to travel to other countries","c":"護照","s":"A: The company wants me to attend a trade fair in Germany next month, but I haven't traveled abroad for over ten years. B: Then check your passport today, because it may have expired, and getting a new one can take two or three weeks during the busy summer season.","t":"A：公司要我下個月去德國參加商展，但我已經十多年沒出國了。 B：那你今天就檢查一下你的【護照】，因為它可能已經過期了，而在忙碌的夏季，申請新的可能要兩、三個星期。"},{"w":"visa","p":"n.","d":"an official document or stamp that allows you to enter or stay in a country","c":"簽證","s":"A: Our new engineer from India is starting work at the Taipei office in March, so has everything been prepared for him? B: Almost everything, but he is still waiting for his work visa, and the human resources department says it should be ready about two weeks before he flies here.","t":"A：我們從印度來的新工程師三月要在台北辦公室上班，所有事情都替他準備好了嗎？ B：幾乎都好了，但他還在等工作【簽證】，人資部說大約在他飛來前兩週就會辦好。"},{"w":"ticket","p":"n.","d":"a piece of paper or electronic document that shows you have paid to travel","c":"票；機票","s":"A: I need to fly to Kaohsiung for a client meeting next Thursday, so should I book the flight myself or ask someone else to do it? B: Please ask the travel coordinator to buy your ticket, because the company gets a special discount, and she also keeps all the receipts for the accounting department.","t":"A：我下週四要飛去高雄和客戶開會，我應該自己訂機票，還是請別人幫忙？ B：請差旅專員幫你買【機票】，因為公司有特別折扣，而且她也會為會計部保留所有收據。"},{"w":"boarding pass","p":"n.phr.","d":"a card or electronic document that allows you to get on a plane","c":"登機證","s":"A: The airline staff at the gate won't let me get on the plane, but I already showed them my passport. B: You also need to show your boarding pass, so open the airline app on your phone, find your trip, and show them the code with your seat number on it.","t":"A：登機門的航空公司人員不讓我上飛機，但我已經給他們看過護照了。 B：你還需要出示你的【登機證】，所以打開手機上的航空公司應用程式，找到你的行程，給他們看有座位號碼的條碼。"},{"w":"aisle","p":"n.","d":"a long narrow space between rows of seats on a plane","c":"走道","s":"A: Would you like me to book a window seat for your long flight to Los Angeles next week? B: No, please get me a seat on the aisle, because I usually drink lots of water on long trips and need to stand up and walk around without asking the other passengers to move.","t":"A：下週你飛洛杉磯的長途航班，要我幫你訂靠窗的座位嗎？ B：不用，請幫我訂靠【走道】的座位，因為我長途旅行時通常會喝很多水，需要站起來走動，不想一直請其他乘客讓開。"},{"w":"overhead","p":"adj.","d":"above your head","c":"頭頂上的；上方的","s":"A: Where should I put my laptop bag and coat after I find my seat on the plane? B: You can put the coat in the overhead bin, but keep the laptop bag under the seat in front of you, because the flight attendants want the space above the seats for larger suitcases.","t":"A：我在飛機上找到座位後，筆電包和外套應該放在哪裡？ B：外套可以放在【頭頂上方的】置物櫃，但筆電包要放在前方座位底下，因為空服員希望座位上方的空間留給較大的行李箱。"},{"w":"carry-on","p":"n.","d":"a small bag that you are allowed to take onto a plane with you","c":"隨身行李","s":"A: Can I bring my large camera bag onto the plane, or do I need to check it at the counter with my suitcase? B: Each passenger can take one carry-on that weighs less than seven kilograms, so you can bring the camera bag if it is light enough to fit those airline rules.","t":"A：我可以把大相機包帶上飛機嗎？還是需要和行李箱一起在櫃台託運？ B：每位乘客可以攜帶一件七公斤以下的【隨身行李】，所以如果相機包夠輕、符合航空公司的規定，你就可以帶上去。"},{"w":"jet lag","p":"n.phr.","d":"a tired feeling after a long flight across different time zones","c":"時差；時差反應","s":"A: You flew back from New York only yesterday, so how are you feeling this morning, and are you ready for the meeting? B: I'm suffering from jet lag, because I woke up at three in the morning and couldn't sleep again, so I'll need lots of coffee to stay awake during the meeting.","t":"A：你昨天才從紐約飛回來，今天早上感覺怎麼樣？準備好開會了嗎？ B：我有【時差】，因為我凌晨三點就醒了，再也睡不著，所以開會時我需要很多咖啡才能保持清醒。"},{"w":"announcement","p":"n.","d":"a public statement giving people information","c":"宣布；廣播；公告","s":"A: Did you hear what the voice just said through the speakers in the waiting area? It was too noisy for me. B: It was an announcement that our flight to Hanoi is ready for boarding, and passengers sitting in rows thirty to forty-five should go to the gate first.","t":"A：你有聽到剛才候機區喇叭說了什麼嗎？太吵了我沒聽清楚。 B：那是一則【廣播】，說我們飛往河內的班機準備登機了，坐在第三十到四十五排的乘客要先到登機門。"},{"w":"queue","p":"n.","d":"a line of people waiting for something","c":"隊伍；行列","s":"A: Why are so many passengers standing near the information desk, and why does everyone look so angry? B: There is a long queue of travelers waiting to change their tickets, because three flights were canceled this morning due to fog, and only two staff members are working at the desk.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多乘客站在服務台附近，而且大家看起來都那麼生氣？ B：有一長串旅客在【排隊】等著換票，因為今天早上有三個航班因大霧取消，而服務台只有兩名工作人員。"},{"w":"transfer","p":"n.","d":"moving from one plane or vehicle to another during a trip","c":"轉機；轉乘；接駁","s":"A: I have to fly from Taipei to Toronto for the conference next month, but there is no direct flight. B: You can take the flight with a transfer in Vancouver, because you only wait two hours there, and your suitcase will go directly to Toronto without you collecting it.","t":"A：下個月我要從台北飛多倫多參加研討會，但沒有直飛班機。 B：你可以搭在溫哥華【轉機】的班機，因為在那裡只要等兩個小時，而且你的行李箱會直接送到多倫多，不用自己領取。"},{"w":"connection","p":"n.","d":"a plane, train, or bus that you take after getting off another one","c":"轉乘班機；銜接的交通工具","s":"A: Our first flight from Taipei is already thirty minutes late, so will we still be able to catch the flight to Paris in Dubai? B: I'm worried that we might miss our connection, because there is only one hour between the two flights, and the airport in Dubai is very large.","t":"A：我們從台北起飛的第一班飛機已經誤點三十分鐘了，我們還趕得上在杜拜飛往巴黎的班機嗎？ B：我擔心我們會錯過【轉機班機】，因為兩個航班之間只有一個小時，而杜拜機場又非常大。"},{"w":"screening","p":"n.","d":"the process of checking people or bags for dangerous items","c":"篩檢；檢查；安全檢查","s":"A: Why did the airport ask all international passengers to arrive three hours early this week? B: The government added extra screening of passengers and bags after some new safety rules started on Monday, so every person now goes through two machines before reaching the gates.","t":"A：為什麼機場這週要求所有國際線旅客提早三個小時到？ B：週一開始實施一些新的安全規定後，政府對旅客和行李增加了額外的【檢查】，所以現在每個人到登機門前都要通過兩台機器。"},{"w":"taxi","p":"v.","d":"(of a plane) to move slowly along the ground before taking off or after landing","c":"（飛機）滑行","s":"A: We landed ten minutes ago, so why are we still sitting on the plane and not at the gate yet? B: The airport is very busy this morning, so the plane has to taxi slowly across the airfield and wait for another aircraft to leave our gate before we can get off.","t":"A：我們十分鐘前就降落了，為什麼還坐在飛機上、還沒到登機門？ B：今天早上機場很忙，所以飛機必須在機坪上緩慢【滑行】，並等另一架飛機離開我們的登機門後，我們才能下機。"},{"w":"depart","p":"v.","d":"to leave a place, especially to start a journey","c":"出發；離開；起飛","s":"A: Is the last flight to Hualien tonight still on schedule, or has it been affected by the strong winds along the coast? B: It is scheduled to depart at eight forty-five, but the airline says it will send passengers a message within the next hour if the weather becomes too dangerous.","t":"A：今晚飛往花蓮的最後一班飛機還照常嗎？還是受到沿海強風的影響？ B：預定八點四十五分【起飛】，但航空公司說如果天氣變得太危險，會在接下來一小時內傳訊息通知乘客。"},{"w":"arrive","p":"v.","d":"to reach a place at the end of a journey","c":"到達；抵達","s":"A: How early should international passengers get to Taoyuan Airport before their flights during the holiday season? B: The airport suggests that they arrive at least three hours before their flight, because the check-in lines and security checks are much slower when so many families are traveling.","t":"A：在假期期間，國際線旅客應該在班機起飛前多早到桃園機場？ B：機場建議他們至少在起飛前三小時【抵達】，因為有這麼多家庭出遊時，報到的隊伍和安檢都會慢很多。"},{"w":"securely","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is firmly fixed or safely protected","c":"牢固地；安全地","s":"A: The plane is shaking a lot, and the seatbelt sign just came on, so is there anything I should do right now? B: Make sure your seatbelt is fastened securely around your waist, and put your hot coffee on the floor so that it doesn't spill on you or the passenger next to you.","t":"A：飛機晃得很厲害，安全帶指示燈剛剛亮了，我現在有什麼該做的嗎？ B：確定你的安全帶有【牢牢地】繫在腰上，並把熱咖啡放到地上，以免灑到你或你旁邊的乘客。"},{"w":"onboard","p":"adj.","d":"available or happening on a plane, ship, or train","c":"機上的；船上的；車上的","s":"A: It's a twelve-hour flight to Amsterdam, so how will you keep busy during the trip if you don't want to work? B: The airline has a great onboard entertainment system with hundreds of films and music albums, so I plan to watch a few movies and then sleep for several hours.","t":"A：飛阿姆斯特丹要十二個小時，如果你不想工作，旅途中要怎麼打發時間？ B：這家航空公司有很棒的【機上】娛樂系統，有數百部電影和音樂專輯，所以我打算看幾部電影，然後睡幾個小時。"}]},{"unit":11,"theme":"Alone 獨處","cards":[{"w":"socialize","p":"v.","d":"to spend time with other people in a friendly way","c":"交際；社交；與人往來","s":"A: Why does the company organize a dinner party for all the staff every three months, even though it costs quite a lot of money? B: The managers want employees from different departments to socialize outside the office, because people who know each other well usually communicate better and solve problems faster at work.","t":"A：為什麼公司每三個月都為全體員工舉辦晚餐派對，即使花費相當多？ B：主管們希望不同部門的員工能在辦公室以外【交流往來】，因為彼此熟悉的人在工作上通常溝通得更好，解決問題也更快。"},{"w":"social life","p":"n.phr.","d":"the time you spend with friends and doing activities for fun","c":"社交生活","s":"A: You've been working until ten o'clock every night since you got promoted, so do you still have time to see your friends? B: Not really, my social life has almost disappeared, so I've decided to leave the office by seven at least three days a week and join my friends for dinner.","t":"A：你升職後每天都工作到晚上十點，還有時間見朋友嗎？ B：其實沒有，我的【社交生活】幾乎消失了，所以我決定每週至少三天七點前下班，和朋友一起吃晚餐。"},{"w":"solitude","p":"n.","d":"the state of being alone, especially when you enjoy it","c":"獨處；孤獨（多指享受的）","s":"A: Why does the writer rent a small cabin in the mountains every winter instead of working from her apartment in the city? B: She needs complete solitude to finish her novels, because there are no phone calls, visitors, or traffic noise there, so she can focus on writing for ten hours a day.","t":"A：為什麼那位作家每年冬天都在山上租一間小木屋，而不在城裡的公寓工作？ B：她需要完全的【獨處】才能完成小說，因為那裡沒有電話、訪客或車聲，她可以一天專心寫作十個小時。"},{"w":"solitary","p":"adj.","d":"done alone or existing alone","c":"單獨的；獨自的；孤獨的","s":"A: You used to love working with large teams, so why did you accept a job as a night guard at the museum? B: I actually enjoy solitary work at this stage of my life, because I can read during quiet hours, and I don't have to attend long meetings or deal with office politics.","t":"A：你以前很喜歡和大團隊一起工作，為什麼接受了博物館夜間警衛的工作？ B：在人生的這個階段，我其實很享受【獨自一人的】工作，因為安靜的時候我可以看書，而且不用參加冗長的會議或應付辦公室政治。"},{"w":"self-reliant","p":"adj.","d":"able to do things and make decisions without help from others","c":"自立的；依靠自己的","s":"A: Your son moved to Australia for university last year, so how is he managing without his family nearby? B: He has become very self-reliant, because he cooks his own meals, works part-time at a café to pay his rent, and solves most of his problems without calling us for help.","t":"A：你兒子去年去澳洲念大學，家人不在身邊，他過得怎麼樣？ B：他變得非常【自立】，因為他自己煮飯、在咖啡館兼職付房租，大部分的問題都自己解決，不會打電話向我們求助。"},{"w":"recharge","p":"v.","d":"to rest so that you get your energy back","c":"恢復精力；充電","s":"A: Why do you always spend your lunch break walking alone in the park instead of eating with the team? B: I talk to customers on the phone all morning, so I need some quiet time to recharge, and a short walk helps me feel fresh and focused for the busy afternoon.","t":"A：為什麼你午休總是獨自在公園散步，而不和團隊一起吃飯？ B：我整個早上都在和顧客講電話，所以需要一些安靜的時間來【恢復精力】，短暫的散步能讓我在忙碌的下午感到清新又專注。"},{"w":"reflect","p":"v.","d":"to think carefully and seriously about something","c":"反思；深思","s":"A: Why did the manager give everyone a notebook at the end of the long project and ask us to write in it? B: She wants each of us to reflect on what went well and what went wrong, so that we can avoid the same problems when we start the next project in January.","t":"A：為什麼經理在漫長的專案結束時發給每個人一本筆記本，要我們在上面寫東西？ B：她希望我們每個人【反思】哪些地方做得好、哪些地方出了錯，好讓我們一月開始下一個專案時，能避免同樣的問題。"},{"w":"relax","p":"v.","d":"to rest and become calm, especially after work","c":"放鬆；休息","s":"A: You look really tired after such a busy week at the trade fair, so what are your plans for the weekend? B: I'm going to stay home, turn off my phone, and just relax with a good book and some music, because I need to rest before the next sales trip on Monday.","t":"A：在商展忙了這麼一整週，你看起來好累，週末有什麼計畫？ B：我要待在家、關掉手機，就看本好書、聽點音樂【放鬆】一下，因為在週一下一趟業務出差前，我需要休息。"},{"w":"relief","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of happiness because something unpleasant has ended or not happened","c":"寬慰；鬆了一口氣","s":"A: How did you feel when the client finally called and said they had approved our design, after making us change it five times? B: It was a huge relief, because the whole team had worked every weekend for a month, and we were worried that we might lose the contract.","t":"A：在客戶要我們修改五次設計後，終於打電話來說核准了，你有什麼感覺？ B：真是大大【鬆了一口氣】，因為整個團隊一個月來每個週末都在工作，我們很擔心可能會失去這份合約。"},{"w":"peaceful","p":"adj.","d":"quiet and calm, without noise or trouble","c":"寧靜的；平和的","s":"A: Why did you choose that small hotel by the lake instead of the big one near the conference center? B: The big hotel is always full of noisy tour groups, but the lake hotel is so peaceful that I can sleep well and prepare for my presentations without any distractions.","t":"A：為什麼你選擇湖邊那間小飯店，而不選會議中心附近的大飯店？ B：大飯店總是擠滿吵鬧的旅行團，但湖邊的飯店非常【寧靜】，我可以睡得很好，並在沒有任何干擾的情況下準備簡報。"},{"w":"release","p":"v.","d":"to let a feeling or energy go so that you feel better","c":"釋放；發洩","s":"A: Why does the company now offer free boxing classes in the gym after work on Tuesdays and Thursdays? B: Many employees said they feel tense after long days at their desks, and hitting a punching bag helps them release stress in a healthy way before they go home.","t":"A：為什麼公司現在每週二和週四下班後在健身房提供免費拳擊課？ B：許多員工說，在辦公桌前坐了一整天後感覺很緊繃，打沙包能幫助他們在回家前用健康的方式【釋放】壓力。"},{"w":"pressure","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of worry caused by difficult demands or too much work","c":"壓力","s":"A: Why has Kevin been so quiet and tired lately, when he used to be the most cheerful person in the office? B: He is under a lot of pressure because he has to finish three big reports before the end of the month, and his manager keeps adding new tasks to his list.","t":"A：凱文以前是辦公室裡最開朗的人，為什麼最近這麼安靜又疲倦？ B：他承受很大的【壓力】，因為他必須在月底前完成三份大型報告，而他的主管還不斷在他的清單上增加新任務。"},{"w":"belong to somebody","p":"v.phr.","d":"to feel that you are an important part of someone's life or a group","c":"歸屬於某人；有歸屬感","s":"A: Why did your elderly neighbor start volunteering at the animal shelter after her husband passed away last year? B: She said that caring for the dogs makes her feel that she still has a purpose and can belong to somebody, because the animals are always so happy to see her each morning.","t":"A：為什麼你年長的鄰居在她先生去年過世後，開始到動物收容所當志工？ B：她說照顧狗狗讓她覺得自己仍有生活目標，並且能【有所歸屬】，因為每天早上動物們見到她總是非常開心。"},{"w":"introvert","p":"n.","d":"a quiet person who prefers to spend time alone or with a few people","c":"內向的人","s":"A: Lisa is one of our best programmers, but she never joins the team lunches or the after-work parties, so is something wrong? B: Nothing is wrong, she's just an introvert, so she prefers to eat quietly at her desk and recharge her energy before the afternoon meetings.","t":"A：麗莎是我們最優秀的程式設計師之一，但她從不參加團隊午餐或下班後的聚會，是出了什麼問題嗎？ B：沒什麼問題，她只是個【內向的人】，所以比較喜歡安靜地在座位上吃飯，在下午的會議前恢復精力。"},{"w":"attractive","p":"adj.","d":"pleasant or interesting, so that people want it","c":"有吸引力的；誘人的","s":"A: Why are so many young professionals choosing to live alone in small studio apartments in the city center? B: Living alone is very attractive to them, because they can decide their own schedules, keep the space exactly how they like it, and walk to work in just ten minutes.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多年輕上班族選擇獨自住在市中心的小套房？ B：獨居對他們來說非常【有吸引力】，因為他們可以自己決定作息、把空間維持成自己喜歡的樣子，而且走路十分鐘就能到公司。"},{"w":"regulate","p":"v.","d":"to control something so that it stays at the right level","c":"調節；控制；管理","s":"A: The new office building has a smart system that turns the heating on and off by itself, so how does it work? B: Sensors in every room regulate the temperature throughout the day, so the building stays comfortable for workers while using about thirty percent less energy than our old office.","t":"A：新辦公大樓有一套會自動開關暖氣的智慧系統，它是怎麼運作的？ B：每個房間的感測器整天都在【調節】溫度，所以大樓能讓員工保持舒適，同時比我們的舊辦公室少用約百分之三十的能源。"},{"w":"emotion","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling such as love, anger, fear, or joy","c":"情緒；情感","s":"A: How did the staff react when the director announced that the company was closing the factory where many of them had worked for years? B: There was a lot of emotion in the room, because some people cried, others were angry, and everyone was worried about finding new jobs.","t":"A：當總監宣布公司要關閉許多員工工作多年的工廠時，員工有什麼反應？ B：會議室裡充滿了【情緒】，因為有些人哭了，有些人很生氣，而且每個人都擔心要找新工作。"},{"w":"avoid","p":"v.","d":"to stay away from someone or something, or to stop something from happening","c":"避免；避開；迴避","s":"A: Why do you always take the earliest train to the office, even though our working day doesn't start until nine? B: I like to avoid the crowds at rush hour, because the trains after eight o'clock are so full that I can't sit down, read, or even think clearly.","t":"A：為什麼你總是搭最早的火車去辦公室，即使我們九點才開始上班？ B：我喜歡【避開】尖峰時段的人潮，因為八點以後的火車擠到我沒辦法坐下、看書，甚至無法好好思考。"},{"w":"scary","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel afraid","c":"可怕的；嚇人的","s":"A: How did you feel when you moved to Berlin alone for your first overseas job, without knowing anyone there? B: It was really scary at first, because I didn't speak German and got lost often, but after a few months I made friends at work and started to enjoy the city.","t":"A：你獨自搬去柏林做第一份海外工作、在那裡一個人都不認識時，有什麼感覺？ B：一開始真的很【可怕】，因為我不會說德語，又常常迷路，但幾個月後我在工作上交了朋友，開始喜歡這座城市了。"},{"w":"wonder","p":"v.","d":"to think about something and want to know more about it","c":"想知道；納悶；好奇","s":"A: The new employee from Canada always eats lunch by herself in the break room and doesn't say much to anyone. B: I wonder whether she feels lonely, so let's invite her to join us for lunch tomorrow and ask her some questions about her life back home.","t":"A：那位從加拿大來的新員工總是自己一個人在休息室吃午餐，也不太和任何人說話。 B：我【想知道】她是否覺得孤單，所以我們明天邀請她和我們一起吃午餐，並問問她在家鄉生活的事吧。"},{"w":"stressful","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel worried and nervous","c":"壓力大的；令人緊張的","s":"A: How was your first month as a manager at the call center, and do you still enjoy the job? B: It has been very stressful, because I have to deal with angry customers, train new staff, and meet sales targets, but I'm learning a lot and starting to feel more confident.","t":"A：你在客服中心當經理的第一個月怎麼樣？你還喜歡這份工作嗎？ B：一直都【壓力很大】，因為我必須應付生氣的顧客、訓練新員工並達成業績目標，但我學到很多，也開始比較有自信了。"},{"w":"triggering","p":"adj.","d":"causing someone to have strong, upsetting feelings or memories","c":"引發情緒反應的；觸發的","s":"A: Why did the company add a short warning before the online safety training video about factory accidents? B: Some scenes in the video show serious injuries, and they could be triggering for workers who have been in accidents before, so the warning allows them to prepare or ask for another format.","t":"A：為什麼公司在關於工廠事故的線上安全訓練影片前加了一段簡短的警語？ B：影片中有些畫面顯示嚴重的傷害，對曾經發生過事故的員工來說可能會【引發強烈情緒】，所以警語讓他們可以做好準備或要求其他形式。"},{"w":"burnout","p":"n.","d":"a state of feeling extremely tired and unable to work because of too much stress","c":"倦怠；身心俱疲","s":"A: Why did the company decide to give all employees an extra week of paid holiday this year? B: Many staff members were working more than sixty hours a week, and the managers wanted to prevent burnout before people became sick or decided to quit their jobs.","t":"A：為什麼公司決定今年給所有員工多一週的帶薪假？ B：許多員工每週工作超過六十小時，主管們想在大家生病或決定辭職之前，預防【過勞倦怠】。"},{"w":"quietly","p":"adv.","d":"without making much noise","c":"安靜地；輕聲地","s":"A: The library on the third floor is the only place in our building where I can concentrate, but people keep chatting there. B: Let's put up a sign asking everyone to talk quietly or go to the café downstairs, because many employees use that room to read and prepare important reports.","t":"A：三樓的圖書室是我們大樓裡唯一能讓我專心的地方，但大家一直在那裡聊天。 B：我們貼一張告示，請大家【輕聲】說話或去樓下咖啡廳，因為很多員工會用那個房間閱讀和準備重要報告。"},{"w":"habit","p":"n.","d":"something that you do often and regularly, often without thinking about it","c":"習慣","s":"A: How do you stay so calm and organized, even when we have five deadlines in the same week? B: I have a habit of spending fifteen minutes alone every morning, planning my tasks with a cup of tea before I open any emails or answer any phone calls.","t":"A：即使我們同一週有五個截止期限，你是怎麼保持這麼冷靜又有條理的？ B：我有一個【習慣】，每天早上會獨自花十五分鐘，在打開任何電子郵件或接任何電話之前，邊喝茶邊規劃我的工作。"},{"w":"bake","p":"v.","d":"to cook food such as bread or cake in an oven","c":"烘烤；烤","s":"A: What do you usually do on Sunday afternoons when you live alone and your family is so far away? B: I like to bake bread and cookies in my small kitchen, because it calms me down after a busy week, and I often bring the extra cookies to the office on Monday.","t":"A：你一個人住、家人又離得那麼遠，週日下午通常都做什麼？ B：我喜歡在我的小廚房裡【烤】麵包和餅乾，因為這能讓我在忙碌的一週後平靜下來，我也常在週一把多的餅乾帶到辦公室。"},{"w":"disturb","p":"v.","d":"to interrupt someone when they are trying to work, sleep, or rest","c":"打擾；干擾","s":"A: I need to finish the budget report for the director by four o'clock, but people keep coming to my desk with questions. B: Book the small meeting room for two hours and put a sign on the door asking people not to disturb you, and I'll answer any questions for you.","t":"A：我必須在四點前完成給總監的預算報告，但一直有人到我座位問問題。 B：預約小會議室兩個小時，在門上貼個告示請大家不要【打擾】你，有任何問題我會幫你回答。"},{"w":"explore","p":"v.","d":"to look around a new place, or to try new activities, to learn about them","c":"探索；嘗試；探究","s":"A: You moved to Tainan alone for this new job two months ago, so how do you spend your free time when you're not working? B: I explore a different neighborhood every weekend, and I've found some wonderful temples, old streets, and food stalls that most tourists never see.","t":"A：你兩個月前為了這份新工作獨自搬到台南，不工作的時候都怎麼打發空閒時間？ B：我每個週末都去【探索】一個不同的街區，已經發現了一些很棒的廟宇、老街和大多數觀光客從沒見過的小吃攤。"},{"w":"bookworm","p":"n.","d":"a person who loves reading and spends a lot of time reading","c":"書蟲；愛看書的人","s":"A: Do you know what we should buy as a farewell gift for Ms. Kim, who is retiring from the accounting department next week? B: She is a real bookworm who reads several novels every month, so a gift card for the big bookstore near her apartment would probably make her very happy.","t":"A：你知道下週從會計部退休的金小姐，我們該買什麼當作送別禮物嗎？ B：她是個真正的【書蟲】，每個月會讀好幾本小說，所以送她公寓附近大型書店的禮券，她大概會很開心。"}]},{"unit":12,"theme":"Ambition 抱負","cards":[{"w":"desire","p":"v.","d":"to want something very much","c":"渴望；想要","s":"A: Why did Mr. Lee leave his well-paid job at the bank last month, even though his manager offered him a promotion and a bigger office? B: He told me he had always wanted to run his own café, and he did not desire a higher position at a company where he felt bored every day.","t":"A：為什麼李先生上個月離開銀行那份高薪工作，即使他的經理提供他升遷和更大的辦公室？ B：他告訴我他一直想經營自己的咖啡店，而且他並不【渴望】在一家每天都讓他覺得無聊的公司裡得到更高的職位。"},{"w":"determination","p":"n.","d":"a strong wish to keep trying until you succeed","c":"決心；毅力","s":"A: How did Sarah finish her MBA while working full-time at the marketing agency and taking care of her two young children? B: She studied late every night after the kids went to bed, and her determination to get a management role helped her pass every exam, even when she felt very tired.","t":"A：莎拉是怎麼在行銷公司全職工作、還要照顧兩個年幼孩子的同時完成企管碩士學位的？ B：她每天晚上等孩子睡了之後讀書讀到很晚，而她想取得管理職位的【決心】幫助她通過了每一場考試，即使她覺得非常疲累。"},{"w":"improve","p":"v.","d":"to make something better","c":"改善；提升","s":"A: Our team leader said the customer survey results were disappointing this quarter, so what is the plan for the next three months? B: We are going to give all the call center staff extra training, because we really need to improve our service quality before the important contract with the hotel chain is renewed.","t":"A：我們的組長說這一季的顧客調查結果令人失望，那接下來三個月的計畫是什麼？ B：我們要給所有客服中心的員工額外的訓練，因為在和連鎖飯店的重要合約續約之前，我們真的需要【改善】我們的服務品質。"},{"w":"achieve","p":"v.","d":"to succeed in reaching a goal","c":"達成；實現","s":"A: Do you think the sales department can reach its target of one million dollars by the end of the year, even with the new competitor in town? B: I think we can achieve it if everyone keeps visiting new clients and the marketing team launches the holiday campaign on time next month.","t":"A：你覺得即使鎮上出現了新的競爭對手，業務部門還是能在年底前達到一百萬美元的目標嗎？ B：我認為如果每個人都持續拜訪新客戶，而且行銷團隊下個月準時推出節慶活動，我們就能【達成】它。"},{"w":"realize","p":"v.","d":"to make a hope or plan really happen","c":"實現（夢想、計畫）；了解","s":"A: I heard you finally opened your own design studio downtown, so how does it feel after dreaming about it for so many years? B: It feels wonderful, because I saved money for ten years and took business classes at night, and now I can finally realize my dream of working for myself.","t":"A：我聽說你終於在市中心開了自己的設計工作室，夢想了這麼多年，現在感覺如何？ B：感覺很棒，因為我存了十年的錢，晚上還去上商業課程，現在我終於可以【實現】自己當老闆的夢想了。"},{"w":"skip","p":"v.","d":"to not do something you usually do","c":"略過；不做","s":"A: You look exhausted this morning, so did you stay at the office late again to prepare the slides for the investors' meeting? B: Yes, I worked until midnight, and I had to skip lunch and dinner yesterday because I want this project to succeed and help me get promoted next year.","t":"A：你今天早上看起來累壞了，你昨天又為了準備投資人會議的簡報留在辦公室到很晚嗎？ B：對，我工作到半夜，昨天還不得不【略過】午餐和晚餐，因為我希望這個專案成功，幫助我明年獲得升遷。"},{"w":"distracted","p":"adj.","d":"not able to pay attention to what you are doing","c":"分心的","s":"A: Why did James make so many mistakes in the monthly budget report that he sent to the finance director on Friday afternoon? B: He was distracted because his phone kept ringing with calls about his new apartment, and he could not focus on the numbers while he was worrying about moving.","t":"A：為什麼詹姆士週五下午寄給財務長的月度預算報告裡有那麼多錯誤？ B：他【分心】了，因為他的手機一直響，都是關於他新公寓的電話，而他在擔心搬家的時候沒辦法專注在數字上。"},{"w":"dull","p":"adj.","d":"boring; not interesting","c":"乏味的；單調的","s":"A: Why did Kevin decide to leave the accounting department and apply for a position on the sales team last month? B: He said his daily work was dull because he entered the same kind of data every day, and he wanted a more exciting job where he could travel and meet new people.","t":"A：為什麼凱文上個月決定離開會計部門，去應徵業務團隊的職位？ B：他說他每天的工作很【乏味】，因為他每天都在輸入同一類的資料，而他想要一份更刺激、可以出差和認識新朋友的工作。"},{"w":"standstill","p":"n.","d":"a situation where nothing moves or makes progress","c":"停頓；停滯","s":"A: What happened with the plan to build the new shopping mall next to the train station, which was supposed to open next spring? B: The project has come to a standstill because the city has not approved the final design yet, so the builders are waiting and nobody knows when work will start again.","t":"A：原本預計明年春天開幕、蓋在火車站旁的新購物中心，計畫後來怎麼樣了？ B：這個專案已經陷入【停頓】，因為市政府還沒有核准最終設計，所以營建商都在等待，也沒有人知道工程什麼時候會再開始。"},{"w":"ignore","p":"v.","d":"to pay no attention to someone or something","c":"忽視；不理會","s":"A: Did the manager listen to your suggestions about the new schedule, or did she decide to keep the old system for the warehouse staff? B: Unfortunately, she decided to ignore my ideas at the meeting, but I will write a detailed report with numbers so she can see how much time we could save.","t":"A：經理有聽你對新班表的建議嗎？還是她決定讓倉庫員工維持舊制度？ B：很可惜，她在會議上決定【忽視】我的想法，但我會寫一份附有數據的詳細報告，讓她看看我們可以節省多少時間。"},{"w":"arrange","p":"v.","d":"to plan or organize something","c":"安排","s":"A: I am interested in learning more about the leadership training program, but I am not sure whom I should contact about it. B: You should talk to Ms. Chen in Human Resources, because she can arrange a meeting with the program director for you next week and explain how to apply before the deadline.","t":"A：我有興趣多了解領導力培訓課程，但我不確定該聯絡誰。 B：你應該去找人資部的陳小姐，因為她可以幫你【安排】下週和課程主任開會，並向你說明如何在截止日期前申請。"},{"w":"uncertain","p":"adj.","d":"not sure about something","c":"不確定的","s":"A: Are you going to accept the job offer from the company in Singapore, or will you stay here in Taipei with your current team? B: I am still uncertain about it, because the salary is much higher, but I would have to move far away from my family and learn a whole new market.","t":"A：你會接受新加坡那家公司的工作邀約，還是會留在台北和你現在的團隊一起？ B：我對這件事還【不確定】，因為薪水高很多，但我必須搬到離家人很遠的地方，還要學習一個全新的市場。"},{"w":"unpredictable","p":"adj.","d":"changing in a way that is hard to know before","c":"難以預測的","s":"A: Why does the restaurant need so many part-time workers on the weekend schedule when some evenings are very quiet? B: The number of customers is very unpredictable on Saturdays and Sundays, so the manager prefers to have extra staff ready in case a large tour group suddenly walks in.","t":"A：為什麼有些晚上很冷清，餐廳週末的班表卻需要那麼多兼職人員？ B：週六和週日的客人數量非常【難以預測】，所以經理寧願多準備一些人手，以防大型旅行團突然上門。"},{"w":"involvement","p":"n.","d":"the act of taking part in something","c":"參與；涉入","s":"A: Why did the company choose Linda to lead the new community project instead of someone with more experience in marketing? B: Her involvement in several charity events over the past three years showed the directors that she works well with volunteers and really cares about helping local families.","t":"A：為什麼公司選琳達帶領新的社區專案，而不是選一個行銷經驗更豐富的人？ B：她過去三年【參與】了好幾場慈善活動，讓董事們看到她很擅長和志工合作，而且真心在乎幫助當地家庭。"},{"w":"mandatory","p":"adj.","d":"required by a rule","c":"強制的；義務的","s":"A: Do all the new employees have to attend the safety workshop on Monday morning, or can some of them join the online version later? B: The workshop is mandatory for everyone who works in the factory, so please tell your team to arrive at eight o'clock and bring their ID cards with them.","t":"A：所有新進員工都必須參加週一早上的安全講習嗎？還是有些人可以之後再參加線上版？ B：這場講習對所有在工廠工作的人來說都是【強制性的】，所以請告訴你的團隊八點到場，並帶上他們的識別證。"},{"w":"path","p":"n.","d":"a way of living or a direction in your career","c":"道路；途徑","s":"A: My younger brother just graduated from university, and he cannot decide whether to work in finance or become a teacher. B: Tell him to try a few internships first, because it takes time to find the right career path, and real work experience will show him what he enjoys doing every day.","t":"A：我弟弟剛從大學畢業，他無法決定要從事金融業還是當老師。 B：告訴他先試試幾份實習，因為要找到對的職涯【道路】需要時間，而真正的工作經驗會讓他知道自己每天喜歡做什麼。"},{"w":"renowned","p":"adj.","d":"famous and respected","c":"著名的；有名望的","s":"A: Why is the hotel ballroom so full tonight, when the business dinner usually has only about fifty guests? B: A renowned chef from Paris is cooking the main course this evening, so many local business owners bought tickets because they wanted to taste his food and meet him in person.","t":"A：為什麼今晚飯店宴會廳這麼滿，而商務晚宴平常只有大約五十位賓客？ B：今晚有一位來自巴黎的【知名】主廚料理主菜，所以很多當地企業老闆都買了票，因為他們想品嚐他的料理並親自見到他。"},{"w":"initiation","p":"n.","d":"the start of a plan or process","c":"開始；啟動；入會","s":"A: When did the new training program for junior managers officially begin, and has it helped the staff so far? B: Since its initiation in January, more than forty employees have joined the program, and many of them say they now feel more confident when they lead meetings and give feedback.","t":"A：給初階主管的新培訓計畫是什麼時候正式開始的？到目前為止對員工有幫助嗎？ B：自從一月【開始實施】以來，已經有四十多名員工參加了這個計畫，其中許多人說他們現在主持會議和給予回饋時更有自信了。"},{"w":"fulfilling","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel happy and satisfied","c":"令人有成就感的；令人滿足的","s":"A: You used to earn a lot more at the law firm, so why did you decide to work for a small charity that helps older people? B: The pay is lower, but the work is much more fulfilling because I can see how my daily efforts make a real difference in people's lives.","t":"A：你以前在律師事務所賺得多很多，為什麼決定到一個幫助長者的小型慈善機構工作？ B：薪水是比較低，但這份工作讓人更有【成就感】，因為我可以看到自己每天的努力真正改變了人們的生活。"},{"w":"frustrated","p":"adj.","d":"upset because you cannot do or change something","c":"挫折的；沮喪的","s":"A: Why did Tom look so upset when he left the meeting with the IT department this afternoon? B: He feels frustrated because he has asked them three times to fix the computer system, but they keep saying they are too busy, so his team still cannot process customer orders quickly.","t":"A：為什麼湯姆今天下午和資訊部開完會離開時看起來那麼不高興？ B：他覺得很【挫折】，因為他已經要求他們修電腦系統三次了，但他們一直說太忙，所以他的團隊還是沒辦法快速處理顧客的訂單。"},{"w":"immense","p":"adj.","d":"very large","c":"巨大的；極大的","s":"A: How did the new product launch go last weekend, and were there many visitors at the company's booth at the trade fair? B: It was an immense success, because thousands of people visited our booth over two days, and we received more orders than we had expected for the whole month.","t":"A：上週末的新產品發表會進行得怎麼樣？公司在商展的攤位有很多訪客嗎？ B：那是一次【巨大的】成功，因為兩天內有數千人參觀我們的攤位，而我們收到的訂單比原本預期整個月的還要多。"},{"w":"possibility","p":"n.","d":"something that might happen or be true","c":"可能性","s":"A: Do you think the company will open a branch office in Tokyo next year, since our sales in Japan have grown so quickly? B: There is a strong possibility that it will happen, because the board discussed it last week, but they still need to find the right location and hire local staff.","t":"A：既然我們在日本的銷售成長得這麼快，你覺得公司明年會在東京開設分公司嗎？ B：這件事很有【可能】發生，因為董事會上週討論過了，但他們還需要找到合適的地點並僱用當地員工。"},{"w":"impressive","p":"adj.","d":"so good that people admire it","c":"令人印象深刻的","s":"A: Did you read the résumé from the woman who applied for the marketing manager position, and what did you think of her experience? B: Yes, her background is very impressive, since she has worked for two international companies and led a team that doubled online sales in only one year.","t":"A：你讀過那位應徵行銷經理職位女士的履歷了嗎？你覺得她的經歷如何？ B：讀過了，她的背景非常【令人印象深刻】，因為她曾在兩家跨國公司工作，還帶領團隊在短短一年內讓線上銷售翻倍。"},{"w":"decent","p":"adj.","d":"good enough; acceptable","c":"還不錯的；像樣的","s":"A: Are you happy with the new job at the logistics company, or are you still looking for something better in the city? B: I am quite happy, because the company pays a decent salary and gives good benefits, and my manager has promised to send me to training courses next year.","t":"A：你對物流公司的新工作滿意嗎？還是你還在城裡找更好的工作？ B：我蠻滿意的，因為公司給的薪水【還不錯】，福利也很好，而且我的主管答應明年會送我去上培訓課程。"},{"w":"dedication","p":"n.","d":"hard work and loyalty to a job or goal","c":"奉獻；投入","s":"A: Why is the CEO giving Ms. Wang a special award at the annual dinner, when she is not a manager or a director? B: She has worked here for twenty-five years and never missed a deadline, so the award is to thank her for her dedication to the company and its customers.","t":"A：為什麼執行長要在年度晚宴上頒特別獎給王小姐，而她既不是經理也不是主管？ B：她在這裡工作了二十五年，從來沒錯過任何截止期限，所以這個獎是為了感謝她對公司和顧客的【奉獻】。"},{"w":"vital","p":"adj.","d":"very important; necessary","c":"極為重要的；必要的","s":"A: Should I spend more time on the slides or on practicing my speech before tomorrow's presentation to the new clients from Korea? B: Practicing is vital, because the clients will judge you by how clearly and confidently you speak, and nice slides will not help if you cannot answer their questions.","t":"A：明天要向來自韓國的新客戶做簡報，在那之前我應該多花時間做投影片還是練習演講？ B：練習是【極為重要的】，因為客戶會根據你說話有多清楚、多有自信來評價你，如果你回答不了他們的問題，漂亮的投影片也沒有用。"},{"w":"fascination","p":"n.","d":"a very strong interest in something","c":"著迷；強烈的興趣","s":"A: How did Maria end up working as an engineer for an airline company after studying history at university? B: She has had a fascination with airplanes since she was a little girl, so after graduation she took night classes in engineering and finally got the job she always dreamed of.","t":"A：瑪莉亞大學念的是歷史，最後怎麼會在航空公司當工程師？ B：她從小就對飛機非常【著迷】，所以畢業後她去上工程的夜間課程，終於得到了她一直夢想的工作。"},{"w":"prospect","p":"n.","d":"the chance that something good will happen in the future","c":"前景；可能性","s":"A: Why are so many young people applying for jobs at the new electric car factory outside the city this year? B: The company offers good training, and the prospect of getting promoted quickly is attractive to graduates who want to build a long career in a growing industry.","t":"A：為什麼今年有這麼多年輕人去應徵城外那間新電動車工廠的工作？ B：這家公司提供很好的訓練，而且快速升遷的【前景】對想在成長產業中長久發展的畢業生很有吸引力。"},{"w":"astonishing","p":"adj.","d":"very surprising","c":"驚人的；令人驚訝的","s":"A: Did you hear that the small startup down the street was bought by a huge technology company for fifty million dollars? B: Yes, it is astonishing news, because the company only started two years ago in a tiny office with three employees, and now everyone in the industry is talking about it.","t":"A：你聽說街上那家小型新創公司被一家大型科技公司以五千萬美元收購了嗎？ B：聽說了，這真是【驚人的】消息，因為那家公司兩年前才在一間小辦公室裡由三名員工創立，現在業界每個人都在談論它。"},{"w":"facility","p":"n.","d":"a building or place used for a special purpose","c":"設施；場所","s":"A: Where will the new employees from the overseas office receive their technical training when they arrive next month? B: They will stay at the company's training facility in Hsinchu, which has modern classrooms, a lab, and a small hotel, so they will not need to travel every day.","t":"A：海外辦公室的新進員工下個月抵達後，會在哪裡接受技術訓練？ B：他們會待在公司位於新竹的訓練【設施】，那裡有現代化的教室、實驗室和一間小旅館，所以他們不需要每天通勤。"},{"w":"aspiration","p":"n.","d":"a strong hope to achieve something","c":"抱負；志向","s":"A: During your job interview, what did you tell the manager when she asked about your goals for the next five years? B: I told her that my aspiration is to become a team leader, so I plan to take management courses and learn as much as I can from experienced colleagues.","t":"A：在你的工作面試中，當經理問你未來五年的目標時，你怎麼回答？ B：我告訴她我的【抱負】是成為團隊領導人，所以我打算去上管理課程，並盡可能向有經驗的同事學習。"},{"w":"contribute","p":"v.","d":"to give money, help, or ideas","c":"貢獻；捐助","s":"A: Our department is collecting money for the new library at the children's hospital, so would you like to join us this month? B: Of course, I would be glad to contribute some money, and I can also ask my friends at the bank if they want to help with books and toys.","t":"A：我們部門正在為兒童醫院的新圖書室募款，你這個月想加入我們嗎？ B：當然，我很樂意【捐】一些錢，我也可以問問我在銀行的朋友，看他們是否想幫忙提供書籍和玩具。"}]},{"unit":13,"theme":"Animal 動物","cards":[{"w":"appreciate","p":"v.","d":"to understand the value of something and be thankful for it","c":"欣賞；感激","s":"A: How did the volunteers from our office feel after spending the whole Saturday cleaning up the city animal shelter last weekend? B: They were tired but happy, and the shelter manager said she really wanted to appreciate their hard work, so she sent each of them a thank-you card with a photo of the dogs.","t":"A：我們辦公室的志工上週末花了整個星期六打掃市立動物收容所，之後他們感覺如何？ B：他們很累但很開心，收容所經理說她非常想【感謝】他們的辛勞，所以她寄給每個人一張附有狗狗照片的感謝卡。"},{"w":"stand out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be easy to see or notice because it is different or better","c":"突出；脫穎而出","s":"A: Why did the pet food company choose that small design agency for its new advertising campaign instead of the big firm in the city? B: The agency's poster showed a sleepy cat sitting inside a coffee cup, and the bright, funny picture made their idea stand out from all the other proposals the marketing team received.","t":"A：為什麼那家寵物食品公司的新廣告活動選了那間小型設計公司，而不是城裡的大公司？ B：那間公司的海報畫了一隻坐在咖啡杯裡打瞌睡的貓，這張明亮又有趣的圖讓他們的點子在行銷團隊收到的所有提案中【脫穎而出】。"},{"w":"creation","p":"n.","d":"the act of making something new, or the new thing that is made","c":"創造；創建；作品","s":"A: What is the main goal of the new project that the city council and the local zoo announced at the press conference yesterday afternoon? B: They are planning the creation of a large wildlife park outside town, which will protect rare birds, provide about two hundred jobs, and attract more tourists to the area.","t":"A：市議會和當地動物園昨天下午在記者會上宣布的新計畫，主要目標是什麼？ B：他們正在規劃在城外【創建】一座大型野生動物園，它將保護稀有鳥類、提供大約兩百個工作機會，並吸引更多觀光客來到這個地區。"},{"w":"special","p":"adj.","d":"different from usual and better or more important","c":"特別的；特殊的","s":"A: Is it true that the hotel downtown now allows guests to bring their dogs, even though pets were not permitted there in the past? B: Yes, they opened a special floor for pet owners last month, with wooden floors, dog beds, and a small garden, and the rooms are fully booked every weekend.","t":"A：市中心那家飯店現在真的允許房客帶狗入住嗎？過去那裡是不准帶寵物的。 B：是的，他們上個月為飼主開放了一個【特別的】樓層，有木頭地板、狗床和一座小花園，而且每個週末房間都被訂滿。"},{"w":"emotional","p":"adj.","d":"having or showing strong feelings","c":"情感的；情緒激動的","s":"A: Why did Mr. Lin leave the meeting early, and why did he look so upset when he returned to his desk this afternoon? B: His family's old dog died this morning after fifteen years together, so he felt very emotional and needed a few minutes alone before he could talk to the clients again.","t":"A：林先生為什麼提早離開會議？他今天下午回到座位時為什麼看起來那麼難過？ B：他家那隻陪伴了十五年的老狗今天早上過世了，所以他的情緒非常【激動】，需要獨處幾分鐘才能再和客戶談話。"},{"w":"connection","p":"n.","d":"a relationship or link between people, animals or things","c":"連結；關係","s":"A: Why does the hospital let trained dogs visit the patients in the children's ward every Wednesday afternoon? B: The doctors found that the kids feel calmer and less lonely when they build a connection with a friendly animal, and many of them also eat better and sleep longer after the visits.","t":"A：為什麼醫院每週三下午讓受過訓練的狗去探訪兒童病房的病人？ B：醫生們發現，孩子們和友善的動物建立【連結】時，會覺得比較平靜、比較不孤單，而且很多孩子在探訪後也吃得更好、睡得更久。"},{"w":"dedicated to something","p":"adj.phr.","d":"giving a lot of time and energy to one thing because you care about it","c":"致力於某事；全心投入某事","s":"A: What kind of person are you looking for to manage the new animal rescue center that the company is sponsoring next year? B: We need someone who is dedicated to something they truly believe in, because the job has long hours and low pay, and the manager must keep working hard even on difficult days.","t":"A：你們在找什麼樣的人來管理公司明年要贊助的新動物救援中心？ B：我們需要一個【全心投入】自己真心相信之事的人，因為這份工作工時長、薪水低，即使在辛苦的日子，管理者也必須持續努力。"},{"w":"come across somebody","p":"v.phr.","d":"to meet or find someone by chance","c":"偶然遇見某人","s":"A: How did you find such an experienced dog trainer for the security team at the warehouse so quickly last month? B: I was walking in the park on Sunday morning when I happened to come across somebody who was training three police dogs, so I asked for her business card and invited her for an interview.","t":"A：上個月你是怎麼這麼快就為倉庫保全團隊找到一位經驗這麼豐富的訓犬師？ B：星期天早上我在公園散步時，碰巧【遇見一個人】正在訓練三隻警犬，所以我向她要了名片，並邀請她來面試。"},{"w":"husky","p":"n.","d":"a strong dog with thick fur that can pull sleds over snow","c":"哈士奇；雪橇犬","s":"A: Have you decided which photo to use on the front page of our winter travel brochure for the trip to northern Canada? B: Yes, the design team picked a picture of a beautiful husky pulling a sled across the snow, because it shows the adventure and excitement that our customers are looking for.","t":"A：你決定好我們加拿大北部旅遊行程的冬季旅遊手冊封面要用哪張照片了嗎？ B：決定了，設計團隊選了一張美麗的【哈士奇】拉著雪橇穿越雪地的照片，因為它呈現出顧客想要的冒險與刺激感。"},{"w":"infeasible","p":"adj.","d":"not possible to do in practice","c":"不可行的","s":"A: Why did the board reject the plan to build a large pet hotel on the empty land next to our shopping mall? B: The engineers reported that the land is too wet and the building costs would be far too high, so the whole project was judged infeasible and the board voted against it.","t":"A：董事會為什麼否決在我們購物中心旁邊空地蓋一間大型寵物旅館的計畫？ B：工程師報告說那塊地太潮濕，建築成本也會高出太多，所以整個計畫被判定為【不可行】，董事會因此投票反對。"},{"w":"child-friendly","p":"adj.","d":"suitable and safe for children","c":"適合兒童的；對兒童友善的","s":"A: Which restaurant should we book for the company family day, since many employees are bringing their young kids this year? B: Let's choose the farm café near the river, because it is very child-friendly, with a small petting zoo, a safe play area, and a special menu for kids under ten.","t":"A：今年很多員工會帶小孩來，公司家庭日我們應該訂哪家餐廳？ B：我們選河邊那家農場咖啡廳吧，因為它非常【適合兒童】，有一個小型動物觸摸區、安全的遊戲區，還有給十歲以下孩子的特別菜單。"},{"w":"fatal","p":"adj.","d":"causing death","c":"致命的","s":"A: Why did the farm owner call the vet so early this morning, and why are all the workers wearing masks and gloves today? B: A few of the chickens became sick overnight, and the vet warned that the disease can be fatal to birds if it spreads, so everyone must follow strict safety rules.","t":"A：農場主人今天一大早為什麼打電話給獸醫？為什麼今天所有工人都戴著口罩和手套？ B：有幾隻雞一夜之間生病了，獸醫警告說這種疾病如果擴散，對鳥類可能是【致命的】，所以大家都必須遵守嚴格的安全規定。"},{"w":"dread to think","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be afraid to imagine something bad that might happen","c":"不敢想像","s":"A: Did you hear that the security guard found a large snake in the storage room just before the school children arrived for their factory tour? B: Yes, luckily he caught it and called the animal control office, but I dread to think what might have happened if one of the kids had opened that door first.","t":"A：你有沒有聽說，就在學童抵達工廠參觀前，保全在儲藏室裡發現了一條大蛇？ B：有，幸好他抓住了牠並打電話給動物管制單位，但我真【不敢想像】如果有個孩子先打開那扇門會發生什麼事。"},{"w":"improvement","p":"n.","d":"a change that makes something better","c":"改善；進步","s":"A: Has the new diet that the zoo started last spring made any difference to the health of the older elephants? B: Yes, the keepers have seen a clear improvement in their weight and energy, and the vet said the animals are now walking longer distances and eating more fresh fruit every day.","t":"A：動物園去年春天開始的新飲食，對年長大象的健康有任何影響嗎？ B：有，飼育員看到牠們的體重和活力都有明顯的【改善】，獸醫也說這些動物現在每天走更遠的距離，也吃更多新鮮水果。"},{"w":"vertical","p":"adj.","d":"standing or pointing straight up","c":"垂直的；直立的","s":"A: How can the pet store fit so many fish tanks and bird houses into such a small shop on the main street? B: The owner installed tall vertical shelves along every wall, so the tanks are stacked from the floor to the ceiling, which saves space and still leaves room for customers to walk around.","t":"A：大街上那間寵物店那麼小，怎麼放得下那麼多魚缸和鳥屋？ B：老闆沿著每面牆裝了高大的【垂直】層架，所以魚缸從地板一路疊到天花板，既節省空間，又還留有讓顧客走動的空間。"},{"w":"beloved","p":"adj.","d":"loved very much","c":"心愛的；深受喜愛的","s":"A: Why is everyone in the office signing that large card on the reception desk, and who is it for? B: Our manager's beloved cat, which used to visit the office every Friday and sleep on the printer, passed away last night, so we want to show her that we care about her.","t":"A：為什麼辦公室裡每個人都在簽櫃台上那張大卡片？是要給誰的？ B：我們經理【心愛的】貓昨晚過世了，牠以前每個星期五都會來辦公室，睡在印表機上，所以我們想讓她知道我們很關心她。"},{"w":"rear","p":"v.","d":"to care for young animals or children until they are fully grown","c":"飼養；養育","s":"A: What does your cousin do on that large farm in the mountains, since she moved away from the city three years ago? B: She and her husband rear sheep and goats for wool and cheese, and they also sell their products online to customers and restaurants all over the country.","t":"A：你表姊三年前搬離城市後，在山上那座大農場做什麼？ B：她和她先生【飼養】綿羊和山羊來生產羊毛和起司，他們也在網路上把產品賣給全國各地的顧客和餐廳。"},{"w":"adopt","p":"v.","d":"to take an animal or child into your home and care for it as your own","c":"領養；收養","s":"A: Are you still planning to buy a puppy from the pet shop near the train station after you move into your new apartment? B: No, I changed my mind after visiting the animal shelter last weekend, and I decided to adopt an older dog that needs a home instead of paying a lot of money.","t":"A：你搬進新公寓後，還打算從火車站附近那家寵物店買一隻小狗嗎？ B：不了，上週末我去過動物收容所後改變主意，我決定【領養】一隻需要家的老狗，而不是花很多錢去買。"},{"w":"hobby","p":"n.","d":"an activity you do for fun in your free time","c":"嗜好；業餘愛好","s":"A: What do you usually do on weekends to relax, since your job at the bank is so stressful during the week? B: My favorite hobby is bird watching, so I often drive to the wetlands with my camera early on Saturday morning and spend a few quiet hours taking photos of the birds.","t":"A：你在銀行的工作平日壓力那麼大，週末通常做什麼來放鬆？ B：我最喜歡的【嗜好】是賞鳥，所以我常在星期六一大早帶著相機開車去濕地，花幾個安靜的小時拍鳥的照片。"},{"w":"immense","p":"adj.","d":"extremely large or great","c":"巨大的；極大的","s":"A: Was the charity event for the wildlife protection group a success, and how much money did your team finally raise? B: It was an immense success, because more than two thousand people attended, and we raised enough money to build a new hospital for injured sea turtles on the coast.","t":"A：為野生動物保護團體舉辦的慈善活動成功嗎？你們團隊最後募到多少錢？ B：那是一次【巨大的】成功，因為有超過兩千人參加，而且我們募到的錢足夠在海岸邊蓋一間新的受傷海龜醫院。"},{"w":"naughty","p":"adj.","d":"behaving badly; used about children or pets","c":"頑皮的；淘氣的","s":"A: Why are you late for the morning meeting, and why is there mud all over the bottom of your trousers? B: Sorry, my naughty puppy ran out of the gate while I was taking out the trash, and I had to chase him through the neighbor's wet garden for almost twenty minutes.","t":"A：你為什麼晨會遲到？褲管下面為什麼全都是泥巴？ B：抱歉，我在倒垃圾的時候，我那隻【頑皮的】小狗從大門跑出去，我只好在鄰居濕答答的花園裡追了牠將近二十分鐘。"},{"w":"relatively","p":"adv.","d":"when compared with other things or people","c":"相對地；比較而言","s":"A: Do you think a rabbit would be a good pet for my daughter, since we live in a small apartment and both work long hours? B: Yes, rabbits are relatively quiet and clean compared with dogs, and they don't need daily walks, but you will still have to clean their space every few days.","t":"A：你覺得兔子適合給我女兒當寵物嗎？我們住在小公寓，而且兩個人工時都很長。 B：適合，和狗相比，兔子【相對】安靜又乾淨，也不需要每天散步，不過你們還是得每隔幾天清理牠們的空間。"},{"w":"absolutely","p":"adv.","d":"completely; totally","c":"絕對地；完全地","s":"A: Is it really all right to bring my guide dog into your restaurant, since I saw a sign at the door that says no animals are allowed? B: Yes, it is absolutely fine, because that rule doesn't apply to working dogs, and our staff will happily find you a quiet table near the window.","t":"A：帶我的導盲犬進你們餐廳真的沒問題嗎？我在門口看到一個寫著禁止動物進入的告示。 B：是的，【完全】沒問題，因為那條規定不適用於工作犬，我們的員工也很樂意為您安排靠窗的安靜座位。"},{"w":"definitely","p":"adv.","d":"certainly; without any doubt","c":"一定；肯定地","s":"A: Should we include the visit to the panda center in the schedule for the overseas clients, or will they be too tired after the long flight? B: We should definitely keep it, because several of the clients said in their emails that seeing the pandas was the thing they were most excited about.","t":"A：我們應該把參觀熊貓中心排進海外客戶的行程嗎？還是他們長途飛行後會太累？ B：我們【一定】要保留這個行程，因為有好幾位客戶在電子郵件中說，看熊貓是他們最期待的事。"},{"w":"cage","p":"n.","d":"a box made of metal bars or wire for keeping birds or animals","c":"籠子","s":"A: How should we send the two parrots that the customer ordered, since they are traveling by plane to another city tomorrow? B: The airline requires each bird to travel in a strong cage with water, food, and holes for fresh air, so please check the size rules on their website before you buy one.","t":"A：客戶訂的兩隻鸚鵡明天要搭飛機去另一個城市，我們應該怎麼寄送？ B：航空公司規定每隻鳥都必須裝在堅固的【籠子】裡運送，要附上水、食物和通風孔，所以你買之前請先到他們網站查看尺寸規定。"},{"w":"dump","p":"v.","d":"to leave something or someone somewhere because you do not want it","c":"丟棄；拋棄","s":"A: Why has the animal shelter asked the city to put more cameras along the country road behind the industrial park? B: Some people drive there at night to dump pets they no longer want, and the shelter hopes the cameras will stop them and help the police find the owners.","t":"A：為什麼動物收容所要求市政府在工業區後方的鄉間道路多裝一些攝影機？ B：有些人晚上開車到那裡【丟棄】他們不想再養的寵物，收容所希望攝影機能阻止他們，並幫助警方找到飼主。"},{"w":"stroke","p":"v.","d":"to move your hand gently over something, such as an animal's fur","c":"撫摸","s":"A: Is it all right for the children on the school tour to touch the animals at your farm, or is that too dangerous for them? B: They can gently stroke the baby goats and the rabbits in the small yard, but they must wash their hands afterward and stay away from the horses.","t":"A：參加校外教學的孩子們可以摸你們農場的動物嗎？還是那對他們來說太危險了？ B：他們可以在小院子裡輕輕【撫摸】小山羊和兔子，但之後一定要洗手，而且要遠離那些馬。"},{"w":"depressed","p":"adj.","d":"very sad and without hope, often for a long time","c":"沮喪的；憂鬱的","s":"A: Why did your sister decide to get a dog after she moved to Taipei for her new job at the advertising company? B: She felt lonely and a little depressed living alone in a new city, so her doctor suggested a pet, and now she walks in the park every evening and has made new friends.","t":"A：你妹妹搬到台北去廣告公司做新工作後，為什麼決定養狗？ B：她一個人住在陌生的城市覺得孤單，也有點【沮喪】，所以她的醫生建議她養寵物，現在她每天傍晚都去公園散步，還交了新朋友。"},{"w":"hesitate","p":"v.","d":"to stop or wait before doing something because you are not sure","c":"猶豫","s":"A: What will you do if my dog gets sick while I am away on my business trip and you are looking after him? B: I will take him to the vet right away, but please don't hesitate to send me his medical records and the clinic's phone number before you leave, so I have everything ready.","t":"A：我出差期間由你照顧我的狗，如果牠生病了你會怎麼做？ B：我會立刻帶牠去看獸醫，不過請你出發前不要【猶豫】，把牠的病歷和診所電話傳給我，這樣我就能把一切準備好。"},{"w":"chores","p":"n.","d":"small regular jobs that you do at home, such as cleaning","c":"家務；雜事","s":"A: How do you manage to keep your house clean while working full-time and taking care of two cats and a large dog? B: My husband and I share the chores every weekend, so he vacuums the pet hair and washes the floors while I clean the litter boxes and do the laundry.","t":"A：你全職工作，還要照顧兩隻貓和一隻大狗，是怎麼保持家裡乾淨的？ B：我先生和我每個週末分擔【家務】，他用吸塵器吸寵物毛並拖地，我則清理貓砂盆和洗衣服。"},{"w":"companion","p":"n.","d":"a person or animal you spend a lot of time with","c":"同伴；伴侶","s":"A: Why does the retirement home in our neighborhood keep a cat in the main lounge, even though some visitors are worried about allergies? B: The staff said the cat is a wonderful companion for the older residents, who feel happier and less lonely when it sits on their laps during the afternoon.","t":"A：我們社區的養老院為什麼在主要交誼廳養了一隻貓，即使有些訪客擔心過敏問題？ B：工作人員說，那隻貓是年長住戶很棒的【同伴】，下午牠坐在他們腿上時，他們會覺得更快樂、比較不孤單。"},{"w":"relieve","p":"v.","d":"to make pain, worry or stress less","c":"減輕；緩解","s":"A: Why did the tech company bring several puppies into the office during the final week of the busy product launch? B: The managers wanted to relieve stress among the engineers, who were working late every night, and playing with the puppies for a few minutes really helped everyone feel calmer.","t":"A：為什麼那家科技公司在忙碌的產品發表最後一週把幾隻小狗帶進辦公室？ B：主管們想【減輕】每天晚上都工作到很晚的工程師們的壓力，和小狗玩幾分鐘真的讓大家感覺平靜許多。"}]},{"unit":14,"theme":"Apologize 道歉","cards":[{"w":"sorry","p":"adj.","d":"feeling sad about something you did wrong","c":"抱歉的；難過的","s":"A: Why did the hotel manager call you so early this morning, and is there a problem with the room we booked for the visiting clients? B: She called to say she was very sorry because the air conditioner in their suite broke last night, so she has moved them to a bigger room for free.","t":"A：為什麼飯店經理今天一大早就打電話給你？我們幫來訪客戶訂的房間有問題嗎？ B：她打來說她非常【抱歉】，因為他們套房的冷氣昨晚壞了，所以她已經免費把他們換到更大的房間。"},{"w":"regret","p":"n.","d":"a sad feeling about something you wish you had not done","c":"遺憾；懊悔","s":"A: Have you heard back from the customer whose order was sent to the wrong address last week, and is she still angry with us? B: Yes, our director wrote to her personally to express deep regret for the mistake, and she was pleased that we also offered her a discount on her next purchase.","t":"A：上週訂單被寄錯地址的那位顧客有回覆了嗎？她還在生我們的氣嗎？ B：有，我們的主管親自寫信給她，對這個錯誤表達深深的【遺憾】，而且她很高興我們還提供她下次購物的折扣。"},{"w":"remorse","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling of being sorry for doing something wrong","c":"懊悔；自責","s":"A: Why did Kevin stay so late at the office yesterday, even though his shift finished at five and his family was waiting for dinner? B: He felt real remorse after he deleted the shared sales report by accident, so he stayed until midnight to rebuild every page before the morning meeting.","t":"A：為什麼凱文昨天在辦公室待到那麼晚？他的班明明五點就結束了，家人還在等他吃晚餐。 B：他不小心刪掉了共用的業績報告之後感到非常【懊悔】，所以他一直待到半夜，在早上開會前把每一頁都重新做好。"},{"w":"forgive","p":"v.","d":"to stop being angry with someone who did something wrong","c":"原諒；寬恕","s":"A: Do you think the restaurant owner will keep working with our catering company after we delivered the wrong cakes to her wedding event on Saturday? B: I hope she will forgive us, because we have already returned her money, sent fresh flowers to her shop, and promised a free dessert table next month.","t":"A：我們星期六把錯的蛋糕送到那位餐廳老闆的婚禮活動上，你覺得她還會繼續跟我們的外燴公司合作嗎？ B：我希望她會【原諒】我們，因為我們已經退錢給她、送了鮮花到她店裡，還承諾下個月免費提供甜點桌。"},{"w":"forgiveness","p":"n.","d":"the act of forgiving someone","c":"原諒；寬恕","s":"A: What did the airline say in the email after our flight to Tokyo was cancelled without any warning and we missed the trade show? B: The customer service team asked for our forgiveness, explained that a storm had closed the airport, and gave each passenger a travel voucher worth three hundred dollars.","t":"A：我們飛往東京的班機在毫無預警下被取消，害我們錯過了商展，航空公司在電子郵件裡怎麼說？ B：客服團隊請求我們的【原諒】，解釋是暴風雨導致機場關閉，並給每位乘客一張價值三百美元的旅遊抵用券。"},{"w":"excuse","p":"v.","d":"to forgive someone for something small, such as being rude or late","c":"原諒（小過失）；請見諒","s":"A: Why did the new trainee leave the meeting room so suddenly while the manager was still explaining the safety rules to everyone? B: She got an urgent call from her daughter's school, so she said, 'Please excuse me,' and promised to read the meeting notes carefully later in the afternoon.","t":"A：為什麼經理還在向大家說明安全規定時，那位新來的實習生突然離開會議室？ B：她接到女兒學校打來的緊急電話，所以她說「請【原諒】我」，並承諾下午稍晚會仔細閱讀會議紀錄。"},{"w":"admit","p":"v.","d":"to say that something bad is true, often that you did it","c":"承認","s":"A: Did anyone find out why the shipment of printers left the warehouse two days late and caused so many complaints from our stores? B: Yes, the new supervisor had the courage to admit that he had forgotten to sign the delivery form, and he has already created a checklist so it won't happen again.","t":"A：有人查出那批印表機為什麼晚了兩天才離開倉庫，讓我們的門市收到那麼多抱怨嗎？ B：有，新來的主管有勇氣【承認】他忘了簽出貨單，而且他已經做了一份檢查清單，以免再發生這種事。"},{"w":"acknowledge","p":"v.","d":"to accept or say that something is true or exists","c":"承認；確認","s":"A: How did the bank respond when you called about the extra charge on your credit card statement this month? B: The manager was very helpful; she was quick to acknowledge that their system had made an error, and she said the money would be returned to my account within three working days.","t":"A：你這個月打電話去問信用卡帳單上多出來的費用時，銀行怎麼回應？ B：經理非常幫忙，她很快就【承認】是他們的系統出錯，並說這筆錢會在三個工作天內退回我的帳戶。"},{"w":"confess","p":"v.","d":"to admit that you did something wrong, often something you kept secret","c":"坦白；招認","s":"A: Why did Mr. Lin look so nervous when he walked into the director's office after lunch today? B: He had to confess that he lost the company laptop on the train last Friday, and he was worried because it contained important files about our new product launch in Singapore.","t":"A：林先生今天午餐後走進主管辦公室時，為什麼看起來那麼緊張？ B：他必須【坦白】他上週五在火車上弄丟了公司的筆電，他很擔心，因為裡面有關於我們在新加坡推出新產品的重要檔案。"},{"w":"fault","p":"n.","d":"responsibility for a mistake or problem","c":"過錯；責任","s":"A: Should we ask the customer to pay for the broken glass table, since it was damaged during the delivery to her new apartment? B: No, it was our driver's fault because he did not tie it down properly in the truck, so we will replace the table and pay for the shipping ourselves.","t":"A：那張玻璃桌在送到她新公寓的途中損壞了，我們應該請顧客付錢嗎？ B：不行，那是我們司機的【過錯】，因為他沒有在貨車上把它綁牢，所以我們會換一張新桌子，運費也由我們自己負擔。"},{"w":"blame","p":"n.","d":"responsibility for something bad that happened","c":"責備；過錯責任","s":"A: Why is the project manager so upset after the client cancelled the contract, when most of the problems came from the design team? B: He feels that he must take the blame as the leader of the project, so he is preparing an apology letter and a plan to win back the client's trust.","t":"A：大部分的問題都出在設計團隊，為什麼客戶取消合約後專案經理會那麼難過？ B：他覺得身為專案的負責人，他必須承擔【過錯責任】，所以他正在準備一封道歉信和一份贏回客戶信任的計畫。"},{"w":"responsibility","p":"n.","d":"the duty to deal with something, or being the one who caused a problem","c":"責任","s":"A: What did the company president say at the press conference after customers found mistakes in the new phone's instruction booklet? B: She accepted full responsibility for the problem, thanked the customers who reported it, and announced that corrected booklets would be mailed to every buyer by the end of the month.","t":"A：顧客發現新手機的說明書有錯誤後，公司總裁在記者會上說了什麼？ B：她為這個問題承擔全部【責任】，感謝回報問題的顧客，並宣布會在月底前把更正後的說明書寄給每位買家。"},{"w":"make amends","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do something good to show you are sorry for something bad you did","c":"彌補；賠罪","s":"A: Why is the café giving free coffee to everyone in our office building this morning, even to people who have never been there before? B: The owner wants to make amends for the loud construction noise last week, which bothered many workers, so she is also handing out discount cards for next month.","t":"A：為什麼那家咖啡店今天早上要送免費咖啡給我們辦公大樓裡的每個人，連從沒去過的人也有？ B：老闆想為上週吵鬧的施工噪音向大家【彌補】，那些噪音打擾了很多上班族，所以她也在發放下個月的折扣卡。"},{"w":"reconcile","p":"v.","d":"to become friendly again after an argument","c":"和解；和好","s":"A: Are the two sales directors still refusing to speak to each other after their argument about the bonus system last month? B: No, the general manager invited them to lunch, listened to both sides, and helped them reconcile, so now they are planning the new marketing campaign together without any problems.","t":"A：那兩位業務主管上個月為了獎金制度吵架之後，現在還是拒絕跟彼此說話嗎？ B：沒有了，總經理請他們吃午餐，聽了雙方的說法，並幫助他們【和解】，所以現在他們正一起順利地規劃新的行銷活動。"},{"w":"repair","p":"v.","d":"to fix something that is broken or damaged, such as a relationship","c":"修補；修復","s":"A: What is the hotel doing now that the online reviews about its rude front desk staff have spread so quickly across social media? B: The new manager is trying to repair the hotel's reputation by training every employee in customer service and personally answering each negative review with a polite apology.","t":"A：關於飯店櫃檯人員態度無禮的網路評論在社群媒體上迅速擴散，飯店現在打算怎麼做？ B：新經理正努力【修補】飯店的名聲，他訓練每位員工的客服能力，並親自以禮貌的道歉回覆每一則負評。"},{"w":"sincere","p":"adj.","d":"honest and really meaning what you say","c":"真誠的；誠懇的","s":"A: How did the customer react when our team leader called her to talk about the missing items in her online order? B: She was angry at first, but she calmed down because his apology sounded sincere, and he also arranged for a courier to bring the missing items to her home that same evening.","t":"A：我們的組長打電話給那位顧客，談她網購訂單裡缺少的商品時，她有什麼反應？ B：她一開始很生氣，但後來冷靜下來了，因為他的道歉聽起來很【真誠】，而且他還安排快遞員當天晚上就把缺少的商品送到她家。"},{"w":"heartfelt","p":"adj.","d":"felt very deeply and honestly","c":"衷心的；真摯的","s":"A: What did the staff do for Mrs. Chen after the office party, when someone accidentally broke the vase her late mother had given her? B: Everyone signed a card with a heartfelt message saying how sorry they were, and the team also bought her a beautiful new vase from her favorite shop.","t":"A：辦公室派對上有人不小心打破陳太太已故母親送她的花瓶後，同事們為她做了什麼？ B：大家在一張卡片上簽名，寫下【衷心的】話語表達他們有多抱歉，團隊也從她最喜歡的店買了一個漂亮的新花瓶送她。"},{"w":"humble","p":"adj.","d":"not proud; not thinking you are better than others","c":"謙虛的；謙卑的","s":"A: Why do so many employees respect the new CEO, even though she has only worked at our company for three months? B: She is very humble; when her plan to change the work schedule failed, she apologized to the whole staff in an email and asked for their ideas to improve it.","t":"A：新任執行長才在我們公司工作三個月，為什麼有那麼多員工尊敬她？ B：她非常【謙虛】；當她更改工作時間表的計畫失敗時，她寫電子郵件向全體員工道歉，並請大家提供改善的想法。"},{"w":"ashamed","p":"adj.","d":"feeling bad or guilty about something you did","c":"羞愧的；慚愧的","s":"A: Did you talk to the new assistant who shouted at a customer on the phone yesterday because the system kept crashing? B: Yes, she said she felt deeply ashamed of her behavior, so she called the customer back this morning to apologize and offered to process his order for him herself.","t":"A：昨天因為系統一直當機而在電話裡對顧客大吼的那位新助理，你跟她談過了嗎？ B：談過了，她說她對自己的行為感到非常【羞愧】，所以今天早上她回電向那位顧客道歉，並主動親自幫他處理訂單。"},{"w":"embarrassed","p":"adj.","d":"feeling shy or uncomfortable because of something you did in front of others","c":"尷尬的；難為情的","s":"A: Why did Tom's face turn so red during the presentation to the investors this afternoon? B: He felt really embarrassed when he noticed that his slides had the wrong company name on them, so he stopped, apologized to everyone in the room, and quickly explained the correct sales figures.","t":"A：今天下午向投資人做簡報時，湯姆的臉為什麼變得那麼紅？ B：他發現投影片上的公司名稱寫錯時感到非常【尷尬】，所以他停下來向會議室裡的每個人道歉，並迅速說明正確的銷售數字。"},{"w":"polite","p":"adj.","d":"speaking and acting in a kind way that shows respect for others","c":"有禮貌的","s":"A: What should I write in the reply to the guest who complained that his room was not cleaned during his three-day stay? B: Keep your email short and polite, say that you are sorry for the trouble, and offer him a free breakfast or a discount the next time he visits our hotel.","t":"A：有位客人抱怨他住宿三天期間房間都沒有打掃，我回信時該寫些什麼？ B：信要寫得簡短又【有禮貌】，說你對造成的麻煩感到抱歉，並在他下次來我們飯店時提供免費早餐或折扣。"},{"w":"respectfully","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows respect","c":"恭敬地；尊重地","s":"A: How should I tell the client that we cannot finish the website by Friday without making her feel that we don't care about her project? B: Speak to her respectfully, apologize for the change, explain clearly why the testing needs more time, and give her a new date that you are sure the team can meet.","t":"A：我該怎麼告訴客戶我們無法在星期五前完成網站，又不讓她覺得我們不在乎她的專案？ B：【恭敬地】跟她說話，為這個變動道歉，清楚說明為什麼測試需要更多時間，並給她一個你確定團隊能趕上的新日期。"},{"w":"honestly","p":"adv.","d":"in a truthful way, without hiding anything","c":"誠實地；坦白地","s":"A: What happened when the shop manager found out that the new cashier had given a customer the wrong change on Monday? B: The cashier explained honestly what had happened, so the manager did not get angry; instead, they called the customer together, apologized, and returned the money that same afternoon.","t":"A：店長發現新來的收銀員星期一找錯錢給顧客時，發生了什麼事？ B：收銀員【誠實地】說明了事情經過，所以店長沒有生氣；他們反而一起打電話給那位顧客道歉，並在當天下午就把錢退還給他。"},{"w":"publicly","p":"adv.","d":"in front of other people or in a way that everyone can see","c":"公開地","s":"A: Why did the food company post a video message on its website and social media accounts last night? B: The president wanted to apologize publicly for the wrong labels on its cookie boxes, because many customers were worried, and she promised that all the boxes in stores would be replaced this week.","t":"A：那家食品公司昨晚為什麼在官網和社群媒體帳號上發布一段影片訊息？ B：總裁想要【公開地】為餅乾盒上的錯誤標示道歉，因為很多顧客都很擔心，她並承諾本週內會更換店裡所有的盒子。"},{"w":"formally","p":"adv.","d":"in an official and serious way","c":"正式地","s":"A: Is a phone call enough to say sorry to our biggest client for the shipping delay that cost them a week of sales? B: I don't think so; we should apologize formally in a signed letter from the director, and then arrange a meeting to discuss how we will prevent similar delays in the future.","t":"A：運送延誤讓我們最大的客戶損失了一週的銷售，只打一通電話道歉夠嗎？ B：我覺得不夠；我們應該用一封主管簽名的信【正式地】道歉，然後安排一場會議，討論我們將來要如何避免類似的延誤。"},{"w":"personally","p":"adv.","d":"by yourself, not by sending someone else","c":"親自地","s":"A: Did the regional manager send an assistant to visit the customer whose washing machine flooded her kitchen after our technician fixed it? B: No, he went personally to her house yesterday afternoon to apologize, check the damage, and promise that our company would pay for the new floor.","t":"A：我們技師修好那位顧客的洗衣機後卻淹了她的廚房，區經理有派助理去拜訪她嗎？ B：沒有，他昨天下午【親自】去她家道歉、查看損壞情況，並承諾我們公司會支付新地板的費用。"},{"w":"promptly","p":"adv.","d":"quickly and without delay","c":"迅速地；立即地","s":"A: What is the most important thing to do when a guest complains about the service in our restaurant during a busy dinner? B: You should respond promptly, listen carefully without interrupting, apologize for the problem, and then ask the kitchen to prepare a new dish so the guest does not have to wait too long.","t":"A：在忙碌的晚餐時段，客人抱怨我們餐廳的服務時，最重要的是做什麼？ B：你應該【迅速地】回應，仔細聆聽不要打斷，為問題道歉，然後請廚房準備一道新菜，讓客人不用等太久。"},{"w":"graciously","p":"adv.","d":"in a kind, polite and generous way","c":"親切地；寬厚地","s":"A: How did the guest speaker react when our team forgot to prepare a microphone for her talk at the annual conference? B: She graciously accepted our apology, smiled at the audience, and spoke loudly for the first ten minutes while our technician brought a new microphone from the hotel's storage room.","t":"A：我們團隊在年會上忘了幫演講嘉賓準備麥克風，她有什麼反應？ B：她【寬厚地】接受了我們的道歉，對觀眾微笑，並在前十分鐘大聲演講，同時我們的技術人員從飯店的儲藏室拿來一支新的麥克風。"},{"w":"accept","p":"v.","d":"to agree to take something that is offered, such as an apology","c":"接受","s":"A: Has the supplier answered the letter we sent after our accountant paid their invoice two months late by mistake? B: Yes, they wrote back to say that they accept our apology and understand that the delay was caused by the new software, so they are happy to continue our partnership next year.","t":"A：我們的會計誤將供應商的發票晚了兩個月才付款後，我們寄了一封信，他們回覆了嗎？ B：回了，他們回信說他們【接受】我們的道歉，也理解延誤是新軟體造成的，所以很樂意明年繼續我們的合作關係。"}]},{"unit":15,"theme":"Apology Letter 道歉信","cards":[{"w":"regret","p":"v.","d":"to feel sorry about something you did or that happened","c":"後悔；遺憾","s":"A: Have you finished the letter to the hotel guests whose wedding party was moved to a smaller room at the last minute? B: Almost, and I want the first line to say that we deeply regret the change, because the couple had planned the decorations for months and were very upset.","t":"A：你寫完給那些婚宴在最後一刻被移到較小廳的飯店客人的信了嗎？ B：快寫完了，我希望第一行就說明我們對這次的更動深感【遺憾】，因為那對新人花了好幾個月規劃佈置，他們非常難過。"},{"w":"mistake","p":"n.","d":"something done wrong because of bad judgment or not paying attention","c":"錯誤；失誤","s":"A: Why did the customer in Kaohsiung receive twenty boxes of printer paper when she only ordered two boxes for her small office? B: A new clerk in the warehouse made a mistake when he typed the order, so we are sending a driver to collect the extra boxes this afternoon at no cost to her.","t":"A：為什麼高雄那位客戶的小辦公室只訂了兩箱影印紙，卻收到二十箱？ B：倉庫一位新來的職員在輸入訂單時犯了【錯誤】，所以我們今天下午會派司機去把多出來的箱子收回，她不需要負擔任何費用。"},{"w":"error","p":"n.","d":"a mistake, especially in numbers, writing or a system","c":"錯誤；差錯","s":"A: I just noticed that our monthly electricity bill is three times higher than usual, even though the office was closed for a week. Should we call the power company? B: Yes, please call them today, because it is probably a billing error, and they usually send a corrected bill within a few business days.","t":"A：我剛注意到我們這個月的電費帳單比平常高了三倍，可是辦公室明明關了一個星期。我們要打電話給電力公司嗎？ B：要，請今天就打給他們，因為這很可能是帳單【錯誤】，他們通常會在幾個工作天內寄來更正後的帳單。"},{"w":"fault","p":"n.","d":"responsibility for a mistake or problem","c":"過錯；責任","s":"A: The client is angry that the brochures arrived with the wrong phone number printed on the back cover. Did our design team cause the problem? B: No, it wasn't our fault, because the client sent us the old number in their email, but we will still reprint the brochures quickly to keep a good relationship.","t":"A：客戶很生氣，因為送到的宣傳手冊封底印錯了電話號碼。是我們設計團隊造成的問題嗎？ B：不是，這不是我們的【過錯】，因為客戶在電子郵件裡給我們的是舊號碼，但為了維持良好的關係，我們還是會盡快重印手冊。"},{"w":"responsibility","p":"n.","d":"the duty of dealing with something, or being the cause of a problem","c":"責任","s":"A: The online store sent the wrong size of jackets to more than fifty customers last weekend. What should our apology email say to them? B: It should say clearly that we take full responsibility for the problem, and then offer each customer a free exchange and a discount code for their next order.","t":"A：上週末網路商店寄錯了五十多位顧客的夾克尺寸。我們的道歉信應該怎麼寫？ B：信中應該清楚說明我們對這個問題負起全部【責任】，然後提供每位顧客免費換貨，以及下次訂購可用的折扣碼。"},{"w":"inconvenience","p":"n.","d":"a problem that causes trouble or makes things less easy","c":"不便；麻煩","s":"A: The elevators in our building will be closed for repairs all day on Friday, and many visitors will have to use the stairs. Should we tell our clients ahead of time? B: Yes, let's send them a short notice today and apologize for any inconvenience, especially to the older clients who have meetings on the tenth floor.","t":"A：我們大樓的電梯星期五整天都要停用維修，很多訪客將必須走樓梯。我們應該事先通知客戶嗎？ B：要，我們今天就寄一封簡短的通知給他們，並為造成的任何【不便】致歉，尤其是要在十樓開會的年長客戶。"},{"w":"trouble","p":"n.","d":"problems, difficulty or extra work","c":"麻煩；困難","s":"A: The supplier drove all the way from Taichung to replace the broken coffee machine in our break room this morning. Should we thank him in some way? B: Yes, I think we should write him a short note, because he went to a lot of trouble to help us, even though his company was already busy with other orders.","t":"A：供應商今天早上大老遠從台中開車過來，替我們更換休息室裡壞掉的咖啡機。我們應該用某種方式謝謝他嗎？ B：應該，我覺得我們該寫張簡短的謝卡給他，因為他不怕【麻煩】、特地來幫我們，即使他們公司已經在忙其他訂單了。"},{"w":"delay","p":"n.","d":"a time when something happens later than planned","c":"延誤；耽擱","s":"A: The new laptops for the sales team were supposed to arrive on Monday, but they still haven't come. Did the shipping company give you any reason? B: They said the delay was caused by a typhoon that closed the port in Keelung for two days, and they expect the laptops to arrive by Thursday afternoon.","t":"A：業務團隊的新筆電原本應該星期一送到，但到現在還沒來。貨運公司有給你任何理由嗎？ B：他們說這次【延誤】是因為颱風讓基隆港關閉了兩天，他們預計筆電會在星期四下午前送達。"},{"w":"late","p":"adj.","d":"happening or arriving after the expected time","c":"遲的；晚的","s":"A: I'm writing an apology to the client because our monthly report reached her two days after the deadline. What else should I mention in the email? B: Explain that the report was late because two team members were sick, and promise that next month's report will be sent at least one day early.","t":"A：我在寫道歉信給客戶，因為我們的月報比截止日期晚了兩天才送到她手上。電子郵件裡我還應該提到什麼？ B：說明報告之所以【遲交】是因為有兩位組員生病，並承諾下個月的報告至少會提早一天寄出。"},{"w":"misunderstanding","p":"n.","d":"a situation where people do not understand each other correctly","c":"誤會；誤解","s":"A: Mr. Wang thought our meeting was at ten in the morning, but the rest of us arrived at two in the afternoon. How did that happen? B: There was a misunderstanding about the time because the invitation used a twenty-four-hour clock, so I will call him today and set up a new meeting that suits his schedule.","t":"A：王先生以為我們的會議是早上十點，但我們其他人卻是下午兩點才到。怎麼會這樣？ B：因為邀請函使用二十四小時制，大家對時間產生了【誤會】，所以我今天會打電話給他，另外安排一個適合他行程的會議。"},{"w":"careless","p":"adj.","d":"not paying enough attention, so mistakes happen","c":"粗心的","s":"A: How did the hotel booking for our visitors from Japan get the dates wrong when they had already sent us all the details by email? B: I'm afraid I was careless when I copied the dates into the booking system, so I will contact the hotel right away and write a short apology to the visitors myself.","t":"A：日本訪客早就用電子郵件把所有細節寄給我們了，為什麼他們的飯店訂房日期還會弄錯？ B：恐怕是我把日期輸入訂房系統時太【粗心】了，所以我會馬上聯絡飯店，並親自寫一封簡短的道歉信給訪客。"},{"w":"unintentional","p":"adj.","d":"not done on purpose","c":"無心的；非故意的","s":"A: One of our customers says our newsletter shared her phone number with everyone on the mailing list. Is that true, and what should we tell her? B: Sadly, it is true, but the mistake was completely unintentional, because the software added a wrong column, so we should apologize and explain how we fixed the system.","t":"A：有位顧客說我們的電子報把她的電話號碼分享給了郵寄名單上的所有人。這是真的嗎？我們該怎麼跟她說？ B：很遺憾，這是真的，但這個錯誤完全是【無心的】，因為軟體多加了一個錯誤的欄位，所以我們應該向她道歉，並說明我們如何修正了系統。"},{"w":"sincere","p":"adj.","d":"honest and really meant","c":"真誠的；誠摯的","s":"A: Our regional manager wants to send flowers to the customer who fell on the wet floor in our store last week. Is that enough, or should we do more? B: Flowers are nice, but I think she would value a sincere letter from the manager more, because it shows that someone really cares about what happened to her.","t":"A：我們的區經理想送花給上週在我們店裡濕滑地板上跌倒的那位顧客。這樣夠嗎？還是我們應該做更多？ B：送花很好，但我覺得她會更看重經理寫的一封【真誠的】信，因為那代表有人真正關心她發生了什麼事。"},{"w":"deeply","p":"adv.","d":"very much; strongly","c":"深深地；非常","s":"A: The restaurant served the wrong dish to one of our guests at the company dinner last night, and she had to wait almost an hour for her meal. Is she all right now? B: She is fine, but the owner was deeply sorry, so he called her this morning and promised to give her a free dinner next week.","t":"A：昨晚公司聚餐時，餐廳把錯的菜端給我們一位客人，她等了將近一小時才吃到她的餐點。她現在還好嗎？ B：她沒事，但老闆【深深地】感到抱歉，所以他今天早上打電話給她，並承諾下週請她免費吃一頓晚餐。"},{"w":"truly","p":"adv.","d":"really; in a real and honest way","c":"真心地；確實","s":"A: Do you think the client will believe our apology after we missed the delivery date for the third time this year? B: She will only believe us if we are truly sorry and show it with action, so let's offer her free delivery for six months and give her a direct phone number for our manager.","t":"A：今年我們已經第三次錯過交貨日期了，你覺得客戶還會相信我們的道歉嗎？ B：只有我們【真心】感到抱歉並用行動證明，她才會相信我們，所以我們就提供她六個月的免運，並給她經理的直撥電話號碼吧。"},{"w":"wholeheartedly","p":"adv.","d":"completely and with all your feelings","c":"全心全意地；由衷地","s":"A: The staff at the branch office worked all weekend to fix the problem our mistake caused in their computer system. How should we thank them? B: Our director will visit them on Monday and wholeheartedly apologize for the extra work, and she will also bring lunch for the whole team to show how grateful we are.","t":"A：分公司的員工整個週末都在加班，修復我們的錯誤在他們電腦系統中造成的問題。我們該如何感謝他們？ B：我們的主管星期一會去拜訪他們，【由衷地】為額外的工作致歉，她也會為整個團隊帶午餐過去，表達我們有多感激。"},{"w":"explain","p":"v.","d":"to make something clear by giving details or reasons","c":"解釋；說明","s":"A: Several passengers missed their connecting flights because our airport shuttle broke down on the highway this morning. What should I write in the email to them? B: First, explain what happened to the shuttle and why it took so long to send another bus, and then tell them how we will pay for their new tickets.","t":"A：今天早上我們的機場接駁車在高速公路上拋錨，好幾位乘客錯過了轉機班機。我應該在給他們的電子郵件裡寫些什麼？ B：首先，【說明】接駁車發生了什麼事，以及為什麼花了那麼久才派另一輛巴士過去，然後告訴他們我們將如何支付他們的新機票。"},{"w":"reason","p":"n.","d":"a cause or explanation for something","c":"原因；理由","s":"A: Our biggest customer canceled the contract renewal meeting this morning without saying much. Do you know why she did that? B: She told me the main reason was our slow customer service last month, so I'm writing her a letter today to apologize and to show her the changes we have already made.","t":"A：我們最大的客戶今天早上取消了續約會議，也沒多說什麼。你知道她為什麼這麼做嗎？ B：她告訴我主要的【原因】是我們上個月的客服太慢，所以我今天會寫一封信給她，向她道歉，並讓她看看我們已經做出的改變。"},{"w":"situation","p":"n.","d":"the things that are happening at a certain time and place","c":"情況；處境","s":"A: The air conditioning in the conference hall stopped working during the product launch, and many guests left early because it was so hot. How should we handle this? B: Let's call each guest personally to explain the situation, apologize for the uncomfortable afternoon, and invite them to a private product demonstration next month.","t":"A：產品發表會期間會議廳的冷氣停止運轉，很多賓客因為太熱而提早離開。我們該怎麼處理？ B：我們親自打電話給每位賓客說明【情況】，為那個不舒服的下午道歉，並邀請他們參加下個月的私人產品展示會。"},{"w":"circumstance","p":"n.","d":"a fact or condition that affects what happens","c":"情況；狀況","s":"A: Why did the training workshop for new employees start an hour late this morning, and why did nobody tell us about the change? B: Because of a circumstance beyond our control, the trainer's train from Hsinchu was stopped for an hour, and the message to staff failed to send, so we will apologize to everyone today.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上的新進員工訓練課程晚了一小時才開始？為什麼都沒人通知我們這個變動？ B：由於我們無法控制的【狀況】，講師從新竹搭的火車停駛了一小時，而且發給員工的通知沒有成功寄出，所以我們今天會向大家道歉。"},{"w":"promise","p":"v.","d":"to say that you will certainly do something","c":"承諾；答應","s":"A: The customer who waited three weeks for her new sofa wants to know if her next order will also take that long. What should I tell her? B: Apologize again and promise that her next delivery will arrive within five days, but only say it if the warehouse manager agrees that it is possible.","t":"A：那位等了三週才收到新沙發的顧客想知道，她下一次訂購是否也要等那麼久。我該怎麼告訴她？ B：再次向她道歉，並【承諾】她下一次的貨會在五天內送達，但前提是倉庫經理同意這是做得到的才說。"},{"w":"assure","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone something firmly so they feel less worried","c":"向…保證；使放心","s":"A: The guests are worried after the fire alarm went off twice in the hotel last night, and some want to check out early. What should the front desk say? B: The staff should apologize for the noise and assure the guests that the building is safe, because the technician found that a faulty sensor caused both alarms.","t":"A：昨晚飯店的火災警報響了兩次，客人們都很擔心，有些人想提早退房。櫃台應該怎麼說？ B：員工應該為噪音道歉，並向客人【保證】大樓是安全的，因為技師發現兩次警報都是一個故障的感應器造成的。"},{"w":"guarantee","p":"v.","d":"to promise firmly that something will happen or be done","c":"保證；擔保","s":"A: Our client is upset because the posters for her concert were printed in the wrong colors. Can we print new ones in time for the event next Saturday? B: Yes, our print shop can work overtime, so we can guarantee that the new posters will be ready by Wednesday, and we won't charge her anything extra for them.","t":"A：我們的客戶很不高興，因為她音樂會的海報印錯了顏色。我們能在下星期六活動前及時印好新的嗎？ B：可以，我們的印刷廠可以加班，所以我們可以【保證】新海報會在星期三前完成，而且不會向她收取任何額外費用。"},{"w":"correct","p":"v.","d":"to make something right or remove the mistakes from it","c":"改正；更正","s":"A: The price list on our website still shows last year's prices, and three customers have already complained that they were charged more at checkout. What should we do? B: Ask the web team to correct the prices before noon today, and then send those three customers an apology and a refund for the difference.","t":"A：我們網站上的價目表還是去年的價格，已經有三位顧客抱怨結帳時被收了比較多錢。我們該怎麼做？ B：請網站團隊今天中午前【更正】價格，然後寄給那三位顧客道歉信，並退還差額。"},{"w":"fix","p":"v.","d":"to repair something or solve a problem","c":"修理；解決","s":"A: Customers keep calling because the payment page on our app shows an error message every time they try to pay by credit card. How long will it take? B: Our technicians think they can fix the problem by tonight, so let's post an apology on our homepage and tell customers to pay by bank transfer until then.","t":"A：顧客一直打電話來，因為他們每次想用信用卡付款時，我們應用程式的付款頁面都會出現錯誤訊息。要多久才能處理好？ B：我們的技術人員認為今晚就能【解決】這個問題，所以我們先在首頁公告致歉，並告訴顧客在那之前改用銀行轉帳付款。"},{"w":"resolve","p":"v.","d":"to find a solution to a problem or disagreement","c":"解決","s":"A: The tenants on the fifth floor have complained for two weeks about the noise from the construction work next door. Has the building manager done anything yet? B: She met the construction company yesterday to resolve the issue, and they agreed to start work after nine in the morning, so she is writing an apology letter to the tenants now.","t":"A：五樓的房客已經抱怨隔壁施工的噪音兩個星期了。大樓管理員做了什麼處理嗎？ B：她昨天和建設公司見面來【解決】這個問題，他們同意早上九點以後才開工，所以她現在正在寫道歉信給房客。"},{"w":"improve","p":"v.","d":"to make something better","c":"改善；改進","s":"A: Our survey shows that many hotel guests were unhappy with the long wait at the front desk during the busy holiday season. What are we going to do about it? B: We plan to improve the check-in process by adding two more staff in the evenings and letting guests check in on our mobile app before they arrive.","t":"A：我們的調查顯示，許多住客對假期旺季時櫃台要等很久感到不滿。我們打算怎麼處理？ B：我們計劃在晚上增加兩名員工，並讓住客抵達前就能用我們的手機應用程式辦理入住，藉此【改善】入住流程。"},{"w":"prevent","p":"v.","d":"to stop something from happening","c":"防止；預防","s":"A: The client was angry when she found that her private files had been sent to the wrong company by email last Friday. What steps are we taking now? B: We have apologized to her, and we added a new check to our email system to prevent the same thing from happening again in the future.","t":"A：那位客戶發現她的私人檔案上星期五被用電子郵件寄到錯誤的公司時非常生氣。我們現在採取了哪些措施？ B：我們已經向她道歉，並在電子郵件系統中新增了一道檢查程序，以【防止】同樣的事情將來再度發生。"},{"w":"ensure","p":"v.","d":"to make certain that something happens","c":"確保","s":"A: The conference organizers apologized because there weren't enough seats for all the guests at last year's event. Will this year be any different? B: Yes, they have booked a much larger hall and hired extra staff to ensure that every guest has a seat and gets a copy of the program at the door.","t":"A：研討會主辦單位曾為去年活動座位不夠所有來賓坐而道歉。今年會有所不同嗎？ B：會，他們訂了一個大得多的會場，並多請了工作人員，以【確保】每位來賓都有座位，並在門口拿到一份議程表。"},{"w":"appreciate","p":"v.","d":"to be grateful for something","c":"感激；感謝","s":"A: How should I end the letter to the customer whose package was lost during our office move last month? She was very calm on the phone with me. B: You should say that we really appreciate her patience while we searched for the package, and that a replacement has already been sent by express mail.","t":"A：上個月我們辦公室搬遷時弄丟了一位顧客的包裹，給她的信我該怎麼結尾？她在電話中對我非常冷靜。 B：你應該說，我們在尋找包裹期間非常【感謝】她的耐心，而且替代品已經用快遞寄出了。"},{"w":"understanding","p":"n.","d":"kindness and patience shown when someone accepts a problem","c":"體諒；諒解","s":"A: The main road to our factory will be closed for a week, so all deliveries to our customers will be one or two days slower than usual. How should I finish the notice? B: End it by thanking customers for their understanding and giving them the phone number of our service desk in case they have any urgent orders.","t":"A：通往我們工廠的主要道路將封閉一週，所以所有送給客戶的貨都會比平常慢一兩天。這份通知我該怎麼結尾？ B：最後感謝客戶的【體諒】，並提供我們服務台的電話號碼，以防他們有任何緊急訂單。"},{"w":"patience","p":"n.","d":"the ability to wait calmly without getting angry","c":"耐心","s":"A: Many passengers at the station have been waiting more than an hour for the train to Tainan because of a signal problem. What should we announce next? B: Announce that the trains will start running again in twenty minutes, apologize for the long wait, and thank the passengers for their patience during this difficult morning.","t":"A：因為號誌問題，車站裡很多旅客已經等前往台南的火車等了一個多小時。我們接下來該廣播什麼？ B：廣播說火車將在二十分鐘後恢復行駛，為長時間的等候致歉，並感謝旅客在這個辛苦的早上所展現的【耐心】。"},{"w":"forgive","p":"v.","d":"to stop being angry with someone for something they did","c":"原諒","s":"A: I accidentally sent the meeting notes with the private salary details to the entire department this morning. Do you think my manager will be angry with me? B: She might be upset at first, but if you tell her the truth right away and help her deal with the problem, I'm sure she will forgive you quickly.","t":"A：我今天早上不小心把附有私人薪資明細的會議紀錄寄給了整個部門。你覺得我的經理會對我生氣嗎？ B：她一開始可能會不高興，但如果你馬上跟她說實話，並幫她處理這個問題，我相信她很快就會【原諒】你。"},{"w":"forgiveness","p":"n.","d":"the act of forgiving someone","c":"原諒；寬恕","s":"A: Our team leader shouted at the new assistant in front of everyone during the busy sales meeting yesterday, and the assistant was very upset. Has he said anything since then? B: Yes, he went to her desk this morning, asked for her forgiveness, and promised to talk to staff more calmly and privately when there is a problem.","t":"A：昨天在忙碌的業務會議上，我們組長當著大家的面對新來的助理大吼，助理非常難過。他之後有說什麼嗎？ B：有，他今天早上走到她的座位，請求她的【原諒】，並承諾以後有問題時會更冷靜、私下地和員工談。"},{"w":"accept","p":"v.","d":"to agree to take something that is offered","c":"接受","s":"A: The hotel offered the guest a free night and dinner for two after the cleaning staff entered his room by mistake while he was sleeping. Did he say yes? B: At first he wanted a full refund, but after the manager called him personally, he decided to accept the apology and the free night.","t":"A：清潔人員在一位客人睡覺時誤闖他的房間，飯店事後招待他免費住一晚和兩人晚餐。他答應了嗎？ B：他一開始想要全額退款，但經理親自打電話給他之後，他決定【接受】道歉和免費住宿。"},{"w":"once again","p":"adv.phr.","d":"one more time","c":"再一次；再次","s":"A: I have finished the letter to the customers whose orders were canceled because of our computer system problem last week. How should I close it? B: Close it by saying that we apologize once again for the trouble, and remind them that their discount code can be used until the end of next month.","t":"A：給上週因電腦系統問題被取消訂單的顧客的信我寫完了。我該怎麼結尾？ B：最後說我們【再一次】為造成的麻煩致歉，並提醒他們折扣碼可以使用到下個月月底。"},{"w":"sincerely","p":"adv.","d":"in an honest and real way; also used to end a formal letter","c":"真誠地；誠摯地","s":"A: The airline canceled our flight to Singapore because of a technical problem, and we missed the first day of the trade fair. Has the airline said anything to us? B: Yes, they sent an email this morning saying they sincerely apologize, and they are offering each of us a voucher worth three hundred dollars for our next trip.","t":"A：航空公司因為技術問題取消了我們飛往新加坡的班機，我們錯過了商展的第一天。航空公司有跟我們說什麼嗎？ B：有，他們今天早上寄了一封電子郵件，說他們【誠摯地】致歉，並且提供我們每人一張價值三百美元的抵用券，供下次旅行使用。"},{"w":"immediately","p":"adv.","d":"at once; without waiting","c":"立即；馬上","s":"A: A customer just called to say that the milk she bought at our supermarket this morning had already gone bad when she opened it at home. What should we do? B: Ask her to come back with the receipt so we can refund her immediately, and please also check every carton on that shelf before more customers buy it.","t":"A：一位顧客剛打電話來說，她今天早上在我們超市買的牛奶，回家打開時就已經壞了。我們該怎麼做？ B：請她帶收據回來，好讓我們【立即】退款給她，也請你在更多顧客購買之前檢查那個貨架上的每一盒牛奶。"},{"w":"soon","p":"adv.","d":"in a short time from now","c":"很快；不久","s":"A: The online shop told me that my printer would be shipped on Monday, but it still hasn't left their warehouse after four days. Did they reply to my email? B: Yes, they apologized for the slow service and said the printer will be sent out very soon, probably tomorrow morning, along with a free box of ink cartridges.","t":"A：網路商店告訴我印表機會在星期一出貨，但四天過去了還沒離開他們的倉庫。他們回覆我的電子郵件了嗎？ B：回了，他們為服務太慢道歉，並說印表機【很快】就會寄出，大概明天早上，還會附送一盒免費的墨水匣。"},{"w":"attention","p":"n.","d":"the act of noticing or dealing with something","c":"注意；關注","s":"A: Who first noticed that the wrong delivery address was printed on all the shipping labels for our biggest customer's order? B: One of the drivers brought the problem to our attention before he left the warehouse, so we stopped the trucks in time and sent the customer an apology for the small delay.","t":"A：是誰最先發現我們最大客戶訂單的所有出貨標籤都印錯了送貨地址？ B：一位司機在離開倉庫前讓我們【注意】到了這個問題，所以我們及時攔下了卡車，並為小小的延誤向客戶道歉。"},{"w":"matter","p":"n.","d":"a subject or situation that you must deal with","c":"事情；問題","s":"A: A customer wrote to our head office to say that a store clerk was rude to her when she tried to return a broken lamp. Who is handling the complaint? B: The regional manager is looking into the matter personally, and she plans to call the customer this afternoon to apologize and offer her a full refund.","t":"A：一位顧客寫信到我們總公司，說她想退回一盞壞掉的檯燈時，店員對她很無禮。誰在處理這件客訴？ B：區經理正親自調查這件【事情】，她打算今天下午打電話給這位顧客道歉，並提供全額退款。"},{"w":"response","p":"n.","d":"an answer or reaction","c":"回應；回覆","s":"A: Mr. Lin wrote to us last week to complain about the noise from our night deliveries, but nobody has answered him yet. Is that a problem? B: Yes, it is, because a slow response can make an angry customer even angrier, so please send him a short apology and explain our new delivery hours today.","t":"A：林先生上週寫信給我們，抱怨我們夜間送貨的噪音，但到現在都還沒人回覆他。這會有問題嗎？ B：會，因為【回應】太慢會讓生氣的顧客更生氣，所以請你今天寄給他一封簡短的道歉信，並說明我們新的送貨時間。"}]},{"unit":16,"theme":"App 應用程式","cards":[{"w":"app","p":"n.","d":"a program you use on a phone or computer","c":"應用程式；App","s":"A: I keep forgetting which meeting rooms are free, and the front desk is always busy when I call, so is there an easier way to book one? B: Yes, the company has a new app on our phones, so you can check which rooms are open and reserve one in a few seconds before you leave your desk.","t":"A：我老是忘記哪些會議室有空，而且我打電話時櫃台總是很忙，有沒有比較簡單的預約方法？ B：有，公司在我們的手機上推出了一個新的【應用程式】，你離開座位前只要幾秒鐘就能查看哪些會議室有空並預約。"},{"w":"application","p":"n.","d":"a computer program designed for a particular job","c":"應用軟體；應用程式","s":"A: Our accounting team spends hours every week typing sales numbers into spreadsheets by hand, and they often make small mistakes, so what can we do about it? B: The IT manager suggested a new software application that collects the numbers from every store automatically, which should save time and reduce errors before the monthly report is due.","t":"A：我們的會計團隊每週都花好幾個小時手動把銷售數字輸入試算表，而且常常出小錯，我們能怎麼辦？ B：資訊部經理建議用一套新的【應用軟體】，它能自動收集每家門市的數字，這應該能在月報截止前節省時間並減少錯誤。"},{"w":"app store","p":"n.phr.","d":"an online shop where you get programs for your phone","c":"應用程式商店","s":"A: Our customers keep asking where they can get our new shopping program for their phones, and the marketing team hasn't sent out any instructions yet, so what should I tell them? B: Tell them to open the app store on their phone and type our company name, and they can get it for free in less than a minute.","t":"A：顧客一直問哪裡可以取得我們新的手機購物程式，行銷團隊還沒發出任何說明，我該怎麼告訴他們？ B：請他們打開手機上的【應用程式商店】，輸入我們的公司名稱，不到一分鐘就能免費取得。"},{"w":"download","p":"v.","d":"to copy files or programs from the internet to your device","c":"下載","s":"A: I'm flying to Tokyo for the trade show tomorrow, and I heard the internet on the plane is very slow and expensive, so how can I read the reports during the flight? B: You should download all the files onto your laptop tonight while you're still at the office, so you can open them later without any connection.","t":"A：我明天要飛去東京參加商展，我聽說飛機上的網路很慢又很貴，飛行途中我要怎麼看報告？ B：你應該今晚還在辦公室時就把所有檔案【下載】到筆電裡，這樣之後沒有網路也能打開。"},{"w":"install","p":"v.","d":"to put a program on a computer or phone so it is ready to use","c":"安裝","s":"A: The new security program that the head office sent us last week still isn't working on my computer, and I have a client meeting in an hour, so can you help me? B: Of course, I'll come to your desk and install it for you now, but you'll need to restart your computer afterward, which takes about five minutes.","t":"A：總公司上週寄給我們的新安全程式在我的電腦上還是不能用，而我一小時後要和客戶開會，你能幫我嗎？ B：當然，我現在就到你座位幫你【安裝】，不過之後你需要重新開機，大概要五分鐘。"},{"w":"update","p":"v.","d":"to add the newest information to something","c":"更新","s":"A: Customers have been complaining that our online menu still shows last month's prices, and some of them were surprised when they paid more at the counter, so who's responsible for that? B: That's my job, actually, and I'm sorry because I forgot to update the menu after the price change, but I'll fix it this afternoon.","t":"A：顧客一直抱怨我們的線上菜單還是顯示上個月的價格，有些人在櫃台付了比較多錢時很驚訝，這是誰負責的？ B：其實那是我的工作，很抱歉我在價格調整後忘了【更新】菜單，我今天下午會修正。"},{"w":"interface","p":"n.","d":"the screens and buttons that let a person use a program","c":"介面；操作介面","s":"A: The older employees in the warehouse said the new inventory system is too difficult, and some of them still write everything on paper instead, so what's the main problem? B: Most of them told me the interface is confusing because the buttons are tiny and the menus are hidden, so we're asking the designers to make the screens simpler.","t":"A：倉庫裡年紀較大的員工說新的庫存系統太難用，有些人甚至還是全部寫在紙上，主要的問題是什麼？ B：他們大部分告訴我【介面】很令人困惑，因為按鈕很小、選單又藏起來，所以我們正請設計師把畫面做得更簡單。"},{"w":"feature","p":"n.","d":"an important or interesting part of a product","c":"功能；特色","s":"A: Why did the sales team choose this new phone for all the staff when it's more expensive than the one we used before? B: They liked one special feature that turns spoken words into written notes during meetings, so salespeople can listen to clients carefully instead of writing everything down by hand.","t":"A：這款新手機比我們以前用的貴，為什麼業務團隊還幫所有員工選它？ B：他們喜歡其中一項特別的【功能】，可以在會議中把口說內容轉成文字筆記，這樣業務員就能專心聽客戶說話，而不用全部手寫下來。"},{"w":"functionality","p":"n.","d":"the range of things a program or machine can do","c":"功能性；功能","s":"A: The free version of the design program looks almost the same as the expensive one, so why does the art department want us to pay for the full package this year? B: The free version has limited functionality, which means designers can't share files with clients or work on large projects together, so it slows the whole team down.","t":"A：這套設計程式的免費版看起來跟昂貴的版本幾乎一樣，為什麼美術部今年要我們付費買完整版？ B：免費版的【功能】有限，也就是說設計師不能和客戶分享檔案，也不能一起做大型專案，所以會拖慢整個團隊。"},{"w":"user","p":"n.","d":"a person who uses a product or service","c":"使用者；用戶","s":"A: Before we spend more money on advertising the new booking website, shouldn't we find out whether people actually enjoy it? B: Good idea, so let's send a short survey to every user who booked a hotel room through it last month, and we can ask them what they liked and what confused them.","t":"A：在我們花更多錢宣傳新的訂房網站之前，不是應該先了解大家是否真的喜歡它嗎？ B：好主意，那我們寄一份簡短的問卷給上個月透過網站訂飯店房間的每一位【使用者】，問問他們喜歡什麼、哪裡讓他們感到困惑。"},{"w":"account","p":"n.","d":"a personal record that lets you use a website or service","c":"帳號；帳戶","s":"A: I'd like to see my order history and change my delivery address on your website, but the page keeps asking me for a password, so what should I do? B: First you need to create an account with your email address and a password, and after that you can manage all your orders and addresses in one place.","t":"A：我想在你們的網站上查看訂單紀錄並更改送貨地址，但頁面一直要我輸入密碼，我該怎麼辦？ B：你需要先用電子郵件地址和密碼建立一個【帳號】，之後就能在同一個地方管理所有訂單和地址。"},{"w":"login","p":"n.","d":"the name and password you use to enter a system","c":"登入帳號；登入","s":"A: I'm starting at the Taipei branch on Monday, and I'll need to check the team schedule and my email from my first morning, so what do I need from the office? B: The IT department will give you a login and a temporary password on your first day, and you should change the password as soon as you sign in.","t":"A：我週一要開始在台北分公司上班，第一天早上就需要查看團隊行程和電子郵件，我需要辦公室提供什麼？ B：資訊部會在你上班第一天給你【登入帳號】和臨時密碼，你一登入就應該馬上更改密碼。"},{"w":"subscribe","p":"v.","d":"to sign up to get something regularly, often by paying","c":"訂閱","s":"A: I really enjoy the business news podcast that you recommended, but I keep forgetting to check when a new episode comes out, so is there an easier way? B: You can subscribe to the program on your phone, and then every new episode will appear automatically each Monday morning, so you can listen on your way to work.","t":"A：我很喜歡你推薦的商業新聞播客，但我老是忘記看新的一集什麼時候出來，有更簡單的方法嗎？ B：你可以在手機上【訂閱】這個節目，之後每週一早上新的一集就會自動出現，你就能在上班途中收聽。"},{"w":"subscription","p":"n.","d":"money you pay regularly to receive a product or service","c":"訂閱；訂閱費","s":"A: Why are we paying the music company every single month, when nobody in the office remembers signing any long contract with them? B: That's for the background music in our shops, and the subscription costs thirty dollars a month, but we can cancel it any time if we find a cheaper service.","t":"A：為什麼我們每個月都要付錢給那家音樂公司？辦公室裡沒有人記得和他們簽過什麼長期合約啊。 B：那是我們店裡的背景音樂，這項【訂閱】每月三十美元，但如果找到更便宜的服務，我們隨時可以取消。"},{"w":"free","p":"adj.","d":"costing no money","c":"免費的","s":"A: Our small café can't afford expensive advertising this year, so how can we let more people in the neighborhood know about our new breakfast menu? B: We could post photos on social media, which is completely free, and ask our regular customers to share them with their friends, so it won't cost us anything at all.","t":"A：我們的小咖啡館今年負擔不起昂貴的廣告，要怎麼讓附近更多人知道我們的新早餐菜單？ B：我們可以在社群媒體上貼照片，那是完全【免費的】，再請常客分享給朋友，這樣一毛錢都不用花。"},{"w":"paid","p":"adj.","d":"that you must pay money to use","c":"付費的","s":"A: Is it true that the language-learning program the company offers has two versions, and why do the managers in our department all use the more expensive one? B: Yes, the paid version has no advertisements and lets you practice speaking with a teacher online, so the company covers the cost for managers who travel abroad.","t":"A：公司提供的語言學習程式真的有兩種版本嗎？為什麼我們部門的經理們都用比較貴的那個？ B：是的，【付費】版沒有廣告，還能和老師線上練習口說，所以公司幫要出國的經理們支付費用。"},{"w":"in-app purchase","p":"n.phr.","d":"something you buy inside a program after you download it","c":"應用程式內購買；內購","s":"A: My son played a game on my work phone during the weekend, and now my credit card bill shows a strange charge of fifty dollars, so what do you think happened? B: He probably made an in-app purchase, like buying extra coins inside the game, so you should turn on a password for payments to stop it from happening again.","t":"A：我兒子週末用我的公務手機玩遊戲，現在我的信用卡帳單上出現一筆奇怪的五十美元費用，你覺得發生了什麼事？ B：他可能做了一筆【應用程式內購買】，例如在遊戲裡買額外的金幣，所以你應該開啟付款密碼，避免再次發生。"},{"w":"rating","p":"n.","d":"a score that shows how good something is","c":"評分；評等","s":"A: Our new delivery service has been running for three months now, so how do customers feel about it compared with the other companies in the city? B: It has an average rating of four and a half stars out of five, which is higher than our competitors, although some people said the drivers sometimes arrive late.","t":"A：我們新的外送服務已經營運三個月了，跟市內其他公司相比，顧客覺得如何？ B：它的平均【評分】是五顆星中的四顆半，比我們的競爭對手高，不過有些人說司機有時候會遲到。"},{"w":"review","p":"n.","d":"a written opinion about how good a product or service is","c":"評論；評價","s":"A: Before we choose a caterer for the company's annual dinner, how can we know which one actually serves good food and arrives on time? B: Let's read what other customers wrote online, because one bad review might be unfair, but if many people complain about cold dishes, we should pick a different company.","t":"A：在替公司年度晚宴挑選外燴業者前，我們要怎麼知道哪一家真的餐點好吃又準時抵達？ B：我們來看看其他顧客在網路上寫了什麼，因為一則負面的【評論】可能不公平，但如果很多人抱怨菜是冷的，我們就該換一家公司。"},{"w":"category","p":"n.","d":"a group of things that are similar in some way","c":"類別；種類","s":"A: Our online shop sells hundreds of office products now, and customers say they can't find what they need quickly, so how can we make the website easier to use? B: We could put every item into a clear category, such as paper, furniture, or printers, so shoppers can click on one group and see only the products they want.","t":"A：我們的網路商店現在賣好幾百種辦公用品，顧客說他們沒辦法快速找到需要的東西，我們要怎麼讓網站更好用？ B：我們可以把每件商品放進清楚的【類別】，例如紙類、家具或印表機，讓購物者點一個分類就只看到想要的商品。"},{"w":"developer","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that creates computer programs","c":"開發人員；開發商","s":"A: The hotel wants a new mobile program that lets guests check in and open their room doors with their phones, so who's going to build it for us? B: We've hired a software developer from a company in Hsinchu, and she'll meet our managers next week to discuss the design, the budget, and the schedule.","t":"A：飯店想要一個新的手機程式，讓房客能用手機辦理入住並打開房門，誰要幫我們做？ B：我們請了一位新竹公司的軟體【開發人員】，她下週會和我們的經理們見面，討論設計、預算和時程。"},{"w":"bug","p":"n.","d":"a mistake in a computer program that stops it working correctly","c":"程式錯誤；漏洞","s":"A: Several customers called this morning to say they were charged twice when they paid for their tickets online, so do we know what caused the problem? B: The technical team found a bug in the payment system that sent each order two times, and they're fixing it now and will return the extra money by Friday.","t":"A：今天早上有好幾位顧客打電話來說，他們在線上購票時被重複扣款，我們知道問題的原因嗎？ B：技術團隊在付款系統裡發現一個【程式錯誤】，會把每筆訂單送出兩次，他們正在修正，並會在週五前退還多收的錢。"},{"w":"crash","p":"v.","d":"(of a computer or program) to suddenly stop working","c":"當機；故障","s":"A: Why didn't you send me the sales presentation last night as you promised, when I needed to review it before this morning's meeting with the clients? B: I'm really sorry, but my laptop started to crash every time I opened the file, so I had to ask the IT team to repair it this morning.","t":"A：你為什麼沒有照答應的昨晚把業務簡報寄給我？我需要在今天早上和客戶開會前先看過。 B：真的很抱歉，但我的筆電每次打開那個檔案就【當機】，所以我今天早上只好請資訊團隊修理。"},{"w":"stable","p":"adj.","d":"working well and not likely to fail or change suddenly","c":"穩定的","s":"A: Our online store had serious problems during the holiday sale last year, so are you confident the website will work well when thousands of shoppers visit at the same time? B: Yes, we moved to a stronger server in the summer, and the system has been very stable since then, without a single breakdown in four months.","t":"A：我們的網路商店去年假期特賣時出了嚴重的問題，你有把握網站在幾千名購物者同時上線時能正常運作嗎？ B：有，我們夏天換了一台更強的伺服器，從那以後系統一直很【穩定】，四個月來沒有故障過一次。"},{"w":"compatible","p":"adj.","d":"able to work together with another machine or system","c":"相容的","s":"A: I just bought a new tablet for my business trips, but will I be able to use our company's sales software on it while I'm visiting clients in Japan? B: You should check with the IT team first, because the program is only compatible with certain systems, and some older tablets can't run it at all.","t":"A：我剛為出差買了一台新平板，在日本拜訪客戶時能在上面使用公司的業務軟體嗎？ B：你應該先跟資訊團隊確認，因為那個程式只和特定系統【相容】，有些較舊的平板完全無法執行。"},{"w":"privacy","p":"n.","d":"the right to keep your personal information secret","c":"隱私","s":"A: Some customers are worried about giving us their phone numbers and home addresses when they join our membership program, so what should our staff tell them? B: Explain that we protect their privacy carefully, and we never sell personal information to other companies, so their details are only used for deliveries and special offers.","t":"A：有些顧客在加入我們的會員計畫時，擔心要提供電話號碼和住家地址，我們的員工該怎麼跟他們說？ B：向他們說明我們會謹慎保護他們的【隱私】，而且絕不會把個人資料賣給其他公司，他們的資料只會用於送貨和特別優惠。"},{"w":"permission","p":"n.","d":"the right to do something that someone allows you to have","c":"權限；許可","s":"A: When I opened the new expense program on my phone, it asked whether it could use my camera, so is it safe to say yes? B: Yes, you should give it permission, because the program needs the camera to take photos of your receipts, and then it sends them straight to the accounting department.","t":"A：我在手機上打開新的報帳程式時，它問我能不能使用相機，答應安全嗎？ B：安全，你應該給它【權限】，因為程式需要用相機拍你的收據，然後直接傳給會計部。"},{"w":"notification","p":"n.","d":"a short message on a phone or computer that tells you about something new","c":"通知","s":"A: I missed the urgent meeting about the client's complaint yesterday because nobody told me it had moved to two o'clock, so how can I avoid that next time? B: Turn on the calendar alerts on your phone, and you'll get a notification every time a meeting is changed or canceled, even when you're away from your desk.","t":"A：昨天我錯過了關於客戶投訴的緊急會議，因為沒有人告訴我會議改到兩點，下次要怎麼避免？ B：打開手機上的行事曆提醒，這樣每次會議變更或取消時，就算你不在座位上也會收到【通知】。"},{"w":"launch","p":"v.","d":"to make a new product available to the public for the first time","c":"推出；發表","s":"A: The marketing team has been working on the new ordering program for almost a year, so when will customers finally be able to use it? B: We plan to launch it at the trade show in March, and we'll offer a ten percent discount to everyone who places an order with it during the first week.","t":"A：行銷團隊已經為新的訂購程式努力了將近一年，顧客到底什麼時候才能使用？ B：我們打算在三月的商展上【推出】它，並在第一週給所有用它下單的人九折優惠。"},{"w":"browse","p":"v.","d":"to look at things casually, especially on the internet","c":"瀏覽","s":"A: I don't know what to buy for my manager's farewell gift, and I don't have time to visit the department store after work this week, so do you have any suggestions? B: You could browse a few online gift shops during your lunch break, because many of them have useful ideas and can deliver to the office by Friday.","t":"A：我不知道該買什麼當經理的歡送禮物，而且這週下班後也沒時間去百貨公司，你有什麼建議嗎？ B：你可以在午休時【瀏覽】幾家網路禮品店，因為很多家都有不錯的點子，而且能在週五前送到辦公室。"},{"w":"search","p":"v.","d":"to look carefully for something, often by typing words into a computer","c":"搜尋；查找","s":"A: The customer called again about the missing order, but I can't find her name anywhere in this long list of deliveries, so what should I do? B: Don't read the whole list line by line, but search the database for her order number instead, which will show you the delivery details in a few seconds.","t":"A：那位顧客又打電話來詢問遺失的訂單，但我在這份很長的送貨清單裡怎麼都找不到她的名字，我該怎麼辦？ B：別一行一行看整份清單，改用她的訂單編號【搜尋】資料庫，幾秒鐘就會顯示送貨細節。"},{"w":"optimize","p":"v.","d":"to make something work as well or as quickly as possible","c":"最佳化；優化","s":"A: Our website takes almost ten seconds to open on mobile phones, and the sales manager thinks many shoppers leave before they see any products, so what can we do? B: The developers can optimize the photos and the code so the pages load faster, which should keep more visitors on the site and increase our sales.","t":"A：我們的網站在手機上要將近十秒才打開，業務經理認為很多購物者還沒看到商品就離開了，我們能怎麼做？ B：開發人員可以【優化】照片和程式碼讓網頁載入更快，這應該能留住更多訪客並提高我們的銷售額。"},{"w":"securely","p":"adv.","d":"in a safe way that protects something from being stolen or seen","c":"安全地","s":"A: I need to send the new employees' salary details to the accountant at our Kaohsiung office today, so can I just attach the file to a normal email? B: No, please upload it securely through the company's protected file system, because personal information like that must never be sent in an ordinary message.","t":"A：我今天需要把新進員工的薪資資料寄給高雄辦公室的會計師，我可以直接把檔案附在一般的電子郵件裡嗎？ B：不行，請透過公司受保護的檔案系統【安全地】上傳，因為那類個人資料絕不能用一般訊息寄送。"}]},{"unit":17,"theme":"Application Letter 求職信","cards":[{"w":"position","p":"n.","d":"a job in a company","c":"職位；職缺","s":"A: I saw on the company website that the marketing department is hiring again this month, so do you know what kind of person they are looking for? B: Yes, the position is for a sales assistant who can speak English and Japanese, and they want someone who can start working in early March.","t":"A：我在公司網站上看到行銷部這個月又在徵人，你知道他們在找什麼樣的人嗎？ B：知道，這個【職位】是業務助理，要會說英文和日文，而且他們希望對方能在三月初開始上班。"},{"w":"vacancy","p":"n.","d":"a job that is open and needs someone to fill it","c":"職缺；空缺","s":"A: Our receptionist is moving to Kaohsiung next month, and the front desk will be very busy without her, so what should we do now? B: I will ask the human resources office to post the vacancy online today, so we can start interviewing new people before she leaves the company.","t":"A：我們的櫃台接待員下個月要搬去高雄，沒有她櫃台會非常忙，我們現在該怎麼辦？ B：我會請人資部今天就把這個【職缺】公告在網路上，這樣我們就能在她離職前開始面試新人。"},{"w":"candidate","p":"n.","d":"a person who is being considered for a job","c":"候選人；應徵者","s":"A: We have interviewed six people for the office manager job this week, and all of them seemed friendly and well prepared, so who do you think we should choose? B: In my opinion, the best candidate is Ms. Chen, because she has managed a busy office before and she answered every question clearly.","t":"A：這週我們為辦公室經理一職面試了六個人，他們看起來都很友善也準備充分，你覺得我們該選誰？ B：我認為最好的【候選人】是陳小姐，因為她以前管理過忙碌的辦公室，而且每個問題都回答得很清楚。"},{"w":"applicant","p":"n.","d":"a person who formally asks for a job","c":"申請人；求職者","s":"A: The deadline for the designer job closed yesterday, and my inbox is completely full of emails from people who want the job, so how many did we receive? B: We got more than eighty letters, so each applicant will first take a short online test before we invite the top ten for an interview.","t":"A：設計師職缺的截止日是昨天，我的收件匣塞滿了想要這份工作的人寄來的信，我們總共收到多少封？ B：我們收到八十多封信，所以每位【求職者】都會先做一個簡短的線上測驗，之後我們再邀請前十名來面試。"},{"w":"employer","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that pays people to work for them","c":"雇主","s":"A: I am writing my first job letter, and I am not sure whether I should talk about my part-time job at the coffee shop, so what do you think? B: You should mention it, because any future employer will be glad to know that you served customers politely and handled money carefully during busy weekends.","t":"A：我正在寫我的第一封求職信，不確定該不該提到我在咖啡店的兼職工作，你覺得呢？ B：你應該提，因為任何未來的【雇主】都會很高興知道你在忙碌的週末能禮貌地服務顧客並謹慎處理金錢。"},{"w":"qualification","p":"n.","d":"an official record, like a degree, showing you have finished training","c":"資格；學歷證明","s":"A: The job advertisement says the company wants an accountant, but I studied business, not accounting, at university, so should I still send my letter? B: You can try, but they will probably ask for a professional qualification, so you might need to finish an accounting course first and then apply next year.","t":"A：這則徵才廣告說公司要找會計人員，但我大學念的是商業而不是會計，我還要寄求職信嗎？ B：你可以試試看，不過他們可能會要求專業【資格】，所以你也許需要先完成會計課程，明年再申請。"},{"w":"experience","p":"n.","d":"knowledge or skill you get from doing a job for some time","c":"經驗","s":"A: This hotel is looking for a front desk supervisor, and I have worked at a hotel reception for five years, so how should I start my letter? B: Start by explaining your experience at the reception desk, because the manager will want to know that you have already handled guests, bookings, and complaints for many years.","t":"A：這家飯店在找櫃台主管，而我在飯店櫃台工作了五年，我的求職信該怎麼開頭？ B：先說明你在櫃台的【經驗】，因為經理會想知道你多年來已經處理過客人、訂房和客訴。"},{"w":"skill","p":"n.","d":"the ability to do something well because you have practiced it","c":"技能；技巧","s":"A: The new travel agency needs someone who can answer calls from foreign tourists, so is it a good idea to say that I speak three languages? B: Of course, because language is a very useful skill in that kind of job, and you should also mention that you can use booking software quickly.","t":"A：那家新的旅行社需要能接聽外國觀光客電話的人，在信裡說我會說三種語言是好主意嗎？ B：當然，因為語言在那種工作中是非常有用的【技能】，而且你也應該提到你能快速使用訂位軟體。"},{"w":"ability","p":"n.","d":"the power or talent to do something","c":"能力","s":"A: The manager of the call center told me she needs a new team leader before the busy holiday season, so what is the most important thing for her? B: She told me she wants someone with the ability to stay calm under pressure, because the team often handles hundreds of angry calls on a single day.","t":"A：客服中心經理告訴我，她需要在忙碌的假期旺季前找到新的組長，對她來說最重要的是什麼？ B：她跟我說她想找一個有【能力】在壓力下保持冷靜的人，因為這個團隊常常一天就要處理好幾百通憤怒的電話。"},{"w":"strength","p":"n.","d":"a good quality or skill that someone has","c":"優點；長處","s":"A: In the interview tomorrow, they will probably ask me to describe myself, and I always get nervous about that question, so how should I answer it? B: Talk about one real strength, such as your careful planning, and then give an example of a project where your planning helped your team finish early.","t":"A：明天面試他們可能會要我描述自己，我每次遇到這個問題都很緊張，我該怎麼回答？ B：談一個真實的【優點】，例如你做事規劃仔細，然後舉一個你的規劃幫助團隊提早完成的專案例子。"},{"w":"education","p":"n.","d":"the learning you get at school, college, or university","c":"教育；學歷","s":"A: I finished high school in Tainan and then studied hotel management at a college in Taipei for four years, so where should I put this information? B: Put it in a short education section under your work history, and list the name of each school, your main subject, and the year you finished.","t":"A：我在台南念完高中，之後在台北一所學院念了四年的飯店管理，這些資料該放在哪裡？ B：把它放在你工作經歷下面一個簡短的【學歷】欄位，列出每所學校的名稱、你的主修科目和畢業年份。"},{"w":"degree","p":"n.","d":"the title a university gives you when you finish your studies","c":"學位","s":"A: This engineering company only hires people who have finished university, and I will graduate this June, so can I apply for the job now? B: Yes, you can, but you should explain in your letter that you will receive your degree in June, and that you can start working right after that.","t":"A：這家工程公司只錄用大學畢業的人，而我今年六月才畢業，我現在可以應徵嗎？ B：可以，但你應該在信中說明你會在六月拿到【學位】，而且之後就能馬上開始上班。"},{"w":"certificate","p":"n.","d":"an official paper that shows you have passed a test or finished a course","c":"證書；證照","s":"A: The job post says that all tour guides must pass the national guide test, and I passed it last spring, so how can I show that to them? B: You should scan your certificate and include it with your email, so the manager can see your test result and the date immediately.","t":"A：這則職缺公告說所有導遊都必須通過國家導遊考試，而我去年春天考過了，我要怎麼向他們證明？ B：你應該把你的【證書】掃描起來，隨電子郵件一起寄出，這樣經理就能馬上看到你的考試結果和日期。"},{"w":"resume","p":"n.","d":"a short document listing your education and work history","c":"履歷","s":"A: My cousin wants to apply for a job at a bank, and she has only written a cover letter, so what else does she need to send? B: She also needs a one-page resume that shows her education, past jobs, and skills, because banks usually check that document before they read anything else.","t":"A：我表妹想應徵銀行的工作，她只寫了一封求職信，她還需要寄什麼？ B：她還需要一份一頁的【履歷】，列出她的學歷、過去的工作和技能，因為銀行通常會先看那份文件再看其他東西。"},{"w":"CV","p":"n.","d":"a document listing your education, work, and skills (curriculum vitae)","c":"履歷（CV）","s":"A: The British company I am applying to asked for a detailed list of my studies, research, and work history, so is that different from a normal job letter? B: Yes, that is your CV, and in the UK it is often two pages long, so you can include your research projects and conference talks there.","t":"A：我要應徵的那家英國公司要求一份詳細列出我的學業、研究和工作經歷的清單，這和一般的求職信不一樣嗎？ B：對，那是你的【履歷（CV）】，在英國通常有兩頁長，所以你可以把你的研究計畫和研討會發表都列在裡面。"},{"w":"attach","p":"v.","d":"to add a file to an email","c":"附加（檔案）","s":"A: I have finished my letter for the assistant manager job, and I am ready to send the email to the hotel, but what about my resume and photo? B: Before you click send, please attach both files and check that they open correctly, because many managers will not read an email without them.","t":"A：我已經寫好應徵副理職位的信，準備把電子郵件寄給飯店了，那我的履歷和照片呢？ B：按下寄出之前，請把兩個檔案都【附加】上去並確認能正常開啟，因為很多經理不會看缺少這些檔案的郵件。"},{"w":"reference","p":"n.","d":"a person who can tell an employer about your work and character","c":"推薦人；介紹人","s":"A: The company has asked me for the name of someone who can talk about my work, and I am not sure who I should choose, so can you help? B: Your old supervisor at the bookstore would be a good reference, because she worked with you for three years and knows how hard you work.","t":"A：公司要我提供一個能談論我工作表現的人，我不確定該選誰，你能幫忙嗎？ B：你以前在書店的主管會是很好的【推薦人】，因為她和你共事了三年，知道你工作多努力。"},{"w":"recommendation","p":"n.","d":"a statement that someone is good for a job","c":"推薦；推薦信","s":"A: I am applying for a teaching job at an international school, and they want a letter from someone who has seen me teach, so who should I ask? B: Ask the head teacher at your current school for a recommendation, because a letter from a senior teacher will make your application much stronger.","t":"A：我正在應徵一所國際學校的教職，他們要一封看過我教學的人寫的信，我該找誰？ B：請你目前學校的主任幫你寫一封【推薦信】，因為資深老師寫的信會讓你的申請更有說服力。"},{"w":"interest","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of wanting to know about or do something","c":"興趣；關注","s":"A: I really want to work for this green energy company, but I do not have much experience yet, so what should I say in the first paragraph? B: Explain your strong interest in solar power, and mention the volunteer project where you helped install solar panels at a school last summer.","t":"A：我真的很想在這家綠能公司工作，但我還沒有太多經驗，第一段該寫什麼？ B：說明你對太陽能有濃厚的【興趣】，並提到去年夏天你在一所學校幫忙安裝太陽能板的志工計畫。"},{"w":"enthusiastic","p":"adj.","d":"showing a lot of excitement and interest","c":"熱情的；熱衷的","s":"A: My letter lists all my skills, but my friend said it sounds a little cold and boring, so how can I make it sound more friendly and positive? B: Add a sentence saying you are enthusiastic about the chance to work with their team, and explain why their products really excite you.","t":"A：我的信列出了我所有的技能，但我朋友說聽起來有點冷淡又無聊，我要怎麼讓它聽起來更友善、更正面？ B：加一句話說你對能和他們團隊共事的機會感到很【熱衷】，並說明為什麼他們的產品真的讓你很興奮。"},{"w":"motivated","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to do something and willing to work hard for it","c":"有動力的；積極的","s":"A: Our sales team lost two people last month, and the new targets for next year are much higher, so what kind of person should we hire now? B: We need a highly motivated person who wants to meet targets, who does not give up easily, and who is happy to visit customers every day.","t":"A：我們的業務團隊上個月走了兩個人，而明年的新目標高很多，我們現在該聘請什麼樣的人？ B：我們需要一個非常【積極】的人，想要達成目標、不輕易放棄，而且樂意每天拜訪客戶。"},{"w":"responsible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be trusted to do the right thing","c":"負責任的；可靠的","s":"A: The restaurant manager is going on vacation next month and needs someone to open the shop and count the money every morning, so who should do it? B: I think Kevin is the most responsible worker here, because he always arrives early, locks the doors carefully, and never makes mistakes with the cash.","t":"A：餐廳經理下個月要去度假，需要有人每天早上開店並清點現金，該由誰來做？ B：我覺得凱文是這裡最【負責任】的員工，因為他總是早到、仔細鎖門，而且處理現金從不出錯。"},{"w":"reliable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be trusted to do something well every time","c":"可靠的；可信賴的","s":"A: I want to show the shipping company that I can be trusted, but I have only had one job, so what is a good example to use in my letter? B: Write that you were a reliable driver at the bakery for two years, and that you delivered every order on time, even during typhoons.","t":"A：我想向那家貨運公司證明我值得信任，但我只做過一份工作，信裡用什麼例子比較好？ B：寫你在麵包店當了兩年【可靠】的司機，每一張訂單都準時送達，連颱風天也一樣。"},{"w":"professional","p":"adj.","d":"showing the skills and polite manner expected at work","c":"專業的","s":"A: I usually write emails to my friends in a very casual way, with lots of short words and emojis, so is that fine for my job letter? B: No, you should use a more professional style, with complete sentences, a polite greeting, and a clear closing, because the manager will judge you by your writing.","t":"A：我平常寫信給朋友都很隨性，用很多簡短的字和表情符號，這種寫法用在求職信可以嗎？ B：不行，你應該用比較【專業】的風格，句子要完整、問候要禮貌、結尾要清楚，因為經理會從你的文字來評斷你。"},{"w":"teamwork","p":"n.","d":"working well together with other people","c":"團隊合作","s":"A: The job post says the company builds websites in small groups of four or five people, so what should I write about my last job? B: Describe how you planned the company trade show with three coworkers, because that example shows your teamwork and your ability to share tasks fairly.","t":"A：這則職缺公告說那家公司以四、五個人的小組來架設網站，我該怎麼寫我上一份工作？ B：描述你和三位同事一起籌劃公司商展的經過，因為這個例子展現你的【團隊合作】以及公平分工的能力。"},{"w":"communication","p":"n.","d":"the sharing of information with other people","c":"溝通","s":"A: This customer service job means talking to clients on the phone and writing emails all day, so what should I show them in my letter? B: Show them your strong communication skills, for example by explaining how you answered more than fifty customer questions a day in your last job.","t":"A：這份客服工作就是整天和客戶講電話、寫電子郵件，我該在信中向他們展現什麼？ B：展現你很強的【溝通】能力，例如說明你在上一份工作中一天回答超過五十個客戶的問題。"},{"w":"opportunity","p":"n.","d":"a chance to do something good","c":"機會","s":"A: I just finished my letter for the internship at the airline, and I want my last sentence to sound polite and thankful, so what can I write? B: You could write that you would welcome the opportunity to meet them in person, and that you hope to hear from them soon.","t":"A：我剛寫完應徵航空公司實習的信，希望最後一句聽起來有禮貌又帶著感謝，我可以怎麼寫？ B：你可以寫你很希望有【機會】和他們當面見面，並希望很快收到他們的消息。"},{"w":"career","p":"n.","d":"the jobs you do in your working life","c":"職涯；事業","s":"A: I have worked as a bank teller for three years, but now I want to move into marketing, so how can I explain this change in my letter? B: Explain that you want to build a long-term career in marketing, and show how your customer service at the bank taught you what clients really need.","t":"A：我當了三年的銀行櫃員，但現在想轉往行銷，我要怎麼在信中解釋這個轉變？ B：說明你想在行銷領域建立長期的【職涯】，並說明你在銀行的客服經驗如何讓你了解客戶真正的需求。"},{"w":"contribute","p":"v.","d":"to give your ideas, time, or work to help something succeed","c":"貢獻","s":"A: The manager asked in the advertisement what new people can bring to the team, but I am not sure how to answer that, so do you have any ideas? B: Write that you can contribute your experience with social media, since their online sales are growing and they will need someone to manage their accounts.","t":"A：經理在廣告中問新人能為團隊帶來什麼，但我不確定該怎麼回答，你有什麼想法嗎？ B：寫你能【貢獻】你的社群媒體經驗，因為他們的網路銷售正在成長，會需要有人管理他們的帳號。"},{"w":"develop","p":"v.","d":"to make something grow or become better","c":"發展；培養","s":"A: Why do you want to leave your job at the small shop and work for a large international company, even though you would earn almost the same salary? B: I want to develop my management skills, and a big company offers training courses and chances to lead larger teams in different countries.","t":"A：雖然薪水幾乎一樣，你為什麼想離開小店的工作，去大型國際公司上班？ B：我想【培養】我的管理能力，而大公司會提供培訓課程，也有機會在不同國家帶領更大的團隊。"},{"w":"learn","p":"v.","d":"to get knowledge or a skill by studying or practicing","c":"學習","s":"A: I have never used the design software that this company uses, and I am worried that they will not hire me because of it, so what should I say? B: Tell them honestly that you are ready to learn new programs quickly, and mention that you taught yourself video editing in only two months.","t":"A：我從來沒用過這家公司使用的設計軟體，我擔心他們會因此不錄用我，我該怎麼說？ B：老實告訴他們你準備好快速【學習】新程式，並提到你只花兩個月就自學會了影片剪輯。"},{"w":"grow","p":"v.","d":"to become bigger, better, or more skilled","c":"成長","s":"A: The last question on the application form asks where I see myself in five years, and I do not want to sound too proud, so how should I answer? B: Say that you hope to grow with the company, take on more responsibility, and maybe lead a small team after a few years of hard work.","t":"A：申請表上最後一個問題問我五年後的自己在哪裡，我不想聽起來太驕傲，該怎麼回答？ B：說你希望能和公司一起【成長】，承擔更多責任，經過幾年努力後也許能帶領一個小團隊。"},{"w":"suitable","p":"adj.","d":"right or good for a particular job or purpose","c":"合適的；適合的","s":"A: We received a letter from a young man who has a law degree, but this job is for a graphic designer, so should we call him for an interview? B: I do not think he is suitable for this job, but we can keep his letter, because our legal department may need an assistant next year.","t":"A：我們收到一位擁有法律學位的年輕人的信，但這個職缺是平面設計師，我們該打電話請他來面試嗎？ B：我不認為他【適合】這份工作，但我們可以留著他的信，因為我們的法務部明年可能需要助理。"},{"w":"qualified","p":"adj.","d":"having the right training or exams for a job","c":"合格的；具備資格的","s":"A: The hospital needs a new nurse for the night shift, and three people have applied this week, so can all of them start working right away? B: Only two of them are fully qualified, because the third person has not passed the national nursing exam yet and cannot work alone at night.","t":"A：醫院需要一位新的夜班護理師，這週有三個人應徵，他們都能馬上開始上班嗎？ B：只有兩位完全【具備資格】，因為第三位還沒通過國家護理考試，不能獨自值夜班。"},{"w":"available","p":"adj.","d":"free to do something, such as start a job or meet someone","c":"有空的；可到職的","s":"A: The manager wants to know when I can come in for the interview, but I am still working at my old job during the day, so what should I say? B: Tell her you are available on weekday evenings after six o'clock or any time on Saturday, and ask which time is best for her.","t":"A：經理想知道我什麼時候能來面試，但我白天還在原本的公司上班，我該怎麼說？ B：告訴她你平日晚上六點以後或星期六任何時間都【有空】，並問她哪個時間最方便。"},{"w":"interview","p":"n.","d":"a formal meeting where someone asks you questions to decide if you get a job","c":"面試","s":"A: I just received an email from the hotel saying they liked my letter and my resume, so what is the next step in their hiring process? B: They will probably invite you to an interview next week, so you should prepare answers about your experience and practice speaking clearly in English.","t":"A：我剛收到飯店的電子郵件，說他們喜歡我的信和履歷，他們招聘流程的下一步是什麼？ B：他們下週可能會邀請你去【面試】，所以你應該準備好關於你經驗的回答，並練習清楚地用英文表達。"},{"w":"discuss","p":"v.","d":"to talk about something with someone","c":"討論","s":"A: How should I end my letter so the manager feels that I really want to meet her, without sounding too pushy or impatient? B: Write that you would be happy to discuss your experience and ideas in more detail at a meeting, and give your phone number so she can call you easily.","t":"A：我的信該怎麼結尾，才能讓經理覺得我真的想見她，又不會顯得太強勢或沒耐心？ B：寫你很樂意在會面時更詳細地【討論】你的經驗和想法，並附上你的電話號碼，讓她方便打給你。"},{"w":"consider","p":"v.","d":"to think carefully about something before deciding","c":"考慮","s":"A: I think my letter is almost ready, but the closing sentence feels too short, so what polite words can I use to thank the company? B: You can write \"Thank you for taking the time to consider my application,\" because it is polite and shows that you respect the manager's busy schedule.","t":"A：我覺得我的信快寫好了，但結尾那句感覺太短，我可以用什麼禮貌的話來感謝公司？ B：你可以寫「感謝您撥冗【考慮】我的申請」，因為這句話很有禮貌，也顯示你尊重經理忙碌的行程。"},{"w":"appreciate","p":"v.","d":"to be thankful for something","c":"感謝；感激","s":"A: The manager of the design studio replied to my letter within one day and gave me some helpful advice about my portfolio, so should I write back? B: Yes, write a short email saying you really appreciate her quick reply and her advice, and tell her you will send the new portfolio by Friday.","t":"A：設計工作室的經理一天內就回了我的信，還給我一些關於作品集的有用建議，我該回信嗎？ B：要，寫一封簡短的電子郵件說你很【感謝】她迅速回覆和她的建議，並告訴她你會在星期五前寄出新的作品集。"},{"w":"response","p":"n.","d":"an answer to a letter, email, or question","c":"回覆；回應","s":"A: I sent my letter to the trading company two weeks ago, and nobody has called or emailed me since then, so is it rude to contact them again? B: It is not rude at all, so send a polite email asking about your application, because a quick response is not always possible when they have many applicants.","t":"A：我兩週前把信寄給那家貿易公司，到現在都沒人打電話或寄信給我，再聯絡他們會不禮貌嗎？ B：一點也不會，寄一封有禮貌的信詢問你的申請狀況吧，因為應徵者很多時，他們不一定能很快【回覆】。"},{"w":"contact","p":"v.","d":"to call, email, or write to someone","c":"聯絡","s":"A: At the end of my letter, I want the manager to know how she can reach me quickly if she wants to set up a meeting, so what should I write? B: Write \"Please contact me at 0912-345-678 or by email at any time,\" and make sure the number and the address are correct.","t":"A：在信的最後，我想讓經理知道如果她想安排面談，要怎樣快速找到我，我該寫什麼？ B：寫「歡迎隨時撥打0912-345-678或以電子郵件與我【聯絡】」，並確認電話號碼和地址正確無誤。"},{"w":"soon","p":"adv.","d":"in a short time from now","c":"很快；不久","s":"A: My letter is finished, but my teacher says the last line should sound hopeful and friendly, not like a demand, so how should I end it? B: You can write \"I look forward to hearing from you soon,\" because almost every business letter in English uses this kind of hopeful closing sentence.","t":"A：我的信寫完了，但老師說最後一句應該聽起來充滿期待又友善，而不是像在要求，我該怎麼結尾？ B：你可以寫「期待【很快】收到您的消息」，因為幾乎每一封英文商業書信都會用這種帶著期待的結尾句。"},{"w":"sincerely","p":"adv.","d":"used before your name at the end of a formal letter","c":"敬上（正式信件結尾用語）","s":"A: I started my letter with \"Dear Ms. Wang\" because I know the manager's name from the website, so which closing phrase should I write before my name? B: Since you know her name, you should write \"Yours sincerely,\" which is the most common polite ending for formal business letters in English.","t":"A：我的信是以「親愛的王小姐」開頭，因為我從網站上知道經理的名字，在我的名字前該用哪個結尾語？ B：既然你知道她的名字，就應該寫「Yours 【sincerely（謹啟）】」，這是英文正式商業書信最常見的禮貌結尾。"},{"w":"faithfully","p":"adv.","d":"used at the end of a formal British letter when you do not know the person's name","c":"敬上（英式正式信件，不知收件人姓名時用）","s":"A: The British company did not give the name of the hiring manager, so I started my letter with \"Dear Sir or Madam,\" and now I need an ending. B: In British English, when you do not know the person's name, you should finish with \"Yours faithfully,\" and then sign your full name below it.","t":"A：那家英國公司沒有提供招聘經理的姓名，所以我的信以「敬啟者」開頭，現在我需要一個結尾。 B：在英式英文中，當你不知道對方姓名時，應該以「Yours 【faithfully（謹上）】」結尾，然後在下方簽上你的全名。"}]},{"unit":18,"theme":"Appointment 預約","cards":[{"w":"schedule","p":"v.","d":"to plan something for a certain time","c":"安排（時間）；排定","s":"A: The new client from Tokyo wants to visit our factory and see the production line next week, so what should I do first? B: Please schedule a visit for Tuesday morning, because the machines run all day then, and send him the address and a map before the weekend.","t":"A：東京來的新客戶下週想來參觀我們的工廠和生產線，我該先做什麼？ B：請把參觀【安排】在星期二早上，因為那天機器整天運轉，並在週末前把地址和地圖寄給他。"},{"w":"booking","p":"n.","d":"an arrangement to have a seat, room, or service at a certain time","c":"預訂；預約","s":"A: Our team dinner for the sales award is on Friday night, and that Italian restaurant is always full on weekends, so did anyone call them? B: Yes, I made a booking for twelve people at seven o'clock, and the restaurant also promised to give us a private room in the back.","t":"A：我們慶祝業績獎的團隊晚餐在星期五晚上，那家義大利餐廳週末總是客滿，有人打電話給他們了嗎？ B：有，我做了七點十二個人的【預訂】，餐廳還答應給我們後面的一間包廂。"},{"w":"reserve","p":"v.","d":"to ask for a room, seat, or table to be kept for you","c":"預訂；保留","s":"A: More than forty people from different branches will come to the training day next month, and our meeting rooms are too small, so where can we hold it? B: I will reserve the large conference hall at the hotel across the street, because it has a projector, good sound, and enough chairs for everyone.","t":"A：下個月有四十多位來自不同分公司的人要來參加訓練日，我們的會議室太小了，可以在哪裡舉辦？ B：我會【預訂】對街飯店的大型會議廳，因為那裡有投影機、良好的音響，也有足夠的椅子給每個人。"},{"w":"reservation","p":"n.","d":"an arrangement to keep a room, table, or ticket for someone","c":"預約；訂位","s":"A: I arrived at the hotel in Singapore after a long flight, but the front desk says they cannot find my name in their system, so what can I do? B: Show them the email with your reservation number, and if they still have a problem, call our travel agent, who booked the room for you last month.","t":"A：我長途飛行後抵達新加坡的飯店，但櫃台說系統裡找不到我的名字，我該怎麼辦？ B：給他們看有你【訂房】編號的電子郵件，如果還有問題，就打給上個月幫你訂房的旅行社人員。"},{"w":"meeting","p":"n.","d":"an event where people come together to discuss something","c":"會議","s":"A: The marketing manager wants to talk with everyone about the new product launch, but half of the team works from home on Mondays, so when should we do it? B: Let's hold the meeting on Wednesday afternoon in Room 5, and we can also share a video link for anyone who cannot come in person.","t":"A：行銷經理想跟大家談新產品上市的事，但星期一有一半的團隊在家工作，我們該什麼時候進行？ B：我們星期三下午在五號會議室開【會議】吧，也可以分享視訊連結給無法親自出席的人。"},{"w":"consultation","p":"n.","d":"a meeting to get advice from an expert","c":"諮詢；諮商","s":"A: Our company wants to open a store in Japan next year, but none of us understand the local tax rules very well, so who can help us? B: I have booked a consultation with a tax expert in Osaka next Thursday, and she will explain the rules and the forms we need to prepare.","t":"A：我們公司明年想在日本開店，但我們沒有人很了解當地的稅務規定，誰能幫我們？ B：我已經預約了下週四和大阪一位稅務專家的【諮詢】，她會說明相關規定和我們需要準備的表格。"},{"w":"interview","p":"n.","d":"a formal meeting where someone is asked questions, for example for a job","c":"面試","s":"A: The human resources office called me this morning about the assistant job I applied for last week, and they sounded very friendly, so what did they say? B: They invited me to an interview at ten o'clock on Monday, and they asked me to bring my diploma and two copies of my resume.","t":"A：人資部今天早上打電話給我，談我上週應徵的助理工作，他們聽起來很友善，他們說了什麼？ B：他們邀請我星期一十點去【面試】，還要我帶畢業證書和兩份履歷影本。"},{"w":"session","p":"n.","d":"a period of time used for a particular activity","c":"（一段）時間；場次","s":"A: The new accounting software is quite difficult, and many staff members have asked for help using it, so how are we going to train everyone? B: We will hold a two-hour training session every Friday afternoon this month, and each person can choose the week that fits their work schedule best.","t":"A：新的會計軟體相當難用，很多員工都要求協助，我們要怎麼訓練每個人？ B：這個月每週五下午我們會舉辦兩小時的訓練【場次】，每個人可以選擇最符合自己工作時間的那一週。"},{"w":"time slot","p":"n.phr.","d":"a short period of time that is kept for one appointment or activity","c":"時段","s":"A: I need to see the eye doctor before my business trip next week, but the clinic's website says almost every day is full, so is there any chance? B: There is only one free time slot left on Thursday at 4:30, so you should book it online right now before someone else takes it.","t":"A：我下週出差前需要看眼科醫生，但診所網站說幾乎每天都額滿了，還有機會嗎？ B：星期四四點半只剩下一個空的【時段】，你應該現在就上網預約，免得被別人搶走。"},{"w":"availability","p":"n.","d":"the times when someone is free to meet or do something","c":"有空的時間；可用性","s":"A: The director wants to meet all five department heads before the budget is finished, but they all have very different schedules, so how can we find a time? B: I will send everyone an online form today to check their availability for next week, and then I will choose the time that works for most people.","t":"A：主任想在預算定案前和五位部門主管見面，但他們的行程都很不一樣，我們要怎麼找到時間？ B：我今天會寄一份線上表單給每個人，確認他們下週【有空的時間】，然後選一個大多數人都可以的時間。"},{"w":"calendar","p":"n.","d":"a list of dates or a digital tool showing your plans and appointments","c":"行事曆","s":"A: I keep forgetting my meetings with clients because I write them on small pieces of paper that I often lose, so do you have any advice? B: Put every appointment in the shared online calendar, because it sends you alerts on your phone and your assistant can see your plans too.","t":"A：我老是忘記和客戶的會面，因為我把它們寫在常常弄丟的小紙條上，你有什麼建議嗎？ B：把每個約會都記在共用的線上【行事曆】，因為它會在你手機上發出提醒，你的助理也能看到你的安排。"},{"w":"confirm","p":"v.","d":"to say or show that something is definite or correct","c":"確認","s":"A: The visitors from the German supplier are flying in on Sunday night, and they plan to come to our office on Monday, but I am not sure about the time. B: Please call their assistant this afternoon to confirm the meeting time, so we can prepare the room and order lunch for everyone.","t":"A：德國供應商的訪客星期天晚上搭機抵達，他們打算星期一來我們辦公室，但我不確定時間。 B：請你今天下午打電話給他們的助理【確認】會議時間，這樣我們才能準備會議室並幫大家訂午餐。"},{"w":"confirmation","p":"n.","d":"a message or document that says something is definite","c":"確認（函）","s":"A: I booked the train tickets for our trip to the trade show in Taichung online last night, but I have not received anything yet, so is something wrong? B: Check your spam folder, because the website usually sends a confirmation email within ten minutes, and you will need its code to pick up the tickets.","t":"A：我昨晚在網路上訂了去台中參加商展的火車票，但到現在什麼都還沒收到，是出了什麼問題嗎？ B：檢查一下你的垃圾郵件匣，因為網站通常會在十分鐘內寄出【確認】信，你取票時需要信裡的代碼。"},{"w":"reminder","p":"n.","d":"a message that helps you remember something","c":"提醒（通知）","s":"A: Many patients forget their appointments at our clinic, and the doctors end up waiting with nothing to do, so how can we fix this problem? B: We can send each patient a text reminder one day before the visit, and they can reply to it if they need to change the time.","t":"A：我們診所很多病人忘記約診，醫生最後只能空等，我們要怎麼解決這個問題？ B：我們可以在看診前一天傳簡訊【提醒】每位病人，如果他們需要改時間也可以直接回覆。"},{"w":"reschedule","p":"v.","d":"to change the time or date of a planned event","c":"改期；重新安排時間","s":"A: My flight back from Hong Kong was delayed, so I will not be in the office on Thursday, but I have a meeting with the bank that morning. B: Then you should call the bank today and reschedule the meeting for Friday or next Monday, because they need you to sign the loan papers in person.","t":"A：我從香港回來的班機延誤了，所以星期四不會進辦公室，但那天早上我和銀行有會議。 B：那你今天應該打電話給銀行，把會議【改期】到星期五或下週一，因為他們需要你親自簽貸款文件。"},{"w":"postpone","p":"v.","d":"to move an event to a later time","c":"延後；延期","s":"A: A strong typhoon is expected to hit northern Taiwan on Saturday, and our company picnic is planned for that day in the park, so what should we do? B: We should postpone the picnic until the following weekend, and I will send an email to all staff members this afternoon to let them know.","t":"A：預計星期六會有強烈颱風侵襲北台灣，而我們的公司野餐就安排在那天在公園舉行，我們該怎麼辦？ B：我們應該把野餐【延後】到下個週末，我今天下午會寄電子郵件通知所有員工。"},{"w":"cancel","p":"v.","d":"to say that a planned event will not happen","c":"取消","s":"A: The client from Seoul just emailed to say she is sick and cannot travel this week, but we booked a hotel room and a car for her. B: Please cancel the hotel room and the car service right away, because we can still get our money back if we tell them before noon today.","t":"A：首爾的客戶剛寄信說她生病了，這週不能出差，但我們已經幫她訂了飯店房間和車子。 B：請馬上【取消】飯店房間和派車服務，因為如果我們今天中午前通知，還能拿回退款。"},{"w":"cancellation","p":"n.","d":"the act of stopping a planned event or order","c":"取消","s":"A: Our hotel has many guests who book rooms and then simply do not arrive, which costs us a lot of money during the busy season, so what can we do? B: We could charge a cancellation fee of fifty percent if guests do not tell us at least two days before their arrival date.","t":"A：我們飯店有很多客人訂了房卻沒來，在旺季讓我們損失很多錢，我們能怎麼做？ B：如果客人沒有在入住日前至少兩天告知我們，我們可以收取百分之五十的【取消】費用。"},{"w":"delay","p":"v.","d":"to make something happen later than planned","c":"延誤；耽擱","s":"A: The heavy rain this morning has caused terrible traffic on the highway, and the delivery truck is still stuck near Taoyuan, so will the client meeting still start on time? B: I think we must delay the start of the meeting by thirty minutes, because the samples we want to show the client are on that truck.","t":"A：今天早上的大雨造成高速公路嚴重塞車，送貨卡車還卡在桃園附近，客戶會議還能準時開始嗎？ B：我想我們必須把會議開始時間【延後】三十分鐘，因為我們要給客戶看的樣品就在那輛卡車上。"},{"w":"punctual","p":"adj.","d":"arriving or doing something at the right time, not late","c":"準時的；守時的","s":"A: Our new client from Switzerland is coming at nine o'clock tomorrow, and I heard that people in her company care a lot about time, so is that true? B: Yes, she is always very punctual, so please be in the lobby by 8:50, and make sure the meeting room is ready before she arrives.","t":"A：我們瑞士的新客戶明天九點要來，我聽說她公司的人很重視時間，是真的嗎？ B：是的，她總是非常【守時】，所以請你八點五十分前到大廳，並確保她到達前會議室已經準備好。"},{"w":"late","p":"adj.","d":"arriving or happening after the expected time","c":"遲到的；晚的","s":"A: I am stuck in a long line of cars because of an accident on the bridge, and my appointment with the lawyer starts in ten minutes, so what should I do? B: Call her office now and tell them you will be about twenty minutes late, because it is polite to let people know before the meeting begins.","t":"A：因為橋上發生車禍，我被困在長長的車陣裡，而我和律師的約再十分鐘就開始了，我該怎麼辦？ B：現在就打電話到她的事務所，告訴他們你大約會【遲到】二十分鐘，因為在會面開始前通知對方是禮貌。"},{"w":"early","p":"adj.","d":"arriving or happening before the expected time","c":"提早的；早的","s":"A: This is my first time visiting the government office to renew my business license, and I heard there are always long lines, so when should I go? B: You should be early and arrive before they open at eight thirty, because by ten o'clock the waiting room is usually completely full.","t":"A：這是我第一次去政府機關更新營業執照，聽說那裡總是大排長龍，我該什麼時候去？ B：你應該【提早】，在他們八點半開門前就到，因為到了十點，等候室通常就完全坐滿了。"},{"w":"urgent","p":"adj.","d":"very important and needing action immediately","c":"緊急的","s":"A: The computer system in the accounting office stopped working an hour ago, and the staff cannot send any invoices to clients, so what is the plan? B: I have asked the IT company for an urgent visit this afternoon, because we must send all the monthly invoices before the end of today.","t":"A：會計室的電腦系統一小時前當機了，員工沒辦法寄任何發票給客戶，計畫是什麼？ B：我已經請資訊公司今天下午【緊急】到場，因為我們必須在今天結束前寄出所有月結發票。"},{"w":"fixed","p":"adj.","d":"not able to be changed","c":"固定的","s":"A: Can we move the presentation for the investors to Thursday, because two people on our team are still finishing the sales charts and need more time? B: I am afraid the date is fixed, since the investors are flying in from Hong Kong only for Wednesday, so we must finish the charts tonight.","t":"A：我們可以把對投資人的簡報改到星期四嗎？因為我們團隊有兩個人還在完成銷售圖表，需要更多時間。 B：恐怕日期是【固定的】，因為投資人只為了星期三從香港飛來，所以我們今晚必須完成圖表。"},{"w":"flexible","p":"adj.","d":"able to change easily","c":"有彈性的；可變通的","s":"A: The supplier wants to visit us next week to show their new packaging, but my schedule is full of meetings, so can you meet them for me? B: Sure, my schedule is quite flexible next week, so I can see them any morning or afternoon, and I will tell you what they show me.","t":"A：供應商下週想來展示他們的新包裝，但我的行程排滿了會議，你可以替我和他們見面嗎？ B：當然，我下週的行程很【有彈性】，所以早上或下午都能見他們，我會告訴你他們展示了什麼。"},{"w":"attend","p":"v.","d":"to go to an event such as a meeting or class","c":"出席；參加","s":"A: The headquarters in Singapore is holding a sales conference next month, and the manager wants two people from our office to go, so who will it be? B: She has asked Emily and me to attend the conference, because we handled the biggest accounts this year and can share our results with the other teams.","t":"A：新加坡總部下個月要舉辦業務會議，經理希望我們辦公室派兩個人去，會是誰？ B：她請艾蜜莉和我去【參加】這場會議，因為我們今年負責最大的客戶，可以和其他團隊分享我們的成果。"},{"w":"miss","p":"v.","d":"to not go to something or not be there at the right time","c":"錯過；缺席","s":"A: I overslept this morning because my phone battery died, and I did not hear the alarm, so what happened at the eight o'clock meeting? B: Do not worry too much, because you only had to miss the first part, and I took notes on the new sales targets, so I can share them with you now.","t":"A：我今天早上因為手機沒電沒聽到鬧鐘而睡過頭，八點的會議發生了什麼事？ B：別太擔心，因為你只是【錯過】了前半段，我有記下新的業績目標筆記，現在可以和你分享。"},{"w":"arrange","p":"v.","d":"to plan and organize something","c":"安排","s":"A: The new manager from our Tokyo office is visiting Taipei next week, and she has never been to Taiwan before, so how can we help her? B: I will arrange a car to pick her up at the airport, and I will also plan a short tour of our three stores on her first afternoon.","t":"A：東京辦公室的新經理下週要來台北，她以前從沒來過台灣，我們能怎麼幫她？ B：我會【安排】一輛車去機場接她，也會規劃在她第一天下午簡短參觀我們的三家門市。"},{"w":"booked","p":"adj.","d":"already reserved, so no more places are available","c":"（被）預訂的；客滿的","s":"A: My boss asked me to find a hotel near the convention center for the trade show next weekend, but I have already called three places, so is there a problem? B: Most hotels in that area are fully booked because of the show, so you should try the hotels near the train station, which are only fifteen minutes away.","t":"A：老闆要我找一家下週末商展時會展中心附近的飯店，我已經打了三家，是有什麼問題嗎？ B：因為商展的關係，那一帶大部分飯店都已經【被訂滿了】，你應該試試火車站附近的飯店，離那裡只有十五分鐘。"},{"w":"officially","p":"adv.","d":"in a formal way that is accepted by people in charge","c":"正式地","s":"A: Everyone in the office is talking about the new branch manager, but I have not received any email or notice about it, so is it really true? B: It is true, but she will start her job officially on the first of next month, and the director will introduce her at the staff meeting on Monday.","t":"A：辦公室裡大家都在談論新的分店經理，但我沒收到任何電子郵件或通知，這是真的嗎？ B：是真的，但她要到下個月一號才【正式】上任，主任會在星期一的員工會議上介紹她。"},{"w":"promptly","p":"adv.","d":"quickly and without delay; exactly at the right time","c":"準時地；迅速地","s":"A: Last week, the training started almost twenty minutes late because some people were still getting coffee, and the trainer was quite unhappy, so what should we do this time? B: Please remind everyone that the session will begin promptly at nine o'clock, and ask them to take their seats five minutes before that.","t":"A：上週訓練幾乎晚了二十分鐘才開始，因為有些人還在拿咖啡，講師很不高興，這次我們該怎麼做？ B：請提醒大家課程將在九點【準時】開始，並請他們提前五分鐘入座。"}]},{"unit":19,"theme":"Argument 爭論","cards":[{"w":"dispute","p":"n.","d":"a serious disagreement, often between groups or companies","c":"糾紛；爭議","s":"A: Why hasn't the shipping company delivered our new office furniture yet, even though we paid for it two months ago and they promised it last week? B: There is a dispute between them and the factory about the final price, and the lawyers say it may take another month before they agree on anything.","t":"A：我們兩個月前就付了錢，他們也承諾上週送達，為什麼貨運公司到現在還沒送來新的辦公家具？ B：他們和工廠之間對最終價格有【糾紛】，律師說可能還要一個月他們才能達成任何共識。"},{"w":"quarrel","p":"n.","d":"an angry argument between people who know each other","c":"爭吵；口角","s":"A: Why are Tom and Kevin sitting so far apart in the meeting room today, when they usually work together on every project and eat lunch together? B: They had a small quarrel yesterday about who should present the report to the director, and now they are both too proud to say sorry first.","t":"A：湯姆和凱文平常每個專案都一起做、也一起吃午餐，為什麼今天在會議室坐得那麼遠？ B：他們昨天為了誰該向主任報告而起了小【口角】，現在兩個人都太驕傲，不肯先道歉。"},{"w":"conflict","p":"n.","d":"a situation where people strongly disagree or want different things","c":"衝突","s":"A: The sales team wants to lower our prices to win more customers, but the finance team says we will lose money, so what is the manager going to do? B: She will meet both teams on Friday to solve this conflict, because the company cannot plan next year's budget until everyone agrees on the prices.","t":"A：業務團隊想降價來爭取更多客戶，但財務團隊說我們會賠錢，經理打算怎麼做？ B：她星期五會和兩個團隊開會解決這個【衝突】，因為在大家對價格達成共識之前，公司沒辦法規劃明年的預算。"},{"w":"debate","p":"n.","d":"a discussion in which people give different opinions on a subject","c":"辯論；討論","s":"A: The board members spent almost three hours yesterday talking about whether we should open a new factory in Vietnam, so did they decide anything at last? B: Not yet, because the debate is still going on, and some members think the costs are too high while others believe the cheaper workers will help us grow.","t":"A：董事會成員昨天花了將近三個小時談論我們是否該在越南開新工廠，他們最後有做出決定嗎？ B：還沒有，因為這場【辯論】還在進行中，有些成員認為成本太高，有些則相信較便宜的人力能幫助我們成長。"},{"w":"clash","p":"n.","d":"a short, strong disagreement or fight","c":"衝突；交鋒","s":"A: I heard there was a lot of shouting in the warehouse this morning, and some workers stopped working for almost an hour, so what happened down there? B: There was a clash between the night shift and the morning shift about who left the loading area so messy, but the supervisor calmed everyone down.","t":"A：我聽說今天早上倉庫裡吵得很兇，有些工人停工了將近一個小時，那裡發生了什麼事？ B：夜班和早班為了誰把裝貨區弄得那麼亂起了【衝突】，不過主管讓大家都冷靜下來了。"},{"w":"disagree","p":"v.","d":"to have a different opinion from someone","c":"不同意；意見不合","s":"A: The manager suggested moving our weekly team meeting from Monday morning to Friday afternoon, so what do you think about her new plan? B: I disagree with her, because many people leave early on Fridays to visit their families, and they would probably miss important news about the week ahead.","t":"A：經理建議把每週的團隊會議從星期一早上改到星期五下午，你覺得她的新計畫怎麼樣？ B：我【不同意】她的看法，因為很多人星期五會提早離開去探望家人，他們可能會錯過下週的重要消息。"},{"w":"argue","p":"v.","d":"to speak angrily with someone because you disagree","c":"爭論；爭吵","s":"A: The two designers were talking very loudly in the meeting room after lunch, and I could hear them from my desk, so is everything all right? B: They often argue about colors and fonts when a deadline is close, but they always find a good solution and stay friends after the project is finished.","t":"A：兩位設計師午餐後在會議室裡講話很大聲，我在座位上都聽得到，一切都還好嗎？ B：截止日快到時，他們常常為了顏色和字體【爭論】，但他們總能找到好的解決方法，專案結束後也依然是朋友。"},{"w":"contest","p":"v.","d":"to formally say that a decision or result is wrong","c":"對…提出異議；爭辯","s":"A: The city government fined our restaurant for putting tables on the sidewalk, but we have a permit that allows us to do that, so what should we do? B: We should contest the fine by sending a copy of our permit to the city office, and our lawyer can help us write a formal letter.","t":"A：市政府因為我們餐廳在人行道上擺桌子而開罰，但我們有允許這麼做的許可證，該怎麼辦？ B：我們應該把許可證影本寄到市政府來對罰單【提出異議】，我們的律師可以幫忙寫正式的信函。"},{"w":"oppose","p":"v.","d":"to disagree with a plan and try to stop it","c":"反對","s":"A: The company wants to build a large parking lot behind our office, but that would mean cutting down all the old trees there, so how do people feel about it? B: Many staff members oppose the plan, because they enjoy eating lunch under those trees, and they have already signed a letter to the director.","t":"A：公司想在我們辦公室後面蓋一座大型停車場，但這表示要砍掉那裡所有的老樹，大家覺得怎麼樣？ B：很多員工【反對】這個計畫，因為他們喜歡在那些樹下吃午餐，而且已經聯名寫信給主任了。"},{"w":"complaint","p":"n.","d":"a statement that you are unhappy about something","c":"抱怨；客訴","s":"A: A customer called this morning and said that her new washing machine was delivered with a broken door, and she sounded very upset, so what did you do? B: I wrote down her complaint in our system and promised that a technician would visit her home tomorrow to replace the door for free.","t":"A：今天早上有位顧客打電話說她的新洗衣機送到時門是壞的，她聽起來很不高興，你怎麼處理？ B：我把她的【客訴】記錄在系統裡，並承諾明天會有技術人員到她家免費更換洗衣機門。"},{"w":"accusation","p":"n.","d":"a statement saying that someone has done something wrong","c":"指控；指責","s":"A: Our new supplier says that our company copied their product design, and they have sent an angry email to our president, so is this a serious problem? B: It is serious, but the accusation is not true, because we have drawings that show our designers finished the design two years before theirs.","t":"A：我們的新供應商說我們公司抄襲他們的產品設計，還寄了一封很生氣的信給我們總裁，這是嚴重的問題嗎？ B：是很嚴重，但這項【指控】不是真的，因為我們有設計圖可以證明我們的設計師比他們早兩年完成設計。"},{"w":"blame","p":"v.","d":"to say that someone is responsible for something bad","c":"責怪；歸咎","s":"A: The project was finished three weeks late, and the client is very unhappy with us, so whose fault was it in the end? B: It is not fair to blame only one person, because the supplier was late, the designs changed twice, and our team was also too small.","t":"A：這個專案晚了三週才完成，客戶對我們非常不滿，最後到底是誰的錯？ B：只【責怪】一個人並不公平，因為供應商延誤、設計改了兩次，我們的團隊人手也太少。"},{"w":"criticism","p":"n.","d":"words that say what is bad or wrong about something","c":"批評","s":"A: The director said many negative things about my marketing plan in front of everyone at the meeting today, and I felt quite embarrassed. B: Try not to take the criticism personally, because she wants the plan to succeed, and her comments about the budget could make your next version much stronger.","t":"A：主任今天在會議上當著大家的面對我的行銷計畫說了很多負面的話，我覺得很難堪。 B：試著不要把這些【批評】當成針對你個人，因為她希望這個計畫成功，她對預算的意見可能會讓你的下一版更有力。"},{"w":"tension","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of worry and anger between people","c":"緊張（關係）","s":"A: Since the company announced it might close one of the two branches, the people in our office seem very quiet and nervous, so have you noticed it too? B: Yes, there is a lot of tension between the two branches now, because everyone is worried about losing their job and nobody wants to share information.","t":"A：自從公司宣布可能要關閉兩間分公司中的一間，我們辦公室的人似乎都很安靜又緊張，你也注意到了嗎？ B：有，現在兩間分公司之間的【緊張關係】很嚴重，因為大家都擔心丟了工作，沒有人願意分享資訊。"},{"w":"hostility","p":"n.","d":"unfriendly and angry feelings or behavior","c":"敵意","s":"A: When the new manager from headquarters came to visit our factory, many workers would not even say hello to her, so why were they so unfriendly? B: There is some hostility toward headquarters because they cut everyone's bonus last year, and the workers still feel that nobody listened to them.","t":"A：總部的新經理來參觀我們工廠時，很多工人連招呼都不跟她打，他們為什麼那麼不友善？ B：大家對總部有些【敵意】，因為他們去年削減了每個人的獎金，工人們到現在仍覺得沒有人聽他們的意見。"},{"w":"anger","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling you have when something is unfair or wrong","c":"憤怒；怒氣","s":"A: The passengers at Gate 12 have been waiting for over four hours because of the delay, and some of them are now shouting at the airline staff, so what should we do? B: We should offer them free meals and a clear update right away, because that will help reduce their anger while the engineers fix the plane.","t":"A：12號登機門的乘客因為班機延誤已經等了四個多小時，有些人現在正對航空公司人員大吼，我們該怎麼辦？ B：我們應該馬上提供免費餐點和清楚的最新消息，因為在工程師修理飛機時，這能幫助緩和他們的【怒氣】。"},{"w":"frustration","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being upset because you cannot do what you want","c":"挫折感；沮喪","s":"A: The new computer system crashes almost every afternoon, and our team cannot finish the orders on time, so what did people say at the meeting? B: Many people talked about their frustration with the system, and the manager promised to ask the IT company to fix the problem by the end of the week.","t":"A：新的電腦系統幾乎每天下午都當機，我們團隊沒辦法準時完成訂單，會議上大家說了什麼？ B：很多人談到他們對這套系統的【挫折感】，經理承諾會請資訊公司在這週結束前解決問題。"},{"w":"escalate","p":"v.","d":"to become more serious or worse","c":"升級；惡化","s":"A: The customer who complained about the late delivery is now threatening to post bad reviews online and call a lawyer, so how should we deal with him? B: We must act quickly before the situation can escalate any further, so please call him today, say sorry, and offer him a full refund.","t":"A：那位抱怨送貨延誤的客戶現在威脅要上網留負評並找律師，我們該怎麼處理他？ B：我們必須在情況進一步【惡化】之前趕快行動，所以請你今天打給他、向他道歉，並提供全額退款。"},{"w":"provoke","p":"v.","d":"to cause a strong, often angry reaction","c":"激起；挑釁","s":"A: The company is planning to send an email that says all workers must work on Saturdays next month without extra pay, so do you think that is a good idea? B: No, that email will surely provoke a lot of anger among the staff, so the managers should explain the reason and offer extra days off instead.","t":"A：公司打算寄一封電子郵件，說所有員工下個月星期六都得上班而且沒有加班費，你覺得這是好主意嗎？ B：不是，那封信一定會【激起】員工很大的怒氣，所以主管們應該說明原因，並改為提供額外的休假。"},{"w":"defend","p":"v.","d":"to speak in support of someone or something that is criticized","c":"為…辯護；捍衛","s":"A: At the meeting yesterday, the director said our new advertisement was too expensive and not very creative, so did anyone say anything about it? B: Yes, Linda stood up to defend the advertisement, and she showed charts proving that it brought in twice as many new customers as last year's one.","t":"A：昨天會議上主任說我們的新廣告太貴又不夠有創意，有人對此表示什麼嗎？ B：有，琳達站起來為這支廣告【辯護】，並拿出圖表證明它帶來的新客戶是去年那支的兩倍。"},{"w":"justify","p":"v.","d":"to give a good reason for something","c":"證明…有理；為…辯解","s":"A: The finance manager wants to know why our department spent so much money on taxis and hotels last month, so what should I tell her? B: You need to justify each cost with receipts and a short note, for example that the client meetings in Taichung ended late and there were no trains.","t":"A：財務經理想知道我們部門上個月為什麼花了那麼多錢在計程車和飯店上，我該怎麼跟她說？ B：你需要用收據和簡短說明來【證明】每一筆費用是合理的，例如在台中的客戶會議結束得很晚，已經沒有火車了。"},{"w":"assert","p":"v.","d":"to say something firmly and with confidence","c":"斷言；堅稱","s":"A: The client says our team made a mistake in the contract and wants us to pay for the extra costs, but our lawyer read it carefully, so what does she think? B: She continues to assert that the contract is completely correct, and she has prepared a letter that explains each section clearly for the client.","t":"A：客戶說我們團隊在合約中犯了錯，要我們負擔額外費用，但我們的律師仔細讀過了，她怎麼看？ B：她依然【堅稱】合約完全正確，並準備了一封信，為客戶清楚說明每一個條款。"},{"w":"counter","p":"v.","d":"to answer an argument by giving a different opinion","c":"反駁；回應","s":"A: During the negotiation, the buyer said our prices were much higher than the prices of other suppliers in Asia, so how did our sales manager respond to that? B: She was able to counter his point by showing that our products last twice as long and come with a free five-year service plan.","t":"A：談判時，買方說我們的價格比亞洲其他供應商高出許多，我們的業務經理是怎麼回應的？ B：她拿出證據說明我們的產品耐用度是兩倍，還附贈五年免費維修方案，成功【反駁】了他的論點。"},{"w":"compromise","p":"n.","d":"an agreement in which each side gives up something it wants","c":"妥協；折衷","s":"A: The workers want a ten percent pay raise, but the company says it can only afford three percent this year, so is there any way to end this disagreement? B: I think a compromise is possible, such as a six percent raise with two extra days off, because both sides really want to avoid a strike.","t":"A：工人想加薪百分之十，但公司說今年只負擔得起百分之三，有沒有辦法結束這個分歧？ B：我認為可能找到【折衷】方案，例如加薪百分之六再多兩天假，因為雙方都真的想避免罷工。"},{"w":"resolution","p":"n.","d":"the act of solving a problem or ending a disagreement","c":"解決（方法）","s":"A: The two companies have been arguing about the unpaid bill for almost six months, and the lawyers' fees are getting very expensive, so is there any good news yet? B: Yes, they finally found a resolution yesterday, and they agreed to share the cost equally and continue working together on the new project.","t":"A：兩家公司為了這筆未付帳款爭執將近六個月，律師費越來越貴，有任何好消息了嗎？ B：有，他們昨天終於找到了【解決方法】，同意平均分擔費用並繼續合作新專案。"},{"w":"reconcile","p":"v.","d":"to become friendly with someone again after an argument","c":"和解；使和好","s":"A: The two founders of the company stopped speaking to each other last year after a big argument about money, so is it true that they are working together again? B: Yes, a close friend helped them reconcile last month, and now they are planning to open a new store in Taichung together next spring.","t":"A：公司的兩位創辦人去年為了錢大吵一架後就不跟對方說話了，聽說他們又一起合作了，是真的嗎？ B：是的，上個月一位好友幫他們【和解】，現在他們正計畫明年春天一起在台中開一家新店。"},{"w":"negotiate","p":"v.","d":"to discuss something in order to reach an agreement","c":"談判；協商","s":"A: The rent for our office will go up by twenty percent next year, and our budget is already very tight, so do we have to accept the new price? B: Not necessarily, because the manager plans to negotiate with the owner next week and ask for a smaller increase if we sign a five-year contract.","t":"A：我們辦公室的租金明年要漲百分之二十，我們的預算已經很緊了，我們一定要接受新價格嗎？ B：不一定，因為經理打算下週和房東【協商】，如果我們簽五年約，就請他少漲一點。"},{"w":"calm","p":"adj.","d":"quiet and not angry or nervous","c":"冷靜的；平靜的","s":"A: A very angry customer is standing at the front desk and shouting about his missing package, and the new receptionist looks scared, so what should she do? B: She should stay calm, speak slowly and politely, and then call the delivery company to find out where the package is right now.","t":"A：一位非常生氣的顧客站在櫃台大吼他遺失的包裹，新來的接待員看起來很害怕，她該怎麼做？ B：她應該保持【冷靜】，慢慢地、有禮貌地說話，然後打電話給貨運公司查出包裹現在在哪裡。"},{"w":"heated","p":"adj.","d":"full of angry and excited feelings","c":"激烈的；激動的","s":"A: The meeting about the new working hours went on for three hours yesterday, and I heard people were shouting, so was it really that bad? B: It was a very heated discussion, because many parents on the team cannot start work at seven, but in the end, the manager agreed to change the plan.","t":"A：昨天關於新工作時間的會議開了三個小時，我聽說有人在大吼，真的那麼糟嗎？ B：那是一場非常【激烈】的討論，因為團隊裡很多家長沒辦法七點開始上班，不過最後經理同意修改計畫。"},{"w":"verbal","p":"adj.","d":"spoken, not written","c":"口頭的；言語的","s":"A: The supplier says we agreed to pay a higher price on the phone last month, but I cannot find that agreement in any of our emails, so is it real? B: It was only a verbal agreement, so we should ask them to send everything in writing before we pay any extra money.","t":"A：供應商說我們上個月在電話中同意支付更高的價格，但我在任何電子郵件中都找不到這項協議，這是真的嗎？ B：那只是【口頭】協議，所以在我們支付任何額外款項之前，應該請他們把所有內容以書面寄來。"},{"w":"hostile","p":"adj.","d":"very unfriendly and ready to argue","c":"有敵意的；不友善的","s":"A: The local people at the town meeting did not seem to like our plan for the new shopping mall, and some of them were shouting, so how did it go? B: The crowd was quite hostile at first, but after we explained the new jobs and the free parking, many of them started to listen.","t":"A：鎮民大會上當地居民似乎不喜歡我們新購物中心的計畫，有些人還在大吼，結果怎麼樣？ B：一開始群眾相當【有敵意】，但在我們說明會有新工作和免費停車之後，很多人開始願意聽了。"},{"w":"peacefully","p":"adv.","d":"in a calm way without fighting or arguing","c":"和平地；平靜地","s":"A: Our two neighbors in the office building have argued about the shared parking spaces for months, and the building manager is tired of it, so what happened today? B: They finally sat down together and solved the problem peacefully, and now each company has five spaces with its name painted on the ground.","t":"A：我們辦公大樓的兩個鄰居為了共用停車位吵了好幾個月，大樓管理員也受夠了，今天發生了什麼事？ B：他們終於坐下來，【和平地】解決了問題，現在每家公司都有五個地上漆著公司名稱的車位。"},{"w":"openly","p":"adv.","d":"in an honest way, without hiding anything","c":"公開地；坦率地","s":"A: Many people on our team are unhappy about the new schedule, but nobody says anything at meetings because they are worried about the boss, so what can we do? B: The boss should invite everyone to talk openly about their concerns, and promise that no one will get into trouble for sharing an honest opinion.","t":"A：我們團隊很多人對新的排班不滿，但開會時沒人敢說話，因為他們擔心老闆，我們能怎麼辦？ B：老闆應該邀請大家【坦率地】說出他們的顧慮，並承諾沒有人會因為說出真心話而惹上麻煩。"}]},{"unit":20,"theme":"Art 藝術","cards":[{"w":"aesthetic","p":"n.","d":"a particular style or idea of what is beautiful","c":"美感；美學風格","s":"A: The new café near our office is always full, even though its coffee costs more than the shops around it, so why do so many people go there? B: Customers love its simple Japanese aesthetic, with wooden tables, soft lights, and plants everywhere, so they enjoy taking photos and sharing them online.","t":"A：我們辦公室附近那家新咖啡廳總是客滿，雖然咖啡比附近店家貴，為什麼那麼多人去？ B：顧客很喜歡它簡約的日式【美學風格】，有木頭桌、柔和的燈光，到處都是植物，所以他們喜歡拍照並上傳網路分享。"},{"w":"composition","p":"n.","d":"the way the parts of a picture or piece of music are arranged","c":"構圖；（作品的）組成","s":"A: The photographer took hundreds of pictures of our new product yesterday, but the marketing manager only chose three of them for the brochure, so why did she pick those? B: She said their composition was the best, because the product is in the center, the background is simple, and the light falls nicely on the logo.","t":"A：攝影師昨天幫我們的新產品拍了好幾百張照片，但行銷經理只選了三張放進手冊，她為什麼選那幾張？ B：她說那幾張的【構圖】最好，因為產品位於中央、背景簡單，光線也很好地打在商標上。"},{"w":"harmony","p":"n.","d":"a pleasant mix of colors, sounds, or parts that go well together","c":"和諧；協調","s":"A: The interior designer used blue, green, and light gray in our new meeting rooms, and everyone says the rooms feel very relaxing, so how did she choose those colors? B: She said these colors work in harmony with each other and with the view of the park, so people feel calm during long meetings.","t":"A：室內設計師在我們新會議室用了藍色、綠色和淺灰色，大家都說房間感覺很放鬆，她是怎麼選這些顏色的？ B：她說這些顏色彼此之間以及和公園景色都很【和諧】，所以大家在長時間開會時會覺得平靜。"},{"w":"texture","p":"n.","d":"the way a surface feels when you touch it","c":"質地；紋理","s":"A: The furniture company sent us two kinds of fabric for the new sofas in the hotel lobby, and both are the same color, so which one should we choose? B: I prefer the one with the soft texture, because guests will sit on these sofas for a long time while they wait, and it feels warm and comfortable.","t":"A：家具公司寄給我們兩種用在飯店大廳新沙發的布料，顏色都一樣，我們該選哪一種？ B：我比較喜歡【質地】柔軟的那一種，因為客人等候時會在沙發上坐很久，而那種布摸起來溫暖又舒服。"},{"w":"palette","p":"n.","d":"the range of colors an artist or designer uses","c":"色調；調色盤","s":"A: The new logo for our tea company looks very bright and modern, but some older customers say it does not feel like our brand anymore, so what can we do? B: The designer can try a softer color palette, such as light green and warm brown, which reminds people of fresh tea leaves and our long history.","t":"A：我們茶葉公司的新商標看起來非常鮮豔又現代，但有些老顧客說感覺不像我們的品牌了，我們能怎麼做？ B：設計師可以試試比較柔和的【色調】，例如淺綠和暖棕色，讓人聯想到新鮮茶葉和我們悠久的歷史。"},{"w":"rhythm","p":"n.","d":"a regular, repeated pattern of sounds or movements","c":"節奏","s":"A: The video for our new running shoes looks great, but the manager says it feels a little slow and boring, so how can we make it more exciting? B: We can add music with a strong rhythm, and then cut the video so that each step of the runners matches the beat of the drums.","t":"A：我們新跑鞋的影片看起來很棒，但經理說感覺有點慢又無聊，我們要怎麼讓它更刺激？ B：我們可以加上【節奏】強烈的音樂，然後剪輯影片，讓跑者的每一步都配合鼓聲的節拍。"},{"w":"contrast","p":"n.","d":"a clear difference between two things, such as colors","c":"對比","s":"A: Many customers say they cannot read the price tags in our store from far away, especially older people, so what is wrong with the design? B: The problem is the low contrast between the light yellow letters and the white background, so we should print the prices in dark blue instead.","t":"A：很多顧客說他們從遠處看不清楚我們店裡的價格標籤，尤其是年長者，設計出了什麼問題？ B：問題在於淡黃色字和白色背景之間的【對比】太低，所以我們應該改用深藍色印價格。"},{"w":"expression","p":"n.","d":"the showing of a feeling or idea through words, art, or the face","c":"表達；表現","s":"A: Our company is paying for an art class for staff every Friday evening, but some people say they cannot draw at all, so should they still join? B: Yes, they should, because the teacher says the class is about personal expression, not perfect drawing, and it is a great way to relax after work.","t":"A：公司每週五晚上出錢讓員工上美術課，但有些人說他們完全不會畫畫，他們還該參加嗎？ B：應該，因為老師說這堂課重點在於個人的【表達】，不是畫得完美，而且這是下班後放鬆的好方法。"},{"w":"inspire","p":"v.","d":"to give someone the idea or wish to do something","c":"啟發；激勵","s":"A: Why did the design team visit the old temples and night markets in Tainan last week, when they are supposed to be designing our new packaging? B: The manager hoped the trip would inspire them with new ideas, because she wants the packaging to show the colors and culture of southern Taiwan.","t":"A：設計團隊應該在設計我們的新包裝，為什麼上週跑去台南參觀老廟和夜市？ B：經理希望這趟旅程能【啟發】他們新的點子，因為她想讓包裝呈現南台灣的色彩和文化。"},{"w":"abstract","p":"adj.","d":"not showing people or things in a realistic way, but using shapes and colors","c":"抽象的","s":"A: The bank bought a large painting for the main lobby, but it only has circles and lines in red and black, and some customers ask what it means. B: It is an abstract painting, so it does not show any real objects, and the artist says each person can find their own meaning in the shapes.","t":"A：銀行買了一幅大畫掛在主大廳，但畫裡只有紅色和黑色的圓圈和線條，有些顧客問那是什麼意思。 B：那是一幅【抽象】畫，所以不呈現任何真實的物體，畫家說每個人都可以在這些形狀中找到自己的意義。"},{"w":"melody","p":"n.","d":"the main tune in a piece of music","c":"旋律","s":"A: Our new TV advertisement is finished, but the manager wants people to remember our brand after they hear the music only once, so what should we do? B: We should use a short and simple melody that people can easily hum, and play it again at the end when our logo appears.","t":"A：我們的新電視廣告完成了，但經理希望人們只聽過一次音樂就能記住我們的品牌，我們該怎麼做？ B：我們應該使用簡短好記、讓人容易哼唱的【旋律】，並在最後商標出現時再播放一次。"},{"w":"tone","p":"n.","d":"the general feeling or style of something, such as writing or music","c":"基調；語氣","s":"A: The poster for our charity concert looks very dark, and the music group thinks it may scare away families with children, so how should we change it? B: Let's use brighter colors and a happier photo, so the poster has a warm and friendly tone that matches the cheerful music of the concert.","t":"A：我們慈善音樂會的海報看起來很陰暗，樂團認為可能會嚇跑有小孩的家庭，我們該怎麼修改？ B：我們用比較明亮的顏色和比較歡樂的照片吧，讓海報有溫暖友善的【基調】，搭配音樂會歡快的音樂。"},{"w":"balance","p":"n.","d":"a pleasing arrangement in which no part looks too strong or heavy","c":"平衡","s":"A: The new website for our hotel has many large pictures on the left side and only a small block of text on the right, so does it look good to you? B: Not really, because the page has no balance, so we should make the pictures smaller and give the text more space on the right side.","t":"A：我們飯店的新網站左邊有很多大張圖片，右邊只有一小塊文字，你覺得好看嗎？ B：不太好看，因為頁面缺乏【平衡】，我們應該把圖片縮小，讓右邊的文字有更多空間。"},{"w":"dynamic","p":"adj.","d":"full of energy and movement","c":"充滿活力的；動感的","s":"A: The sports company wants its new advertisement to look exciting and powerful, but our first version shows the athletes just standing and smiling, so what should we change? B: We need more dynamic shots of the athletes jumping and running, with fast camera movement and bright lights, so the advertisement feels full of energy.","t":"A：那家運動公司希望新廣告看起來刺激又有力量，但我們的第一版只拍運動員站著微笑，我們該改什麼？ B：我們需要更多運動員跳躍和奔跑的【動感】鏡頭，加上快速的鏡頭移動和明亮的燈光，讓廣告充滿活力。"},{"w":"form","p":"n.","d":"the shape of something, or a type of art","c":"形式；形狀","s":"A: Our company wants to add some art to the garden in front of the new office building, but we cannot decide between paintings, photographs, and other ideas, so what do you suggest? B: I think a large metal sculpture is the best form of art for a garden, because it can stay outside in the rain and the sun.","t":"A：我們公司想在新辦公大樓前的花園增添一些藝術品，但我們在畫作、攝影和其他點子之間猶豫不決，你有什麼建議？ B：我認為大型金屬雕塑是最適合花園的藝術【形式】，因為它可以在雨天和大太陽下放在戶外。"},{"w":"improvise","p":"v.","d":"to make up music, words, or actions without planning","c":"即興演出；臨時發揮","s":"A: The band at our company dinner lost their song sheets in the taxi, and they are supposed to start playing in ten minutes, so are they going to cancel the show? B: No, the band leader says they will improvise for the first part of the evening, and their manager is bringing new copies from the studio.","t":"A：公司晚宴的樂團把樂譜掉在計程車上了，他們再十分鐘就要開始演奏，表演會取消嗎？ B：不會，樂團團長說晚會前半段他們會【即興演奏】，他們的經理正從錄音室帶新的樂譜過來。"},{"w":"mood","p":"n.","d":"the feeling that a place, picture, or piece of music gives you","c":"氛圍；情緒","s":"A: The owner of the new restaurant wants guests to feel relaxed and stay longer at dinner, but the room still feels cold and too bright, so what can we change? B: We can create a warm mood with soft yellow lights, quiet jazz music, and a few paintings of the countryside on the walls.","t":"A：新餐廳的老闆希望客人用晚餐時感到放鬆並待久一點，但空間還是感覺冰冷又太亮，我們能改什麼？ B：我們可以用柔和的黃色燈光、輕柔的爵士樂，再加上幾幅鄉村風景畫掛在牆上，營造溫暖的【氛圍】。"},{"w":"motif","p":"n.","d":"a shape or idea that is repeated in a design or work of art","c":"圖案；主題（重複出現的元素）","s":"A: The new uniforms for our hotel staff look nice, but the manager feels they do not show anything special about our hotel, so how can we improve them? B: We could add a small flower motif from our hotel logo on the collar and the pockets, so every uniform clearly matches the style of the building.","t":"A：我們飯店員工的新制服看起來不錯，但經理覺得無法展現我們飯店的特色，我們要怎麼改進？ B：我們可以在領口和口袋加上飯店商標中的小花【圖案】，讓每件制服都明顯和建築風格相配。"},{"w":"interpret","p":"v.","d":"to explain or understand the meaning of something","c":"詮釋；解讀","s":"A: Our art gallery is showing modern paintings this month, and many visitors say they do not understand them at all, so how can we help them? B: We can hire a guide to help visitors interpret each painting, and we can also put short notes beside the paintings in both Chinese and English.","t":"A：我們美術館這個月展出現代畫作，很多參觀者說完全看不懂，我們要怎麼幫助他們？ B：我們可以聘請導覽員幫助參觀者【解讀】每一幅畫，也可以在畫作旁放上中英文的簡短說明。"},{"w":"canvas","p":"n.","d":"a strong cloth that artists paint on, or a painting on it","c":"畫布；油畫","s":"A: The artist we hired is going to paint a large picture of the city for our new office lobby, so how big will the finished painting be? B: She is using a canvas that is three meters wide, so we will need to clear the wall near the entrance and ask the building manager for a special light.","t":"A：我們聘請的畫家要為新辦公室大廳畫一幅大型城市畫作，完成的畫會有多大？ B：她用的【畫布】有三公尺寬，所以我們需要清空入口附近的牆面，並請大樓管理員裝一盞特別的燈。"},{"w":"lyrical","p":"adj.","d":"expressing feelings in a beautiful, song-like way","c":"抒情的；如詩般的","s":"A: The hotel wants to play some music in the lobby in the evening, but the guests did not like the loud pop songs we tried last week, so what should we play now? B: Try some soft and lyrical piano music, because it sounds beautiful and emotional, and guests can still talk quietly while they wait.","t":"A：飯店想在晚上的大廳播放一些音樂，但客人不喜歡我們上週試的大聲流行歌曲，現在該播什麼？ B：試試輕柔又【抒情】的鋼琴音樂，因為它聽起來優美又感人，客人等候時也還能小聲交談。"},{"w":"vivid","p":"adj.","d":"very bright and strong (colors) or very clear (descriptions)","c":"鮮豔的；生動的","s":"A: Our travel agency's brochure for Hualien uses gray and pale photos, and very few customers have booked that tour, so how can we make it more attractive? B: We should use vivid pictures of the blue sea and the green mountains, because bright colors make people want to visit a place right away.","t":"A：我們旅行社的花蓮手冊用的是灰暗又淡的照片，很少顧客報名那個行程，要怎麼讓它更吸引人？ B：我們應該使用藍色大海和翠綠山脈的【鮮豔】照片，因為明亮的色彩會讓人想立刻去那個地方。"},{"w":"craft","p":"n.","d":"a skill of making things by hand, or the things made","c":"工藝；手藝","s":"A: Our company wants to give special gifts to our overseas clients this year, but we do not want to buy the usual cheap souvenirs from the airport, so do you have ideas? B: We could buy local bamboo craft from a small workshop in Nantou, because each piece is handmade and shows a traditional skill from Taiwan.","t":"A：公司今年想送特別的禮物給海外客戶，但不想買機場那種常見的便宜紀念品，你有什麼點子嗎？ B：我們可以向南投一間小工坊購買當地的竹【工藝】品，因為每件都是手工製作，展現台灣的傳統技藝。"},{"w":"symbolism","p":"n.","d":"the use of images or objects to represent ideas","c":"象徵手法；象徵意義","s":"A: The new poster for our bank shows a small tree growing out of a pile of coins, and some customers are asking why it looks like that, so what does it mean? B: The symbolism is simple, because the tree shows that your savings can grow slowly but strongly over time if you keep them in our bank.","t":"A：我們銀行的新海報畫著一棵從一堆硬幣中長出來的小樹，有些顧客在問為什麼長那樣，那是什麼意思？ B：它的【象徵意義】很簡單，那棵樹代表只要把存款放在我們銀行，你的儲蓄就能隨著時間慢慢穩健地成長。"},{"w":"tempo","p":"n.","d":"the speed of a piece of music","c":"（音樂的）速度；節拍","s":"A: The fitness center wants new music for its morning exercise class, but the members say the current songs are too slow to keep them moving, so what should we choose? B: Choose songs with a faster tempo, about one hundred and thirty beats per minute, because quick music helps people move and work harder.","t":"A：健身中心想為早上的運動課換新音樂，但會員說目前的歌太慢，沒辦法讓他們一直動，該選什麼？ B：選擇【速度】較快的歌，大約每分鐘一百三十拍，因為快節奏的音樂能幫助人們動起來、更賣力運動。"},{"w":"gesture","p":"n.","d":"a movement of the hands or body that shows a meaning or feeling","c":"手勢；姿態","s":"A: The dancer in our new advertisement only moves her hands slowly at the end, but the client says that last moment is the most important part, so why is that? B: Her final gesture looks like she is opening a door, and it shows that our company opens new chances for young people.","t":"A：我們新廣告裡的舞者在最後只是慢慢地移動雙手，但客戶說最後那一刻是最重要的部分，為什麼？ B：她最後的【手勢】看起來像是在打開一扇門，表示我們公司為年輕人開啟新的機會。"},{"w":"creative","p":"adj.","d":"good at making new and original things or ideas","c":"有創意的","s":"A: Our sales of the new juice are lower than we expected, and the old advertisements have not worked well with young people, so who should we ask for help? B: We should hire a more creative advertising team, because they can make fun short videos and new ideas that young people want to share online.","t":"A：我們新果汁的銷量比預期低，以前的廣告對年輕人效果不好，我們該找誰幫忙？ B：我們應該聘請一個更有【創意】的廣告團隊，因為他們能做出有趣的短影片和年輕人想上網分享的新點子。"},{"w":"nuance","p":"n.","d":"a very small difference in color, meaning, or feeling","c":"細微差別","s":"A: The translation of our English advertisement into Japanese is finished, but the manager in Tokyo says it sounds a little strange, so what is the problem? B: The translator missed a small nuance in the slogan, because the Japanese word sounds too serious, while the English one sounds friendly and light.","t":"A：我們英文廣告的日文翻譯完成了，但東京的經理說聽起來有點奇怪，問題在哪裡？ B：譯者漏掉了標語中一個【細微差別】，因為日文用字聽起來太嚴肅，而英文的則聽起來親切又輕鬆。"},{"w":"visual","p":"adj.","d":"relating to seeing or things that you can see","c":"視覺的","s":"A: Our sales presentation has twenty slides full of long sentences and numbers, and the clients looked bored last time, so how can we make it better? B: Let's add more visual information, such as charts, photos, and simple icons, because people understand and remember pictures much faster than long text.","t":"A：我們的業務簡報有二十張投影片，都塞滿長句和數字，上次客戶看起來很無聊，我們要怎麼改善？ B：我們多加一些【視覺】資訊吧，像是圖表、照片和簡單的圖示，因為人們理解和記住圖片的速度比長篇文字快得多。"},{"w":"perform","p":"v.","d":"to play music, dance, or act in front of an audience","c":"表演；演出","s":"A: The company's year-end party is in three weeks, and the manager wants some entertainment after dinner, so has anyone offered to do something? B: Yes, five people from the accounting department will perform a traditional dance, and they have been practicing every evening after work in the meeting room.","t":"A：公司尾牙再三週就到了，經理希望晚餐後有些表演節目，有人自願要做什麼嗎？ B：有，會計部的五個人要【表演】一支傳統舞蹈，他們每天下班後都在會議室裡練習。"}]},{"unit":21,"theme":"Athlete 運動員","cards":[{"w":"endurance","p":"n.","d":"the ability to keep doing something hard for a long time","c":"耐力","s":"A: Our company is sponsoring a runner in the Taipei Marathon this year, and the marketing team wants to make a short video about her, so what makes her special? B: She has amazing endurance, because she can run for more than three hours without slowing down, and she trains every morning before she goes to work.","t":"A：我們公司今年贊助一位參加台北馬拉松的跑者，行銷團隊想幫她拍一支短片，她有什麼特別之處？ B：她有驚人的【耐力】，可以跑三個多小時都不減速，而且她每天早上上班前都會練習。"},{"w":"strength","p":"n.","d":"the physical power of the body","c":"力量；體力","s":"A: The moving company wants to hire three new workers to carry furniture up and down stairs in old apartment buildings, so what should they look for? B: They need people with good physical strength, because the workers often have to carry heavy sofas and refrigerators up five floors without an elevator.","t":"A：搬家公司想再雇三名工人，在老公寓裡上下樓梯搬家具，他們應該找什麼樣的人？ B：他們需要體能【力量】好的人，因為工人常常得在沒有電梯的情況下把沉重的沙發和冰箱搬上五樓。"},{"w":"speed","p":"n.","d":"how fast someone or something moves","c":"速度","s":"A: The sports shoe company says its new running shoes are much lighter than last year's model, so why do professional runners like them so much? B: The lighter shoes help runners increase their speed in short races, and several athletes broke their personal records while wearing them at the national games.","t":"A：那家運動鞋公司說他們的新跑鞋比去年的款式輕很多，職業跑者為什麼這麼喜歡？ B：比較輕的鞋子能幫跑者在短跑比賽中提升【速度】，好幾位運動員穿著它在全國運動會上打破了個人紀錄。"},{"w":"agility","p":"n.","d":"the ability to move quickly and change direction easily","c":"敏捷","s":"A: The basketball coach at our company team keeps asking the players to run between small cones on the floor, and some of them think it is boring, so why does he do it? B: That exercise improves their agility, so they can turn quickly, move around other players, and react faster during real games.","t":"A：我們公司籃球隊的教練一直要球員在地上的小三角錐之間跑，有些人覺得很無聊，他為什麼要這樣做？ B：那個練習能提升他們的【敏捷度】，讓他們在真正比賽時能迅速轉身、繞過其他球員並更快反應。"},{"w":"stamina","p":"n.","d":"the energy to keep doing physical or mental work for a long time","c":"體力；精力","s":"A: The tour guides at our travel agency often walk with groups for eight hours a day in the mountains, and some new guides feel very tired by lunchtime, so what can help them? B: They should go swimming or jogging a few times a week to build up their stamina, so they will not feel so tired on long tours.","t":"A：我們旅行社的導遊常常一天帶團在山裡走八個小時，有些新導遊到午餐時間就覺得很累，有什麼辦法能幫助他們？ B：他們應該每週游泳或慢跑幾次來增強【體力】，這樣帶長途行程就不會那麼累了。"},{"w":"discipline","p":"n.","d":"the ability to control yourself and follow rules or plans","c":"自律；紀律","s":"A: How does that young tennis player manage to study at university and still train for four hours every day, when most students can barely finish their homework? B: She has very strong discipline, because she follows a strict schedule, goes to bed early, and never skips a training session, even on weekends.","t":"A：大部分學生連作業都快寫不完，那位年輕網球選手是怎麼一邊念大學、一邊每天練球四個小時的？ B：她非常【自律】，因為她遵守嚴格的時間表、早早上床睡覺，就算週末也從不缺席任何一次訓練。"},{"w":"dedicated","p":"adj.","d":"working hard because you care a lot about something","c":"投入的；專注的","s":"A: Our company wants to choose one local athlete to be the face of our new sports drink, and we have three names on the list, so who do you suggest? B: I suggest the swimmer from Kaohsiung, because she is very dedicated to her sport and also spends her free time teaching poor children to swim.","t":"A：我們公司想挑一位本地運動員擔任新運動飲料的代言人，名單上有三個人，你建議誰？ B：我建議那位高雄的游泳選手，因為她對這項運動非常【投入】，空閒時還會教弱勢孩童游泳。"},{"w":"competitive","p":"adj.","d":"wanting very much to win or be better than others","c":"好勝的；有競爭力的","s":"A: When we play basketball after work on Fridays, Jason always gets angry when his team loses, even though it is only a friendly game, so why is he like that? B: He is very competitive, because he played on the national team in college, and he still hates losing at anything, even card games.","t":"A：我們週五下班後打籃球時，傑森的隊伍一輸他就生氣，雖然那只是友誼賽，他為什麼會這樣？ B：他非常【好勝】，因為他大學時是國家隊的，到現在還是很討厭輸，連玩牌都一樣。"},{"w":"training","p":"n.","d":"the process of preparing for a sport through exercise and practice","c":"訓練","s":"A: The baseball team that our bank sponsors will play in an important tournament in Japan next month, so how are the players getting ready for it? B: They have started a special training program that includes running, weight lifting, and batting practice six days a week, and they will rest only on Sundays.","t":"A：我們銀行贊助的棒球隊下個月要去日本參加重要的錦標賽，球員們怎麼準備？ B：他們開始了一套特別的【訓練】計畫，包含跑步、重量訓練和打擊練習，每週六天，只有星期天休息。"},{"w":"coach","p":"n.","d":"a person who trains athletes or a sports team","c":"教練","s":"A: Our company volleyball team has lost every game this season, and the players are starting to feel unhappy, so what does the manager plan to do? B: She wants to hire a professional coach who can train the team twice a week and teach them better ways to play together.","t":"A：我們公司的排球隊這一季每場比賽都輸，球員開始覺得不開心，經理打算怎麼做？ B：她想聘請一位專業【教練】，每週訓練球隊兩次，教他們更好的團隊打法。"},{"w":"technique","p":"n.","d":"a special way of doing something that needs skill","c":"技巧；技術","s":"A: The golf club is offering lessons for our sales team because many of our clients like to play golf, but none of us are good at it, so is it worth it? B: Yes, because the lessons will teach you the correct technique for holding the club and swinging it, so you can play with clients without feeling embarrassed.","t":"A：高爾夫球俱樂部要為我們業務團隊開課，因為很多客戶喜歡打高爾夫，但我們都打得不好，值得去上嗎？ B：值得，因為課程會教你握桿和揮桿的正確【技巧】，這樣你和客戶打球時就不會覺得難為情。"},{"w":"flexibility","p":"n.","d":"the ability to bend and stretch your body easily","c":"柔軟度","s":"A: Many people in our office complain about back pain after sitting at their desks all day, so the company wants to offer an exercise class, but which one? B: I think a yoga class is the best choice, because it improves flexibility and helps people stretch the muscles that become tight after long hours at the computer.","t":"A：我們辦公室很多人抱怨整天坐在辦公桌前造成背痛，公司想開一堂運動課，要開哪一種？ B：我認為瑜伽課是最好的選擇，因為它能改善【柔軟度】，幫助大家伸展長時間使用電腦後變緊繃的肌肉。"},{"w":"focus","p":"n.","d":"the act of giving all your attention to one thing","c":"專注；焦點","s":"A: The archer we interviewed for our sports magazine said she does not listen to music or look at her phone on the day of a competition, so why does she do that? B: She wants to keep her focus completely on the target, because even a small distraction can cause her to miss by a few centimeters.","t":"A：我們運動雜誌採訪的那位射箭選手說，比賽當天她不聽音樂也不看手機，她為什麼這樣做？ B：她想讓自己的【專注力】完全放在箭靶上，因為即使一點小小的分心都可能讓她偏差幾公分。"},{"w":"mental","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the mind","c":"心理的；精神的","s":"A: Our company now offers free talks with a sports psychologist for staff who play in the city tennis league, so why would players need that kind of help? B: Many players say that mental strength is just as important as physical skill, because staying calm under pressure often decides who wins a close game.","t":"A：我們公司現在為參加市立網球聯賽的員工提供和運動心理師免費談話的機會，球員為什麼需要那種協助？ B：很多球員說【心理】素質和體能技巧一樣重要，因為在壓力下保持冷靜往往決定誰能贏得勢均力敵的比賽。"},{"w":"resilient","p":"adj.","d":"able to recover quickly after something bad happens","c":"有韌性的；能迅速恢復的","s":"A: That baseball player hurt his shoulder badly last year, and many people thought his career was over, so how is he playing so well this season? B: He is very resilient, because he worked hard with doctors for months, never gave up, and came back even stronger than before.","t":"A：那位棒球選手去年肩膀受了重傷，很多人以為他的職業生涯結束了，他這一季怎麼打得這麼好？ B：他非常【有韌性】，因為他和醫生努力了好幾個月，從不放棄，回來後甚至比以前更強。"},{"w":"motivation","p":"n.","d":"the reason or energy that makes you want to do something","c":"動力；動機","s":"A: Our company started a walking challenge last month, but many people stopped joining after the first two weeks, so how can we get them interested again? B: We can give small prizes every week, because rewards often increase people's motivation, and we can show each team's steps on a big screen in the lobby.","t":"A：公司上個月開始了健走挑戰，但很多人在前兩週後就不參加了，我們要怎麼讓他們重新感興趣？ B：我們可以每週發小獎品，因為獎勵常常能提高人們的【動力】，也可以在大廳的大螢幕上顯示每一隊的步數。"},{"w":"practice","p":"n.","d":"the regular activity of doing something again and again to improve","c":"練習","s":"A: Why does our company soccer team meet in the park at six thirty every Tuesday and Thursday morning, before the office opens? B: They have practice twice a week before work, because many players have family duties in the evening and the park is quiet and cool early in the morning.","t":"A：為什麼我們公司的足球隊每週二和週四早上六點半，在辦公室開門前就到公園集合？ B：他們每週上班前有兩次【練習】，因為很多球員晚上要照顧家庭，而且公園一大早既安靜又涼爽。"},{"w":"recovery","p":"n.","d":"the process of getting healthy again after an injury or hard exercise","c":"恢復；康復","s":"A: Our star runner hurt her knee during training last month, and the big race is in eight weeks, so can she still compete in it? B: The doctor says her recovery is going well, and if she continues her treatment and rests properly, she should be ready to race in about six weeks.","t":"A：我們的明星跑者上個月訓練時傷了膝蓋，而大型比賽在八週後，她還能參賽嗎？ B：醫生說她的【康復】狀況良好，只要繼續治療並適當休息，大約六週後就能準備好比賽。"},{"w":"performance","p":"n.","d":"how well someone does in a game or activity","c":"表現","s":"A: The sports drink company wants to know if their new product really helps athletes, so how are they going to test it this summer? B: They will measure each runner's performance in races with and without the drink, and then they will compare the results to see if there is a real difference.","t":"A：運動飲料公司想知道他們的新產品是否真的對運動員有幫助，今年夏天他們打算怎麼測試？ B：他們會測量每位跑者在有喝和沒喝飲料時比賽的【表現】，然後比較結果，看看是否真的有差異。"},{"w":"strategy","p":"n.","d":"a plan for achieving a goal","c":"策略；戰術","s":"A: Our company team is playing against the bank's team in the final of the basketball tournament next week, and they are much taller than us, so how can we win? B: We need a smart strategy, such as passing the ball quickly and shooting from far away, so their tall players cannot block us easily.","t":"A：我們公司隊下週要在籃球錦標賽決賽中對上銀行隊，他們比我們高很多，我們要怎麼贏？ B：我們需要聰明的【戰術】，例如快速傳球和遠距離投籃，讓他們的高個子球員沒辦法輕易阻擋我們。"},{"w":"injury","p":"n.","d":"harm done to the body, for example in an accident or sport","c":"受傷；傷害","s":"A: Our best soccer player could not play in yesterday's game, and the team lost by three goals, so what happened to him? B: He has a knee injury from a fall during practice last week, and the doctor told him to rest for at least a month before he plays again.","t":"A：我們最好的足球員沒辦法參加昨天的比賽，球隊輸了三球，他發生了什麼事？ B：他上週練習時跌倒造成膝蓋【受傷】，醫生要他至少休息一個月才能再上場。"},{"w":"conditioning","p":"n.","d":"exercise that makes the body fit and strong for a sport","c":"體能訓練；體能狀況","s":"A: The new fitness coach at our company gym makes the volleyball players run up and down the stairs for twenty minutes before each practice, so what is the point of that? B: It is part of their conditioning program, because it builds the strong legs and heart they need to jump and play hard for the whole match.","t":"A：我們公司健身房的新體能教練每次練習前都要排球員在樓梯上下跑二十分鐘，這樣做有什麼用意？ B：那是他們【體能訓練】計畫的一部分，因為它能鍛鍊出整場比賽跳躍和全力打球所需的強壯雙腿和心臟。"},{"w":"balance","p":"n.","d":"the ability to stay steady without falling","c":"平衡（感）","s":"A: The sports equipment store wants to sell more of its new surfboards this summer, but many beginners are afraid to try surfing, so what can the store do? B: The store can offer free lessons on the beach, where teachers show beginners how to keep their balance on the board before they go into the deeper water.","t":"A：運動用品店今年夏天想多賣一些新的衝浪板，但很多初學者不敢嘗試衝浪，店家能怎麼做？ B：店家可以在海灘上提供免費課程，讓老師在初學者下到深水區之前，教他們如何在板子上保持【平衡】。"},{"w":"coordination","p":"n.","d":"the ability to make different parts of the body work well together","c":"協調性","s":"A: The video game company wants to test whether its new dance game is good exercise for children, so what will the researchers measure during the study? B: They will check the children's coordination before and after two months of playing, because the game asks players to move their hands and feet together to the music.","t":"A：電玩公司想測試他們的新跳舞遊戲對孩子來說是否是好的運動，研究人員在研究期間會測量什麼？ B：他們會在孩子玩兩個月前後檢查他們的【協調性】，因為這個遊戲要求玩家隨著音樂同時移動手腳。"},{"w":"power","p":"n.","d":"physical strength and force","c":"力量；爆發力","s":"A: The sports company is making an advertisement for its new tennis racket, and it wants to show how strong the racket is, so what kind of scene should we film? B: We should film a famous player hitting a serve with great power, and then show the ball flying past the other player at more than two hundred kilometers an hour.","t":"A：運動公司在為新網球拍拍廣告，想展現球拍有多強，我們該拍什麼樣的畫面？ B：我們應該拍一位知名選手以強大【力量】發球，然後呈現球以時速超過兩百公里飛過對手身邊。"},{"w":"goal-oriented","p":"adj.","d":"focused on reaching a clear aim","c":"目標導向的","s":"A: The sales manager said that she likes to hire former athletes for her team, but she did not explain why, so what do you think her reason is? B: Former athletes are usually very goal-oriented, so they set clear targets, plan each step carefully, and keep working hard until they reach them.","t":"A：業務經理說她喜歡雇用前運動員加入團隊，但她沒解釋原因，你覺得她的理由是什麼？ B：前運動員通常非常【目標導向】，所以他們會設定明確的目標、仔細規劃每一步，並且持續努力直到達成。"},{"w":"compete","p":"v.","d":"to take part in a race or contest in order to win","c":"比賽；競爭","s":"A: Our company has sent five of its staff members to the city's half-marathon every year, and they always enjoy it, so who is joining this year? B: This year, ten people want to compete in the race, so we will order matching shirts with our company logo and arrange a bus to the starting line.","t":"A：我們公司每年都派五名員工參加市區半程馬拉松，他們總是玩得很開心，今年有誰參加？ B：今年有十個人想【參加】這場比賽，所以我們會訂製印有公司商標的同款上衣，並安排巴士送大家到起點。"},{"w":"teamwork","p":"n.","d":"the ability of a group to work well together","c":"團隊合作","s":"A: Our company volleyball team does not have any very tall or famous players, but they won the city tournament this year, so how did they do it? B: Their teamwork was excellent, because they talked to each other on every point, trusted each other, and always covered for a teammate who made a mistake.","t":"A：我們公司排球隊沒有很高或很有名的球員，但今年卻贏得了市錦標賽，他們是怎麼做到的？ B：他們的【團隊合作】非常出色，因為每一分他們都互相溝通、彼此信任，而且總是幫犯錯的隊友補位。"},{"w":"victory","p":"n.","d":"a win in a game, competition, or fight","c":"勝利","s":"A: The baseball team that our company sponsors won the national championship last night, and the whole office is talking about it, so how should we celebrate? B: Let's hold a small party for the team on Friday to celebrate their victory, and we can put a big photo of them holding the trophy in the lobby.","t":"A：我們公司贊助的棒球隊昨晚贏得全國冠軍，整個辦公室都在討論，我們該怎麼慶祝？ B：我們星期五為球隊辦個小派對慶祝他們的【勝利】吧，還可以在大廳放一張他們捧著獎盃的大照片。"}]},{"unit":22,"theme":"Bags 包包","cards":[{"w":"backpack","p":"n.","d":"a bag you carry on your back with two straps","c":"背包；後背包","s":"A: I have to walk from the train station to the client's office every morning this week, and my laptop and files are getting heavy, so what kind of bag should I buy? B: You should get a backpack with padded straps, because it spreads the weight across both shoulders and leaves your hands free for your phone and umbrella.","t":"A：這週我每天早上都得從火車站走到客戶辦公室，筆電和文件越來越重，我該買什麼樣的包包？ B：你應該買一個肩帶有襯墊的【後背包】，因為它能把重量分散在兩邊肩膀上，讓你的雙手可以拿手機和雨傘。"},{"w":"handbag","p":"n.","d":"a small bag that women often use to carry money, keys, and other things","c":"手提包","s":"A: The department store wants to put a new display near the main entrance before Mother's Day, so which products should we show there to attract shoppers? B: We should display our new leather handbag in red and cream, because many customers buy them as gifts for their mothers and they look great in the window.","t":"A：百貨公司想在母親節前於大門口附近擺一個新的展示區，我們該展示哪些商品來吸引顧客？ B：我們應該展示紅色和米色的新款皮革【手提包】，因為很多顧客會買來當作送給媽媽的禮物，而且放在櫥窗裡很好看。"},{"w":"tote","p":"n.","d":"a large open bag with two handles, used for carrying many things","c":"托特包；大手提袋","s":"A: Our company is giving away free gifts at the trade show next month, and the manager wants something useful that people will keep, so what do you suggest? B: Let's give each visitor a cotton tote with our logo on it, because people can use it for shopping, and our name will be seen all over the city.","t":"A：我們公司下個月要在商展上贈送免費禮物，經理想要大家會留著用的實用東西，你有什麼建議？ B：我們送每位參觀者一個印有公司商標的棉布【托特包】吧，因為大家可以拿來購物，我們的名字就會出現在城市各處。"},{"w":"satchel","p":"n.","d":"a bag with a long strap and a flap, often used for books or papers","c":"側背書包；公事包","s":"A: My new job is at a law office, and I need to carry a lot of papers and a small laptop to court, but I do not like backpacks, so what is a good choice? B: A brown leather satchel would look professional, because it has a long shoulder strap, a flap that closes tightly, and enough room for your documents.","t":"A：我的新工作在律師事務所，需要帶很多文件和一台小筆電去法院，但我不喜歡後背包，有什麼好選擇？ B：一個棕色皮革【側背公事包】看起來會很專業，因為它有長肩帶、可以緊緊扣住的掀蓋，空間也夠放你的文件。"},{"w":"clutch","p":"n.","d":"a small, flat bag without a handle, held in the hand, usually for formal events","c":"手拿包","s":"A: The company's year-end party is at a fancy hotel this year, and everyone has to dress formally, but my everyday bag is far too big, so what should I bring? B: You could carry a small silver clutch, because it holds your phone, keys, and a lipstick, and it looks elegant with an evening dress.","t":"A：今年公司尾牙在高級飯店舉行，大家都要穿正式服裝，但我平常的包包太大了，我該帶什麼？ B：你可以拿一個小小的銀色【手拿包】，因為它能裝手機、鑰匙和口紅，搭配晚禮服也很優雅。"},{"w":"duffel","p":"n.","d":"a large soft bag shaped like a tube, used for sports clothes or travel","c":"圓筒旅行袋；行李袋","s":"A: I am going on a three-day team-building trip in the mountains with my coworkers, and we have to carry our things from the bus to the cabin, so is a suitcase okay? B: A suitcase is hard to roll on the mountain path, so take a soft duffel instead, because you can carry it on your shoulder and squeeze it into small spaces.","t":"A：我要和同事去山上參加三天的團隊建立活動，我們得自己把東西從巴士搬到小木屋，帶行李箱可以嗎？ B：行李箱在山路上很難拉，所以改帶軟的【圓筒行李袋】吧，因為你可以把它扛在肩上，也能塞進狹小的空間。"},{"w":"pouch","p":"n.","d":"a small soft bag for keeping small things","c":"小袋子；收納包","s":"A: Every time I travel for work, my phone charger, earphones, and cables get mixed up at the bottom of my bag, and it takes forever to find them. B: Put them all in a small zip pouch, and then you can take everything out at once when you get to the hotel or the meeting room.","t":"A：每次出差，我的手機充電器、耳機和傳輸線都混在包包底部，要找很久才找得到。 B：把它們全部放進一個有拉鍊的小【收納包】，這樣到了飯店或會議室時，你就能一次把所有東西拿出來。"},{"w":"zipper","p":"n.","d":"a metal or plastic device with two rows of teeth that closes a bag or clothes","c":"拉鍊","s":"A: A customer brought back the suitcase she bought from our shop two weeks ago, and she seems quite upset, so what is wrong with it? B: The zipper on the front pocket broke on her first trip, so we should replace the suitcase for free and tell the factory to check that part more carefully.","t":"A：有位顧客把兩週前在我們店裡買的行李箱拿回來，她看起來很不高興，是出了什麼問題？ B：前面口袋的【拉鍊】在她第一次旅行時就壞了，所以我們應該免費幫她換一個行李箱，並請工廠更仔細檢查那個零件。"},{"w":"strap","p":"n.","d":"a narrow piece of leather or cloth used to carry a bag","c":"背帶；肩帶","s":"A: Many customers like the design of our new laptop bag, but some of them say it hurts their shoulder after they walk for a while, so how can we improve it? B: We can make the strap wider and add a soft pad, so the weight of the laptop does not press so hard on one small area of the shoulder.","t":"A：很多顧客喜歡我們新筆電包的設計，但有些人說走一陣子後肩膀會痛，我們要怎麼改進？ B：我們可以把【背帶】加寬並加上軟墊，這樣筆電的重量就不會集中壓在肩膀的一小塊地方。"},{"w":"compartment","p":"n.","d":"a separate section inside a bag for keeping things apart","c":"隔層；夾層","s":"A: I often carry my laptop and my lunch box in the same bag on my way to the office, and I am worried that the soup might leak onto the computer. B: Choose a bag with a separate padded compartment for the laptop, so your computer stays safe and dry even if something spills in the main part.","t":"A：我上班途中常把筆電和便當盒放在同一個包包裡，擔心湯會漏到電腦上。 B：選一個有獨立襯墊筆電【隔層】的包包，這樣即使主袋裡有東西灑出來，你的電腦也能保持安全乾燥。"},{"w":"pocket","p":"n.","d":"a small bag sewn onto or into a larger bag or clothes","c":"口袋","s":"A: At the airport, I always have to look through my whole bag to find my passport and boarding pass, and the people behind me in line get impatient. B: Keep them in the small outside pocket of your backpack, because you can reach it quickly without opening the main part of the bag.","t":"A：在機場我總是得翻遍整個包包才找得到護照和登機證，排在我後面的人都不耐煩了。 B：把它們放在後背包外側的小【口袋】裡，因為你不用打開包包主袋就能很快拿到。"},{"w":"lining","p":"n.","d":"a layer of material covering the inside of a bag","c":"內襯；襯裡","s":"A: The outside of this handbag is made of beautiful leather, but the price is much higher than the other bags on the shelf, so why does it cost so much? B: It has a silk lining inside, which protects your things and makes the bag look elegant every time you open it, and it is all sewn by hand.","t":"A：這個手提包外層是用漂亮的皮革做的，但價格比架上其他包包高很多，為什麼這麼貴？ B：它裡面有絲質【內襯】，能保護你的物品，每次打開包包時看起來都很優雅，而且全部都是手工縫製。"},{"w":"leather","p":"n.","d":"animal skin that is treated and used to make bags, shoes, and clothes","c":"皮革","s":"A: Our company wants to give the top salespeople a special gift at the end of the year, something that lasts for many years and looks professional, so what would be good? B: A briefcase made of real leather would be a great choice, because it becomes softer and more beautiful with age and can last more than ten years.","t":"A：公司想在年底送一份特別的禮物給頂尖業務員，要能用很多年又看起來專業的東西，什麼比較好？ B：真【皮】製的公事包會是很好的選擇，因為它會隨著時間變得更柔軟、更漂亮，而且可以用十年以上。"},{"w":"canvas","p":"n.","d":"a strong, heavy cloth used for bags, shoes, and tents","c":"帆布","s":"A: The bookstore wants to sell its own shopping bags, but the manager does not want plastic because many customers care about the environment, so which material should we use? B: We should use thick cotton canvas, because it is strong enough to carry heavy books, easy to print a logo on, and can be washed many times.","t":"A：書店想販售自己的購物袋，但經理不想用塑膠，因為很多顧客在意環保，我們該用什麼材質？ B：我們應該用厚棉【帆布】，因為它夠堅固能裝重的書、容易印上商標，而且可以洗很多次。"},{"w":"waterproof","p":"adj.","d":"not letting water go through","c":"防水的","s":"A: I will be visiting construction sites in Keelung all next week, and the weather report says it will rain almost every day, so how can I keep my documents dry? B: Use a waterproof bag with a roll-top opening, because even heavy rain cannot get inside, and your plans and contracts will stay completely dry.","t":"A：下週我整週都要去基隆的工地，氣象報告說幾乎每天都會下雨，我要怎麼讓文件保持乾燥？ B：用一個捲口式開口的【防水】包，因為就算大雨也進不去，你的設計圖和合約都能保持完全乾燥。"},{"w":"durable","p":"adj.","d":"able to last a long time without breaking","c":"耐用的","s":"A: Our delivery workers carry heavy packages in their bags all day, and the cheap bags we bought last year all fell apart within a few months, so what should we buy now? B: We need more durable bags made of thick nylon with strong stitching, even if they cost more, because they will last for several years and save money.","t":"A：我們的送貨員整天用包包背重物，去年買的便宜包包幾個月內就都壞了，我們現在該買什麼？ B：我們需要更【耐用】的包包，用厚尼龍和堅固的縫線製成，即使比較貴，因為它們能用好幾年，反而省錢。"},{"w":"lightweight","p":"adj.","d":"not heavy","c":"輕量的；輕便的","s":"A: The flight attendants at our airline walk through long airports every day with their bags, and many of them have complained about sore backs, so what can we do? B: We can give them new lightweight bags that weigh less than one kilogram when empty, so they will carry much less weight during long workdays.","t":"A：我們航空公司的空服員每天都要提著包包走過很長的機場，很多人抱怨背痛，我們能怎麼做？ B：我們可以發給他們空包重量不到一公斤的新款【輕量】包包，這樣他們在漫長的工作日中就能少背很多重量。"},{"w":"spacious","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of room inside","c":"寬敞的；容量大的","s":"A: I am going to Singapore for a week-long sales conference, and I need to bring business suits, product samples, and a laptop, so will my small bag be enough? B: No, you will need a more spacious suitcase, because the samples take up a lot of room, and you may also bring back gifts from the clients.","t":"A：我要去新加坡參加為期一週的業務會議，需要帶西裝、產品樣品和筆電，我的小包包夠用嗎？ B：不夠，你需要一個更【寬敞】的行李箱，因為樣品很佔空間，而且你可能還會帶客戶送的禮物回來。"},{"w":"compact","p":"adj.","d":"small and using little space","c":"小巧的；輕巧的","s":"A: Many young office workers in Taipei ride scooters to work, and they say large bags are hard to store under the seat, so what product should we design for them? B: We should design a compact bag that fits easily under a scooter seat but still holds a tablet, a wallet, and a raincoat.","t":"A：台北很多年輕上班族騎機車通勤，他們說大包包很難放進座墊下，我們該為他們設計什麼產品？ B：我們應該設計一款【小巧】的包包，能輕鬆放進機車座墊下，但還是能裝平板、皮夾和雨衣。"},{"w":"fashionable","p":"adj.","d":"popular and in a style that many people like now","c":"時髦的；流行的","s":"A: Our bags are well made and practical, but sales to young customers have been falling this year, so what do you think is the main problem? B: Young people want bags that look fashionable, so we should work with a popular designer and add brighter colors and modern shapes to our collection.","t":"A：我們的包包做工好又實用，但今年賣給年輕顧客的銷量一直下滑，你覺得主要問題是什麼？ B：年輕人想要看起來【時髦】的包包，所以我們應該和受歡迎的設計師合作，在產品系列中加入更亮的顏色和現代的造型。"},{"w":"functional","p":"adj.","d":"practical and useful, made to do a job well","c":"實用的；功能性的","s":"A: The customer survey shows that business travelers do not care much about the color of a bag, so what do they want most when they choose one? B: They want a functional bag with many pockets, a laptop section, and a charging port, because they need to work in airports and hotels.","t":"A：顧客調查顯示商務旅客不太在意包包的顏色，那他們挑選時最想要的是什麼？ B：他們想要一個【實用】的包包，有很多口袋、筆電夾層和充電孔，因為他們需要在機場和飯店工作。"},{"w":"capacity","p":"n.","d":"the amount that something can hold","c":"容量","s":"A: The hiking company wants to know which backpack it should rent to customers for the two-day mountain tour, because some customers carry a lot of clothes. B: Choose the one with a forty-liter capacity, because it holds clothes, food, and water for two days, but it is still light enough for most people.","t":"A：登山公司想知道兩天山區行程該出租哪一款背包給客人，因為有些客人會帶很多衣服。 B：選四十公升【容量】的那一款，因為它能裝兩天份的衣服、食物和水，而且對大多數人來說還是夠輕。"},{"w":"organize","p":"v.","d":"to arrange things in a neat and useful way","c":"整理；收納","s":"A: My bag is always so messy that I cannot find my pens, business cards, or keys when a client is waiting, and it makes me look unprofessional. B: You should organize your things with small pouches, putting each type of item in its own place, so you can find anything in a few seconds.","t":"A：我的包包總是很亂，客戶在等的時候我都找不到筆、名片或鑰匙，讓我看起來很不專業。 B：你應該用小收納袋來【整理】你的東西，把每一類物品放在固定的位置，這樣幾秒鐘就能找到任何東西。"},{"w":"carry","p":"v.","d":"to hold something and take it with you","c":"攜帶；拿","s":"A: The new rules at the factory say that workers cannot bring large bags onto the production floor, so where should they keep their personal things? B: They can only carry a small clear bag with their phone and water bottle, and everything else must stay in the lockers near the main entrance.","t":"A：工廠的新規定說工人不能帶大包包進入生產區，那他們的私人物品要放哪裡？ B：他們只能【攜帶】一個裝手機和水壺的小透明袋，其他東西都必須放在大門附近的置物櫃裡。"},{"w":"pack","p":"v.","d":"to put things into a bag or suitcase for a trip","c":"打包；收拾（行李）","s":"A: My flight to Tokyo leaves at seven tomorrow morning, and I still have a lot of work to finish at the office tonight, so when will I have time to get ready? B: You should pack your suitcase as soon as you get home, before you do anything else, so you can sleep early and not forget anything important.","t":"A：我飛東京的班機明天早上七點起飛，今晚在辦公室還有很多工作要做，我什麼時候才有時間準備？ B：你一到家就應該先【打包】行李，再做其他事，這樣你才能早點睡，也不會忘記任何重要的東西。"},{"w":"travel","p":"v.","d":"to go from one place to another, especially far away","c":"旅行；出差","s":"A: Our sales manager is going to Japan, Korea, and Thailand in two weeks, and she will only have one bag, so what kind should she take? B: She will travel light with a carry-on suitcase, because she can take it on the plane and avoid waiting at baggage claim in every airport.","t":"A：我們業務經理兩週後要去日本、韓國和泰國，她只會帶一個包包，她該帶哪一種？ B：她會帶一個登機箱輕裝【出差】，因為可以帶上飛機，在每個機場都不必等行李。"},{"w":"reusable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be used again and again","c":"可重複使用的","s":"A: The supermarket wants to stop giving out plastic bags next year, but some shoppers may be unhappy about it, so how can we help them change their habits? B: We can sell cheap reusable bags near the checkout and give a small discount to customers who bring their own bags from home.","t":"A：超市明年想停止提供塑膠袋，但有些購物者可能會不高興，我們要怎麼幫助他們改變習慣？ B：我們可以在結帳處附近販售便宜的【可重複使用】購物袋，並給自己從家裡帶袋子的顧客小折扣。"},{"w":"handle","p":"n.","d":"the part of a bag that you hold in your hand","c":"提把；把手","s":"A: The new shopping bags for our bakery look beautiful, but several customers said they broke when they carried heavy cakes home, so what went wrong? B: The paper handle is too thin for heavy boxes, so we should ask the printing company to use stronger rope instead.","t":"A：我們麵包店的新購物袋看起來很漂亮，但有幾位顧客說提重蛋糕回家時袋子壞了，問題出在哪裡？ B：紙製【提把】對重的盒子來說太薄了，所以我們應該請印刷公司改用比較堅固的繩子。"},{"w":"secure","p":"adj.","d":"safe and protected from being opened or stolen","c":"安全的；牢固的","s":"A: Many tourists in our city have complained about pickpockets in crowded night markets, so what kind of bag should our travel shop recommend to them? B: We should recommend a secure bag with hidden zippers and a lock, so thieves cannot open it easily while people are walking through crowds.","t":"A：我們城市很多觀光客抱怨在擁擠的夜市遇到扒手，我們旅行用品店應該推薦他們什麼樣的包包？ B：我們應該推薦有隱藏式拉鍊和鎖的【安全】包包，這樣人們走在人群中時，小偷就不容易打開。"}]},{"unit":23,"theme":"Baking 烘焙","cards":[{"w":"bake","p":"v.","d":"to cook food such as bread or cake in an oven","c":"烘烤；烘焙","s":"A: Our café has been buying cakes from a big factory, but customers say they do not taste fresh, so what can we do to improve them? B: We could hire a pastry chef to bake cakes in our own kitchen every morning, so customers can enjoy fresh cakes and smell them as soon as they walk in.","t":"A：我們咖啡廳一直向大工廠買蛋糕，但顧客說吃起來不新鮮，我們能怎麼改善？ B：我們可以聘請一位甜點師每天早上在自己的廚房【烘烤】蛋糕，讓顧客能吃到新鮮的蛋糕，一走進來就聞得到香味。"},{"w":"oven","p":"n.","d":"a box-shaped machine that heats and cooks food inside","c":"烤箱","s":"A: The bakery is getting more and more orders for birthday cakes, but the bakers can only make ten cakes at a time, so how can we increase production? B: We should buy a second large oven, because then the bakers can cook twenty cakes at the same time and finish all the orders before noon.","t":"A：麵包店接到的生日蛋糕訂單越來越多，但烘焙師一次只能做十個，我們要怎麼提高產量？ B：我們應該再買一台大型【烤箱】，這樣烘焙師就能同時烤二十個蛋糕，在中午前完成所有訂單。"},{"w":"dough","p":"n.","d":"a thick mix of flour and water used to make bread","c":"麵團","s":"A: The new pizza restaurant near our office is always full at lunchtime, and people say the pizza base is soft but crispy, so what is their secret? B: The owner told me they make the dough by hand every night and let it rest in the fridge for twenty-four hours before they use it.","t":"A：我們辦公室附近的新披薩店午餐時總是客滿，大家都說餅皮又軟又脆，他們的秘訣是什麼？ B：老闆告訴我，他們每天晚上手工製作【麵團】，並讓它在冰箱裡靜置二十四小時後才使用。"},{"w":"batter","p":"n.","d":"a liquid mix of flour, eggs, and milk used for cakes or pancakes","c":"麵糊","s":"A: The breakfast shop is going to start selling pancakes next month, but the cooks are worried that they will be too slow during the morning rush, so what can they do? B: They can prepare the batter the night before and keep it in the fridge, so in the morning they only need to pour it onto the hot pan.","t":"A：早餐店下個月要開始賣鬆餅，但廚師擔心早上尖峰時段會做得太慢，他們能怎麼辦？ B：他們可以前一天晚上先準備好【麵糊】放在冰箱，這樣早上只要倒在熱鍋上就好。"},{"w":"flour","p":"n.","d":"a powder made from wheat, used to make bread and cakes","c":"麵粉","s":"A: The price of our bread has gone up twice this year, and some customers have started to complain, so why are our costs rising so fast? B: The price of flour has risen because of the bad wheat harvest in several countries, and it is the main ingredient in almost everything we bake.","t":"A：我們的麵包今年漲價兩次了，有些顧客開始抱怨，為什麼我們的成本漲得這麼快？ B：因為好幾個國家小麥歉收，【麵粉】的價格上漲了，而它幾乎是我們所有烘焙產品的主要原料。"},{"w":"yeast","p":"n.","d":"a substance used to make bread rise and become soft","c":"酵母","s":"A: The new baker's bread came out flat and hard this morning, and we had to throw away three trays of rolls, so what went wrong in the kitchen? B: He used old yeast that had been open for months, so the dough could not grow, and we need to check the dates on everything in the storeroom.","t":"A：新烘焙師今天早上烤出來的麵包又扁又硬，我們只好丟掉三盤餐包，廚房裡出了什麼問題？ B：他用了開封好幾個月的舊【酵母】，所以麵團發不起來，我們需要檢查儲藏室裡所有東西的日期。"},{"w":"sugar","p":"n.","d":"a sweet substance used in food and drinks","c":"糖","s":"A: Many of our customers have asked for healthier cakes because they are trying to eat better, but they still want them to taste good, so what should we change? B: We can use less sugar in our recipes and add fresh fruit instead, because the fruit makes the cakes sweet in a more natural way.","t":"A：很多顧客要求更健康的蛋糕，因為他們想吃得更好，但還是希望好吃，我們該改什麼？ B：我們可以在食譜中少用一點【糖】，改加新鮮水果，因為水果能讓蛋糕以更自然的方式變甜。"},{"w":"butter","p":"n.","d":"a soft yellow food made from cream","c":"奶油","s":"A: Our croissants are much more expensive than the ones at the supermarket, and some customers ask why they should pay more, so what should we tell them? B: Tell them we use real French butter, which gives our croissants their rich taste and many light, flaky layers that cheap ones do not have.","t":"A：我們的可頌比超市的貴很多，有些顧客問為什麼要多付錢，我們該怎麼告訴他們？ B：告訴他們我們用的是真正的法國【奶油】，讓我們的可頌有濃郁的風味和許多輕盈酥脆的層次，這是便宜可頌沒有的。"},{"w":"mix","p":"v.","d":"to put different things together and stir them","c":"混合；攪拌","s":"A: The new kitchen helper is making cookies for the first time, and she is not sure what to do after measuring all the ingredients, so can you help her? B: Tell her to mix the butter and sugar first until they are soft and smooth, and then slowly add the eggs and the flour.","t":"A：新來的廚房助手第一次做餅乾，她量好所有材料後不確定接下來要做什麼，你能幫她嗎？ B：告訴她先把奶油和糖【攪拌】到柔軟滑順，然後再慢慢加入蛋和麵粉。"},{"w":"knead","p":"v.","d":"to press and fold dough again and again with your hands","c":"揉（麵團）","s":"A: The bakery is thinking about buying a large machine for making bread dough, but it costs a lot of money, so is it really worth it? B: Yes, because our bakers spend almost two hours every morning trying to knead the dough by hand, and the machine can do the same job in fifteen minutes.","t":"A：麵包店考慮買一台製作麵團的大型機器，但要花很多錢，真的值得嗎？ B：值得，因為我們的烘焙師每天早上要花將近兩小時用手【揉】麵團，而機器只要十五分鐘就能做好同樣的工作。"},{"w":"rise","p":"v.","d":"(of bread dough) to get bigger because of yeast","c":"（麵團）發酵膨脹","s":"A: Why do the bakers come to work at four o'clock in the morning, when the shop does not open until seven thirty? B: The bread dough needs about two hours to rise before it goes into the oven, so they must start very early to have fresh bread ready when customers arrive.","t":"A：店裡七點半才開門，為什麼烘焙師凌晨四點就要來上班？ B：麵團進烤箱前大約需要兩個小時【發酵膨脹】，所以他們必須很早開始，才能在顧客到來時準備好新鮮麵包。"},{"w":"proof","p":"v.","d":"to let bread dough rest so it can grow before baking","c":"（使麵團）醒發；發酵","s":"A: Our kitchen is very cold in winter, and the bread has been coming out smaller and heavier than usual, so how can we fix this problem? B: We can buy a warm cabinet to proof the dough at the right temperature, so it grows properly before baking even on the coldest mornings.","t":"A：我們的廚房冬天很冷，烤出來的麵包比平常小又重，要怎麼解決這個問題？ B：我們可以買一個保溫櫃，讓麵團在適當溫度下【醒發】，這樣即使在最冷的早晨，它也能在烘烤前好好膨脹。"},{"w":"preheat","p":"v.","d":"to heat an oven to the right temperature before cooking","c":"預熱","s":"A: The cookies from the new baker's first tray were pale and soft in the middle, but the second tray was perfect, so why did that happen? B: He forgot to preheat the oven before he put in the first tray, so the cookies started baking at a low temperature and did not cook evenly.","t":"A：新烘焙師第一盤餅乾顏色很淡、中間軟軟的，但第二盤卻很完美，為什麼會這樣？ B：他放第一盤之前忘了【預熱】烤箱，所以餅乾一開始是在低溫下烤，沒有烤得均勻。"},{"w":"pan","p":"n.","d":"a metal container used for baking or cooking","c":"烤盤；平底鍋","s":"A: Customers say our cakes sometimes break into pieces when we take them out for decorating, and we have wasted a lot of cakes this month, so what is the problem? B: We should put baking paper in each pan before we pour in the batter, so the cakes come out easily without sticking.","t":"A：顧客說我們的蛋糕在取出來裝飾時有時會碎掉，這個月我們浪費了很多蛋糕，問題出在哪？ B：我們應該在倒入麵糊前在每個【烤盤】裡鋪烘焙紙，這樣蛋糕就能輕鬆取出而不會沾黏。"},{"w":"measure","p":"v.","d":"to find the exact amount or size of something","c":"測量；量","s":"A: Our cakes taste a little different every day, and some customers have noticed it, so how can we make sure they always taste the same? B: Every baker must measure each ingredient with a digital scale instead of using cups or spoons, because even small differences can change the taste.","t":"A：我們的蛋糕每天吃起來都有點不一樣，有些顧客也注意到了，要怎麼確保味道始終如一？ B：每位烘焙師都必須用電子秤來【量】每一樣材料，而不是用量杯或湯匙，因為即使是小小的差異也會改變味道。"},{"w":"recipe","p":"n.","d":"a set of instructions for making a type of food","c":"食譜；配方","s":"A: Our pineapple cakes have been the most popular gift in the shop for twenty years, and a large company wants to buy our business, so what do they really want? B: They mainly want our secret recipe, because it was created by the owner's grandmother, and no other bakery knows exactly how to make the filling.","t":"A：我們的鳳梨酥二十年來都是店裡最受歡迎的伴手禮，有家大公司想收購我們，他們真正想要的是什麼？ B：他們主要是想要我們的秘密【配方】，因為那是老闆的祖母創造的，沒有其他麵包店知道內餡確切的做法。"},{"w":"texture","p":"n.","d":"the way food feels in your mouth","c":"口感；質地","s":"A: The test group liked the taste of our new rice bread, but some people said it was a little too sticky, so what should we change? B: We can add a little more wheat flour to make the texture lighter and softer, and then we will ask the group to try it again next week.","t":"A：試吃小組喜歡我們新米麵包的味道，但有些人說有點太黏，我們該改什麼？ B：我們可以多加一點小麥麵粉，讓【口感】更輕盈柔軟，然後下週再請試吃小組試一次。"},{"w":"crust","p":"n.","d":"the hard outside part of bread or a pie","c":"（麵包或派的）外皮","s":"A: The French customer who comes in every morning said our baguettes are good, but not quite like the ones in Paris, so what is different? B: She wants a harder and crispier crust, so we should bake the bread a little longer at a higher temperature and add steam at the beginning.","t":"A：每天早上來的那位法國顧客說我們的法國長棍不錯，但不太像巴黎的，有什麼不一樣？ B：她想要更硬更脆的【外皮】，所以我們應該用稍高的溫度烤久一點，並在一開始加入蒸氣。"},{"w":"crumb","p":"n.","d":"a very small piece of bread or cake; also the soft inside of bread","c":"麵包屑；麵包內部組織","s":"A: The cleaning staff say there is a lot of mess under the tables in our café every evening, and it takes them a long time to clean, so what is causing it? B: Every small crumb from the croissants falls on the floor, so we should serve them on larger plates and give customers more napkins.","t":"A：清潔人員說每天晚上咖啡廳桌子底下都很髒亂，要花很多時間清理，是什麼造成的？ B：可頌的每一小片【碎屑】都會掉到地上，所以我們應該用比較大的盤子盛裝，並給顧客多一點餐巾紙。"},{"w":"golden","p":"adj.","d":"having a warm yellow-brown color, like gold","c":"金黃色的","s":"A: How do the bakers know exactly when the egg tarts are ready to come out of the oven, because they do not use a timer? B: They watch the tops carefully, and when the pastry turns golden brown and the filling stops moving, they take the tray out right away.","t":"A：烘焙師沒有用計時器，他們怎麼知道蛋塔什麼時候可以出爐？ B：他們會仔細看塔的表面，當酥皮變成【金黃】褐色、內餡不再晃動時，就立刻把烤盤拿出來。"},{"w":"moist","p":"adj.","d":"slightly wet in a pleasant way, not dry","c":"濕潤的","s":"A: Several customers wrote online that our chocolate cake was too dry last week, and our rating dropped a little, so what should we do about it? B: We can add more butter and a little yogurt to keep the cake moist, and we should also store it in a sealed box instead of on the open shelf.","t":"A：上週有好幾位顧客在網路上留言說我們的巧克力蛋糕太乾，我們的評分也下降了一點，該怎麼辦？ B：我們可以多加點奶油和一些優格讓蛋糕保持【濕潤】，也應該把它存放在密封盒裡，而不是放在開放的架子上。"},{"w":"fluffy","p":"adj.","d":"soft, light, and full of air","c":"鬆軟的；蓬鬆的","s":"A: The Japanese pancakes at the new café are so popular that people wait in line for an hour, so what makes them so special? B: They are very tall and fluffy, because the cooks beat the egg whites until they are full of air, and the pancakes almost shake on the plate.","t":"A：新咖啡廳的日式鬆餅超受歡迎，大家要排一個小時，它們有什麼特別之處？ B：它們又高又【蓬鬆】，因為廚師把蛋白打到充滿空氣，鬆餅放在盤子上幾乎會晃動。"},{"w":"dense","p":"adj.","d":"heavy and thick, with little air inside","c":"紮實的；密實的","s":"A: Our new whole wheat bread is healthy, but some customers say it feels too heavy, and they do not buy it again, so how can we improve it? B: The bread is too dense because whole wheat flour is heavy, so we can mix in some white flour and let the dough rise a little longer.","t":"A：我們新的全麥麵包很健康，但有些顧客說感覺太重，不會再買，我們要怎麼改善？ B：因為全麥麵粉比較重，麵包太【紮實】了，所以我們可以混入一些白麵粉，並讓麵團發酵久一點。"},{"w":"sweet","p":"adj.","d":"having the taste of sugar","c":"甜的","s":"A: Our cakes sell very well in Japan, but the sales team in Korea says customers there think they taste too strong, so what should we change for that market? B: We can make them less sweet for Korean customers by using half the sugar, and we can add more fresh cream and fruit instead.","t":"A：我們的蛋糕在日本賣得很好，但韓國的業務團隊說當地顧客覺得味道太重，我們該為那個市場改什麼？ B：我們可以只用一半的糖，讓蛋糕對韓國顧客來說不那麼【甜】，再改加更多鮮奶油和水果。"},{"w":"savory","p":"adj.","d":"salty or spicy rather than sweet","c":"鹹的；鹹香的","s":"A: Many office workers buy breakfast at our bakery, but some of them say they get tired of sweet buns every morning, so what new products could we offer? B: We could add more savory items, such as cheese and ham rolls or tuna sandwiches, because many people prefer salty food in the morning.","t":"A：很多上班族在我們麵包店買早餐，但有些人說每天早上吃甜麵包吃膩了，我們可以推出什麼新產品？ B：我們可以增加更多【鹹的】品項，例如起司火腿捲或鮪魚三明治，因為很多人早上比較喜歡吃鹹的。"},{"w":"cool","p":"v.","d":"to become or make something less hot","c":"冷卻；放涼","s":"A: The new staff member tried to put cream on the cakes as soon as they came out of the oven, and the cream melted everywhere, so what should she do next time? B: She should let the cakes cool on a rack for at least an hour first, because cream only stays firm on a cake that is completely cold.","t":"A：新員工在蛋糕一出爐時就想抹上奶油，結果奶油融得到處都是，她下次該怎麼做？ B：她應該先讓蛋糕在架子上【放涼】至少一小時，因為奶油只有在完全冷卻的蛋糕上才能保持定型。"},{"w":"decorate","p":"v.","d":"to make something look nicer by adding things to it","c":"裝飾","s":"A: A large company ordered fifty cakes for its twentieth anniversary party next Friday, and they want each cake to look special, so how much time will we need? B: We need two full days to decorate the cakes with the company's logo, flowers made of sugar, and the words \"Happy 20th Anniversary\" on each one.","t":"A：一家大公司為下週五的二十週年派對訂了五十個蛋糕，他們希望每個蛋糕看起來都很特別，我們需要多少時間？ B：我們需要整整兩天，在每個蛋糕上用公司商標、糖做的花朵和「二十週年快樂」的字樣來【裝飾】。"},{"w":"icing","p":"n.","d":"a sweet mix of sugar and liquid used to cover cakes","c":"糖霜","s":"A: Children love the cupcakes at our shop, but their parents say they have too much sugar on top, so how can we make them healthier but still pretty? B: We can use a thinner layer of icing and add colorful fresh fruit on top, so the cupcakes still look fun but contain less sugar.","t":"A：小朋友很愛我們店裡的杯子蛋糕，但家長說上面的糖太多，我們要怎麼讓它更健康又一樣漂亮？ B：我們可以用薄一點的【糖霜】，再在上面放色彩繽紛的新鮮水果，這樣杯子蛋糕看起來還是很有趣，但含糖量比較少。"},{"w":"batch","p":"n.","d":"an amount of food made at one time","c":"一批","s":"A: The hotel has ordered two hundred cookies for the conference coffee break tomorrow, but our oven can only bake fifty at once, so can we finish them in time? B: Yes, each batch takes about fifteen minutes, so we can make all four in about one hour and still have time to pack them.","t":"A：飯店為明天的會議茶敘訂了兩百片餅乾，但我們的烤箱一次只能烤五十片，來得及做完嗎？ B：可以，每【一批】大約十五分鐘，所以四批大約一個小時就能做完，還有時間包裝。"},{"w":"aroma","p":"n.","d":"a strong pleasant smell, especially of food","c":"香氣；香味","s":"A: Our bakery is on a busy street, but many people walk past without coming in, so how can we attract more customers without spending a lot of money on advertising? B: We can open the front door when the bread comes out of the oven, because the warm aroma of fresh bread often makes people stop and walk inside.","t":"A：我們麵包店在熱鬧的街上，但很多人經過卻沒進來，要怎麼在不花大錢打廣告的情況下吸引更多顧客？ B：我們可以在麵包出爐時打開前門，因為新鮮麵包溫暖的【香氣】常常會讓人停下腳步走進來。"}]},{"unit":24,"theme":"Bar Chart 長條圖","cards":[{"w":"axis","p":"n.","d":"a line at the side or bottom of a chart used to show values","c":"座標軸","s":"A: I am making a bar chart of our monthly sales for tomorrow's meeting, but I am not sure where to put the names of the months and the sales numbers. B: Put the months along the bottom and the sales amounts on the vertical axis, so everyone can see how high each month's bar goes.","t":"A：我正在為明天的會議做每月銷售的長條圖，但不確定月份名稱和銷售數字該放在哪裡。 B：把月份放在底部，銷售金額放在垂直【座標軸】上，這樣大家就能看出每個月的長條有多高。"},{"w":"category","p":"n.","d":"a group of things that have similar features","c":"類別；種類","s":"A: The store manager wants a chart that shows which kinds of products sold best last quarter, but we sell more than five hundred different items, so how can I make it simple? B: Put the items into groups like drinks, snacks, and frozen food, and then draw one bar for each category so the chart stays clear and easy to read.","t":"A：店長想要一張圖表顯示上一季哪些種類的商品賣得最好，但我們賣五百多種商品，要怎麼讓它簡單一點？ B：把商品分成飲料、零食和冷凍食品等組別，然後每個【類別】畫一根長條，這樣圖表就會清楚易讀。"},{"w":"value","p":"n.","d":"a number or amount shown on a chart","c":"數值","s":"A: When I showed my chart to the director, she said she could not tell the exact sales for each region just by looking at the bars, so how can I fix that? B: Write the value at the top of each bar, such as \"2.5 million,\" so she can read the exact number without guessing from the lines on the side.","t":"A：我給主任看圖表時，她說光看長條沒辦法知道每個地區確切的銷售額，我要怎麼修正？ B：在每根長條頂端寫上【數值】，例如「250萬」，這樣她不必從旁邊的格線猜，就能讀到確切的數字。"},{"w":"scale","p":"n.","d":"the set of numbers used to measure the size of things on a chart","c":"刻度；比例尺","s":"A: In my chart, the small differences between our three stores look huge, and the manager thinks the Tainan store is doing terribly, but that is not true. B: The scale on your chart starts at ninety instead of zero, so you should change it to start at zero, and the differences will look as small as they really are.","t":"A：在我的圖表裡，我們三家門市之間的小差距看起來很大，經理以為台南店表現很差，但其實不是。 B：你圖表上的【刻度】從九十開始而不是從零，你應該改成從零開始，這樣差距看起來就會和實際一樣小。"},{"w":"frequency","p":"n.","d":"how often something happens","c":"頻率；次數","s":"A: The customer service team wants to know which problems customers call about most often, so that they can train new staff better, so what chart should I make? B: Make a bar chart that shows the frequency of each type of complaint last month, so the team can see that late delivery calls happen three times more than any other.","t":"A：客服團隊想知道顧客最常為了哪些問題打電話，好更有效地訓練新員工，我該做什麼圖表？ B：做一張長條圖，顯示上個月每一種客訴的【次數】，讓團隊看到送貨延遲的電話比其他任何問題多三倍。"},{"w":"compare","p":"v.","d":"to look at things to see how they are similar or different","c":"比較","s":"A: The board wants to see whether our new advertisement worked, but they only have ten minutes for our report at the meeting, so what should I show them? B: Use one bar chart to compare sales in the three months before and after the advertisement, because the difference will be easy to see in a few seconds.","t":"A：董事會想知道我們的新廣告有沒有效，但會議上只給我們十分鐘報告，我該給他們看什麼？ B：用一張長條圖來【比較】廣告前後三個月的銷售，因為幾秒鐘內就能輕鬆看出差異。"},{"w":"comparison","p":"n.","d":"the act of looking at things to see how they are similar or different","c":"比較；對照","s":"A: Our manager asked me to show how our prices are different from those of our three main competitors, but I only have the numbers in a long table. B: Turn the table into a bar chart, because a visual comparison of prices is much easier for people to understand than a page full of numbers.","t":"A：經理要我呈現我們的價格和三家主要競爭對手有什麼不同，但我只有一張很長的數字表格。 B：把表格轉成長條圖，因為價格的視覺化【比較】比整頁數字更容易讓人理解。"},{"w":"distribution","p":"n.","d":"the way something is spread out among different groups","c":"分布","s":"A: Human resources wants to know the ages of our employees, because many senior workers may retire soon, so how should I present this information? B: Make a bar chart showing the age distribution of all staff in five-year groups, so managers can quickly see how many people are over fifty-five.","t":"A：人資部想知道員工的年齡，因為很多資深員工可能快退休了，我該怎麼呈現這些資訊？ B：做一張長條圖，以每五歲為一組顯示全體員工的年齡【分布】，讓主管能很快看出有多少人超過五十五歲。"},{"w":"label","p":"n.","d":"a word or short phrase that names part of a chart","c":"標籤；標示","s":"A: I showed my sales chart to the new interns, and none of them understood what the bars meant, even though the colors looked nice. B: You forgot to add a label under each bar, so people cannot tell which bar is for which store, and you should also give the chart a title.","t":"A：我把銷售圖表給新來的實習生看，雖然顏色很好看，但沒人看得懂那些長條代表什麼。 B：你忘了在每根長條下面加上【標籤】，所以大家分不出哪根長條是哪家門市的，你也應該幫圖表加個標題。"},{"w":"legend","p":"n.","d":"a small box on a chart that explains what each color or symbol means","c":"圖例","s":"A: My chart uses blue bars for this year and gray bars for last year, but the manager asked me which color was which during the meeting, and I felt embarrassed. B: Add a small legend in the top right corner that explains each color, so people can understand the chart without asking you.","t":"A：我的圖表用藍色長條代表今年、灰色長條代表去年，但經理在會議中問我哪個顏色是哪個，讓我很難為情。 B：在右上角加一個小【圖例】說明每個顏色，這樣大家不必問你也能看懂圖表。"},{"w":"dataset","p":"n.","d":"a collection of related information, usually stored on a computer","c":"資料集","s":"A: The marketing team wants charts about customer spending for the last five years, but our sales numbers are stored in many different files, so where should I start? B: First, combine all the files into one clean dataset in a spreadsheet, and check for missing numbers before you make any charts from it.","t":"A：行銷團隊想要過去五年顧客消費的圖表，但我們的銷售數字存放在很多不同的檔案裡，我該從哪裡開始？ B：先把所有檔案整合成試算表裡一個乾淨的【資料集】，在用它做任何圖表之前，先檢查有沒有缺漏的數字。"},{"w":"variable","p":"n.","d":"a factor or quantity that can change","c":"變數；變項","s":"A: Our ice cream sales went up a lot in July, and the manager thinks it was because of our new advertisement, but I am not so sure about that. B: Temperature is another important variable, so you should show the weather data in the chart as well, because hot days usually increase ice cream sales.","t":"A：我們的冰淇淋銷量在七月大幅上升，經理認為是新廣告的關係，但我不太確定。 B：氣溫是另一個重要的【變數】，所以你也應該在圖表中呈現天氣資料，因為炎熱的天氣通常會讓冰淇淋銷量增加。"},{"w":"horizontal","p":"adj.","d":"going from side to side, flat like the ground","c":"水平的；橫向的","s":"A: The names of our product lines are very long, such as \"premium organic green tea,\" and they do not fit under the bars in my chart, so what can I do? B: Turn the chart into a horizontal bar chart, with the bars going from left to right, so the long names fit easily on the left side.","t":"A：我們的產品線名稱很長，例如「頂級有機綠茶」，在我的圖表長條下面放不下，我該怎麼辦？ B：把圖表改成【橫向】長條圖，讓長條從左往右延伸，這樣長名稱就能輕鬆放在左側。"},{"w":"vertical","p":"adj.","d":"going straight up and down","c":"垂直的；直立的","s":"A: Our designer made the sales chart with bars going up from the bottom of the page, but the director said she prefers bars that go across, so should we change it? B: For monthly sales, vertical bars are usually easier to read because time goes from left to right, so I would explain that and keep the original design.","t":"A：我們的設計師把銷售圖表做成從頁面底部往上的長條，但主任說她比較喜歡橫向的長條，我們該改嗎？ B：對每月銷售來說，【垂直】長條通常比較容易閱讀，因為時間是從左往右排列的，所以我會向她說明並保留原本的設計。"},{"w":"discrete","p":"adj.","d":"separate and different from each other","c":"離散的；個別的","s":"A: Why did you use a bar chart instead of a line chart to show sales in our five different stores, when the manager usually likes line charts? B: Because the stores are discrete groups that are not connected to each other, a line would suggest a change over time, which is not what the data shows.","t":"A：經理通常喜歡折線圖，你為什麼用長條圖而不是折線圖來呈現五家不同門市的銷售？ B：因為這些門市是彼此不相連的【個別】群組，用折線會讓人以為是隨時間的變化，但資料呈現的並不是這個。"},{"w":"magnitude","p":"n.","d":"the great size or importance of something","c":"規模；大小","s":"A: The bar for online sales is three times taller than the bar for store sales this year, and some managers were very surprised, so what does it mean? B: It shows the magnitude of the change in how customers shop, because online sales have grown much faster than anyone expected in just two years.","t":"A：今年網路銷售的長條比門市銷售高了三倍，有些經理非常驚訝，這代表什麼？ B：這顯示了顧客購物方式改變的【規模】，因為網路銷售在短短兩年內的成長速度遠超出任何人的預期。"},{"w":"proportion","p":"n.","d":"a part of a whole, often shown as a percentage","c":"比例","s":"A: The director wants to know how much of our total income comes from overseas customers, because she is planning a trip to Japan and Korea next month. B: My chart shows that a large proportion of our income, about forty percent, comes from overseas, and most of it is from Japanese customers.","t":"A：主任想知道我們總收入中有多少來自海外顧客，因為她下個月打算去日本和韓國。 B：我的圖表顯示我們收入中很大的【比例】，大約百分之四十，來自海外，其中大多數是日本顧客。"},{"w":"trend","p":"n.","d":"a general direction in which something is changing","c":"趨勢","s":"A: Our sales went up in some months and down in others this year, so the board is confused about whether the business is doing well or not. B: If you look at all five years together in one chart, the overall trend is clearly upward, even though a few months were weaker than others.","t":"A：我們今年的銷售有幾個月上升、有幾個月下降，所以董事會搞不清楚業務到底好不好。 B：如果你把五年的資料放在一張圖表裡一起看，整體【趨勢】顯然是向上的，即使有幾個月比較弱。"},{"w":"gap","p":"n.","d":"a large difference between two things","c":"差距","s":"A: The chart shows that the Taipei store sold far more than the Hualien store last year, and the manager wants to understand why the difference is so large. B: Part of the gap comes from the size of the city, but the Hualien store also has fewer staff and much shorter opening hours.","t":"A：圖表顯示台北店去年的銷量遠高於花蓮店，經理想了解為什麼差異這麼大。 B：部分【差距】來自城市的規模，但花蓮店的員工也比較少，營業時間也短得多。"},{"w":"interval","p":"n.","d":"the space between two numbers or points on a scale","c":"間隔；區間","s":"A: My chart has numbers on the side going 0, 7, 14, 21, and 28, and the manager said they are hard to read, so what numbers should I use instead? B: Use an interval of ten, with numbers like 0, 10, 20, and 30, because round numbers make it much easier to estimate the height of each bar.","t":"A：我的圖表側邊數字是0、7、14、21、28，經理說很難閱讀，我該改用什麼數字？ B：用十為一個【間隔】，像是0、10、20、30，因為整數能讓人更容易估計每根長條的高度。"},{"w":"rank","p":"v.","d":"to put things in order from highest to lowest","c":"排名；排序","s":"A: The sales director wants to see which of our twenty salespeople did best this year, but my chart puts them in alphabetical order, so is that a problem? B: Yes, it is, so you should rank them from the highest sales to the lowest, because then the top performers will appear right at the top of the chart.","t":"A：業務總監想看我們二十位業務員中今年誰表現最好，但我的圖表是按字母順序排列，這樣有問題嗎？ B：有，你應該把他們從銷售最高到最低【排序】，這樣表現最好的人就會出現在圖表最上方。"},{"w":"highlight","p":"v.","d":"to make something easy to notice","c":"突顯；強調","s":"A: My chart shows sales for all twelve products, but I really want the board to notice that our new green tea drink sold the most, so how can I do that? B: You can highlight that bar in bright orange and make all the other bars light gray, so their eyes will go straight to the green tea.","t":"A：我的圖表呈現了全部十二項產品的銷售，但我真的希望董事會注意到我們新的綠茶飲料賣得最多，要怎麼做？ B：你可以用亮橘色【突顯】那根長條，把其他長條都改成淺灰色，這樣他們的目光就會直接落在綠茶上。"},{"w":"summary","p":"n.","d":"a short statement of the main points","c":"摘要；總結","s":"A: The president will only look at my report for a few minutes before her flight to Singapore this afternoon, so what should I put on the first page? B: Put a short summary of the main results with one simple bar chart, so she can understand the key points even if she does not read the rest.","t":"A：總裁今天下午搭機去新加坡前只會看我的報告幾分鐘，我第一頁該放什麼？ B：放一段主要結果的簡短【摘要】，再搭配一張簡單的長條圖，這樣即使她沒讀其他部分，也能了解重點。"},{"w":"baseline","p":"n.","d":"a starting point used to compare later changes","c":"基準；基線","s":"A: We started a new training program for the sales team in March, and the manager wants to know if it really made a difference to their results. B: Use the sales in February as the baseline, and then show each month after that in the chart, so everyone can see how much sales grew after the training.","t":"A：我們三月為業務團隊開辦了新的培訓課程，經理想知道它是否真的對業績有影響。 B：以二月的銷售作為【基準】，然後在圖表中呈現之後的每個月，讓大家看出培訓後銷售成長了多少。"},{"w":"contrast","p":"n.","d":"a clear difference that is easy to see","c":"對比；差異","s":"A: The bars for 2025 and 2026 in my chart are light blue and slightly darker blue, and people say they look almost the same on the projector screen. B: Use colors with more contrast, such as dark blue and orange, so the two years are easy to tell apart, even in a bright meeting room.","t":"A：我圖表中2025年和2026年的長條是淺藍色和稍深的藍色，大家說在投影幕上看起來幾乎一樣。 B：用【對比】更強的顏色，例如深藍和橘色，這樣即使在明亮的會議室裡也很容易分辨這兩年。"},{"w":"clarity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being clear and easy to understand","c":"清晰；清楚","s":"A: My chart has a 3D design, shadows, and many different colors, and I think it looks very modern, but the director did not seem to like it. B: She cares more about clarity than style, so you should use a simple flat design with only two colors, so the numbers are easy to understand.","t":"A：我的圖表有立體設計、陰影和很多不同顏色，我覺得看起來很現代，但主任似乎不喜歡。 B：她比較在意【清晰度】而不是風格，所以你應該用只有兩種顏色的簡單平面設計，讓數字容易理解。"},{"w":"color","p":"n.","d":"red, blue, green, and so on","c":"顏色","s":"A: The marketing report has five charts, and each one uses different colors for the same three products, so the readers keep getting confused. B: Give each product one color and use it in every chart, for example green for tea and brown for coffee, so readers recognize them right away.","t":"A：行銷報告有五張圖表，每張都用不同顏色代表同樣的三項產品，讓讀者一直搞混。 B：每項產品都給一種【顏色】，並在每張圖表中使用，例如綠色代表茶、棕色代表咖啡，讓讀者馬上就能認出來。"},{"w":"measure","p":"v.","d":"to find out the size or amount of something","c":"衡量；測量","s":"A: The manager wants a chart to show whether our customers are happier with our service this year, but happiness is not a number, so how can we show it? B: We can measure customer satisfaction with a short online survey that asks people to score our service from one to ten after each visit.","t":"A：經理想要一張圖表顯示今年顧客是否對我們的服務更滿意，但滿意度不是數字，要怎麼呈現？ B：我們可以用簡短的線上問卷來【衡量】顧客滿意度，請顧客在每次光顧後為我們的服務打一到十分。"},{"w":"insight","p":"n.","d":"a clear, deep understanding of something","c":"洞察；深入了解","s":"A: The chart shows that most of our customers shop late at night, which nobody in the company expected, so how can this help our business? B: It gives us a useful insight into our customers' habits, so we can send special offers in the evening and keep our online help desk open later.","t":"A：圖表顯示我們大多數顧客都在深夜購物，公司裡沒人預料到，這對我們的業務有什麼幫助？ B：它讓我們對顧客的習慣有了有用的【深入了解】，所以我們可以在晚上發送特別優惠，並延長線上客服的服務時間。"}]},{"unit":25,"theme":"Barbecue 烤肉","cards":[{"w":"grill","p":"v.","d":"to cook food on metal bars over strong heat","c":"燒烤；炙烤","s":"A: Our company is holding a Moon Festival party on the rooftop this year, and the manager wants everyone to cook together, so what food should we prepare? B: Let's buy plenty of meat, corn, and mushrooms so everyone can grill their own food, and we can also order some mooncakes and fruit for dessert.","t":"A：公司今年要在頂樓舉辦中秋派對，經理希望大家一起烤肉，我們該準備什麼食物？ B：我們買很多肉、玉米和香菇，讓大家可以自己【燒烤】食物，也可以訂些月餅和水果當甜點。"},{"w":"smoke","p":"n.","d":"the gray cloud that comes from something burning","c":"煙","s":"A: The neighbors in the apartment building next to our restaurant have complained to the city about our outdoor grill, so what exactly is the problem? B: Too much smoke from the grill is blowing into their windows in the evening, so we need to install a better fan and move the grill to the other side.","t":"A：我們餐廳隔壁公寓大樓的住戶向市政府投訴我們的戶外烤爐，問題到底是什麼？ B：晚上烤爐冒出太多【煙】吹進他們的窗戶，所以我們需要裝一台更好的抽風機，並把烤爐移到另一邊。"},{"w":"charcoal","p":"n.","d":"black material made from burnt wood, used as fuel for grilling","c":"木炭","s":"A: We are planning a barbecue at the beach for our clients next Saturday, but the beach has no electricity, so how are we going to cook all the food? B: We will use charcoal in three large grills, so please buy about ten bags, some lighters, and a few buckets of water for safety.","t":"A：我們計畫下週六在海邊為客戶舉辦烤肉，但海灘沒有電，我們要怎麼煮那麼多食物？ B：我們會在三個大烤爐裡用【木炭】，所以請你買大約十袋，再準備一些打火機和幾桶水以策安全。"},{"w":"flame","p":"n.","d":"the hot, bright light that comes from a fire","c":"火焰","s":"A: The steaks at the staff barbecue were black on the outside but raw in the middle, and some people did not want to eat them, so what went wrong? B: The flame was too high and touched the meat directly, so next time we should wait until the fire burns down and the coals turn white.","t":"A：員工烤肉時牛排外面焦黑、裡面卻是生的，有些人都不想吃，出了什麼問題？ B：【火焰】太高，直接碰到了肉，所以下次我們應該等火勢變小、炭變白之後再烤。"},{"w":"marinate","p":"v.","d":"to leave meat or fish in a mix of oil, spices, and sauce before cooking","c":"醃製；浸泡","s":"A: The chicken we grilled at last year's company barbecue was dry and did not have much taste, and many people left it on their plates. B: This year we should marinate the chicken in soy sauce, garlic, and honey the night before, so it will be soft and full of flavor.","t":"A：去年公司烤肉時我們烤的雞肉又乾又沒什麼味道，很多人都剩在盤子上。 B：今年我們應該前一晚用醬油、大蒜和蜂蜜【醃】雞肉，這樣它就會柔軟又充滿風味。"},{"w":"seasoning","p":"n.","d":"salt, pepper, herbs, or spices added to food for flavor","c":"調味料","s":"A: The new barbecue restaurant wants its meat to taste special, so that customers will remember it and come back again, but it does not want to use heavy sauces. B: The chef created a secret seasoning of sea salt, black pepper, and dried herbs from Hualien, which he puts on the meat just before grilling.","t":"A：那家新的燒烤餐廳想讓肉吃起來很特別，讓顧客記住並再次光臨，但又不想用很重的醬汁。 B：主廚調配了一款秘製【調味料】，有海鹽、黑胡椒和花蓮的乾燥香草，他會在燒烤前才撒在肉上。"},{"w":"rub","p":"n.","d":"a dry mix of spices pressed onto meat before cooking","c":"乾醃料；香料粉","s":"A: The American customers who visited our restaurant last week said our ribs tasted good, but they missed the strong flavor of barbecue from their home in Texas. B: We could try a spicy rub made of brown sugar, paprika, and garlic powder, which we press into the meat several hours before we cook it.","t":"A：上週來我們餐廳的美國顧客說我們的肋排好吃，但他們想念家鄉德州烤肉的濃郁風味。 B：我們可以試試用紅糖、紅椒粉和蒜粉做成的辣味【乾醃料】，在烹調前幾小時把它抹進肉裡。"},{"w":"sauce","p":"n.","d":"a thick liquid served with or on food","c":"醬汁；烤肉醬","s":"A: We are selling grilled meat at the night market for our company's charity event, and many visitors have asked whether we have anything to add more taste. B: We should put bottles of sweet barbecue sauce on every table, because in Taiwan most people like to brush it on grilled meat and corn.","t":"A：我們在夜市為公司慈善活動賣烤肉，很多遊客問有沒有可以增添風味的東西。 B：我們應該在每張桌子上放幾瓶甜的烤肉【醬】，因為在台灣大多數人喜歡把它刷在烤肉和玉米上。"},{"w":"slow-cook","p":"v.","d":"to cook food for a long time at a low temperature","c":"慢燉；低溫慢煮","s":"A: The beef at the new barbecue restaurant is so soft that you can cut it with a spoon, and customers wait over an hour for a table, so how do they do it? B: The chefs slow-cook the beef for twelve hours at a low temperature, so the meat becomes very soft and takes in all the smoky flavor.","t":"A：那家新烤肉餐廳的牛肉軟到可以用湯匙切開，顧客要等一個多小時才有位子，他們是怎麼做到的？ B：廚師用低溫把牛肉【慢煮】十二個小時，讓肉變得非常軟嫩，並吸收所有煙燻風味。"},{"w":"tender","p":"adj.","d":"soft and easy to cut and chew","c":"軟嫩的","s":"A: Several customers wrote online that our steak was too tough and hard to chew, and our restaurant's rating dropped this month, so what should we do? B: We should buy better beef and let it rest for a few minutes after grilling, because that keeps the meat tender and easy to cut.","t":"A：好幾位顧客在網路上留言說我們的牛排太硬、很難咀嚼，餐廳這個月的評分也下降了，我們該怎麼做？ B：我們應該買品質更好的牛肉，並在烤好後讓它靜置幾分鐘，因為這能讓肉保持【軟嫩】又容易切。"},{"w":"juicy","p":"adj.","d":"containing a lot of liquid in a way that tastes good","c":"多汁的","s":"A: Our new burger is selling very well, and a food blogger even wrote that it was the best in Taipei, so what makes it so popular with customers? B: The meat stays juicy because we grill it quickly over high heat, and people love the way the flavor fills their mouths with every bite.","t":"A：我們的新漢堡賣得很好，有位美食部落客甚至寫說那是台北最好吃的，是什麼讓它這麼受顧客歡迎？ B：肉能保持【多汁】是因為我們用大火快速燒烤，大家都很喜歡每一口都滿嘴風味的感覺。"},{"w":"smoky","p":"adj.","d":"tasting or smelling of smoke","c":"煙燻味的","s":"A: Our sausages taste fine, but the customers at the food fair said they wanted something that really tastes like a real outdoor barbecue, so how can we do that? B: We can cook them over apple wood for an hour, which gives them a rich, smoky flavor that people usually only get from cooking outside.","t":"A：我們的香腸味道還不錯，但美食展的顧客說想要真正像戶外烤肉那樣的味道，我們要怎麼做？ B：我們可以用蘋果木烤一個小時，讓它們有濃郁的【煙燻】風味，這通常只有在戶外烹調才吃得到。"},{"w":"grill marks","p":"n.phr.","d":"dark lines left on food by the hot metal bars of a grill","c":"烤痕；烤紋","s":"A: The photographer for our restaurant's new menu says the grilled chicken in the photos looks pale and not very attractive, so how can we make it look better? B: The chef can press the chicken onto a very hot grill for one minute to make dark grill marks, because those lines show customers that the meat is freshly grilled.","t":"A：我們餐廳新菜單的攝影師說照片裡的烤雞看起來很蒼白、不太吸引人，我們要怎麼讓它更好看？ B：主廚可以把雞肉壓在很燙的烤架上一分鐘，烤出深色的【烤痕】，因為這些紋路能讓顧客知道肉是現烤的。"},{"w":"skewer","p":"n.","d":"a long thin stick used to hold pieces of food for cooking","c":"烤肉串籤；串燒","s":"A: About two hundred guests are coming to our company's outdoor party, and we do not have enough plates or forks, so what kind of food should we serve? B: Let's serve meat and vegetables on a bamboo skewer, because guests can hold the stick and eat while they walk around and talk to each other.","t":"A：公司的戶外派對大約有兩百位賓客，我們的盤子和叉子不夠，該提供什麼樣的食物？ B：我們把肉和蔬菜串在竹【籤】上吧，因為賓客可以拿著竹籤邊走邊吃，同時和彼此聊天。"},{"w":"patty","p":"n.","d":"a flat round piece of chopped meat, often used in burgers","c":"肉餅；漢堡肉","s":"A: Our fast-food restaurant wants to add a vegetarian burger to the menu next month, because more and more young customers are asking for one. B: We can make a patty from beans, mushrooms, and rice, and grill it just like a beef one, so it looks and feels like a normal burger.","t":"A：我們速食店下個月想在菜單上加一款素食漢堡，因為越來越多年輕顧客在要求。 B：我們可以用豆子、香菇和米做成【肉餅】，然後像牛肉餅一樣燒烤，讓它看起來、吃起來都像一般的漢堡。"},{"w":"sausage","p":"n.","d":"chopped meat with spices inside a long thin skin","c":"香腸","s":"A: Many foreign visitors to our night market tour want to try a typical Taiwanese barbecue snack, so what is the best thing for our guides to recommend? B: They should try the sweet grilled pork sausage with a piece of raw garlic, because it is cheap, popular, and very different from the ones in Europe.","t":"A：參加我們夜市導覽的很多外國遊客都想嚐嚐典型的台灣烤肉小吃，導遊最適合推薦什麼？ B：他們應該試試甜甜的烤豬肉【香腸】配一瓣生蒜，因為它便宜、受歡迎，而且和歐洲的很不一樣。"},{"w":"brisket","p":"n.","d":"meat from the lower chest of a cow, often cooked slowly","c":"牛胸肉","s":"A: The new Texas-style restaurant only serves one main meat dish, but it sells out by two o'clock every afternoon, so what is so special about it? B: It serves smoked brisket, which is a cut of beef from the chest that the cooks smoke for fifteen hours until it becomes very soft.","t":"A：那家新的德州風味餐廳只賣一道主菜肉類，但每天下午兩點就賣完了，到底有什麼特別？ B：它賣的是煙燻【牛胸肉】，這是來自胸部的牛肉部位，廚師要煙燻十五個小時直到它變得非常軟嫩。"},{"w":"rib","p":"n.","d":"one of the curved bones of the chest; meat cut with this bone","c":"肋排；肋骨","s":"A: Our restaurant's barbecue platter is the most expensive item on the menu, so customers sometimes ask what they will get if they order it. B: Tell them it includes chicken wings, sausages, and a large pork rib with honey sauce, which is enough for three or four people to share.","t":"A：我們餐廳的烤肉拼盤是菜單上最貴的品項，所以顧客有時會問點了會吃到什麼。 B：告訴他們有雞翅、香腸和一大份蜂蜜醬豬【肋排】，夠三、四個人分享。"},{"w":"baste","p":"v.","d":"to pour or brush liquid over meat while it is cooking","c":"（烹調時）塗油；淋汁","s":"A: The roast chicken at our company's Christmas dinner was very dry last year, and the hotel chef wants to make sure it does not happen again. B: He plans to baste the chickens with melted butter and their own juices every twenty minutes while they cook, so the meat stays soft.","t":"A：去年公司聖誕晚宴的烤雞非常乾，飯店主廚想確保這種事不會再發生。 B：他打算在烤雞時每二十分鐘用融化的奶油和雞肉本身的肉汁幫雞【淋汁】，讓肉保持軟嫩。"},{"w":"flip","p":"v.","d":"to turn something over quickly","c":"翻面；翻動","s":"A: I am cooking the burgers at our team barbecue this afternoon, but I have never done it before, and I am worried that I will burn them in front of everyone. B: Do not worry, just flip each burger once after about four minutes, and do not press it down, so the juice stays inside the meat.","t":"A：今天下午團隊烤肉由我負責烤漢堡肉，但我從來沒烤過，擔心會在大家面前烤焦。 B：別擔心，大約四分鐘後把每片漢堡肉【翻面】一次就好，也不要往下壓，這樣肉汁才會留在肉裡。"},{"w":"coal","p":"n.","d":"a hard black material that is burned for heat","c":"煤炭；炭火","s":"A: How do the cooks at the barbecue restaurant know when the grill is hot enough to start cooking the meat, because they do not use a thermometer? B: They wait until every piece of coal is covered with white ash and glowing red underneath, which usually takes about twenty minutes after they light it.","t":"A：燒烤餐廳的廚師不用溫度計，他們怎麼知道烤爐熱到可以開始烤肉了？ B：他們會等到每一塊【炭】都覆蓋白色灰燼、底下發出紅光，點火後通常大約需要二十分鐘。"},{"w":"outdoor","p":"adj.","d":"happening or used outside, not in a building","c":"戶外的","s":"A: Our staff have been working hard all year, and the manager wants to plan a fun event in the spring where people can relax and enjoy the fresh air. B: Let's hold an outdoor barbecue at the riverside park, where there are tables, grills, and plenty of space for games and music.","t":"A：我們員工一整年都很努力工作，經理想在春天規劃一個有趣的活動，讓大家放鬆並享受新鮮空氣。 B：我們在河濱公園辦一場【戶外】烤肉吧，那裡有桌子、烤爐，還有很多空間可以玩遊戲和放音樂。"},{"w":"picnic","p":"n.","d":"a meal eaten outside, often in a park","c":"野餐","s":"A: The weather is going to be warm and sunny this Saturday, and our team has finished the big project early, so how should we celebrate together? B: Let's have a picnic in Daan Park, where everyone can bring some food, sit on blankets under the trees, and play games.","t":"A：這週六天氣會很溫暖晴朗，我們團隊也提早完成了大專案，我們該怎麼一起慶祝？ B：我們去大安森林公園【野餐】吧，大家可以帶些食物，在樹下鋪墊子坐著玩遊戲。"},{"w":"platter","p":"n.","d":"a large plate used for serving food","c":"大淺盤；拼盤","s":"A: Our sales team is meeting a group of clients at the barbecue restaurant tonight, and there will be ten people, so should each person order a separate dish? B: It is easier to order a large mixed platter for the table, because it comes with beef, pork, chicken, and vegetables, and everyone can share.","t":"A：我們業務團隊今晚要在燒烤餐廳和一群客戶見面，總共十個人，每個人應該各點一道菜嗎？ B：幫整桌點一份大的綜合【拼盤】比較簡單，因為裡面有牛肉、豬肉、雞肉和蔬菜，大家都可以分享。"},{"w":"sizzle","p":"v.","d":"to make a hissing sound like food cooking in hot oil","c":"（煎炸時）發出嘶嘶聲","s":"A: The advertising agency wants our new TV commercial for the barbecue restaurant to make people feel hungry right away, so what should it show? B: It should show steaks as they sizzle on a hot grill, because the sound and the smoke make people imagine the smell and taste of the meat.","t":"A：廣告公司希望我們燒烤餐廳的新電視廣告能讓人立刻覺得餓，廣告應該呈現什麼？ B：應該呈現牛排在熱烤架上【滋滋作響】的畫面，因為那聲音和煙會讓人想像到肉的香味和滋味。"},{"w":"aroma","p":"n.","d":"a strong pleasant smell, especially of food","c":"香氣；香味","s":"A: Our barbecue stall is hidden at the back of the night market, and many visitors do not see it, so how can we attract more customers to our stall? B: We can place the grill near the walkway, because the aroma of grilled meat and garlic will reach people walking by and make them follow it.","t":"A：我們的烤肉攤藏在夜市後方，很多遊客看不到，要怎麼吸引更多顧客到我們攤位？ B：我們可以把烤爐放在走道旁，因為烤肉和大蒜的【香氣】會飄到路過的人那裡，讓他們循著香味過來。"},{"w":"glaze","p":"n.","d":"a shiny coating of sauce brushed on food","c":"亮面醬汁；糖漿塗層","s":"A: The ribs at our restaurant taste great, but they do not look as attractive as the ones in the photos on the menu, so what is missing? B: The cooks should brush a sweet honey glaze on the ribs during the last five minutes, so the meat looks shiny and brown when it reaches the table.","t":"A：我們餐廳的肋排很好吃，但看起來沒有菜單照片上那麼誘人，少了什麼？ B：廚師應該在最後五分鐘刷上甜甜的蜂蜜【亮面醬汁】，讓肉送上桌時看起來閃亮又金黃。"},{"w":"well-done","p":"adj.","d":"(of meat) cooked completely, with no pink inside","c":"全熟的","s":"A: One of our clients from the Middle East is joining the barbecue dinner tonight, and he told me he does not like any pink color in his meat. B: Then please ask the chef to cook his steak well-done, and make sure it is grilled on a separate part of the grill from the pork.","t":"A：今晚有一位來自中東的客戶要參加烤肉晚宴，他跟我說他不喜歡肉裡有任何粉紅色。 B：那就請主廚把他的牛排烤到【全熟】，並確保是在烤架上和豬肉分開的地方烤。"},{"w":"feast","p":"n.","d":"a large special meal for many people","c":"盛宴；大餐","s":"A: Our company had a record year, and the president wants to thank all two hundred staff members with something more exciting than a normal dinner. B: Let's plan a barbecue feast at the beach resort, with whole roast pigs, fresh seafood, and live music, so everyone can celebrate together.","t":"A：公司創下紀錄的一年，總裁想用比一般晚餐更精彩的方式感謝全體兩百名員工。 B：我們在海灘度假村規劃一場燒烤【盛宴】吧，有烤全豬、新鮮海鮮和現場音樂，讓大家一起慶祝。"}]},{"unit":26,"theme":"Bargain 划算交易","cards":[{"w":"deal","p":"n.","d":"something bought for a good price; a business agreement","c":"划算的交易；協議","s":"A: The electronics store is selling last year's laptop model for half price this weekend, and our office needs five new computers, so should we buy them there? B: Yes, that is a great deal, because last year's model is still fast enough for our work, and we can save almost fifty thousand dollars.","t":"A：電器行這個週末用半價賣去年的筆電款式，我們辦公室需要五台新電腦，應該去那裡買嗎？ B：應該，那是很划算的【交易】，因為去年的款式對我們的工作來說還是夠快，而且能省下將近五萬元。"},{"w":"discount","p":"n.","d":"an amount taken off the usual price","c":"折扣","s":"A: Our company orders a lot of paper and ink from the same supplier every month, but we always pay the normal price, so is there a way to pay less? B: We should ask the supplier for a ten percent discount, because we are one of their biggest customers and we have ordered from them for five years.","t":"A：我們公司每個月都向同一家供應商訂很多紙張和墨水，但總是付原價，有沒有辦法少付一點？ B：我們應該向供應商要求打九折的【折扣】，因為我們是他們最大的客戶之一，而且已經跟他們訂貨五年了。"},{"w":"sale","p":"n.","d":"a time when a store sells things at lower prices","c":"特價；拍賣","s":"A: My suit is getting old, and I have an important job interview next month, but new suits are very expensive at the department store, so what should I do? B: Wait until next weekend, because the department store is having its big anniversary sale, and most clothes will be thirty to fifty percent off.","t":"A：我的西裝舊了，下個月有個重要的工作面試，但百貨公司的新西裝很貴，我該怎麼辦？ B：等到下個週末吧，因為百貨公司要舉辦週年慶【特賣】，大部分衣服都會打五到七折。"},{"w":"negotiate","p":"v.","d":"to discuss something to reach an agreement, often about price","c":"談判；議價","s":"A: The office we want to rent costs eighty thousand dollars a month, which is more than our budget allows, but the location is perfect for our business. B: We should negotiate with the owner, because the office has been empty for six months, and he may accept a lower rent if we sign a long contract.","t":"A：我們想租的辦公室每個月八萬元，超出了預算，但地點對我們的業務來說很完美。 B：我們應該和房東【議價】，因為那間辦公室已經空了六個月，如果我們簽長約，他可能會接受較低的租金。"},{"w":"haggle","p":"v.","d":"to argue about the price of something, especially at a market","c":"討價還價；殺價","s":"A: I am taking a group of clients to a traditional market in Bangkok tomorrow, and they want to buy some silk scarves, but they are not sure about the prices. B: Tell them it is normal to haggle with the sellers there, so they should start at about half the price the seller asks and slowly go up.","t":"A：我明天要帶一群客戶去曼谷的傳統市場，他們想買絲巾，但不確定價格。 B：告訴他們在那裡跟賣家【討價還價】是很正常的，所以他們應該從賣家開價的一半左右開始，再慢慢往上加。"},{"w":"cheap","p":"adj.","d":"low in price","c":"便宜的","s":"A: The new printer we bought for the office last month already stopped working, and the shop says it is not worth fixing, so what went wrong? B: It was very cheap, but it was also badly made, so this time we should spend a little more and buy a better brand with a three-year warranty.","t":"A：我們上個月為辦公室買的新印表機已經壞了，店家說不值得修，是哪裡出了問題？ B：它很【便宜】，但做工也很差，所以這次我們應該多花一點錢，買有三年保固的好品牌。"},{"w":"affordable","p":"adj.","d":"not too expensive, so most people can pay for it","c":"價格實惠的；負擔得起的","s":"A: Many young workers in our company say they cannot pay the high rents in Taipei, and some of them are leaving for jobs in other cities, so what can we do? B: The company could build staff apartments with affordable rents, so young workers can live near the office without spending most of their salary.","t":"A：我們公司很多年輕員工說付不起台北的高房租，有些人因此離職去其他城市工作，我們能怎麼辦？ B：公司可以興建租金【負擔得起】的員工宿舍，讓年輕員工能住在辦公室附近，又不必花掉大部分薪水。"},{"w":"price","p":"n.","d":"the amount of money you need to pay for something","c":"價格","s":"A: Our coffee shop has been losing customers since a new chain store opened across the street, and they sell coffee for much less than we do. B: We could lower the price of our basic coffee, but I think we should also offer better service and free Wi-Fi, so customers have more reasons to stay.","t":"A：自從對街開了一家新的連鎖店後，我們咖啡店的顧客一直流失，他們賣的咖啡比我們便宜很多。 B：我們可以降低基本款咖啡的【價格】，但我認為也應該提供更好的服務和免費無線網路，讓顧客有更多理由留下來。"},{"w":"worth","p":"adj.","d":"having a certain value; good enough to deserve the money or time spent","c":"值得的；有…價值的","s":"A: The new office chairs cost three times as much as the ones we usually buy, and the finance manager is not happy about it, so should we still order them? B: I think they are worth the money, because they last ten years and help prevent the back pain that has caused so many sick days.","t":"A：新的辦公椅價格是我們平常買的三倍，財務經理不太高興，我們還要訂嗎？ B：我認為它們【值得】這個價錢，因為它們可以用十年，還能預防造成那麼多病假的背痛。"},{"w":"value","p":"n.","d":"how useful or important something is compared with its price","c":"價值；划算程度","s":"A: The hotel near the airport costs a little more than the others, but the manager still wants our staff to stay there on business trips, so why is that? B: The room price includes breakfast, free airport transfers, and a gym, so it gives us better value than the cheaper hotels with no extra services.","t":"A：機場附近那家飯店比其他家貴一點，但經理還是希望員工出差時住那裡，為什麼？ B：房價包含早餐、免費機場接送和健身房，所以比起沒有額外服務的便宜飯店，它對我們更【划算】。"},{"w":"save","p":"v.","d":"to keep money instead of spending it","c":"節省；存（錢）","s":"A: Our electricity bill has gone up a lot this year, and the manager wants every department to find ways to reduce costs, so what can our team do? B: We can save money by turning off the lights and computers every evening and setting the air conditioner two degrees higher in summer.","t":"A：我們今年的電費漲了很多，經理希望每個部門都想辦法降低成本，我們團隊能做什麼？ B：我們可以每天晚上關燈和電腦，夏天把冷氣調高兩度來【節省】開支。"},{"w":"cost","p":"n.","d":"the amount of money needed to buy, make, or do something","c":"成本；費用","s":"A: The marketing team wants to hold a large product launch at a five-star hotel next month, but the director is worried about spending too much money. B: The total cost of the event will be about five hundred thousand dollars, including the room, food, and decorations, so we need her approval before we book.","t":"A：行銷團隊想在下個月於五星級飯店舉辦大型產品發表會，但主任擔心花太多錢。 B：活動總【費用】大約五十萬元，包含場地、餐點和佈置，所以我們在預訂前需要她核准。"},{"w":"reasonable","p":"adj.","d":"fair and not too expensive","c":"合理的；價格公道的","s":"A: We need a printing company to make two thousand brochures for the trade show, and I have received prices from four different companies, so which one should we choose? B: The company in Banqiao gave us the most reasonable price, and their quality is good, so I think we should give the order to them.","t":"A：我們需要一家印刷公司為商展印兩千份手冊，我收到了四家公司的報價，該選哪一家？ B：板橋那家給我們的價格最【合理】，品質也很好，所以我認為應該把訂單交給他們。"},{"w":"overpriced","p":"adj.","d":"more expensive than it should be","c":"定價過高的；太貴的","s":"A: The sandwiches at the café in our office building cost two hundred dollars each, and many people now go to the convenience store instead, so what is the problem? B: Most staff think the food there is overpriced, because the same sandwich costs less than half that price at the shop just across the street.","t":"A：我們辦公大樓裡咖啡廳的三明治一個要兩百元，很多人現在改去便利商店，問題在哪裡？ B：大多數員工認為那裡的食物【太貴了】，因為同樣的三明治在對街的店裡價格不到一半。"},{"w":"budget","p":"n.","d":"the amount of money you plan to spend on something","c":"預算","s":"A: The team wants to buy new laptops, chairs, and a coffee machine for the office this year, but we cannot afford everything at once, so what should we do? B: Our budget for equipment is only two hundred thousand dollars, so we should buy the laptops first and wait until next year for the other things.","t":"A：團隊今年想為辦公室買新筆電、椅子和咖啡機，但我們沒辦法一次買齊，該怎麼辦？ B：我們的設備【預算】只有二十萬元，所以應該先買筆電，其他東西等明年再說。"},{"w":"compare","p":"v.","d":"to look at two or more things to see how they are different","c":"比較","s":"A: I need to book flights to Tokyo for five people from our sales team next month, and the prices on different websites are very different, so where should I start? B: First, compare the prices on three or four travel websites and the airline's own site, because the same seat can sometimes cost much less on one of them.","t":"A：我下個月要幫業務團隊五個人訂飛東京的機票，不同網站的價格差很多，我該從哪裡開始？ B：先【比較】三、四個旅遊網站和航空公司官網的價格，因為同一個座位有時在其中一個網站上便宜很多。"},{"w":"offer","p":"n.","d":"a special lower price or deal for a short time","c":"優惠；特價","s":"A: Our gym has fewer members this year than last year, and many people say the monthly fee is too high, so how can we attract new customers quickly? B: We can create a special offer for new members, such as three months for the price of two, which starts on the first day of next month.","t":"A：我們健身房今年的會員比去年少，很多人說月費太高，我們要怎麼快速吸引新顧客？ B：我們可以為新會員推出特別【優惠】，例如三個月只收兩個月的費用，從下個月第一天開始。"},{"w":"coupon","p":"n.","d":"a piece of paper or code that lets you pay less for something","c":"優惠券；折價券","s":"A: Our pizza restaurant wants more customers to order online on weekday evenings, because the kitchen is not very busy then, so what can we try first? B: We can send every customer a coupon by email that gives one hundred dollars off any order placed from Monday to Thursday.","t":"A：我們披薩店希望平日晚上有更多顧客線上訂餐，因為那時廚房不太忙，我們可以先試什麼？ B：我們可以用電子郵件寄給每位顧客一張【優惠券】，週一到週四下的任何訂單都可折抵一百元。"},{"w":"clearance","p":"n.","d":"a sale to sell old products quickly and cheaply","c":"清倉拍賣","s":"A: The warehouse is full of last season's winter jackets, and we need the space for the new summer clothes arriving next month, so what should we do with them? B: Let's hold a clearance sale this weekend with prices up to seventy percent off, because it is better to sell them cheaply than keep them for another year.","t":"A：倉庫堆滿了上一季的冬季外套，而下個月到貨的新夏裝需要空間，我們該怎麼處理？ B：我們這個週末辦一場【清倉】拍賣吧，價格最低打三折，因為便宜賣掉總比再留一年好。"},{"w":"secondhand","p":"adj.","d":"owned or used by someone else before","c":"二手的","s":"A: Our small company is opening a new branch office, but we do not have much money for furniture this year, so where can we find desks and cabinets? B: We can buy secondhand furniture from a company that is moving out of our building, because it is in good condition and costs much less than new furniture.","t":"A：我們這家小公司要開新的分公司，但今年沒有太多錢買家具，在哪裡可以找到辦公桌和櫃子？ B：我們可以向一家要搬離我們大樓的公司買【二手】家具，因為它們狀況良好，價格也比新家具便宜很多。"},{"w":"markdown","p":"n.","d":"a reduction in the price of something in a store","c":"降價；減價","s":"A: The new phone cases are not selling well, even though we put them right next to the cash register, so how can we sell them before the new models come out? B: We can give them a thirty percent markdown and put red stickers with the new price on each one, so customers can see the lower price easily.","t":"A：新手機殼就算放在收銀台旁邊也賣得不好，我們要怎麼在新款推出前把它們賣掉？ B：我們可以將它們【降價】百分之三十，並在每個上面貼上標示新價格的紅色貼紙，讓顧客容易看到較低的價格。"},{"w":"shop","p":"v.","d":"to go to stores to look at and buy things","c":"購物；逛街","s":"A: My manager wants me to buy small gifts for twenty clients before the Lunar New Year, but I do not have much time during the day, so what should I do? B: You can shop online tonight, because many websites offer free gift wrapping and can deliver all twenty gifts to the office by Friday.","t":"A：經理要我在農曆新年前買小禮物送給二十位客戶，但我白天沒什麼時間，該怎麼辦？ B：你今晚可以上網【購物】，因為很多網站提供免費禮品包裝，還能在星期五前把二十份禮物全送到辦公室。"},{"w":"splurge","p":"v.","d":"to spend a lot of money on something special that you do not really need","c":"揮霍；大手筆花錢","s":"A: Our team finally finished the biggest project of the year, and the manager says we can use the extra money in our budget to celebrate together. B: Let's splurge on a dinner at that famous steak restaurant, because everyone worked late every night for three months and deserves something special.","t":"A：我們團隊終於完成今年最大的專案，經理說可以用預算中多出來的錢一起慶祝。 B：我們就【大手筆】去那家知名牛排館吃一頓晚餐吧，因為大家三個月來每晚都加班，值得享受一點特別的。"},{"w":"thrifty","p":"adj.","d":"careful about spending money and not wasting it","c":"節儉的","s":"A: Our new accountant always brings lunch from home, uses both sides of the paper, and finds the cheapest train tickets for every business trip. B: She is very thrifty, and that is good for our small company, because her careful habits saved us almost two hundred thousand dollars last year.","t":"A：我們的新會計總是從家裡帶午餐、紙張雙面使用，每次出差都會找到最便宜的火車票。 B：她非常【節儉】，這對我們這家小公司是好事，因為她謹慎的習慣去年幫我們省下了將近二十萬元。"},{"w":"economical","p":"adj.","d":"using little money, fuel, or energy","c":"經濟的；省錢的","s":"A: Our delivery company needs to buy ten new vans this year, and fuel prices keep going up, so what kind of vans should we choose? B: We should choose electric or hybrid vans, because they are more economical to run and will save us a lot of money on fuel over the next ten years.","t":"A：我們的貨運公司今年需要買十輛新廂型車，油價又一直上漲，我們該選哪一種車？ B：我們應該選電動車或油電混合車，因為它們運作起來更【省錢】，未來十年能幫我們省下很多油錢。"},{"w":"steal","p":"n.","d":"something that costs much less than it is really worth","c":"非常便宜的東西；超值品","s":"A: I found a used projector online for only three thousand dollars, and it is the same model that costs twenty thousand dollars new, so should I buy it for the meeting room? B: At that price, it is a steal, but please ask the seller to show you that it works before you pay, just to be safe.","t":"A：我在網路上找到一台二手投影機只要三千元，和新的要兩萬元的是同一款，我該買來放會議室嗎？ B：以那個價格來說，簡直是【超值】，不過付錢前為了安全起見，請賣家先證明它能正常運作。"},{"w":"fair","p":"adj.","d":"reasonable and right for both sides","c":"公平的；合理的","s":"A: Our long-time supplier wants to raise the price of rice by five percent next year, and the restaurant owner is not sure whether he should agree. B: I think it is a fair price, because the cost of rice has gone up much more than that this year, and the supplier has always been reliable.","t":"A：我們長期合作的供應商明年想把米價調漲百分之五，餐廳老闆不確定是否該同意。 B：我認為那是【合理】的價格，因為今年米的成本漲得比那還多，而且這家供應商一直都很可靠。"},{"w":"retail","p":"n.","d":"the sale of goods to the public in stores","c":"零售","s":"A: Our company makes kitchen tools and has only sold them to hotels and restaurants until now, but the director wants to grow our business next year. B: We could start selling in retail, through department stores and online shops, so ordinary families can also buy our products for their homes.","t":"A：我們公司生產廚房用具，到目前為止只賣給飯店和餐廳，但主任想在明年擴大業務。 B：我們可以開始做【零售】，透過百貨公司和網路商店販售，讓一般家庭也能買我們的產品回家用。"},{"w":"profit","p":"n.","d":"money you earn after paying all your costs","c":"利潤；獲利","s":"A: Our store sold more items during the big sale last month than in any other month this year, but the manager does not seem very happy, so why is that? B: Because the prices were so low, our profit on each item was very small, and after paying the staff for extra hours, we earned almost nothing.","t":"A：我們店上個月大特賣賣出的商品數量是今年最多的，但經理似乎不太高興，為什麼？ B：因為價格太低，我們每件商品的【利潤】非常少，付完員工加班費之後幾乎沒賺到錢。"}]},{"unit":27,"theme":"Believing 信念","cards":[{"w":"belief","p":"n.","d":"an idea that you accept as true","c":"信念；相信","s":"A: Why did the new manager spend so much time talking with the team before she changed the weekly schedule at the office? B: It is her strong belief that workers do better when they understand the reasons for a change, so she always explains her plans clearly and listens to their questions first.","t":"A：為什麼新經理在更改辦公室的每週班表之前，花了那麼多時間和團隊談話？ B：她堅定的【信念】是，員工了解改變的原因時會表現得更好，所以她總是先清楚說明計畫並聽取他們的問題。"},{"w":"believer","p":"n.","d":"a person who strongly thinks that something is good or true","c":"信奉者；深信…的人","s":"A: Are you surprised that the head of the sales department now rides her bicycle to work every day, even when it rains in the morning? B: Not at all, because she has been a firm believer in healthy habits for years, and she often tells new staff that regular exercise helps her stay focused at meetings.","t":"A：業務部主管現在每天騎腳踏車上班，即使早上下雨也一樣，你會感到驚訝嗎？ B：一點也不，因為她多年來一直是健康習慣的堅定【信奉者】，她也常告訴新員工規律運動能幫助她在開會時保持專注。"},{"w":"trust","p":"v.","d":"to believe that someone is honest or will do the right thing","c":"信任；信賴","s":"A: Why did the director let the new assistant handle the important client meeting in Singapore by himself last week? B: She has worked with him on several difficult projects, and he always finishes his tasks carefully and on time, so she knows she can trust him with serious responsibilities.","t":"A：為什麼主任上週讓新助理獨自負責在新加坡的重要客戶會議？ B：她和他合作過好幾個困難的專案，他總是仔細又準時完成任務，所以她知道可以【信任】他、交付重大的責任。"},{"w":"faith","p":"n.","d":"strong trust in someone or something","c":"信心；信任；信仰","s":"A: The company lost money for two years in a row, so why are the investors still giving it more support this year? B: They have great faith in the new CEO because she turned around two other businesses before, and her plan to cut costs and open online stores looks very practical.","t":"A：這家公司連續兩年虧損，為什麼投資人今年還繼續給予更多支持？ B：他們對新任執行長很有【信心】，因為她之前曾讓另外兩家企業轉虧為盈，而且她削減成本和開設網路商店的計畫看起來非常務實。"},{"w":"confidence","p":"n.","d":"the feeling that you can do something well","c":"信心；自信","s":"A: How did the new intern manage to give such a clear presentation to the board of directors without looking nervous at all? B: Her supervisor practiced with her several times during the week and gave her helpful advice, which built up her confidence and helped her speak calmly in front of everyone.","t":"A：新來的實習生是怎麼在董事會面前做出這麼清楚的簡報，而且一點都不緊張？ B：她的主管那週陪她練習了好幾次，並給她有用的建議，這建立了她的【信心】，讓她能在大家面前冷靜地發言。"},{"w":"convince","p":"v.","d":"to make someone believe that something is true","c":"說服；使相信","s":"A: The finance team was against the idea at first, so how did you get approval to buy new computers for the design department? B: I showed them a report on how much time the old machines were wasting every day, and that was enough to convince them that the purchase would save money.","t":"A：財務團隊起初反對這個想法，你是怎麼取得核准，為設計部門購買新電腦的？ B：我給他們看了一份報告，說明舊電腦每天浪費多少時間，這就足以【說服】他們相信這筆採購會省錢。"},{"w":"convinced","p":"adj.","d":"completely sure that something is true","c":"確信的；深信的","s":"A: Why does the marketing manager want to move most of our advertising money from newspapers to social media next year? B: After studying last year's sales numbers carefully, she is convinced that younger customers find our products online, so she believes the change will bring in many more orders.","t":"A：為什麼行銷經理明年想把大部分廣告預算從報紙轉到社群媒體？ B：仔細研究去年的銷售數字後，她【確信】年輕顧客是在網路上找到我們的產品，所以她認為這項改變會帶來更多訂單。"},{"w":"convincing","p":"adj.","d":"able to make people believe something is true","c":"令人信服的","s":"A: Did the hotel manager accept the guest's complaint about the noisy air conditioner, or did she refuse to give him a refund? B: He recorded the loud noise on his phone and showed her the video at the front desk, so his story was convincing enough for her to return half of his payment.","t":"A：飯店經理有接受那位房客對冷氣噪音的投訴嗎？還是她拒絕退款給他？ B：他用手機錄下了很大的噪音，並在櫃台給她看影片，所以他的說法夠【令人信服】，她便退還了一半的費用。"},{"w":"doubt","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of not being sure about something","c":"懷疑；疑慮","s":"A: Why hasn't the manager signed the agreement with the new supplier yet, since their prices are much lower than our current ones? B: She has some doubt about whether such a small company can deliver large orders on time, so she wants to visit their factory before she makes a final decision.","t":"A：新供應商的價格比我們目前的低很多，為什麼經理還沒和他們簽約？ B：她對這麼小的公司能否準時交付大量訂單有些【疑慮】，所以她想在做最後決定之前先參觀他們的工廠。"},{"w":"uncertain","p":"adj.","d":"not sure or not clearly known","c":"不確定的","s":"A: Has the travel agency told you yet when your group can fly to Tokyo for the trade show next month? B: Not yet, because a big storm is moving toward Japan, and the schedule for flights out of Taipei is still uncertain, so they promised to call me as soon as they hear any news.","t":"A：旅行社告訴你了嗎？你們這團下個月什麼時候可以飛去東京參加商展？ B：還沒，因為一個大型暴風正往日本移動，從台北出發的航班時刻仍然【不確定】，所以他們答應一有消息就打電話給我。"},{"w":"certain","p":"adj.","d":"completely sure","c":"確定的；肯定的","s":"A: Should we order extra chairs for the company's annual dinner, or do you think the hall already has enough for all our guests? B: I called the event center this morning and checked the numbers twice, so I am certain they have two hundred chairs, which is more than enough for everyone we invited.","t":"A：我們應該為公司年度晚宴多訂一些椅子嗎？還是你覺得會場已經有足夠的椅子給所有賓客了？ B：我今天早上打電話給活動中心，也核對了兩次數字，所以我【確定】他們有兩百張椅子，對所有受邀的人來說綽綽有餘。"},{"w":"certainty","p":"n.","d":"the state of being completely sure","c":"確定；確信","s":"A: Can you tell the customer exactly when the repair team will arrive to fix the broken elevator in her office building? B: I can't say with certainty, because the team is still working at another site downtown, but they usually finish by noon, so they should reach her building early in the afternoon.","t":"A：你能明確告訴客戶維修團隊何時會到她的辦公大樓修理故障的電梯嗎？ B：我無法【確定】地說，因為團隊還在市中心的另一個地點施工，但他們通常中午前會完成，所以應該在下午早些時候抵達她的大樓。"},{"w":"assume","p":"v.","d":"to think something is true without checking it","c":"假定；以為","s":"A: Why did so many people arrive at the wrong meeting room on the third floor this morning? B: The room was changed late last night, and most of the staff didn't read the new email, so it was natural for them to assume that the meeting was still in the usual place, and they went there out of habit.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上有這麼多人跑錯到三樓的會議室？ B：會議室昨晚很晚才更改，大部分員工沒看到新的電子郵件，所以他們很自然地【以為】會議還在平常的地點，就習慣性地去了那裡。"},{"w":"assumption","p":"n.","d":"something you believe is true without proof","c":"假設；設想","s":"A: Why is the sales report for the new store so different from the numbers the planning team expected last spring? B: Their plan was based on the assumption that many tourists would visit the area, but the new train station opened late, so far fewer shoppers came than they had hoped.","t":"A：為什麼新門市的銷售報告和規劃團隊去年春天預期的數字差這麼多？ B：他們的計畫是基於很多觀光客會來這個地區的【假設】，但新的火車站延後開通，所以來的購物者比他們希望的少很多。"},{"w":"opinion","p":"n.","d":"what you think or feel about something","c":"意見；看法","s":"A: Before we choose a design for the new company logo, should we ask the staff in the other branches what they think? B: Yes, I'd like to hear everyone's opinion because they meet our customers every day, so I'll send a short online survey to all of our offices this afternoon.","t":"A：在我們選定公司新標誌的設計之前，應該問問其他分公司員工的想法嗎？ B：是的，我想聽聽每個人的【意見】，因為他們每天都接觸我們的顧客，所以我今天下午會寄一份簡短的線上問卷給我們所有的辦公室。"},{"w":"persuade","p":"v.","d":"to make someone agree to do something by giving reasons","c":"說服；勸說","s":"A: Our best engineer said she was going to leave for a job in Singapore, so is she really staying with us now? B: Yes, the director met her for lunch and offered her a team of her own and more flexible hours, which helped persuade her to stay for at least another two years.","t":"A：我們最優秀的工程師說她要去新加坡工作，那她現在真的會留下來嗎？ B：是的，主任和她共進午餐，提供她一個自己的團隊和更彈性的工時，這幫助【說服】她至少再留兩年。"},{"w":"persuasion","p":"n.","d":"the act of making someone agree with you","c":"說服；勸說","s":"A: How did the hotel finally agree to give us a lower price for the conference rooms during the busy holiday season? B: It took a lot of persuasion, but our manager explained that we would book fifty guest rooms every year, so the hotel decided a long-term customer was worth the discount.","t":"A：飯店最後怎麼會同意在忙碌的假期旺季給我們會議室較低的價格？ B：花了很多【說服】的功夫，但我們經理說明我們每年都會訂五十間客房，所以飯店認為一位長期客戶值得這個折扣。"},{"w":"credible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be believed or trusted","c":"可信的；可靠的","s":"A: Why did the reporter call so many different people before she wrote her story about the factory closing next year? B: She wanted to make sure her information came from credible sources, such as company managers and city officials, because readers would complain if the news turned out to be wrong.","t":"A：為什麼那位記者在寫工廠明年關閉的報導之前，打電話給這麼多不同的人？ B：她想確保她的資訊來自【可靠的】消息來源，例如公司經理和市府官員，因為如果新聞內容錯誤，讀者會抱怨。"},{"w":"credibility","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being trusted and believed","c":"可信度；信譽","s":"A: Why is the company so worried about a small mistake in the price list it sent to customers last week? B: Several clients already noticed the wrong numbers, and if we don't correct them quickly and apologize, we could lose our credibility with buyers who have trusted us for many years.","t":"A：為什麼公司這麼擔心上週寄給客戶的價目表裡的一個小錯誤？ B：好幾位客戶已經注意到錯誤的數字，如果我們不快點更正並道歉，可能會失去在多年來信任我們的買家心中的【信譽】。"},{"w":"skeptical","p":"adj.","d":"having doubts that something is true or useful","c":"懷疑的；持懷疑態度的","s":"A: Did the board members like the idea of letting all the staff work from home three days a week? B: Most of them were skeptical at first because they worried that people would work less, but the results from a small test group last month changed their minds completely.","t":"A：董事會成員喜歡讓所有員工每週在家工作三天的想法嗎？ B：他們大多數起初都抱持【懷疑】態度，因為擔心大家工作量會減少，但上個月一個小型測試小組的結果完全改變了他們的想法。"},{"w":"skepticism","p":"n.","d":"an attitude of doubting that something is true","c":"懷疑態度；質疑","s":"A: How did the customers react when the company said its new phone battery could last a full week without charging? B: Many people reacted with skepticism because other brands had made similar promises before, so the company invited reporters to test the phones themselves for seven days.","t":"A：公司宣稱新手機電池不用充電就能用整整一週時，顧客有什麼反應？ B：很多人以【懷疑】的態度回應，因為其他品牌以前也做過類似的承諾，所以公司邀請記者親自測試手機七天。"},{"w":"devotion","p":"n.","d":"great love, care, or loyalty to someone or something","c":"奉獻；忠誠；熱愛","s":"A: Why did the restaurant owner give the head chef a special award at the staff party on Friday night? B: He has worked there for twenty years, often staying late to train young cooks and test new dishes, so the owner wanted to thank him for his devotion to the business.","t":"A：為什麼餐廳老闆在週五晚上的員工派對上頒給主廚一個特別獎？ B：他在那裡工作了二十年，常常留到很晚訓練年輕廚師和試做新菜，所以老闆想感謝他對這家店的【奉獻】。"},{"w":"loyal","p":"adj.","d":"always supporting a person, company, or idea","c":"忠誠的；忠實的","s":"A: Why does the small coffee shop near our office give free drinks to some customers on their birthdays? B: The owner wants to thank the people who come in almost every morning, because loyal customers like them keep the shop busy even when the big chain store across the street has a sale.","t":"A：為什麼我們辦公室附近那家小咖啡店會在某些顧客生日時送免費飲料？ B：老闆想感謝那些幾乎每天早上都來的人，因為像他們這樣的【忠實】顧客，即使在對街的大型連鎖店打折時也讓店裡生意興隆。"},{"w":"loyalty","p":"n.","d":"the quality of always supporting someone or something","c":"忠誠；忠誠度","s":"A: Why did the supermarket start giving points to shoppers every time they buy groceries with their membership card? B: The managers hope the program will build customer loyalty, because people who collect points usually come back every week instead of trying the new store that opened nearby.","t":"A：為什麼超市開始在顧客每次用會員卡買雜貨時給他們點數？ B：經理們希望這個計畫能建立顧客【忠誠度】，因為收集點數的人通常每週都會回來，而不是去試試附近新開的商店。"},{"w":"commit","p":"v.","d":"to promise to give your time or effort to something","c":"承諾；致力於","s":"A: Is the new partner company really serious about working with us on the hospital building project next year? B: Yes, they are ready to commit to the full three-year plan, and they have already agreed to send ten engineers and share half of the costs for the design work.","t":"A：新的合作公司真的認真要在明年和我們合作醫院大樓專案嗎？ B：是的，他們準備好【承諾】投入完整的三年計畫，而且已經同意派十位工程師並分擔一半的設計費用。"},{"w":"commitment","p":"n.","d":"a promise or strong decision to do something","c":"承諾；投入","s":"A: Why did the customers choose our cleaning company again this year, even though another company offered them lower prices? B: They told us they valued our commitment to quality, since our team always arrives on time, uses safe products, and fixes any problem within one day of a complaint.","t":"A：為什麼客戶今年又選擇了我們的清潔公司，即使另一家公司提供更低的價格？ B：他們告訴我們，他們重視我們對品質的【承諾】，因為我們的團隊總是準時抵達、使用安全的產品，並在接到投訴一天內解決任何問題。"},{"w":"accept","p":"v.","d":"to agree to take or receive something","c":"接受","s":"A: Did the young designer decide to take the job offer from the advertising agency in Taichung, or is she still thinking about it? B: She plans to accept it tomorrow morning, because the salary is good, the office is close to her parents' home, and the team works on interesting international projects.","t":"A：那位年輕設計師決定要去台中那家廣告公司工作了嗎？還是她還在考慮？ B：她打算明天早上【接受】這份工作，因為薪水不錯、辦公室離她父母家很近，而且團隊做的都是有趣的國際專案。"},{"w":"acceptance","p":"n.","d":"the act of agreeing to take or approve something","c":"接受；錄取；認可","s":"A: Have we heard back from the conference organizers about the research paper our team sent them in September? B: Yes, we received a letter of acceptance this morning, so two of our engineers will fly to Berlin in March to present the results to experts from around the world.","t":"A：我們有收到研討會主辦單位關於我們團隊九月寄去的研究論文的回覆嗎？ B：有，我們今天早上收到了【接受】通知函，所以我們的兩位工程師三月會飛往柏林，向世界各地的專家發表研究成果。"},{"w":"conviction","p":"n.","d":"a strong belief or opinion","c":"堅定的信念；確信","s":"A: Why did the director spend so much of the company's budget on training programs during such a difficult year? B: It is her deep conviction that skilled workers are the key to long-term success, so she would rather cut office costs than stop helping employees learn new skills.","t":"A：為什麼主任在這麼艱難的一年裡，把公司這麼多預算花在培訓課程上？ B：她深深【確信】，有技能的員工是長期成功的關鍵，所以她寧願削減辦公室開支，也不願停止幫助員工學習新技能。"},{"w":"devout","p":"adj.","d":"believing strongly in a religion and following its rules","c":"虔誠的","s":"A: Why did the hotel staff prepare a quiet prayer room and special meals for the group of visitors arriving from Indonesia next week? B: The travel agent told us that many of the guests are devout Muslims who pray several times a day, so we want them to feel comfortable and respected during their stay.","t":"A：為什麼飯店員工為下週從印尼來的旅客團準備了一間安靜的祈禱室和特別餐點？ B：旅行社告訴我們，許多客人是一天祈禱好幾次的【虔誠】穆斯林，所以我們希望他們在住宿期間感到舒適並受到尊重。"},{"w":"ideology","p":"n.","d":"a set of ideas and beliefs that guide a group or a system","c":"意識形態；思想體系；理念","s":"A: Why did the two business partners decide to end their company after working together successfully for more than ten years? B: Their management ideology became very different, because one wanted fast growth and big profits while the other cared more about small shops, fair pay, and protecting the environment.","t":"A：為什麼那兩位事業夥伴在成功合作十多年後決定結束他們的公司？ B：他們的經營【理念】變得非常不同，因為一個想要快速成長和高利潤，另一個則更在意小商店、公平的薪資和保護環境。"}]},{"unit":28,"theme":"Bicycle 自行車","cards":[{"w":"pedal","p":"v.","d":"to push the pedals of a bike with your feet to make it move","c":"踩踏板；騎（腳踏車）","s":"A: Why are you so tired this morning, and did you have to come to the office by bike again because your car is still at the repair shop? B: Yes, and the route from my apartment goes up a long, steep hill, so I had to pedal very hard for twenty minutes before I finally reached the building.","t":"A：你今天早上為什麼這麼累？是不是因為你的車還在修車廠，所以又得騎腳踏車來辦公室？ B：對，而且從我公寓出發的路線要爬一段又長又陡的坡，所以我得用力【踩踏板】整整二十分鐘才終於到達大樓。"},{"w":"wheel","p":"n.","d":"a round object that turns to let a bike or car move","c":"輪子；車輪","s":"A: Can you tell me why the delivery bike didn't arrive at the customer's address on time yesterday afternoon? B: The rider hit a deep hole near the train station, and the front wheel got badly bent, so he had to push the bike to the nearest shop and wait an hour for repairs.","t":"A：你能告訴我為什麼昨天下午送貨腳踏車沒有準時抵達客戶地址嗎？ B：騎士在火車站附近撞到一個很深的坑洞，前【輪】嚴重變形，所以他必須把車推到最近的店，等了一個小時修理。"},{"w":"tire","p":"n.","d":"the rubber ring filled with air around a wheel","c":"輪胎","s":"A: Before we lend these company bikes to the visitors for the city tour this weekend, is there anything we should check first? B: Please make sure each tire has enough air in it, because the bikes have been sitting in the storage room for months, and a flat one could ruin the whole trip.","t":"A：這個週末我們把公司腳踏車借給訪客做城市導覽之前，有什麼需要先檢查的嗎？ B：請確認每個【輪胎】的氣都夠，因為這些腳踏車已經在儲藏室放了好幾個月，一個洩了氣的就可能毀了整趟行程。"},{"w":"handlebar","p":"n.","d":"the bar at the front of a bike that you hold to steer","c":"（腳踏車的）把手；車把","s":"A: Do you think this used bike is a good choice for my daily trip to the office, or should I spend more money on a new one? B: It looks fine overall, but the handlebar is a little loose, so you should tighten it before you ride in heavy traffic, or you might lose control when you turn.","t":"A：你覺得這台二手腳踏車適合我每天上班騎嗎？還是我應該多花點錢買台新的？ B：整體看起來不錯，但【車把手】有點鬆，所以你在車流量大的地方騎之前應該先鎖緊，否則轉彎時可能會失控。"},{"w":"seat","p":"n.","d":"the part of a bike or vehicle that you sit on","c":"座位；座椅","s":"A: My back hurts after riding to work every day this week, so what do you think the problem could be? B: I noticed that your seat is too low for someone as tall as you, so you should raise it a few centimeters, and your knees and back will feel much better after a few days.","t":"A：這週我每天騎車上班後背都很痛，你覺得可能是什麼問題？ B：我注意到你的【座椅】對像你這麼高的人來說太低了，所以你應該把它調高幾公分，幾天後你的膝蓋和背就會舒服很多。"},{"w":"frame","p":"n.","d":"the main metal or carbon structure of a bike","c":"車架；框架","s":"A: Why is this bike in the shop window so much more expensive than the others, even though it looks almost the same? B: Its frame is made of carbon instead of steel, so the whole bike is lighter and stronger, which is why professional racers and serious riders are willing to pay the higher price.","t":"A：櫥窗裡這台腳踏車看起來和其他的幾乎一樣，為什麼貴這麼多？ B：它的【車架】是用碳纖維而不是鋼做的，所以整台車更輕更堅固，這就是為什麼職業選手和認真的車友願意付較高的價錢。"},{"w":"chain","p":"n.","d":"a line of metal rings that turns the back wheel when you pedal","c":"（腳踏車）鏈條","s":"A: I heard a strange noise from my bike all the way to the meeting this morning, so do you know what might be wrong with it? B: It is probably the chain, because it looks dry and a little rusty, so you should clean it and add some oil before you ride home this evening.","t":"A：今天早上我一路騎去開會，腳踏車都發出奇怪的聲音，你知道可能是哪裡出問題嗎？ B：可能是【鏈條】，因為它看起來很乾又有點生鏽，所以你今晚騎回家前應該先清理並上點油。"},{"w":"gear","p":"n.","d":"a part that controls how hard or easy it is to pedal","c":"排檔；齒輪","s":"A: How did you manage to ride all the way up that steep hill to the conference center without stopping even once? B: I changed to a lower gear at the bottom of the hill, so pedaling became much easier, and I could keep a steady pace even though I was carrying a heavy laptop bag.","t":"A：你是怎麼一路騎上那個陡坡到會議中心，中間一次都沒停下來的？ B：我在坡底就換到較低的【檔位】，所以踩起來輕鬆多了，即使背著很重的筆電包也能保持穩定的速度。"},{"w":"brake","p":"n.","d":"the part you use to slow down or stop a bike","c":"煞車；制動器","s":"A: Why did the bike rental shop give you a discount when you returned the bike yesterday afternoon? B: The back brake didn't work well when I was riding down the hill near the river, so I almost hit a car, and the manager apologized and gave me half my money back.","t":"A：你昨天下午還車時，腳踏車租借店為什麼給你折扣？ B：我在河邊附近騎下坡時，後【煞車】不太靈，所以我差點撞到一台車，經理向我道歉並退還一半的錢。"},{"w":"helmet","p":"n.","d":"a hard hat that protects your head","c":"安全帽；頭盔","s":"A: Does the company require us to wear any special safety equipment if we join the charity bike race next month? B: Yes, every rider must wear a helmet during the whole race, and the organizers will check each person at the starting line, so please remember to bring yours or rent one.","t":"A：如果我們參加下個月的慈善單車賽，公司要求我們穿戴特別的安全裝備嗎？ B：要，每位騎士整場比賽都必須戴【安全帽】，主辦單位會在起跑線檢查每個人，所以請記得帶你自己的或租一頂。"},{"w":"saddle","p":"n.","d":"the seat on a bicycle or on a horse","c":"（腳踏車）坐墊；鞍座","s":"A: After the long weekend bike tour along the coast, which part of the trip was the most uncomfortable for you? B: Honestly, sitting for six hours was hard because the saddle on my rental bike was narrow and very hard, so next time I will bring a soft cover or rent a better model.","t":"A：沿著海岸騎了漫長的週末單車之旅後，對你來說行程中哪個部分最不舒服？ B：說實話，坐六個小時很辛苦，因為我租的腳踏車【坐墊】又窄又硬，所以下次我會帶個軟墊套或租個比較好的車款。"},{"w":"spoke","p":"n.","d":"one of the thin metal bars that join the center of a wheel to its edge","c":"（車輪的）輻條","s":"A: The repair technician said my back wheel is not perfectly round anymore, so what exactly caused that problem? B: One thin metal spoke broke when you rode over the curb last week, so the wheel lost its shape, and he will need to replace it and adjust the others before you ride again.","t":"A：維修技師說我的後輪已經不再是完美的圓形，到底是什麼造成這個問題？ B：上週你騎過路緣石時，一根細細的金屬【輻條】斷了，所以車輪變形，他在你再騎之前需要更換它並調整其他的輻條。"},{"w":"hub","p":"n.","d":"the center part of a wheel that turns around the axle; also a central place","c":"（車輪的）輪轂；花鼓；中心","s":"A: Why does my front wheel make a grinding sound and turn so slowly, even after I pumped up the tires this morning? B: The hub in the center of the wheel probably needs new bearings, so take the bike to the shop downtown, and they can usually fix it within one day.","t":"A：為什麼我的前輪會發出摩擦聲而且轉得那麼慢，即使今天早上已經把輪胎打飽氣了？ B：車輪中心的【花鼓】可能需要換新的軸承，所以把車牽去市中心的店，他們通常一天內就能修好。"},{"w":"ride","p":"v.","d":"to sit on and control a bike, motorbike or horse as it moves","c":"騎（腳踏車、馬等）","s":"A: Since the subway is closed for repairs all next week, how are you planning to get to the office downtown every morning? B: I will ride my bike along the river path, because it only takes about twenty-five minutes, and I can avoid the crowded buses and the heavy traffic on the main streets.","t":"A：既然下週地鐵整週都因維修而關閉，你打算每天早上怎麼去市中心的辦公室？ B：我會沿著河濱步道【騎】腳踏車，因為只要大約二十五分鐘，而且可以避開擁擠的公車和主要街道上的車潮。"},{"w":"cycle","p":"v.","d":"to ride a bicycle","c":"騎自行車","s":"A: What did your team decide to do for the company's health month, since many people wanted an outdoor activity this year? B: We decided to cycle together around the lake every Saturday morning, and the company will pay for bike rentals and breakfast for everyone who joins at least three times.","t":"A：既然今年很多人想要戶外活動，你們團隊決定在公司健康月做什麼？ B：我們決定每週六早上一起繞湖【騎單車】，而且公司會替參加至少三次的每個人支付租車費和早餐。"},{"w":"balance","p":"n.","d":"the ability to stay steady without falling","c":"平衡","s":"A: Why did the new delivery worker fall off his bike in front of the restaurant this afternoon? Was anyone hurt? B: He was carrying too many boxes on the back, so he lost his balance when he turned the corner too quickly, but luckily he only hurt his arm a little and the food was fine.","t":"A：新來的外送員今天下午為什麼在餐廳前從腳踏車上摔下來？有人受傷嗎？ B：他後座載了太多箱子，所以轉彎太快時失去了【平衡】，但幸好他只是手臂受了點輕傷，餐點也沒事。"},{"w":"speed","p":"n.","d":"how fast something moves","c":"速度","s":"A: Are there any special rules for riding company bikes inside the factory area that new employees should know about? B: Yes, you must keep your speed under ten kilometers per hour near the loading area, because forklifts and workers move around there all day and accidents can happen very easily.","t":"A：在工廠區內騎公司腳踏車，有沒有什麼新員工應該知道的特別規定？ B：有，在裝卸區附近你必須把【速度】保持在每小時十公里以下，因為堆高機和工人整天都在那裡來來去去，很容易發生意外。"},{"w":"trail","p":"n.","d":"a path through the countryside, a forest, or mountains","c":"小徑；步道","s":"A: Do you know a good place where our department could go cycling for the team-building day next month? B: There is a beautiful trail through the forest just outside the city, and it is wide and flat enough for beginners, so even colleagues who rarely ride could enjoy it safely.","t":"A：你知道下個月團隊建立日我們部門可以去哪裡騎單車嗎？ B：城外有一條穿過森林的美麗【小徑】，夠寬也夠平坦，適合初學者，所以就算是很少騎車的同事也能安全地享受。"},{"w":"commute","p":"v.","d":"to travel regularly between home and work","c":"通勤","s":"A: Why did you decide to move to an apartment so close to the office, even though the rent there is much higher? B: I used to commute by bus for almost two hours every day, which made me very tired, so now I save time and can simply bike to work in ten minutes.","t":"A：你為什麼決定搬到離公司這麼近的公寓，即使那裡的房租貴很多？ B：我以前每天搭公車【通勤】將近兩個小時，讓我非常疲累，所以現在我省下時間，只要騎十分鐘腳踏車就能上班。"},{"w":"mountain","p":"n.","d":"a very high hill","c":"山；山岳","s":"A: What are your plans for the long holiday weekend, since the weather report says it will be sunny and cool? B: A few friends from the marketing team and I are going to ride our bikes up a mountain near the national park, and we plan to camp at the top and watch the sunrise.","t":"A：氣象預報說天氣會晴朗涼爽，你連假週末有什麼計畫？ B：我和行銷團隊的幾個朋友要騎腳踏車登上國家公園附近的一座【山】，我們打算在山頂露營看日出。"},{"w":"road","p":"n.","d":"a wide way for cars and bikes to travel on","c":"道路；馬路","s":"A: Is it safe to ride a bike from the hotel to the convention center, or should our guests take a taxi instead? B: It is fairly safe, but the main road has no bike lane and lots of trucks, so guests should use the quieter side streets and follow the green signs.","t":"A：從飯店騎腳踏車到會展中心安全嗎？還是我們的客人應該改搭計程車？ B：還算安全，但主要【道路】沒有自行車道而且卡車很多，所以客人應該走比較安靜的小巷並跟著綠色標誌走。"},{"w":"grip","p":"n.","d":"a firm hold on something","c":"緊握；抓握力；抓地力","s":"A: It rained heavily during my ride to work this morning, so why did I feel like my hands kept sliding while I was steering? B: The rubber covers on your handlebars are old and smooth, so you have a poor grip, and you should buy new ones before riding in wet weather again.","t":"A：今天早上我騎車上班時下大雨，為什麼我在控制方向時一直覺得手在打滑？ B：你把手上的橡膠套又舊又光滑，所以【抓握力】很差，你在下次雨天騎車之前應該買新的。"},{"w":"reflector","p":"n.","d":"a small piece of plastic or glass that shines when light hits it","c":"反光片；反光鏡","s":"A: The police stopped me on my way home last night and warned me about my bike, but what did I do wrong? B: Your bike has no light or reflector on the back, so drivers can't see you in the dark, and the law requires every bike to have one for riding safely at night.","t":"A：昨晚我回家路上被警察攔下來，警告我腳踏車的問題，我到底做錯了什麼？ B：你的腳踏車後面沒有車燈或【反光片】，所以駕駛在黑暗中看不到你，法律規定每台腳踏車都要裝一個才能在夜間安全騎乘。"},{"w":"lightweight","p":"adj.","d":"not heavy","c":"輕量的；重量輕的","s":"A: Which bike would you recommend for our sales staff, who often need to carry their bikes up the stairs to the train platform? B: I suggest this lightweight folding model, because it weighs less than ten kilos, and it fits easily under a desk when they arrive at the office.","t":"A：我們的業務員常常需要把腳踏車扛上樓梯到火車月台，你會推薦哪一款腳踏車？ B：我建議這款【輕量】摺疊車，因為它重量不到十公斤，而且他們抵達辦公室時可以輕鬆地放在桌子底下。"},{"w":"durable","p":"adj.","d":"able to last a long time without breaking","c":"耐用的；持久的","s":"A: Why did the delivery company choose these bikes even though they cost more than the cheaper models from other suppliers? B: They are very durable, so they can be used every day in rain and heat for many years, and in the end the company actually saves money on repairs and replacements.","t":"A：外送公司為什麼選這些腳踏車，即使它們比其他供應商的便宜款式還貴？ B：它們非常【耐用】，可以在雨天和高溫下每天使用好幾年，所以最後公司其實在維修和更換上省了錢。"},{"w":"maintenance","p":"n.","d":"the work of keeping something in good condition","c":"保養；維修","s":"A: How often should the office send the shared bikes to the repair shop to make sure they stay in good condition? B: They should get regular maintenance every three months, including cleaning, oiling the chains, and checking the brakes, so small problems don't turn into expensive repairs later.","t":"A：辦公室應該多久把共用腳踏車送去修車店一次，以確保它們維持良好狀態？ B：它們應該每三個月做一次定期【保養】，包括清潔、替鏈條上油和檢查煞車，這樣小問題才不會在之後變成昂貴的維修。"},{"w":"fitness","p":"n.","d":"the condition of being healthy and strong","c":"健康；體能","s":"A: Have you noticed that Daniel seems much healthier and more energetic at work since the beginning of this year? B: Yes, he started cycling thirty kilometers every weekend to improve his fitness, and he told me he has lost five kilos and sleeps much better than before.","t":"A：你有沒有注意到，從今年年初開始，丹尼爾在工作時看起來健康許多、也更有活力？ B：有，他開始每個週末騎三十公里來提升【體能】，他告訴我他瘦了五公斤，而且睡得比以前好多了。"},{"w":"eco-friendly","p":"adj.","d":"not harmful to the environment","c":"環保的；對環境友善的","s":"A: Why is the city government giving free bike passes to office workers in the downtown area this year? B: It wants people to choose a more eco-friendly way to get to work, because fewer cars mean cleaner air, less noise, and lower carbon emissions for everyone living in the city.","t":"A：市政府今年為什麼要發免費的腳踏車通行證給市中心的上班族？ B：它希望大家選擇更【環保】的方式上班，因為汽車少了，代表城市裡的每個人都能享有更乾淨的空氣、更少的噪音和更低的碳排放。"}]},{"unit":29,"theme":"Birds 鳥類","cards":[{"w":"keen","p":"adj.","d":"very interested in something and eager to do it","c":"熱衷的；渴望的","s":"A: Why did the marketing director ask Linda to plan the company's weekend trip to the wetlands park this year instead of hiring a travel agency? B: Linda is very keen on bird watching, so she already knows the best walking paths, the quietest viewing spots, and the time when most of the birds come out to feed.","t":"A：為什麼行銷總監今年要琳達規劃公司週末去濕地公園的旅遊，而不是請旅行社？ B：琳達非常【熱衷於】賞鳥，所以她早就知道最好的步道、最安靜的觀賞地點，以及大部分鳥類出來覓食的時間。"},{"w":"fond","p":"adj.","d":"liking someone or something very much","c":"喜愛的","s":"A: Why does Mr. Chen always eat his lunch on the bench beside the pond instead of joining the rest of the team in the staff cafeteria? B: He has always been fond of the ducks and small birds that live there, and he says that watching them for twenty minutes helps him relax before his busy afternoon meetings.","t":"A：為什麼陳先生總是在池塘邊的長椅上吃午餐，而不是和團隊其他人一起去員工餐廳？ B：他一直都很【喜愛】住在那裡的鴨子和小鳥，他說看牠們二十分鐘能幫助他在忙碌的下午會議前放鬆。"},{"w":"attract","p":"v.","d":"to make a person or animal come to a place","c":"吸引","s":"A: The hotel garden looks so quiet these days, so what is the manager planning to do before the spring tourist season begins next month? B: She has ordered several wooden feeders and some colorful flowering plants to attract more birds, because many of our guests enjoy taking photos of wildlife while they have breakfast on the terrace.","t":"A：飯店花園最近看起來好冷清，經理打算在下個月春季旅遊旺季開始前做些什麼？ B：她訂購了幾個木製餵食器和一些色彩鮮豔的開花植物，來【吸引】更多鳥類，因為我們許多客人喜歡在露台吃早餐時拍野生動物的照片。"},{"w":"creature","p":"n.","d":"a living animal, especially a small or unusual one","c":"生物；動物","s":"A: What did the children in the after-school nature class find most exciting about yesterday's field trip to the forest center? B: They loved the guided walk, but the best moment was when the guide showed them a tiny creature with bright blue feathers sitting quietly on a branch just above the visitors' path.","t":"A：課後自然課的孩子們覺得昨天去森林中心的校外教學中最令人興奮的是什麼？ B：他們很喜歡導覽步行，但最精彩的時刻是導遊讓他們看到一隻有著亮藍色羽毛的小【生物】，靜靜地停在遊客步道正上方的樹枝上。"},{"w":"vertebrate","p":"n.","d":"an animal that has a backbone","c":"脊椎動物","s":"A: Our new exhibition sign at the science museum needs a simple explanation, so how should we describe birds for the young visitors? B: We could say that a bird is a vertebrate, which means it has a backbone just like fish, frogs, snakes, and people, and then add a colorful picture of a bird's skeleton next to the text.","t":"A：我們科學博物館的新展覽告示牌需要簡單的說明，那我們要如何向年輕參觀者描述鳥類？ B：我們可以說鳥是一種【脊椎動物】，意思是牠和魚、青蛙、蛇以及人一樣有脊椎，然後在文字旁邊加上一張彩色的鳥類骨骼圖。"},{"w":"feather","p":"n.","d":"one of the soft, light parts that cover a bird's body","c":"羽毛","s":"A: Why did the furniture company decide to stop selling the expensive pillows that were so popular in last year's winter catalog? B: Several customers complained that a feather kept coming out through the cotton cover every night, so the product team is now testing a stronger cover and a different filling.","t":"A：為什麼家具公司決定停賣那款在去年冬季型錄中很受歡迎的昂貴枕頭？ B：好幾位顧客抱怨每天晚上都有【羽毛】從棉質枕套裡跑出來，所以產品團隊現在正在測試更牢固的枕套和不同的填充物。"},{"w":"beak","p":"n.","d":"the hard, pointed mouth of a bird","c":"鳥喙","s":"A: How did the zoo's animal doctor know that the old parrot was sick, even though it still looked active and noisy in the bird house? B: She noticed that its beak had a small crack near the tip, so the bird could not break open its seeds properly and had been eating much less food than usual.","t":"A：雖然那隻老鸚鵡在鳥舍裡看起來仍然很活潑又吵鬧，動物園的獸醫怎麼知道牠生病了？ B：她注意到牠的【鳥喙】靠近尖端處有一道小裂縫，所以這隻鳥無法好好啄開種子，吃的食物也比平常少了很多。"},{"w":"Aves","p":"n.","d":"the scientific name for the class of all birds","c":"鳥綱（鳥類的學名）","s":"A: The publisher wants the new animal guidebook to look more professional, so what should we print at the top of the chapter about birds? B: Let's print the scientific class name Aves under the main title, and then explain in a short note that every bird, from the tiny hummingbird to the huge ostrich, belongs to this group.","t":"A：出版社希望新的動物圖鑑看起來更專業，那我們應該在鳥類那一章的頂端印些什麼？ B：我們在主標題下方印上科學分類名稱【鳥綱】，然後用一段簡短說明解釋每一種鳥，從小小的蜂鳥到巨大的鴕鳥，都屬於這一類。"},{"w":"distinctive","p":"adj.","d":"special or different, so it is easy to recognize","c":"獨特的；與眾不同的","s":"A: Why did the design team choose a small red bird for the new logo instead of the blue circle that the director first suggested? B: They wanted something distinctive that customers would remember after seeing it only once, and the red bird stands out clearly on our product boxes, website, and delivery trucks.","t":"A：為什麼設計團隊為新標誌選了一隻小紅鳥，而不是總監一開始建議的藍色圓圈？ B：他們想要一個【獨特的】東西，讓顧客只看一次就記得，而且這隻紅鳥在我們的產品盒子、網站和送貨卡車上都非常顯眼。"},{"w":"flora","p":"n.","d":"all the plants that grow in a particular area","c":"植物群；（某地區的）植物","s":"A: What will the tour guide talk about during the first part of the afternoon nature walk around the island for our company group? B: She will first introduce the local flora, such as the tall palm trees and wild orchids, and explain how these plants give the island's birds both food and safe places to rest.","t":"A：導遊在下午為我們公司團體安排的環島自然步行前半段會介紹什麼？ B：她會先介紹當地的【植物】，例如高大的棕櫚樹和野生蘭花，並說明這些植物如何為島上的鳥類提供食物和安全的休息處。"},{"w":"fauna","p":"n.","d":"all the animals that live in a particular area","c":"動物群；（某地區的）動物","s":"A: Why is the environmental group asking our construction company to delay the new factory project near the river until next year? B: They are worried that the noise and dust will harm the local fauna, especially the rare birds, frogs, and fish that depend on the quiet riverbanks during their breeding season.","t":"A：為什麼環保團體要求我們的營建公司把河邊的新工廠案延到明年？ B：他們擔心噪音和灰塵會傷害當地的【動物】，尤其是在繁殖季節依賴安靜河岸的珍稀鳥類、青蛙和魚類。"},{"w":"rare","p":"adj.","d":"not seen or found very often","c":"稀有的；罕見的","s":"A: Why were so many photographers waiting outside the city park with their big cameras when I walked past this morning on my way to the office? B: A birdwatcher posted online that a rare owl from the mountains had been seen there, so people came early hoping to get a picture before it flew away.","t":"A：今天早上我走路去辦公室經過時，為什麼有那麼多攝影師帶著大相機在市立公園外等？ B：一位賞鳥人士在網路上發文說，有人在那裡看見一隻來自山區的【稀有】貓頭鷹，所以大家一早就來，希望在牠飛走前拍到照片。"},{"w":"shiny","p":"adj.","d":"bright and reflecting light","c":"發亮的；閃亮的","s":"A: Why did the restaurant staff put plastic covers over the outdoor tables after the lunch rush ended yesterday afternoon? B: A group of crows kept landing on the patio and stealing the shiny spoons and forks, so the manager decided to protect the silverware until the birds stop visiting.","t":"A：為什麼餐廳員工昨天下午午餐尖峰過後，要在戶外餐桌上蓋上塑膠罩？ B：有一群烏鴉一直降落在露台上偷走【亮晶晶的】湯匙和叉子，所以經理決定在那些鳥不再來之前先保護好餐具。"},{"w":"breed","p":"v.","d":"to keep animals so that they produce young animals","c":"繁殖；飼養","s":"A: How does the small family farm outside the city make enough money now that fewer people are buying their fresh vegetables at the market? B: The owners started to breed chickens and ducks for local restaurants, and they also sell the eggs online, which has become their most successful product this year.","t":"A：現在在市場買新鮮蔬菜的人變少了，城外那座小型家庭農場要如何賺足夠的錢？ B：農場主人開始【繁殖飼養】雞和鴨供應給當地餐廳，他們也在網路上賣雞蛋，這已成為他們今年最成功的產品。"},{"w":"pigeon","p":"n.","d":"a gray bird often seen in cities and parks","c":"鴿子","s":"A: Why is the building manager putting thin metal spikes along the edges of the roof and above all the office windows this week? B: Every pigeon from the train station seems to land on our roof, and the birds leave such a mess on the windows that the cleaning company says washing them every day costs too much.","t":"A：為什麼大樓管理員這週要在屋頂邊緣和所有辦公室窗戶上方裝上細細的金屬尖刺？ B：火車站那邊的每一隻【鴿子】似乎都會降落在我們的屋頂上，而且這些鳥把窗戶弄得好髒，清潔公司說每天清洗的費用太高了。"},{"w":"sparrow","p":"n.","d":"a small, common brown bird","c":"麻雀","s":"A: What was that small brown bird that flew into the café this morning and made all the customers laugh while they were waiting in line? B: It was just a sparrow looking for bread crumbs, and after one of our servers opened the back door, it hopped outside and flew up into the tree by the parking lot.","t":"A：今天早上飛進咖啡廳、讓排隊的客人都笑出來的那隻棕色小鳥是什麼？ B：那只是一隻在找麵包屑的【麻雀】，我們一位服務生打開後門後，牠就跳到外面，飛上停車場旁的那棵樹。"},{"w":"finch","p":"n.","d":"a small singing bird with a short, thick beak","c":"雀鳥（雀科鳴禽）","s":"A: My manager wants a small pet for the reception area that is quiet, cheerful, and easy to care for, so what would you recommend from your shop? B: I would suggest a finch, because it is a small, colorful songbird that eats simple seeds, does not need much space, and sings softly enough not to disturb your visitors.","t":"A：我的經理想為接待區找一隻安靜、討喜又好照顧的小寵物，你會推薦你們店裡的哪一種？ B：我建議養一隻【雀鳥】，因為牠是一種色彩繽紛的小型鳴禽，吃簡單的種子、不需要太多空間，而且歌聲輕柔，不會打擾你們的訪客。"},{"w":"exotic","p":"adj.","d":"coming from a faraway country and unusual","c":"異國的；外來的；奇特的","s":"A: Why has the number of visitors to the botanical garden increased so much since the new section opened in the summer? B: The garden built a warm glass house full of exotic birds from South America and Africa, and many families now visit on weekends to see their bright colors and listen to their unusual songs.","t":"A：為什麼植物園從夏天新區開放後，遊客人數增加了那麼多？ B：植物園蓋了一座溫暖的玻璃屋，裡面滿是來自南美洲和非洲的【異國】鳥類，現在很多家庭週末都會來看牠們鮮豔的色彩、聽牠們奇特的歌聲。"},{"w":"remote","p":"adj.","d":"far away from towns and cities","c":"偏遠的","s":"A: Why does the research team need a helicopter for their bird study next month instead of driving there in the company vans? B: The birds they want to study only live on a remote island about two hundred kilometers from the coast, and there are no roads, ferries, or hotels anywhere near it.","t":"A：為什麼研究團隊下個月的鳥類研究需要直升機，而不是開公司的廂型車去？ B：他們想研究的鳥只住在離海岸約兩百公里的一座【偏遠的】島上，而且附近完全沒有道路、渡輪或旅館。"},{"w":"hunt","p":"v.","d":"to chase and catch animals for food or sport","c":"狩獵；獵捕","s":"A: Why did the national park office put up so many new signs near the lake entrance before the autumn holiday weekend? B: The signs tell visitors that it is against the law to hunt the ducks and geese in the park, because the number of these birds has dropped sharply over the past few years.","t":"A：為什麼國家公園管理處在秋季連假前，在湖畔入口附近豎立了那麼多新告示牌？ B：告示牌告訴遊客，在園內【獵捕】鴨子和鵝是違法的，因為這些鳥的數量在過去幾年大幅減少。"},{"w":"roast","p":"v.","d":"to cook meat in an oven or over a fire","c":"烤；烘烤","s":"A: The hotel is hosting a large holiday dinner for our clients next Friday, so how will the kitchen prepare the main dish for so many guests? B: The head chef plans to roast twenty turkeys slowly in the big ovens for several hours, and then serve them with potatoes, fresh vegetables, and a special fruit sauce.","t":"A：飯店下週五要為我們的客戶舉辦大型節日晚宴，廚房要如何為這麼多客人準備主菜？ B：主廚打算用大烤箱慢慢地【烤】二十隻火雞好幾個小時，然後搭配馬鈴薯、新鮮蔬菜和特製水果醬一起上菜。"},{"w":"game birds","p":"n.phr.","d":"wild birds that people hunt for sport or food","c":"獵禽（可狩獵食用的野鳥）","s":"A: Why does the new restaurant near the old castle have such a short menu and change it every few weeks during the autumn and winter? B: The chef only cooks game birds, such as wild duck, pheasant, and quail, that local hunters bring in each week, so the dishes depend on what is available during the season.","t":"A：為什麼古堡附近那家新餐廳的菜單那麼短，而且在秋冬期間每幾週就換一次？ B：主廚只烹調當地獵人每週送來的【獵禽】，像是野鴨、雉雞和鵪鶉，所以菜色取決於當季能取得的食材。"},{"w":"delicacy","p":"n.","d":"a rare or expensive food that people think is special","c":"珍饈；美味佳餚","s":"A: What dish should we order for the visiting Japanese clients at tonight's business dinner if we want them to try something truly local? B: Let's order the roast pigeon, which is a famous delicacy in this region, and the restaurant only serves a few plates each night, so I will call now to reserve two.","t":"A：如果我們想讓來訪的日本客戶嚐嚐道地的料理，今晚的商務晚宴該點什麼菜？ B：我們點烤乳鴿吧，那是這個地區有名的【美味佳餚】，而且餐廳每晚只供應幾盤，所以我現在就打電話預訂兩份。"},{"w":"cage","p":"n.","d":"a box made of wire or bars for keeping birds or animals","c":"籠子","s":"A: The pet shop customer said her parrot keeps trying to escape, so what advice did you give her before she left the store? B: I told her to buy a bigger cage with a stronger lock on the door, because a bird that has too little space often gets bored and looks for ways to get out.","t":"A：那位寵物店顧客說她的鸚鵡一直想逃跑，她離開店之前你給了她什麼建議？ B：我告訴她買一個更大、門鎖更牢固的【籠子】，因為空間太小的鳥常常會覺得無聊，並想辦法跑出來。"},{"w":"nest","p":"n.","d":"a place a bird builds to lay its eggs and keep its babies","c":"鳥巢","s":"A: Why haven't the workers started painting the outside of the office building yet, even though the job was supposed to begin on Monday? B: They found a nest with four small eggs under the roof near the main entrance, so the manager decided to wait until the young birds can fly before the painting begins.","t":"A：為什麼工人還沒開始粉刷辦公大樓外牆，明明工程應該在星期一開始？ B：他們在主要入口附近的屋簷下發現一個有四顆小蛋的【鳥巢】，所以經理決定等到幼鳥會飛之後再開始粉刷。"},{"w":"habitat","p":"n.","d":"the natural place where an animal or plant lives","c":"棲息地","s":"A: Why is our company giving money to the wetland project this year instead of sponsoring the city marathon like we did before? B: The CEO believes we should help protect the natural habitat of the water birds, since the new housing developments near the coast have already destroyed many of the places where they feed and rest.","t":"A：為什麼我們公司今年要捐錢給濕地計畫，而不是像以前那樣贊助城市馬拉松？ B：執行長認為我們應該幫忙保護水鳥的自然【棲息地】，因為沿海附近的新住宅開發已經破壞了許多牠們覓食和休息的地方。"},{"w":"perch","p":"v.","d":"(of a bird) to sit on a branch or an edge","c":"（鳥）棲息；停歇","s":"A: Why did the café owner put a small wooden bar outside the front window when she redecorated the shop last month? B: She noticed that birds like to perch near the window in the morning, so she gave them a safe place to sit, and now customers enjoy watching them while they drink their coffee.","t":"A：為什麼咖啡廳老闆上個月重新裝潢店面時，在前窗外放了一根小木桿？ B：她注意到鳥兒喜歡在早上【停歇】在窗戶附近，所以她給牠們一個安全的地方坐，現在客人都喜歡一邊喝咖啡一邊看牠們。"},{"w":"amuse","p":"v.","d":"to make someone laugh or smile","c":"逗樂；使開心","s":"A: The children in the hospital waiting room looked bored and tired this morning, so what did the nurses do to make them feel better? B: A volunteer brought a friendly talking parrot to amuse them, and the kids laughed loudly every time the bird said hello or copied the sound of a ringing phone.","t":"A：今天早上醫院候診室的孩子們看起來又無聊又疲倦，護理師們做了什麼讓他們感覺好一點？ B：一位志工帶來一隻友善、會說話的鸚鵡來【逗樂】他們，每次那隻鳥說哈囉或模仿電話鈴聲時，孩子們都大聲笑出來。"}]},{"unit":30,"theme":"Birthday 生日","cards":[{"w":"celebrate","p":"v.","d":"to do something enjoyable for a special day or success","c":"慶祝","s":"A: Our department finally reached its sales target for the year, so what are we planning to do for the team before the holiday break starts next week? B: The director wants to celebrate the success with a dinner at the Italian restaurant downtown on Friday evening, and she has already booked a private room for everyone.","t":"A：我們部門終於達成了今年的業績目標，那在下週假期開始前，我們打算為團隊做些什麼？ B：主任想在週五晚上到市中心的義大利餐廳【慶祝】這次的成功，而且她已經為大家訂好了包廂。"},{"w":"party","p":"n.","d":"a social event where people meet to eat, drink and have fun","c":"派對；聚會","s":"A: Do you know why the conference room on the third floor is closed this afternoon, because I wanted to use it for a quick meeting with a supplier? B: The human resources team is holding a birthday party there for Mr. Chen at three o'clock, so you could book the small meeting room near the elevator instead.","t":"A：你知道為什麼三樓的會議室今天下午不開放嗎？因為我想用它和供應商開個簡短的會議。 B：人資團隊三點要在那裡為陳先生舉辦生日【派對】，所以你可以改訂電梯旁邊的小會議室。"},{"w":"cake","p":"n.","d":"a sweet baked food, often eaten at birthdays","c":"蛋糕","s":"A: I'm going to the bakery on Main Street during my lunch break, so is there anything special you would like me to order for Linda's birthday tomorrow? B: Could you please order a chocolate cake large enough for twenty people, and ask them to write her name on top, because the whole office will be celebrating together after the morning meeting?","t":"A：我午休時要去大街上的麵包店，明天琳達生日，你有什麼特別想要我訂的嗎？ B：可以請你訂一個夠二十個人吃的巧克力【蛋糕】，並請他們在上面寫她的名字嗎？因為早上開完會後全辦公室要一起慶祝。"},{"w":"candle","p":"n.","d":"a stick of wax that gives light when it burns","c":"蠟燭","s":"A: The hotel manager said we have to follow strict safety rules at the banquet hall, so are we still allowed to have a real fire on the birthday cake tonight? B: Yes, but only one small candle is permitted, and a staff member must stand nearby with a fire extinguisher until the guest of honor blows it out.","t":"A：飯店經理說我們在宴會廳必須遵守嚴格的安全規定，那今晚生日蛋糕上還可以點真的火嗎？ B：可以，但只允許一根小【蠟燭】，而且在壽星吹熄之前，必須有一位工作人員拿著滅火器站在旁邊。"},{"w":"gift","p":"n.","d":"something you give to someone without asking for payment","c":"禮物；贈品","s":"A: Our most important client from Japan is turning sixty next month, so what should our company send him to show our appreciation for his long business relationship with us? B: I think a high-quality tea set would be a thoughtful gift, and we should include a handwritten note from the president thanking him for twenty years of cooperation.","t":"A：我們最重要的日本客戶下個月滿六十歲，我們公司應該送他什麼來感謝他與我們長久的業務往來？ B：我覺得一套高品質的茶具會是很貼心的【禮物】，而且我們應該附上一張總裁的親筆短箋，感謝他二十年來的合作。"},{"w":"present","p":"n.","d":"something you give to someone on a special day","c":"禮物","s":"A: Everyone in the accounting department is giving fifty dollars for Peter's birthday this Friday, but have we decided what to buy him with the money yet? B: Sarah suggested a new pair of wireless headphones as a present, since he often complains about the noise in the office while he is working on the monthly reports.","t":"A：會計部的每個人都為彼得這週五的生日出了五十美元，但我們決定好要用這筆錢買什麼給他了嗎？ B：莎拉建議買一副新的無線耳機當作【禮物】，因為他在做每月報表時常常抱怨辦公室很吵。"},{"w":"wish","p":"v.","d":"to say that you hope someone will have something good","c":"祝；祝福","s":"A: I heard that the vice president is leaving for a business trip to London on the same day as his birthday, so how can the team show that we remember it? B: We could all sign a card and give it to him at the airport, so we can wish him a happy birthday and a safe flight before he boards the plane.","t":"A：我聽說副總裁生日當天要出發去倫敦出差，那團隊要怎麼表示我們記得他的生日？ B：我們可以大家一起在卡片上簽名，然後在機場交給他，這樣就能在他登機前【祝】他生日快樂、一路平安。"},{"w":"balloon","p":"n.","d":"a small colorful rubber bag filled with air or gas","c":"氣球","s":"A: The children's birthday event at the shopping mall starts at ten o'clock on Saturday morning, so what still needs to be done to get the stage ready? B: We still need to tie a big red balloon to every chair in the front row, and then the sound technician has to test the microphones before the families begin to arrive.","t":"A：購物中心的兒童生日活動星期六早上十點開始，那要把舞台準備好還有什麼事要做？ B：我們還需要在第一排的每張椅子上綁一顆大紅【氣球】，然後音響技師要在各個家庭開始抵達前測試麥克風。"},{"w":"card","p":"n.","d":"a folded piece of thick paper with a picture and a message","c":"卡片","s":"A: Ms. Wang from the marketing team is celebrating her fortieth birthday on Monday, but she is working at our branch office in Kaohsiung all week, so what can we do? B: Let's buy a large birthday card, ask everyone here to write a short message in it, and send it by express mail so it arrives before the weekend.","t":"A：行銷部的王小姐星期一要過四十歲生日，但她整週都在我們高雄的分公司工作，那我們能做些什麼？ B：我們去買一張大的生日【卡片】，請這裡的每個人在上面寫一段簡短的話，然後用快遞寄出，這樣週末前就能送到。"},{"w":"surprise","p":"n.","d":"something that happens that you did not expect","c":"驚喜；意外","s":"A: Why did the manager ask all of us to hide in the meeting room and turn off the lights at exactly five o'clock this afternoon? B: It's Kevin's birthday today, and she wants it to be a complete surprise, so please stay quiet and don't send him any messages until he walks through the door.","t":"A：為什麼經理要我們全部的人在今天下午五點整躲進會議室並把燈關掉？ B：今天是凱文的生日，她希望這是一個完全的【驚喜】，所以請保持安靜，而且在他走進門之前不要傳任何訊息給他。"},{"w":"invite","p":"v.","d":"to ask someone to come to an event","c":"邀請","s":"A: The restaurant can only hold thirty people for the company's tenth birthday dinner next month, so how are we going to choose who can attend? B: The general manager has decided to invite our top ten clients and their partners first, and then the remaining seats will be offered to employees who have worked here the longest.","t":"A：下個月公司十週年的晚宴，餐廳只能容納三十人，那我們要怎麼決定誰可以參加？ B：總經理決定先【邀請】我們前十大客戶及其伴侶，然後剩下的座位會提供給在這裡服務最久的員工。"},{"w":"guest","p":"n.","d":"a person who is invited to an event or a home","c":"賓客；客人","s":"A: Have you finished the seating plan for Mr. Lin's birthday banquet at the Grand Hotel, because the event coordinator needs it by tomorrow morning? B: Almost, but one more guest confirmed this afternoon that she is coming from Singapore, so I need to add another chair at the table near the stage.","t":"A：你完成林先生在格蘭大飯店生日晚宴的座位安排了嗎？因為活動協調人明天早上就要。 B：快好了，但今天下午又有一位【賓客】確認她會從新加坡過來，所以我需要在靠近舞台的那桌再加一張椅子。"},{"w":"decorate","p":"v.","d":"to make a place look nicer by adding pretty things","c":"裝飾；佈置","s":"A: The office looks really plain for tomorrow's birthday lunch, and the guests from head office will arrive at noon, so what should we do tonight? B: A few of us will stay after work to decorate the break room with paper flowers, colorful lights, and a banner, so it will look cheerful when everyone walks in.","t":"A：明天的生日午餐，辦公室看起來真的很單調，而且總公司的客人中午就會到，那我們今晚該做什麼？ B：我們幾個人下班後會留下來，用紙花、彩色燈串和一條布條【裝飾】休息室，這樣大家走進來時就會覺得很歡樂。"},{"w":"decoration","p":"n.","d":"a thing used to make a place look attractive","c":"裝飾；裝飾品","s":"A: The event company sent us a bill for the hotel birthday celebration, but why is the total so much higher than the price we agreed on last month? B: They charged us extra for the decoration on every table, including the flowers and gold ribbons, which the client asked for at the last minute without telling our department.","t":"A：活動公司寄來了飯店生日慶祝會的帳單，但為什麼總金額比我們上個月談好的價格高出這麼多？ B：他們為每張桌子上的【裝飾】額外收費，包括花和金色緞帶，那是客戶在最後一刻要求的，卻沒有告訴我們部門。"},{"w":"celebration","p":"n.","d":"a special event to enjoy an important day or success","c":"慶祝活動；慶典","s":"A: Our company is turning fifty years old this spring, so is the board planning any special events for the employees and their families? B: Yes, there will be a big celebration at the city park on the last Saturday of April, with live music, food stands, and games for children, and every worker can bring three guests.","t":"A：我們公司今年春天滿五十週年，董事會有計劃為員工和家屬舉辦什麼特別活動嗎？ B：有，四月最後一個星期六會在市立公園舉辦盛大的【慶祝活動】，有現場音樂、食物攤位和兒童遊戲，每位員工可以帶三位賓客。"},{"w":"song","p":"n.","d":"a short piece of music with words that you sing","c":"歌；歌曲","s":"A: When the waiters bring out the cake for Mr. Huang's birthday at the end of dinner tonight, what should the rest of us at the table do? B: We'll all stand up and sing the birthday song together, and then the president will give a short speech to thank him for his hard work this year.","t":"A：今晚晚餐結束時，服務生端出黃先生的生日蛋糕，我們桌上其他人該做什麼？ B：我們會全部站起來一起唱生日【歌】，然後總裁會發表簡短的致詞，感謝他今年的辛勞。"},{"w":"age","p":"n.","d":"the number of years a person has lived","c":"年齡","s":"A: The new gym near our office is offering a free birthday membership this month, but can anyone in the company sign up for it? B: No, there is a minimum age of eighteen, so the summer interns cannot join, but all full-time staff can register at the front desk with their employee cards.","t":"A：我們辦公室附近新開的健身房這個月提供免費的生日會員資格，但公司裡的任何人都可以報名嗎？ B：不行，最低【年齡】是十八歲，所以暑期實習生不能加入，但所有全職員工都可以拿員工證到櫃台登記。"},{"w":"special","p":"adj.","d":"better or more important than usual","c":"特別的","s":"A: Our sales director is celebrating his birthday during the trade show in Berlin, so is there anything we can arrange for him after the busy exhibition day? B: I've booked a special dinner at a famous German restaurant near the hotel, and the chef will prepare a dessert with his name written on the plate.","t":"A：我們的業務總監在柏林商展期間過生日，那在忙碌的展覽日結束後，我們有什麼可以為他安排的嗎？ B：我在飯店附近一家有名的德國餐廳訂了一頓【特別的】晚餐，主廚會準備一道在盤子上寫著他名字的甜點。"},{"w":"happy","p":"adj.","d":"feeling pleased and glad","c":"快樂的；高興的","s":"A: How did Ms. Lee react when she saw that the whole department had stayed late to prepare a birthday surprise for her yesterday evening? B: She was so happy that she almost cried, and she told us it was the best birthday she has had since she joined the company five years ago.","t":"A：昨天傍晚李小姐看到整個部門留下來為她準備生日驚喜時，她有什麼反應？ B：她【高興】到差點哭出來，還告訴我們這是她五年前進公司以來最棒的一次生日。"},{"w":"treat","p":"n.","d":"something nice that you buy or do for someone","c":"請客；招待（的東西）","s":"A: Why is there a big box of chocolates and fresh fruit on the reception desk this morning, and who brought it into the office? B: It's Daniel's birthday, so he bought it as a treat for everyone, and he said we can take as much as we like during our coffee break.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上接待櫃台上有一大盒巧克力和新鮮水果，是誰帶進辦公室的？ B：今天是丹尼爾的生日，所以他買來當作給大家的【招待點心】，他說我們在喝咖啡休息時間想拿多少都可以。"},{"w":"family","p":"n.","d":"a group of people who are related, such as parents and children","c":"家人；家庭","s":"A: Are you going to join the team at the karaoke bar after work on Friday to celebrate Tom's promotion and his birthday at the same time? B: I'm sorry, but I can't come, because my whole family is coming up from Tainan by high-speed train that evening for my grandmother's eightieth birthday dinner, and I promised to pick them up.","t":"A：你週五下班後要和團隊一起去KTV同時慶祝湯姆升職和生日嗎？ B：很抱歉我不能去，因為那天晚上我全【家】人要坐高鐵從台南上來參加我奶奶的八十歲生日晚餐，而我答應要去接他們。"},{"w":"friend","p":"n.","d":"a person you know well and like","c":"朋友","s":"A: Who is the woman talking with the CEO near the window, because I don't think she works in our building or for any of our partners? B: She is an old friend of his from university, and she flew in from Canada to surprise him at his birthday reception, so they haven't stopped talking all evening.","t":"A：在窗邊和執行長說話的那位女士是誰？因為我不覺得她在我們大樓工作，也不像是我們合作夥伴的人。 B：她是他大學時代的老【朋友】，特地從加拿大飛過來在他的生日酒會上給他驚喜，所以他們整晚都聊個不停。"},{"w":"photo","p":"n.","d":"a picture taken with a camera","c":"照片","s":"A: The marketing department wants to post something on the company website about yesterday's birthday celebration for our founder, so do we have any good pictures? B: Yes, the photographer took a great group photo of all the employees standing in front of the building, and I'll email it to you before lunch.","t":"A：行銷部想在公司網站上發布關於昨天創辦人生日慶祝會的內容，那我們有好的照片嗎？ B：有，攝影師拍了一張很棒的全體員工站在大樓前的團體【照】，我會在午餐前用電子郵件寄給你。"},{"w":"memory","p":"n.","d":"something from the past that you remember","c":"回憶；記憶","s":"A: You have worked at this company for over thirty years, so what is your favorite moment from all the events and parties you have attended here? B: My best memory is the surprise birthday dinner my team organized during my first year, when everyone secretly saved money for weeks to buy me a watch.","t":"A：你在這家公司工作超過三十年了，在這裡參加過的所有活動和派對中，你最喜歡的時刻是什麼？ B：我最美好的【回憶】是我第一年時團隊為我籌辦的驚喜生日晚餐，那時大家偷偷存了好幾週的錢買了一支手錶給我。"},{"w":"greeting","p":"n.","d":"words or actions used to say hello or send good wishes","c":"問候；祝賀","s":"A: Our online store wants to keep loyal customers coming back, so what new idea did the marketing team suggest at this morning's meeting? B: They plan to send every member a personal birthday greeting by email, together with a coupon for fifteen percent off any item purchased during their birthday month.","t":"A：我們的網路商店想讓忠實顧客持續回購，那行銷團隊在今天早上的會議中提出了什麼新點子？ B：他們打算透過電子郵件寄給每位會員一封個人化的生日【祝福】，並附上一張在生日當月購買任何商品都可享八五折的優惠券。"},{"w":"fun","p":"adj.","d":"enjoyable and pleasant","c":"好玩的；有趣的","s":"A: How was the team-building trip to the beach that the company organized for the manager's fiftieth birthday last weekend? B: It was really fun, because we played volleyball, had a barbecue by the sea, and sang songs around a campfire, and even the quiet engineers from the research department joined in.","t":"A：上週末公司為經理五十歲生日舉辦的海灘團隊建立旅行怎麼樣？ B：真的很【好玩】，因為我們打了排球、在海邊烤肉，還圍著營火唱歌，連研發部那些安靜的工程師也都加入了。"},{"w":"party hat","p":"n.phr.","d":"a colorful paper hat worn at a party","c":"派對帽","s":"A: The photographer for the children's birthday event at the toy store wants a cute picture for the advertisement, so what should each kid wear? B: Please give every child a colorful paper party hat and a small flag with our store logo, and ask them to stand together in front of the big window display.","t":"A：玩具店兒童生日活動的攝影師想要一張可愛的照片用在廣告上，那每個小孩應該戴什麼？ B：請給每個小孩一頂彩色紙製【派對帽】和一面印有我們商店標誌的小旗子，並請他們一起站在大型櫥窗展示前面。"},{"w":"celebratory","p":"adj.","d":"done to celebrate a happy event","c":"慶祝的","s":"A: The CEO just announced that we won the government contract, and it's also her birthday today, so what has the office manager arranged for this evening? B: She has ordered a celebratory dinner with champagne at the rooftop restaurant, and everyone in the project team is invited to join after work.","t":"A：執行長剛宣布我們拿到了政府合約，而今天剛好也是她的生日，那辦公室經理為今晚安排了什麼？ B：她在頂樓餐廳訂了一頓有香檳的【慶祝】晚餐，專案團隊的每個人下班後都受邀參加。"}]},{"unit":31,"theme":"Book 書籍","cards":[{"w":"author","p":"n.","d":"a person who writes a book","c":"作者；作家","s":"A: Who is going to speak at the bookstore event next Friday evening, and do we need to prepare extra chairs for the guests? B: The author of the new business guide will talk about her career, so please set up about fifty chairs and ask the café staff to serve coffee after her speech.","t":"A：下週五晚上誰要在書店活動上演講？我們需要為來賓準備額外的椅子嗎？ B：那本新商業指南的【作者】會談談她的職涯，所以請擺大約五十張椅子，並請咖啡廳員工在她演講後供應咖啡。"},{"w":"title","p":"n.","d":"the name of a book or other piece of writing","c":"書名；標題","s":"A: Have you decided what to call the new guide for small business owners, or is the marketing team still arguing about it? B: We finally agreed on a short and simple title, so the designer can start working on the front of the book, and we can send it to the printer next week.","t":"A：你們決定好那本給小企業主的新指南要叫什麼名字了嗎？還是行銷團隊還在爭論？ B：我們終於同意採用一個簡短的【書名】，所以設計師可以開始設計書的封面，我們下週就能把它送去印刷廠。"},{"w":"chapter","p":"n.","d":"one of the main parts of a book","c":"章；章節","s":"A: How much of the training manual have you finished translating, because the Tokyo office needs it before the workshop starts? B: I have completed the first chapter about customer service, and I will finish the part on handling complaints by Thursday if nobody gives me extra work this week.","t":"A：那本訓練手冊你翻譯完多少了？因為東京辦公室在研習開始前就需要它。 B：我已經完成了關於客戶服務的第一【章】，如果這週沒有人給我額外工作，我會在星期四前完成處理客訴的部分。"},{"w":"page","p":"n.","d":"one side of a sheet of paper in a book","c":"頁；頁面","s":"A: Why did the printer call us this morning, and is there a problem with the catalog we sent them yesterday? B: Yes, one page near the end is missing the product prices, so they have stopped printing until we send them a corrected file before noon today.","t":"A：印刷廠今天早上為什麼打電話給我們？我們昨天寄給他們的型錄有問題嗎？ B：是的，接近最後的一【頁】少了產品價格，所以他們暫停印刷，直到我們今天中午前寄給他們修正過的檔案。"},{"w":"cover","p":"n.","d":"the outside front and back of a book","c":"封面；書皮","s":"A: What do customers usually notice first when they walk past the new books table at the front of our store? B: Most people look at the cover, so we chose bright colors and a large photo of the city to make the travel guide stand out from the others.","t":"A：顧客走過我們店門口的新書桌時，通常最先注意到什麼？ B：大多數人會看【封面】，所以我們選了鮮豔的顏色和一張大幅城市照片，讓這本旅遊指南在其他書中脫穎而出。"},{"w":"genre","p":"n.","d":"a type of book, film, or music","c":"類型；體裁","s":"A: Which kind of books should we put on the main display this month, since sales have been slow since the holidays? B: Mystery is the most popular genre with our customers right now, so let's choose ten crime stories and add a small sign that offers a twenty percent discount.","t":"A：既然假期後銷售一直很慢，我們這個月應該在主要展示區放哪一類書？ B：推理是目前我們顧客最喜歡的【類型】，所以我們選十本犯罪小說，再加一個提供八折優惠的小標示。"},{"w":"novel","p":"n.","d":"a long story about imaginary people and events","c":"小說","s":"A: What is the new book by the famous journalist about, and should we order more copies for the store before the weekend? B: It is her first novel, a long story about a family running a small hotel, and early reviews are so good that we should order at least two hundred copies.","t":"A：那位知名記者的新書是關於什麼的？我們週末前應該為店裡多訂一些嗎？ B：這是她的第一本【小說】，一個關於一家人經營小旅館的長篇故事，早期書評非常好，我們應該至少訂兩百本。"},{"w":"fiction","p":"n.","d":"stories about imaginary people and events","c":"小說；虛構作品","s":"A: Why are you moving all those books to the second floor, and where will customers find the travel guides now? B: The manager wants all the fiction together upstairs, so stories about imaginary people will be on the second floor, while travel guides and cookbooks will stay near the entrance.","t":"A：你為什麼要把那些書都搬到二樓？顧客現在要去哪裡找旅遊指南？ B：經理希望把所有【小說類書籍】集中放在樓上，所以關於虛構人物的故事會放在二樓，而旅遊指南和食譜會留在入口附近。"},{"w":"nonfiction","p":"n.","d":"writing about real facts, people, and events","c":"非小說類作品；紀實文學","s":"A: What kind of books do the employees in our company book club prefer, and should we choose a mystery for next month? B: Most members prefer nonfiction, such as true stories about successful business leaders, so I suggest choosing a biography instead of a mystery for our next meeting.","t":"A：我們公司讀書會的員工喜歡哪一類書？下個月我們應該選一本推理小說嗎？ B：大多數成員比較喜歡【非小說類書籍】，例如成功企業領袖的真實故事，所以我建議下次聚會選一本傳記而不是推理小說。"},{"w":"plot","p":"n.","d":"the series of events in a story","c":"情節；故事梗概","s":"A: Did you enjoy the mystery novel that the book club chose for this month, or did you stop halfway through it? B: I finished it in two days because the plot was full of surprises, and I never guessed who stole the money from the bank until the last chapter.","t":"A：你喜歡讀書會這個月選的那本推理小說嗎？還是讀到一半就放棄了？ B：我兩天就讀完了，因為【情節】充滿驚喜，直到最後一章我都沒猜到是誰偷了銀行的錢。"},{"w":"character","p":"n.","d":"a person in a story, film, or play","c":"角色；人物","s":"A: What did the readers at the library discussion say about the new novel, and did they like the ending? B: Most of them loved the main character, a hard-working young nurse who opens her own clinic, but several people thought the ending was too sad and too sudden.","t":"A：圖書館討論會的讀者對那本新小說有什麼看法？他們喜歡結局嗎？ B：他們大多數人都很喜歡主要【角色】，一位開設自己診所的勤奮年輕護士，但有幾個人覺得結局太悲傷也太突然。"},{"w":"setting","p":"n.","d":"the place and time in which a story happens","c":"背景；場景","s":"A: Why does the publisher want the writer to make changes to the story before it is printed next spring? B: They think the setting should be modern Taipei instead of a small village in the past, because young readers will connect more easily with a busy city they know.","t":"A：出版社為什麼要作者在明年春天印刷前修改故事？ B：他們認為故事【背景】應該是現代的台北，而不是過去的小村莊，因為年輕讀者會更容易對他們熟悉的繁忙城市產生共鳴。"},{"w":"theme","p":"n.","d":"the main subject or idea in a piece of writing","c":"主題","s":"A: What is the main idea of the business novel we are discussing at lunch, since I only finished half of it? B: The central theme is teamwork, because the story shows how a small group of workers saves their failing company by listening to each other and sharing ideas.","t":"A：我們午餐時要討論的那本商業小說主要想法是什麼？我只讀完了一半。 B：核心【主題】是團隊合作，因為故事描述一小群員工如何透過互相傾聽和分享想法，拯救了他們快倒閉的公司。"},{"w":"narrative","p":"n.","d":"a story or a description of events","c":"敘述；故事","s":"A: Why did the editor ask you to rewrite the company history book, when you already spent six months on it? B: She said the narrative jumped between different years too often, so readers got confused, and she wants the story told in order from the founding of the company.","t":"A：既然你已經花了六個月寫那本公司歷史書，編輯為什麼還要你重寫？ B：她說【敘述】太常在不同年份之間跳來跳去，讓讀者感到混亂，她希望故事從公司創立開始依序講述。"},{"w":"dialogue","p":"n.","d":"a conversation between people in a book, play, or film","c":"對話","s":"A: What do you think of the new English textbook for our staff training, and is it useful for beginners? B: I like it because each lesson has a short dialogue between a hotel clerk and a guest, so the trainees can practice speaking in pairs before they talk to real customers.","t":"A：你覺得我們員工訓練用的新英文課本怎麼樣？對初學者有用嗎？ B：我喜歡它，因為每一課都有一段飯店櫃台人員和客人之間的簡短【對話】，所以受訓者可以在和真正的顧客交談前兩人一組練習口說。"},{"w":"description","p":"n.","d":"words that tell what something is like","c":"描述；說明","s":"A: Has the online bookstore added the new cookbook to its website yet, because several customers have asked when they can order it? B: Not yet, they are still waiting for a short description of the book, so I need to send them a paragraph about the recipes and the chef by tomorrow morning.","t":"A：網路書店把新食譜書放上網站了嗎？因為有好幾位顧客問什麼時候可以訂購。 B：還沒有，他們還在等這本書的簡短【介紹】，所以我需要在明天早上前寄給他們一段關於食譜和主廚的文字。"},{"w":"edition","p":"n.","d":"one version of a book printed at a particular time","c":"版本；版次","s":"A: Why are some customers returning the accounting textbook they bought from us last month, and is something wrong with it? B: The publisher released a new edition with updated tax rules last week, so the professors told their students to buy the latest version instead of the old one.","t":"A：為什麼有些顧客要退回上個月向我們買的會計課本？書有什麼問題嗎？ B：出版社上週發行了更新稅法的新【版本】，所以教授們要學生改買最新版而不是舊版。"},{"w":"publisher","p":"n.","d":"a company that prepares and sells books","c":"出版社；出版商","s":"A: Have you heard back from anyone about the business guide you wrote last year, or are you still waiting for an answer? B: Yes, a large publisher in Taipei called me yesterday and offered to print five thousand copies, so I am meeting their editor next Tuesday to sign the contract.","t":"A：你去年寫的那本商業指南有收到任何回音嗎？還是你還在等回覆？ B：有，台北一家大型【出版社】昨天打電話給我，提議印五千本，所以我下週二要和他們的編輯見面簽約。"},{"w":"hardcover","p":"n.","d":"a book with a stiff, strong cover","c":"精裝本","s":"A: Should we order the cheaper version of the art book for the store, or will customers pay more for a better one? B: For art books, many customers prefer the hardcover because it is strong and looks beautiful on a shelf, so let's order mostly that version even though it costs more.","t":"A：我們店裡應該訂那本藝術書比較便宜的版本，還是顧客會願意多付錢買比較好的？ B：對藝術書來說，很多顧客偏好【精裝本】，因為它很堅固，放在書架上也很好看，所以即使比較貴，我們還是大多訂那個版本吧。"},{"w":"paperback","p":"n.","d":"a book with a soft paper cover","c":"平裝本","s":"A: Which version of the novel should I take on my business trip to Singapore, since my suitcase is already quite heavy? B: You should take the paperback, because it is light and small enough to fit in your jacket pocket, and it costs only half the price of the other one.","t":"A：我去新加坡出差應該帶哪個版本的小說？我的行李箱已經很重了。 B：你應該帶【平裝本】，因為它又輕又小，可以放進外套口袋，而且價格只有另一種的一半。"},{"w":"illustration","p":"n.","d":"a picture in a book","c":"插圖；圖解","s":"A: Why is the children's book about saving energy taking so long to finish, when the writer sent us the story in May? B: The artist is still drawing the last illustration for the final page, and she wants every picture to be bright and clear so young readers can understand the ideas.","t":"A：既然作者五月就把故事寄給我們了，那本關於節約能源的童書為什麼要花這麼久才完成？ B：畫家還在畫最後一頁的最後一張【插圖】，她希望每張圖都鮮明清楚，讓年輕讀者能理解其中的概念。"},{"w":"read","p":"v.","d":"to look at words and understand them","c":"閱讀；讀","s":"A: Have you had time to look at the new safety manual before the training session with the factory workers this afternoon? B: Yes, I managed to read the whole thing on the train this morning, and I wrote down three questions about the fire exits that I want to ask the manager.","t":"A：今天下午和工廠員工的訓練課程之前，你有時間看新的安全手冊嗎？ B：有，我今天早上在火車上把整本【讀】完了，還寫下了三個關於逃生出口的問題要問經理。"},{"w":"review","p":"n.","d":"a written report that gives an opinion about a book, film, etc.","c":"評論；書評","s":"A: How did the newspaper describe our company's new travel guide, and will it help us sell more copies this month? B: The review in Sunday's newspaper said it was clear, useful, and full of great photos, so I expect sales to rise quickly over the next few weeks.","t":"A：報紙怎麼描述我們公司的新旅遊指南？這會幫助我們這個月多賣一些嗎？ B：週日報紙上的【書評】說它內容清楚、實用，而且有很多很棒的照片，所以我預期接下來幾週銷售會快速上升。"},{"w":"bookmark","p":"n.","d":"a thin strip put in a book to mark a page","c":"書籤","s":"A: Are we giving customers anything free with their purchases during the book fair this weekend, like we did last year? B: Yes, every customer will get a paper bookmark with our store's logo and website on it, so they can keep their place in a book and remember to shop with us again.","t":"A：這週末書展期間，我們會像去年一樣隨購買贈送顧客任何東西嗎？ B：會，每位顧客都會拿到一張印有我們店標誌和網址的紙製【書籤】，這樣他們可以標記閱讀的位置，也會記得再來我們店購物。"},{"w":"library","p":"n.","d":"a place where books are kept for people to read or borrow","c":"圖書館；圖書室","s":"A: Where can I find old reports about the market in Southeast Asia, since I need them for my presentation on Monday? B: The company library on the third floor keeps copies of all reports from the past ten years, and you can borrow them for two weeks if you show your staff card.","t":"A：我可以在哪裡找到東南亞市場的舊報告？我星期一的簡報需要用到。 B：三樓的公司【圖書室】保存了過去十年所有報告的副本，只要出示員工證，你就可以借兩個星期。"},{"w":"literature","p":"n.","d":"books, poems, and plays that are thought to be important art","c":"文學","s":"A: Why did the bookstore hire a new staff member for the second floor, and what will she be responsible for? B: She studied English literature at university and knows a lot about famous poems and plays, so she will help customers choose good books and organize our monthly reading events.","t":"A：書店為什麼為二樓僱用了一位新員工？她會負責什麼？ B：她大學念英國【文學】，對著名的詩和劇本很了解，所以她會幫顧客挑選好書，並籌辦我們每月的讀書活動。"},{"w":"classic","p":"n.","d":"a famous book that people have admired for a long time","c":"經典作品；名著","s":"A: Which books should we include in the gift box for our loyal customers this holiday season, since we want something that lasts? B: Let's include a famous classic that people have loved for over a hundred years, along with a new bestseller, so the box appeals to both older and younger readers.","t":"A：這個假期我們要在送給忠實顧客的禮盒裡放哪些書？我們想要有長久價值的東西。 B：我們放一本人們喜愛了一百多年的著名【經典作品】，再加一本新的暢銷書，讓禮盒同時吸引年長和年輕的讀者。"},{"w":"bestseller","p":"n.","d":"a book that sells a very large number of copies","c":"暢銷書","s":"A: Why did the publishing company decide to print another twenty thousand copies of the cookbook this month? B: It became a bestseller just two weeks after it came out, because a famous TV chef recommended it on her show, and many bookstores have already sold all their copies.","t":"A：出版公司為什麼決定這個月再加印兩萬本那本食譜書？ B：它出版短短兩週就成為【暢銷書】，因為一位知名電視主廚在節目中推薦了它，許多書店都已經賣光了。"},{"w":"inspiring","p":"adj.","d":"making people feel excited and want to do something","c":"激勵人心的；鼓舞人的","s":"A: Why are so many employees talking about the speaker at yesterday's training event, and what did she talk about? B: Her speech was very inspiring, because she described how she started her bookstore with almost no money, and now many of us feel ready to try new ideas at work.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多員工在談論昨天訓練活動的講者？她講了什麼？ B：她的演講非常【激勵人心】，因為她描述了自己如何在幾乎沒有錢的情況下開了書店，現在我們很多人都覺得準備好在工作上嘗試新點子了。"}]},{"unit":32,"theme":"Bookstore 書店","cards":[{"w":"bookshelf","p":"n.","d":"a piece of furniture with shelves for books","c":"書架","s":"A: The new store manager wants the travel guides to be easier for visitors to find, so where should we put the boxes that arrived from the publisher this morning? B: Let's move them to the tall bookshelf next to the front window, because tourists usually walk in from the street and look there first before they explore the rest of the shop.","t":"A：新店長希望旅遊指南能讓客人更容易找到，那今天早上出版社送來的那幾箱書我們該放在哪裡？ B：我們把它們移到前窗旁邊那個高高的【書架】上吧，因為觀光客通常從街上走進來，會先看那裡，再逛店裡其他地方。"},{"w":"aisle","p":"n.","d":"a long, narrow path between rows of shelves or seats","c":"走道","s":"A: A woman just called to ask where she can find our cookbooks, but I only started working here yesterday, so do you know where they are? B: Tell her to walk past the cashier and turn left into the third aisle, where the cookbooks are on the lower shelves right beside the gardening magazines.","t":"A：有位女士剛打電話來問我們的食譜書在哪裡，但我昨天才開始在這裡上班，你知道在哪嗎？ B：告訴她走過收銀員後左轉進入第三條【走道】，食譜書就在園藝雜誌旁邊的下層架子上。"},{"w":"section","p":"n.","d":"one part or area of a store, book, or place","c":"區；部分","s":"A: Our sales report shows that more parents are buying learning materials for young kids this year, so how should we change the layout of the second floor? B: I think we should make the children's section bigger and add some small chairs and tables, so families can sit together and read before they decide what to buy.","t":"A：我們的銷售報告顯示今年有更多家長購買幼兒學習教材，那我們應該怎麼調整二樓的配置？ B：我認為我們應該把兒童【區】擴大，並增加一些小椅子和小桌子，讓家人可以先坐在一起閱讀，再決定要買什麼。"},{"w":"genre","p":"n.","d":"a type or style of book, film, or music","c":"類型；體裁","s":"A: Since the store is planning a summer promotion for adult readers, which kind of story do you think we should feature on the big table near the entrance? B: Mystery is the most popular genre among our regular shoppers, especially office workers who like exciting stories during their long train rides home, so let's choose that.","t":"A：既然書店計畫為成人讀者舉辦夏季促銷，你覺得我們應該在入口附近的大桌子上主打哪一類故事？ B：推理小說是我們常客最喜歡的【類型】，尤其是喜歡在漫長回家火車上看刺激故事的上班族，所以就選這個吧。"},{"w":"display","p":"n.","d":"an arrangement of things put out for people to see","c":"陳列；展示","s":"A: The publisher is sending us fifty copies of the new cookbook next Monday, so how can we make sure people notice it as soon as they come in? B: We could build a colorful display near the front door with a few sample dishes, some posters, and a sign showing the special opening price for the first week.","t":"A：出版社下週一會寄五十本新食譜書給我們，我們要怎麼確保客人一進門就注意到它？ B：我們可以在前門附近佈置一個色彩繽紛的【陳列】，擺上幾道範例菜餚、一些海報，以及標示第一週特別開幕價的牌子。"},{"w":"counter","p":"n.","d":"a long, flat surface where customers are served","c":"櫃檯","s":"A: Where should customers pick up the books they ordered online, since many of them complain that they can't find anyone to help them when they arrive? B: From next week, they can go straight to the service counter beside the entrance, where one employee will check their order number and hand them their package.","t":"A：顧客應該在哪裡領取他們網路訂購的書？很多人抱怨到店時找不到人幫忙。 B：從下週開始，他們可以直接到入口旁的服務【櫃檯】，會有一位員工核對訂單編號並把包裹交給他們。"},{"w":"cashier","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to take payments in a store","c":"收銀員","s":"A: The lines at the front of the store were really long on Saturday afternoon, and several shoppers left without buying anything, so what can we do about it? B: The manager has decided to hire another part-time cashier for weekends, so two people can take payments at the same time when the store gets busy.","t":"A：星期六下午店門口排隊的人潮很長，好幾位客人什麼都沒買就走了，我們能怎麼辦？ B：經理決定在週末再雇用一位兼職【收銀員】，這樣店裡忙碌時就能有兩個人同時收款。"},{"w":"customer","p":"n.","d":"a person who buys things from a store or business","c":"顧客","s":"A: Why does the store manager want everyone to learn the names of the people who come in every week, even though we are always so busy? B: She believes that when a regular customer feels welcome and remembered, he or she will keep coming back and will probably tell friends about our shop too.","t":"A：為什麼店長要大家記住每週都來的人的名字，即使我們總是這麼忙？ B：她相信當一位常來的【顧客】覺得受到歡迎、被記住時，就會一直回來，而且很可能也會跟朋友介紹我們的店。"},{"w":"browse","p":"v.","d":"to look at things in a store without a clear plan to buy","c":"瀏覽；隨意看看","s":"A: Do you think it is a good idea to put some comfortable chairs near the travel section, even though people might sit there for hours without buying anything? B: Yes, because many visitors like to browse for a while before they choose something, and if they feel relaxed, they usually end up buying more than one item.","t":"A：你覺得在旅遊區附近放幾張舒適的椅子是個好主意嗎？即使有人可能在那裡坐上好幾個小時卻什麼都不買。 B：是的，因為很多客人喜歡先【瀏覽】一會兒再做選擇，而且如果他們感到放鬆，最後通常會買不只一樣東西。"},{"w":"purchase","p":"v.","d":"to buy something","c":"購買","s":"A: The school librarian called this morning and said she has a budget for new English readers, but she isn't sure how many copies she can afford this year. B: If she decides to purchase more than thirty copies at once, we can give her a fifteen percent discount and deliver the boxes to her school for free.","t":"A：學校圖書館員今天早上打電話來說她有預算買新的英文讀本，但她不確定今年能負擔幾本。 B：如果她決定一次【購買】超過三十本，我們可以給她八五折，並免費把書送到她的學校。"},{"w":"checkout","p":"n.","d":"the place in a store where you pay for things; the act of paying","c":"結帳處；結帳","s":"A: Several shoppers wrote online that paying at our store takes too long, especially in the evening after work, so what is the company planning to do? B: Head office is installing a self-service checkout machine next month, so people with only one or two items can pay by card quickly without waiting in line.","t":"A：好幾位顧客在網路上寫說在我們店裡付款太久，尤其是下班後的晚上，公司打算怎麼做？ B：總公司下個月會安裝一台自助【結帳】機，這樣只買一兩樣東西的人就能快速刷卡付款，不用排隊。"},{"w":"receipt","p":"n.","d":"a piece of paper that shows you paid for something","c":"收據","s":"A: A woman wants to return a cookbook she bought as a gift last week because her friend already has a copy, so can we give her the money back? B: Yes, as long as she shows the receipt and the book is still in good condition, we can return the money to her credit card or give her store credit.","t":"A：有位女士想退回她上週買來送人的食譜，因為她朋友已經有一本了，我們可以退錢給她嗎？ B：可以，只要她出示【收據】而且書的狀況仍然良好，我們就可以把錢退到她的信用卡，或給她店內購物金。"},{"w":"bestseller","p":"n.","d":"a book that sells a very large number of copies","c":"暢銷書","s":"A: Why did the store order so many extra copies of that new business book, even though most new titles only sell a few copies each week? B: The author was interviewed on a popular TV program last night, and the book has become a bestseller in just a few days, so we expect lots of people to ask for it.","t":"A：為什麼書店多訂了那麼多本那本新的商業書？大部分新書每週只賣出幾本而已。 B：作者昨晚上了一個熱門電視節目接受訪問，這本書短短幾天就成了【暢銷書】，所以我們預期會有很多人來問。"},{"w":"staff","p":"n.","d":"the people who work for a business","c":"員工；職員","s":"A: The holiday season is our busiest time of the year, so what is the manager doing to make sure customers get help quickly when they come in? B: She is hiring extra staff for December, and every new employee will get two days of training on the cash register and our online ordering system.","t":"A：假期是一年中最忙的時候，經理打算怎麼確保顧客一進來就能很快得到協助？ B：她正在為十二月招募額外的【員工】，每位新進人員都會接受兩天的收銀機和線上訂購系統訓練。"},{"w":"recommend","p":"v.","d":"to say that something is good and suggest it to someone","c":"推薦","s":"A: A businessman just asked me for a good book to read on his long flight to London tomorrow, but I don't know much about his interests at all. B: Ask him what kinds of stories he enjoyed in the past, and then recommend two or three titles from our staff favorites table near the cashier.","t":"A：一位商人剛問我有沒有好書可以在他明天飛往倫敦的長途航班上看，但我完全不了解他的興趣。 B：問問他以前喜歡哪類故事，然後從收銀台附近的員工推薦桌上【推薦】兩三本書給他。"},{"w":"quiet","p":"adj.","d":"making little or no noise","c":"安靜的","s":"A: Why do so many university students come to our café on the second floor in the afternoon, even though there is a larger coffee shop across the street? B: They say our place is much more quiet than other cafés nearby, so they can study for their exams and read without being disturbed by loud music or noisy groups.","t":"A：為什麼下午有那麼多大學生來我們二樓的咖啡廳，即使對街就有一家更大的咖啡店？ B：他們說我們這裡比附近其他咖啡廳【安靜】多了，所以他們可以準備考試、看書，不會被大聲的音樂或吵鬧的團體打擾。"},{"w":"cozy","p":"adj.","d":"warm, comfortable, and relaxing","c":"溫暖舒適的","s":"A: The designer has shown us the plans for the new reading corner, but what kind of feeling does the owner want customers to have when they sit down there? B: She wants it to feel warm and cozy, like a living room at home, with soft lamps, a thick carpet, and comfortable armchairs where people can relax for hours.","t":"A：設計師已經給我們看了新閱讀角的規劃，但老闆希望顧客坐在那裡時有什麼樣的感覺？ B：她希望那裡感覺溫暖又【舒適】，就像家裡的客廳一樣，有柔和的檯燈、厚地毯和舒服的扶手椅，讓人可以放鬆好幾個小時。"},{"w":"independent","p":"adj.","d":"not owned or controlled by a larger company","c":"獨立的","s":"A: How is your small shop able to survive when the big online companies sell most books at much lower prices than you can offer? B: As an independent store that is not owned by a large company, we can choose unusual titles, hold local events, and give personal advice that people cannot get from a website.","t":"A：當大型網路公司賣的書大多比你們便宜很多時，你們這家小店要怎麼生存？ B：身為一家不屬於大公司的【獨立】書店，我們可以挑選特別的書、舉辦地方活動，並提供網站無法給的個人化建議。"},{"w":"chain","p":"n.","d":"a group of shops owned by the same company","c":"連鎖店","s":"A: I heard the old bookshop on Main Street was sold last month, so do you know whether the new owners are going to keep the same name and employees? B: It was bought by a national chain with more than two hundred stores, so they will probably change the sign and use the same design as their other branches.","t":"A：我聽說主街上那家老書店上個月被賣掉了，你知道新老闆會保留原來的店名和員工嗎？ B：它被一家擁有兩百多家門市的全國【連鎖店】買下了，所以他們可能會換招牌，並採用和其他分店一樣的設計。"},{"w":"inventory","p":"n.","d":"all the goods a store has; a list of these goods","c":"存貨；庫存清單","s":"A: Why is the store closing early this Sunday afternoon, since weekends are usually when we make most of our sales? B: All employees need to count every book and magazine on the shelves and in the storeroom, because the accountant needs an exact record of our inventory before the end of the financial year.","t":"A：為什麼書店這週日下午要提早打烊？週末通常是我們銷售最多的時候。 B：所有員工都需要清點架上和倉庫裡的每一本書和雜誌，因為會計師需要在會計年度結束前取得我們【存貨】的精確紀錄。"},{"w":"hardcover","p":"n.","d":"a book with a strong, stiff cover","c":"精裝本","s":"A: A customer wants to buy the new history book as a birthday gift for her grandfather, so which version should I suggest to her? B: Suggest the hardcover, because it has a strong, beautiful cover that will last for many years, even though it costs about ten dollars more than the soft version.","t":"A：有位顧客想買那本新的歷史書當作送給祖父的生日禮物，我該建議她哪一個版本？ B：建議她買【精裝本】，因為它有堅固又漂亮的封面，可以保存很多年，雖然比軟皮版貴大約十元。"},{"w":"paperback","p":"n.","d":"a book with a soft paper cover","c":"平裝本","s":"A: Many students say our textbooks and novels are too heavy to carry around in their school bags every day, so is there anything cheaper and lighter we can offer? B: Yes, most of those titles are also available in paperback, which is much lighter and usually costs about half the price of the hard version.","t":"A：很多學生說我們的教科書和小說太重，不適合每天放在書包裡帶著走，有沒有更便宜、更輕的選擇？ B：有，那些書大多也有【平裝本】，輕很多，價格通常只有精裝版的一半左右。"},{"w":"magazine","p":"n.","d":"a thin publication with articles and photos that comes out regularly","c":"雜誌","s":"A: The owner wants to attract more young office workers who stop by during their lunch break, so what kind of products should we add near the entrance? B: Let's add a rack with a monthly business magazine, some fashion titles, and a few travel guides, because people can read them quickly while they wait for their coffee.","t":"A：老闆想吸引更多午休時間順道進來的年輕上班族，我們應該在入口附近加哪類商品？ B：我們加一個架子，擺放每月出刊的商業【雜誌】、一些時尚刊物和幾本旅遊指南吧，因為大家等咖啡時可以快速翻閱。"},{"w":"stationery","p":"n.","d":"paper, pens, envelopes, and other writing materials","c":"文具","s":"A: Sales of books have been slow this spring, so is there anything else we can sell to bring more students and office workers into the shop? B: The manager plans to add a stationery corner with notebooks, pens, envelopes, and greeting cards, since people often need these items for school, work, and special occasions.","t":"A：今年春天書籍銷售一直很慢，我們有沒有其他東西可以賣，吸引更多學生和上班族來店裡？ B：經理打算增設一個【文具】區，販售筆記本、筆、信封和賀卡，因為大家上學、上班和特殊場合常常需要這些東西。"},{"w":"signing","p":"n.","d":"an event where an author signs copies of a book","c":"簽書會；簽名活動","s":"A: Why are there so many people waiting outside the store with copies of that new novel this morning, even though we don't open until ten o'clock? B: The famous author is coming at eleven for a book signing, so fans want to be first in line to meet her and get their copies autographed.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上有這麼多人拿著那本新小說在店外等？我們十點才開門。 B：那位知名作家十一點會來舉辦新書【簽書會】，所以書迷們想排在最前面跟她見面並取得簽名書。"},{"w":"event","p":"n.","d":"a planned public or social occasion","c":"活動","s":"A: The owner wants to bring more families into the shop on weekends, so do you have any ideas that won't cost the company too much money? B: We could hold a free storytelling event for children every Saturday morning, and parents could look around and buy books while their kids listen to the stories.","t":"A：老闆想在週末吸引更多家庭來店裡，你有沒有不會讓公司花太多錢的點子？ B：我們可以每週六早上為孩子舉辦免費的說故事【活動】，家長可以在孩子聽故事時四處逛逛、買書。"},{"w":"reading","p":"n.","d":"an event where a writer reads his or her work aloud to an audience","c":"朗讀會；閱讀","s":"A: The poet who wrote that new collection is visiting our city next week, so is the store planning anything special for her visit? B: Yes, she will give a public reading of her poems in the café on Thursday evening, and afterwards guests can ask her questions about her work and her writing habits.","t":"A：寫那本新詩集的詩人下週要來我們城市，書店有計畫為她的來訪安排什麼特別活動嗎？ B：有，她星期四晚上會在咖啡廳舉行公開詩作【朗讀會】，之後來賓可以問她有關作品和寫作習慣的問題。"},{"w":"community","p":"n.","d":"the people who live in one area","c":"社區；社群","s":"A: Why does our store offer its meeting room for free to local book clubs and parent groups, even though we could rent it out to companies instead? B: The owner believes a bookstore should be an important part of the neighborhood community, and when local people feel connected to the shop, they support it for many years.","t":"A：為什麼我們書店免費提供會議室給當地讀書會和家長團體使用，明明可以租給公司？ B：老闆相信書店應該成為鄰近【社區】重要的一部分，而當地居民對書店有歸屬感時，他們會支持它很多年。"},{"w":"literary","p":"adj.","d":"connected with literature or serious writing","c":"文學的","s":"A: The store has been asked to organize a weekend festival with famous writers, poets, and university professors, so what should we call it on the posters? B: Let's call it a literary festival, because the program focuses on novels, poetry, and serious writing, and that name will attract readers who love good books.","t":"A：書店受邀籌辦一場有知名作家、詩人和大學教授參加的週末節慶，我們在海報上該怎麼稱呼它？ B：就叫它【文學】節吧，因為節目重點是小說、詩和嚴肅寫作，這個名稱會吸引喜愛好書的讀者。"}]},{"unit":33,"theme":"Bored 感到無聊","cards":[{"w":"boredom","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being tired and unhappy because nothing is interesting","c":"無聊；厭倦","s":"A: Why did so many workers in the packing department ask to change jobs last month, even though the pay there is quite good? B: The HR survey showed that doing the same simple task for eight hours every day caused great boredom, so the manager is now planning to rotate staff between different stations each week.","t":"A：雖然包裝部門的薪水相當不錯，為什麼上個月有那麼多員工要求調職？ B：人資的調查顯示，每天八小時重複同樣簡單的工作讓人感到非常【無聊】，所以經理現在打算每週讓員工在不同的工作站之間輪調。"},{"w":"weary","p":"adj.","d":"very tired, especially after working hard for a long time","c":"疲倦的；厭倦的","s":"A: How did the sales team look when they finally came back from the trade show in Singapore after five long days? B: They all looked weary because they had been standing at the booth from early morning until late evening, so the director told them to take Monday off and rest at home.","t":"A：業務團隊在新加坡參加了漫長的五天商展終於回來時，看起來怎麼樣？ B：他們看起來都很【疲憊】，因為他們從清晨到深夜一直站在攤位前，所以主管要他們星期一休假，在家好好休息。"},{"w":"restless","p":"adj.","d":"unable to stay still or relaxed, often because you are bored or worried","c":"坐立不安的；焦躁的","s":"A: Why did the trainer suddenly stop her presentation and give everyone a fifteen-minute coffee break in the middle of the afternoon? B: She noticed that the new employees were becoming restless, moving in their chairs and checking their phones, after sitting and listening to her for nearly three hours without a pause.","t":"A：為什麼訓練講師在下午中途突然停止簡報，讓大家休息十五分鐘喝咖啡？ B：她注意到新進員工在沒有休息的情況下坐著聽她講了將近三個小時後，變得【坐立不安】，在椅子上動來動去，還一直看手機。"},{"w":"listless","p":"adj.","d":"having no energy or interest in doing anything","c":"無精打采的","s":"A: Is something wrong with Kevin from the accounting department, because he hardly said a word during the budget meeting this morning? B: He has seemed listless ever since his big project was cancelled last week, so his supervisor is going to talk with him and maybe give him a new task that he will enjoy more.","t":"A：會計部的凱文是不是怎麼了？他今天早上的預算會議中幾乎一句話也沒說。 B：自從他的大專案上週被取消後，他看起來一直【無精打采】，所以他的主管打算跟他談談，或許會給他一個他會更喜歡的新任務。"},{"w":"apathetic","p":"adj.","d":"showing no interest or concern about something","c":"冷漠的；漠不關心的","s":"A: Why did only twelve people vote in the election for the new staff committee, when the company has more than three hundred employees? B: Many workers have become apathetic because they believe the committee never changes anything, so the managers want to show some real results this year to win back their trust.","t":"A：公司有三百多名員工，為什麼新員工委員會的選舉只有十二個人投票？ B：許多員工變得【漠不關心】，因為他們認為委員會從來沒有改變任何事情，所以經理們希望今年能展現一些實際成果，以贏回大家的信任。"},{"w":"indifferent","p":"adj.","d":"not caring about or interested in something","c":"不在乎的；冷淡的","s":"A: Did the customers in the survey care much about the new color of our coffee cups, or were they more interested in something else? B: Most of them were completely indifferent to the color, but they complained a lot about the high prices and the long lines in the morning, so we should fix those problems first.","t":"A：調查中的顧客很在意我們咖啡杯的新顏色嗎？還是他們對別的事更感興趣？ B：他們大多對顏色完全【不在乎】，但對高價格和早上大排長龍抱怨很多，所以我們應該先解決那些問題。"},{"w":"disengaged","p":"adj.","d":"not feeling involved in or interested in your work or activity","c":"不投入的；疏離的","s":"A: What did the consultant say about the results of the employee satisfaction survey that we did across all our branches in March? B: She said that almost a third of our staff feel disengaged from their work because they rarely get feedback from managers, so she suggested holding short monthly meetings with every team member.","t":"A：顧問對我們三月在所有分店進行的員工滿意度調查結果怎麼說？ B：她說我們將近三分之一的員工對工作感到【不投入】，因為他們很少得到主管的回饋，所以她建議每個月和每位團隊成員舉行簡短的面談。"},{"w":"uninvolved","p":"adj.","d":"not taking part in something","c":"未參與的；置身事外的","s":"A: Should we ask the designers from the marketing department to join our planning meeting for the new product launch next week? B: No, they have been uninvolved in this project from the start, so it would be better to send them a short summary later instead of asking them to sit through a two-hour discussion.","t":"A：我們要不要請行銷部的設計師參加下週新產品發表的企劃會議？ B：不用，他們從一開始就【沒有參與】這個專案，所以與其要他們坐著聽兩個小時的討論，不如之後寄一份簡短的摘要給他們。"},{"w":"lethargic","p":"adj.","d":"feeling sleepy and having very little energy","c":"昏昏欲睡的；懶洋洋的","s":"A: Why does the office manager want to open the windows and turn up the lights in the meeting room every afternoon now? B: Many staff members said they felt lethargic after lunch in the warm, dark room, so she hopes that fresh air and brighter lights will help everyone stay awake and focused during the long meetings.","t":"A：為什麼辦公室經理現在每天下午都要打開會議室的窗戶並把燈開亮一點？ B：很多員工說午餐後在溫暖又昏暗的房間裡會感到【昏昏欲睡、提不起勁】，所以她希望新鮮空氣和明亮的燈光能幫助大家在冗長的會議中保持清醒和專注。"},{"w":"unmotivated","p":"adj.","d":"not having any reason or wish to work hard","c":"缺乏動力的","s":"A: Why are the new sales assistants making so few calls to customers, even though the manager has asked them several times to try harder? B: They feel unmotivated because there is no bonus for reaching their targets this year, so the director is thinking about bringing back a small reward for the top three sellers each month.","t":"A：雖然經理已經多次要求新的業務助理更努力，為什麼他們打給客戶的電話還是那麼少？ B：他們覺得【缺乏動力】，因為今年達成目標沒有獎金，所以主管正在考慮恢復每月給前三名業績最好的人一份小獎勵。"},{"w":"ennui","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of being bored and unhappy because life seems dull","c":"倦怠；百無聊賴","s":"A: Why did Laura decide to leave her well-paid office job at the bank and open a small bakery near the train station? B: After ten years of the same reports and the same meetings, she felt a deep ennui every morning, so she decided to follow her dream and do something creative that would make her happy.","t":"A：蘿拉為什麼決定辭掉銀行裡高薪的辦公室工作，在火車站附近開一間小烘焙坊？ B：做了十年同樣的報告、開同樣的會議之後，她每天早上都感到深深的【倦怠】，所以她決定追隨夢想，做些能讓她快樂的創意工作。"},{"w":"fed up","p":"adj.phr.","d":"annoyed and tired of something that has continued for too long","c":"受夠了的；厭煩的","s":"A: Why is the receptionist asking the building manager for a new air conditioner for the lobby again this week? B: She is fed up with the old machine because it breaks down almost every day in summer, and visitors keep complaining about the heat while they wait for their appointments.","t":"A：為什麼接待員這週又在向大樓管理員要求為大廳換新冷氣？ B：她已經【受夠了】那台舊機器，因為它夏天幾乎每天都故障，而訪客在等候約會時一直抱怨很熱。"},{"w":"tired","p":"adj.","d":"needing rest or sleep","c":"疲倦的；累的","s":"A: Why did the project manager decide to postpone the client presentation from this morning until tomorrow afternoon? B: The whole team worked until two o'clock last night to finish the slides, so they were too tired to explain the plan clearly, and she thought a good night's sleep would help them do much better.","t":"A：專案經理為什麼決定把客戶簡報從今天早上延到明天下午？ B：整個團隊昨晚工作到凌晨兩點才把投影片做完，所以他們太【累】了，沒辦法把計畫解釋清楚，她認為好好睡一晚會讓他們表現得好很多。"},{"w":"jaded","p":"adj.","d":"no longer interested or excited because you have seen or done something too often","c":"厭倦的；麻木的（因經歷太多）","s":"A: Why didn't the senior engineers get excited about the new software system that the IT department showed them yesterday? B: They have become jaded after watching so many \"amazing\" systems fail over the past twenty years, so they want to see real test results before they believe this one will work.","t":"A：昨天資訊部門展示新軟體系統時，資深工程師們為什麼一點都不興奮？ B：過去二十年看過太多「了不起」的系統失敗後，他們已經變得【麻木厭倦】，所以他們要先看到真正的測試結果，才會相信這套系統行得通。"},{"w":"unenthusiastic","p":"adj.","d":"not showing excitement or interest","c":"不熱衷的；冷淡的","s":"A: How did the staff react when the manager announced that the annual company trip would be a hiking tour in the mountains this year? B: Most of them were quite unenthusiastic because they had hoped for a beach resort, so the manager promised to send out a survey and let everyone vote on next year's destination.","t":"A：經理宣布今年的員工旅遊是山區健行之旅時，員工們有什麼反應？ B：他們大多相當【不熱衷】，因為他們原本希望去海灘度假村，所以經理答應會發問卷，讓大家投票決定明年的目的地。"},{"w":"detached","p":"adj.","d":"not emotionally involved; showing little interest or feeling","c":"冷漠疏離的；超然的","s":"A: Why did the customers give the new call center workers such low scores in last month's service survey? B: Many callers said the workers sounded detached and read from a script without really listening to their problems, so the manager is planning extra training on how to show care and understanding on the phone.","t":"A：上個月的服務調查中，顧客為什麼給新的客服中心人員這麼低的分數？ B：很多來電者說那些人員聽起來很【冷漠疏離】，只照著稿子念，沒有真正傾聽他們的問題，所以經理打算額外培訓他們如何在電話中表現關心和理解。"},{"w":"blank","p":"adj.","d":"showing no feeling, understanding, or interest","c":"茫然的；無表情的","s":"A: How did the audience react when the speaker started explaining the complicated tax rules at the end of the long conference yesterday? B: Most people just had blank looks on their faces because they were exhausted and did not understand the details, so the organizer decided to email everyone a simple summary the next day.","t":"A：昨天漫長的研討會快結束時，講者開始解釋複雜的稅務規定，聽眾有什麼反應？ B：大多數人臉上只是一臉【茫然】，因為他們已經筋疲力盡又聽不懂細節，所以主辦單位決定隔天寄一份簡單的摘要給大家。"},{"w":"passive","p":"adj.","d":"accepting what happens without trying to take action or change things","c":"被動的；消極的","s":"A: Why does the training manager want to change the format of the new employee workshops starting next month? B: She thinks that sitting and listening to long lectures makes trainees too passive, so she wants to add group tasks and role-plays that will get everyone talking and working together actively.","t":"A：訓練經理為什麼想從下個月開始改變新進員工研習的形式？ B：她認為坐著聽冗長的講課會讓學員太過【被動】，所以她想加入小組任務和角色扮演，讓每個人都積極地發言和合作。"},{"w":"uninterested","p":"adj.","d":"not wanting to learn more about something or take part in it","c":"不感興趣的","s":"A: Did the visitors from the hotel group want to hear more about our new cleaning service after the short demonstration this morning? B: Sadly, they seemed uninterested and kept looking at their watches, so I think we should prepare a cheaper package and contact them again when their current contract ends next spring.","t":"A：今天早上簡短的示範之後，飯店集團的訪客有想進一步了解我們的新清潔服務嗎？ B：可惜他們似乎【不感興趣】，一直看手錶，所以我想我們應該準備一個更便宜的方案，等他們目前的合約明年春天到期時再聯絡他們。"},{"w":"monotony","p":"n.","d":"a boring lack of change in something","c":"單調；千篇一律","s":"A: Why does the factory now play music and give workers a short break every two hours on the production line? B: The manager wanted to reduce the monotony of checking thousands of identical bottles all day long, because tired, bored workers were missing more mistakes and the number of customer complaints was rising.","t":"A：為什麼工廠現在在生產線上播放音樂，而且每兩小時讓工人短暫休息？ B：經理想減少整天檢查成千上萬個一模一樣的瓶子所帶來的【單調】，因為疲倦又無聊的工人漏掉更多錯誤，顧客投訴的數量也一直在增加。"},{"w":"drowsy","p":"adj.","d":"feeling sleepy","c":"昏昏欲睡的","s":"A: Why did the safety officer tell the delivery drivers not to take that cold medicine before their long trips? B: The medicine can make people feel drowsy, and falling asleep for even a second on the highway could cause a serious accident, so drivers should ask a doctor for a different kind that is safe to take.","t":"A：安全主管為什麼告訴送貨司機在長途行車前不要吃那種感冒藥？ B：那種藥會讓人感到【昏昏欲睡】，而在高速公路上即使只睡著一秒鐘也可能造成嚴重事故，所以司機應該請醫生開另一種可以安全服用的藥。"},{"w":"vacant","p":"adj.","d":"showing no interest, thought, or feeling","c":"茫然的；空洞的（表情）","s":"A: Did the interns understand the new filing system after Mr. Chen explained it to them for over an hour yesterday afternoon? B: I don't think so, because they just stared at him with vacant expressions the whole time, so I am going to make a simple step-by-step guide with pictures for them this morning.","t":"A：陳先生昨天下午花了一個多小時向實習生解釋新的歸檔系統，他們聽懂了嗎？ B：我覺得沒有，因為他們整個過程都用【茫然空洞】的表情盯著他，所以我今天早上要為他們做一份有圖片的簡單步驟說明。"},{"w":"resigned","p":"adj.","d":"accepting something unpleasant because you feel you cannot change it","c":"認命的；無奈接受的","s":"A: Are the staff still angry that the office will move to the industrial park outside the city at the end of this year? B: Not really anymore; they seem resigned to the change now because the decision is final, and the company has promised a free shuttle bus from the main train station every morning.","t":"A：員工們還在為辦公室今年年底要搬到市郊的工業區生氣嗎？ B：其實已經不太會了；他們現在似乎已經【無奈接受】這個改變，因為決定已成定局，而且公司答應每天早上提供從火車總站出發的免費接駁車。"},{"w":"numb","p":"adj.","d":"unable to feel emotions, often after a shock","c":"麻木的；失去感覺的","s":"A: How did the employees at the branch office feel when they heard that the company would close it after thirty years? B: At first, many of them just felt numb and could not react at all, but after a few days they started asking HR about job openings at the other branches in the city.","t":"A：分公司的員工聽到公司要在三十年後關閉分公司時，有什麼感受？ B：一開始他們很多人只是感到【麻木】，完全無法反應，但幾天後他們開始向人資詢問市內其他分店的職缺。"},{"w":"dispirited","p":"adj.","d":"having lost hope or enthusiasm","c":"灰心的；沮喪的","s":"A: Why does the sales team look so unhappy this morning, even though they worked very hard on the proposal for the airport project? B: They feel dispirited because the client chose a cheaper company yesterday, so the director is taking them out for lunch to thank them and talk about the next big opportunity.","t":"A：雖然業務團隊為機場專案的提案非常努力，為什麼他們今天早上看起來那麼不開心？ B：他們感到【灰心沮喪】，因為客戶昨天選擇了一家較便宜的公司，所以主管要請他們吃午餐表達謝意，並討論下一個大好機會。"},{"w":"unresponsive","p":"adj.","d":"not reacting or answering","c":"無回應的；反應遲鈍的","s":"A: Has the supplier in Vietnam replied to our emails about the late shipment of fabric that should have arrived last Friday? B: No, they have been completely unresponsive for over a week, so the purchasing manager plans to call their head office directly this afternoon and look for a backup supplier just in case.","t":"A：越南的供應商回覆我們關於上週五就該送達的布料延遲出貨的電子郵件了嗎？ B：沒有，他們已經一個多星期完全【沒有回應】，所以採購經理打算今天下午直接打電話到他們總公司，並且找一家備用供應商以防萬一。"},{"w":"drained","p":"adj.","d":"very tired, with no energy left","c":"精疲力竭的","s":"A: How do you feel after spending the whole day answering angry customers' calls about yesterday's system problem? B: I feel completely drained, because I talked to more than eighty people and had to stay calm and polite with every single one of them, so I am going straight home to rest tonight.","t":"A：花了一整天接聽顧客因為昨天系統問題打來的憤怒電話後，你感覺怎麼樣？ B：我覺得完全【精疲力竭】，因為我跟八十多個人通話，每一個都得保持冷靜和禮貌，所以我今晚要直接回家休息。"},{"w":"stagnant","p":"adj.","d":"not growing, changing, or developing","c":"停滯的；不景氣的","s":"A: Why is the board of directors so worried about the results of the company's clothing business in Asia this year? B: Sales have been stagnant for three years in a row while our competitors keep growing, so the board wants a new marketing plan that will attract younger customers and bring fresh energy to the brand.","t":"A：董事會為什麼對公司今年在亞洲的服飾業務成果這麼擔心？ B：我們的銷售已經連續三年【停滯不前】，而競爭對手卻持續成長，所以董事會想要一個能吸引年輕顧客、為品牌注入新活力的新行銷計畫。"},{"w":"burned out","p":"adj.phr.","d":"extremely tired and unable to work well because of too much work or stress","c":"身心俱疲的；職業倦怠的","s":"A: Why did the head nurse ask the hospital director to hire three more nurses for the night shift as soon as possible? B: Her team has been working twelve-hour shifts six days a week for months, and many of them are burned out, so she is afraid that some of them will quit or make serious mistakes.","t":"A：護理長為什麼要求醫院院長盡快為夜班多聘請三名護理師？ B：她的團隊好幾個月來每週工作六天、每班十二小時，很多人都已經【身心俱疲】，所以她擔心有些人會辭職或犯下嚴重錯誤。"}]},{"unit":34,"theme":"Boring 乏味的","cards":[{"w":"tedious","p":"adj.","d":"long and boring, making you tired","c":"冗長乏味的","s":"A: Why did Mark stay so late at the office last night when he usually leaves at six? B: He had to check five hundred customer addresses one by one in the old database, which is a really tedious job, but the manager needs the mailing list ready before the holiday sale begins next week.","t":"A：Mark平常六點就下班，為什麼他昨晚在辦公室待到那麼晚？ B：他必須在舊資料庫裡逐一核對五百個客戶地址，這是非常【冗長乏味的】工作，但經理需要在下週假期特賣開始前把郵寄名單準備好。"},{"w":"monotonous","p":"adj.","d":"always the same and boring, with no change","c":"單調的","s":"A: How was the training webinar about the new accounting software that the finance team attended yesterday afternoon? B: The software itself looks useful, but the speaker talked in a slow, monotonous voice for two hours without any slides or examples, so several people fell asleep before it ended.","t":"A：財務團隊昨天下午參加的新會計軟體培訓網路研討會怎麼樣？ B：軟體本身看起來很有用，但講者用緩慢、【單調的】聲音講了兩個小時，沒有任何投影片或例子，所以好幾個人在結束前就睡著了。"},{"w":"dull","p":"adj.","d":"not interesting or exciting; (of a blade) not sharp","c":"枯燥的；無聊的；鈍的","s":"A: Did you enjoy the company's annual dinner at the hotel on Friday night, or did you leave early like last year? B: I left early again, because the speeches were very dull and long, the music was too quiet, and most of my friends from the sales department had already gone home.","t":"A：你喜歡週五晚上在飯店舉行的公司年度晚宴嗎？還是你又像去年一樣提早離開了？ B：我又提早離開了，因為致詞非常【枯燥】又冗長，音樂太小聲，而且我業務部的大多數朋友都已經回家了。"},{"w":"repetitive","p":"adj.","d":"doing or saying the same thing many times","c":"重複的；反覆的","s":"A: Why does the factory want to buy those expensive new robots for the packaging line next year? B: The workers there do the same repetitive movements all day long, putting bottles into boxes, so many of them get sore arms, and the robots can do that work faster and more safely.","t":"A：工廠為什麼明年要為包裝線購買那些昂貴的新機器人？ B：那裡的工人整天都在做相同的【重複】動作，把瓶子裝進箱子裡，所以很多人手臂痠痛，而機器人可以更快、更安全地完成這項工作。"},{"w":"uninteresting","p":"adj.","d":"not able to hold your attention","c":"無趣的；引不起興趣的","s":"A: Why did so few visitors stop at our booth at the trade fair, even though we had the best location near the entrance? B: I think our display looked plain and uninteresting compared with the other companies, which had bright lights, free samples, and video screens that attracted crowds all day.","t":"A：雖然我們的攤位在入口附近位置最好，為什麼在商展上停下來的訪客這麼少？ B：我覺得和其他公司比起來，我們的展示看起來單調又【無趣】，他們有明亮的燈光、免費樣品和影片螢幕，整天都吸引人潮。"},{"w":"tiresome","p":"adj.","d":"annoying and boring, making you feel tired","c":"令人厭煩的","s":"A: Why do you look so annoyed after the phone call from that customer in Osaka this morning? B: He called for the fifth time this week to complain about the same small delay, and answering the same questions again and again is becoming very tiresome, even though I try to stay polite.","t":"A：今天早上大阪那位客戶打電話來之後，你為什麼看起來這麼不高興？ B：他這週已經第五次打來抱怨同一個小延誤，一再回答同樣的問題變得非常【令人厭煩】，雖然我還是努力保持禮貌。"},{"w":"dreary","p":"adj.","d":"dull, dark, and making you feel sad","c":"沉悶陰鬱的","s":"A: Why is the human resources team planning to repaint the staff room and buy new furniture this spring? B: The room is small, gray, and dreary, with no windows and old chairs, so employees don't want to spend their lunch break there, and the manager hopes brighter colors will improve everyone's mood.","t":"A：人資團隊為什麼打算今年春天重新粉刷員工休息室並購買新家具？ B：那個房間又小又灰、【沉悶陰鬱】，沒有窗戶，椅子也很舊，所以員工都不想在那裡度過午休，經理希望明亮的顏色能改善大家的心情。"},{"w":"mind-numbing","p":"adj.","d":"so boring that you cannot think clearly","c":"極其無聊的；令人麻木的","s":"A: How is your summer internship at the bank going, and are they giving you any interesting projects yet? B: Not really, I spend eight hours a day typing numbers from paper forms into a computer, which is mind-numbing work, but my supervisor promised that I can join a client meeting next month.","t":"A：你在銀行的暑期實習進行得如何？他們有給你任何有趣的專案了嗎？ B：還沒有，我每天花八小時把紙本表格上的數字輸入電腦，這是【極其無聊的】工作，不過我的主管答應下個月讓我參加一場客戶會議。"},{"w":"pointless","p":"adj.","d":"having no purpose or use","c":"毫無意義的","s":"A: Should we hold another meeting tomorrow to discuss the new office layout with the design team? B: I think it would be pointless, because the director already made the final decision yesterday, and the furniture has been ordered, so we should spend our time preparing for the move instead.","t":"A：我們明天要不要再開一次會，和設計團隊討論新辦公室的配置？ B：我覺得那會【毫無意義】，因為主任昨天已經做了最後決定，家具也已經訂了，所以我們應該把時間花在準備搬遷上。"},{"w":"uninspiring","p":"adj.","d":"not making people feel excited or interested","c":"平淡無奇的；無法激勵人心的","s":"A: What did the marketing director think of the first design for our new summer advertising campaign? B: She said the design was uninspiring because it used the same old colors and slogans as last year, and she asked us to create something fresh that would make young customers notice our products.","t":"A：行銷主任對我們新夏季廣告活動的初版設計有什麼看法？ B：她說那個設計【平淡無奇】，因為用的是和去年一樣的老顏色和標語，她要我們創造一些新鮮的東西，讓年輕顧客注意到我們的產品。"},{"w":"stale","p":"adj.","d":"no longer fresh; old and not interesting","c":"不新鮮的；陳腐的","s":"A: Why didn't anyone eat the cookies that were left on the table in the break room after the client visit? B: They had been sitting there without a cover since Monday, so they were hard and stale, and someone finally threw them away and bought fresh fruit for the afternoon meeting instead.","t":"A：客戶來訪後留在休息室桌上的餅乾，為什麼都沒人吃？ B：它們從週一開始就沒蓋著一直放在那裡，所以變得又硬又【不新鮮】，最後有人把它們丟掉，改買新鮮水果給下午的會議。"},{"w":"lifeless","p":"adj.","d":"without energy or excitement; dead-looking","c":"死氣沉沉的；缺乏生氣的","s":"A: Why did the restaurant owner decide to change the music and lighting in the dining area last month? B: Customers said the place felt cold and lifeless on weekday evenings, so she added warm lights, soft jazz, and some plants, and now more couples come in for dinner after work.","t":"A：餐廳老闆上個月為什麼決定改變用餐區的音樂和燈光？ B：顧客說平日晚上那裡感覺冷冰冰又【死氣沉沉】，所以她加了溫暖的燈光、輕柔的爵士樂和一些植物，現在有更多情侶下班後來吃晚餐。"},{"w":"routine","p":"n.","d":"the usual things you do regularly in the same order","c":"例行公事；慣例","s":"A: How do you stay so organized when you have to manage three different projects at the same time? B: I follow the same daily routine: I check my email at eight, plan my tasks before nine, and review the progress of each project at four, so nothing important gets forgotten.","t":"A：你同時要管理三個不同的專案，怎麼還能保持這麼有條理？ B：我每天都遵循相同的【例行公事】：八點查看電子郵件，九點前規劃工作，四點檢查每個專案的進度，這樣就不會忘記任何重要的事。"},{"w":"drag","p":"n.","d":"something boring or annoying (informal)","c":"令人厭煩的事；累贅","s":"A: Are you looking forward to the three-hour train ride to the branch office in Kaohsiung tomorrow morning? B: Not really, the trip is a real drag because the train is always crowded and the internet is slow, but at least I can read the sales report before I meet the branch manager.","t":"A：你期待明天早上搭三小時火車去高雄分公司嗎？ B：不太期待，這趟路程真是件【令人厭煩的事】，因為火車總是很擠、網路又慢，但至少我可以在見分公司經理前把銷售報告讀完。"},{"w":"chore","p":"n.","d":"a boring job that you have to do regularly","c":"雜務；乏味的工作","s":"A: Who is responsible for cleaning the coffee machine and emptying the recycling bins in our office every Friday? B: We take turns, so each person on the team does the chore once a month, and the schedule is posted on the kitchen wall so that nobody can forget their turn.","t":"A：每週五誰負責清理咖啡機和清空我們辦公室的回收桶？ B：我們輪流做，所以團隊中每個人每個月做一次這項【雜務】，值日表貼在茶水間的牆上，這樣就沒人會忘記輪到自己。"},{"w":"tedium","p":"n.","d":"the state of being long and boring","c":"單調乏味；沉悶","s":"A: How do the night security guards at the warehouse stay awake during their long twelve-hour shifts? B: They walk around the building every hour and listen to the radio between rounds, which helps them break the tedium of watching the same quiet cameras all night when nothing usually happens.","t":"A：倉庫的夜班保全在十二小時的長班中怎麼保持清醒？ B：他們每小時繞大樓巡邏一次，在巡邏之間聽收音機，這能幫助他們打破整晚盯著通常什麼事都沒發生的安靜監視器的【單調乏味】。"},{"w":"ennui","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of being bored and not satisfied with life","c":"倦怠；無聊感","s":"A: Why did your manager suddenly decide to take a six-month break from her job after working at the company for fifteen years? B: She told me she felt a deep ennui because every year looked exactly the same, so she wants to travel, study design, and find new energy before she returns.","t":"A：你的經理在公司工作了十五年之後，為什麼突然決定休假六個月？ B：她告訴我，她感到一種深深的【倦怠】，因為每一年看起來都一模一樣，所以她想去旅行、學設計，並在回來之前找到新的活力。"},{"w":"plodding","p":"adj.","d":"slow and boring, without excitement","c":"緩慢乏味的；拖沓的","s":"A: Why did the publisher ask the author to rewrite the first three chapters of her new mystery novel? B: The editor said the story moved at a slow, plodding pace at the beginning, so readers might stop reading before the exciting murder scene finally happens in chapter four.","t":"A：出版社為什麼要求作者重寫她新推理小說的前三章？ B：編輯說故事開頭的節奏緩慢又【拖沓】，所以讀者可能在第四章終於出現精彩的謀殺場景之前就不想讀了。"},{"w":"predictable","p":"adj.","d":"happening in a way that you expected","c":"可預料的；老套的","s":"A: Did you enjoy the action movie that the team watched together after the company dinner on Friday? B: The special effects were great, but the story was so predictable that I knew exactly how it would end after twenty minutes, so I spent most of the time checking my phone.","t":"A：你喜歡週五公司晚餐後團隊一起看的那部動作片嗎？ B：特效很棒，但劇情太【老套】了，二十分鐘後我就完全知道會怎麼結束，所以我大部分時間都在看手機。"},{"w":"uneventful","p":"adj.","d":"with nothing interesting or unusual happening","c":"平靜無事的；平淡的","s":"A: How was your first week at the new branch, and did anything exciting happen while the manager was away? B: It was quite uneventful, to be honest, because there were only a few customers, no problems with the computers, and I spent most of my time reading training manuals.","t":"A：你在新分行的第一週過得怎麼樣？經理不在的時候有發生什麼令人興奮的事嗎？ B：老實說相當【平靜無事】，因為只有少數幾位顧客，電腦也沒有出問題，我大部分時間都在讀培訓手冊。"},{"w":"bland","p":"adj.","d":"without a strong taste or interest","c":"淡而無味的；平淡的","s":"A: Why did the hotel restaurant get so many bad reviews from guests on the travel website last month? B: Many guests said the food was too bland, with almost no salt or spices, so the new chef is now changing the menu and adding more local flavors to every dish.","t":"A：飯店餐廳上個月為什麼在旅遊網站上收到那麼多房客的負評？ B：很多房客說食物太【淡而無味】，幾乎沒有鹽或香料，所以新主廚正在更改菜單，並在每道菜中加入更多在地風味。"},{"w":"dry","p":"adj.","d":"boring because it is serious and has no humor or pictures","c":"枯燥的；乏味的","s":"A: Why do so many new employees skip the online course about company rules and safety laws? B: The course is very dry because it only has long pages of legal text with no pictures or examples, so the training team is planning to add short videos and quizzes next year.","t":"A：為什麼那麼多新進員工都跳過關於公司規定和安全法規的線上課程？ B：那門課程非常【枯燥】，因為只有一頁頁冗長的法律文字，沒有圖片或例子，所以培訓團隊打算明年加入短片和小測驗。"},{"w":"unvaried","p":"adj.","d":"always the same, with no change","c":"一成不變的","s":"A: Why are the staff complaining about the lunch boxes that the company provides in the cafeteria? B: The menu has been completely unvaried for six months, with the same chicken, rice, and cabbage every single day, so many workers now buy their lunch from shops near the office.","t":"A：員工為什麼在抱怨公司餐廳提供的便當？ B：六個月來菜單完全【一成不變】，每天都是一樣的雞肉、米飯和高麗菜，所以現在很多員工都去辦公室附近的店買午餐。"},{"w":"wearisome","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel tired and bored","c":"令人疲倦厭煩的","s":"A: How did the negotiations with the supplier go after you spent the whole week at their head office? B: It was a long and wearisome process, because we argued about the same prices every day, but in the end we signed a two-year contract that saves us ten percent.","t":"A：你在供應商總部待了一整週之後，和他們的談判進行得如何？ B：那是一個冗長又【令人疲倦厭煩的】過程，因為我們每天都在爭論同樣的價格，但最後我們簽了一份兩年合約，為我們省下了百分之十。"},{"w":"flat","p":"adj.","d":"without energy or growth; not changing","c":"平淡的；停滯的","s":"A: How were the sales of our new sports drink during the first quarter of this year? B: Sales were quite flat, with almost no growth from January to March, so the marketing team plans to give out free samples at gyms and running events to attract more customers.","t":"A：我們的新運動飲料今年第一季的銷售如何？ B：銷售相當【停滯】，從一月到三月幾乎沒有成長，所以行銷團隊打算在健身房和路跑活動發送免費樣品來吸引更多顧客。"},{"w":"humdrum","p":"adj.","d":"ordinary and boring","c":"平凡乏味的","s":"A: Why did Kevin leave his comfortable job at the insurance office to become a tour guide in Europe? B: He said his life felt too humdrum, with the same desk, the same forms, and the same bus ride every day, and he wanted a job where he could meet new people.","t":"A：Kevin 為什麼離開保險公司舒適的工作，去歐洲當導遊？ B：他說他的生活感覺太【平凡乏味】，每天都是同樣的辦公桌、同樣的表格和同樣的公車路程，他想要一份能認識新朋友的工作。"},{"w":"dreariness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being dull, dark, and sad","c":"沉悶；陰鬱","s":"A: What made you decide to move your small design company out of that old building near the train station? B: The dreariness of the place was affecting our creativity, with dark hallways and gray walls everywhere, so we rented a bright studio with large windows near the river.","t":"A：是什麼讓你決定把你的小設計公司搬出火車站附近那棟舊大樓？ B：那個地方的【陰鬱沉悶】正在影響我們的創意，到處都是昏暗的走廊和灰色牆壁，所以我們在河邊租了一間有大窗戶的明亮工作室。"},{"w":"unstimulating","p":"adj.","d":"not making you think or feel interested","c":"缺乏刺激的；無法激發興趣的","s":"A: Why did the young engineer quit after only three months, even though the salary was very good? B: She found the work unstimulating because she only copied old drawings and never solved any real problems, so she accepted an offer from a smaller company with more challenging projects.","t":"A：那位年輕工程師為什麼才三個月就辭職了，即使薪水很好？ B：她覺得工作【缺乏刺激】，因為她只是複製舊圖紙，從來沒有解決過任何真正的問題，所以她接受了一家有更多挑戰性專案的小公司的錄取。"},{"w":"mechanical","p":"adj.","d":"done without thinking or feeling, like a machine","c":"機械式的；呆板的","s":"A: Why did the customer service manager change the way the staff answer phone calls last month? B: Customers said the staff sounded mechanical because they read the same script word for word, so now employees are trained to listen carefully and answer in a more natural and friendly way.","t":"A：客服經理上個月為什麼改變了員工接電話的方式？ B：顧客說員工聽起來很【機械式】，因為他們逐字照讀同一份稿子，所以現在員工都接受訓練，要仔細聆聽，並用更自然友善的方式回答。"},{"w":"lacklustre","p":"adj.","d":"lacking energy, excitement, or success","c":"平淡無奇的；表現不佳的","s":"A: Why is the board of directors meeting again this afternoon after the meeting they had on Monday? B: The company announced lacklustre results for the third quarter, with profits much lower than expected, so the directors need to discuss a new plan to reduce costs and win back investors.","t":"A：董事會週一才開過會，為什麼今天下午又要開會？ B：公司公布了第三季【表現不佳的】業績，利潤比預期低很多，所以董事們需要討論一個降低成本、贏回投資人的新計畫。"}]},{"unit":35,"theme":"Borrow 借用","cards":[{"w":"avid","p":"adj.","d":"very keen and interested in something","c":"熱衷的；熱心的","s":"A: Why does the library want to invite Mr. Chen to speak at next month's reading event, even though he is not a famous author or a teacher? B: He is an avid reader who borrows about ten books every week, so the staff believe his stories and advice will encourage more local families to visit.","t":"A：為什麼圖書館想邀請陳先生在下個月的閱讀活動上演講，即使他不是知名作家也不是老師？ B：他是一位【熱衷的】讀者，每週借大約十本書，所以館員相信他的故事和建議會鼓勵更多當地家庭來館。"},{"w":"recommend","p":"v.","d":"to say that someone or something is good or that someone should do something","c":"推薦；建議","s":"A: I need to borrow a projector for the sales presentation on Friday, but our department's one is broken, so do you know where I can get another one quickly? B: I would recommend asking the IT office on the third floor, because they usually lend equipment to staff for a few days without any charge.","t":"A：我週五的業務簡報需要借一台投影機，但我們部門的那台壞了，你知道我可以去哪裡很快借到另一台嗎？ B：我會【建議】你去問三樓的資訊部辦公室，因為他們通常會免費把設備借給員工使用幾天。"},{"w":"awkward","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel uncomfortable or embarrassed","c":"尷尬的；令人不自在的","s":"A: Why didn't you ask your manager if you could borrow her laptop while yours was being repaired at the service center last week? B: It felt a little awkward to ask her, because she had just lent me her car the week before, so I used an old computer in the meeting room instead.","t":"A：上週你的筆電在維修中心修理時，你為什麼不問經理能不能借她的筆電？ B：向她開口讓我覺得有點【尷尬】，因為她前一週才剛借我車，所以我改用了會議室裡的一台舊電腦。"},{"w":"seldom","p":"adv.","d":"not often; rarely","c":"很少；不常","s":"A: Do you think we should buy our own ladder for the shop, or should we keep borrowing one from the hardware store next door whenever we need it? B: Let's keep borrowing, because we seldom need a ladder more than twice a year, and a new one would take up too much space in our small storage room.","t":"A：你覺得我們應該替店裡買一把自己的梯子，還是每次需要時繼續向隔壁五金行借？ B：繼續借吧，因為我們一年【很少】需要用到梯子超過兩次，而且買新的會占用我們小儲藏室太多空間。"},{"w":"innumerable","p":"adj.","d":"too many to be counted","c":"數不清的；無數的","s":"A: Why is the public library planning to move its old newspapers and magazines into a digital system next year? B: Because there are innumerable paper copies in the basement, and the staff spend hours finding the right one whenever a visitor wants to borrow an article for research.","t":"A：公立圖書館為什麼打算明年把舊報紙和雜誌移到數位系統？ B：因為地下室裡有【數不清的】紙本，每當有訪客想借閱某篇文章做研究時，館員都要花好幾個小時才找得到。"},{"w":"make ends meet","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have just enough money to pay for the things you need","c":"維持收支平衡；勉強維持生計","s":"A: Why did the young designer decide to borrow money from his parents instead of applying for a bank loan last month? B: His rent went up sharply in January, and he could barely make ends meet with his small salary, so his parents offered him a loan without any interest until he finds a better job.","t":"A：那位年輕設計師上個月為什麼決定向父母借錢，而不是去申請銀行貸款？ B：他的房租在一月大幅上漲，靠著微薄的薪水他幾乎無法【維持收支平衡】，所以他父母提供他無息借款，直到他找到更好的工作。"},{"w":"wear and tear","p":"n.phr.","d":"damage that happens to things through normal use over time","c":"（正常使用造成的）磨損；耗損","s":"A: The customer returned the camera that she rented from us for two weeks, so do we need to charge her extra for the small scratches on the lens cover? B: No, those marks are just normal wear and tear, and our rental agreement clearly says that customers only pay for serious damage or missing parts.","t":"A：那位客戶歸還了她向我們租了兩週的相機，我們需要因為鏡頭蓋上的小刮痕向她額外收費嗎？ B：不用，那些痕跡只是正常的【磨損】，而且我們的租賃合約寫得很清楚，客戶只需為嚴重損壞或遺失零件付費。"},{"w":"on time","p":"phr.","d":"at the correct time; not late","c":"準時","s":"A: Will the bank give us a lower interest rate if we ask for a second loan to open another branch of our restaurant next spring? B: There is a good chance, because we have made every monthly payment on time for the last three years, and the bank manager said they value reliable customers like us.","t":"A：如果我們申請第二筆貸款，在明年春天開餐廳的另一家分店，銀行會給我們較低的利率嗎？ B：很有可能，因為過去三年我們每一期月付款都【準時】繳納，而且銀行經理說他們很重視像我們這樣可靠的客戶。"},{"w":"fragile","p":"adj.","d":"easily broken or damaged","c":"易碎的；脆弱的","s":"A: Can I borrow the glass display stands from your shop for our product launch at the hotel this weekend? B: Sure, but please pack them carefully in the boxes with plenty of paper, because they are very fragile and could break easily if the delivery van hits a bump on the way.","t":"A：這週末我們在飯店舉辦產品發表會，我可以向你的店借那些玻璃展示架嗎？ B：當然可以，但請用大量紙張仔細把它們裝進箱子裡，因為它們非常【易碎】，如果貨車在途中顛簸，很容易就會破掉。"},{"w":"persist","p":"v.","d":"to continue to exist or happen for a long time","c":"持續；持續存在","s":"A: What should I do about the printer that we borrowed from the head office, since it keeps showing an error message even though I have restarted it several times this morning? B: If the problems persist after lunch, please call the technician, because we must print two hundred brochures for the trade fair by tomorrow morning.","t":"A：我們向總公司借來的印表機一直出現錯誤訊息，雖然我今天早上已經重新啟動好幾次了，我該怎麼辦？ B：如果午餐後問題【持續存在】，請打電話給技術人員，因為我們明天早上前必須印好兩百份商展用的手冊。"},{"w":"compromise","p":"n.","d":"an agreement in which each side accepts less than it wanted","c":"妥協；折衷","s":"A: Did you and the landlord finally agree on how much rent you have to pay while the office building is being repaired? B: Yes, we reached a compromise yesterday afternoon, so we will pay only half the normal rent for three months, and he will lend us some extra desks for the temporary rooms.","t":"A：大樓整修期間你們要付多少租金，你和房東終於談好了嗎？ B：是的，我們昨天下午達成了【妥協】，所以這三個月我們只付一半的正常租金，而且他還會借我們一些額外的桌子放在臨時辦公室。"},{"w":"write off","p":"v.phr.","d":"to decide that a debt will never be paid and remove it from the accounts","c":"註銷（債務）；勾銷","s":"A: What did the finance department decide about the money that a small customer borrowed from us two years ago and never paid back? B: Since the customer's company has closed and nobody can contact the owner, the director agreed to write off the debt and remove it from this year's accounts.","t":"A：關於一位小客戶兩年前向我們借了卻一直沒還的錢，財務部決定怎麼處理？ B：由於那位客戶的公司已經倒閉，也沒有人聯絡得上老闆，主管同意把這筆債務【註銷】，並從今年的帳目中移除。"},{"w":"assume","p":"v.","d":"to think something is true without being sure","c":"以為；假定；猜想","s":"A: Why didn't Ms. Lin bring back the meeting room keys that she borrowed from the reception desk yesterday afternoon? B: I assume that she simply forgot about them, because she left for the airport in a hurry, so I'll send her a text message and ask her to drop them off tomorrow morning.","t":"A：林小姐為什麼沒有把她昨天下午向櫃檯借的會議室鑰匙還回來？ B：我【猜想】她只是忘了，因為她匆忙趕去機場，所以我會傳簡訊給她，請她明天早上把鑰匙送回來。"},{"w":"reasonable","p":"adj.","d":"fair and not too expensive or too much","c":"合理的；價格公道的","s":"A: Is the interest rate on the small business loan from the local bank too high for our new bakery, or should we accept their offer? B: I think the rate is quite reasonable compared with the other banks that we visited, and the payment plan gives us five years to pay back the full amount.","t":"A：當地銀行提供的小型企業貸款利率對我們新開的麵包店來說會太高嗎？還是我們應該接受他們的條件？ B：和我們拜訪過的其他銀行相比，我覺得這個利率相當【合理】，而且還款計畫給我們五年時間償還全部金額。"},{"w":"tiny","p":"adj.","d":"very small","c":"極小的；很小的","s":"A: Can you lend me your storage room for a few days, because I need somewhere to keep the extra chairs for the company party? B: I'm sorry, but my storage room is really tiny, and it is already full of boxes, so maybe you should ask the building manager whether the basement is free.","t":"A：你可以把你的儲藏室借我幾天嗎？因為我需要地方放公司派對多出來的椅子。 B：抱歉，我的儲藏室真的很【小】，而且已經堆滿箱子了，也許你應該問問大樓管理員地下室是否有空。"},{"w":"let go","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop holding or keeping something (often with \"of\")","c":"放手；放開","s":"A: Why did your brother finally agree to lend his old car to his cousin, since he loved it so much and never allowed anyone else to drive it? B: He realized that he hardly ever drove it anymore, so he decided to let go of it for a while, and his cousin can now use it for her new job in the city.","t":"A：你哥哥那麼愛他的舊車，從不讓別人開，為什麼最後同意把它借給他的表妹？ B：他發現自己幾乎不再開那台車了，所以決定暫時【放手】，現在他表妹可以開它去城裡上新工作。"},{"w":"give in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to finally agree to something after first refusing","c":"讓步；屈服","s":"A: Did the store manager agree to lend the customer a free phone while her broken one was being repaired? B: At first he said no, but the customer complained for twenty minutes in front of other shoppers, so he finally decided to give in and offered her an older model for one week.","t":"A：店經理有同意在顧客壞掉的手機維修期間借她一支免費手機嗎？ B：一開始他拒絕了，但那位顧客在其他購物者面前抱怨了二十分鐘，所以他最後決定【讓步】，借她一支舊型號手機使用一週。"},{"w":"frustrating","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel annoyed because you cannot do what you want","c":"令人沮喪的；令人洩氣的","s":"A: How was your experience applying for a student loan at the bank downtown last week? B: It was really frustrating, because I waited in line for two hours, and then the clerk told me that I had to fill out the same forms again on the bank's website.","t":"A：你上週在市區那家銀行申請學生貸款的經驗如何？ B：真的很【令人沮喪】，因為我排隊等了兩個小時，然後行員告訴我必須在銀行網站上重新填一次同樣的表格。"},{"w":"upset","p":"adj.","d":"unhappy and worried or angry","c":"不高興的；心煩的","s":"A: Why does Mr. Wang look so unhappy this morning, and why isn't he talking to anyone in the design team? B: He is upset because someone borrowed his expensive drawing tablet without asking, and when it came back yesterday, the screen had a long crack across the middle.","t":"A：王先生今天早上為什麼看起來這麼不開心，而且都不跟設計團隊的任何人說話？ B：他很【不高興】，因為有人沒問過他就借走了他昂貴的繪圖板，昨天還回來時，螢幕中間多了一道長長的裂痕。"},{"w":"repay","p":"v.","d":"to pay back money that you borrowed","c":"償還；還（錢）","s":"A: How long will it take our company to pay off the loan that we used to buy the new delivery trucks last year? B: If sales keep growing like this, we should be able to repay the full amount by next summer, which is almost two years earlier than the bank expected.","t":"A：我們公司去年用來買新貨車的那筆貸款，要多久才能還清？ B：如果銷售持續這樣成長，我們應該能在明年夏天前【償還】全部金額，比銀行預期的提早了將近兩年。"},{"w":"give back","p":"v.phr.","d":"to return something to the person who owns it","c":"歸還；還給","s":"A: Have you finished using the tools that you borrowed from the maintenance department for the shelves in the new meeting room? B: Almost, I just need to fix the last shelf, and then I'll give back the drill and the ladder before the department closes at five o'clock this afternoon.","t":"A：你向維修部借來裝新會議室架子的工具用完了嗎？ B：快好了，我只要再裝好最後一個架子，然後我會在維修部今天下午五點下班前把電鑽和梯子【歸還】。"}]},{"unit":36,"theme":"Break 休息","cards":[{"w":"rest","p":"n.","d":"a period of relaxing or sleeping to get back your energy","c":"休息","s":"A: You look exhausted after flying back from the trade show in Singapore, so are you planning to come to the sales meeting this afternoon? B: No, my manager told me to go home and get some rest first, because I barely slept on the plane and I need a clear head for tomorrow's client visit.","t":"A：你從新加坡的商展飛回來看起來累壞了，你打算來參加今天下午的業務會議嗎？ B：不，我的經理叫我先回家好好【休息】，因為我在飛機上幾乎沒睡，而且明天拜訪客戶需要頭腦清醒。"},{"w":"pause","p":"n.","d":"a short stop in speaking or doing something","c":"暫停；停頓","s":"A: The speaker at this morning's training session talked very fast, so how did the new employees manage to take notes on all the safety rules? B: She made a short pause after each important point, which gave everyone a few seconds to write things down and ask questions before she moved on to the next slide.","t":"A：今天早上訓練課程的講者講得很快，新員工是怎麼把所有安全規定都記下來的？ B：她在每個重點之後都會短暫【停頓】一下，讓大家有幾秒鐘可以寫下來並發問，然後才進到下一張投影片。"},{"w":"interval","p":"n.","d":"the time between two events","c":"間隔；間隔時間","s":"A: How often does the shuttle bus run between the train station and the convention center during the international technology fair next week? B: The organizers said there will be a fifteen-minute interval between buses from seven in the morning until nine at night, so visitors should never have to wait very long in the cold.","t":"A：下週國際科技展期間，火車站和會展中心之間的接駁車多久一班？ B：主辦單位說從早上七點到晚上九點，每班車之間【間隔】十五分鐘，所以參觀者不必在寒冷中等太久。"},{"w":"time off","p":"n.phr.","d":"time when you are not at work","c":"休假；不上班的時間","s":"A: Have you decided what you're going to do after the big product launch is finished at the end of this month? B: I've asked my supervisor for some time off in early December, because I have been working overtime for weeks and I really want to visit my parents in the countryside.","t":"A：你決定這個月底大型產品發表會結束後要做什麼了嗎？ B：我已經向主管申請十二月初【休假】幾天，因為我已經連續加班好幾週了，真的很想回鄉下看看我爸媽。"},{"w":"relax","p":"v.","d":"to rest and become calm","c":"放鬆","s":"A: The hotel guests in room 512 just complained that the meeting next door was too noisy, so what should we offer them? B: Let's give them free tickets to the spa on the top floor, where they can relax in the hot pool and enjoy a massage while we move the conference to a different room.","t":"A：512號房的房客剛剛抱怨隔壁的會議太吵，我們應該提供他們什麼？ B：我們送他們頂樓水療中心的免費券吧，他們可以在溫水池裡【放鬆】、享受按摩，同時我們把會議移到別的房間。"},{"w":"unwind","p":"v.","d":"to relax after work or a stressful time","c":"放鬆心情；紓壓","s":"A: Most of the accountants have been staying in the office until midnight to finish the annual report, so how can we help them feel better? B: I'm planning a casual dinner at the Italian restaurant across the street on Friday night, so everyone can unwind together and forget about numbers for a few hours.","t":"A：大部分會計師為了完成年度報告都待在辦公室到半夜，我們要怎麼讓他們好過一點？ B：我打算週五晚上在對街的義大利餐廳辦個輕鬆的晚餐，讓大家可以一起【放鬆心情】，暫時忘掉數字幾個小時。"},{"w":"recharge","p":"v.","d":"to get your energy back by resting","c":"恢復精力；充電","s":"A: Why did the company decide to give every employee an extra day off after the busy holiday shopping season? B: The managers believe that people need time to rest and recharge after working long hours, so they come back to work with more energy and new ideas for the coming year.","t":"A：公司為什麼決定在忙碌的假期購物季後給每位員工多放一天假？ B：主管們認為大家在長時間工作後需要休息、【恢復精力】，這樣回來上班時才會更有活力，並為新的一年帶來新點子。"},{"w":"recover","p":"v.","d":"to get well again after being sick, hurt or in trouble","c":"康復；恢復","s":"A: Is the warehouse manager coming back to work on Monday, or should we ask someone else to check the deliveries next week? B: He called this morning and said he needs a few more days at home to recover from the flu, so please ask Linda to handle the deliveries until he returns.","t":"A：倉庫經理星期一會回來上班嗎？還是我們下週應該請別人檢查送貨？ B：他今天早上打電話來說還需要在家幾天從流感中【康復】，所以在他回來之前請琳達處理送貨的事。"},{"w":"refresh","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel less tired and more lively","c":"使恢復精神；使清爽","s":"A: The workshop has been going on for three hours, and some of the participants look like they are falling asleep in their chairs. B: Let's stop for fifteen minutes so people can get a cup of coffee and some fresh air outside, which should refresh everyone before we start the final group activity.","t":"A：研習已經進行三個小時了，有些參加者看起來快在椅子上睡著了。 B：我們停十五分鐘，讓大家去喝杯咖啡、到外面呼吸新鮮空氣，這應該能讓大家【恢復精神】，再開始最後的小組活動。"},{"w":"breather","p":"n.","d":"a short rest from work or effort","c":"短暫休息；喘口氣","s":"A: We have been answering customer emails nonstop since eight o'clock, and I can't even think clearly anymore. B: Why don't we take a quick breather and walk to the bakery around the corner, because a short walk will help us focus better when we come back to finish the rest of the messages.","t":"A：我們從八點開始就不停地回覆客戶的電子郵件，我已經沒辦法清楚思考了。 B：我們何不【稍作喘息】，走到轉角的麵包店，因為短暫散步能幫助我們回來處理剩下的訊息時更專心。"},{"w":"respite","p":"n.","d":"a short time of relief from something unpleasant","c":"暫緩；喘息","s":"A: The construction work outside our office has been extremely loud every day this month, so has anything changed? B: Yes, the workers are stopping for the national holiday this weekend, so we will finally get a short respite from the noise, although they will start drilling again on Monday morning.","t":"A：這個月我們辦公室外面的工程每天都非常吵，有什麼改變嗎？ B：有，工人們這個週末因國定假日停工，所以我們終於可以從噪音中得到短暫的【喘息】，不過他們星期一早上又會開始鑽地了。"},{"w":"timeout","p":"n.","d":"a short stop in a game so a team can rest or plan","c":"（比賽中的）暫停","s":"A: The basketball team that our company sponsors was losing badly at halftime, so what happened in the second half of the game? B: The coach called a timeout in the third quarter and gave the players a new plan, and after that they scored twenty points in a row and won the match.","t":"A：我們公司贊助的籃球隊上半場輸得很慘，下半場發生了什麼事？ B：教練在第三節喊了【暫停】，給球員們一個新戰術，之後他們連得二十分，贏了比賽。"},{"w":"intermission","p":"n.","d":"a short break between the parts of a show or concert","c":"中場休息","s":"A: The clients we invited to the concert tonight might want something to eat, so is there a good time to visit the snack bar? B: Yes, there is a twenty-minute intermission between the first and second parts of the show, so we can take them to the lobby for drinks and sandwiches then.","t":"A：我們今晚邀去聽音樂會的客戶可能會想吃點東西，有沒有適合去點心吧的時間？ B：有，表演上下半場之間有二十分鐘的【中場休息】，我們可以那時帶他們去大廳喝飲料、吃三明治。"},{"w":"downtime","p":"n.","d":"time when a machine or system is not working","c":"停機時間；（系統）無法運作的時間","s":"A: Why couldn't our customers place any online orders last night between midnight and three in the morning? B: The IT department planned some downtime to update the website's payment system, and they sent an email to all customers last week to explain that the site would be unavailable for a few hours.","t":"A：為什麼我們的顧客昨晚午夜到凌晨三點之間無法在線上下單？ B：資訊部門安排了一段【停機時間】來更新網站的付款系統，他們上週也寄了電子郵件給所有顧客，說明網站會有幾個小時無法使用。"},{"w":"leisure","p":"n.","d":"free time when you are not working","c":"閒暇；空閒時間","s":"A: What kinds of facilities will the new apartment building near our head office offer to the people who live there? B: Besides a swimming pool and a gym, there will be a large garden and a reading room, so residents can enjoy their leisure without leaving the building on weekends.","t":"A：我們總公司附近的新公寓大樓會提供住戶哪些設施？ B：除了游泳池和健身房，還會有大花園和閱讀室，所以住戶週末不必離開大樓就能享受【閒暇時光】。"},{"w":"vacation","p":"n.","d":"a period of time away from work or school for rest or travel","c":"假期；度假","s":"A: I noticed that Mr. Chen's desk has been empty all week, so is he working from home or visiting a client overseas? B: Neither, he is on a two-week vacation with his family in Japan, and he asked me to answer his phone calls and forward any urgent emails until he gets back.","t":"A：我注意到陳先生的座位整個禮拜都空著，他是在家工作還是去國外拜訪客戶？ B：都不是，他和家人在日本【度假】兩週，他請我在他回來之前幫他接電話並轉寄緊急郵件。"},{"w":"holiday","p":"n.","d":"a day when most people do not have to work","c":"假日；節日","s":"A: Will the bank downtown be open on Monday, because I need to deposit the payments we received from our customers? B: No, Monday is a national holiday, so all the banks and government offices will be closed, but you can use the machine in the lobby or wait until Tuesday.","t":"A：市中心的銀行星期一會開嗎？我需要把客戶付的款項存進去。 B：不會，星期一是國定【假日】，所有銀行和政府機關都不上班，不過你可以使用大廳的機器，或等到星期二。"},{"w":"nap","p":"n.","d":"a short sleep during the day","c":"小睡；午睡","s":"A: You seem much more cheerful this afternoon than you were this morning, so did you drink another cup of strong coffee? B: Actually, I took a short nap in the staff lounge during my lunch hour, and twenty minutes of sleep made me feel much more awake for the rest of the day.","t":"A：你今天下午看起來比早上開心多了，是又喝了一杯濃咖啡嗎？ B：其實我午休時間在員工休息室【小睡】了一下，睡二十分鐘讓我接下來一整天都清醒多了。"},{"w":"step back","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop and think about a situation from a distance","c":"退一步（思考）","s":"A: Our team has been arguing about the new advertising plan for two hours, and nobody wants to change their opinion. B: I think we should step back and look at the bigger picture, because the main goal is to attract younger customers, not to prove who has the best idea.","t":"A：我們團隊為了新的廣告企劃已經吵了兩個小時，沒有人想改變意見。 B：我想我們應該【退一步】看看大局，因為主要目標是吸引年輕顧客，而不是證明誰的點子最好。"},{"w":"slow down","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do things less quickly or work less hard","c":"放慢腳步；減速","s":"A: The doctor at the company health check said my blood pressure is too high, and I'm worried because I work twelve hours a day. B: Maybe it's time to slow down a little and let your assistant handle some of the smaller tasks, because your health is more important than any project deadline.","t":"A：公司健康檢查的醫生說我的血壓太高，我很擔心，因為我一天工作十二個小時。 B：或許是時候【放慢腳步】，讓你的助理處理一些比較小的工作了，因為你的健康比任何專案截止日都重要。"},{"w":"switch off","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop thinking about work and relax","c":"放空；不再想工作","s":"A: Even when you're at home in the evening, you keep checking your work messages, so don't you ever feel tired? B: You're right, and my wife says I need to switch off after dinner, so from now on I will leave my work phone in my bag and spend time with my children instead.","t":"A：即使晚上在家，你也一直在看工作訊息，你都不會覺得累嗎？ B：你說得對，我太太說我晚餐後需要【放空】，所以從現在起我會把工作手機放在包包裡，改成陪孩子。"},{"w":"take it easy","p":"v.phr.","d":"to rest and not work too hard","c":"放輕鬆；別太勞累","s":"A: I just got back from the hospital after my knee operation, but I'm thinking about returning to the office on Wednesday. B: Please take it easy for at least another week and work from home if you need to, because the doctor said walking too much could make your knee worse.","t":"A：我膝蓋開完刀剛出院，但我在考慮星期三就回辦公室。 B：請至少再【放輕鬆、別太勞累】一個禮拜，有需要的話就在家工作，因為醫生說走太多路會讓你的膝蓋更糟。"},{"w":"wind down","p":"v.phr.","d":"to slowly relax after a busy or stressful time","c":"（逐漸）放鬆下來","s":"A: What do you usually do in the evening after a stressful day of meetings with difficult customers? B: I like to wind down by taking a warm bath and listening to soft music, and I try not to look at any screens for an hour before I go to bed.","t":"A：和難搞的客戶開了一整天壓力很大的會之後，你晚上通常做什麼？ B：我喜歡泡個熱水澡、聽輕柔的音樂來【放鬆下來】，而且睡前一小時我會盡量不看任何螢幕。"},{"w":"retreat","p":"n.","d":"a quiet place or trip where people go to rest, think or plan","c":"休養處；靜修（會議）","s":"A: Where is the management team going for their two-day planning meeting next month, since the conference room here is being repainted? B: They booked a quiet mountain retreat about two hours from the city, where they can discuss next year's goals, go hiking together, and stay away from daily office problems.","t":"A：會議室在重新粉刷，管理團隊下個月兩天的規劃會議要去哪裡開？ B：他們預訂了距離市區大約兩小時、一處安靜的山中【休養所】，可以在那裡討論明年的目標、一起健行，並遠離日常辦公室的問題。"},{"w":"escape","p":"n.","d":"a way to get away from a stressful situation for a while","c":"逃離；解脫","s":"A: Why are so many office workers from the city booking rooms at that small beach hotel every weekend this summer? B: The hotel advertises itself as the perfect escape from busy city life, and its quiet rooms, fresh seafood, and beautiful sunsets make guests feel calm after a stressful week.","t":"A：為什麼今年夏天有那麼多城市上班族每週末都去訂那家小海濱飯店？ B：那家飯店宣傳自己是【逃離】忙碌都市生活的完美去處，安靜的房間、新鮮海鮮和美麗的夕陽，讓客人在壓力大的一週後感到平靜。"},{"w":"recreation","p":"n.","d":"activities people do for fun in their free time","c":"休閒娛樂；消遣","s":"A: The city government wants to turn the old factory near the river into something useful for local families, so what is the plan? B: They are going to build a park with tennis courts, bicycle paths, and a children's playground, so people will have more space for recreation on evenings and weekends.","t":"A：市政府想把河邊的舊工廠改造成對當地家庭有用的地方，計畫是什麼？ B：他們要蓋一座公園，有網球場、自行車道和兒童遊樂場，讓大家在晚上和週末有更多空間從事【休閒娛樂】。"},{"w":"refreshment","p":"n.","d":"light food and drinks","c":"茶點；點心飲料","s":"A: Our seminar for new clients will last from nine in the morning until four in the afternoon, so will the guests get anything to eat or drink? B: Yes, the hotel will set up a refreshment table with coffee, tea, cookies, and fresh fruit during each break, and a full lunch will be served in the restaurant at noon.","t":"A：我們的新客戶研討會從早上九點到下午四點，來賓會有東西吃喝嗎？ B：有，飯店會在每次休息時擺設一張放有咖啡、茶、餅乾和新鮮水果的【茶點】桌，中午也會在餐廳供應完整的午餐。"},{"w":"reset","p":"v.","d":"to start again in a fresh way; to set again","c":"重新設定；重整","s":"A: I came back from my week at the beach feeling great, but I'm worried that the stress will return as soon as I open my email. B: A good vacation can really help you reset your mind, so try to keep some of those calm habits, like taking a walk at lunch, now that you're back at work.","t":"A：我在海邊待了一週回來感覺很棒，但我擔心一打開電子郵件壓力就會回來。 B：一個好的假期真的能幫你【重新整理】心情，所以既然回來上班了，試著保留一些平靜的習慣，例如午餐時去散步。"},{"w":"disconnect","p":"v.","d":"to stop being connected to work, people or the internet","c":"斷開；中斷聯繫","s":"A: Are you going to bring your laptop on your camping trip next weekend in case the office needs to contact you? B: No, I want to completely disconnect from work and the internet for three days, so I told my team to call my manager if any serious problems happen while I'm away.","t":"A：你下週末去露營會帶筆電嗎？以防辦公室需要聯絡你。 B：不會，我想完全【斷開】工作和網路三天，所以我已經告訴團隊，如果我不在時發生任何嚴重問題就打給我的經理。"}]},{"unit":37,"theme":"Building 建築","cards":[{"w":"architect","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to design buildings","c":"建築師","s":"A: The new head office downtown looks amazing with all that glass and natural light, so who was in charge of the design? B: Our company hired a young architect from Taipei who won an award last year, and she spent months meeting staff to understand how we actually work before drawing anything.","t":"A：市中心的新總部有那麼多玻璃和自然光，看起來太棒了，是誰負責設計的？ B：我們公司聘請了一位來自台北、去年得過獎的年輕【建築師】，她在動手畫圖之前，花了好幾個月和員工見面，了解我們實際上如何工作。"},{"w":"planner","p":"n.","d":"a person who decides how land and buildings in a town should be used","c":"都市規劃師；規劃者","s":"A: Why hasn't the shopping mall project started yet, even though the builders were ready to begin work last month? B: The city planner asked us to change the parking area and add more trees along the road, so our team is still updating the drawings before we can get final approval.","t":"A：為什麼購物中心的工程還沒開始？建商上個月就已經準備好要動工了。 B：市政府的【都市規劃師】要求我們修改停車區，並在道路旁加種更多樹木，所以我們團隊還在更新設計圖，之後才能取得最後核准。"},{"w":"delay","p":"v.","d":"to make something happen later than planned","c":"延誤；延後","s":"A: Do you think the new factory will still open in March as the manager promised at the shareholders' meeting? B: Probably not, because the heavy rain this winter has flooded the site twice, and the builders say the bad weather will delay the opening by at least two months.","t":"A：你認為新工廠還會像經理在股東大會上承諾的那樣在三月開幕嗎？ B：大概不會，因為今年冬天的大雨已經淹了工地兩次，建商說惡劣的天氣會讓開幕【延後】至少兩個月。"},{"w":"detection","p":"n.","d":"the act of noticing or discovering something, often with a machine","c":"偵測；發現","s":"A: Why did the hotel spend so much money on new equipment for every guest room and hallway this year? B: After a small kitchen fire last spring, the owners decided to install a modern smoke detection system, so the staff can find any danger quickly and guide guests out safely.","t":"A：為什麼飯店今年在每間客房和走廊都花那麼多錢買新設備？ B：去年春天廚房發生小火災後，業主決定安裝現代化的煙霧【偵測】系統，讓員工能快速發現任何危險，並安全地引導房客離開。"},{"w":"faulty","p":"adj.","d":"not working correctly because something is wrong with it","c":"有缺陷的；故障的","s":"A: The lights on the third floor keep turning off during our afternoon meetings, and it's really annoying everyone in the department. B: The building manager checked it this morning and found some faulty wiring behind the ceiling, so an electrician is coming tomorrow to replace it before anyone gets hurt.","t":"A：三樓的燈在我們下午開會時一直熄掉，讓部門裡每個人都很困擾。 B：大樓管理員今天早上檢查過了，發現天花板後面有一些【有缺陷的】電線，所以明天會有電工來更換，以免有人受傷。"},{"w":"inspection","p":"n.","d":"a careful check of something to make sure it is safe or correct","c":"檢查；視察","s":"A: Are we allowed to move our office furniture into the new building on Monday, or do we need to wait longer? B: We have to wait until Thursday, because a safety officer from the city government is coming for a final inspection of the fire exits, elevators and electrical systems on Wednesday afternoon.","t":"A：我們星期一可以把辦公家具搬進新大樓嗎？還是要再等久一點？ B：我們要等到星期四，因為市政府的安全人員星期三下午會來對逃生出口、電梯和電力系統做最後的【檢查】。"},{"w":"hype","p":"v.","d":"to advertise something a lot so that it seems better than it really is","c":"大肆宣傳；炒作","s":"A: Everyone in the marketing team seems excited about the new apartment tower by the river, but is it really that special? B: Not really, because the developer paid a lot of famous bloggers to hype it online, but when I visited last weekend, the rooms were small and the views were ordinary.","t":"A：行銷部的每個人好像都對河邊那棟新公寓大樓很興奮，它真的那麼特別嗎？ B：其實沒有，建商花錢請了很多知名部落客在網路上【大肆宣傳】，但我上週末去參觀時，房間很小，景觀也很普通。"},{"w":"amenity","p":"n.","d":"something in a building or area that makes life more comfortable or useful","c":"便利設施","s":"A: The rent at the new business center is higher than our current office, so why are you recommending that we move there? B: The price includes a gym, free parking and a rooftop café, and I think the most useful amenity for our team is the twenty-four-hour meeting room that clients can book online.","t":"A：新商務中心的租金比我們目前的辦公室高，你為什麼還建議我們搬過去？ B：價格包含健身房、免費停車和頂樓咖啡廳，而我認為對我們團隊最有用的【設施】是客戶可以上網預約的二十四小時會議室。"},{"w":"wander","p":"v.","d":"to walk slowly around a place without a clear purpose","c":"閒逛；漫步","s":"A: What did you do while you were waiting for the property agent at the old train station building yesterday afternoon? B: She was forty minutes late because of traffic, so I decided to wander around the empty halls and take photos of the beautiful windows and wooden ceilings for our report.","t":"A：昨天下午你在舊火車站大樓等房仲的時候做了什麼？ B：她因為塞車晚了四十分鐘，所以我決定在空蕩蕩的大廳裡隨意【閒逛】，並替我們的報告拍下美麗的窗戶和木頭天花板。"},{"w":"run-down","p":"adj.","d":"in very poor condition because nobody has taken care of it","c":"破舊的；失修的","s":"A: Why did the company choose such an old warehouse near the harbor for its new design studio? B: The building was very run-down when we bought it, with broken windows and peeling paint, but the price was low, and we had enough money left to repair everything and make it bright and modern.","t":"A：公司為什麼為新的設計工作室選了港口附近那麼舊的倉庫？ B：我們買下時那棟建築非常【破舊】，窗戶破了、油漆剝落，但價格很低，我們剩下的錢足夠把一切修好，讓它變得明亮又現代。"},{"w":"donkey's years","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very long time (informal)","c":"很長一段時間；好多年","s":"A: Do you know when the convention center across the street was last repainted, because the outside looks really dirty now? B: Nobody in our office remembers exactly, but my manager says it hasn't been painted for donkey's years, probably since before she joined the company over twenty years ago.","t":"A：你知道對街的會議中心上次重新粉刷是什麼時候嗎？外觀現在看起來真的很髒。 B：我們辦公室沒人記得確切時間，但我的經理說它已經【好多年】沒粉刷了，可能是在她二十多年前進公司之前。"},{"w":"laughing stock","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person or thing that everyone laughs at","c":"笑柄","s":"A: Why is the mayor so worried about the design of the new city library that was shown in the newspaper today? B: Many people online say it looks like a giant shoebox, and he's afraid the town will become a laughing stock if the builders finish it without making any changes to the plan.","t":"A：為什麼市長對今天報上刊登的新市立圖書館設計那麼擔心？ B：網路上很多人說它看起來像一個巨大的鞋盒，他擔心如果建商不修改計畫就完工，整個城鎮會成為大家的【笑柄】。"},{"w":"run-of-the-mill","p":"adj.","d":"ordinary and not special in any way","c":"普通的；平凡的","s":"A: The client said our first design for their new hotel lobby was nice, so why do they want us to start again? B: They felt it was too run-of-the-mill and looked like every other hotel in the city, so they're asking for something more creative that guests will remember and share on social media.","t":"A：客戶說我們為他們新飯店大廳做的第一版設計還不錯，為什麼還要我們重新開始？ B：他們覺得太【普通】了，看起來就跟城裡其他飯店一樣，所以他們想要更有創意、讓房客會記住並分享到社群媒體的設計。"},{"w":"pass the time","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do something so that a period of waiting does not feel long","c":"打發時間","s":"A: How did the visitors keep busy while the elevator in the tower was being repaired for nearly two hours yesterday? B: Our receptionist offered them coffee in the lobby, and many of them chose to pass the time by reading magazines, chatting with each other or looking at the photos of the building's history on the walls.","t":"A：昨天大樓電梯維修了將近兩個小時，訪客們是怎麼打發時間的？ B：我們的接待員在大廳請他們喝咖啡，許多人選擇看雜誌、彼此聊天或欣賞牆上大樓歷史照片來【打發時間】。"},{"w":"stack up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to compare with something else in quality or value","c":"比得上；與……相比","s":"A: Our team must choose between two office buildings by Friday, so how does the new one near the station compare? B: When you look at the rent, the parking and the distance to the metro, it doesn't really stack up well against the older building on Main Street, which is cheaper and has much bigger rooms.","t":"A：我們團隊必須在星期五前從兩棟辦公大樓中選一棟，車站附近那棟新的比起來怎麼樣？ B：從租金、停車和到捷運的距離來看，它跟主街上那棟較舊的大樓相比並不怎麼【比得上】，那棟比較便宜，房間也大得多。"},{"w":"density","p":"n.","d":"how many people or things there are in a certain area","c":"密度","s":"A: Why does the government want to build so many tall apartment towers near the new metro line this year? B: The area already has a high population density, and officials think more homes close to the trains will help reduce traffic, since thousands of people can walk to the station instead of driving.","t":"A：為什麼政府今年要在新捷運線附近蓋那麼多高樓公寓？ B：這個區域的人口【密度】已經很高，官員認為在車站附近多蓋住宅可以幫助減少交通量，因為成千上萬的人可以走路去車站而不用開車。"},{"w":"skyrocket","p":"v.","d":"to rise very quickly and suddenly","c":"飆漲；急速上升","s":"A: Why are so many young families moving out of the city center and into the suburbs this year? B: Since the new high-speed rail station opened downtown, house prices have started to skyrocket, and most couples who work nearby can no longer afford even a small apartment close to their offices.","t":"A：為什麼今年有那麼多年輕家庭搬離市中心、搬到郊區？ B：自從市中心的新高鐵站啟用後，房價開始【飆漲】，大多數在附近上班的夫妻甚至買不起離辦公室近的小公寓了。"},{"w":"torn","p":"adj.","d":"unable to decide between two choices","c":"左右為難的；猶豫不決的","s":"A: Have the managers decided whether to repair the old headquarters or build a completely new one outside the city? B: Not yet, because they're torn between saving the historic building that the founder loved and moving to a modern space that would be much cheaper to heat, cool and maintain.","t":"A：經理們決定好要修繕舊總部，還是在城外蓋全新的總部了嗎？ B：還沒，因為他們在保留創辦人喜愛的歷史建築和搬到冷暖氣與維護都便宜許多的現代空間之間【左右為難】。"},{"w":"monstrosity","p":"n.","d":"a large building or object that is very ugly","c":"龐大醜陋的建築；怪物","s":"A: What do local residents think about the huge parking garage the company built next to the old temple last year? B: Most of them hate it and call it a concrete monstrosity, because it blocks the view of the mountains and looks completely out of place among the small traditional shops.","t":"A：當地居民對公司去年在老廟旁蓋的那座巨大停車場有什麼看法？ B：大多數人很討厭它，稱它為水泥【怪物】，因為它擋住了山景，而且和周圍的小型傳統商店完全格格不入。"},{"w":"justification","p":"n.","d":"a good reason for doing something","c":"正當理由","s":"A: The board wants to spend millions on a new glass entrance for the head office, but do we really need it? B: I asked the same question at the meeting, and nobody could give a clear justification for the cost, especially when our factory roofs are leaking and need urgent repairs before the rainy season.","t":"A：董事會想花幾百萬元替總部建一個新的玻璃入口，但我們真的需要嗎？ B：我在會議上問了同樣的問題，沒有人能為這筆花費給出明確的【理由】，尤其是我們工廠的屋頂在漏水，需要在雨季前緊急修理。"},{"w":"renovate","p":"v.","d":"to repair and improve an old building or room","c":"翻修；整修","s":"A: Why is the restaurant on the ground floor of our building closed for the whole summer this year? B: The owner plans to renovate the kitchen and dining area, adding new lights, larger windows and an outdoor terrace, so they can serve more customers when they reopen in September.","t":"A：為什麼我們大樓一樓的餐廳今年整個夏天都關門？ B：老闆打算【翻修】廚房和用餐區，加裝新燈具、更大的窗戶和戶外露台，好讓九月重新開幕時能服務更多客人。"},{"w":"castle","p":"n.","d":"a large strong building with thick walls, built long ago to protect people","c":"城堡","s":"A: Where are we holding the company's anniversary dinner next month, since the usual hotel ballroom is fully booked? B: The event team found a beautiful stone castle on a hill outside the city that was built three hundred years ago, and it now rents out its great hall for weddings and business events.","t":"A：既然平常用的飯店宴會廳都訂滿了，下個月的公司週年晚宴要在哪裡舉辦？ B：活動團隊在城外的山丘上找到一座三百年前建造的美麗石造【城堡】，它現在把大廳出租給婚禮和商務活動使用。"},{"w":"ruin","p":"v.","d":"to damage or spoil something completely","c":"破壞；毀掉","s":"A: Why are the people who live near the beach so angry about the new hotel the developer wants to build there? B: They believe a twenty-floor tower would ruin the natural beauty of the coastline, and they worry that tourists will stop coming if the quiet little fishing village disappears.","t":"A：為什麼住在海灘附近的人對開發商想在那裡蓋新飯店那麼生氣？ B：他們認為一棟二十層樓的大樓會【破壞】海岸線的自然美景，而且擔心如果寧靜的小漁村消失，遊客就不會再來了。"},{"w":"quaint","p":"adj.","d":"attractive in an unusual or old-fashioned way","c":"古色古香的；別緻的","s":"A: Where did you stay during the business trip to the countryside last week, since there are no big hotels there? B: The client booked us into a quaint little guesthouse with old wooden doors, flower boxes on every window and a garden, and the owner cooked us a delicious breakfast every morning.","t":"A：上週你去鄉下出差時住在哪裡？那裡沒有大飯店。 B：客戶幫我們訂了一間【古色古香】的小民宿，有老木門、每扇窗都有花箱，還有一座花園，老闆每天早上都替我們煮美味的早餐。"},{"w":"attraction","p":"n.","d":"a place or thing that people visit for interest or fun","c":"景點；吸引人的事物","s":"A: Why does the city want to spend so much money restoring the old sugar factory by the river? B: The tourism office hopes it will become a major attraction for visitors, with shops, a museum and restaurants inside, which would bring more jobs and money to the local businesses nearby.","t":"A：為什麼市政府要花那麼多錢修復河邊的舊糖廠？ B：觀光局希望它能成為吸引遊客的主要【景點】，裡面有商店、博物館和餐廳，能為附近的在地商家帶來更多工作機會和收入。"},{"w":"hassle","p":"n.","d":"something annoying that causes trouble or takes a lot of effort","c":"麻煩事","s":"A: Why did your team decide to rent a furnished office instead of buying your own desks, chairs and cabinets? B: Buying, delivering and setting up all that furniture would be a real hassle for a small company like ours, and we'd rather spend our time and energy finding new clients and growing the business.","t":"A：為什麼你們團隊決定租附家具的辦公室，而不是自己買桌椅和櫃子？ B：對我們這樣的小公司來說，購買、運送和組裝所有家具真的很【麻煩】，我們寧願把時間和精力花在開發新客戶和拓展業務上。"},{"w":"irrelevant","p":"adj.","d":"not connected with or important to the subject","c":"無關的；無關緊要的","s":"A: The buyer keeps asking about the color of the curtains in the empty office, but shouldn't we focus on more important things? B: Yes, those details are completely irrelevant right now, because we still need to agree on the price, the length of the lease and who will pay for the roof repairs.","t":"A：買方一直問空辦公室窗簾的顏色，但我們不是應該專注在更重要的事情上嗎？ B：對，那些細節現在完全【無關緊要】，因為我們還需要談妥價格、租約期限，以及誰要支付屋頂維修費用。"},{"w":"aesthetically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is connected with beauty and how something looks","c":"在美學上；外觀上","s":"A: The new art museum downtown cost a lot of money, so are people happy with the final result? B: Most visitors say it is aesthetically pleasing, with its curved white walls and huge windows, but some staff complain that the building is hard to clean and difficult to heat in winter.","t":"A：市中心的新美術館花了很多錢，大家對最後的成果滿意嗎？ B：大多數參觀者說它在【美學上】令人賞心悅目，有彎曲的白牆和巨大的窗戶，但有些員工抱怨這棟建築很難清潔，冬天也很難保暖。"},{"w":"outskirts","p":"n.","d":"the outer areas of a city or town","c":"郊區；市郊","s":"A: Why is the furniture company building its new warehouse so far away from the city center? B: Land on the outskirts of the city is much cheaper, and the location is close to the highway, so trucks can deliver products quickly without getting stuck in downtown traffic every morning.","t":"A：家具公司為什麼要把新倉庫蓋在離市中心那麼遠的地方？ B：城市【郊區】的土地便宜得多，而且位置靠近高速公路，所以卡車可以快速送貨，不會每天早上卡在市中心的車陣裡。"},{"w":"handful","p":"n.","d":"a small number of people or things","c":"少數；一把","s":"A: How many people actually came to see the model apartments at the open house last Saturday? B: Only a handful of visitors showed up in the morning because of the typhoon warning, but more families arrived after lunch when the rain stopped, and we sold three units by evening.","t":"A：上週六的開放參觀日到底有多少人來看樣品屋？ B：因為颱風警報，早上只有【少數幾位】訪客到場，但雨停後、午餐過後來了更多家庭，到晚上我們賣出了三戶。"},{"w":"façade","p":"n.","d":"the front wall of a building","c":"建築物正面；外牆","s":"A: The old bank building on the corner looks completely different now, so what exactly did the new owners change? B: They kept the inside almost the same, but they cleaned and repaired the stone façade facing the street, so the front of the building looks bright and elegant again.","t":"A：轉角那棟舊銀行大樓現在看起來完全不一樣，新屋主到底改了什麼？ B：他們內部幾乎沒變，但清洗並修復了面向街道的石造【外牆】，所以建築正面看起來再度明亮又優雅。"},{"w":"blight","p":"n.","d":"something ugly or harmful that spoils a place","c":"損害景觀的事物；禍害","s":"A: Why does the city council want to tear down those empty factories near the train station? B: Residents say the buildings have become a blight on the neighborhood, because they're covered in graffiti, attract rats and make visitors think the whole area is unsafe at night.","t":"A：為什麼市議會想拆掉火車站附近那些空置的工廠？ B：居民說這些建築已成為社區的【禍害】，因為上面滿是塗鴉、會招來老鼠，還讓訪客覺得整個地區晚上不安全。"},{"w":"landscape","p":"n.","d":"everything you can see when you look across a large area of land","c":"景觀；風景","s":"A: Why did the designers plan the new hotel with only three floors when the land is big enough for a tower? B: The owners wanted the building to fit naturally into the green hills and rice fields, so they kept it low to protect the beautiful landscape that guests come here to enjoy.","t":"A：既然土地大到可以蓋高樓，為什麼設計師把新飯店只規劃成三層樓？ B：業主希望建築能自然地融入綠色山丘和稻田中，所以把樓層壓低，以保護房客來這裡欣賞的美麗【景觀】。"},{"w":"inclination","p":"n.","d":"a feeling that you want to do something","c":"意願；傾向","s":"A: Are you going to apply for the facilities manager position at our new headquarters next year? B: To be honest, I have no inclination to deal with builders and repair problems every day, so I'd rather stay in the finance department, where I can focus on numbers, budgets and long-term planning.","t":"A：你明年會申請我們新總部的設施經理職位嗎？ B：老實說，我沒有每天處理建商和維修問題的【意願】，所以我寧願待在財務部，專心處理數字、預算和長期規劃。"},{"w":"erect","p":"v.","d":"to build or put up a structure","c":"建造；豎立；搭建","s":"A: How long will it take to get the temporary stage ready for the outdoor product launch next weekend? B: The event company says their workers can erect the main structure in just one day, but they'll need another afternoon to set up the lights, speakers and the large video screen.","t":"A：下週末戶外產品發表會的臨時舞台要多久才能準備好？ B：活動公司說他們的工人只要一天就能【搭建】主結構，但還需要再一個下午來架設燈光、喇叭和大型螢幕。"}]},{"unit":38,"theme":"Business 商業","cards":[{"w":"company","p":"n.","d":"a business that makes or sells goods or services","c":"公司","s":"A: I heard you're leaving the bank after eight years, so where are you going to work from next month? B: I'm joining a small software company in Neihu that builds booking apps for hotels, and although the salary is a little lower, the team is friendly and I can work from home on Fridays.","t":"A：聽說你在銀行工作八年後要離職了，下個月你要去哪裡上班？ B：我要加入內湖一家小型軟體【公司】，他們為飯店開發訂房應用程式，雖然薪水低一點，但團隊很友善，而且我週五可以在家工作。"},{"w":"enterprise","p":"n.","d":"a business or company, often one that someone starts and runs","c":"企業；事業","s":"A: Our bank is launching a new loan program next quarter, so which business owners are we hoping to reach with it? B: We want to help people who run a small family enterprise, such as a local bakery or a repair shop, because those owners often struggle to borrow money from large lenders when they need new equipment.","t":"A：我們銀行下一季要推出新的貸款方案，我們希望接觸到哪些業主？ B：我們想幫助經營小型家族【企業】的人，例如當地的麵包店或修理店，因為這些老闆需要新設備時，常常很難向大型貸方借到錢。"},{"w":"firm","p":"n.","d":"a business, especially one that gives professional services like law or accounting","c":"公司；事務所","s":"A: The new office lease looks quite complicated, and I don't understand several of the clauses, so who should we ask to check it before we sign? B: Let's contact the law firm that helped us last year, because their lawyers are careful, they reply quickly, and they already know our business well.","t":"A：新辦公室的租約看起來相當複雜，有好幾條條款我看不懂，簽約前我們應該請誰檢查？ B：我們聯絡去年幫過我們的那家律師【事務所】吧，因為他們的律師很細心、回覆很快，而且已經很了解我們的業務。"},{"w":"corporation","p":"n.","d":"a large company or group of companies that acts as one legal unit","c":"大公司；股份有限公司","s":"A: Why are there so many security guards and reporters in the lobby downstairs this morning? B: A huge international corporation from Japan is signing an agreement with our CEO today, and because the deal is worth millions of dollars, everyone wants photos of the meeting before the official press conference at noon.","t":"A：今天早上樓下大廳為什麼有那麼多警衛和記者？ B：一家來自日本的大型跨國【公司】今天要和我們的執行長簽協議，因為這筆交易價值數百萬美元，大家都想在中午正式記者會前拍到會議的照片。"},{"w":"startup","p":"n.","d":"a new, small company, often in technology, that is just beginning","c":"新創公司","s":"A: You used to work at a big bank downtown, so why did you decide to quit such a stable job last spring? B: Two friends and I opened a small startup that makes a phone app for booking dog walkers, and although we work long hours, it is exciting to build something new from nothing.","t":"A：你以前在市中心的大銀行上班，為什麼去年春天決定辭掉這麼穩定的工作？ B：我和兩個朋友開了一家小型【新創公司】，開發預約遛狗員的手機應用程式，雖然我們工作時間很長，但從無到有打造新東西很令人興奮。"},{"w":"industry","p":"n.","d":"all the businesses that make or sell a particular kind of product or service","c":"產業；工業","s":"A: You have worked in hotels for over ten years, so how has your job changed since the pandemic ended? B: The whole tourism industry has changed a lot, because travelers now book everything online at the last minute, so hotels must use new software and train staff to answer guests quickly through chat apps.","t":"A：你在飯店工作超過十年了，疫情結束後你的工作有什麼改變？ B：整個觀光【產業】改變很多，因為旅客現在都在最後一刻上網預訂一切，所以飯店必須使用新軟體，並訓練員工透過聊天應用程式迅速回覆客人。"},{"w":"commerce","p":"n.","d":"the activity of buying and selling goods, especially on a large scale","c":"商業；貿易","s":"A: Why is our team spending so much time improving the website instead of opening another shop at the mall? B: Online commerce is growing much faster than store shopping, because busy people prefer ordering from their phones at night, so the director believes a better website will bring us more buyers than a new shop.","t":"A：為什麼我們團隊花這麼多時間改善網站，而不是在購物中心再開一家店？ B：線上【商務】的成長比實體店購物快得多，因為忙碌的人喜歡晚上用手機下單，所以主管認為更好的網站會比新店帶來更多買家。"},{"w":"market","p":"n.","d":"an area or group of people where a product can be sold","c":"市場","s":"A: Our new energy drink sold very well in Taiwan this year, so what is the next step for the product? B: The board wants to enter the Japanese market next spring, so we are hiring a local research team to learn what young people there like to drink and how much they usually pay.","t":"A：我們的新能量飲料今年在台灣賣得很好，這項產品下一步是什麼？ B：董事會希望明年春天打入日本【市場】，所以我們正在聘請當地的研究團隊，了解那裡的年輕人喜歡喝什麼，以及他們通常願意付多少錢。"},{"w":"profit","p":"n.","d":"money you earn from business after paying all costs","c":"利潤；盈利","s":"A: The café on the corner always seems full, so is the owner making good money from it? B: Not really, because rent in this area is very high and coffee beans have become more expensive, so after paying staff and bills, she only made a small profit last year and is thinking about moving.","t":"A：轉角那家咖啡店好像總是客滿，老闆賺很多錢嗎？ B：其實沒有，因為這一區的租金很高，咖啡豆也變貴了，所以付完員工薪水和帳單後，她去年只賺到一點【利潤】，正在考慮搬家。"},{"w":"revenue","p":"n.","d":"the total money a business receives from selling goods or services","c":"營收；收入","s":"A: The finance team looked very happy at the meeting this morning, so did the quarterly report bring good news? B: Yes, our total revenue rose by fifteen percent compared to last year, mostly because the new online store attracted many overseas buyers, so the managers are planning to give everyone a bonus.","t":"A：財務團隊今天早上開會時看起來很開心，季報帶來好消息了嗎？ B：是的，我們的總【營收】比去年成長了百分之十五，主要是因為新的網路商店吸引了許多海外買家，所以經理們打算發獎金給大家。"},{"w":"investment","p":"n.","d":"money or time you put into something to get a benefit later","c":"投資","s":"A: Our old printers break down almost every week, so should we just keep repairing them to save money? B: I think buying new machines would be a smart investment, because although they are expensive at first, they will save us repair fees and many hours of waiting, which helps the whole office work faster.","t":"A：我們的舊印表機幾乎每週都故障，我們是不是應該繼續修理來省錢？ B：我認為買新機器會是明智的【投資】，因為雖然一開始很貴，但能省下維修費和許多等待的時間，讓整個辦公室工作更快。"},{"w":"capital","p":"n.","d":"money used to start or grow a business","c":"資本；資金","s":"A: You have wanted to open your own bakery for years, so what is stopping you from doing it now? B: I still don't have enough capital to rent a shop and buy ovens, so I am saving part of my salary every month and also talking to the bank about a small loan.","t":"A：你想開自己的麵包店已經很多年了，現在是什麼阻止你去做？ B：我還沒有足夠的【資金】租店面和買烤箱，所以我每個月存一部分薪水，也正在和銀行洽談一筆小額貸款。"},{"w":"expense","p":"n.","d":"money spent on something, especially for work","c":"費用；開支","s":"A: The hotel in Osaka was quite expensive, so will the company pay for my room during the trade fair? B: Yes, the hotel is a business expense, so just keep every receipt, fill in the online form when you return, and the accounting department will pay the money back into your account within two weeks.","t":"A：大阪那家飯店相當貴，商展期間公司會幫我付房費嗎？ B：會的，住宿屬於出差【費用】，所以只要保留每張收據，回來後填寫線上表單，會計部門會在兩週內把錢退到你的帳戶。"},{"w":"cost","p":"n.","d":"the amount of money needed to buy, make, or do something","c":"成本；費用","s":"A: Why did management decide to move the factory from the city to a small town in the south? B: The main reason is that the cost of land and labor there is much lower, so the company can save money every year and still deliver products to its customers on time.","t":"A：管理階層為什麼決定把工廠從城市搬到南部的小鎮？ B：主要原因是那裡的土地和勞工【成本】低很多，所以公司每年都能省錢，還能準時把產品交給顧客。"},{"w":"budget","p":"n.","d":"a plan of how much money can be spent on something","c":"預算","s":"A: The marketing team wants to hire a famous singer for our new advertisement, so can we afford it? B: I'm afraid not, because our budget for this campaign is only two million dollars, and that singer usually asks for more than that, so we should look for a less expensive option.","t":"A：行銷團隊想請一位知名歌手拍我們的新廣告，我們負擔得起嗎？ B：恐怕不行，因為這次活動的【預算】只有兩百萬元，而那位歌手通常要價更高，所以我們應該找比較便宜的選擇。"},{"w":"management","p":"n.","d":"the people who control a company, or the work of controlling it","c":"管理；管理階層","s":"A: The staff seem much happier this year, so what changed in the office after the new director arrived? B: The management started listening to employees' ideas at monthly meetings and allowed flexible working hours, so people feel more respected, and fewer workers have quit compared to last year.","t":"A：員工今年似乎開心多了，新主管上任後辦公室有什麼改變？ B：【管理階層】開始在每月會議上聽取員工的想法，並允許彈性工時，所以大家覺得更受尊重，離職的員工也比去年少。"},{"w":"strategy","p":"n.","d":"a careful plan to reach a goal","c":"策略；戰略","s":"A: Sales of our phones dropped again this quarter, so what is the director planning to do about it? B: She is working on a new strategy that focuses on students, because they buy new phones often, and she wants to offer cheaper models with good cameras and special discounts during the school holidays.","t":"A：我們手機的銷量這一季又下滑了，主管打算怎麼處理？ B：她正在擬定一個以學生為主的新【策略】，因為學生常常換新手機，她想推出相機不錯的平價機型，並在學校假期提供特別折扣。"},{"w":"operation","p":"n.","d":"the work or activity of a business, or a part of it","c":"營運；業務","s":"A: Why are so many engineers flying to Vietnam next month instead of staying at the main office here? B: Our company is moving part of its manufacturing operation to Hanoi, so the engineers need to set up the machines, train the local workers, and make sure everything runs smoothly before production begins.","t":"A：為什麼下個月有這麼多工程師要飛去越南，而不是留在這裡的總部？ B：我們公司要把部分製造【業務】移到河內，所以工程師需要安裝機器、訓練當地員工，並確保生產開始前一切運作順利。"},{"w":"productivity","p":"n.","d":"how much work a person or company produces in a certain time","c":"生產力","s":"A: Since we started working from home two days a week, have you noticed any change in how much the team gets done? B: Actually, our productivity has gone up, because people spend less time on crowded trains and fewer meetings interrupt them, so they finish reports faster and make fewer mistakes.","t":"A：自從我們開始每週在家工作兩天，你有注意到團隊完成的工作量有什麼變化嗎？ B：其實我們的【生產力】提升了，因為大家花在擁擠火車上的時間變少，被會議打斷的次數也減少，所以他們更快完成報告，錯誤也更少。"},{"w":"efficiency","p":"n.","d":"the ability to do something well without wasting time, money, or energy","c":"效率","s":"A: The new delivery software looks complicated, so why did the manager insist that every driver must use it? B: It plans the shortest routes and shows traffic jams in real time, which improves the efficiency of our deliveries, so drivers use less fuel and customers get their packages much sooner.","t":"A：新的配送軟體看起來很複雜，經理為什麼堅持每位司機都要用？ B：它會規劃最短路線並即時顯示塞車狀況，提升我們配送的【效率】，所以司機用油更少，顧客也能更快收到包裹。"},{"w":"competition","p":"n.","d":"the situation when businesses try to be more successful than others","c":"競爭","s":"A: Why did our coffee chain suddenly lower prices and start offering free cookies this month? B: Two new cafés opened on the same street last week, so the competition is much stronger now, and we need to give people a good reason to keep coming to us instead of trying the new places.","t":"A：為什麼我們的連鎖咖啡店這個月突然降價，還開始送免費餅乾？ B：上週同一條街開了兩家新咖啡店，所以現在【競爭】激烈得多，我們需要給大家一個好理由，讓他們繼續光顧我們，而不是去試新的店。"},{"w":"client","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that pays for a professional service","c":"客戶；委託人","s":"A: You look nervous, and you've checked your slides three times, so what is happening this afternoon? B: I'm meeting an important client from a large hotel group who wants to redesign all their websites, and if she likes my presentation, our agency could win a contract worth over a million dollars.","t":"A：你看起來很緊張，投影片已經檢查三次了，今天下午有什麼事？ B：我要和一家大型飯店集團的重要【客戶】見面，她想重新設計他們所有的網站，如果她喜歡我的簡報，我們公司可能會拿到價值超過一百萬元的合約。"},{"w":"customer","p":"n.","d":"a person who buys goods or services from a shop or business","c":"顧客","s":"A: Why is the store manager standing at the counter and talking to that woman for so long? B: A customer bought a coffee machine here last week, but it stopped working after two days, so he is apologizing, checking her receipt, and offering her a new one or a full refund.","t":"A：為什麼店經理站在櫃檯跟那位女士談了那麼久？ B：一位【顧客】上週在這裡買了咖啡機，但兩天後就壞了，所以他正在道歉、核對她的收據，並提供她換一台新的或全額退款。"},{"w":"supplier","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that provides goods to other businesses","c":"供應商","s":"A: Our restaurant ran out of fresh vegetables twice last week, so what went wrong with the deliveries? B: Our usual supplier had problems with his trucks because of the typhoon, so I have already contacted another farm near Taoyuan that can deliver every morning before we open.","t":"A：我們餐廳上週兩次沒有新鮮蔬菜可用，送貨出了什麼問題？ B：我們平常的【供應商】因為颱風，貨車出了問題，所以我已經聯絡桃園附近另一家農場，他們每天早上開店前可以送貨。"},{"w":"contract","p":"n.","d":"a written legal agreement between two or more people or companies","c":"合約；契約","s":"A: The design agency agreed to all our requests on the phone yesterday, so can we start the project on Monday? B: Not yet, because both sides still need to sign the contract, and our lawyer wants to check the payment terms and deadlines carefully before anyone puts their name on it.","t":"A：設計公司昨天在電話中同意了我們所有的要求，我們星期一可以開始這個專案嗎？ B：還不行，因為雙方還需要簽【合約】，而我們的律師想在任何人簽名之前仔細檢查付款條件和截止日期。"},{"w":"negotiation","p":"n.","d":"formal discussion between people who are trying to reach an agreement","c":"協商；談判","s":"A: The supplier asked for a ten percent price increase, so did we finally accept their new offer? B: Not completely, because after three hours of negotiation yesterday, they agreed to raise prices by only five percent if we promise to keep buying from them for two more years.","t":"A：供應商要求漲價百分之十，我們最後接受他們的新報價了嗎？ B：沒有完全接受，因為昨天經過三個小時的【協商】，他們同意只要我們承諾再向他們採購兩年，就只漲價百分之五。"},{"w":"marketing","p":"n.","d":"the work of advertising and promoting products so people buy them","c":"行銷","s":"A: We have a great new product, but hardly anyone has heard of it, so what should we do next? B: We need to spend more on marketing, such as short videos on social media and free samples at train stations, because people will not buy something if they don't even know it exists.","t":"A：我們有很棒的新產品，但幾乎沒人聽過，接下來該怎麼做？ B：我們需要在【行銷】上投入更多，例如社群媒體上的短影片和在火車站發送免費試用品，因為如果大家連它存在都不知道，就不會買。"},{"w":"brand","p":"n.","d":"a name of a product or company that people know","c":"品牌","s":"A: These two pairs of running shoes look almost the same, so why does one cost twice as much as the other? B: The expensive pair is from a famous sports brand that many athletes wear, so people are happy to pay more for the name and the feeling that the quality is better.","t":"A：這兩雙跑鞋看起來幾乎一樣，為什麼其中一雙貴了一倍？ B：比較貴的那雙來自一個許多運動員都穿的知名運動【品牌】，所以大家很樂意為了這個名字，以及品質更好的感覺多付錢。"},{"w":"sales","p":"n.","d":"the number of products sold, or the money received from selling them","c":"銷售額；銷售","s":"A: You stayed at the office very late every night last December, so why was that month so busy for you? B: Our sales always increase sharply before Christmas, because many families buy our toys as gifts, so the whole team had to pack and ship hundreds of extra orders every day.","t":"A：你去年十二月每天晚上都在辦公室待到很晚，為什麼那個月那麼忙？ B：我們的【銷售額】在聖誕節前總是大幅增加，因為許多家庭會買我們的玩具當禮物，所以整個團隊每天都要多包裝和寄送數百筆訂單。"},{"w":"growth","p":"n.","d":"an increase in size, amount, or success","c":"成長；增長","s":"A: Your small online shop only had two workers three years ago, so how many people work there now? B: We have thirty employees today, because the fast growth of our business came from selling healthy snacks during the pandemic, and many of those customers still order from us every month.","t":"A：你的小網店三年前只有兩名員工，現在有多少人在那裡工作？ B：我們現在有三十名員工，我們生意的快速【成長】來自疫情期間販售健康零食，而且許多顧客至今每個月仍向我們訂購。"},{"w":"expansion","p":"n.","d":"the act of becoming larger, such as opening new branches","c":"擴張；擴展","s":"A: Why is the company hiring so many new staff and looking at office buildings in Kaohsiung? B: The board approved an expansion into southern Taiwan, so we are opening a second office there next year, and they need people who know the local customers and can speak Taiwanese with them.","t":"A：公司為什麼要招聘這麼多新員工，還在高雄看辦公大樓？ B：董事會批准了向南台灣【擴展】的計畫，所以我們明年要在那裡開設第二個辦公室，他們需要了解當地顧客、能用台語和他們溝通的人。"},{"w":"risk","p":"n.","d":"the chance that something bad, like losing money, may happen","c":"風險","s":"A: My brother wants to put all his savings into his friend's new restaurant, so do you think that's a good idea? B: It's a big risk, because many new restaurants close within the first year, so he should only invest money he can afford to lose and ask to see a clear business plan first.","t":"A：我哥哥想把所有積蓄投入他朋友的新餐廳，你覺得這是好主意嗎？ B：這是很大的【風險】，因為許多新餐廳在第一年內就倒閉，所以他應該只投資輸得起的錢，並先要求看清楚的營運計畫。"},{"w":"sustainability","p":"n.","d":"using resources in a way that does not harm the environment in the future","c":"永續性；永續發展","s":"A: Why did our company stop using plastic bags and start buying electricity from solar farms this year? B: The new CEO cares a lot about sustainability, and many young customers now choose brands that protect the environment, so going green helps the planet and also improves our image.","t":"A：為什麼我們公司今年停止使用塑膠袋，並開始向太陽能電廠購電？ B：新任執行長非常重視【永續發展】，而且許多年輕顧客現在會選擇保護環境的品牌，所以走向環保既能幫助地球，也能提升我們的形象。"}]},{"unit":39,"theme":"Busy 忙碌","cards":[{"w":"occupied","p":"adj.","d":"busy doing something, or being used by someone","c":"忙碌的；（座位、房間）有人使用的","s":"A: I wanted to ask the director about the new budget plan this morning, but is she available to talk for a few minutes before lunch? B: I'm afraid she will be occupied with job interviews until two o'clock, so you should send her an email now and she can reply after the last candidate leaves.","t":"A：我今天早上想問主任有關新預算計畫的事，她午餐前有空談幾分鐘嗎？ B：恐怕她到兩點前都會【忙著】面試應徵者，所以你現在應該寄電子郵件給她，等最後一位應徵者離開後她就可以回覆你。"},{"w":"overworked","p":"adj.","d":"having too much work to do","c":"工作過度的；過勞的","s":"A: Why did three people from the customer service team quit last month, even though the company had just raised everyone's salary in January? B: Most of them felt overworked because they had to answer hundreds of calls every day without enough breaks, and the manager never hired anyone new to help them.","t":"A：為什麼客服團隊上個月有三個人離職，即使公司一月才剛幫大家加薪？ B：他們大多覺得【工作過度】，因為每天必須接數百通電話又沒有足夠的休息時間，而經理也從沒僱用新人來幫忙。"},{"w":"swamped","p":"adj.","d":"having so much work that you can hardly deal with it","c":"忙得不可開交的；應接不暇的","s":"A: Could you help me check these sales figures before the meeting with our partners from Tokyo tomorrow morning? B: I'd love to, but I'm completely swamped with customer orders since the holiday promotion started, so maybe you could ask Kevin in the finance department, who usually has more free time on Thursdays.","t":"A：你可以幫我在明天早上和東京合作夥伴開會前檢查這些銷售數字嗎？ B：我很樂意，但自從假期促銷開始後，我就完全被顧客訂單【淹沒】了，所以也許你可以問財務部的凱文，他星期四通常比較有空。"},{"w":"loaded","p":"adj.","d":"carrying or having a large amount of something","c":"裝滿的；堆滿的","s":"A: Are you sure you can take on the hotel booking for the sales conference as well as the monthly report? B: To be honest, my desk is already loaded with files from the new clients, but if you give me until Friday afternoon, I can finish the report first and then book the rooms.","t":"A：你確定你能在處理月報之外，也負責業務研討會的飯店訂房嗎？ B：老實說，我的桌上已經【堆滿】了新客戶的檔案，但如果你給我到星期五下午的時間，我可以先完成報告再訂房間。"},{"w":"stretched","p":"adj.","d":"having hardly enough time, money or people for what is needed","c":"（人力、資源）吃緊的","s":"A: Can our design team start working on the new website for the restaurant chain next week, as the client requested? B: I'm not sure, because the team is already stretched with two other big projects, and two designers are on vacation, so we might need to ask the client for an extra month.","t":"A：我們的設計團隊可以照客戶要求，下週開始製作連鎖餐廳的新網站嗎？ B：我不確定，因為團隊已經因為另外兩個大案子而【人手吃緊】，而且有兩位設計師在休假，所以我們可能需要請客戶多給一個月。"},{"w":"hectic","p":"adj.","d":"very busy and full of activity","c":"忙亂的；繁忙的","s":"A: How was your first week at the airport information desk, now that the summer travel season has begun? B: It was really hectic, because thousands of passengers kept asking about delayed flights and lost bags, but my supervisor was very kind and showed me how to stay calm and handle each problem one by one.","t":"A：既然夏季旅遊旺季已經開始，你在機場服務台的第一週過得如何？ B：真的很【忙亂】，因為成千上萬的旅客一直詢問延誤的航班和遺失的行李，但我的主管人很好，教我如何保持冷靜，一一處理每個問題。"},{"w":"frantic","p":"adj.","d":"done in a hurried and worried way, without control","c":"慌亂的；瘋狂的","s":"A: Why was everyone in the marketing office running around and shouting this morning before the product launch? B: They were in a frantic search for the USB drive with the presentation slides, because the CEO was arriving in twenty minutes and nobody could remember where the intern had put it last night.","t":"A：今天早上產品發表前，行銷辦公室的每個人為什麼都跑來跑去還大聲喊叫？ B：他們在【慌亂地】尋找存有簡報投影片的隨身碟，因為執行長二十分鐘後就要到了，卻沒人記得實習生昨晚把它放在哪裡。"},{"w":"rushed","p":"adj.","d":"done too quickly, or having to hurry","c":"匆忙的；倉促的","s":"A: Did you enjoy the business lunch with the new suppliers from Vietnam at the hotel yesterday? B: Not really, because it felt very rushed, since we only had forty minutes before their train left, so we had to eat quickly and couldn't discuss the delivery prices in much detail.","t":"A：你昨天在飯店和越南新供應商的商務午餐吃得愉快嗎？ B：不太愉快，感覺很【匆忙】，因為他們的火車開之前我們只有四十分鐘，所以我們得吃很快，也沒辦法詳細討論運費價格。"},{"w":"pressed","p":"adj.","d":"not having enough of something, especially time","c":"（時間、金錢）緊迫的；不足的","s":"A: Would you like to join us for a coffee and a quick chat about the training program in the lobby café? B: I'm a little pressed for time today, because I have to prepare a sales presentation for an important client by four o'clock, but I'd be happy to meet you tomorrow morning instead.","t":"A：你要不要和我們一起去大廳的咖啡廳喝杯咖啡，簡短聊一下培訓課程？ B：我今天時間有點【緊迫】，因為我得在四點前為一位重要客戶準備銷售簡報，但我很樂意改成明天早上和你碰面。"},{"w":"demanding","p":"adj.","d":"needing a lot of time, energy or skill","c":"費力的；要求高的","s":"A: Why did Linda decide to leave her well-paid position at the international bank after only one year? B: She said the job was too demanding, since she often worked late into the night and traveled abroad twice a month, so she hardly saw her family and felt tired all the time.","t":"A：為什麼琳達在國際銀行待了才一年就決定離開她高薪的職位？ B：她說那份工作太【吃力】了，因為她常常工作到深夜，而且每個月出國兩次，所以她幾乎見不到家人，總是覺得很累。"},{"w":"time-consuming","p":"adj.","d":"taking a lot of time","c":"耗時的；費時的","s":"A: Should we check every customer survey by hand, or is there a faster way to find the most common complaints? B: Reading them one by one would be very time-consuming, because we received more than five thousand forms last month, so I suggest we use the new software that sorts the comments automatically.","t":"A：我們應該人工檢查每份顧客問卷，還是有更快的方法找出最常見的抱怨？ B：一份一份看會非常【耗時】，因為我們上個月收到超過五千份表格，所以我建議用那套能自動分類意見的新軟體。"},{"w":"engaged","p":"adj.","d":"busy; (of a phone line) being used","c":"忙碌的；（電話）佔線的","s":"A: I've been trying to call the shipping company all morning to ask about our missing boxes, but why can't I get through? B: Their line is probably engaged because many customers are calling after the storm delayed deliveries, so why don't you send them a message through their website instead?","t":"A：我整個早上一直打電話給貨運公司詢問我們遺失的箱子，但為什麼都打不通？ B：他們的電話大概【佔線中】，因為暴風雨延誤了送貨，很多顧客都在打電話，所以你何不改成透過他們的網站傳訊息？"},{"w":"active","p":"adj.","d":"busy doing many things; full of energy","c":"活躍的；積極的","s":"A: Your grandfather is almost eighty, so does he still spend most of his time at home since he retired from the factory? B: Not at all, he's still very active, because he volunteers at the local library three mornings a week, plays tennis on weekends, and even takes an English class at the community center.","t":"A：你祖父快八十歲了，他從工廠退休後是不是大部分時間都待在家裡？ B：完全不是，他還是非常【活躍】，因為他每週有三個早上在當地圖書館當志工，週末打網球，甚至還在社區中心上英文課。"},{"w":"on the go","p":"adj.phr.","d":"very busy and moving around all the time","c":"忙個不停的","s":"A: How does your sister manage to run her own bakery and take care of three young children at the same time? B: She's always on the go from six in the morning until late at night, but she says she enjoys it, and her husband helps with the kids after he finishes work at the hospital.","t":"A：你姊姊是怎麼同時經營自己的麵包店又照顧三個小孩的？ B：她從早上六點到深夜總是【忙個不停】，但她說她很享受，而且她先生在醫院下班後也會幫忙照顧孩子。"},{"w":"full","p":"adj.","d":"having no free space or time left","c":"滿的；排滿的","s":"A: Can I book an appointment with Dr. Chen this Friday afternoon to talk about the results of my health check? B: I'm sorry, but her calendar is completely full on Friday because of the medical conference, so the earliest time I can offer you is next Monday at ten o'clock in the morning.","t":"A：我可以預約陳醫師這個星期五下午，談一下我的健康檢查結果嗎？ B：很抱歉，因為醫學研討會，她星期五的行事曆完全【排滿】了，所以我能提供給您最早的時間是下星期一早上十點。"},{"w":"packed","p":"adj.","d":"very crowded; full of people or things","c":"擠滿的；塞滿的","s":"A: Do you think we can find seats on the train to Kaohsiung if we arrive at the station around five o'clock on Friday? B: I doubt it, because the trains are always packed with office workers going home for the long weekend, so we should buy our tickets online tonight to be safe.","t":"A：如果我們星期五五點左右到車站，你覺得我們找得到往高雄火車的座位嗎？ B：我很懷疑，因為火車上總是【擠滿】了要回家過連假的上班族，所以為了保險起見，我們今晚應該在網路上買票。"},{"w":"jam-packed","p":"adj.","d":"extremely full or crowded","c":"擠得水洩不通的；塞得滿滿的","s":"A: What did you think of the trade fair in Taipei, and did your company get many new business contacts? B: The exhibition hall was jam-packed with visitors from all over Asia, so it was hard to move around, but we collected more than two hundred business cards and received several large orders.","t":"A：你覺得台北的商展怎麼樣，你們公司有得到很多新的商業人脈嗎？ B：展覽館裡【擠得水洩不通】，都是來自亞洲各地的訪客，所以很難走動，但我們收集了兩百多張名片，還接到好幾筆大訂單。"},{"w":"tight","p":"adj.","d":"with very little free time or money","c":"緊湊的；拮据的","s":"A: Is it possible to add a visit to the new factory during the clients' trip to Taichung next week? B: The program is already very tight, since they have meetings from nine to six both days and fly back on Wednesday night, but I'll ask whether they'd like to skip the city tour instead.","t":"A：下週客戶到台中的行程中，有可能加入參觀新工廠嗎？ B：行程已經非常【緊湊】，因為他們兩天都從九點開會到六點，而且星期三晚上就要飛回去，但我會問他們是否願意改為取消市區觀光。"},{"w":"burdened","p":"adj.","d":"having a heavy load of work, duties or problems","c":"負擔沉重的","s":"A: Why does the new accountant look so stressed during our team meetings these days? B: She feels burdened with too many responsibilities, because she has to handle the annual tax report, train two interns, and cover for a colleague who is on maternity leave until the end of next month.","t":"A：為什麼新來的會計師最近在我們的團隊會議上看起來壓力那麼大？ B：她覺得被太多責任【壓得喘不過氣】，因為她必須處理年度稅務報告、訓練兩位實習生，還要代理一位休產假到下個月底的同事。"},{"w":"workload","p":"n.","d":"the amount of work a person has to do","c":"工作量","s":"A: Since two people left the accounting team last month, how are the rest of you dealing with all the extra work? B: Our workload has nearly doubled, so we've asked the manager to hire a temporary assistant, and in the meantime we've agreed to share the urgent jobs and work one extra hour each evening.","t":"A：自從會計團隊上個月有兩個人離職後，你們其他人怎麼應付那些額外的工作？ B：我們的【工作量】幾乎加倍了，所以我們已經請經理僱用一位臨時助理，同時我們也同意分擔緊急的工作，每天晚上多工作一小時。"},{"w":"schedule","p":"n.","d":"a plan that lists when things will happen","c":"時間表；行程表","s":"A: Have you planned the visit for the Japanese buyers who are coming to see our showroom on Tuesday? B: Yes, I've prepared a detailed schedule for their visit, starting with a factory tour at nine, followed by a product demonstration and lunch, and I'll email a copy to everyone on the sales team this afternoon.","t":"A：你安排好星期二要來參觀我們展示間的日本買家的行程了嗎？ B：是的，我已經為他們的參訪準備了一份詳細的【行程表】，九點從工廠參觀開始，接著是產品示範和午餐，我今天下午會把副本寄給業務團隊的每個人。"},{"w":"deadline","p":"n.","d":"the latest time by which something must be done","c":"截止期限","s":"A: When does the marketing department need the final version of the brochure for the new hotel? B: The deadline is next Monday at noon, because the printing company needs three days to print five thousand copies before the grand opening, so we must not make any more changes after this weekend.","t":"A：行銷部什麼時候需要新飯店宣傳手冊的最終版本？ B：【截止期限】是下星期一中午，因為印刷公司需要三天在盛大開幕前印好五千份，所以這個週末之後我們不能再做任何修改了。"},{"w":"commitment","p":"n.","d":"something you have promised to do, which takes your time","c":"承諾；應盡的責任","s":"A: Would you like to lead the planning team for the company's twentieth anniversary party in December? B: I'd love to help, but I have a family commitment on weekends, since I travel to Tainan to take care of my elderly parents, so I wouldn't be able to attend the planning meetings held on Saturday mornings.","t":"A：你願意帶領十二月公司二十週年派對的籌備小組嗎？ B：我很樂意幫忙，但我週末有家庭【責任】，因為我要去台南照顧年邁的父母，所以我沒辦法參加星期六早上舉行的籌備會議。"},{"w":"task","p":"n.","d":"a piece of work that must be done","c":"任務；工作","s":"A: What should I do first on my first day as a receptionist at the hotel, since everything here seems so new to me? B: Your first task is to learn how to use the booking system, and after lunch Sarah will show you how to welcome guests, check their passports, and give them their room keys.","t":"A：我第一天在飯店當櫃檯人員應該先做什麼呢？這裡的一切對我來說都好新。 B：你的第一項【任務】是學會使用訂房系統，午餐後莎拉會教你如何接待客人、檢查他們的護照，並把房間鑰匙交給他們。"},{"w":"assignment","p":"n.","d":"a piece of work or job that someone is given to do","c":"（分派的）任務；派任工作","s":"A: Why is Mark flying to Jakarta next month when he only joined the engineering department in March? B: The company gave him a six-month assignment at our new factory there, because he speaks Indonesian and can help the local staff learn how to use the machines we bought from Germany.","t":"A：馬克三月才加入工程部，為什麼下個月就要飛去雅加達？ B：公司給了他一項在那裡新工廠為期六個月的【派任工作】，因為他會說印尼語，可以幫助當地員工學會使用我們從德國買來的機器。"},{"w":"multitask","p":"v.","d":"to do several things at the same time","c":"同時處理多項工作","s":"A: What kind of skills are you looking for in the new office assistant you plan to hire next month? B: We need someone who can multitask well, because the assistant will answer phone calls, greet visitors, and update the sales records at the same time, especially during our busy morning hours.","t":"A：你們下個月打算僱用的新辦公室助理，需要具備什麼樣的技能？ B：我們需要一個很能【同時處理多項工作】的人，因為助理要同時接電話、招呼訪客和更新銷售紀錄，特別是在早上忙碌的時段。"},{"w":"juggle","p":"v.","d":"to try to deal with several jobs or duties at the same time","c":"兼顧；同時應付","s":"A: How do you manage to study for your MBA while working full-time at the advertising agency in the city center? B: It's hard to juggle work and school, but I study on the train every morning, attend classes online on weekends, and my manager kindly lets me leave early on exam days.","t":"A：你怎麼能在市中心的廣告公司全職工作的同時，又讀企管碩士？ B：要【兼顧】工作和學業很難，但我每天早上在火車上讀書，週末上線上課程，而且考試那天我的經理會好心讓我提早下班。"},{"w":"rush","p":"v.","d":"to move or do something very quickly","c":"趕；匆忙行事","s":"A: The meeting with the bank doesn't start until three o'clock, so should we leave the office right now? B: There's no need to rush, because the bank is only a ten-minute walk from here, so let's finish checking the loan documents carefully first and then leave at around half past two.","t":"A：和銀行的會議三點才開始，所以我們應該現在就離開辦公室嗎？ B：不需要【趕】，因為銀行從這裡走路只要十分鐘，所以我們先把貸款文件仔細檢查完，大約兩點半再出發。"},{"w":"prioritise","p":"v.","d":"to decide which things are most important and do them first","c":"排定優先順序","s":"A: I have to finish the sales report, answer twenty customer emails, and prepare for tomorrow's training session, so where should I start? B: You need to prioritise your work, so start with the sales report, because the director needs it by noon, and then reply to the customers who have complained about late deliveries.","t":"A：我得完成銷售報告、回覆二十封顧客郵件，還要準備明天的訓練課程，我應該從哪裡開始？ B：你需要把工作【排定優先順序】，所以先從銷售報告開始，因為主任中午前要，然後再回覆那些抱怨送貨延遲的顧客。"},{"w":"crammed","p":"adj.","d":"too full of people, things or activities","c":"塞滿的；擠滿的","s":"A: Why didn't you enjoy the guided tour of Europe that your company gave you as a reward for being the top salesperson? B: The tour was crammed with too many activities, so we visited six cities in seven days and spent most of our time on the bus instead of relaxing and enjoying the local food.","t":"A：公司為了獎勵你成為頂尖業務員而送你的歐洲導覽旅遊，你為什麼玩得不開心？ B：那趟旅遊【塞滿】了太多活動，所以我們七天去了六個城市，大部分時間都在巴士上，而不是放鬆享受當地美食。"},{"w":"nonstop","p":"adj.","d":"continuing without stopping or resting","c":"不停的；直達的","s":"A: You look really tired today, so did you have a difficult day at the call center? B: Yes, it was nonstop work from the moment I arrived, because our internet service went down across the whole city, and hundreds of angry customers called, so I couldn't eat lunch until three o'clock.","t":"A：你今天看起來真的很累，你在客服中心度過了辛苦的一天嗎？ B：是的，從我一到就是【不停歇的】工作，因為我們的網路服務在全市都斷線了，數百位生氣的顧客打電話來，所以我到三點才能吃午餐。"},{"w":"overloaded","p":"adj.","d":"given too much work or too much to carry or handle","c":"超載的；負擔過重的","s":"A: Why did the company's online shopping website crash during the big sale last Friday night? B: The system was overloaded with too many visitors at the same time, because over two hundred thousand people tried to buy the discounted phones in the first ten minutes, so the technical team is now upgrading the servers.","t":"A：上週五晚上大特賣時，為什麼公司的網路購物網站當機了？ B：系統因為同時有太多訪客而【超載】，因為前十分鐘就有超過二十萬人想搶購打折手機，所以技術團隊現在正在升級伺服器。"},{"w":"snowed under","p":"adj.phr.","d":"having so much work that you cannot deal with it all","c":"忙得不可開交的","s":"A: Can you come to the farewell dinner for Mr. Lin at the Italian restaurant on Thursday evening? B: I'd really like to, but I'm snowed under with end-of-year reports right now, so I might have to stay in the office until nine, though I'll try to join you for dessert if I can.","t":"A：你星期四晚上能來義大利餐廳參加林先生的歡送晚宴嗎？ B：我真的很想去，但我現在被年終報告弄得【忙得不可開交】，所以我可能得在辦公室待到九點，不過如果可以的話，我會盡量趕去和你們一起吃甜點。"},{"w":"flat out","p":"adj.phr.","d":"working as hard or as fast as possible","c":"全力以赴的；忙到極點的","s":"A: Has the factory been able to produce enough air conditioners for all the stores during this extremely hot summer? B: The workers have been flat out for weeks, running the machines day and night, but the demand is still higher than we expected, so we're planning to open a second production line in August.","t":"A：在這個極度炎熱的夏天，工廠有辦法為所有門市生產足夠的冷氣機嗎？ B：工人們好幾週來一直【全力以赴】，機器日夜運轉，但需求還是比我們預期的高，所以我們打算八月開設第二條生產線。"}]},{"unit":40,"theme":"Buy 購買","cards":[{"w":"purchase","p":"v.","d":"to buy something, especially for a business","c":"購買；採購","s":"A: Our team needs six new laptops before the training program starts next month, so who should I talk to about getting them quickly? B: You should email Mr. Chen in the finance office, because every department must get his approval before it can purchase any equipment that is worth more than five thousand dollars.","t":"A：我們團隊在下個月培訓計畫開始前需要六台新筆電，我該找誰才能快點拿到？ B：你應該寄電子郵件給財務室的陳先生，因為每個部門在【購買】任何價值超過五千元的設備之前，都必須先得到他的核准。"},{"w":"pay","p":"v.","d":"to give money for something you buy or a service","c":"付款；支付","s":"A: The hotel front desk just told me that the conference room charge was not included in our package, so what should I do now? B: Don't worry, just pay with the company credit card, keep the receipt, and send it to accounting when we get back to the office on Monday.","t":"A：飯店櫃台剛剛告訴我，會議室的費用不包含在我們的套裝方案裡，我現在該怎麼辦？ B：別擔心，就用公司信用卡【付款】，把收據留著，等我們星期一回辦公室再交給會計部。"},{"w":"price","p":"n.","d":"the amount of money you must pay to buy something","c":"價格","s":"A: I found a printer online that has all the features we need, but the shop near our office sells the same model, so which one should we choose? B: Let's check the price at both places first, because the website also charges a shipping fee, and the local shop might give us free setup.","t":"A：我在網路上找到一台功能完全符合我們需求的印表機，但辦公室附近的店也賣同一款，我們該選哪一個？ B：我們先查一下兩邊的【價格】吧，因為網站還要收運費，而附近的店可能會免費幫我們安裝。"},{"w":"cost","p":"n.","d":"the amount of money needed to buy, do, or make something","c":"費用；成本","s":"A: The manager wants to send all twenty sales staff to the trade fair in Tokyo next spring, but is there enough money in our travel budget? B: I'm not sure yet, because the total cost of flights, hotels, and meals for that many people could be much higher than what we spent on last year's event.","t":"A：經理想在明年春天派全部二十位業務人員去東京參加商展，但我們的差旅預算夠嗎？ B：我還不確定，因為那麼多人的機票、飯店和餐費的總【費用】，可能會比我們去年活動花的錢高出許多。"},{"w":"afford","p":"v.","d":"to have enough money to pay for something","c":"負擔得起","s":"A: The new office building downtown looks amazing, and it is very close to the subway station, so why didn't the company decide to move there? B: The rent is almost twice what we pay now, and with sales falling this year, we simply cannot afford such a large expense until business improves again.","t":"A：市中心那棟新辦公大樓看起來很棒，而且離捷運站很近，公司為什麼沒決定搬過去？ B：那裡的租金幾乎是我們現在的兩倍，而且今年業績下滑，在生意好轉之前我們根本【負擔不起】這麼大的開銷。"},{"w":"spend","p":"v.","d":"to use money to buy or pay for things","c":"花費（金錢）","s":"A: Our department received an extra two thousand dollars at the end of the year, and the director said we must use it by December, right? B: Yes, so I suggest we spend most of it on comfortable new chairs for the meeting room, since everyone has been complaining that the old ones hurt their backs.","t":"A：我們部門年底多拿到兩千元，主任說我們必須在十二月前用掉，對吧？ B：對，所以我建議我們把大部分的錢【花】在會議室的舒適新椅子上，因為大家一直抱怨舊椅子坐得背痛。"},{"w":"sale","p":"n.","d":"a time when a shop sells things at lower prices than usual","c":"特價；拍賣","s":"A: Are you going to the department store after work tonight, because I heard many people are lining up outside even though it's a Tuesday? B: Yes, they are having a huge end-of-season sale this week, and winter coats are fifty percent off, so I want to buy one before the popular sizes are gone.","t":"A：你今晚下班後要去百貨公司嗎？我聽說雖然今天才星期二，外面就已經大排長龍了。 B：對，他們這週在辦換季大【拍賣】，冬季外套打五折，所以我想在熱門尺寸賣完之前買一件。"},{"w":"discount","p":"n.","d":"an amount taken off the usual price","c":"折扣","s":"A: We want to order two hundred company T-shirts for the charity run next month, but the price on the website seems quite high for our small budget. B: Call the supplier directly and explain that it's a large order, because they usually give a ten percent discount to businesses that buy more than one hundred items.","t":"A：我們想為下個月的慈善路跑訂兩百件公司T恤，但網站上的價格對我們的小預算來說似乎太高了。 B：直接打電話給供應商，說明這是大量訂單，因為他們通常會給購買超過一百件的公司九折的【折扣】。"},{"w":"bargain","p":"n.","d":"something bought for much less than its usual price","c":"便宜貨；划算的東西","s":"A: I can't believe you bought that leather briefcase for only fifty dollars, because it looks exactly like the ones they sell in the luxury shops downtown. B: I know, it was a real bargain, since the shop was closing down and selling everything at very low prices, so I went there during my lunch break and got it.","t":"A：真不敢相信你只花五十元就買到那個皮革公事包，它看起來跟市中心精品店賣的一模一樣。 B：我知道，真的很【划算】，因為那家店要結束營業，所有東西都超低價出清，所以我趁午休去把它買下來了。"},{"w":"cheap","p":"adj.","d":"costing little money","c":"便宜的","s":"A: Should we book the hotel next to the convention center for the sales team, or look for somewhere farther away to save money? B: The hotels near the center are full and expensive, but there's a clean, cheap guesthouse two stops away by train, so we could save a lot and still arrive on time.","t":"A：我們該幫業務團隊訂會展中心旁邊的飯店，還是找遠一點的地方來省錢？ B：中心附近的飯店都客滿又貴，但搭火車兩站外有一間乾淨又【便宜】的民宿，所以我們可以省很多錢，而且還是能準時抵達。"},{"w":"expensive","p":"adj.","d":"costing a lot of money","c":"昂貴的","s":"A: Why did the marketing team decide to cancel the TV commercial they were planning for the new energy drink launch in the spring? B: Advertising on television turned out to be far too expensive for a small company like ours, so we are going to promote the drink on social media and at local events instead.","t":"A：行銷團隊為什麼決定取消原本為春季新能量飲料上市規劃的電視廣告？ B：在電視上打廣告對我們這樣的小公司來說實在太【昂貴】了，所以我們改在社群媒體和地方活動上宣傳這款飲料。"},{"w":"value","p":"n.","d":"how useful or important something is compared with its price","c":"價值；划算程度","s":"A: Do you think it's worth paying more for the premium coffee machine for our office kitchen, or should we just buy the basic model? B: The premium one is pricier at first, but it lasts much longer and uses less costly coffee pods, so I think it offers better value for money over the next few years.","t":"A：你覺得辦公室茶水間值得多花錢買高級咖啡機嗎？還是我們就買基本款就好？ B：高級款一開始比較貴，但它耐用得多，而且用的咖啡膠囊比較便宜，所以我認為接下來幾年它更【物超所值】。"},{"w":"receipt","p":"n.","d":"a piece of paper that shows you have paid for something","c":"收據","s":"A: I took two clients out for dinner last night after we signed the contract, so can the company pay me back for the meal? B: Yes, but you'll need to attach the original receipt to your expense form and submit it to the accounting department before Friday, or they won't be able to process your claim this month.","t":"A：我昨晚簽完合約後請兩位客戶吃晚餐，公司可以幫我報帳嗎？ B：可以，但你需要把【收據】正本附在費用申請單上，並在星期五前交給會計部，否則他們這個月就無法處理你的申請。"},{"w":"refund","p":"n.","d":"money that is given back to you when you return something","c":"退款","s":"A: The projector we bought last week stopped working after only two presentations, and the technician says it can't be repaired easily. B: Take it back to the electronics shop with the box and paperwork, and ask for a full refund, because their policy says shoppers can return faulty items within thirty days of buying them.","t":"A：我們上週買的投影機只用了兩次簡報就壞了，技術人員說不容易修好。 B：把它連同盒子和文件一起拿回電器行，要求全額【退款】，因為他們的規定是顧客在購買後三十天內可以退回有瑕疵的商品。"},{"w":"checkout","p":"n.","d":"the place or final step where you pay for what you buy","c":"結帳（處）","s":"A: I've been trying to buy the plane tickets for our business trip, but the website keeps showing an error message, and I don't know why. B: That often happens at the checkout page when your session times out, so log in again, add the tickets to your basket, and finish the payment within ten minutes this time.","t":"A：我一直想買我們出差的機票，但網站一直跳出錯誤訊息，我不知道為什麼。 B：當你的登入逾時，【結帳】頁面常常會這樣，所以重新登入，把機票加進購物籃，這次要在十分鐘內完成付款。"},{"w":"cart","p":"n.","d":"a list of items you plan to buy on a website; a shopping trolley","c":"購物車","s":"A: I'm ordering office supplies on the website right now, and I've already chosen paper, pens, and ink, but is there anything else we need? B: Please add two boxes of staples and some sticky notes to the shopping cart before you pay, because we're almost out and the next supply run won't be until next month.","t":"A：我現在正在網站上訂辦公用品，已經選了紙、筆和墨水，我們還需要什麼嗎？ B：付款前請把兩盒訂書針和一些便利貼加進【購物車】，因為快用完了，而下一次補貨要等到下個月。"},{"w":"customer","p":"n.","d":"a person who buys things from a shop or business","c":"顧客","s":"A: Why does the manager want all the shop assistants to attend a training session on Saturday morning, when that's usually our busiest time? B: She received several complaints last month, so she wants us to learn how to stay polite and patient when a customer is angry about a late delivery or a damaged product.","t":"A：經理為什麼要所有店員星期六早上參加培訓？那通常是我們最忙的時候。 B：她上個月收到好幾件客訴，所以她希望我們學會當【顧客】因為送貨延誤或商品損壞而生氣時，如何保持禮貌和耐心。"},{"w":"seller","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that sells something","c":"賣家；賣方","s":"A: I want to buy a used van for our flower business, and I found one online that looks good, but how can I be sure it's safe? B: Arrange to meet the seller in person, ask to see the service records, and bring a mechanic friend to check the engine before you agree to pay any money.","t":"A：我想為我們的花店買一台二手廂型車，在網路上找到一台看起來不錯，但我怎麼確定它安全？ B：約【賣家】當面見面，要求看保養紀錄，並帶一位當技師的朋友檢查引擎，然後再同意付錢。"},{"w":"order","p":"v.","d":"to ask for goods to be made, supplied, or delivered","c":"訂購；點（餐）","s":"A: We're expecting forty guests at the product launch on Friday evening, so how much food should we get from the catering company? B: Let's order enough sandwiches and drinks for fifty people, just in case some guests bring colleagues, because running out of food at an important event would make our company look bad.","t":"A：星期五晚上的產品發表會預計有四十位來賓，我們該向外燴公司訂多少食物？ B：我們就【訂】夠五十人份的三明治和飲料吧，以防有些來賓帶同事來，因為在重要活動上食物不夠會讓公司很沒面子。"},{"w":"delivery","p":"n.","d":"the act of bringing goods to a place","c":"送貨；運送","s":"A: The new furniture for the reception area was supposed to arrive this morning, but nothing has come yet, and the visitors arrive tomorrow. B: I just called the supplier, and they said the delivery was delayed because of heavy traffic on the highway, but the truck should reach our building before four o'clock this afternoon.","t":"A：接待區的新家具本來應該今天早上送到，但到現在什麼都還沒來，而訪客明天就到了。 B：我剛打給供應商，他們說因為高速公路塞車，【送貨】延誤了，但卡車應該會在今天下午四點前抵達我們大樓。"},{"w":"online","p":"adj.","d":"using the internet","c":"線上的；網路的","s":"A: Our small bakery has been getting fewer customers since the new supermarket opened across the street, so what do you think we should do? B: We could open an online shop on our website, so people can order cakes and bread from home and pick them up, or even have them delivered to their door.","t":"A：自從對面新超市開幕後，我們的小麵包店客人越來越少，你覺得我們該怎麼辦？ B：我們可以在網站上開一家【網路】商店，讓大家在家就能訂蛋糕和麵包，再來店取貨，甚至直接送到家門口。"},{"w":"store","p":"n.","d":"a shop, especially a large one","c":"商店","s":"A: Excuse me, I'm visiting from Taipei for a business meeting and forgot my phone charger, so where can I buy a new one near this hotel? B: There's a large electronics store just around the corner, next to the bank, and it stays open until ten o'clock at night, so you still have plenty of time.","t":"A：不好意思，我從台北來這裡開商務會議，忘了帶手機充電器，這間飯店附近哪裡可以買到新的？ B：轉角就有一家大型電器【商店】，就在銀行旁邊，營業到晚上十點，所以你還有很多時間。"},{"w":"market","p":"n.","d":"an area or group of people where products can be sold","c":"市場","s":"A: Our company wants to start selling its tea products overseas next year, but which country do you think we should try first? B: Japan could be a good market for us, because many young people there enjoy Taiwanese bubble tea, and our research shows that demand for healthy drinks is growing quickly in big cities.","t":"A：我們公司明年想開始在海外銷售茶類產品，你覺得我們應該先試哪個國家？ B：日本可能是很好的【市場】，因為那裡很多年輕人喜歡台灣珍珠奶茶，而且我們的研究顯示大城市對健康飲品的需求成長很快。"},{"w":"brand","p":"n.","d":"a type of product made by a particular company with its own name","c":"品牌","s":"A: Why are you buying this printer paper when there's a cheaper one on the shelf right next to it that looks almost the same? B: I prefer this brand because the paper never jams in our office machines, and I'd rather pay a little more than waste time fixing the printer every week.","t":"A：架上旁邊就有一款更便宜、看起來幾乎一樣的影印紙，你為什麼還要買這款？ B：我比較喜歡這個【品牌】，因為它的紙從來不會卡在我們辦公室的機器裡，我寧願多付一點錢，也不想每週浪費時間修印表機。"},{"w":"quality","p":"n.","d":"how good or bad something is","c":"品質","s":"A: The supplier from overseas offered us shirts at half the price of our current factory, so why didn't the manager accept the deal? B: She ordered some samples first, and the quality was very poor, because the stitching came apart after one wash, and our customers would definitely complain about that.","t":"A：海外供應商開給我們的襯衫價格只有現在工廠的一半，經理為什麼不接受這筆交易？ B：她先訂了一些樣品，結果【品質】非常差，洗一次縫線就裂開了，我們的顧客一定會抱怨。"},{"w":"compare","p":"v.","d":"to look at two or more things to see how they are similar or different","c":"比較","s":"A: I need to choose a new mobile phone plan for the whole sales team, but there are so many companies offering different deals. B: Make a simple chart and compare the monthly fees, data limits, and contract lengths of the three biggest providers, and then show it to the manager so she can decide by Friday.","t":"A：我需要為整個業務團隊選一個新的手機方案，但有好多公司提供不同的優惠。 B：做一張簡單的表格，【比較】三大電信業者的月租費、數據上限和合約長度，然後拿給經理看，讓她在星期五前做決定。"},{"w":"budget","p":"n.","d":"the amount of money you have to spend on something","c":"預算","s":"A: The design team wants to hire a famous photographer for the new catalog, but do we have enough money for that this quarter? B: Unfortunately, our marketing budget was cut by twenty percent this year, so we will probably need to use our own staff photographer and save the extra money for internet advertising.","t":"A：設計團隊想為新型錄請一位知名攝影師，但我們這一季有足夠的錢嗎？ B：很遺憾，我們今年的行銷【預算】被砍了百分之二十，所以我們可能得用自己公司的攝影師，把多出來的錢留給網路廣告。"},{"w":"installment","p":"n.","d":"one of several payments made over a period of time","c":"分期付款（的一期）","s":"A: The new accounting software costs twelve thousand dollars, and that's a lot of money for a small company like ours to pay all at once. B: The software company allows small businesses to pay the first installment of one thousand dollars this month, and then pay the same amount every month for the rest of the year.","t":"A：新的會計軟體要一萬兩千元，對我們這樣的小公司來說，一次付清是一大筆錢。 B：軟體公司允許小企業這個月先付第一期一千元的【分期款】，然後在今年剩下的每個月都付同樣的金額。"},{"w":"warranty","p":"n.","d":"a written promise that a company will repair or replace a product if it breaks","c":"保固；保證書","s":"A: My office laptop suddenly stopped charging this morning, and I have an important presentation to finish by tomorrow afternoon, so what can I do? B: Check the paperwork in the IT office, because I think that laptop is still under a two-year warranty, which means the manufacturer will repair or replace it for free.","t":"A：我的辦公室筆電今天早上突然無法充電，而我有一份重要的簡報要在明天下午前完成，我該怎麼辦？ B：去資訊室查一下文件，因為我記得那台筆電還在兩年【保固】期內，這表示製造商會免費維修或更換。"}]},{"unit":41,"theme":"Cafe 咖啡館","cards":[{"w":"coffeehouse","p":"n.","d":"a café where people drink coffee and meet","c":"咖啡館","s":"A: Our team needs a relaxed place to meet the new designer from Osaka on Friday morning, so do you have any suggestions near the office? B: There is a charming old coffeehouse on Maple Street that opened in the 1950s, and it has large wooden tables where we can spread out the drawings and talk for hours.","t":"A：週五早上我們團隊需要一個輕鬆的地方和來自大阪的新設計師見面，你在辦公室附近有什麼建議嗎？ B：楓樹街上有一家1950年代開業的迷人老【咖啡館】，裡面有大木桌，我們可以把圖稿攤開，聊上好幾個小時。"},{"w":"barista","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is making coffee drinks in a café","c":"咖啡師","s":"A: The coffee at the new branch tastes much better than it did last month, so did the owner change suppliers or buy a new machine? B: Actually, she hired an experienced barista who won a national competition last year, and he has been training the other staff to prepare every drink more carefully.","t":"A：新分店的咖啡比上個月好喝多了，老闆是換了供應商還是買了新機器？ B：其實她聘請了一位去年贏得全國比賽的資深【咖啡師】，他一直在訓練其他員工更用心地準備每一杯飲料。"},{"w":"espresso","p":"n.","d":"a small cup of very strong black coffee","c":"濃縮咖啡","s":"A: You have to finish the quarterly report before the board meeting at nine tomorrow, so are you going to stay late at the office tonight? B: Yes, I probably will, so I'm going downstairs to get a double espresso first, because I need something strong to keep me awake while I check all the figures.","t":"A：你必須在明天九點董事會前完成季報，所以你今晚要在辦公室待到很晚嗎？ B：是的，大概會，所以我要先下樓買一杯雙份【濃縮咖啡】，因為我需要喝點濃的東西，讓我在核對所有數字時保持清醒。"},{"w":"latte","p":"n.","d":"a coffee drink made with espresso and a lot of hot milk","c":"拿鐵咖啡","s":"A: I'm going to the café across the street to pick up drinks for the visitors from the head office, so what would you like? B: Please get me a large latte with oat milk, because normal milk upsets my stomach, and I'd like something warm and creamy on a cold, rainy afternoon like this.","t":"A：我要去對街的咖啡店幫總公司來的訪客買飲料，你想喝什麼？ B：請幫我買一杯加燕麥奶的大杯【拿鐵】，因為一般牛奶會讓我胃不舒服，而且在這樣寒冷下雨的下午，我想喝點溫暖又綿密的東西。"},{"w":"cappuccino","p":"n.","d":"a coffee drink made with espresso, hot milk and milk foam","c":"卡布奇諾","s":"A: The client from Milan will arrive at the office around ten, so what should we prepare for her while she waits for the director? B: Let's offer her a fresh cappuccino with a little chocolate powder on top, since her assistant told me she drinks one every morning and doesn't like tea or juice at all.","t":"A：米蘭來的客戶大約十點會到辦公室，她等主任的時候我們該為她準備什麼？ B：我們給她一杯上面撒點巧克力粉的新鮮【卡布奇諾】吧，因為她的助理告訴我她每天早上都喝一杯，而且完全不喜歡茶或果汁。"},{"w":"menu","p":"n.","d":"a list of the food and drinks you can order and their prices","c":"菜單","s":"A: Sales at our café have dropped since the new bakery opened next door, so what do you think we should change first? B: I think we should update the menu with more healthy options like salads and fruit bowls, because many office workers nearby told us they want lighter lunches that don't cost too much.","t":"A：自從隔壁新麵包店開幕後，我們咖啡店的業績就下滑了，你認為我們應該先改變什麼？ B：我認為我們應該更新【菜單】，加入更多像沙拉和水果碗之類的健康選擇，因為附近很多上班族告訴我們，他們想要清淡又不會太貴的午餐。"},{"w":"counter","p":"n.","d":"a long table in a shop or café where customers order and pay","c":"櫃台","s":"A: I've been waiting for my sandwich for almost twenty minutes, and my lunch break ends soon, so should I ask a waiter about it? B: Here they don't bring food to the tables, so you need to pick it up at the counter near the entrance when the staff calls your number on the screen.","t":"A：我的三明治已經等了將近二十分鐘，我的午休快結束了，我應該問服務生嗎？ B：這裡不會把餐點送到桌上，所以當員工在螢幕上叫你的號碼時，你需要到入口附近的【櫃台】取餐。"},{"w":"atmosphere","p":"n.","d":"the feeling or mood that a place gives you","c":"氣氛","s":"A: Why do you always hold your team meetings at that little café on the corner instead of in the conference room upstairs? B: The atmosphere there is relaxed and friendly, with soft lights and comfortable chairs, so my staff feel free to share new ideas without worrying about what the managers might think.","t":"A：你為什麼總是在轉角那間小咖啡店開團隊會議，而不是在樓上的會議室？ B：那裡的【氣氛】輕鬆友善，有柔和的燈光和舒服的椅子，所以我的員工可以自由地分享新點子，不用擔心主管會怎麼想。"},{"w":"cozy","p":"adj.","d":"warm, comfortable and pleasant, like a small home","c":"溫馨舒適的","s":"A: We need a place to interview the two job candidates on Thursday afternoon, but the meeting rooms are all booked, so where should we go? B: There's a small, cozy café behind the train station with soft sofas and a fireplace, so the candidates will feel comfortable and probably speak more naturally about their experience.","t":"A：週四下午我們需要找個地方面試兩位應徵者，但會議室都被預訂了，我們該去哪裡？ B：火車站後面有一間小而【溫馨舒適】的咖啡館，有柔軟的沙發和壁爐，所以應徵者會覺得自在，可能會更自然地談論他們的經驗。"},{"w":"aroma","p":"n.","d":"a strong, pleasant smell, especially of food or coffee","c":"香氣","s":"A: Why did the café owner decide to roast the coffee beans by the front window every morning instead of in the back kitchen? B: She noticed that the rich aroma of fresh coffee spreads into the street, and it attracts many people on their way to work, so her morning sales have nearly doubled.","t":"A：咖啡店老闆為什麼決定每天早上在前窗邊烘咖啡豆，而不是在後面的廚房？ B：她發現新鮮咖啡濃郁的【香氣】會飄到街上，吸引許多上班途中的人，所以她早上的營業額幾乎翻倍了。"},{"w":"brew","p":"v.","d":"to make a hot drink such as coffee or tea","c":"沖泡；釀造","s":"A: The coffee machine in the staff kitchen broke again this morning, so what are we going to do for the clients' meeting at eleven? B: Don't worry, I brought a French press from home, so I can brew a large pot of coffee for everyone in about ten minutes before they arrive.","t":"A：員工廚房的咖啡機今天早上又壞了，那十一點的客戶會議我們要怎麼辦？ B：別擔心，我從家裡帶了一個法式濾壓壺，所以我可以在他們到之前，用大約十分鐘為大家【沖泡】一大壺咖啡。"},{"w":"pastry","p":"n.","d":"a small sweet baked food made with butter and flour","c":"酥皮點心；糕點","s":"A: The training session tomorrow starts at eight, and most of the new staff will come straight from the train station, so should we provide breakfast? B: Yes, let's order coffee and a fresh pastry for each person from the bakery downstairs, because people learn better when they aren't hungry or tired.","t":"A：明天的訓練課程八點開始，大部分新員工會直接從火車站過來，我們應該提供早餐嗎？ B：好，我們從樓下的麵包店幫每個人訂咖啡和一份新鮮的【糕點】吧，因為人不餓也不累的時候學習效果比較好。"},{"w":"dessert","p":"n.","d":"sweet food you eat at the end of a meal","c":"甜點","s":"A: The dinner with our Japanese partners went very well, but should we order anything else before we ask for the bill? B: Let's ask the waiter to bring a dessert for everyone, like the chocolate cake or the mango pudding, because sharing something sweet is a nice way to end a successful evening together.","t":"A：和日本夥伴的晚餐很順利，但我們在結帳前還要點些什麼嗎？ B：我們請服務生為大家送上一份【甜點】吧，像是巧克力蛋糕或芒果布丁，因為一起分享甜食是結束一個成功夜晚的好方式。"},{"w":"takeaway","p":"n.","d":"food or a drink that you buy in a shop and take away to eat or drink","c":"外帶餐點","s":"A: I have a conference call with the London office in fifteen minutes, so do you think I have enough time to eat lunch at the café downstairs? B: Probably not, so you should get a takeaway instead and eat it at your desk, because the café is always very busy and slow at this time of day.","t":"A：我十五分鐘後要和倫敦辦公室開電話會議，你覺得我有足夠時間在樓下咖啡店吃午餐嗎？ B：大概沒有，所以你應該改買【外帶餐點】在座位上吃，因為這個時段咖啡店總是很忙，出餐很慢。"},{"w":"dine","p":"v.","d":"to eat a meal, especially dinner, often at a restaurant","c":"用餐","s":"A: The visitors from our Singapore branch arrive on Friday evening, so where would be a good place to take them after the factory tour? B: I think we should dine at the Italian restaurant by the river, because it has a quiet private room and the chef can prepare vegetarian dishes for the manager.","t":"A：新加坡分公司的訪客週五晚上抵達，參觀工廠之後帶他們去哪裡好？ B：我想我們應該在河邊那家義大利餐廳【用餐】，因為它有安靜的包廂，而且主廚可以為經理準備素食料理。"},{"w":"serve","p":"v.","d":"to give food or drinks to people","c":"供應；上（菜）","s":"A: We expect over a hundred guests at the product launch on Saturday, so how many staff will the café need to send to help us? B: They will send six people, and they will serve coffee, tea and sandwiches in the lobby from two o'clock until the presentations finish around five.","t":"A：週六的產品發表會預計會有超過一百位賓客，咖啡店需要派多少員工來幫忙？ B：他們會派六個人，從兩點到大約五點簡報結束，他們會在大廳【供應】咖啡、茶和三明治。"},{"w":"seat","p":"n.","d":"a place where you can sit, such as a chair","c":"座位","s":"A: The café near the station is always crowded at lunchtime, so how can we make sure we have somewhere to sit with the client on Monday? B: I'll call them this afternoon and ask them to save a seat for each of us by the window, because they let regular customers book tables before noon.","t":"A：車站附近那家咖啡店午餐時間總是很擁擠，我們要怎麼確定週一和客戶有地方坐？ B：我今天下午會打電話給他們，請他們在窗邊為我們每人保留一個【座位】，因為他們讓常客在中午前訂位。"},{"w":"crowded","p":"adj.","d":"full of too many people","c":"擁擠的","s":"A: Why did you leave the café so quickly this morning when you had planned to finish your sales report there before work? B: It was too crowded because a tour group had just arrived, and there were people everywhere, so I couldn't find a table or think clearly about my numbers.","t":"A：你原本計畫上班前在咖啡店完成業務報告，為什麼今天早上那麼快就離開了？ B：因為有個旅行團剛到，裡面太【擁擠】了，到處都是人，所以我找不到桌子，也沒辦法好好思考我的數字。"},{"w":"quiet","p":"adj.","d":"making very little noise; peaceful","c":"安靜的","s":"A: I need to prepare for an important phone interview with a bank this afternoon, but the office is noisy because of the renovation, so where should I go? B: You could use the small room upstairs, because it's usually quiet after lunch and nobody will disturb you while you practice your answers.","t":"A：我今天下午要準備一場銀行的重要電話面試，但辦公室因為裝修很吵，我該去哪裡？ B：你可以用樓上的小房間，因為午餐後那裡通常很【安靜】，你練習回答時不會有人打擾。"},{"w":"wifi","p":"n.","d":"a way of connecting to the internet without wires","c":"無線網路","s":"A: I'm planning to work from the café near my apartment tomorrow because the office air conditioning is being repaired, but will I be able to join the video meeting? B: Yes, they offer free wifi for customers, and the connection is fast enough for video calls, though you should ask the staff for the password first.","t":"A：明天因為辦公室冷氣在維修，我打算在我公寓附近的咖啡店工作，但我能參加視訊會議嗎？ B：可以，他們為顧客提供免費【無線網路】，連線速度足以進行視訊通話，不過你應該先向店員要密碼。"},{"w":"regular","p":"n.","d":"a customer who often goes to the same shop, café or restaurant","c":"常客","s":"A: The waiter at the corner café knew exactly what you wanted before you even said anything this morning, so how does he know you so well? B: I've been a regular there for almost three years, because I stop by every morning on my way to the office and always order the same thing.","t":"A：今天早上轉角咖啡店的服務生在你開口前就知道你要什麼，他怎麼會那麼了解你？ B：我在那裡當【常客】快三年了，因為我每天早上上班途中都會順道過去，而且總是點一樣的東西。"},{"w":"refreshment","p":"n.","d":"a small amount of food or drink that makes you feel less tired or thirsty","c":"茶點；提神飲食","s":"A: The workshop for the new sales team will last about four hours on Wednesday, so do you think the attendees will need a break in the middle? B: Yes, and the café downstairs can deliver juice, tea and cookies at three, which will be a welcome refreshment for everyone after hours of training.","t":"A：週三新業務團隊的研習大約會持續四個小時，你覺得參加者中間需要休息嗎？ B：需要，樓下的咖啡店可以在三點送果汁、茶和餅乾來，對受訓好幾個小時的大家來說會是很受歡迎的【茶點】。"},{"w":"specialty","p":"n.","d":"a food or product that a place is famous for or does very well","c":"招牌菜；特色商品","s":"A: We are taking the visitors from Korea to the café on the top floor of the shopping mall, so is there anything we must try there? B: Their specialty is a honey cake made with fruit from local farms, and it has won several awards, so the visitors will probably enjoy it with their coffee.","t":"A：我們要帶韓國訪客去購物中心頂樓的咖啡店，那裡有什麼我們一定要嚐嚐的嗎？ B：他們的【招牌】是用當地農場水果做的蜂蜜蛋糕，得過好幾個獎，所以訪客們大概會很喜歡配著咖啡吃。"},{"w":"order","p":"v.","d":"to ask for food, drinks or goods that you want to buy","c":"點（餐）；訂購","s":"A: The meeting with the investors might go past lunchtime, and nobody wants to leave the room while we're discussing the contract, so what should we do? B: I'll order sandwiches and salads from the café across the street at half past eleven, and they can deliver everything to the conference room by noon.","t":"A：和投資人的會議可能會超過午餐時間，而且討論合約時沒人想離開會議室，我們該怎麼辦？ B：我會在十一點半向對街的咖啡店【訂購】三明治和沙拉，他們可以在中午前把所有東西送到會議室。"},{"w":"receipt","p":"n.","d":"a piece of paper that shows you have paid for something","c":"收據","s":"A: I bought coffee and cakes for the whole team after the client meeting, so how can I get the money back from the company? B: Just give the receipt to Linda in the accounting department before Friday, and she will add the amount to your salary at the end of the month.","t":"A：客戶會議之後我替整個團隊買了咖啡和蛋糕，我要怎麼向公司拿回這筆錢？ B：只要在週五前把【收據】交給會計部的琳達，她會在月底把金額加到你的薪水裡。"},{"w":"tip","p":"n.","d":"extra money you give to a waiter or driver to thank them","c":"小費","s":"A: The service at the restaurant last night was excellent, and the waiter even helped our guests call a taxi, so how much extra should we pay? B: In this country people usually leave a tip of about fifteen percent of the bill, but since he was so helpful, I think twenty percent would be fair.","t":"A：昨晚餐廳的服務非常好，服務生甚至幫我們的客人叫計程車，我們應該多付多少錢？ B：在這個國家，人們通常會留下帳單約百分之十五的【小費】，不過既然他那麼熱心幫忙，我想百分之二十比較合理。"},{"w":"music","p":"n.","d":"sounds such as songs that people play or sing","c":"音樂","s":"A: Some customers have complained that it's hard to have a conversation in our café during the afternoon, so do you know what the problem is? B: I think the background music is too loud, especially the rock songs the new staff like to play, so we should choose softer jazz and turn the volume down.","t":"A：有些顧客抱怨下午在我們咖啡店很難交談，你知道問題出在哪裡嗎？ B：我覺得背景【音樂】太大聲了，尤其是新員工喜歡放的搖滾歌曲，所以我們應該選擇比較柔和的爵士樂，並把音量調低。"},{"w":"interior","p":"n.","d":"the inside part of a building or room and its design","c":"內部；室內裝潢","s":"A: The new café on Park Road has become very popular on social media in just a few weeks, so what makes it so special? B: The interior was designed by a famous architect, with green plants, wooden walls and large windows, so customers love taking photos and sharing them online with their friends.","t":"A：公園路上那家新咖啡店短短幾週就在社群媒體上大受歡迎，它有什麼特別之處？ B：它的【室內裝潢】是由一位知名建築師設計的，有綠色植物、木頭牆面和大窗戶，所以顧客很喜歡拍照並上網分享給朋友。"},{"w":"local","p":"adj.","d":"from or in the area near you","c":"在地的；當地的","s":"A: Our company wants to choose a coffee supplier for the new office kitchen, so should we use the big international brand we had before? B: I'd prefer a local roaster from our own neighborhood, because the beans are fresher, the prices are similar, and we can support small businesses in our community.","t":"A：公司想為新辦公室的茶水間挑選咖啡供應商，我們應該用之前那個國際大品牌嗎？ B：我比較想選我們附近社區的【在地】烘豆商，因為咖啡豆比較新鮮、價格差不多，而且我們還能支持社區裡的小型企業。"}]},{"unit":42,"theme":"Cake 蛋糕","cards":[{"w":"slice","p":"n.","d":"a thin flat piece cut from something like cake or bread","c":"一片；一塊","s":"A: The client meeting starts at three, and Mr. Lee asked for some light refreshments, so how much of the lemon cake should I bring to the conference room? B: Please cut it so that each of the twelve visitors can have one small slice, and put the rest in the staff kitchen for our team to enjoy later.","t":"A：客戶會議三點開始，李先生要求準備一些簡單的茶點，所以我該帶多少檸檬蛋糕到會議室？ B：請把它切好，讓十二位訪客每人都能拿到一小【片】，剩下的放到員工廚房，讓我們團隊晚點享用。"},{"w":"bake","p":"v.","d":"to cook food such as bread or cake in an oven","c":"烘烤","s":"A: Our café has received an order for fifty cupcakes for a company party on Saturday morning, so do you think we can finish them in time? B: If we start early on Friday afternoon and bake them in two batches, they will be ready, cooled, and packed before the delivery driver arrives.","t":"A：我們咖啡館接到一筆訂單，要為週六早上的公司派對準備五十個杯子蛋糕，你覺得我們來得及完成嗎？ B：如果我們週五下午早點開始，分兩批【烘烤】，它們就能在送貨司機抵達前烤好、放涼並包裝完成。"},{"w":"oven","p":"n.","d":"a box-shaped machine that heats food so you can bake or cook it","c":"烤箱","s":"A: The cakes in the bakery came out burned on one side again this morning, and two customers complained, so what do you think is causing the problem? B: I believe the old oven is not heating evenly anymore, so I have already asked the manager to call a technician and get a quote for a new one.","t":"A：今天早上麵包店的蛋糕又有一邊烤焦了，還有兩位客人抱怨，你覺得是什麼原因造成的？ B：我認為那台舊【烤箱】已經無法均勻加熱了，所以我已經請經理打電話找技師來，並請他們報價換一台新的。"},{"w":"flour","p":"n.","d":"a white powder made from wheat, used to make bread and cakes","c":"麵粉","s":"A: The supplier just called to say that our delivery of baking ingredients will be two days late because of the storm, so can we still make the wedding cake? B: We only have half a bag of flour left in the storeroom, so I will buy a few more kilograms from the supermarket on my way back from lunch.","t":"A：供應商剛打電話來說，因為暴風雨，我們的烘焙材料要晚兩天才會送到，那我們還能做婚禮蛋糕嗎？ B：儲藏室裡只剩下半袋【麵粉】了，所以我午餐回來的路上會去超市再多買幾公斤。"},{"w":"sugar","p":"n.","d":"a sweet white or brown substance added to food and drinks","c":"糖","s":"A: Several of our older customers have asked whether we could offer healthier desserts, so do you have any ideas for changing our popular carrot cake? B: We could use less sugar and add more fresh fruit and nuts instead, which would keep the flavor pleasant while making the cake better for people who watch their diet.","t":"A：好幾位年長的顧客問我們能不能提供更健康的甜點，你對改良我們那款熱賣的胡蘿蔔蛋糕有什麼想法嗎？ B：我們可以少放一點【糖】，改加更多新鮮水果和堅果，這樣既能保持好吃的味道，也讓蛋糕更適合注重飲食的人。"},{"w":"butter","p":"n.","d":"a soft yellow food made from milk, used in cooking and baking","c":"奶油；牛油","s":"A: The head baker said the new pound cakes taste a little dry and plain compared with last month's, so did something change in the kitchen? B: Yes, the purchasing department switched to a cheaper brand of butter to save money, but I think we should go back to the old one because quality matters more to our customers.","t":"A：首席烘焙師說新的磅蛋糕吃起來比上個月的稍微乾又平淡，廚房裡有什麼改變嗎？ B：是的，採購部門為了省錢改用比較便宜的【奶油】品牌，但我認為我們應該換回原來的，因為品質對顧客來說更重要。"},{"w":"egg","p":"n.","d":"a round object laid by a hen, used as food and in baking","c":"蛋；雞蛋","s":"A: I am preparing the shopping list for tomorrow's baking class at the community center, so how many ingredients will each of the twenty students need? B: Every student needs one fresh egg, two cups of flour, and a small bowl of milk, so please buy a few extra in case someone drops something on the floor.","t":"A：我正在為明天社區中心的烘焙課準備購物清單，二十位學員每人需要多少材料？ B：每位學員需要一顆新鮮的【蛋】、兩杯麵粉和一小碗牛奶，所以請多買一些，以防有人把東西掉到地上。"},{"w":"icing","p":"n.","d":"a sweet mixture of sugar and water or butter used to cover or decorate cakes","c":"糖霜","s":"A: The marketing team wants the company logo to appear on top of the anniversary cake for Friday's event, so is that something your bakery can do? B: Certainly, our designer can draw the logo in blue and white icing on a smooth surface, but we need the image file by Wednesday so that we have time to practice.","t":"A：行銷團隊希望週五活動的週年蛋糕上能有公司標誌，你們麵包店做得到嗎？ B：當然可以，我們的設計師可以在平滑的表面上用藍白兩色的【糖霜】畫出標誌，不過我們需要在週三前拿到圖檔，才有時間練習。"},{"w":"frosting","p":"n.","d":"a thick, soft, sweet mixture spread on cakes and cupcakes","c":"（蛋糕上的）糖霜；奶油霜","s":"A: The children's hospital asked us to provide cupcakes for their holiday party next week, so what kind of decoration do you think the kids would like? B: I suggest a thick layer of pink and green frosting with colorful sprinkles on top, because it looks cheerful and is easy for young children to eat with their hands.","t":"A：兒童醫院請我們為下週的節日派對提供杯子蛋糕，你覺得孩子們會喜歡什麼樣的裝飾？ B：我建議塗上一層厚厚的粉紅色和綠色【糖霜】，上面撒上彩色糖粒，因為看起來很歡樂，而且小孩用手拿著吃也很方便。"},{"w":"cream","p":"n.","d":"the thick fatty part of milk, often whipped and put on desserts","c":"鮮奶油","s":"A: The strawberry cakes we sent to the hotel yesterday were not as fresh as usual, and the event planner was quite unhappy, so what went wrong? B: The delivery van's cooling system broke down during the trip, so the whipped cream melted in the heat, and we have offered the hotel a full refund and a free replacement.","t":"A：我們昨天送到飯店的草莓蛋糕不像平常那麼新鮮，活動策劃人相當不滿，到底出了什麼問題？ B：送貨車的冷藏系統在途中故障了，所以打發的【鮮奶油】在高溫下融化了，我們已經向飯店提出全額退款並免費補送。"},{"w":"chocolate","p":"n.","d":"a sweet brown food made from cocoa beans","c":"巧克力","s":"A: We are choosing a cake for the sales department's farewell party for Ms. Chen, so do you know what flavor she likes best? B: Her assistant told me that she loves dark chocolate more than anything else, so let's order a rich, bitter cake with fresh berries from the bakery near the train station.","t":"A：我們正在為業務部替陳小姐舉辦的歡送會挑選蛋糕，你知道她最喜歡什麼口味嗎？ B：她的助理告訴我，她最愛黑【巧克力】，所以我們就向火車站附近的麵包店訂一個濃郁微苦、配上新鮮莓果的蛋糕吧。"},{"w":"vanilla","p":"n.","d":"a sweet flavor that comes from the seeds of a tropical plant","c":"香草","s":"A: A customer is planning a small office party for forty people and cannot decide which flavor will please everyone, so what should I recommend to her? B: Tell her that classic vanilla is the safest choice because almost everyone enjoys it, and she can add fresh fruit on top if she wants something more colorful.","t":"A：一位顧客正在籌劃一場四十人的小型辦公室派對，無法決定哪種口味能讓大家都滿意，我該推薦她什麼？ B：告訴她經典的【香草】口味是最保險的選擇，因為幾乎每個人都喜歡，如果她想要更繽紛一點，也可以在上面加些新鮮水果。"},{"w":"dessert","p":"n.","d":"sweet food eaten at the end of a meal","c":"甜點","s":"A: The restaurant manager wants to attract more business lunch customers on weekdays, so do you have any suggestions for the new set menu? B: We could include a small dessert, such as a piece of cheesecake or a fruit tart, with every main course, because office workers love having something sweet after a busy morning.","t":"A：餐廳經理想在平日吸引更多商務午餐客人，你對新的套餐菜單有什麼建議嗎？ B：我們可以在每份主餐附上一份小【甜點】，例如一塊起司蛋糕或水果塔，因為上班族在忙碌的早上之後很喜歡吃點甜的。"},{"w":"recipe","p":"n.","d":"a set of instructions for cooking a dish, with a list of ingredients","c":"食譜","s":"A: Our new pastry chef from Paris will start next Monday, so should we ask her to follow the instructions we have always used for our famous apple cake? B: Yes, please give her a printed copy of the recipe on her first day, because customers expect the taste to stay exactly the same as it has been for years.","t":"A：我們從巴黎來的新甜點師下週一開始上班，我們要請她照著我們一直以來做招牌蘋果蛋糕的做法嗎？ B：是的，請在她上班第一天給她一份印好的【食譜】，因為顧客期待味道和多年來完全一樣。"},{"w":"layer","p":"n.","d":"one level of something that lies on top of another","c":"層","s":"A: The bride and groom want a tall, impressive wedding cake for their reception at the hotel, so how big do you think it should be for two hundred guests? B: I recommend four round levels stacked on top of each other, and each layer can have a different flavor so that guests with different tastes will all find something they enjoy.","t":"A：新郎新娘想在飯店喜宴上擺一個高大氣派的結婚蛋糕，你覺得兩百位賓客需要多大的蛋糕？ B：我建議堆疊四層圓形蛋糕，每一【層】可以有不同口味，這樣口味不同的賓客都能找到喜歡的。"},{"w":"decorate","p":"v.","d":"to add things to something to make it look more attractive","c":"裝飾","s":"A: The office manager wants to surprise the team with a cake for reaching our sales target this quarter, so could your shop add something special to it? B: Of course, our staff can decorate it with fresh flowers, gold letters, and small sugar stars, and we can deliver it to your building before the afternoon meeting starts.","t":"A：辦公室經理想用蛋糕給達成本季業績目標的團隊一個驚喜，你們店能在上面加點特別的東西嗎？ B：當然可以，我們的員工可以用鮮花、金色字母和小糖星星來【裝飾】它，還能在下午會議開始前送到你們大樓。"},{"w":"topping","p":"n.","d":"food put on top of a dish, such as fruit, nuts or sauce","c":"（食物上的）配料","s":"A: Our café is creating a new cheesecake for the summer menu, and the owner wants it to look bright and fresh in photos, so what do you suggest? B: We could add a topping of mango, kiwi, and blueberries, because the colorful fruit will look great on social media and taste refreshing on hot days.","t":"A：我們咖啡館正在為夏季菜單研發新的起司蛋糕，老闆希望它拍照時看起來明亮清新，你有什麼建議？ B：我們可以加上芒果、奇異果和藍莓的【配料】，因為色彩繽紛的水果在社群媒體上看起來很棒，而且在炎熱的日子吃起來也很清爽。"},{"w":"candle","p":"n.","d":"a stick of wax with a string in the middle that you burn for light","c":"蠟燭","s":"A: Everything is ready for Mr. Wang's retirement party in the meeting room, but the lights are still on, so when should we bring in the cake? B: Turn off the lights first, and then I will carry it in slowly with one tall candle burning in the middle while everyone starts to sing and clap.","t":"A：王先生退休派對在會議室都準備好了，但燈還亮著，我們應該什麼時候把蛋糕拿進來？ B：先把燈關掉，然後我會端著中間點著一根高【蠟燭】的蛋糕慢慢走進來，同時大家開始唱歌拍手。"},{"w":"birthday","p":"n.","d":"the day each year when a person was born","c":"生日","s":"A: I noticed that Ms. Park from the accounting department has been working late every night this month, so is there anything special happening next week? B: Yes, her birthday is next Thursday, so the team is planning to order a small cake and have a short party in the break room during lunch.","t":"A：我注意到會計部的朴小姐這個月每晚都加班，下週有什麼特別的事嗎？ B：有啊，下週四是她的【生日】，所以團隊打算訂一個小蛋糕，午餐時間在休息室辦個簡短的派對。"},{"w":"sweet","p":"adj.","d":"tasting of sugar or honey","c":"甜的","s":"A: Some guests at yesterday's conference said the chocolate cake was delicious, but a few others left most of it on their plates, so did they say why? B: They felt it was too sweet for them after a heavy lunch, so next time we should choose a lighter dessert with less sugar and more fruit.","t":"A：昨天研討會上有些來賓說巧克力蛋糕很好吃，但也有幾位把大部分都剩在盤子裡，他們有說為什麼嗎？ B：他們覺得吃完豐盛的午餐後，那個蛋糕對他們來說太【甜】了，所以下次我們應該選擇少糖、多水果的清爽甜點。"},{"w":"moist","p":"adj.","d":"slightly wet in a pleasant way; not dry","c":"濕潤的","s":"A: Our online reviews have improved a lot since we hired the new baker in March, so what do customers say they like most about our cakes now? B: Many people write that the cakes are soft and moist inside, not dry like before, because she adds yogurt to the batter and never leaves them in the oven too long.","t":"A：自從三月聘請新烘焙師之後，我們的網路評價改善很多，顧客現在說他們最喜歡我們蛋糕的哪一點？ B：很多人寫說蛋糕裡面鬆軟又【濕潤】，不像以前那樣乾，因為她在麵糊裡加了優格，而且從不讓蛋糕在烤箱裡烤太久。"},{"w":"fluffy","p":"adj.","d":"soft and light, with a lot of air inside","c":"蓬鬆的","s":"A: The Japanese cheesecake we sell is one of our best products, and a reporter wants to know what makes it so popular, so what should I tell her? B: Tell her that the cake is light and fluffy, almost like a cloud, because our bakers beat the egg whites carefully by hand for more than ten minutes.","t":"A：我們賣的日式起司蛋糕是最暢銷的產品之一，有位記者想知道它為什麼這麼受歡迎，我該怎麼告訴她？ B：告訴她這款蛋糕輕盈又【蓬鬆】，幾乎像雲朵一樣，因為我們的烘焙師會用手仔細打發蛋白超過十分鐘。"},{"w":"rich","p":"adj.","d":"(of food) containing a lot of butter, cream, sugar or chocolate, with a strong taste","c":"（食物）濃郁的","s":"A: The hotel's head chef wants a dessert for the formal dinner that will impress the company directors, so which cake do you recommend? B: I recommend our dark chocolate cake because it has a deep, rich flavor, and a small piece is enough to satisfy guests after a large meal of several courses.","t":"A：飯店主廚想為正式晚宴準備一道能讓公司董事們印象深刻的甜點，你推薦哪款蛋糕？ B：我推薦我們的黑巧克力蛋糕，因為它的味道深沉又【濃郁】，在吃完好幾道菜的豐盛晚餐後，一小塊就足以讓客人滿足。"},{"w":"sponge","p":"n.","d":"a light, soft cake made with eggs, sugar and flour","c":"海綿蛋糕","s":"A: A customer would like a simple, light cake for her grandmother, who does not enjoy heavy cream or chocolate, so what can we offer her? B: We can make a plain sponge with a little lemon juice and powdered sugar on top, which is soft, easy to eat, and not too heavy for older people.","t":"A：一位顧客想為不喜歡厚重鮮奶油或巧克力的奶奶買一個簡單清爽的蛋糕，我們可以提供什麼？ B：我們可以做一個原味【海綿蛋糕】，上面淋一點檸檬汁、撒上糖粉，口感柔軟、容易入口，對長輩來說也不會太膩。"},{"w":"fill","p":"v.","d":"to put something inside until it is full","c":"填滿；填入","s":"A: The new cream puffs on our menu look beautiful, but some customers said the inside was almost empty, so how can we fix this problem quickly? B: From now on, the kitchen staff should fill each one completely with custard before it goes on display, and a supervisor will check a few every morning.","t":"A：菜單上新推出的泡芙看起來很漂亮，但有些顧客說裡面幾乎是空的，我們要怎麼迅速解決這個問題？ B：從現在起，廚房員工應該在陳列前把每一個都用卡士達醬完全【填滿】，而且主管每天早上會抽查幾個。"},{"w":"mix","p":"v.","d":"to combine two or more things so they become one","c":"混合；攪拌","s":"A: This is my first week working in the bakery, and I want to make sure I do everything correctly, so what is the most important step for making the muffins? B: You should mix the dry ingredients and the wet ingredients gently for only about one minute, because if you stir too much, the muffins will become hard and heavy.","t":"A：這是我在麵包店工作的第一週，我想確保每件事都做對，做馬芬最重要的步驟是什麼？ B：你應該把乾性材料和濕性材料輕輕【混合】大約一分鐘就好，因為攪拌太久的話，馬芬會變得又硬又紮實。"},{"w":"batter","p":"n.","d":"a liquid mixture of flour, eggs and milk used to make cakes","c":"麵糊","s":"A: The cakes from this morning did not rise properly in the oven, and they look flat and heavy, so do you know what might have happened? B: I think the new assistant forgot to add baking powder when he prepared the batter, so I will show him the correct steps again before the lunch rush begins.","t":"A：今天早上的蛋糕在烤箱裡沒有好好膨脹，看起來又扁又紮實，你知道可能發生了什麼事嗎？ B：我想新來的助手在準備【麵糊】時忘了加泡打粉，所以我會在午餐尖峰時段開始前再教他一次正確步驟。"},{"w":"serve","p":"v.","d":"to give food or drinks to people at a meal","c":"供應；端上（食物）","s":"A: The guests at the awards dinner have almost finished their main course, and the speeches will begin in twenty minutes, so when should the waiters bring out the cake? B: Please ask them to serve it right after the last speech, together with coffee and tea, so that people can relax and chat while they eat.","t":"A：頒獎晚宴的來賓主餐快吃完了，致詞將在二十分鐘後開始，服務生應該什麼時候把蛋糕端出來？ B：請他們在最後一位致詞結束後馬上【端上】蛋糕，搭配咖啡和茶，讓大家可以邊吃邊放鬆聊天。"},{"w":"celebration","p":"n.","d":"a special event or party held because something good has happened","c":"慶祝；慶祝活動","s":"A: Our company has just won the biggest contract in its history, and the CEO wants to thank everyone who worked so hard on it, so what is the plan? B: She is organizing a big celebration in the hotel ballroom next Friday evening, with a buffet dinner, live music, and a huge cake with the client's logo on it.","t":"A：我們公司剛贏得史上最大的合約，執行長想感謝所有為此努力的人，有什麼計畫？ B：她下週五晚上要在飯店宴會廳舉辦一場盛大的【慶祝活動】，有自助晚餐、現場音樂，還有一個印著客戶標誌的巨型蛋糕。"}]},{"unit":43,"theme":"Cancellation 取消","cards":[{"w":"cancel","p":"v.","d":"to decide that a planned event or booking will not happen","c":"取消","s":"A: The airline just sent a message saying that heavy snow is expected in Chicago tomorrow morning, so what should we do about our sales trip? B: I think we should cancel the flights today and book a video call with the clients instead, because the roads will probably be dangerous anyway.","t":"A：航空公司剛傳訊息說明天早上芝加哥預計會下大雪，那我們的業務出差該怎麼辦？ B：我覺得我們今天就應該【取消】航班，改和客戶約視訊會議，因為路況可能也會很危險。"},{"w":"postpone","p":"v.","d":"to move an event to a later time","c":"延後；延期","s":"A: Half of the marketing team is still sick with the flu this week, so are we going to hold the product launch meeting on Thursday as planned? B: No, the manager decided to postpone it until next Monday, when everyone should be back in the office and ready to share their ideas.","t":"A：行銷團隊有一半的人這週還在感冒生病，我們還要照原計畫在星期四開產品發表會議嗎？ B：不，經理決定把它【延後】到下週一，到時候大家應該都回到辦公室，準備好分享想法了。"},{"w":"delay","p":"v.","d":"to make something happen later than planned","c":"延誤；耽擱","s":"A: The new office furniture was supposed to arrive this morning, but the warehouse is still empty, so did the supplier explain what happened? B: Yes, they said a problem at the port will delay the shipment by about three days, so we will have to use the old desks until Friday.","t":"A：新的辦公家具原本應該今天早上送到，但倉庫還是空的，供應商有解釋發生什麼事嗎？ B：有，他們說港口的問題會使貨運【延誤】大約三天，所以我們得用舊桌子用到星期五。"},{"w":"reschedule","p":"v.","d":"to change the time or date of a planned event","c":"重新安排時間","s":"A: I just realized that my dentist appointment on Wednesday afternoon is at the same time as the budget review with the finance department, so what should I do? B: Just call the clinic and ask them to reschedule it for another day, because the budget review is much more important for your project.","t":"A：我剛發現我星期三下午的牙醫預約和財務部的預算審查撞期了，我該怎麼辦？ B：打電話給診所，請他們把預約【重新安排】到別天就好，因為預算審查對你的專案重要得多。"},{"w":"call off","p":"v.phr.","d":"to decide that a planned event will not take place","c":"取消（活動等）","s":"A: The weather report says a strong typhoon will hit the coast on Saturday, so is the company still having its annual beach picnic for employees and their families? B: Unfortunately, the organizers had to call off the whole event this afternoon, but they promised to choose a new date in November when the weather is better.","t":"A：氣象報告說週六會有強颱登陸沿海，公司還要為員工和家屬舉辦年度海灘野餐嗎？ B：很遺憾，主辦人今天下午不得不【取消】整個活動，但他們承諾會在天氣比較好的十一月另選日期。"},{"w":"withdraw","p":"v.","d":"to stop taking part in something; to take back an offer","c":"退出；撤回","s":"A: I heard that one of the biggest companies in the city was planning to join our trade fair next month, so is that still true? B: Sadly, they decided to withdraw from the fair yesterday because their new products will not be ready in time, so we now have an empty booth near the entrance.","t":"A：我聽說市內一家大公司下個月打算參加我們的商展，現在還是這樣嗎？ B：很可惜，他們昨天決定【退出】商展，因為他們的新產品來不及準備好，所以入口附近現在空出一個攤位。"},{"w":"termination","p":"n.","d":"the act of ending something, such as a contract or a job","c":"終止；結束","s":"A: Our cleaning company has been missing several visits every month, and the office looks terrible, so can we simply stop working with them? B: Yes, but the contract says we must send a written letter of termination at least thirty days in advance, so I will prepare it and ask the director to sign it today.","t":"A：我們的清潔公司每個月都缺好幾次，辦公室看起來很糟，我們可以直接不跟他們合作嗎？ B：可以，但合約規定我們必須至少提前三十天寄出書面的【終止】合作通知信，所以我會準備好，今天請主任簽名。"},{"w":"suspension","p":"n.","d":"a short stop of a service or activity","c":"暫停；中止","s":"A: Why are so many passengers standing outside the train station looking at their phones and trying to find taxis this morning? B: There was a power failure on the main line, so the railway company announced a suspension of all services until noon, and many people are worried about being late for work.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上這麼多乘客站在火車站外面看手機、想找計程車？ B：主線發生停電，所以鐵路公司宣布所有班次【暫停】到中午，很多人擔心上班會遲到。"},{"w":"abandon","p":"v.","d":"to stop doing a plan or activity before it is finished","c":"放棄；中止","s":"A: The research team spent almost two years developing that new smartphone app, so why did it never appear in the online store? B: After testing it with customers, the company found that very few people wanted it, so they decided to abandon the project and spend the money on improving their popular products.","t":"A：研發團隊花了將近兩年開發那個新手機應用程式，為什麼它從來沒有出現在線上商店？ B：用客戶測試後，公司發現很少人想要它，所以他們決定【放棄】這個專案，把錢花在改進熱賣商品上。"},{"w":"revocation","p":"n.","d":"the official act of taking away a right or permit","c":"撤銷；吊銷","s":"A: I read in the newspaper that the restaurant near our office has suddenly closed, even though it was always busy at lunchtime, so what happened? B: Health inspectors found serious problems in the kitchen, which led to the revocation of its business license, and the owner cannot reopen until everything is fixed.","t":"A：我在報紙上看到我們辦公室附近那家餐廳突然關門了，雖然它午餐時間總是客滿，發生什麼事了？ B：衛生稽查員在廚房發現嚴重問題，導致它的營業執照被【撤銷】，老闆在一切改善之前都不能重新開業。"},{"w":"annul","p":"v.","d":"to officially say that an agreement or marriage is not legal","c":"宣告無效；廢除","s":"A: The two companies signed an agreement last spring, but now they are arguing about it in court, so what does the smaller company want? B: Its lawyers are asking the judge to annul the agreement completely, because they believe the other side gave them false information about the sales numbers before they signed it.","t":"A：這兩家公司去年春天簽了協議，但現在他們在法庭上爭執，比較小的那家公司想要什麼？ B：它的律師要求法官將這份協議完全【宣告無效】，因為他們認為對方在簽約前提供了不實的銷售數據。"},{"w":"void","p":"adj.","d":"not legal or not valid any more","c":"無效的","s":"A: I bought a ticket for the concert from a stranger on the internet, but the staff at the gate would not let me enter last night, so why not? B: They said the ticket was void because it had already been reported as stolen, so you should contact your bank and ask for help getting your money back.","t":"A：我在網路上跟陌生人買了一張演唱會門票，但昨晚門口的工作人員不讓我進去，為什麼？ B：他們說那張票是【無效的】，因為已經被通報為失竊票，所以你應該聯絡銀行，請他們幫忙把錢拿回來。"},{"w":"nullify","p":"v.","d":"to make something have no effect or value","c":"使無效；抵銷","s":"A: Our team worked very hard to reduce costs in the factory this year, so why are our total profits still lower than last year? B: The sharp rise in fuel prices this summer managed to nullify most of our savings, so the management is now looking for cheaper energy suppliers for next year.","t":"A：我們團隊今年很努力降低工廠成本，為什麼總利潤還是比去年低？ B：今年夏天燃料價格急遽上漲，【抵銷】了我們大部分節省下來的錢，所以管理層正在為明年尋找比較便宜的能源供應商。"},{"w":"refund","p":"n.","d":"money that is paid back to a customer","c":"退款","s":"A: The printer I ordered online for the office arrived with a broken screen, and it will not even turn on, so what should I do? B: Take some photos of the damage and send them to the store's customer service team, and they should give you a full refund within a week or send a new printer.","t":"A：我在網路上幫辦公室訂的印表機送來時螢幕是壞的，甚至開不了機，我該怎麼辦？ B：拍幾張損壞的照片寄給那家店的客服團隊，他們應該會在一週內給你全額【退款】或寄一台新的印表機。"},{"w":"charge","p":"n.","d":"the amount of money you must pay for something","c":"費用；收費","s":"A: I want to change my hotel booking from Friday to Saturday because my meeting in Tokyo was moved, so is that going to be a problem? B: The hotel allows changes, but there is an extra charge of twenty dollars if you do it less than forty-eight hours before arrival, so you should call them right away.","t":"A：我的東京會議改期了，我想把飯店訂房從星期五改到星期六，會有問題嗎？ B：飯店允許更改，但如果在抵達前四十八小時內更改，要額外收二十美元的【費用】，所以你應該馬上打電話給他們。"},{"w":"policy","p":"n.","d":"a set of rules that a company or group follows","c":"政策；規定","s":"A: A customer bought a jacket from our shop three months ago, and today she brought it back without a receipt, asking for her money, so can I accept it? B: I am sorry, but our store policy only allows returns within thirty days with a receipt, so please explain that politely and offer her a discount on something new.","t":"A：有位顧客三個月前在我們店裡買了一件外套，今天她沒帶收據拿回來要求退錢，我可以接受嗎？ B：很抱歉，我們店的【政策】只允許三十天內持收據退貨，所以請禮貌地向她解釋，並提供她購買新商品的折扣。"},{"w":"notice","p":"n.","d":"information or a warning given before something happens","c":"通知；預先通知","s":"A: The landlord told us yesterday that we have to move out of this office because he plans to sell the whole building, so how much time do we have? B: According to our rental agreement, he must give us at least two months' notice, so we have enough time to find a new place near the station.","t":"A：房東昨天告訴我們必須搬離這間辦公室，因為他打算賣掉整棟大樓，我們還有多少時間？ B：根據我們的租約，他必須至少提前兩個月【通知】我們，所以我們有足夠時間在車站附近找新地方。"},{"w":"deadline","p":"n.","d":"the latest time by which something must be done","c":"截止期限","s":"A: If our guests want to stay at the conference hotel but change their plans later, when do they need to tell the hotel so they do not lose money? B: The deadline for free changes is next Friday at five o'clock, so please remind everyone in your department to check their travel plans before then.","t":"A：如果我們的客人想住會議飯店但之後改變計畫，他們需要什麼時候告訴飯店才不會損失金錢？ B：免費更改的【截止期限】是下週五五點，所以請提醒你部門的每個人在那之前確認行程。"},{"w":"penalty","p":"n.","d":"money you must pay for breaking a rule or agreement","c":"罰金；違約金","s":"A: I need to end my phone contract six months early because the company is giving me a new work phone with free service, so is that expensive? B: Yes, the phone company asks for a penalty of about one hundred dollars for leaving early, but the free work phone will save you more than that by the end of the year.","t":"A：公司要給我一支免費通話的新公務手機，所以我得提前六個月終止手機合約，這樣會很貴嗎？ B：會，電信公司對提前解約會收大約一百美元的【違約金】，但到年底時，這支免費的公務手機幫你省下的錢會更多。"},{"w":"fee","p":"n.","d":"money paid for a service or to join something","c":"費用","s":"A: Our department wants to join the international business conference in Singapore next spring, but we have not decided yet, so when should we register? B: If we sign up before the end of this month, the registration fee is only two hundred dollars per person, but it will double in January, so we should decide soon.","t":"A：我們部門想參加明年春天在新加坡舉辦的國際商務會議，但還沒決定，應該什麼時候報名？ B：如果在這個月底前報名，每人報名【費】只要兩百美元，但一月起會翻倍，所以我們應該盡快決定。"},{"w":"unexpected","p":"adj.","d":"not expected; surprising","c":"意料之外的；意外的","s":"A: The sales report looked great on Monday, so why did the manager call an emergency meeting this morning and look so worried? B: There was a completely unexpected problem with our biggest customer, who suddenly said they could not pay their bill this month, and nobody in the company had seen it coming.","t":"A：星期一的銷售報告看起來很好，為什麼經理今天早上召開緊急會議，而且看起來那麼擔心？ B：我們最大的客戶出了一個完全【意料之外的】問題，他們突然說這個月付不出帳款，公司裡沒有人預料到。"},{"w":"sudden","p":"adj.","d":"happening very quickly and without warning","c":"突然的","s":"A: Why did the outdoor concert in the city park end so early last night, when the band had only played three songs? B: A sudden storm with strong wind and heavy rain arrived without any warning, so the organizers stopped the show and asked everyone to go to the nearby shopping mall for safety.","t":"A：昨晚市立公園的戶外音樂會為什麼那麼早就結束了，樂團才唱了三首歌？ B：一場夾帶強風豪雨的【突如其來的】暴風雨毫無預警地來襲，所以主辦單位停止演出，請大家到附近的購物中心避難。"},{"w":"official","p":"adj.","d":"approved by or coming from a government or organization","c":"正式的；官方的","s":"A: Everyone is saying that the summer music festival will not happen this year because of the new road construction, so is it really true? B: I have heard the same thing from friends, but we should wait for the official announcement from the city government before we cancel our hotel rooms and train tickets.","t":"A：大家都在說今年的夏季音樂節因為新的道路工程不會舉辦，這是真的嗎？ B：我也從朋友那裡聽說了，但我們應該等市政府的【正式】公告，再取消飯店房間和火車票。"},{"w":"notify","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone officially about something","c":"通知","s":"A: The water company plans to repair the pipes in our building next Tuesday, and there will be no water from nine to three, so what should we do? B: Please send an email to notify all the staff today, so they can bring bottled water and plan their lunch breaks outside the office.","t":"A：自來水公司下週二要修理我們大樓的水管，九點到三點會停水，我們該怎麼做？ B：請今天寄電子郵件【通知】全體員工，這樣他們可以帶瓶裝水，並計畫到辦公室外面吃午餐。"},{"w":"confirm","p":"v.","d":"to say or show that a plan or booking is definite","c":"確認","s":"A: I booked a table for twelve people at the Italian restaurant for our team dinner on Friday night, so is there anything else I need to do? B: Yes, the restaurant asked us to call on Thursday to confirm the reservation, or they may give the table to other customers because Friday nights are very busy.","t":"A：我在義大利餐廳為週五晚上的團隊晚餐訂了十二人的位子，還有什麼需要做的嗎？ B：有，餐廳要求我們星期四打電話【確認】訂位，否則他們可能會把桌子給其他客人，因為週五晚上很忙。"},{"w":"disruption","p":"n.","d":"a problem that stops something from working normally","c":"中斷；干擾","s":"A: The city is going to repair the main bridge downtown for the next three weeks, so how will that affect our delivery drivers? B: There will be some disruption to traffic during rush hour, so the drivers should leave earlier in the morning and take the highway to reach our customers on time.","t":"A：市政府接下來三週要修理市中心的主要橋梁，這會對我們的送貨司機有什麼影響？ B：尖峰時段交通會受到一些【干擾】，所以司機早上應該早點出發，走高速公路才能準時送達客戶。"},{"w":"alternative","p":"n.","d":"another choice you can use instead","c":"替代方案；其他選擇","s":"A: Our flight to Hong Kong was cancelled because of the typhoon, and the airline says the next available seats are on Thursday, so what can we do? B: One good alternative is to take the high-speed train to another city and fly from there tomorrow, which means we can still attend the meeting.","t":"A：我們飛往香港的班機因颱風取消了，航空公司說下一個有位子的是星期四，我們能怎麼辦？ B：一個不錯的【替代方案】是搭高鐵到另一個城市，明天從那裡起飛，這樣我們還是能參加會議。"},{"w":"compensation","p":"n.","d":"money paid to someone because of a loss or problem","c":"賠償；補償","s":"A: The airline kept us waiting at the gate for more than seven hours without any food, and we missed an important business dinner, so can we ask for something? B: Yes, under the new travel rules you can apply for compensation on their website, and they may pay you up to three hundred dollars for the long wait.","t":"A：航空公司讓我們在登機門等了七個多小時，而且沒有提供任何食物，我們也錯過了重要的商務晚餐，我們可以要求什麼嗎？ B：可以，根據新的旅遊規定，你可以在他們的網站上申請【賠償】，他們可能會因為長時間等候付你最多三百美元。"},{"w":"reinstate","p":"v.","d":"to bring back a service, rule or person to an earlier position","c":"恢復；使復職","s":"A: Many customers complained after the bus company stopped the late-night service from the airport last year, so has anything changed since then? B: Yes, the company has agreed to reinstate the service starting next month, so travelers arriving on evening flights will be able to get home cheaply again.","t":"A：去年公車公司停駛機場深夜班次後，很多乘客抱怨，從那之後有任何改變嗎？ B：有，公司已同意從下個月起【恢復】這項服務，所以搭晚班飛機抵達的旅客又能便宜地回家了。"}]},{"unit":44,"theme":"Car 汽車","cards":[{"w":"vehicle","p":"n.","d":"a machine such as a car, bus or truck that carries people or goods","c":"車輛","s":"A: Our sales team will visit five clients in the countryside next week, and the roads there are narrow and muddy, so which company car should we book? B: I suggest the large vehicle with four-wheel drive, because it can carry all six of us and our sample boxes without any trouble on those rough mountain roads.","t":"A：我們業務團隊下週要拜訪鄉下的五位客戶，那裡的道路又窄又泥濘，我們該預訂哪一輛公司車？ B：我建議那台四輪驅動的大型【車輛】，因為它可以載我們六個人和樣品箱，在崎嶇的山路上也不會有任何問題。"},{"w":"engine","p":"n.","d":"the part of a car that makes the power to move it","c":"引擎","s":"A: The delivery van made a loud knocking noise this morning when I started it, and then it stopped twice on the highway, so what do you think is wrong? B: The mechanic checked it at lunchtime and said the engine is overheating because it has not had fresh oil for almost a year.","t":"A：今天早上我發動送貨車時它發出很大的敲擊聲，接著在高速公路上熄火了兩次，你覺得是哪裡出了問題？ B：技師午餐時間檢查過了，他說【引擎】過熱，因為它將近一年沒換新機油了。"},{"w":"fuel","p":"n.","d":"something such as gas or oil that is burned to give power","c":"燃料","s":"A: The trip to the trade fair in Kaohsiung is about four hours by car, so how often do you think we will need to stop on the way? B: The tank holds enough fuel for around six hundred kilometers, so we should only need one short stop, and we can buy coffee and snacks at the same time.","t":"A：開車去高雄的商展大約要四個小時，你覺得我們路上需要停幾次？ B：油箱裡的【燃料】足夠跑大約六百公里，所以我們應該只需要短暫停一次，同時還可以買咖啡和點心。"},{"w":"petrol","p":"n.","d":"the British word for gasoline, the liquid fuel for cars","c":"汽油","s":"A: The company is paying for our travel expenses during the sales tour around the island, so do I need to keep every receipt from the gas station? B: Yes, please keep them all, because the accounting department will only pay you back for the petrol if you attach the original receipts to your expense report.","t":"A：公司會支付我們環島業務之旅的差旅費，那我需要保留加油站的每一張收據嗎？ B：是的，請全部保留，因為只有你在費用報告上附上收據正本，會計部才會退還你的【汽油】費用。"},{"w":"diesel","p":"n.","d":"a heavy fuel used in many trucks, buses and some cars","c":"柴油","s":"A: Our moving company is planning to replace the old trucks next year, so are you going to choose the same type of fuel as before or try something different? B: We will probably stay with diesel for the heavy trucks because it gives them more power on long trips, but the small vans may become fully electric.","t":"A：我們搬家公司打算明年汰換舊卡車，你們會選擇和以前一樣的燃料，還是嘗試不同的？ B：重型卡車我們可能會繼續用【柴油】，因為它在長途行駛時提供更大的動力，但小型廂型車可能會全面改為電動。"},{"w":"electric","p":"adj.","d":"using electricity for power","c":"電動的","s":"A: The city government is offering money to companies that reduce air pollution this year, so should we think about changing the vehicles we use for deliveries? B: That is a great idea, because an electric van does not need gasoline, it is much quieter in busy streets, and charging it overnight at the warehouse is quite cheap.","t":"A：市政府今年提供補助給減少空氣汙染的公司，我們是否該考慮更換送貨用的車輛？ B：這是個好主意，因為【電動】廂型車不需要汽油，在繁忙的街道上安靜得多，而且晚上在倉庫充電也相當便宜。"},{"w":"battery","p":"n.","d":"an object that stores electricity to start a car or run a machine","c":"電瓶；電池","s":"A: I tried to start my car in the parking lot after the late meeting last night, but nothing happened at all, even though the lights had been switched off. B: That usually means the battery is dead, so you should ask a coworker to help you with jump leads or call the roadside assistance number.","t":"A：昨晚開完很晚的會後，我在停車場想發動車子，但完全沒反應，雖然車燈都已經關掉了。 B：那通常表示【電瓶】沒電了，你應該請同事用救車線幫忙，或打道路救援電話。"},{"w":"brake","p":"v.","d":"to make a vehicle slow down or stop","c":"煞車","s":"A: When you were driving the company van down that steep hill in the rain yesterday afternoon, did you notice anything strange about how it handled the road? B: Yes, I had to brake much harder than usual to slow down before the traffic lights, so I think the pedals need to be checked as soon as possible.","t":"A：昨天下午你在雨中開公司廂型車下那個陡坡時，有沒有注意到車子的操控有什麼奇怪的地方？ B：有，我必須比平常更用力【煞車】才能在紅綠燈前減速，所以我認為踏板需要盡快檢查。"},{"w":"accelerate","p":"v.","d":"to make a vehicle go faster","c":"加速","s":"A: I am a little nervous about driving on the highway for the first time with my new job, so do you have any advice for joining the fast lane? B: When you enter from the ramp, you need to accelerate smoothly until you match the speed of the other cars, and always check your mirrors before you change lanes.","t":"A：新工作讓我第一次要開上高速公路，我有點緊張，你對切入快車道有什麼建議嗎？ B：從匝道進入時，你需要平穩地【加速】直到跟上其他車的速度，而且變換車道前一定要看後照鏡。"},{"w":"steer","p":"v.","d":"to control the direction a vehicle goes","c":"駕駛；操控方向","s":"A: The rental company gave us a very large van for moving the office furniture this weekend, and I have only ever driven small cars, so is it difficult? B: It is not too bad, but you must steer slowly and carefully around corners, because the back of the van needs much more space than you might expect.","t":"A：租車公司給了我們一台很大的廂型車，這週末用來搬辦公室家具，而我只開過小車，這會很難嗎？ B：還好，但轉彎時你必須慢慢地、小心地【操控方向】，因為廂型車的後半部需要的空間比你想像的多得多。"},{"w":"wheel","p":"n.","d":"one of the round parts under a car that turn so it can move","c":"車輪","s":"A: Why did the delivery driver arrive almost two hours late this afternoon when the customer had been waiting since lunch? B: He said a nail went through one of the front tires on the highway, so he had to stop at the side of the road and change the wheel by himself before he could continue.","t":"A：客戶從午餐時間就在等，為什麼送貨司機今天下午遲到將近兩個小時？ B：他說在高速公路上有根釘子刺穿了一個前輪胎，所以他得停在路邊自己換【車輪】才能繼續上路。"},{"w":"tire","p":"n.","d":"the rubber ring around a wheel that is filled with air","c":"輪胎","s":"A: The company minibus feels a bit unsteady when I drive it at high speed on the highway, and it seems to pull to the left, so what should I do? B: One tire probably does not have enough air in it, so stop at the next gas station and check the pressure on all four before you drive any further.","t":"A：我在高速公路上高速駕駛公司的小巴時感覺有點不穩，而且好像會往左偏，我該怎麼辦？ B：可能有一個【輪胎】氣不足，所以在下一個加油站停下來，四個都檢查胎壓後再繼續開。"},{"w":"seat","p":"n.","d":"a place where a person sits in a vehicle","c":"座位","s":"A: I am driving three clients from the airport to the hotel tonight, and one of them is quite tall, so how can I make the trip more pleasant for him? B: Offer him the front passenger seat, because it has the most room for his legs, and he can enjoy the view of the city lights on the way.","t":"A：我今晚要開車載三位客戶從機場到飯店，其中一位個子很高，我該怎麼讓他的車程更舒服？ B：讓他坐前面的副駕駛【座位】，因為那裡的腿部空間最大，而且他可以沿途欣賞城市的燈光。"},{"w":"seatbelt","p":"n.","d":"a belt in a car that holds you in your seat for safety","c":"安全帶","s":"A: Our new driving rules for staff say that everyone in a company car must follow certain safety steps, so what is the most important one? B: Before the car moves, the driver must make sure that every passenger, including those in the back, has fastened their seatbelt, because it can save lives in an accident.","t":"A：我們新的員工駕駛規定說，每個坐公司車的人都必須遵守某些安全步驟，最重要的是哪一個？ B：車子開動前，司機必須確認每位乘客，包括後座的人，都已經繫好【安全帶】，因為發生事故時它能救命。"},{"w":"dashboard","p":"n.","d":"the panel in front of the driver that shows speed, fuel and other information","c":"儀表板","s":"A: While I was driving to the branch office this morning, a small orange light suddenly came on in front of me, and I wasn't sure whether it was serious. B: If a warning light appears on the dashboard, you should check the owner's manual right away, because it might mean the engine oil is low.","t":"A：今天早上我開車去分公司時，面前突然亮起一個橘色小燈，我不確定是否嚴重。 B：如果【儀表板】上出現警示燈，你應該立刻查看車主手冊，因為那可能表示引擎機油不足。"},{"w":"mirror","p":"n.","d":"a piece of glass in a car that lets the driver see behind or beside","c":"後照鏡","s":"A: I almost hit a motorcycle when I was turning right into the hotel entrance yesterday, and I still feel shaken about it, so what went wrong? B: Before you turn or change lanes, always look in the side mirror and also turn your head, because motorcycles can hide in places you cannot easily see.","t":"A：我昨天右轉進飯店入口時差點撞到一台機車，到現在還心有餘悸，是哪裡出了錯？ B：轉彎或變換車道前，一定要看側邊【後照鏡】，也要轉頭確認，因為機車可能躲在你不容易看到的地方。"},{"w":"headlight","p":"n.","d":"one of the large lights at the front of a car","c":"車頭燈","s":"A: I have to drive back from the factory late tonight after the inspection, and the country road there has no street lamps at all, so is that dangerous? B: Just drive slowly, and before you leave, ask the security guard to check that each headlight is working, because you will need strong light to see the road clearly.","t":"A：今晚檢查完後我得很晚才從工廠開車回來，那裡的鄉間道路完全沒有路燈，這樣危險嗎？ B：慢慢開就好，出發前請警衛幫你確認每一個【車頭燈】都正常運作，因為你需要強光才能看清楚路面。"},{"w":"license","p":"n.","d":"an official card that shows you are allowed to drive","c":"執照；駕照","s":"A: We are hiring a new sales assistant who will often visit customers by car, so what documents should we ask the candidates to bring to the interview? B: Besides their résumé, they must bring a valid driver's license, and we should also ask how many years of driving experience they have on busy city roads.","t":"A：我們要招聘一位常需要開車拜訪客戶的新業務助理，應該請應徵者帶哪些文件來面試？ B：除了履歷，他們還必須帶有效的駕駛【執照】，我們也應該問他們在繁忙市區道路有幾年的駕駛經驗。"},{"w":"traffic","p":"n.","d":"the cars, buses and other vehicles moving on a road","c":"交通；車流","s":"A: The meeting with the investors starts at nine o'clock tomorrow morning in the city center, so what time should we leave the office to get there? B: Let's leave by seven thirty, because the traffic on the main road is always heavy during rush hour, and we don't want to arrive late and stressed.","t":"A：明天早上九點在市中心和投資人開會，我們該幾點離開辦公室才能到？ B：我們七點半前出發吧，因為尖峰時段主要道路上的【車流】總是很多，我們不想遲到又緊張兮兮地抵達。"},{"w":"parking","p":"n.","d":"space for leaving cars; the act of leaving a car somewhere for a time","c":"停車；停車位","s":"A: Many visitors are coming to our product launch at the convention center on Saturday, so how will they find a place to leave their cars? B: The center has free parking for up to three hundred cars behind the main hall, and we will put clear signs at the entrance to guide drivers there.","t":"A：週六會有很多訪客來會展中心參加我們的產品發表會，他們要怎麼找到地方放車？ B：會展中心主廳後方有可容納三百輛車的免費【停車位】，我們會在入口放置清楚的指標引導駕駛人過去。"},{"w":"garage","p":"n.","d":"a building where cars are kept or repaired","c":"車庫；修車廠","s":"A: The weather report says there will be a strong typhoon this weekend with heavy rain and wind, so where should we keep the company cars? B: Please move all of them into the underground garage below the office building on Friday evening, because branches and flying objects could easily damage them outside.","t":"A：氣象報告說這週末會有強烈颱風，伴隨大雨和強風，我們該把公司車放在哪裡？ B：請在週五傍晚把所有車都移到辦公大樓下方的地下【車庫】，因為在外面樹枝和飛落物很容易把它們弄壞。"},{"w":"service","p":"v.","d":"to check and fix a vehicle or machine regularly so it keeps working well","c":"保養；檢修","s":"A: Our delivery vans have traveled more than ten thousand kilometers since January, and two drivers say the brakes feel soft, so what should we do? B: We should service all of them at the dealer next week, so the mechanics can check the oil, the brakes and the tires before any real problems appear.","t":"A：我們的送貨車從一月以來已經跑了一萬多公里，有兩位司機說煞車感覺很軟，我們該怎麼辦？ B：我們下週應該把它們全部送到經銷商那裡【保養】，讓技師在真正出問題之前檢查機油、煞車和輪胎。"},{"w":"repair","p":"v.","d":"to fix something that is broken or damaged","c":"修理","s":"A: Someone backed into my car in the shopping mall parking lot on Sunday and broke the back door, so how long will it take to fix? B: The body shop told me they can repair the damage in about three days, and the insurance company will pay for most of the cost because the other driver admitted it.","t":"A：週日有人在購物中心停車場倒車撞到我的車，撞壞了後車門，要多久才能修好？ B：鈑金廠告訴我他們大約三天就能【修理】好損壞的地方，而且因為對方駕駛承認了，保險公司會支付大部分費用。"},{"w":"speed","p":"n.","d":"how fast something moves","c":"速度","s":"A: I got a ticket in the mail this morning for driving too fast near the school on my way to the office last month, and I'm very surprised. B: The speed limit on that street is only thirty kilometers per hour during school hours, and there is a camera hidden near the crossing.","t":"A：今天早上我收到一張罰單，是上個月上班途中在學校附近開太快，我非常驚訝。 B：那條街在上學時段的【速度】限制只有每小時三十公里，而且斑馬線附近藏了一台測速相機。"},{"w":"model","p":"n.","d":"a particular type or version of a product","c":"車款；型號","s":"A: The sales manager wants to replace her old company car with something more modern this year, so which car is she thinking about buying? B: She likes the latest model from the Japanese maker, because it has a bigger trunk for her samples, better fuel economy, and a smart system that connects to her phone.","t":"A：業務經理今年想把她的舊公司車換成更現代化的車，她考慮買哪一台？ B：她喜歡那家日本車廠的最新【車款】，因為它的後車廂更大可以放樣品、更省油，還有能連接手機的智慧系統。"},{"w":"used","p":"adj.","d":"owned by someone before; not new","c":"二手的","s":"A: Our small catering business needs a second van for weekend events, but we don't have a large budget this year, so what are our choices? B: We could buy a used van from a trusted dealer, because it costs about half the price of a brand-new one, and many come with a one-year warranty.","t":"A：我們的小型外燴公司週末活動需要第二台廂型車，但今年預算不多，我們有哪些選擇？ B：我們可以向信譽良好的車商買一台【二手】廂型車，因為價格大約是全新車的一半，而且很多附有一年保固。"},{"w":"new","p":"adj.","d":"recently made or bought; not used before","c":"新的","s":"A: I heard that the company finally replaced the old delivery trucks that kept breaking down last winter, so how do the drivers feel about it? B: They are very happy with the new trucks, which arrived straight from the factory last week, because they are quieter, cleaner and much more reliable on long trips.","t":"A：我聽說公司終於汰換了去年冬天一直故障的舊送貨卡車，司機們覺得怎麼樣？ B：他們對上週直接從工廠送來的【新】卡車非常滿意，因為它們更安靜、更乾淨，長途行駛也可靠得多。"},{"w":"safe","p":"adj.","d":"not likely to cause harm or danger","c":"安全的","s":"A: My elderly parents want to buy a car for their weekend trips to the countryside, and they asked me for advice, so what should they look for? B: They should choose a safe car with good airbags, automatic emergency braking and high test scores, because protecting the people inside matters more than style or speed.","t":"A：我年邁的父母想買一台車週末去鄉下玩，他們問我的意見，他們應該注意什麼？ B：他們應該選擇一台有良好安全氣囊、自動緊急煞車和高測試分數的【安全】車款，因為保護車內的人比外型或速度更重要。"},{"w":"comfortable","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel relaxed and physically pleasant","c":"舒適的","s":"A: The marketing team will drive six hours to the exhibition in Taichung and back on Friday, so which car should I reserve from the rental company? B: Please book the large sedan with soft leather seats and plenty of leg room, because it is much more comfortable for long trips than the small city car.","t":"A：行銷團隊週五要開六個小時的車往返台中的展覽，我該向租車公司預訂哪一台車？ B：請預訂那台有柔軟皮椅和寬敞腿部空間的大型轎車，因為長途旅行時它比小型城市車【舒適】得多。"}]},{"unit":45,"theme":"Career 職涯","cards":[{"w":"profession","p":"n.","d":"a type of job that needs special training or education","c":"職業；專業","s":"A: My niece is finishing her degree in health sciences next spring, but she still seems unsure about her future, so what advice did you give her at dinner last night? B: I told her that nursing is a respected profession with many chances to work abroad, and that hospitals in Taipei are always looking for caring, well-trained staff.","t":"A：我外甥女明年春天就要拿到健康科學學位了，但她似乎對未來還不確定，你昨晚吃飯時給了她什麼建議？ B：我告訴她護理是一個受人尊敬、有很多出國工作機會的【職業】，而且台北的醫院一直在找有愛心、受過良好訓練的人員。"},{"w":"occupation","p":"n.","d":"a person's job or regular work","c":"職業","s":"A: The bank's loan application asks for a lot of personal details, so what should I write in the box near the bottom of the second page? B: That box is for your occupation, so just write \"accountant,\" and then add the name of your company and how many years you have worked there.","t":"A：銀行的貸款申請表要填很多個人資料，第二頁底部附近的那一格我該寫什麼？ B：那一格是填你的【職業】，就寫「會計師」，然後再加上你公司的名稱以及你在那裡工作了幾年。"},{"w":"job","p":"n.","d":"work that you do regularly to earn money","c":"工作","s":"A: You looked really tired at the team meeting this morning, so is everything all right with your new role in the marketing department? B: I'm fine, but the job keeps me busier than I expected, because I have to write reports, answer client emails, and plan two product launches before the end of the month.","t":"A：你今天早上開團隊會議時看起來很累，你在行銷部的新職務一切都還好嗎？ B：我很好，只是這份【工作】比我預期的還要忙，因為我得寫報告、回覆客戶郵件，還要在月底前規劃兩場產品發表會。"},{"w":"position","p":"n.","d":"a job in a company or organization","c":"職位","s":"A: I saw that the hotel downtown is hiring again this month, so are you thinking about sending them your application before the deadline on Friday? B: Yes, they have an open position at the front desk, and since I speak English and Japanese well, I think I have a good chance of getting it.","t":"A：我看到市中心那家飯店這個月又在徵人了，你打算在星期五截止前寄申請給他們嗎？ B：是的，他們櫃檯有一個空缺的【職位】，而且我英文和日文都說得不錯，我覺得我很有機會錄取。"},{"w":"employment","p":"n.","d":"the state of having paid work","c":"就業；受雇","s":"A: Many students in my evening class will graduate this summer, so do you know what kind of support the city government offers to young people looking for work? B: The local employment center runs free workshops every Saturday, where career advisers help graduates write cover letters, practice answering questions, and search for suitable openings online.","t":"A：我夜間班的很多學生今年夏天就要畢業了，你知道市政府為找工作的年輕人提供哪些協助嗎？ B：當地的【就業】服務中心每週六都有免費工作坊，職涯顧問會協助畢業生寫求職信、練習回答問題，並在網路上搜尋合適的職缺。"},{"w":"employer","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that pays people to work for them","c":"雇主","s":"A: You have worked at the same electronics company for almost twelve years now, so what makes you stay there when so many other firms offer higher pay? B: My employer treats people fairly, provides excellent health insurance, and even pays for evening classes, so I feel valued and have never wanted to leave.","t":"A：你在同一家電子公司已經工作快十二年了，有那麼多公司開出更高的薪水，是什麼讓你留下來？ B：我的【雇主】待人公平，提供很好的健康保險，甚至幫我們付夜間課程的學費，所以我覺得被重視，從來沒想過要離開。"},{"w":"employee","p":"n.","d":"a person who is paid to work for a company","c":"員工","s":"A: The manager gave a special award at the year-end party last night, so who received it, and why did everyone clap so loudly? B: It went to a quiet employee from the shipping department who worked extra hours during the busy season and helped train three new team members without being asked.","t":"A：經理昨晚在尾牙上頒了一個特別獎，是誰得獎了？為什麼大家拍手拍得那麼大聲？ B：得獎的是出貨部一位安靜的【員工】，他在旺季時加班，而且主動幫忙訓練了三位新同事。"},{"w":"salary","p":"n.","d":"fixed money paid to a worker, usually every month","c":"薪水（月薪；年薪）","s":"A: The software company in Hsinchu offered you the job yesterday, so are you going to accept it, or are you still comparing it with the other offer? B: I'm probably going to accept, because the monthly salary is twenty percent higher than what I earn now, and they also give a bonus at the end of the year.","t":"A：新竹那家軟體公司昨天錄取你了，你要接受嗎？還是還在跟另一個工作機會比較？ B：我大概會接受，因為每個月的【薪水】比我現在多百分之二十，而且年底還有獎金。"},{"w":"wage","p":"n.","d":"money paid per hour or day for work","c":"工資（時薪；日薪）","s":"A: Many part-time workers at the supermarket have been complaining recently, so what exactly are they unhappy about? B: They say their hourly wage hasn't gone up in three years, even though rent and food prices have risen, so they want the owner to discuss a fair increase with them next week.","t":"A：超市很多兼職員工最近一直在抱怨，他們到底在不滿什麼？ B：他們說雖然房租和食物都漲價了，但他們的時薪【工資】三年來都沒調漲，所以希望老闆下週和他們討論合理的加薪。"},{"w":"promotion","p":"n.","d":"a move to a higher, more important job","c":"升遷；晉升","s":"A: Jessica has been working late almost every night and taking extra training courses, so is she preparing for something special at work? B: Yes, she hopes to get a promotion to sales manager next spring, because the current manager is moving to the Singapore office and the director wants someone from inside the team.","t":"A：Jessica幾乎每晚都加班，還額外上培訓課程，她是在為工作上什麼特別的事做準備嗎？ B：是的，她希望明年春天能【升遷】為業務經理，因為現任經理要調到新加坡辦公室，而主管希望從團隊內部找人接任。"},{"w":"experience","p":"n.","d":"knowledge or skill you get from doing a job","c":"經驗","s":"A: We received over fifty applications for the accounting role, so how are we going to choose the five people to interview next week? B: Let's first look for candidates with at least three years of experience in a large firm, and then compare their language ability and the software they can use.","t":"A：會計職缺我們收到超過五十份申請，要怎麼選出下週面試的五個人？ B：我們先找在大公司有至少三年【經驗】的應徵者，然後再比較他們的語言能力和會用的軟體。"},{"w":"skill","p":"n.","d":"an ability to do something well because you have practiced it","c":"技能","s":"A: The new customer service team will start answering calls on Monday, so what is the most important thing they should learn during training this week? B: Listening carefully is the key skill, because angry customers calm down quickly when they feel understood, and then our staff can solve the problem much more easily.","t":"A：新的客服團隊星期一就要開始接電話了，這週培訓期間他們最該學的是什麼？ B：仔細聆聽是關鍵【技能】，因為生氣的顧客覺得被理解時會很快冷靜下來，這樣我們的員工就能更輕鬆地解決問題。"},{"w":"qualification","p":"n.","d":"an exam or course result that shows you can do a job","c":"資格；證照","s":"A: I'd love to teach English at a public high school after I move back to Taiwan, so what do I need to prepare before applying? B: You'll need a teaching qualification from a recognized university, a good English test score, and some classroom practice, so start collecting your documents as early as possible.","t":"A：我搬回台灣後很想在公立高中教英文，申請之前我需要準備什麼？ B：你需要一所認可大學核發的教師【資格】、不錯的英文檢定成績，以及一些實際教學經驗，所以盡早開始準備文件吧。"},{"w":"training","p":"n.","d":"teaching people the skills for a job","c":"培訓；訓練","s":"A: The factory is installing new machines next month, so how will the workers learn to use them safely without slowing down production? B: The supplier will send two engineers to give every shift three days of hands-on training, and they will also leave a detailed manual in Chinese for later reference.","t":"A：工廠下個月要安裝新機器，工人要怎麼在不拖慢生產的情況下學會安全操作？ B：供應商會派兩位工程師為每個班次提供三天的實作【培訓】，還會留下一份詳細的中文手冊供日後參考。"},{"w":"resume","p":"n.","d":"a document listing your education and work history","c":"履歷","s":"A: I'm applying for a design job at an advertising agency next week, so could you look at my documents and tell me what to improve? B: Your resume is too long, so cut it down to one page, put your best projects at the top, and remove the part-time jobs you had in high school.","t":"A：我下週要應徵一家廣告公司的設計工作，你可以看看我的資料，告訴我哪裡要改進嗎？ B：你的【履歷】太長了，刪減到一頁，把最好的作品放在最上面，並拿掉你高中時做過的打工。"},{"w":"interview","p":"n.","d":"a formal meeting where an employer asks a job seeker questions","c":"面試","s":"A: You're wearing a suit today, and you keep checking your watch, so do you have an important meeting with a client this afternoon? B: Not exactly, I have a job interview with a bank at two o'clock, and I'm nervous because they will ask me questions in English in front of three managers.","t":"A：你今天穿西裝，又一直看手錶，下午是要跟客戶開重要的會嗎？ B：不完全是，我兩點要去一家銀行【面試】，我很緊張，因為他們會在三位經理面前用英文問我問題。"},{"w":"hire","p":"v.","d":"to give someone a job","c":"雇用","s":"A: Our online orders have doubled since the holiday sale started, and the warehouse staff are exhausted, so what is the boss planning to do about it? B: She has decided to hire five temporary workers until the end of January, so the regular team can rest and customers can still receive their packages on time.","t":"A：假期特賣開始後我們的網路訂單翻倍了，倉庫員工都累壞了，老闆打算怎麼處理？ B：她決定【雇用】五名臨時工到一月底，這樣正職團隊可以休息，顧客也能準時收到包裹。"},{"w":"fire","p":"v.","d":"to make someone leave their job, usually as a punishment","c":"開除；解雇","s":"A: I heard that the new cashier at the downtown branch suddenly stopped coming to work, so did she quit, or did something happen? B: The manager had to fire her after she was caught taking money from the register twice, even though he had given her a clear warning the first time.","t":"A：聽說市區分店的新收銀員突然不來上班了，她是辭職了，還是發生了什麼事？ B：她被抓到兩次從收銀機拿錢，經理只好【開除】她，即使第一次他已經明確警告過她了。"},{"w":"success","p":"n.","d":"achieving what you planned or wanted","c":"成功","s":"A: Your bakery has opened three new shops in the past two years, so what do you think is the main reason customers keep coming back? B: Much of our success comes from using fresh local ingredients and listening to feedback, because we change the menu whenever regular customers suggest something new and interesting.","t":"A：你的麵包店過去兩年開了三家新店，你覺得顧客一再回訪的主要原因是什麼？ B：我們的【成功】大多來自使用新鮮的在地食材並傾聽意見，因為只要熟客提出新奇有趣的建議，我們就會調整菜單。"},{"w":"ambition","p":"n.","d":"a strong wish to achieve something","c":"抱負；雄心","s":"A: Your younger brother just started his first job as a sales assistant, so what kind of future does he hope to have in the company? B: His biggest ambition is to open his own sporting goods store one day, so he is learning everything he can about buying, pricing, and managing staff while he works there.","t":"A：你弟弟剛開始他的第一份工作當銷售助理，他希望在公司裡有什麼樣的未來？ B：他最大的【抱負】是有一天開自己的運動用品店，所以他在那裡工作時盡可能學習採購、定價和管理員工的一切。"},{"w":"goal","p":"n.","d":"something you are trying to achieve","c":"目標","s":"A: The sales team had a difficult first half of the year, so what did the director say at the planning meeting this morning? B: She set a clear goal of winning ten new corporate clients by December, and she promised a team trip to Japan if we reach it before the holidays.","t":"A：業務團隊上半年很辛苦，主管今天早上在規劃會議上說了什麼？ B：她訂了一個明確的【目標】，要在十二月前爭取到十家新的企業客戶，還承諾如果我們在假期前達成，就招待團隊去日本旅遊。"},{"w":"path","p":"n.","d":"a series of steps or choices that lead somewhere, such as in a career","c":"道路；（職涯）路線","s":"A: You studied engineering at university, but now you work in human resources, so how did you end up in such a different field? B: My career path changed after I organized training events at my first company, because I discovered that I enjoyed helping people grow much more than designing machines.","t":"A：你大學念工程，現在卻在人資部門工作，你怎麼會走進這麼不同的領域？ B：我在第一家公司籌辦培訓活動後，職涯【道路】就改變了，因為我發現比起設計機器，我更喜歡幫助別人成長。"},{"w":"opportunity","p":"n.","d":"a chance to do something good","c":"機會","s":"A: The head office in London has invited two staff members from our branch to work there for six months, so are you going to apply? B: Definitely, because it's a great opportunity to improve my English, learn how a global team works, and build connections that could help my career later.","t":"A：倫敦總公司邀請我們分公司兩位員工去那裡工作六個月，你要申請嗎？ B：當然，因為這是提升英文、了解國際團隊如何運作，以及建立日後對職涯有幫助的人脈的好【機會】。"},{"w":"balance","p":"n.","d":"a healthy mix of different parts, such as work and private life","c":"平衡","s":"A: You used to stay at the office until ten every night, but lately you leave at six, so what made you change your routine? B: I realized I needed a better balance between work and family, so now I finish my tasks earlier, have dinner with my kids, and go jogging on weekends.","t":"A：你以前每晚都在辦公室待到十點，最近卻六點就下班，是什麼讓你改變作息？ B：我發現我需要在工作和家庭之間取得更好的【平衡】，所以現在我提早完成工作，和孩子一起吃晚餐，週末去慢跑。"},{"w":"retire","p":"v.","d":"to stop working, usually because you are older","c":"退休","s":"A: Mr. Lin has managed the accounting department for almost thirty years, so is it true that the company is planning a big farewell party for him? B: Yes, he will retire at the end of March so he can travel around Europe with his wife, and the staff are collecting money to buy him a nice camera.","t":"A：林先生管理會計部將近三十年了，公司真的要為他辦一場盛大的歡送會嗎？ B：是的，他三月底就要【退休】了，好和太太去歐洲旅行，員工們正在集資買一台好相機送他。"},{"w":"long-term","p":"adj.","d":"lasting or planned for a long time","c":"長期的","s":"A: The startup offered me a higher salary than my current company, but I'm worried because it's so new, so what do you think I should do? B: Think about your long-term plans first, because if you want to stay in one place for many years and buy a home, a stable company might be the safer choice.","t":"A：那家新創公司開的薪水比我現在的公司高，但我擔心它太新了，你覺得我該怎麼做？ B：先想想你的【長期】計畫，因為如果你想在一個地方待很多年並買房子，穩定的公司可能是比較安全的選擇。"},{"w":"stable","p":"adj.","d":"not likely to change; steady","c":"穩定的","s":"A: Your sister left her exciting job at a travel startup to work for the city government, so why did she make such a big change? B: After her son was born, she wanted a stable income with regular hours, so she chose a government office where the pay is lower but she never worries about losing her job.","t":"A：你姊姊離開了旅遊新創公司那份刺激的工作，去市政府上班，她為什麼要做這麼大的改變？ B：她兒子出生後，她想要有【穩定的】收入和規律的工時，所以選擇了政府機關，雖然薪水較低，但她從不擔心失業。"},{"w":"rewarding","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel satisfied and happy","c":"有意義的；有成就感的","s":"A: You gave up a well-paid position at a bank to teach science at a rural elementary school, so do you ever regret that decision? B: Not at all, because the work is very rewarding, and seeing my students get excited about experiments every week makes me happier than any bonus I received at the bank.","t":"A：你放棄銀行的高薪職位，去鄉下的小學教自然科學，你曾後悔過這個決定嗎？ B：一點也不，因為這份工作很【有成就感】，每週看到學生對實驗感到興奮，比我在銀行領過的任何獎金都讓我開心。"}]},{"unit":46,"theme":"Celebration 慶祝","cards":[{"w":"celebrate","p":"v.","d":"to do something enjoyable because of a special event","c":"慶祝","s":"A: Our sales team finally reached its yearly target last Friday, so how is the manager planning to thank everyone for all the extra hours? B: She has booked a private room at an Italian restaurant downtown, and we will celebrate the success with dinner and a short speech next Thursday evening.","t":"A：我們銷售團隊上週五終於達成年度目標，經理打算怎麼感謝大家加了那麼多班？ B：她在市中心一家義大利餐廳訂了包廂，下週四晚上我們會用晚餐和簡短致詞來【慶祝】這次的成功。"},{"w":"festival","p":"n.","d":"a special event or time with performances, food, or celebrations","c":"節慶；節日活動","s":"A: The hotels in the city center are almost fully booked for the second week of October, so do you know why so many visitors are coming? B: The annual food festival is taking place along the river that week, and thousands of tourists usually arrive to try dishes from over fifty local restaurants.","t":"A：市中心的飯店十月第二週幾乎都客滿了，你知道為什麼有這麼多遊客要來嗎？ B：那週河岸邊會舉辦一年一度的美食【節】，通常有成千上萬的遊客前來品嚐五十多家在地餐廳的料理。"},{"w":"party","p":"n.","d":"a social event where people meet to eat, drink, and have fun","c":"派對","s":"A: Mr. Chen is retiring at the end of this month after working here for thirty years, so is the department doing anything special for him? B: Yes, we are organizing a surprise farewell party in the staff lounge on his last afternoon, and his family has secretly agreed to join us.","t":"A：陳先生在這裡工作了三十年，這個月底就要退休了，部門有沒有為他準備什麼特別的活動？ B：有，我們正在籌辦一場驚喜歡送【派對】，就在他最後一天下午於員工休息室舉行，他的家人也已經偷偷答應要參加。"},{"w":"ceremony","p":"n.","d":"a formal public event held for a special purpose","c":"典禮；儀式","s":"A: The new factory in Taichung is ready to start production next month, so will the company hold any official event to mark the opening? B: The CEO will cut a red ribbon at the opening ceremony on Monday morning, and several local officials and reporters have been invited to watch.","t":"A：台中的新工廠下個月就要開始生產了，公司會舉辦任何正式活動來紀念開幕嗎？ B：執行長星期一早上會在開幕【典禮】上剪綵，也邀請了幾位地方官員和記者到場觀禮。"},{"w":"occasion","p":"n.","d":"a special event or an important time","c":"場合；特殊時刻","s":"A: I want to buy a nice pen for my boss because she just got promoted to regional director, but do you think a present like that is too expensive? B: Not at all, because a promotion is an important occasion, and a quality pen is something she will use at meetings every day.","t":"A：我想買一支好筆送老闆，因為她剛升任區域總監，但你覺得這樣的禮物會不會太貴？ B：一點也不會，因為升遷是很重要的【時刻】，而且一支好筆是她每天開會都會用到的東西。"},{"w":"anniversary","p":"n.","d":"the date each year when an important event happened in the past","c":"週年紀念","s":"A: Why is the lobby full of balloons and old photographs of the original office building this morning? B: Our company was founded exactly twenty years ago today, so management is marking the anniversary with a photo exhibition and a free lunch for every employee in the building.","t":"A：今天早上大廳為什麼擺滿了氣球和原本辦公大樓的老照片？ B：我們公司正好是二十年前的今天成立的，所以管理階層用攝影展和為大樓裡每位員工準備的免費午餐來紀念這個【週年紀念日】。"},{"w":"birthday","p":"n.","d":"the day each year when someone was born","c":"生日","s":"A: Everyone in the accounting office signed a big card this morning, so what is the reason for it? B: It is Linda's fortieth birthday today, and while she is at a meeting with the auditors, we are going to hide a chocolate cake in the kitchen to surprise her later.","t":"A：今天早上會計辦公室每個人都在一張大卡片上簽名，是什麼原因呢？ B：今天是琳達的四十歲【生日】，趁她在和查帳人員開會時，我們要把一個巧克力蛋糕藏在茶水間，晚點給她驚喜。"},{"w":"wedding","p":"n.","d":"a ceremony at which two people get married","c":"婚禮","s":"A: Could you cover my shifts at the front desk next Friday and Saturday, because I need to fly to Kaohsiung for a family event? B: Sure, I remember you mentioned that your younger sister is getting married, so please have a great time at the wedding and send my congratulations to the happy couple.","t":"A：你下週五和週六可以幫我代櫃檯的班嗎？因為我要飛去高雄參加家族活動。 B：當然，我記得你提過你妹妹要結婚了，祝你在【婚禮】上玩得開心，也幫我向這對新人道賀。"},{"w":"gathering","p":"n.","d":"a meeting of people for a social purpose","c":"聚會","s":"A: The new employees from our overseas branches seem a little lonely in the city, so how can we help them make friends quickly? B: The HR department is planning a casual gathering on the rooftop next Friday evening, with snacks, drinks, and simple games so that people can talk freely.","t":"A：海外分公司來的新員工在這城市好像有點孤單，我們要怎麼幫他們快點交到朋友？ B：人資部正計畫下週五晚上在頂樓辦一場輕鬆的【聚會】，有點心、飲料和簡單遊戲，讓大家可以自在聊天。"},{"w":"tradition","p":"n.","d":"a custom or belief passed down over many years","c":"傳統","s":"A: Why does everyone in your office eat a big lunch in the meeting room on the last working day of every year? B: It is a long tradition that started when the founder ran the company, and even though we now have three hundred staff, we still keep it to thank everyone.","t":"A：為什麼你們辦公室每年最後一個上班日大家都在會議室吃大餐？ B：這是創辦人經營公司時就開始的悠久【傳統】，雖然我們現在有三百名員工，還是保留下來感謝大家。"},{"w":"custom","p":"n.","d":"a usual way of behaving in a society or group","c":"習俗；風俗","s":"A: I am visiting our partners in Seoul next week for the first time, so is there anything I should know before the business dinner? B: It is a local custom to wait until the oldest person at the table starts eating, so be patient and follow what the others do during the meal.","t":"A：我下週第一次去首爾拜訪合作夥伴，商務晚宴之前有什麼該知道的嗎？ B：當地的【習俗】是要等桌上最年長的人先開動，所以用餐時要有耐心，跟著其他人的做法就對了。"},{"w":"toast","p":"n.","d":"the act of raising glasses and drinking to wish someone success or happiness","c":"敬酒；祝酒","s":"A: The managing director just stood up and lifted her glass at the end of the annual dinner, so what is she going to do? B: She is about to propose a toast to the whole sales team for their excellent results, so pick up your glass and get ready to drink with everyone.","t":"A：常務董事在年度晚宴尾聲站起來舉起酒杯，她要做什麼？ B：她要為整個業務團隊的優異成績提議【敬酒】，所以拿起你的杯子，準備和大家一起乾杯。"},{"w":"cheer","p":"v.","d":"to shout loudly to show you are happy or to support someone","c":"歡呼；喝采","s":"A: What was all that noise coming from the conference room during the lunch break today? B: The whole marketing department gathered to watch the live announcement of the design awards, and everyone started to cheer loudly when our team's poster won first prize.","t":"A：今天午休時會議室傳來的那些吵鬧聲是什麼？ B：整個行銷部聚在一起看設計獎的直播頒獎，當我們團隊的海報拿下首獎時，大家都大聲【歡呼】起來。"},{"w":"joyful","p":"adj.","d":"very happy; full of joy","c":"歡樂的；喜悅的","s":"A: How did the staff react when the CEO announced that everyone would get an extra week of paid holiday this year? B: The atmosphere in the hall was very joyful, with people laughing, hugging their coworkers, and immediately talking about where they wanted to travel in the summer.","t":"A：執行長宣布今年大家都多一週帶薪假時，員工反應如何？ B：大廳裡的氣氛非常【歡樂】，大家笑著擁抱同事，馬上就聊起夏天想去哪裡旅行。"},{"w":"festive","p":"adj.","d":"bright and cheerful because of a holiday or celebration","c":"節慶的；喜氣洋洋的","s":"A: The department store downtown looks completely different this December, so what has the management changed? B: They hung red lanterns and thousands of small lights across the entrance, and they play holiday songs all day, so the whole building feels really festive for shoppers.","t":"A：市中心那家百貨公司今年十二月看起來完全不一樣，管理部門改了什麼？ B：他們在入口處掛了紅燈籠和成千上萬顆小燈，還整天播放節日歌曲，讓整棟建築對購物者來說充滿【節慶氣氛】。"},{"w":"decorate","p":"v.","d":"to make a place look nicer by adding pretty things to it","c":"裝飾；布置","s":"A: The holiday party starts at six o'clock in the main hall, so what should the volunteers do after lunch? B: Please decorate the walls with paper stars and balloons, set up the tables near the windows, and check that the speakers work before the guests arrive.","t":"A：節日派對六點在大廳開始，志工們午餐後該做什麼？ B：請用紙星星和氣球【裝飾】牆面，把桌子擺在窗邊，並在賓客抵達前確認喇叭正常運作。"},{"w":"decoration","p":"n.","d":"a thing used to make something look more attractive","c":"裝飾品","s":"A: The cleaning staff asked me what to do with all the paper lanterns and lights from last night's company party, so do you have any idea? B: Please put every decoration back into the large boxes in the storage room, because we plan to use them again at next year's event.","t":"A：清潔人員問我昨晚公司派對留下的紙燈籠和燈飾要怎麼處理，你有什麼想法嗎？ B：請把每一件【裝飾品】放回儲藏室的大箱子裡，因為我們打算明年的活動再用。"},{"w":"music","p":"n.","d":"pleasant sounds made by voices or instruments","c":"音樂","s":"A: The guests at the hotel's anniversary dinner seemed bored during the first hour, so how can we make the evening more lively? B: Let's ask the jazz band to start playing some cheerful music near the dance floor, because people usually relax and talk more once they hear a good rhythm.","t":"A：飯店週年晚宴前一小時賓客似乎很無聊，我們怎麼讓晚上更熱鬧？ B：請爵士樂團在舞池附近開始演奏一些歡快的【音樂】吧，因為人們聽到好節奏通常就會放鬆、聊得更多。"},{"w":"dance","p":"v.","d":"to move your body to music","c":"跳舞","s":"A: Is the year-end banquet just a formal dinner, or will there be some activities after the speeches are finished? B: After dessert, the lights will go down and a DJ will play popular songs, so anyone who wants to dance can join their coworkers on the floor until midnight.","t":"A：尾牙只是正式晚餐嗎？還是致詞結束後會有些活動？ B：甜點之後燈光會調暗，DJ會播放流行歌曲，想【跳舞】的人可以和同事一起到舞池直到午夜。"},{"w":"gift","p":"n.","d":"something you give to someone, often on a special day","c":"禮物","s":"A: Our biggest client, Ms. Tanaka, is celebrating her company's tenth year in business, so what should we send to her office? B: I think a basket of high-quality Taiwanese tea would be a thoughtful gift, and we can attach a handwritten card from our president as well.","t":"A：我們最大的客戶田中女士的公司正在慶祝創立十週年，我們該送什麼到她辦公室？ B：我覺得一籃高品質的台灣茶會是一份貼心的【禮物】，我們也可以附上總裁的親筆卡片。"},{"w":"cake","p":"n.","d":"a sweet baked food made from flour, sugar, and eggs","c":"蛋糕","s":"A: We are holding a small celebration for the team's tenth project this afternoon, so have you ordered something sweet for everyone? B: Yes, the bakery across the street is making a large strawberry cake with our company logo on top, and they will deliver it at three o'clock.","t":"A：今天下午我們要為團隊第十個專案辦個小慶祝，你有幫大家訂甜點嗎？ B：有，對街的麵包店正在做一個上面有公司標誌的大草莓【蛋糕】，三點會送來。"},{"w":"fireworks","p":"n.","d":"colorful explosions in the sky used for celebrations","c":"煙火","s":"A: Why are so many people waiting outside the office buildings near Taipei 101 at almost midnight on December 31st? B: They are hoping to get a good view of the famous New Year's fireworks, which light up the sky for several minutes and are shown live on TV around the world.","t":"A：為什麼十二月三十一日快午夜時，台北101附近的辦公大樓外面有這麼多人在等？ B：他們希望能清楚看到著名的跨年【煙火】，煙火會照亮天空好幾分鐘，並在全世界的電視上現場直播。"},{"w":"crowd","p":"n.","d":"a large number of people together in one place","c":"人群","s":"A: Should we drive to the stadium for the city's victory parade tomorrow, or will it be difficult to find a parking space? B: The news says a huge crowd of about fifty thousand fans is expected, so taking the subway early in the morning is definitely the safer and faster choice.","t":"A：明天市區的勝利遊行我們要開車去體育場嗎？還是會很難找到停車位？ B：新聞說預計會有約五萬名球迷的龐大【人群】，所以一早搭捷運絕對是比較安全又快速的選擇。"},{"w":"invite","p":"v.","d":"to ask someone to come to an event","c":"邀請","s":"A: The company is opening its new branch in Hsinchu next month, so who should we ask to attend the opening event? B: We should invite our main suppliers, a few important customers, and the local reporters, and we need to mail the cards at least three weeks in advance.","t":"A：公司下個月要在新竹開新分店，開幕活動我們該請誰出席？ B：我們應該【邀請】主要供應商、幾位重要客戶和地方記者，而且至少要提前三週寄出卡片。"},{"w":"guest","p":"n.","d":"a person who is invited to an event or a home","c":"客人；賓客","s":"A: How many chairs should I set up in the ballroom for the award dinner on Saturday night? B: According to the final list from the events team, two hundred and twenty people have replied, and every guest will receive a name card, so please prepare ten extra seats for any last-minute visitors as well.","t":"A：週六晚上的頒獎晚宴，我在宴會廳要擺多少張椅子？ B：根據活動團隊的最終名單，共有兩百二十人回覆，每位【賓客】都會拿到名牌，所以也請多準備十個座位給臨時來的訪客。"},{"w":"host","p":"v.","d":"to organize an event and welcome the people who come","c":"主辦；招待","s":"A: Our department won the best customer service award this year, so where will the celebration dinner take place? B: The general manager has offered to host the dinner at her house in Yangmingshan, and she will even hire a chef to cook for the whole team that night.","t":"A：我們部門今年拿到最佳客服獎，慶功晚宴會在哪裡舉行？ B：總經理主動提議在她陽明山的家裡【主辦】晚宴，她甚至會請一位廚師當晚為整個團隊下廚。"},{"w":"enjoy","p":"v.","d":"to get pleasure from something","c":"享受；喜愛","s":"A: You took the new interns to the night market after their first week at work, so how did they like it? B: They seemed to enjoy the evening very much, because they tried a lot of local snacks, played some games, and kept taking photos until nearly eleven o'clock.","t":"A：實習生第一週上班後你帶他們去夜市，他們覺得怎麼樣？ B：他們似乎非常【享受】那個晚上，因為吃了很多在地小吃、玩了一些遊戲，還一直拍照到快十一點。"},{"w":"memorable","p":"adj.","d":"special and easy to remember","c":"難忘的","s":"A: The customers who joined our boat tour for the company's anniversary sent many thank-you emails, so what did they like most? B: Many of them said it was a memorable trip, because the sunset over the harbor was beautiful and the staff served fresh seafood on the deck.","t":"A：參加我們公司週年遊船行程的客戶寄來很多感謝信，他們最喜歡什麼？ B：很多人說那是一趟【難忘的】旅程，因為港口的夕陽很美，員工還在甲板上提供新鮮海鮮。"},{"w":"together","p":"adv.","d":"with each other; in the same place","c":"一起；在一起","s":"A: The team has been working remotely for almost a year, so how can we improve communication between the members? B: I suggest that we bring everyone together for a weekend trip to Hualien, where they can share meals, go hiking, and get to know each other better.","t":"A：團隊遠距工作快一年了，我們要怎麼改善成員之間的溝通？ B：我建議把大家聚集【在一起】去花蓮週末旅遊，讓他們可以共享餐點、健行，彼此更加了解。"}]},{"unit":47,"theme":"Celebrity 名人","cards":[{"w":"impressed","p":"adj.","d":"feeling admiration because of what someone did","c":"印象深刻的","s":"A: How did the film director react when the young actress performed her scene in the rehearsal yesterday afternoon? B: He was so impressed by her natural performance and clear voice that he offered her a bigger role in the movie, and he even called her agent before lunch.","t":"A：昨天下午排練時，那位年輕女演員演出她的那場戲，電影導演有什麼反應？ B：他對她自然的表演和清晰的聲音感到非常【印象深刻】，所以給了她電影中更重要的角色，甚至在午餐前就打電話給她的經紀人。"},{"w":"renowned","p":"adj.","d":"famous and respected by many people","c":"著名的；有名望的","s":"A: Who is giving the opening speech at the international food festival that our company is sponsoring next month in the convention center? B: A renowned chef from Paris will speak about healthy cooking, and many restaurant owners have already bought tickets because they want to hear her advice in person.","t":"A：下個月我們公司在會議中心贊助的國際美食節，開幕演講由誰負責？ B：一位來自巴黎的【著名】主廚會談健康烹飪，很多餐廳老闆已經買了票，因為他們想親耳聽她的建議。"},{"w":"contribute","p":"v.","d":"to give money, time, or ideas to help something","c":"貢獻；捐助","s":"A: The famous singer visited the children's hospital last weekend, but did she just take photos with the patients and leave quickly? B: No, she promised to contribute part of the money from her next concert tour to build a new playroom, and she also stayed for three hours to sing with the kids.","t":"A：那位知名歌手上週末去兒童醫院探訪，她是不是只和病人拍照就很快離開了？ B：不是，她承諾要把下一次巡迴演唱會的部分收入【捐助】出來蓋一間新的遊戲室，而且她還待了三個小時和孩子們一起唱歌。"},{"w":"prominent","p":"adj.","d":"important and well known","c":"重要的；著名的","s":"A: Why are so many reporters and photographers waiting outside the hotel lobby this morning, and should we warn our guests about the noise? B: A prominent business leader from Singapore is staying here during the trade conference, so yes, please tell guests that the main entrance may be busy until noon.","t":"A：今天早上為什麼有這麼多記者和攝影師在飯店大廳外面等，我們要提醒客人會有噪音嗎？ B：一位來自新加坡的【知名】企業領袖在貿易會議期間住在這裡，所以是的，請告訴客人正門到中午之前可能都會很擁擠。"},{"w":"ingenuity","p":"n.","d":"skill at thinking of new and clever ideas","c":"獨創力；巧思","s":"A: The cooking show host only had a small kitchen and very few ingredients on today's episode, so how did she make such a beautiful dinner? B: Her ingenuity really surprised everyone, because she turned leftover rice and a few vegetables into a colorful dish, and the audience clapped loudly when she finished.","t":"A：那位烹飪節目主持人今天這集只有一個小廚房和很少的食材，她怎麼做出這麼漂亮的晚餐？ B：她的【巧思】真的讓大家很驚訝，因為她把剩飯和幾樣蔬菜變成了一道色彩繽紛的菜，她做完時觀眾都大聲鼓掌。"},{"w":"dedication","p":"n.","d":"hard work and strong commitment to a goal","c":"奉獻；專注投入","s":"A: That famous tennis player has won so many tournaments over the past ten years, so what do you think is the secret of her long success? B: I think it is her dedication to training, because she practices six hours every day, follows a strict diet, and never skips her morning run, even on holidays.","t":"A：那位知名網球選手過去十年贏了這麼多錦標賽，你覺得她長久成功的秘訣是什麼？ B：我認為是她對訓練的【投入】，因為她每天練習六小時、遵守嚴格的飲食，而且即使在假日也從不跳過晨跑。"},{"w":"enthusiasm","p":"n.","d":"strong excitement and interest","c":"熱情；熱忱","s":"A: The new host of our company's podcast has never worked in radio before, so are you worried about how listeners will react to her? B: Not at all, because her enthusiasm for technology is easy to hear in every episode, and the number of listeners has already doubled since she joined us in March.","t":"A：我們公司播客的新主持人以前從沒在廣播界工作過，你擔心聽眾對她的反應嗎？ B：一點也不，因為每一集都很容易聽出她對科技的【熱情】，而且自從她三月加入以來，聽眾人數已經增加了一倍。"},{"w":"lauded","p":"adj.","d":"highly praised in public","c":"備受讚揚的","s":"A: Is the new museum downtown worth visiting this weekend, or should I take my parents somewhere else when they come to Taipei? B: You should definitely go, because the museum was designed by a widely lauded architect from Japan, and newspapers have praised its bright galleries and peaceful rooftop garden.","t":"A：市中心的新博物館這週末值得去嗎？還是我爸媽來台北時應該帶他們去別的地方？ B：你一定要去，因為那座博物館是由一位來自日本、廣受【讚揚】的建築師設計的，報紙都稱讚它明亮的展廳和寧靜的屋頂花園。"},{"w":"demeanor","p":"n.","d":"the way a person looks and behaves","c":"舉止；態度","s":"A: The actor was asked many difficult questions about his private life at the press conference, so did he become angry with the journalists? B: No, his calm and polite demeanor impressed everyone in the room, and he simply smiled and said he would rather talk about his new film.","t":"A：那位演員在記者會上被問了很多關於他私生活的困難問題，他有對記者發脾氣嗎？ B：沒有，他冷靜又有禮貌的【舉止】讓在場的每個人都印象深刻，他只是微笑著說他比較想談談他的新電影。"},{"w":"integrity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being honest and having strong morals","c":"正直；誠信","s":"A: Why did the sports drink company choose that particular basketball player as the face of their new advertising campaign this year? B: They chose him mainly because of his integrity, since he has always been honest with fans, refused money to lose games, and treated his teammates with respect.","t":"A：那家運動飲料公司今年為什麼選那位籃球員當新廣告活動的代言人？ B：他們主要是因為他的【正直】才選他，因為他一向對球迷誠實、拒絕收錢打假球，而且尊重他的隊友。"},{"w":"pursuit","p":"n.","d":"the act of trying to get or achieve something","c":"追求","s":"A: The famous pianist left her comfortable job at a bank when she was twenty-five, so wasn't her family worried about that decision? B: They were nervous at first, but they supported her pursuit of a music career, and now they travel with her to concerts in Europe every summer.","t":"A：那位知名鋼琴家二十五歲時辭去了銀行的安穩工作，她的家人不擔心那個決定嗎？ B：他們一開始很緊張，但他們支持她對音樂事業的【追求】，現在他們每年夏天都陪她到歐洲參加音樂會。"},{"w":"converted","p":"adj.","d":"changed so it can be used for a different purpose","c":"改建的；改裝的","s":"A: Where is the TV star planning to hold the launch party for her new clothing brand, since the hotels downtown are all fully booked? B: She rented a converted factory near the river that is now a stylish event space, and it has enough room for two hundred guests and a small stage.","t":"A：那位電視明星打算在哪裡舉辦她新服裝品牌的發表派對？市中心的飯店都已經被訂滿了。 B：她租了河邊一間【改建的】工廠，現在是一個時尚的活動場地，有足夠的空間容納兩百位賓客和一個小舞台。"},{"w":"representative","p":"n.","d":"a person who speaks or acts for another person or group","c":"代表；代理人","s":"A: The famous actor can't come to the charity dinner tonight because his flight from Los Angeles was delayed, so who will accept the award for him? B: His representative from the agency will come instead, and she will read a short thank-you message that he wrote on the plane this morning.","t":"A：那位知名演員因為從洛杉磯來的班機延誤，今晚無法出席慈善晚宴，誰會替他領獎？ B：他經紀公司的【代表】會代替他出席，她會朗讀一段他今天早上在飛機上寫的簡短感謝詞。"},{"w":"professionalism","p":"n.","d":"the high skill and good behavior expected of a worker","c":"專業精神；專業素養","s":"A: The singer's concert was delayed for an hour because of the heavy rain last night, so were the fans angry when she finally walked on stage? B: Some were upset, but her professionalism helped a lot, because she apologized sincerely, explained the safety problem clearly, and then sang three extra songs for free.","t":"A：昨晚因為大雨，那位歌手的演唱會延遲了一個小時，她最後上台時歌迷生氣嗎？ B：有些人不高興，但她的【專業精神】幫了很大的忙，因為她真誠地道歉、清楚說明安全問題，然後還免費多唱了三首歌。"},{"w":"outstanding","p":"adj.","d":"extremely good; much better than others","c":"傑出的；出色的","s":"A: Which employee is going to receive the special prize at the year-end party, since the managers met for a long time yesterday afternoon? B: They chose Linda from customer service, because her work this year was truly outstanding, and three of our biggest clients wrote letters to thank her personally.","t":"A：誰會在尾牙上拿到特別獎？經理們昨天下午開了很久的會。 B：他們選了客服部的琳達，因為她今年的工作表現真的很【傑出】，我們三位最大的客戶還親自寫信感謝她。"},{"w":"bias","p":"n.","d":"an unfair preference for or against someone or something","c":"偏見；偏袒","s":"A: Why did the TV station change the judges for the singing competition before the final round next Saturday night? B: Viewers complained about bias, because one judge was a close friend of a contestant, so the station replaced him to make sure every singer would be treated fairly.","t":"A：電視台為什麼在下週六晚上決賽前更換了歌唱比賽的評審？ B：觀眾抱怨有【偏袒】，因為其中一位評審是某位參賽者的好朋友，所以電視台換掉他，確保每位歌手都能被公平對待。"},{"w":"inspiring","p":"adj.","d":"making people want to do or achieve something","c":"鼓舞人心的","s":"A: What did you think of the talk by that famous mountain climber at the leadership workshop yesterday afternoon in the main hall? B: It was really inspiring, because she described how she reached the top after failing twice, and many of my coworkers said they now want to set bigger goals.","t":"A：你覺得昨天下午在大禮堂領導力工作坊上那位知名登山家的演講怎麼樣？ B：真的很【鼓舞人心】，因為她講述了自己失敗兩次後如何登頂，我很多同事都說他們現在想設定更遠大的目標。"},{"w":"stardom","p":"n.","d":"the state of being a very famous performer","c":"明星地位；成名","s":"A: That young actor worked as a waiter in a small restaurant only two years ago, so how did his life change so quickly? B: He rose to stardom after his first movie became a huge hit online, and now fans follow him everywhere and companies pay him to advertise their products.","t":"A：那位年輕演員兩年前還在一家小餐廳當服務生，他的人生怎麼變化得這麼快？ B：他的第一部電影在網路上爆紅之後，他就一躍【成名】，現在粉絲到處跟著他，還有公司付錢請他代言產品。"},{"w":"appreciate","p":"v.","d":"to be thankful for something; to value something","c":"感激；欣賞","s":"A: The famous author spent two hours signing books for our customers on Saturday, so should we send her something to say thank you? B: Yes, let's send flowers and a card, because I'm sure she will appreciate the gesture, and we hope she will visit our bookstore again when her next novel comes out.","t":"A：那位知名作家星期六花了兩個小時幫我們的顧客簽書，我們要送她什麼東西表示感謝嗎？ B：好啊，我們送花和卡片吧，我相信她會【感激】這份心意，而且希望她下一本小說出版時能再來我們書店。"},{"w":"curious","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to know or learn about something","c":"好奇的","s":"A: Why are there so many people standing outside the shopping mall entrance this afternoon, and is something wrong with the building? B: Nothing is wrong, but people are curious because a popular movie star is filming a scene inside, and everyone wants to see who it is before the security guards close the doors.","t":"A：今天下午為什麼有這麼多人站在購物中心門口？大樓出了什麼問題嗎？ B：沒有問題，只是大家都很【好奇】，因為一位當紅電影明星正在裡面拍戲，每個人都想在保全關門前看看是誰。"},{"w":"determined","p":"adj.","d":"having a strong wish to do something and not giving up","c":"下定決心的；堅決的","s":"A: The famous swimmer hurt her shoulder badly last year, so does she really plan to compete in the national games again this summer? B: Yes, she is determined to win another gold medal, so she has been doing physical therapy every morning and training in the pool every evening for months.","t":"A：那位知名游泳選手去年肩膀受了重傷，她今年夏天真的打算再參加全國運動會嗎？ B：是的，她【下定決心】要再拿一面金牌，所以好幾個月來她每天早上做物理治療，每天晚上在泳池訓練。"},{"w":"overcome","p":"v.","d":"to succeed in dealing with a problem or difficulty","c":"克服","s":"A: Our new spokesperson used to be very shy when she was young, so how did she become such a confident speaker on television? B: She worked hard to overcome her fear by joining a drama club in college, and she practiced speaking in front of small groups until she felt comfortable with large audiences.","t":"A：我們的新發言人小時候很害羞，她是怎麼變成在電視上這麼有自信的講者的？ B：她大學時參加戲劇社，努力【克服】她的恐懼，她練習在小團體面前說話，直到她面對大批觀眾也能感到自在。"},{"w":"character","p":"n.","d":"the qualities that make a person who they are","c":"品格；性格","s":"A: The hotel manager said the famous guest in room 801 was very kind to the cleaning staff, so is he always like that? B: Yes, people who know him say he has strong character, because he treats everyone with the same respect, whether they are company presidents or waiters in a small café.","t":"A：飯店經理說801號房那位知名房客對清潔人員很友善，他一直都是這樣嗎？ B：是的，認識他的人都說他【品格】很好，因為不管對方是公司總裁還是小咖啡館的服務生，他都一樣尊重。"},{"w":"iconic","p":"adj.","d":"very famous and seen as a symbol of something","c":"標誌性的；具代表性的","s":"A: The tour group from Korea only has one free afternoon in Taipei next week, so which place should we take them to see? B: I think we should take them to Taipei 101, because it is the city's most iconic building, and they can enjoy the view from the top and shop in the mall below.","t":"A：韓國旅行團下週在台北只有一個自由的下午，我們應該帶他們去看哪裡？ B：我覺得應該帶他們去台北101，因為那是這座城市最具【代表性】的建築，他們可以在頂樓欣賞風景，再到樓下的購物中心逛街。"},{"w":"adore","p":"v.","d":"to love and admire someone very much","c":"非常喜愛；崇拜","s":"A: Why is the toy company paying so much money to put that cartoon voice actor in its new television commercial this winter? B: Young children adore her because she voices their favorite rabbit character, so the marketing team believes parents will buy more toys when kids hear her voice.","t":"A：那家玩具公司為什麼要花這麼多錢，請那位卡通配音員拍今年冬天的新電視廣告？ B：小孩子都很【喜愛】她，因為她為他們最喜歡的兔子角色配音，所以行銷團隊相信孩子聽到她的聲音時，父母就會買更多玩具。"},{"w":"admire","p":"v.","d":"to respect and approve of someone or something","c":"欽佩；讚賞","s":"A: You have read every book written by that famous business leader, so what do you like most about him as a person? B: I really admire the way he started his company with almost no money, and even after becoming rich, he still spends weekends teaching free classes to young people.","t":"A：那位知名企業領袖寫的每本書你都讀過了，你最喜歡他這個人哪一點？ B：我真的很【欽佩】他幾乎沒有錢就創立了公司，而且即使變得富有之後，他週末仍然為年輕人免費上課。"},{"w":"ordeal","p":"n.","d":"a very difficult and unpleasant experience","c":"苦難；痛苦的經歷","s":"A: The famous travel blogger was stuck at the airport for two days because of the typhoon, so how is she feeling now that she is home? B: She is tired but fine, and she wrote a long post about the ordeal, describing how she slept on the floor and shared snacks with other passengers.","t":"A：那位知名旅遊部落客因為颱風被困在機場兩天，她現在回到家了，感覺怎麼樣？ B：她很累但還好，她寫了一篇長文描述這段【痛苦的經歷】，說她怎麼睡在地板上，還和其他旅客分享零食。"},{"w":"model","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to wear clothes in photos or fashion shows; a good example to copy","c":"模特兒；模範","s":"A: The clothing company needs someone to wear the new winter jackets in next month's catalog, so have you found anyone yet? B: Yes, we hired a young model from Tainan who has worked for several big brands, and the photo shoot will take place at the beach next Tuesday if the weather is good.","t":"A：服裝公司需要有人穿新款冬季夾克拍下個月的型錄，你們找到人了嗎？ B：找到了，我們聘請了一位來自台南的年輕【模特兒】，她曾為好幾個大品牌工作過，如果天氣好，下週二會在海邊拍照。"},{"w":"awesome","p":"adj.","d":"very good or impressive","c":"很棒的；令人驚嘆的","s":"A: How was the concert you went to with your coworkers on Friday night at the new stadium near the train station? B: It was absolutely awesome, because the band played all their famous songs, the light show was amazing, and we even got a chance to take a photo with the drummer afterward.","t":"A：你星期五晚上和同事去火車站附近新體育館看的演唱會怎麼樣？ B：真的太【棒了】，因為樂團唱了所有的經典歌曲，燈光秀很精彩，我們之後甚至還有機會和鼓手合照。"}]},{"unit":48,"theme":"Challenge 挑戰","cards":[{"w":"difficulty","p":"n.","d":"a problem that makes something hard to do","c":"困難","s":"A: Why did the new accounting software take three weeks to install when the vendor promised it would only need a few days? B: Our technicians had real difficulty connecting it to the old customer database, because the two systems store dates in different formats, so they had to rewrite several files by hand.","t":"A：廠商保證只要幾天，為什麼新的會計軟體花了三週才安裝好？ B：我們的技術人員在把它連接到舊的客戶資料庫時遇到很大的【困難】，因為兩個系統儲存日期的格式不同，所以他們必須手動改寫好幾個檔案。"},{"w":"obstacle","p":"n.","d":"something that blocks you or makes progress hard","c":"障礙","s":"A: The board likes your plan to open a second store in Tainan, but what do you think could stop the project from moving forward this year? B: The biggest obstacle is the shortage of trained staff in that area, so we will need to start recruiting and training people at least six months before opening.","t":"A：董事會喜歡你在台南開第二家店的計畫，但你認為今年有什麼可能讓這個專案無法推進？ B：最大的【障礙】是那個地區缺乏受過訓練的員工，所以我們至少要在開幕前六個月開始招募和培訓人員。"},{"w":"problem","p":"n.","d":"a situation that causes trouble and needs to be fixed","c":"問題","s":"A: Several customers called this morning to say they could not log in to their online accounts, so do you know what is going on with the website? B: The IT team found a problem with the main server after last night's update, and they expect to fix it and restore full service before lunch.","t":"A：今天早上有好幾位顧客打電話來說他們無法登入線上帳戶，你知道網站怎麼了嗎？ B：IT團隊發現昨晚更新後主伺服器出了【問題】，他們預計在午餐前修好並恢復全部服務。"},{"w":"pressure","p":"n.","d":"a worried feeling caused by too much work or by demands from others","c":"壓力","s":"A: You have been staying at the office until ten o'clock every night this month, so is the new product launch really that difficult? B: Yes, the managers are under a lot of pressure from the head office to finish before the trade show, so everyone on the team is working extra hours.","t":"A：你這個月每天晚上都待在辦公室到十點，新產品上市真的那麼困難嗎？ B：是的，經理們承受總公司很大的【壓力】，必須在商展前完成，所以團隊裡每個人都在加班。"},{"w":"stressful","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel worried and tense","c":"有壓力的；令人緊張的","s":"A: How was your first week as the new customer service supervisor at the airport branch? B: It was very stressful because two flights were canceled during a typhoon, hundreds of angry passengers came to our desk at once, and I had to organize hotel rooms for all of them before midnight.","t":"A：你在機場分店擔任新的客服主管，第一週過得怎麼樣？ B：非常【有壓力】，因為颱風期間有兩班航班取消，數百名憤怒的乘客同時湧到我們的櫃檯，而我必須在午夜前幫他們全部安排好飯店房間。"},{"w":"demanding","p":"adj.","d":"needing a lot of time, energy or skill","c":"要求高的；費力的","s":"A: I heard that you turned down the offer from the consulting firm last week, so may I ask why you decided not to take it? B: The salary was attractive, but the job was too demanding for me right now, since it required traveling abroad every week and answering clients' emails late at night.","t":"A：我聽說你上週拒絕了那家顧問公司的工作邀約，可以問你為什麼決定不接受嗎？ B：薪水很吸引人，但那份工作對我現在來說太【費力】了，因為它要求每週出國出差，還要在深夜回覆客戶的電子郵件。"},{"w":"tough","p":"adj.","d":"difficult to do or deal with","c":"艱難的；棘手的","s":"A: Our sales dropped by almost twenty percent in the last quarter, so how is the company going to explain this to the shareholders at next month's meeting? B: The CEO will admit it was a tough year for the whole industry, and then she will present her plan to cut costs and reach new markets in Asia.","t":"A：我們上一季的銷售額下滑了將近百分之二十，公司要怎麼在下個月的會議上向股東解釋？ B：執行長會承認這對整個產業來說是【艱難】的一年，然後她會提出削減成本並開拓亞洲新市場的計畫。"},{"w":"struggle","p":"v.","d":"to try very hard to do something that is difficult","c":"努力；吃力應付","s":"A: Why does the new intern stay late every evening and ask so many questions during team meetings? B: She is a hard worker, but she seems to struggle with our complicated ordering system, so I have asked one of the senior clerks to sit with her for an hour each afternoon this week.","t":"A：為什麼新來的實習生每天晚上都留得很晚，而且在團隊會議中問這麼多問題？ B：她很認真，但她似乎在我們複雜的訂購系統上【很吃力】，所以我請了一位資深職員這週每天下午陪她一個小時。"},{"w":"setback","p":"n.","d":"something that delays progress or makes a situation worse","c":"挫折；阻礙","s":"A: Is the new shopping center near the train station still going to open in March as the developer announced last year? B: Unfortunately, there has been a serious setback, because heavy rain flooded the underground parking area last month, and the builders now think the opening will be delayed until summer.","t":"A：火車站附近的新購物中心還會像開發商去年宣布的那樣在三月開幕嗎？ B：很遺憾，出現了嚴重的【挫折】，因為上個月大雨淹沒了地下停車場，建商現在認為開幕會延到夏天。"},{"w":"risk","p":"n.","d":"the chance that something bad may happen","c":"風險","s":"A: Our competitor is selling a cheaper version of our printer, so should we lower our prices right away to keep our customers? B: That might help in the short term, but there is a real risk that we will lose money on every unit, so let's study the numbers carefully with the finance team first.","t":"A：我們的競爭對手在賣我們印表機的較便宜版本，我們該立刻降價來留住顧客嗎？ B：短期內可能有幫助，但真的有每台都虧錢的【風險】，所以我們先和財務團隊仔細研究數字吧。"},{"w":"overcome","p":"v.","d":"to succeed in dealing with a difficulty","c":"克服","s":"A: Your presentation to the investors was excellent, but I remember you used to feel very nervous about speaking in front of large groups, didn't you? B: Yes, I joined a public speaking club two years ago, and practicing every week with friendly members really helped me overcome my fear of talking to an audience.","t":"A：你對投資人的簡報非常出色，但我記得你以前在大群人面前說話會很緊張，不是嗎？ B：是的，我兩年前參加了一個演講社，每週和友善的社員一起練習，真的幫助我【克服】了對觀眾說話的恐懼。"},{"w":"cope","p":"v.","d":"to deal successfully with a difficult situation","c":"應付；處理","s":"A: Since the factory received that huge order from Germany, how are the workers on the production line handling the extra work? B: They are managing to cope with the heavy workload for now, but the manager plans to hire twenty temporary workers next month so that nobody has to work weekends.","t":"A：自從工廠接到德國那筆大訂單後，生產線上的工人如何處理額外的工作？ B：他們目前還能【應付】繁重的工作量，但經理打算下個月聘請二十名臨時工，這樣就沒有人必須週末上班。"},{"w":"effort","p":"n.","d":"the energy or hard work used to do something","c":"努力","s":"A: The client from Singapore just signed the contract for three more years, so what do you think finally convinced him to stay with us? B: I think he noticed the extra effort our team made to deliver every order on time, even during the busy holiday season when other suppliers were often late.","t":"A：新加坡的客戶剛簽了再延三年的合約，你認為最後是什麼說服他繼續和我們合作？ B：我想他注意到我們團隊為了準時交付每一筆訂單所付出的額外【努力】，即使在其他供應商常常延遲的忙碌假期季節也是如此。"},{"w":"persistence","p":"n.","d":"continuing to try even when something is difficult","c":"毅力；堅持不懈","s":"A: How did you finally get that big hotel chain to become our customer after they rejected our offer twice last year? B: It took a lot of persistence, because I kept calling their purchasing manager every few months, sent her samples of our new towels, and finally she agreed to meet me in person.","t":"A：去年那家大型連鎖飯店兩度拒絕我們的提案，你最後是怎麼讓他們成為我們的客戶的？ B：這需要很大的【毅力】，因為我每隔幾個月就打電話給他們的採購經理，寄給她我們新毛巾的樣品，最後她終於同意和我見面。"},{"w":"resilience","p":"n.","d":"the ability to recover quickly after something bad happens","c":"韌性；恢復力","s":"A: Many small restaurants in this neighborhood closed during the economic crisis, so how did your family's noodle shop manage to stay open? B: I think it was our resilience, because we quickly started a delivery service, changed the menu to cheaper dishes, and kept our loyal customers coming back every week.","t":"A：經濟危機期間這附近許多小餐廳都倒閉了，你們家的麵店是怎麼撐下來的？ B：我想是靠我們的【韌性】，因為我們很快就開始提供外送服務，把菜單換成較便宜的菜色，並讓忠實顧客每週持續回來光顧。"},{"w":"adapt","p":"v.","d":"to change in order to suit a new situation","c":"適應；調整","s":"A: You moved from the Taipei office to our branch in Toronto six months ago, so how are you finding life and work in Canada? B: At first the cold weather and the different working style were hard, but I am slowly learning to adapt to the new environment, and my colleagues have been very helpful.","t":"A：你六個月前從台北辦公室調到我們多倫多的分公司，你覺得在加拿大的生活和工作如何？ B：一開始寒冷的天氣和不同的工作方式很辛苦，但我正慢慢學著【適應】新環境，而且我的同事們一直很幫忙。"},{"w":"solution","p":"n.","d":"a way to solve a problem","c":"解決辦法","s":"A: Our meeting rooms are always fully booked, and teams keep arguing about who can use them, so what should we do about it? B: One possible solution is to install an online booking system, so every team can reserve a room in advance and see clearly which rooms are free each day.","t":"A：我們的會議室總是被訂滿，各團隊一直為了誰可以使用而爭吵，我們該怎麼辦？ B：一個可行的【解決辦法】是安裝線上預約系統，這樣每個團隊都能事先預約會議室，並清楚看到每天哪些會議室是空的。"},{"w":"failure","p":"n.","d":"a lack of success","c":"失敗","s":"A: Last year's online advertising campaign cost a lot of money, so why are we not using the same agency again this year? B: The campaign was a complete failure, because it attracted very few new customers, and the agency never sent us the reports they promised, so the director decided to look for a new partner.","t":"A：去年的網路廣告活動花了很多錢，為什麼我們今年不再找同一家廣告公司？ B：那次活動完全【失敗】，因為它吸引到的新顧客非常少，而且那家公司從來沒有寄給我們他們承諾的報告，所以主任決定另找新的合作夥伴。"},{"w":"lesson","p":"n.","d":"something useful you learn from an experience","c":"教訓","s":"A: Last month the shipment to our biggest customer arrived a week late because nobody checked the address, so what did the team decide after that mistake? B: We all learned an important lesson from it, and now two people must check every shipping document carefully before any package leaves the warehouse.","t":"A：上個月寄給我們最大客戶的貨晚了一週才到，因為沒有人檢查地址，那次錯誤之後團隊決定了什麼？ B：我們都從中學到了重要的【教訓】，現在每個包裹離開倉庫前，都必須由兩個人仔細檢查所有運送文件。"},{"w":"growth","p":"n.","d":"an increase in size, amount or importance","c":"成長","s":"A: The figures in this report look very good, so which part of the business did best during the past twelve months? B: Our online store showed the strongest growth, with sales rising by thirty-five percent, mainly because more young customers started ordering our skincare products through their phones.","t":"A：這份報告的數字看起來非常好，過去十二個月哪個部分的業務表現最好？ B：我們的網路商店【成長】最強勁，銷售額上升了百分之三十五，主要是因為更多年輕顧客開始用手機訂購我們的保養品。"},{"w":"opportunity","p":"n.","d":"a chance to do something good or useful","c":"機會","s":"A: The head office is looking for someone to manage the new branch in Vietnam for two years, so are you going to apply for the position? B: Yes, I think it is a great opportunity to gain international experience, learn a new language, and show the directors that I am ready for a bigger role.","t":"A：總公司正在找人管理越南的新分公司兩年，你會申請這個職位嗎？ B：會，我認為這是一個累積國際經驗、學習新語言，並向董事們證明我準備好擔任更重要角色的好【機會】。"},{"w":"brave","p":"adj.","d":"willing to do something difficult or frightening","c":"勇敢的","s":"A: I heard that Mr. Lin told the board directly that their plan to close the factory was a mistake, so how did they react? B: Everyone agreed it was a brave thing to do, because he could have lost his job, but in the end the directors listened and found a way to keep most of the workers.","t":"A：我聽說林先生直接告訴董事會他們關閉工廠的計畫是個錯誤，他們有什麼反應？ B：大家都認為這是很【勇敢】的舉動，因為他可能會因此丟掉工作，但最後董事們聽進去了，並找到辦法保留大部分的工人。"},{"w":"determined","p":"adj.","d":"having a strong wish to do something and not letting anything stop you","c":"有決心的；堅決的","s":"A: The new manager has only been here for two months, but the store already looks cleaner and sales are much higher, so how did she do it? B: She is very determined to make this branch the best in the city, so she meets the staff every morning and checks every shelf herself before the doors open.","t":"A：新經理才來兩個月，店裡就已經看起來更乾淨，銷售額也高了很多，她是怎麼做到的？ B：她非常【有決心】要讓這家分店成為全市最好的，所以她每天早上都和員工開會，並在開門前親自檢查每一個貨架。"},{"w":"positive","p":"adj.","d":"hopeful and confident; thinking about the good side","c":"正面的；積極的","s":"A: Our team lost the government contract that we worked on for six months, so how is everyone feeling in the office today? B: People are disappointed, of course, but the director told us to stay positive, because the client praised our proposal and promised to invite us to bid again next year.","t":"A：我們團隊失去了花了六個月爭取的政府合約，今天辦公室裡大家的心情如何？ B：大家當然很失望，但主任要我們保持【積極】，因為客戶稱讚了我們的提案，並答應明年會再邀請我們投標。"},{"w":"mentally","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is connected with the mind","c":"在心理上；精神上","s":"A: You have a job interview with the airline tomorrow morning, and you said there will be five people asking questions, so how are you getting ready? B: I have practiced my answers many times, and tonight I will go to bed early so that I feel mentally prepared and calm when I walk into the room.","t":"A：你明天早上要去航空公司面試，你說會有五個人問你問題，你怎麼準備？ B：我已經練習回答很多次了，今晚我會早點睡，這樣走進面試室時我就會覺得【心理上】已準備好而且很冷靜。"},{"w":"success","p":"n.","d":"the achievement of something you planned or wanted","c":"成功","s":"A: The charity concert last weekend raised more money than any event we have organized before, so what do you think made it work so well? B: Its success came from careful planning, a popular local band that performed for free, and dozens of volunteers who sold tickets in shopping malls for a whole month.","t":"A：上週末的慈善音樂會募到的錢比我們以前辦的任何活動都多，你認為它為什麼這麼順利？ B：它的【成功】來自周詳的規劃、一個免費演出的當地人氣樂團，以及數十位志工整整一個月在購物中心賣票。"},{"w":"confidence","p":"n.","d":"the feeling that you can do something well","c":"信心；自信","s":"A: The new sales assistant seemed very shy when she started, but yesterday she gave an excellent product demonstration to a large group of buyers, didn't she? B: Yes, after three months of training and good feedback from customers, she has gained a lot of confidence, and now she enjoys speaking to people.","t":"A：新的銷售助理剛開始時看起來很害羞，但昨天她為一大群買家做了很出色的產品示範，不是嗎？ B：是的，經過三個月的訓練和顧客的好評，她增加了很多【自信】，現在她很喜歡和人說話。"}]},{"unit":49,"theme":"Change 改變","cards":[{"w":"routine","p":"n.","d":"the usual order in which you do things every day","c":"例行公事；慣例","s":"A: Since the company moved our start time from nine to eight o'clock last month, how have you managed to get your children ready for school every morning? B: It was difficult at first, but we created a new morning routine where everyone packs their bags the night before and eats breakfast together at seven.","t":"A：自從公司上個月把上班時間從九點改到八點，你每天早上是怎麼讓孩子準備好上學的？ B：一開始很困難，但我們建立了一套新的早晨【例行程序】，每個人前一晚就把書包整理好，七點一起吃早餐。"},{"w":"habit","p":"n.","d":"something you do often, almost without thinking","c":"習慣","s":"A: I noticed you stopped buying coffee from the shop downstairs every afternoon, so did the doctor tell you to cut down on caffeine? B: No, I just wanted to save money for my trip to Japan, so I replaced that expensive habit with drinking tea that I bring from home in a bottle.","t":"A：我注意到你不再每天下午到樓下店裡買咖啡了，是醫生叫你少喝咖啡因嗎？ B：不是，我只是想為日本之旅存錢，所以我把那個昂貴的【習慣】換成喝我用瓶子從家裡帶來的茶。"},{"w":"challenging","p":"adj.","d":"difficult in a way that tests your ability","c":"具挑戰性的","s":"A: How do you feel about moving from the sales team to the new project management position that the director offered you last week? B: I think the job will be quite challenging because I have to lead twelve people and manage a tight budget, but I am excited to learn new skills and grow.","t":"A：你對於從業務團隊轉到主任上週提供給你的新專案管理職位感覺如何？ B：我覺得這份工作會相當【具挑戰性】，因為我必須帶領十二個人並管理緊縮的預算，但我很期待學習新技能並成長。"},{"w":"afraid","p":"adj.","d":"feeling fear or worry about something","c":"害怕的；擔心的","s":"A: Why didn't Tom say anything during the meeting when the manager asked for opinions about the new working schedule? B: He told me later that he was afraid that his ideas would sound silly, because he only joined the company two weeks ago and does not know everyone yet.","t":"A：經理在會議中詢問大家對新工作時間表的意見時，湯姆為什麼什麼都沒說？ B：他後來告訴我，他【害怕】自己的想法聽起來很蠢，因為他兩週前才進公司，還不認識每個人。"},{"w":"resist","p":"v.","d":"to refuse to accept something or try to stop it","c":"抗拒；抵抗","s":"A: Several older workers in the warehouse are unhappy about the new scanning system, so what is the best way to help them accept it? B: People often resist changes when they do not understand the reasons, so let's hold a short training session and show them how the system will save them time.","t":"A：倉庫裡好幾位年長員工對新的掃描系統不滿，幫助他們接受它最好的方法是什麼？ B：人們不了解原因時常常會【抗拒】改變，所以我們來辦一場簡短的訓練課程，讓他們看看這套系統如何幫他們節省時間。"},{"w":"frequently","p":"adv.","d":"often; many times","c":"頻繁地；經常","s":"A: Do you know why the printer on the third floor keeps breaking down, even though the technician repaired it last month? B: The marketing team uses it very frequently to print large posters and brochures, so I think we should buy a stronger machine instead of fixing this old one again.","t":"A：你知道為什麼三樓的印表機一直故障嗎？明明技術人員上個月才修好。 B：行銷團隊非常【頻繁地】用它來印大型海報和手冊，所以我認為我們應該買一台更耐用的機器，而不是再修這台舊的。"},{"w":"permanent","p":"adj.","d":"lasting for a long time or forever","c":"永久的；長期的","s":"A: You have been working at the front desk as a temporary staff member for six months, so has the hotel offered you a contract yet? B: Yes, the manager called me yesterday and said they want to give me a permanent position starting in January, with health insurance and paid holidays.","t":"A：你在櫃檯當臨時員工已經六個月了，飯店給你合約了嗎？ B：有，經理昨天打電話給我，說他們想從一月開始給我一個【長期正式的】職位，有健康保險和帶薪假。"},{"w":"promotion","p":"n.","d":"a move to a higher job or rank","c":"升職；晉升","s":"A: Congratulations, I heard you will be the new head of the customer service department next month, so how did you hear the news? B: Thank you, my boss invited me to lunch on Friday and told me about the promotion, and she also said my salary will increase by fifteen percent.","t":"A：恭喜，我聽說你下個月要成為客服部門的新主管，你是怎麼得知消息的？ B：謝謝，我老闆週五請我吃午餐，告訴我【升職】的事，她還說我的薪水會增加百分之十五。"},{"w":"adapt","p":"v.","d":"to change your behavior to fit a new situation","c":"適應","s":"A: The company is moving our office from Taipei to Kaohsiung next spring, so are you worried about living in a new city? B: A little, but I have moved several times before, and I usually adapt quickly to new places by joining local clubs and exploring the neighborhood on weekends.","t":"A：公司明年春天要把辦公室從台北搬到高雄，你擔心住在新城市嗎？ B：有一點，但我以前搬過好幾次家，我通常會參加當地社團、週末探索街坊，很快就【適應】新的地方。"},{"w":"develop","p":"v.","d":"to create something new or make it better over time","c":"開發；發展","s":"A: Our online shop is getting more orders from customers in Japan and Korea, so what should the IT team focus on this year? B: I think they should develop a mobile app in Japanese and Korean, because most of these customers shop on their phones during their train rides to work.","t":"A：我們的網路商店接到越來越多日本和韓國顧客的訂單，IT團隊今年應該把重點放在哪裡？ B：我認為他們應該【開發】一個日文和韓文的手機應用程式，因為這些顧客大多在搭火車上班時用手機購物。"},{"w":"decade","p":"n.","d":"a period of ten years","c":"十年","s":"A: The town looks so different from the photos in the lobby, so how long has this hotel been here? B: It opened in the 1980s, and during the last decade the area has changed a lot, with new shopping malls, office towers, and a subway station built right across the street.","t":"A：這個小鎮和大廳裡的照片看起來差好多，這間飯店在這裡多久了？ B：它在1980年代開幕，在過去【十年】裡，這一帶改變了很多，蓋了新的購物中心、辦公大樓，對街還蓋了一座地鐵站。"},{"w":"metamorphosis","p":"n.","d":"a complete change into something very different","c":"蛻變；徹底轉變","s":"A: I visited your restaurant again last night, and I could hardly believe it was the same place after the renovation, so who designed the new interior? B: A young designer from Tainan planned the whole metamorphosis, turning our dark old dining room into a bright, modern space with plants, large windows, and an open kitchen.","t":"A：我昨晚又去了你的餐廳，裝修後我幾乎不敢相信是同一個地方，新的室內是誰設計的？ B：一位台南的年輕設計師規劃了整個【蛻變】，把我們陰暗的老用餐區變成一個有植物、大窗戶和開放式廚房的明亮現代空間。"},{"w":"secure","p":"v.","d":"to get something important after a lot of effort","c":"獲得；爭取到","s":"A: The factory almost closed last year because of falling orders, so how did it manage to stay open and keep all its workers? B: The new sales director worked very hard to secure a three-year contract with a large car company, which brought in enough money to buy new machines.","t":"A：去年工廠因為訂單下滑差點關門，它是怎麼撐下去並保住所有員工的？ B：新的業務總監非常努力地【爭取到】一份與大型汽車公司簽的三年合約，帶進了足夠的錢買新機器。"},{"w":"incumbent","p":"n.","d":"the person who holds an official position now","c":"現任者","s":"A: Do you think the city will finally build the new bike lanes after the mayor election next month? B: It depends on who wins, because the incumbent has promised to finish the project, but the other candidate says the money should go to repairing old roads and public schools instead.","t":"A：你認為下個月市長選舉後，市政府終於會蓋新的自行車道嗎？ B：要看誰贏，因為【現任者】承諾要完成這個計畫，但另一位候選人說這筆錢應該改用來修舊道路和公立學校。"},{"w":"improve","p":"v.","d":"to make something better","c":"改善；提升","s":"A: Our customers have complained that the website is slow and confusing, so what are we going to do about it this quarter? B: We have hired an outside company to improve the design, and they promise that people will be able to find products and pay in less than two minutes.","t":"A：顧客抱怨網站又慢又難用，這一季我們打算怎麼處理？ B：我們請了一家外部公司來【改善】設計，他們保證大家能在兩分鐘內找到產品並付款。"},{"w":"lazy","p":"adj.","d":"not wanting to work or make an effort","c":"懶惰的","s":"A: Why did the manager decide to change the cleaning company that looks after our office building? B: Some of the old staff were quite lazy and often left the kitchen dirty and the trash bins full, so many employees complained, and the manager found a more reliable company last week.","t":"A：經理為什麼決定更換負責我們辦公大樓的清潔公司？ B：之前有些員工相當【懶惰】，常常讓廚房髒亂、垃圾桶滿出來，所以很多員工抱怨，經理上週就找了一家更可靠的公司。"},{"w":"awkward","p":"adj.","d":"uncomfortable or embarrassing","c":"尷尬的；不自在的","s":"A: How was your first day at the new branch after you transferred from the head office? B: It felt a little awkward in the morning because nobody knew my name and I sat alone at lunch, but in the afternoon my team leader introduced me to everyone, and things became much easier.","t":"A：你從總公司調到新分店後的第一天怎麼樣？ B：早上感覺有點【尷尬】，因為沒人知道我的名字，午餐時我一個人坐，但下午組長把我介紹給大家，事情就輕鬆多了。"},{"w":"struggle","p":"v.","d":"to try very hard to do something difficult","c":"努力掙扎；奮鬥","s":"A: Many small bookstores in this neighborhood have closed in the past few years, so how is your shop doing? B: We still struggle to pay the rent some months because more people buy books online, but we have started holding reading events and selling coffee, which brings in new customers.","t":"A：這一帶很多小書店在過去幾年關門了，你的店經營得如何？ B：有些月份我們還是【很吃力地】付房租，因為越來越多人在網路上買書，但我們開始舉辦讀書活動和賣咖啡，吸引了新顧客。"},{"w":"boost","p":"v.","d":"to increase or improve something","c":"提升；促進","s":"A: Sales of our winter jackets have been lower than expected this year, so what can we do before the season ends? B: The marketing team suggests a weekend discount and a social media contest, which should boost sales quickly and help us clear the stock before the spring collection arrives.","t":"A：我們的冬季外套今年銷售比預期差，在季節結束前我們能做什麼？ B：行銷團隊建議週末打折和社群媒體比賽，應該能迅速【提升】銷售量，幫我們在春季新品到貨前清掉庫存。"},{"w":"recognize","p":"v.","d":"to know someone or something because you have seen it before","c":"認出；辨認","s":"A: You have not been back to your hometown for fifteen years, so did it still look the same when you visited last weekend? B: Not at all, I could hardly recognize the main street because the old market was replaced by a shopping center and most of the small shops had new names.","t":"A：你已經十五年沒回家鄉了，上週末回去時還是一樣嗎？ B：完全不一樣，我幾乎無法【認出】大街，因為舊市場被購物中心取代，大多數小店也都換了新名字。"},{"w":"catch","p":"v.","d":"to get on a bus, train, or plane in time","c":"趕上；搭上","s":"A: Since the bus company changed its timetable last week, how have you been getting to the office on time? B: I now leave home twenty minutes earlier to catch the 7:15 bus, because the next one does not come until 7:50, and that would make me late for the morning meeting.","t":"A：自從公車公司上週更改時刻表後，你都怎麼準時到公司？ B：我現在提早二十分鐘出門去【趕上】7點15分的公車，因為下一班要到7點50分才來，那會讓我晨會遲到。"},{"w":"positive","p":"adj.","d":"hopeful and confident; showing approval","c":"積極的；正面的","s":"A: How did the staff react when the CEO announced that everyone could work from home two days a week? B: Most people were very positive about it, because they will save time on commuting, but a few team leaders worried that it might be harder to hold meetings and share ideas.","t":"A：執行長宣布每個人每週可以在家工作兩天時，員工的反應如何？ B：大多數人對此非常【正面】，因為能節省通勤時間，但有幾位組長擔心開會和交流想法可能會變得比較困難。"},{"w":"inevitable","p":"adj.","d":"certain to happen and impossible to stop","c":"不可避免的","s":"A: Do you think the bank will close more of its small branches now that so many customers use the mobile app? B: I am afraid it is inevitable, because fewer people visit the branches each year, and the company says it needs to cut costs and invest more money in online services.","t":"A：既然這麼多顧客使用手機應用程式，你認為銀行會關閉更多小分行嗎？ B：恐怕這是【無可避免的】，因為每年去分行的人越來越少，而公司說需要削減成本，把更多錢投入線上服務。"},{"w":"transformation","p":"n.","d":"a complete change in form or character","c":"轉變；轉型","s":"A: The old textile factory near the river has been empty for years, so what is the city planning to do with it? B: The city has hired an architect to lead its transformation into a cultural center with art studios, a small theater, and a market where local farmers can sell vegetables on weekends.","t":"A：河邊那間舊紡織廠已經空了好幾年，市政府打算怎麼處理？ B：市政府聘請了一位建築師主導它的【轉型】，把它變成一個有藝術工作室、小劇場和週末讓當地農民賣菜的市集的文化中心。"},{"w":"favorable","p":"adj.","d":"good and likely to help something succeed","c":"有利的；良好的","s":"A: The weather has been terrible this month, so do you think the outdoor company sports day can still happen on Saturday? B: The forecast looks favorable for the weekend, with sunny skies and light wind, so we will go ahead with the plan, but we will also book the gym in case it rains.","t":"A：這個月天氣很糟，你覺得公司戶外運動會週六還能舉行嗎？ B：週末的天氣預報看起來很【有利】，晴天又微風，所以我們會照計畫進行，但也會預訂體育館以防下雨。"},{"w":"frustrating","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel annoyed because you cannot do what you want","c":"令人沮喪的","s":"A: You look tired today, so did something happen with the new accounting software that the company installed on Monday? B: Yes, it has been really frustrating because the program keeps freezing whenever I try to save a report, and I had to type the same numbers three times this morning.","t":"A：你今天看起來很累，週一公司安裝的新會計軟體出了什麼事嗎？ B：對，真的很【令人沮喪】，因為每次我要儲存報表程式就當掉，我今天早上同樣的數字打了三次。"},{"w":"transitional","p":"adj.","d":"relating to a change from one state to another","c":"過渡的","s":"A: The new manager starts in March, but our current manager leaves at the end of January, so who will lead the team in February? B: During this transitional period, the senior supervisor will take care of daily decisions, and both managers will also hold a video call every week to share important information.","t":"A：新經理三月上任，但現任經理一月底就離職，那二月誰來帶領團隊？ B：在這段【過渡】期間，資深主管會處理日常決策，兩位經理也會每週開一次視訊會議交接重要資訊。"},{"w":"inquisitive","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to learn and asking many questions","c":"好奇的；愛發問的","s":"A: The new intern asks so many questions about every department, so do you think it bothers the other staff members? B: Not at all, most people like how inquisitive she is, because her questions show that she really wants to learn how the company works, and some of them even helped us find problems.","t":"A：新來的實習生對每個部門都問好多問題，你覺得會打擾到其他員工嗎？ B：一點也不，大多數人都喜歡她這麼【好奇好問】，因為她的問題顯示她真的想了解公司如何運作，有些問題甚至幫我們發現了問題。"},{"w":"fascinating","p":"adj.","d":"extremely interesting","c":"極有趣的；引人入勝的","s":"A: How was the conference in Singapore that you attended last week with the research team? B: It was really fascinating, especially a talk about how robots are changing hospitals, and I took so many notes that I want to share them with everyone at our team meeting on Thursday afternoon.","t":"A：你上週和研究團隊去參加的新加坡會議怎麼樣？ B：真的非常【引人入勝】，尤其是一場關於機器人如何改變醫院的演講，我做了好多筆記，想在星期四下午的團隊會議上跟大家分享。"},{"w":"inspiring","p":"adj.","d":"making people feel excited and want to do something good","c":"鼓舞人心的","s":"A: Why did so many employees sign up for the volunteer program after the company's annual meeting? B: The guest speaker gave a very inspiring talk about how she changed her life by helping children in poor villages, and many people said they wanted to do something meaningful too.","t":"A：公司年會後，為什麼這麼多員工報名志工計畫？ B：特別來賓發表了一場非常【鼓舞人心】的演講，講她如何透過幫助貧困村莊的孩子改變自己的人生，很多人說他們也想做些有意義的事。"},{"w":"regrettable","p":"adj.","d":"that you feel sorry about; unfortunate","c":"令人遺憾的","s":"A: The online store sent hundreds of customers the wrong items during the holiday sale, so what did the company say about the problem? B: The CEO called the mistake very regrettable and promised that every customer will receive a full refund, free shipping, and a discount code for their next order.","t":"A：網路商店在假期特賣期間寄錯了幾百位顧客的商品，公司對這個問題怎麼說？ B：執行長稱這個錯誤非常【令人遺憾】，並承諾每位顧客都會獲得全額退款、免運費和下次訂購的折扣碼。"}]},{"unit":50,"theme":"Changing Room 更衣室","cards":[{"w":"fitting room","p":"n.","d":"a small room in a shop where you try on clothes","c":"試衣間","s":"A: I want to check whether these dark blue trousers suit me before I pay, but I can't see anywhere private in this busy department store, so where should I go? B: The fitting room is just behind the shoe section on the second floor, and a staff member there will give you a number card for each item you take in.","t":"A：我想在付款前看看這條深藍色褲子適不適合我，但在這間繁忙的百貨公司裡我看不到任何隱密的地方，我該去哪裡？ B：【試衣間】就在二樓鞋區的後面，那裡的工作人員會為你帶進去的每件衣物發一張號碼牌。"},{"w":"locker room","p":"n.","d":"a room where people change clothes before or after sports","c":"（運動場所的）更衣室","s":"A: After the company football match on Saturday afternoon, where can the players take a shower and get dressed before we all go out for dinner together? B: The sports center has a large locker room next to the main field, with hot showers and plenty of space, so everyone can get ready there in about twenty minutes.","t":"A：週六下午公司足球賽結束後，球員們可以在哪裡沖澡換衣服，然後大家再一起去吃晚餐？ B：運動中心主球場旁邊有一間很大的【更衣室】，有熱水淋浴和充足的空間，所以大家大約二十分鐘就能在那裡準備好。"},{"w":"locker","p":"n.","d":"a small cupboard with a lock for keeping your things safe","c":"置物櫃","s":"A: I'm going to the gym straight from the office tonight, but I'm worried about leaving my laptop and wallet somewhere unsafe while I exercise, so what do you suggest? B: Each member can rent a small locker with a key for just fifty dollars a month, and it is large enough for a laptop bag and a jacket.","t":"A：我今晚要從辦公室直接去健身房，但我擔心運動時把筆電和錢包放在不安全的地方，你有什麼建議？ B：每位會員每個月只要五十元就可以租一個附鑰匙的小【置物櫃】，空間大到可以放下筆電包和一件外套。"},{"w":"mirror","p":"n.","d":"a piece of glass in which you can see yourself","c":"鏡子","s":"A: The customers keep complaining that they cannot see how the clothes look from behind after they try them on, so how can we solve this problem cheaply? B: Let's put a tall mirror on the back wall of each changing area, so people can turn around and check the whole outfit without asking a salesperson for help.","t":"A：顧客一直抱怨試穿後看不到衣服背面的樣子，我們要怎麼便宜地解決這個問題？ B：我們在每個更衣區的後牆裝一面高的【鏡子】，這樣大家可以轉身檢查整套服裝，不必請店員幫忙。"},{"w":"bench","p":"n.","d":"a long seat for two or more people","c":"長凳","s":"A: Some older customers have told us that they feel tired while they wait for their family members outside the changing rooms, so is there anything simple we can do? B: We could place a long wooden bench along the wall near the entrance, so they can sit down comfortably and keep an eye on the shopping bags.","t":"A：有些年長顧客告訴我們，他們在更衣室外等家人時覺得很累，有什麼簡單的方法可以改善嗎？ B：我們可以在入口附近沿著牆放一張長的木製【長凳】，讓他們可以舒服地坐著，同時看顧購物袋。"},{"w":"curtain","p":"n.","d":"a piece of cloth that hangs down to cover a window or an opening","c":"簾子；窗簾","s":"A: One of the changing rooms in the women's section doesn't close properly anymore, and a customer felt uncomfortable using it this morning, so what exactly is wrong with it? B: The thick curtain that covers the entrance is too short and keeps sliding open, so I have already ordered a longer one that should arrive on Thursday.","t":"A：女裝區有一間更衣室關不好了，今天早上有位顧客用起來覺得很不自在，到底是哪裡出了問題？ B：遮住入口的那條厚【簾子】太短，而且一直滑開，所以我已經訂了一條更長的，應該週四會到。"},{"w":"door","p":"n.","d":"the thing you open and close to go into a room","c":"門","s":"A: The new changing rooms look really modern, but I noticed that several customers had trouble locking themselves in while they were trying things on, so what is the issue? B: The lock on each door is placed too high for shorter people to reach easily, so the builder will come back next week and move them lower.","t":"A：新的更衣室看起來很現代，但我注意到有好幾位顧客試穿時很難把自己鎖在裡面，問題出在哪裡？ B：每扇【門】上的鎖裝得太高，個子較矮的人不容易搆到，所以施工人員下週會回來把鎖裝低一點。"},{"w":"privacy","p":"n.","d":"the state of being alone and not seen by other people","c":"隱私","s":"A: Why did the manager decide to replace all the old plastic panels in the changing area with solid wooden walls, even though it cost the store a lot of money? B: Many shoppers complained that people walking by could see inside, and she believes every customer deserves complete privacy while trying on clothes.","t":"A：為什麼經理決定把更衣區所有的舊塑膠隔板換成實心木牆，即使這花了店裡很多錢？ B：許多顧客抱怨路過的人看得到裡面，而她認為每位顧客在試穿衣服時都應該享有完全的【隱私】。"},{"w":"clothes","p":"n.","d":"things you wear, such as shirts and trousers","c":"衣服","s":"A: The hotel staff change into their work uniforms when they arrive every morning, so where should they leave the things they wore on the way to work? B: There is a staff room on the basement level where everyone can hang their own clothes on a rail and pick them up again at the end of the shift.","t":"A：飯店員工每天早上到班後會換上工作制服，那他們上班途中穿的東西要放在哪裡？ B：地下室有一間員工休息室，每個人都可以把自己的【衣服】掛在衣架桿上，下班時再拿回來。"},{"w":"outfit","p":"n.","d":"a set of clothes worn together","c":"一套服裝","s":"A: I have an important job interview at a bank next Tuesday, but I'm not sure what to wear, so could you come shopping with me this weekend? B: Of course, I think a dark jacket with matching trousers and simple shoes would make a smart and professional outfit, and the mall downtown is having a sale.","t":"A：我下週二在一家銀行有個重要的面試，但我不確定要穿什麼，你這個週末可以陪我去逛街嗎？ B：當然，我覺得深色外套配上同色系長褲和簡單的鞋子，會是一套俐落又專業的【服裝】，而且市中心的購物中心正在特價。"},{"w":"try on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to put on clothes to see if they fit or look good","c":"試穿","s":"A: I really like the gray coat in the window, but this brand often makes its clothes a little small, so should I just buy it online to save time? B: I think you should try on the coat in the store first, because the changing rooms are free right now and you can return it easily if it feels wrong.","t":"A：我很喜歡櫥窗裡那件灰色大衣，但這個牌子的衣服常常偏小，我是不是直接在網路上買比較省時間？ B：我覺得你應該先在店裡【試穿】那件大衣，因為現在更衣室剛好沒人，而且如果覺得不對也很容易退貨。"},{"w":"change","p":"v.","d":"to take off your clothes and put on different ones","c":"換（衣服）","s":"A: Our client meeting finishes at five, and the charity dinner starts at six on the other side of the city, so will we have enough time to get ready? B: Yes, the hotel has agreed to give us a small room near the lobby, so we can quickly change into our evening clothes there and take a taxi straight to the event.","t":"A：我們的客戶會議五點結束，而慈善晚宴六點在城市的另一頭開始，我們有足夠的時間準備嗎？ B：有，飯店同意在大廳附近給我們一間小房間，我們可以在那裡迅速【換】上晚禮服，然後直接搭計程車去會場。"},{"w":"size","p":"n.","d":"how big or small something is, such as clothes or shoes","c":"尺寸","s":"A: The blue shirt I ordered for the team photo is much too small around the shoulders, so do you think the store will let me exchange it? B: Yes, as long as you keep the receipt and the label, they will happily give you a larger size, and they usually have extra stock in the back room.","t":"A：我為團體照訂的藍色襯衫肩膀太小了，你覺得店家會讓我換嗎？ B：會的，只要你保留收據和標籤，他們會很樂意給你大一號的【尺寸】，而且他們後面的倉庫通常有額外庫存。"},{"w":"fit","p":"v.","d":"to be the right size and shape for someone","c":"合身","s":"A: You bought those black trousers for the company dinner last month, so why haven't you worn them to the office yet? B: Unfortunately, they don't fit me well anymore because I've been eating so many snacks at my desk during busy weeks, so I'll take them to a tailor this weekend to have them made bigger.","t":"A：你上個月為了公司晚宴買了那條黑色長褲，為什麼還沒穿來辦公室？ B：可惜它已經不太【合身】了，因為忙碌的那幾週我在座位上吃了太多零食，所以這個週末我會拿去給裁縫改大一點。"},{"w":"tight","p":"adj.","d":"fitting your body very closely, often too closely","c":"緊的","s":"A: You look a little uncomfortable in that new suit, so is something wrong with it, or are you just nervous about giving the presentation this afternoon? B: To be honest, the jacket feels quite tight around my arms, so I can hardly lift them, and I should have tried a bigger one before I bought it.","t":"A：你穿那套新西裝看起來有點不自在，是衣服有問題，還是你只是對今天下午的簡報感到緊張？ B：老實說，這件外套的手臂部分感覺很【緊】，我幾乎舉不起手臂，我買之前應該先試穿大一號的。"},{"w":"loose","p":"adj.","d":"too big and not fitting closely","c":"寬鬆的；鬆的","s":"A: The new warehouse uniforms arrived this morning, but several workers say they are uncomfortable, so what seems to be the main problem with them? B: The trousers are so loose around the waist that people keep pulling them up while they carry boxes, which could be dangerous near the heavy machines.","t":"A：新的倉庫制服今天早上送到了，但有好幾位工人說穿起來不舒服，主要問題是什麼？ B：褲子腰部太【鬆】了，大家搬箱子時一直要把褲子往上拉，在重型機器附近可能很危險。"},{"w":"comfortable","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel relaxed, with no pain","c":"舒適的","s":"A: Our team will be walking around the trade fair for about eight hours tomorrow, meeting suppliers and visiting booths, so what kind of shoes should I wear? B: Choose something soft and comfortable instead of your new leather shoes, because the halls are huge and your feet will hurt badly by lunchtime otherwise.","t":"A：我們團隊明天要在商展裡走大約八個小時，和供應商見面並參觀攤位，我該穿什麼鞋子？ B：選一雙柔軟又【舒適】的鞋，不要穿你的新皮鞋，因為展館很大，不然到午餐時間你的腳就會很痛。"},{"w":"crowded","p":"adj.","d":"full of people","c":"擁擠的","s":"A: I'd like to buy a few shirts for my business trip, so do you think Saturday afternoon is a good time to visit the shopping mall near the station? B: I wouldn't go then, because the stores are always crowded on weekends and you might wait twenty minutes for a changing room, so try a weekday evening instead.","t":"A：我想為出差買幾件襯衫，你覺得週六下午去車站附近的購物中心是好時機嗎？ B：我不會那時候去，因為週末店裡總是很【擁擠】，你可能要等二十分鐘才有更衣室，改在平日晚上去吧。"},{"w":"empty","p":"adj.","d":"with no people or things inside","c":"空的","s":"A: The staff changing room downstairs is usually full of people at eight in the morning, so when is the best time for me to use it before my shift? B: It is almost always empty around seven thirty, because most of the early workers have already gone upstairs and the others don't arrive until later.","t":"A：樓下的員工更衣室早上八點通常擠滿了人，我上班前什麼時候使用最好？ B：七點半左右那裡幾乎都是【空的】，因為大部分早班員工已經上樓了，其他人則要晚一點才會到。"},{"w":"clean","p":"adj.","d":"not dirty","c":"乾淨的","s":"A: A gym member wrote an angry online review saying that the shower area smelled bad last weekend, so how should we respond to make customers trust us again? B: Let's hire an extra cleaner for the weekends and promise that the changing area will be kept clean and dry at all times, then reply politely to the review.","t":"A：一位健身房會員在網路上寫了一則憤怒的評論，說上週末淋浴區很臭，我們該如何回應才能讓顧客重新信任我們？ B：我們週末多請一位清潔人員，並承諾更衣區隨時保持【乾淨】和乾燥，然後禮貌地回覆那則評論。"},{"w":"messy","p":"adj.","d":"untidy, with things in the wrong places","c":"凌亂的","s":"A: The store manager looked very unhappy after she checked the changing rooms at closing time yesterday, so did something go wrong during the evening shift? B: Yes, the rooms were really messy, with shirts and jeans lying on the floor everywhere, because nobody had time to collect them during the busy sale.","t":"A：店長昨天打烊時檢查完更衣室後看起來很不高興，晚班是不是出了什麼問題？ B：是的，那些房間真的很【凌亂】，到處都是丟在地上的襯衫和牛仔褲，因為在忙碌的特賣期間沒有人有時間收。"},{"w":"hook","p":"n.","d":"a curved piece of metal or plastic for hanging things on","c":"掛鉤","s":"A: Customers keep putting their coats and handbags on the floor of the changing rooms, which makes the area look dirty, so how can we improve this? B: We should fix a metal hook on the wall inside each room, so people have a proper place to hang their things while they are trying on clothes.","t":"A：顧客一直把外套和手提包放在更衣室地上，讓那裡看起來很髒，我們該如何改善？ B：我們應該在每間更衣室的牆上裝一個金屬【掛鉤】，讓大家試穿衣服時有適當的地方掛東西。"},{"w":"bag","p":"n.","d":"a container for carrying things","c":"袋子；包包","s":"A: I'm flying to Singapore for a two-day conference next week, and I don't want to wait at the airport for my luggage, so what should I bring? B: Just pack one small bag that fits in the overhead space, with two shirts, a pair of trousers, and your laptop, and you can walk straight out after landing.","t":"A：我下週要飛去新加坡參加為期兩天的會議，我不想在機場等行李，我該帶什麼？ B：只要帶一個能放進頭頂置物櫃的小【包包】，裝兩件襯衫、一條長褲和你的筆電，降落後就可以直接走出去。"},{"w":"shoes","p":"n.","d":"things you wear on your feet","c":"鞋子","s":"A: The office is installing new carpet throughout the meeting rooms this month, so is there any new rule that the staff should follow during that time? B: Yes, everyone must take off their outdoor shoes at the entrance and wear the slippers provided, so the carpet will stay clean and won't get damaged.","t":"A：辦公室這個月要在所有會議室鋪新地毯，這段期間員工有什麼新規定要遵守嗎？ B：有，每個人在入口都必須脫掉外面穿的【鞋子】並換上提供的拖鞋，這樣地毯才能保持乾淨、不會損壞。"},{"w":"uniform","p":"n.","d":"special clothes that all workers or students of a group wear","c":"制服","s":"A: I start my new job at the hotel reception desk on Monday morning, but nobody has told me what I'm supposed to wear on the first day, so do you know? B: The hotel will give you a dark green uniform with your name badge, and you can pick it up from the staff office before your shift begins.","t":"A：我週一早上要開始在飯店櫃檯的新工作，但沒有人告訴我第一天應該穿什麼，你知道嗎？ B：飯店會給你一套深綠色的【制服】和名牌，你可以在上班前到員工辦公室領取。"},{"w":"sportswear","p":"n.","d":"clothes and shoes made for doing sports","c":"運動服裝","s":"A: Our company is organizing a team hiking day in the mountains next month, so should I wear my usual office clothes or something else? B: You'd better wear light sportswear and running shoes, because the trail is long and hot, and you'll want clothes that dry quickly when you sweat.","t":"A：我們公司下個月要在山上舉辦團隊健行日，我該穿平常的上班服裝還是別的？ B：你最好穿輕便的【運動服裝】和跑鞋，因為步道又長又熱，你會需要流汗時能快乾的衣服。"},{"w":"queue","p":"v.","d":"to wait in a line of people for your turn","c":"排隊","s":"A: The department store is having its biggest sale of the year this weekend, so how early should we arrive if we want to try on the discounted coats? B: We'll probably have to queue for at least half an hour outside the changing rooms, so let's get there right when the doors open at ten.","t":"A：百貨公司這個週末舉辦年度最大的特賣，如果我們想試穿打折的大衣，應該多早到？ B：我們可能得在更衣室外【排隊】至少半小時，所以我們十點一開門就到吧。"},{"w":"available","p":"adj.","d":"free to be used","c":"可用的；空出來的","s":"A: There are only three changing rooms in this small shop, and all of them seem to have people inside right now, so how will I know when it's my turn? B: The assistant will call you as soon as a room is available, and in the meantime you can look at the new scarves near the front counter.","t":"A：這間小店只有三間更衣室，現在好像都有人在裡面，我怎麼知道什麼時候輪到我？ B：一有房間【空出來】，店員就會馬上叫你，在這期間你可以看看櫃檯附近的新圍巾。"},{"w":"sign","p":"n.","d":"a board with words or pictures that gives information","c":"標示；告示牌","s":"A: Some customers walked right past the changing rooms yesterday because they didn't know where they were, so how can we make them easier to find? B: Let's put a large sign with an arrow above the hallway near the escalator, so shoppers can see the way to the changing area from anywhere on the floor.","t":"A：昨天有些顧客直接走過了更衣室，因為他們不知道在哪裡，我們要怎麼讓它更容易被找到？ B：我們在手扶梯附近的走廊上方放一個大的箭頭【標示】，讓顧客在樓層任何地方都能看到往更衣區的路。"}]},{"unit":51,"theme":"Charity 慈善","cards":[{"w":"donation","p":"n.","d":"money or goods given to help people or a group","c":"捐款；捐贈物","s":"A: The hospital's children's ward needs new beds and toys before the winter holidays, so how can our company help them without spending too much time on planning? B: We could ask every department to make a small donation this month, and the finance team will collect the money and send it to the hospital together.","t":"A：醫院的兒童病房在寒假前需要新的病床和玩具，我們公司要怎麼幫忙又不必花太多時間規劃？ B：我們可以請每個部門這個月做一筆小額【捐款】，由財務團隊收齊後一起送到醫院。"},{"w":"donate","p":"v.","d":"to give money or things to help others","c":"捐贈；捐款","s":"A: Our office is moving to the new building downtown next month, and we have dozens of old desks, chairs, and computers that still work well, so what should we do with them? B: I called a local school yesterday, and they would be very happy if we donate the furniture and computers to their new library.","t":"A：我們辦公室下個月要搬到市中心的新大樓，我們有好幾十張還能用的舊桌椅和電腦，該怎麼處理？ B：我昨天打電話給一所當地學校，如果我們把家具和電腦【捐贈】給他們的新圖書館，他們會非常開心。"},{"w":"volunteer","p":"v.","d":"to offer to do work without being paid","c":"自願做；當志工","s":"A: The community center is organizing a beach clean-up on Saturday morning, but they still need about twenty more people to pick up trash and carry bags, so are you free that day? B: Yes, my sister and I both want to volunteer, because we often swim there and are worried about all the plastic on the sand.","t":"A：社區中心週六早上要舉辦淨灘活動，但他們還需要大約二十個人撿垃圾和搬袋子，你那天有空嗎？ B：有，我和我姊姊都想去【當志工】，因為我們常在那裡游泳，很擔心沙灘上那些塑膠垃圾。"},{"w":"fundraising","p":"n.","d":"the activity of collecting money for a cause","c":"募款","s":"A: The school orchestra wants to travel to Japan for an international music competition next spring, but the trip will cost a lot of money, so how will the parents pay for it? B: They are planning a big fundraising effort, including a bake sale, a concert, and an online page where friends and relatives can give money.","t":"A：學校管弦樂團明年春天想去日本參加國際音樂比賽，但這趟旅程要花很多錢，家長們要怎麼負擔？ B：他們正在規劃一場大型【募款】活動，包括義賣烘焙點心、一場音樂會，還有一個讓親友可以捐錢的網頁。"},{"w":"fundraiser","p":"n.","d":"an event held to collect money for a cause","c":"募款活動","s":"A: I saw on the company website that the marketing team rented the hotel ballroom next Friday evening, so is it for a product launch or a party? B: Neither, it is a fundraiser for the children's hospital, and tickets cost two thousand dollars each, with all the money going to buy medical equipment.","t":"A：我在公司網站上看到行銷團隊租了下週五晚上的飯店宴會廳，是要辦產品發表會還是派對？ B：都不是，那是為兒童醫院舉辦的【募款活動】，每張票兩千元，所有收入都會用來購買醫療設備。"},{"w":"support","p":"v.","d":"to help someone, often by giving money or encouragement","c":"支持；援助","s":"A: Many small farms in the mountains lost most of their fruit after the typhoon last week, and the farmers are worried about paying their bills, so is there anything our supermarket chain can do? B: We could support them by buying their remaining fruit at a fair price and selling it in our stores with a special sign.","t":"A：上週颱風過後，山區許多小農場損失了大部分的水果，農民們擔心付不出帳單，我們連鎖超市能做些什麼嗎？ B：我們可以用合理的價格收購他們剩下的水果，並在店裡放上特別標示販售，以此來【支持】他們。"},{"w":"aid","p":"n.","d":"help such as food, money, or medicine given to people in need","c":"援助；救援物資","s":"A: After the earthquake destroyed several villages in the south, many families had no food, clean water, or blankets, so how did the government respond so quickly? B: It sent trucks full of emergency aid within twenty-four hours, and the army helped deliver everything to the areas that were hardest to reach.","t":"A：地震摧毀了南部幾個村莊後，許多家庭沒有食物、乾淨的水或毯子，政府怎麼能那麼快回應？ B：它在二十四小時內派出滿載緊急【援助物資】的卡車，軍隊也協助把物資送到最難抵達的地區。"},{"w":"relief","p":"n.","d":"food, money, or help given to people after a disaster","c":"救濟；救援","s":"A: The flood last weekend left hundreds of people in the river town without homes, and many of them are staying in schools, so what is our bank doing to help? B: We have started a disaster relief fund, and for every dollar that customers give, the bank will add another dollar until we reach one million.","t":"A：上週末的水災讓河邊小鎮數百人無家可歸，很多人暫住在學校裡，我們銀行在做什麼幫忙？ B：我們成立了災害【救濟】基金，客戶每捐一元，銀行就再加一元，直到達到一百萬元為止。"},{"w":"community","p":"n.","d":"the people who live in one area","c":"社區；社群","s":"A: Why did the company decide to build a small park and playground next to the new factory instead of using the land for more parking spaces? B: The managers wanted to give something back to the local community, because many of our workers live nearby and their children had no safe place to play.","t":"A：公司為什麼決定在新工廠旁邊蓋一座小公園和遊樂場，而不是把那塊地拿來做更多停車位？ B：主管們想回饋當地【社區】，因為我們很多員工住在附近，他們的孩子之前沒有安全的地方可以玩。"},{"w":"nonprofit","p":"adj.","d":"not set up to make money for its owners","c":"非營利的","s":"A: My cousin left her well-paid job at an investment bank last year, so where is she working now, and does she still enjoy her career? B: She joined a small nonprofit group that teaches computer skills to older people, and although she earns less money, she says the work makes her feel useful every day.","t":"A：我表姊去年辭掉了投資銀行的高薪工作，她現在在哪裡工作？還喜歡她的職涯嗎？ B：她加入了一個教長者電腦技能的小型【非營利】團體，雖然賺得比較少，但她說這份工作讓她每天都覺得自己有用。"},{"w":"organization","p":"n.","d":"a group of people who work together for a purpose","c":"組織；機構","s":"A: I would like to give some of my year-end bonus to help stray animals, but I am worried that the money will not be used properly, so do you have any advice? B: Choose an organization that publishes clear reports every year showing how much it spends on food, medical care, and staff.","t":"A：我想把部分年終獎金拿來幫助流浪動物，但我擔心錢沒被妥善使用，你有什麼建議嗎？ B：選擇一個每年公開清楚報告、說明在食物、醫療和人事上花了多少錢的【組織】。"},{"w":"cause","p":"n.","d":"an aim or idea that people support or work for","c":"理想；公益目標","s":"A: Every year our department chooses one social issue to focus on during the holiday season, so which one should we pick this December? B: I think clean drinking water in poor villages is a good cause, because a small amount of money can build a well that helps hundreds of people for many years.","t":"A：我們部門每年都會在假期選一個社會議題來關注，今年十二月我們該選哪一個？ B：我覺得貧困村莊的乾淨飲用水是個很好的【公益目標】，因為一小筆錢就能蓋一口井，幫助數百人許多年。"},{"w":"campaign","p":"n.","d":"a planned set of activities to reach a goal","c":"（有組織的）活動；宣傳運動","s":"A: The posters about recycling old phones are everywhere in the subway stations this month, so who is paying for all of them? B: A large electronics company started the campaign in October, and it plans to collect fifty thousand phones by the end of the year and give the profits to schools.","t":"A：這個月捷運站到處都是回收舊手機的海報，是誰出錢做的？ B：一家大型電子公司在十月發起了這項【活動】，計畫在年底前收集五萬支手機，並把收益捐給學校。"},{"w":"event","p":"n.","d":"a planned social occasion or activity","c":"活動；大型聚會","s":"A: The hotel manager asked me how many guests will attend our charity dinner, but I have not finished counting the replies yet, so what should I tell her? B: Tell her that about three hundred people will come to the event, and we will send the final number by Wednesday afternoon at the latest.","t":"A：飯店經理問我有多少賓客會參加我們的慈善晚宴，但我還沒算完回覆，我該怎麼跟她說？ B：告訴她大約三百人會來參加這場【活動】，最晚週三下午我們會提供最終人數。"},{"w":"benefit","p":"n.","d":"an event held to raise money for people in need","c":"義演；慈善活動","s":"A: I heard that several famous singers will perform at the stadium on Sunday night, but the tickets seem very cheap, so why is that? B: It is a benefit concert for families who lost their homes in the fire, and the singers agreed to perform for free so that more money can go to the victims.","t":"A：我聽說幾位知名歌手週日晚上會在體育場表演，但票價看起來很便宜，為什麼？ B：那是一場為火災中失去家園的家庭舉辦的【慈善義演】音樂會，歌手們同意免費演出，好讓更多錢能送到災民手中。"},{"w":"helpful","p":"adj.","d":"willing to help; useful","c":"有幫助的；樂於助人的","s":"A: This was the first time our team organized a book drive for the rural schools, so how did everything go when you delivered the boxes on Thursday? B: The teachers there were very helpful, because they carried the boxes into the library with us and showed us which books the students needed most.","t":"A：這是我們團隊第一次為偏鄉學校辦募書活動，你週四送箱子過去時一切順利嗎？ B：那裡的老師們很【樂於幫忙】，他們跟我們一起把箱子搬進圖書館，還告訴我們學生最需要哪些書。"},{"w":"generous","p":"adj.","d":"happy to give money, time, or help","c":"慷慨的；大方的","s":"A: The animal shelter finally has enough money to repair its roof before the rainy season, so where did the money come from? B: A generous businessman who adopted a dog there last year gave half a million dollars, and he also promised to pay for food for the next three years.","t":"A：動物收容所終於有足夠的錢在雨季前修好屋頂了，錢是從哪裡來的？ B：一位去年在那裡領養了狗的【慷慨】商人捐了五十萬元，他還答應未來三年負擔飼料費。"},{"w":"kindness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being friendly and helpful to others","c":"仁慈；善意","s":"A: Why did you buy a big box of chocolates for the woman who works at the reception desk downstairs? B: When I lost my wallet last Monday, she paid for my taxi home and called the police for me, so I wanted to thank her for her kindness and let her know how much it meant to me.","t":"A：你為什麼買了一大盒巧克力送給樓下櫃檯的那位女士？ B：上週一我掉了錢包，她幫我付了回家的計程車錢，還幫我打電話報警，所以我想謝謝她的【善意】，讓她知道這對我意義有多大。"},{"w":"care","p":"n.","d":"the work of looking after people who need help","c":"照顧；照護","s":"A: The new center for elderly people opened near our office last month, so what kind of services does it offer to the families in this neighborhood? B: It provides daily care for older people who cannot live alone, with nurses who check their health, cook healthy meals, and take them for short walks.","t":"A：我們辦公室附近上個月開了新的長者中心，它提供這一帶家庭什麼樣的服務？ B：它為無法獨居的長者提供日間【照護】，有護理師幫他們檢查健康、煮健康的餐點，還會帶他們去散步。"},{"w":"poor","p":"adj.","d":"having very little money","c":"貧窮的","s":"A: The volunteers from our company are going to the mountain villages again next weekend, so what will they bring to the families there this time? B: They will bring warm jackets and school supplies, because many families in that area are poor and cannot afford new clothes before the cold winter arrives.","t":"A：我們公司的志工下週末又要去山區村落了，這次他們要帶什麼給那裡的家庭？ B：他們會帶保暖外套和文具，因為那一帶很多家庭很【貧窮】，在寒冬來臨前買不起新衣服。"},{"w":"needy","p":"adj.","d":"not having enough money, food, or clothes","c":"貧困的；有需要的","s":"A: Our restaurant always has a lot of fresh bread and soup left at closing time, and it feels terrible to throw it away, so do you have a better idea? B: We could work with the local food bank, which picks up extra food every night and gives it to needy families in the neighborhood.","t":"A：我們餐廳打烊時總是剩很多新鮮麵包和湯，丟掉感覺很糟，你有更好的主意嗎？ B：我們可以跟當地的食物銀行合作，他們每晚會來收多餘的食物，再送給附近【有需要的】家庭。"},{"w":"homeless","p":"adj.","d":"having no place to live","c":"無家可歸的","s":"A: Why are so many staff members bringing sleeping bags and thick blankets to the office lobby this week? B: The human resources team is collecting them for homeless people who sleep in the train station, because the weather report says the temperature will drop below ten degrees this weekend.","t":"A：為什麼這週有這麼多員工把睡袋和厚毯子帶到辦公室大廳？ B：人資團隊正在為睡在火車站的【無家可歸的】人收集這些物品，因為氣象預報說這個週末氣溫會降到十度以下。"},{"w":"shelter","p":"n.","d":"a place where people or animals in need can stay","c":"收容所；庇護所","s":"A: My neighbor found three small kittens in a box behind the supermarket yesterday, but she cannot keep them in her apartment, so where should she take them? B: She can bring them to the animal shelter on Green Road, where the staff will give them medical checks and help them find new families.","t":"A：我鄰居昨天在超市後面的箱子裡發現三隻小貓，但她的公寓不能養，她該把牠們送去哪裡？ B：她可以帶去綠園路上的動物【收容所】，那裡的工作人員會幫牠們做健康檢查，並協助牠們找到新家庭。"},{"w":"mission","p":"n.","d":"the main purpose of a group or organization","c":"使命；任務","s":"A: The new director of the charity gave a long speech at the meeting this morning, but I arrived late, so what was the main point? B: She explained that the group's mission is to make sure every child in the city has three healthy meals a day, and all future projects must follow that goal.","t":"A：慈善團體的新主任今天早上在會議上發表了長篇演講，但我遲到了，重點是什麼？ B：她說明了這個團體的【使命】是確保市內每個孩子每天都有三頓健康的餐點，未來所有計畫都必須遵循這個目標。"},{"w":"impact","p":"n.","d":"a strong effect on someone or something","c":"影響；衝擊","s":"A: The board members want to know whether the reading program we paid for last year really helped the students, so what results can we show them? B: The program had a clear impact on the children, because their test scores went up by twenty percent and more of them now borrow books every week.","t":"A：董事會想知道我們去年出資的閱讀計畫是否真的幫助了學生，我們能給他們看什麼成果？ B：這個計畫對孩子們有明顯的【影響】，他們的考試成績提高了百分之二十，而且現在有更多人每週借書。"},{"w":"awareness","p":"n.","d":"knowing about something and understanding that it is important","c":"意識；認識","s":"A: Why is the hospital putting up colorful boards in the shopping mall and giving free health checks to everyone this weekend? B: They want to raise public awareness of heart disease, because many people do not know the early warning signs and only see a doctor when it is too late.","t":"A：醫院為什麼這個週末在購物中心擺放彩色看板，並幫每個人做免費健康檢查？ B：他們想提高大眾對心臟病的【意識】，因為很多人不知道早期警訊，等到看醫生時已經太晚了。"},{"w":"fair","p":"n.","d":"an outdoor event where people sell goods, often to raise money","c":"市集；園遊會","s":"A: Our department made a lot of handmade soap and candles in the workshop last month, so where are we going to sell them? B: We will rent a table at the charity fair in the city park on Saturday, where many companies and schools will sell goods and give the money to the children's hospital.","t":"A：我們部門上個月在工作坊做了很多手工皂和蠟燭，要拿去哪裡賣？ B：我們會在週六市立公園的慈善【市集】租一張桌子，那裡會有很多公司和學校販售物品，並把收入捐給兒童醫院。"},{"w":"hope","p":"v.","d":"to want something to happen and think it is possible","c":"希望","s":"A: The team has collected almost four hundred thousand dollars for the new children's library, but the building will cost half a million, so what will happen next? B: We hope to reach our goal by the end of next month, because two large companies have promised to match the money that employees give.","t":"A：團隊已經為新的兒童圖書館募到將近四十萬元，但建築需要五十萬元，接下來會怎樣？ B：我們【希望】在下個月底前達成目標，因為有兩家大公司承諾會配合員工捐款金額捐出同等的錢。"}]},{"unit":52,"theme":"Chatting 聊天","cards":[{"w":"chat","p":"v.","d":"to talk in a friendly, informal way","c":"聊天、閒聊","s":"A: I noticed that you spent almost an hour in the break room with the new intern this afternoon, so was there a problem with her first project? B: No, everything is fine, we just wanted to chat about her hometown and her favorite restaurants, because I want her to feel welcome on the team.","t":"A：我注意到你今天下午和新實習生在休息室待了快一個小時，她的第一個專案有問題嗎？ B：沒有，一切都很好，我們只是想【聊聊】她的家鄉和她最喜歡的餐廳，因為我希望她在團隊裡感到受歡迎。"},{"w":"chatter","p":"n.","d":"quick, continuous talk about unimportant things","c":"喋喋不休、閒聊聲","s":"A: Why did you move your desk from the open area to the small room next to the storage closet last Monday? B: The loud chatter from the sales team near the coffee machine made it hard for me to concentrate on the monthly budget report, so my manager kindly let me work somewhere quieter.","t":"A：你上週一為什麼把辦公桌從開放區搬到儲藏室旁邊的小房間？ B：咖啡機附近業務團隊吵雜的【閒聊聲】讓我很難專心做每月預算報告，所以經理好心讓我到比較安靜的地方工作。"},{"w":"conversation","p":"n.","d":"a talk between two or more people","c":"對話、交談","s":"A: How did you find out that the client in Singapore was unhappy with our delivery schedule before the official complaint arrived? B: I had a long phone conversation with their purchasing manager yesterday evening, and she told me openly that the last two shipments were late and that her boss was worried.","t":"A：在正式投訴送到之前，你是怎麼發現新加坡的客戶對我們的交貨時程不滿意的？ B：我昨天傍晚和他們的採購經理進行了很長的電話【交談】，她坦白告訴我最近兩批貨都遲到了，而且她的老闆很擔心。"},{"w":"talk","p":"n.","d":"a short speech to a group of people about a subject","c":"演講、談話","s":"A: Are you going to the marketing conference in Taichung next month, or are you too busy with the new product launch? B: I'm definitely going, because our director asked me to give a short talk about how we used social media to attract younger customers, and I've already started preparing my slides.","t":"A：你下個月要去台中的行銷研討會嗎？還是你忙著新產品上市太忙了？ B：我一定會去，因為我們的主管請我做一場簡短的【演講】，談談我們如何利用社群媒體吸引年輕顧客，我已經開始準備投影片了。"},{"w":"discussion","p":"n.","d":"a talk in which people share ideas and opinions about something","c":"討論","s":"A: Did the managers finally decide whether the company will allow employees to work from home two days a week? B: Not yet, they had a long discussion about it during this morning's meeting, but they still disagree about how to measure productivity, so they will meet again next Thursday.","t":"A：經理們最後決定公司是否允許員工每週在家工作兩天了嗎？ B：還沒，他們在今天早上的會議中對此進行了很長的【討論】，但對於如何衡量生產力仍有分歧，所以下週四會再開會。"},{"w":"dialogue","p":"n.","d":"a serious talk between groups to solve a problem or understand each other","c":"對話、溝通","s":"A: The two departments have been arguing about the shared budget for weeks, so what is the new manager planning to do about it? B: She wants to start an open dialogue between the team leaders, so every Friday they will sit down together, explain their needs honestly, and try to find a fair solution.","t":"A：兩個部門為了共用預算已經爭吵好幾週了，新經理打算怎麼處理？ B：她想在團隊主管之間展開開放的【對話】，所以每週五他們會坐下來一起坦誠說明各自的需求，並試著找出公平的解決辦法。"},{"w":"gossip","p":"n.","d":"talk about other people's private lives, often not true","c":"八卦、閒話","s":"A: Is it true that our branch office in Kaohsiung is going to close at the end of the year? B: I don't think so, that is probably just gossip from the staff lounge, because the regional manager told me yesterday that sales there have actually increased and they are hiring more people.","t":"A：我們高雄分公司年底要關閉是真的嗎？ B：我不這麼認為，那大概只是員工休息室流傳的【八卦】，因為區域經理昨天告訴我那裡的業績其實有成長，而且他們正在招募更多人。"},{"w":"small talk","p":"n.phr.","d":"polite talk about unimportant topics, often with people you don't know well","c":"寒暄、閒聊","s":"A: I always feel nervous at networking events because I never know what to say to people I have just met. B: Start with some easy small talk about the weather, the food, or the traffic on the way there, and after a few minutes the conversation usually becomes more natural and relaxed.","t":"A：我在交流活動上總是很緊張，因為我從來不知道要對剛認識的人說什麼。 B：先從一些輕鬆的【寒暄】開始，例如天氣、食物或來的路上的交通，幾分鐘後對話通常就會變得比較自然和放鬆。"},{"w":"banter","p":"n.","d":"friendly joking talk between people","c":"打趣、玩笑話","s":"A: The new designers seem to get along really well, don't they, even though they only joined the company two weeks ago? B: Yes, there is always friendly banter between them during lunch, and they joke about each other's favorite sports teams, which makes the whole office feel more cheerful.","t":"A：新來的設計師們似乎相處得很好，對吧？雖然他們兩週前才進公司。 B：是啊，午餐時他們之間總是有友善的【玩笑話】，還會互相開對方最喜歡的運動隊伍的玩笑，讓整個辦公室感覺更愉快。"},{"w":"exchange","p":"v.","d":"to give something to someone and receive something from them","c":"交換","s":"A: The conference in Tokyo was very busy, so did you have any chance to meet people from other companies in our industry? B: Yes, during the coffee breaks I was able to exchange business cards with several suppliers, and two of them have already emailed me about possible partnerships next year.","t":"A：東京的研討會很忙，你有機會認識我們產業其他公司的人嗎？ B：有，在咖啡休息時間我和幾家供應商【交換】了名片，其中兩家已經寄電子郵件給我，談明年可能的合作。"},{"w":"message","p":"n.","d":"a short piece of information you send or leave for someone","c":"訊息、留言","s":"A: I called the accounting department twice this morning to ask about my travel refund, but nobody answered the phone. B: Most of them are attending a training session until noon, so you should leave a message with the receptionist, and someone will call you back as soon as the session ends.","t":"A：我今天早上打了兩次電話給會計部詢問我的差旅退款，但沒有人接電話。 B：他們大部分人在參加訓練課程到中午，所以你應該請櫃檯人員幫你留個【訊息】，課程一結束就會有人回電給你。"},{"w":"text","p":"v.","d":"to send a written message by mobile phone","c":"傳簡訊","s":"A: The shuttle bus from the hotel to the exhibition center might be late tomorrow morning because of the road repairs. B: In that case, please text me as soon as you leave the hotel, and I will tell the organizers to keep a seat for you near the front of the main hall.","t":"A：因為道路施工，明天早上從飯店到展覽中心的接駁車可能會遲到。 B：這樣的話，你一離開飯店就請【傳簡訊】給我，我會告訴主辦單位幫你在主廳前面保留一個座位。"},{"w":"reply","p":"v.","d":"to answer someone in speech or writing","c":"回覆、回答","s":"A: The customer from Melbourne has sent us three emails about the missing package since Monday, and she sounds very upset now. B: I know, I promised to reply to her before lunch today, as soon as the warehouse manager confirms where the package is and when it can be delivered.","t":"A：墨爾本的那位顧客從週一起已經寄了三封關於遺失包裹的電子郵件給我們，她現在聽起來很不高興。 B：我知道，我答應今天午餐前【回覆】她，只要倉庫經理確認包裹在哪裡以及何時可以送達。"},{"w":"respond","p":"v.","d":"to say or do something as an answer or reaction","c":"回應","s":"A: Our online store received a lot of negative reviews after the website crashed during the holiday sale last weekend. B: The marketing team will respond to each review personally this week, apologize for the problem, and offer every unhappy customer a discount code for their next purchase.","t":"A：上週末假期特賣期間網站當機後，我們的網路商店收到很多負評。 B：行銷團隊這週會親自【回應】每一則評論，為問題道歉，並提供每位不滿意的顧客下次購物的折扣碼。"},{"w":"communicate","p":"v.","d":"to share information or ideas with others","c":"溝通、傳達","s":"A: Since half of our project team works in Vietnam and the other half is here in Taipei, how do you keep everyone informed? B: We communicate mainly through a shared online platform, and we also hold a video meeting every Tuesday morning so that everyone can ask questions and report problems.","t":"A：既然我們專案團隊一半在越南、一半在台北，你們怎麼讓大家掌握最新消息？ B：我們主要透過共用的線上平台【溝通】，每週二早上也會開視訊會議，讓大家可以提問並回報問題。"},{"w":"interaction","p":"n.","d":"the act of talking or doing things with other people","c":"互動","s":"A: Why does the hotel manager want the front desk staff to take a customer service course next month? B: Because guests said in the survey that their interaction with the staff at check-in felt cold and rushed, and she believes a warmer welcome will bring more guests back.","t":"A：飯店經理為什麼要櫃檯人員下個月上客戶服務課程？ B：因為房客在問卷中表示，他們入住時與員工的【互動】感覺冷淡又匆忙，而她相信更溫暖的接待會讓更多客人回流。"},{"w":"socialize","p":"v.","d":"to spend time with other people in a friendly way","c":"交際、社交","s":"A: The company has planned a barbecue by the river on Saturday afternoon, but I'm not sure if I should go because I don't know many people. B: You should come, because it's a great chance to socialize with colleagues from other departments outside the office, and the food is always delicious.","t":"A：公司星期六下午在河邊辦了烤肉活動，但我不確定要不要去，因為我認識的人不多。 B：你應該來，因為那是在辦公室以外和其他部門同事【交際】的好機會，而且食物總是很好吃。"},{"w":"catch up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to talk with someone you have not seen for a while about recent news","c":"敘舊、了解近況","s":"A: You and your old university roommate haven't seen each other for almost five years, right? B: That's right, but she is visiting Taipei for a business trip next week, so we are going to have dinner at a night market on Wednesday and catch up on everything that has happened in our lives.","t":"A：你和你大學時的老室友快五年沒見面了，對吧？ B：沒錯，但她下週來台北出差，所以我們週三要去夜市吃晚餐，好好【敘敘舊】，聊聊我們生活中發生的一切。"},{"w":"ramble","p":"v.","d":"to talk for a long time in a confused way, without staying on the topic","c":"漫談、東拉西扯","s":"A: The presentation by the new consultant was supposed to last twenty minutes, so why did it take over an hour? B: He started to ramble about his own travels and past clients instead of focusing on our sales data, and several people in the audience began checking their phones.","t":"A：新顧問的簡報應該只有二十分鐘，為什麼花了一個多小時？ B：他開始【東拉西扯】地講自己的旅行和以前的客戶，而不是專注在我們的銷售數據上，台下好幾個人都開始看手機了。"},{"w":"interrupt","p":"v.","d":"to stop someone while they are speaking or doing something","c":"打斷、打擾","s":"A: The director is still on a video call with the investors from Hong Kong, but the delivery company is waiting for her signature downstairs. B: Please don't interrupt her right now, because the meeting is very important, so ask the driver to wait ten more minutes or come back after lunch.","t":"A：主管還在和香港投資人進行視訊會議，但快遞公司在樓下等她簽名。 B：現在請不要【打斷】她，因為這場會議非常重要，請司機再等十分鐘，或午餐後再來。"},{"w":"listen","p":"v.","d":"to pay attention to what someone says","c":"聆聽、傾聽","s":"A: Several employees complained that the new manager makes decisions without asking anyone for their opinions. B: I heard about that too, so the HR director advised him to listen carefully to his team during weekly meetings and to take notes on their ideas before he decides anything important.","t":"A：好幾位員工抱怨新經理做決定時都不問任何人的意見。 B：我也聽說了，所以人資主管建議他在每週會議中仔細【聆聽】團隊的意見，並在做任何重要決定之前記下大家的想法。"},{"w":"share","p":"v.","d":"to tell others about your ideas, feelings or experiences","c":"分享","s":"A: What should we do during the first fifteen minutes of the workshop to help the participants relax? B: Let's ask everyone to share one interesting story about their first job, because it is a fun way to break the ice and helps people remember each other's names.","t":"A：工作坊的前十五分鐘我們該做什麼，讓參加者放鬆一點？ B：我們請每個人【分享】一個關於自己第一份工作的有趣故事，因為這是打破僵局的有趣方式，也能幫助大家記住彼此的名字。"},{"w":"debate","p":"n.","d":"a discussion in which people give different opinions on a topic","c":"辯論、爭論","s":"A: Did the city council make a final decision about building the new shopping mall near the train station? B: Not yet, there was a heated debate at last night's public meeting, because local shop owners worry about losing customers while residents hope for more jobs and better parking.","t":"A：市議會對於在火車站附近興建新購物中心做出最後決定了嗎？ B：還沒，昨晚的公聽會上有一場激烈的【辯論】，因為當地店家擔心失去顧客，而居民則希望有更多工作機會和更好的停車空間。"},{"w":"comment","p":"n.","d":"something you say or write that gives an opinion","c":"評論、意見","s":"A: Have you read the feedback forms that the trainees filled out after yesterday's safety workshop? B: Yes, and one comment was especially useful, because a trainee suggested adding more real examples from our factory, so I'm going to update the slides before the next session in December.","t":"A：你看過受訓人員在昨天安全工作坊後填寫的意見回饋表嗎？ B：看過了，其中一則【評論】特別有用，有位受訓人員建議加入更多我們工廠的真實案例，所以我會在十二月的下一堂課之前更新投影片。"}]},{"unit":53,"theme":"Child 兒童","cards":[{"w":"children","p":"n.","d":"young people who are not yet adults","c":"兒童；孩子們（複數）","s":"A: Our hotel is planning a family weekend package for the summer holidays, so what should we include to attract more parents? B: We should offer a supervised play area and a special menu for children under twelve, because parents can relax at the pool while their kids have fun safely nearby.","t":"A：我們飯店正在規劃暑假的家庭週末套裝行程，應該包含什麼才能吸引更多家長？ B：我們應該提供有人看顧的遊戲區，以及給十二歲以下【兒童】的特別菜單，因為家長可以在泳池邊放鬆，而孩子就在附近安全地玩樂。"},{"w":"kid","p":"n.","d":"a child (informal)","c":"小孩（口語）","s":"A: You look tired this morning, and you usually arrive at the office before everyone else, so did something happen at home last night? B: My youngest kid had a high fever, so my wife and I took turns staying awake with him until the doctor's office opened at eight.","t":"A：你今天早上看起來很累，而且你通常比大家早到辦公室，昨晚家裡發生什麼事了嗎？ B：我最小的【孩子】發高燒，所以我和太太輪流熬夜照顧他，直到早上八點診所開門。"},{"w":"infant","p":"n.","d":"a very young baby","c":"嬰兒","s":"A: The airline called to confirm our flight to Tokyo next month, and they asked whether anyone in our group is traveling with a baby, so what did you tell them? B: I said my sister is bringing her six-month-old infant, so they will reserve a front-row seat with a special bed attached to the wall.","t":"A：航空公司打電話來確認我們下個月飛東京的班機，他們問我們團體中是否有人帶嬰兒同行，你怎麼回答？ B：我說我姊姊會帶她六個月大的【嬰兒】，所以他們會保留一個前排座位，並在牆上加裝一個特別的嬰兒床。"},{"w":"toddler","p":"n.","d":"a young child who is learning to walk","c":"學步的幼兒","s":"A: The new daycare center near our office is opening next week, so do you know what age groups they accept and how much it costs? B: They accept any toddler between one and three years old, and the monthly fee includes lunch, afternoon snacks, and a short music class every Friday.","t":"A：我們辦公室附近新的托兒中心下週開幕，你知道他們收哪些年齡層、費用多少嗎？ B：他們收一到三歲的任何【幼兒】，月費包含午餐、下午點心，以及每週五的簡短音樂課。"},{"w":"baby","p":"n.","d":"a very young child","c":"嬰兒；寶寶","s":"A: Linda has not been in the office for two weeks, and her desk is completely empty, so did she leave the company? B: No, she is on maternity leave because she just had a baby girl last Tuesday, and she plans to return to work in about three months.","t":"A：琳達已經兩週沒來辦公室了，而且她的桌子完全清空，她離職了嗎？ B：沒有，她在請產假，因為她上週二剛生了一個女【寶寶】，她打算大約三個月後回來上班。"},{"w":"youth","p":"n.","d":"young people as a group; the time of being young","c":"青少年；青年；青春時期","s":"A: The city government gave our company a grant this year, so how are we going to use the money to help the local community? B: We are starting a summer training program for youth from low-income families, where teenagers can learn computer skills and get real work experience in our offices.","t":"A：今年市政府給了我們公司一筆補助金，我們要怎麼用這筆錢來幫助當地社區？ B：我們要為低收入家庭的【青少年】開辦暑期訓練計畫，讓他們可以學習電腦技能，並在我們的辦公室獲得實際工作經驗。"},{"w":"teenager","p":"n.","d":"a person aged 13 to 19","c":"青少年（13–19歲）","s":"A: Our new smartphone sold well with office workers, but the marketing team wants to reach younger customers, so what do you suggest? B: Since almost every teenager spends hours on video apps after school, we should hire popular online creators to show the phone's camera features in short, funny clips.","t":"A：我們的新智慧型手機在上班族之間賣得很好，但行銷團隊想觸及更年輕的顧客，你有什麼建議？ B：既然幾乎每個【青少年】放學後都花好幾個小時在影音應用程式上，我們應該聘請受歡迎的網路創作者，用簡短有趣的影片展示手機的相機功能。"},{"w":"minor","p":"n.","d":"a person who is not yet an adult by law","c":"未成年人","s":"A: A customer at the front desk wants to rent one of our scooters for his sixteen-year-old son this afternoon, so is that allowed? B: I'm afraid company rules say we cannot rent vehicles to a minor, even when a parent is present and is willing to sign all the forms.","t":"A：櫃檯有位顧客想在今天下午幫他十六歲的兒子租一台我們的機車，這樣可以嗎？ B：恐怕公司規定我們不能把車輛租給【未成年人】，即使有家長在場而且願意簽署所有文件也不行。"},{"w":"juvenile","p":"adj.","d":"related to young people, especially young people who break the law","c":"青少年的；少年的","s":"A: I read that the city is building a new center near the train station, so do you know what it will be used for? B: It will be a juvenile support center where young people who have gotten into trouble can receive counseling, finish their studies, and learn job skills.","t":"A：我看到市政府在火車站附近蓋一座新中心，你知道它要做什麼用嗎？ B：那會是一座【青少年】輔導中心，讓惹上麻煩的年輕人可以接受諮商、完成學業，並學習工作技能。"},{"w":"youngster","p":"n.","d":"a young person or child","c":"年輕人；小孩","s":"A: The weekend art workshop at the museum was fully booked again, so why do you think it has become so popular with local families? B: Every youngster who joins gets to paint a real canvas with a professional artist, and the parents love taking photos of the finished work at the end.","t":"A：博物館的週末藝術工作坊又額滿了，你覺得為什麼它在本地家庭之間這麼受歡迎？ B：每個參加的【小朋友】都能和專業藝術家一起在真正的畫布上作畫，而家長們很喜歡在最後幫完成的作品拍照。"},{"w":"offspring","p":"n.","d":"a person's or animal's children or young","c":"子女；後代（動物的幼崽）","s":"A: The documentary team wants to film the sea turtles on the island this summer, so when is the best time for them to visit? B: They should come in August, because that is when the mother turtles' offspring hatch on the beach at night and crawl toward the ocean for the first time.","t":"A：紀錄片團隊今年夏天想去島上拍攝海龜，他們什麼時候去最好？ B：他們應該八月去，因為那是海龜媽媽的【後代】在夜裡於沙灘上孵化、第一次爬向大海的時候。"},{"w":"descendant","p":"n.","d":"a person in a later generation of the same family","c":"後裔；子孫","s":"A: The hotel's new brochure says the building has a long history, so who owns it now and how did they get it? B: The current owner is a descendant of the merchant who built it in 1890, and the property has passed down through five generations of the same family.","t":"A：飯店的新簡介說這棟建築歷史悠久，現在是誰擁有它，他們又是怎麼得到的？ B：現任屋主是1890年建造它的那位商人的【後裔】，這份產業在同一個家族中傳了五代。"},{"w":"pupil","p":"n.","d":"a child who goes to school","c":"學童；小學生","s":"A: The elementary school down the street asked our bank to help with its financial education day, so what are we planning to do? B: Our staff will visit each class and teach every pupil how to save money with a simple piggy bank game that takes about forty minutes.","t":"A：街上那間小學請我們銀行協助他們的理財教育日，我們打算做什麼？ B：我們的員工會到每個班級，用一個大約四十分鐘的簡單撲滿遊戲，教每位【學童】如何存錢。"},{"w":"student","p":"n.","d":"a person who studies at a school or university","c":"學生","s":"A: We need extra help at the shop during the busy holiday season, but our budget is tight, so who should we hire? B: Let's hire a university student for part-time weekend shifts, because many young people want flexible work and some extra money during their winter break.","t":"A：假期旺季時店裡需要額外人手，但我們預算很緊，應該雇用誰？ B：我們雇一位大學【學生】來上週末兼職班吧，因為很多年輕人在寒假期間想要彈性的工作和額外的收入。"},{"w":"playmate","p":"n.","d":"a friend that a child plays with","c":"玩伴","s":"A: Your daughter seems much happier since you moved into the new apartment last month, so what changed for her? B: The family next door has a girl the same age, so now she has a playmate to ride bikes with in the courtyard every afternoon after school.","t":"A：你女兒自從上個月搬進新公寓後好像快樂多了，她有什麼改變？ B：隔壁那家有個同年齡的女孩，所以現在她每天放學後都有【玩伴】可以一起在中庭騎腳踏車。"},{"w":"classmate","p":"n.","d":"a person in the same class as you","c":"同學","s":"A: How did you find out about the job opening at the design company, since they never posted it online? B: An old classmate from my university marketing course works there now, and she told me about the position and recommended me to the manager before the interview.","t":"A：你怎麼知道那間設計公司有職缺的？他們從來沒有在網路上公布。 B：我大學行銷課的一位老【同學】現在在那裡工作，她告訴我這個職位，還在面試前把我推薦給經理。"},{"w":"dependent","p":"n.","d":"a person, such as a child, who needs someone else for money and care","c":"受撫養人；家屬","s":"A: I'm filling out the new health insurance form from human resources, but I'm not sure about one question, so can you help me? B: Sure, they want to know whether you have a dependent, such as a child or an elderly parent who relies on your income, because that changes your monthly payment.","t":"A：我在填人資部新的健康保險表格，但有一題不太確定，你可以幫我嗎？ B：當然，他們想知道你是否有【受撫養人】，例如依靠你收入生活的孩子或年長父母，因為這會影響你每月的保費。"},{"w":"young","p":"adj.","d":"not old; in an early part of life","c":"年輕的；年幼的","s":"A: The new manager seems very confident in meetings, but some staff members think she lacks experience, so how old is she? B: She is quite young, only twenty-eight, but she has already led three successful projects overseas and speaks four languages fluently, so the directors trust her completely.","t":"A：新經理在會議上看起來很有自信，但有些員工覺得她經驗不足，她幾歲？ B：她相當【年輕】，只有二十八歲，但她已經在海外帶領過三個成功的專案，還能流利說四種語言，所以董事們完全信任她。"},{"w":"childish","p":"adj.","d":"behaving in a silly way, like a small child (negative)","c":"幼稚的","s":"A: Did the meeting between the two department heads go well this morning, or are they still arguing about the budget? B: It went badly, because they refused to look at each other and kept blaming each other loudly, which was really childish behavior for two experienced managers in their fifties.","t":"A：今天早上兩位部門主管的會議順利嗎？還是他們仍在為預算爭吵？ B：很糟糕，因為他們拒絕看對方，還一直大聲互相指責，對兩位五十多歲的資深經理來說，這種行為真的很【幼稚】。"},{"w":"childlike","p":"adj.","d":"having the good qualities of a child, such as trust and wonder","c":"孩子般（天真）的","s":"A: Why do so many visitors love the old toy designer who runs the workshop at the craft fair every year? B: Even at eighty, he still has a childlike sense of wonder, and he gets excited about every new idea, which makes both kids and adults smile when they talk with him.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多遊客喜歡那位每年在手工藝市集經營工作坊的老玩具設計師？ B：即使八十歲了，他仍保有【孩子般】的好奇心，對每個新點子都很興奮，讓小孩和大人跟他聊天時都會微笑。"},{"w":"playful","p":"adj.","d":"full of fun and liking to play","c":"愛玩的；頑皮可愛的","s":"A: We need a new mascot for the pet food brand, so what kind of character do you think customers would like best? B: I suggest a playful puppy that jumps around and chases balls in the commercials, because cheerful and energetic animals usually make shoppers feel happy and remember the product.","t":"A：我們的寵物食品品牌需要一個新吉祥物，你覺得顧客會最喜歡什麼樣的角色？ B：我建議在廣告裡用一隻跳來跳去、追著球跑的【愛玩的】小狗，因為開朗又有活力的動物通常會讓消費者感到快樂並記住產品。"},{"w":"curious","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to know or learn about something","c":"好奇的","s":"A: The science museum wants more families to visit on weekends, so what kind of exhibition should they design next? B: They should build a hands-on space where curious children can touch robots, try simple experiments, and ask staff questions, because kids learn best when they can explore by themselves.","t":"A：科學博物館希望週末有更多家庭來參觀，他們接下來應該設計什麼樣的展覽？ B：他們應該建造一個動手做的空間，讓【好奇的】孩子可以摸機器人、試做簡單實驗並向員工提問，因為孩子能自己探索時學得最好。"},{"w":"innocent","p":"adj.","d":"not guilty of a crime; not knowing about bad things","c":"無辜的；清白的；天真的","s":"A: The security camera showed someone taking money from the cash register last night, so did the police find out who did it? B: Yes, and luckily the new cashier was completely innocent, because the video clearly showed a delivery driver opening the drawer after she had already gone home.","t":"A：監視器顯示昨晚有人從收銀機拿錢，警方查出是誰做的嗎？ B：查出來了，幸好新來的收銀員完全是【清白的】，因為影片清楚顯示，在她已經回家後，是一名送貨司機打開了抽屜。"},{"w":"naughty","p":"adj.","d":"behaving badly; not doing what adults say","c":"頑皮的；不聽話的","s":"A: The restaurant manager looked upset during lunch today, so did something go wrong in the dining room? B: A naughty boy kept running between the tables and knocked over a tray of drinks, and his parents just laughed instead of asking him to sit down and behave.","t":"A：餐廳經理今天午餐時看起來很不高興，用餐區出了什麼問題嗎？ B：一個【頑皮的】男孩一直在桌子之間跑來跑去，還撞翻了一盤飲料，他的父母只是笑，而沒有叫他坐下守規矩。"},{"w":"obedient","p":"adj.","d":"doing what you are told to do","c":"聽話的；順從的","s":"A: You said your team is training dogs for the hotel's new pet-friendly program, so how long does the training usually take? B: It takes about six weeks before each dog is calm and obedient enough to sit quietly in the lobby, follow simple commands, and greet guests without jumping on them.","t":"A：你說你們團隊在為飯店新的寵物友善計畫訓練狗，訓練通常要多久？ B：大約要六週，每隻狗才會冷靜、【聽話】到能安靜地坐在大廳、遵守簡單指令，並在不撲向客人的情況下迎接他們。"},{"w":"develop","p":"v.","d":"to grow or make something grow stronger or better","c":"發展；培養","s":"A: The kindergarten across the street wants to buy new toys for its classrooms, so what kind should they choose? B: They should choose building blocks and puzzles, because these toys help young children develop problem-solving skills and learn to work together while they are having fun.","t":"A：對街的幼兒園想為教室買新玩具，他們應該選哪一種？ B：他們應該選積木和拼圖，因為這些玩具能幫助幼童在玩樂中【培養】解決問題的能力，並學會互相合作。"},{"w":"grow up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to change from a child into an adult","c":"長大；成長","s":"A: You know so much about farming and fresh vegetables, and our restaurant buyers always ask for your opinion, so where did you learn all this? B: I was lucky to grow up on my grandparents' farm in the south of Taiwan, so I spent every summer picking fruit and helping them sell it at the market.","t":"A：你對農業和新鮮蔬菜懂這麼多，我們餐廳的採購總是問你的意見，你是在哪裡學到這些的？ B：我很幸運能在台灣南部祖父母的農場【長大】，所以每年夏天我都在摘水果，並幫他們在市場上販賣。"},{"w":"educate","p":"v.","d":"to teach someone, especially in a school or about an issue","c":"教育","s":"A: Many customers still throw plastic bottles into the regular trash bins at our supermarket, so how can we change this? B: We should put clear signs and short videos near the entrance to educate shoppers about recycling, and we can give small discounts to people who bring back empty bottles.","t":"A：很多顧客還是把塑膠瓶丟進我們超市的一般垃圾桶，我們要怎麼改變這種情況？ B：我們應該在入口附近放清楚的標示和短片來【教育】顧客關於回收的事，並且可以給帶回空瓶的人小額折扣。"},{"w":"raise","p":"v.","d":"to take care of a child until he or she is an adult","c":"養育；撫養","s":"A: Why did Mr. Chen decide to move his family from the city center to a small town after his promotion last year? B: He wanted to raise his two sons in a quieter place with clean air, good schools, and large parks, even though it means a longer drive to the office.","t":"A：陳先生去年升職後，為什麼決定把家人從市中心搬到一個小鎮？ B：他想在空氣乾淨、學校好、公園大的安靜地方【養育】他的兩個兒子，即使那表示要開更久的車去上班。"},{"w":"nurture","p":"v.","d":"to care for and help someone or something grow","c":"培育；養育","s":"A: Our company keeps losing talented young engineers to bigger competitors, so what can we do to keep them? B: We need to nurture their talent by giving each new engineer an experienced mentor, regular training courses, and clear chances for promotion during their first three years.","t":"A：我們公司一直流失有才華的年輕工程師給大型競爭對手，我們能做什麼來留住他們？ B：我們需要【培育】他們的才能，在他們最初三年給每位新工程師安排一位資深導師、定期訓練課程和明確的升遷機會。"},{"w":"protect","p":"v.","d":"to keep someone or something safe from harm","c":"保護","s":"A: Parents have been complaining that the playground in our shopping mall is not safe enough, so what are we going to do about it? B: We will install soft rubber floors and higher fences to protect small children from falls, and a security guard will watch the area during busy weekend hours.","t":"A：家長一直抱怨我們購物中心的遊樂場不夠安全，我們要怎麼處理？ B：我們會鋪設柔軟的橡膠地板和加高圍欄來【保護】幼童免於跌倒，而且在週末熱門時段會有一名警衛看守這個區域。"},{"w":"discipline","p":"v.","d":"to punish someone for breaking rules so they behave better","c":"懲處；管教","s":"A: One of the new sales assistants keeps arriving late and leaving early without telling anyone, so what should the store manager do? B: She needs to discipline him fairly by giving him a written warning first, and if the problem continues next month, she may have to reduce his shifts.","t":"A：其中一位新銷售助理一直遲到早退又不告訴任何人，店長應該怎麼做？ B：她需要公平地【懲處】他，先給他一份書面警告，如果下個月問題持續，她可能必須減少他的班次。"},{"w":"mature","p":"v.","d":"to become more adult in behavior; to become fully developed","c":"成熟；長成","s":"A: Our youngest team member made a lot of mistakes when he first joined, but his recent reports are excellent, so what changed? B: He has really started to mature over the past year, because he now plans his work carefully, listens to feedback, and stays calm when clients are difficult.","t":"A：我們團隊最年輕的成員剛加入時犯了很多錯，但他最近的報告非常出色，有什麼改變？ B：他過去一年真的開始【成熟】了，因為他現在會仔細規劃工作、聽取回饋，並在客戶難搞時保持冷靜。"}]},{"unit":54,"theme":"Childhood Activities 童年活動","cards":[{"w":"play","p":"v.","d":"to do things for fun, especially as a child","c":"玩耍","s":"A: The new apartment complex near our office has a large green yard, so do you think families with young kids will like living there? B: Definitely, because parents can watch their children play safely outside while they cook dinner, and the security guard checks the gate every evening.","t":"A：我們辦公室附近的新公寓社區有一大片綠色庭院，你覺得有小孩的家庭會喜歡住在那裡嗎？ B：當然，因為父母煮晚餐時可以看著孩子在外面安全地【玩耍】，而且保全每天晚上都會檢查大門。"},{"w":"game","p":"n.","d":"an activity with rules that people play for fun","c":"遊戲","s":"A: We need an activity for the children at the company family day next Saturday, but the weather might be rainy, so what should we prepare? B: Let's set up a simple board game in the meeting room, because it only needs a table and some chairs, and kids of different ages can join in together.","t":"A：下週六公司家庭日我們需要為孩子準備一個活動，但天氣可能會下雨，我們該準備什麼？ B：我們在會議室擺一個簡單的桌上【遊戲】吧，因為只需要一張桌子和幾把椅子，不同年齡的孩子都能一起參加。"},{"w":"hide-and-seek","p":"n.","d":"a game in which one child looks for the others who are hiding","c":"捉迷藏","s":"A: The kindergarten teachers want a cheap activity for the open house that keeps the children busy in the garden, so do you have any ideas? B: They could organize a round of hide-and-seek, where one child closes their eyes and counts to twenty while the others find secret places behind the trees and bushes.","t":"A：幼兒園老師想在開放日辦一個便宜的活動，讓孩子們在花園裡玩得忙不停，你有什麼點子嗎？ B：他們可以辦一輪【捉迷藏】，一個孩子閉上眼睛數到二十，其他孩子則在樹木和灌木叢後面找祕密的地方躲起來。"},{"w":"tag","p":"n.","d":"a children's game in which one player chases and touches the others","c":"鬼抓人","s":"A: Why were the children at the summer camp so tired and hungry when they came back to the hotel lobby this afternoon? B: They spent almost an hour playing tag on the beach, so whoever was 'it' had to chase the others and touch them before they reached the big umbrella.","t":"A：夏令營的孩子們今天下午回到飯店大廳時，為什麼又累又餓？ B：他們在海灘上玩了將近一小時的【鬼抓人】，當鬼的人必須追其他人，並在他們跑到大陽傘之前碰到他們。"},{"w":"outdoor play","p":"n.phr.","d":"games and activities that children do outside","c":"戶外遊戲","s":"A: The new daycare center downtown charges more than the one near the station, so why are so many working parents choosing it? B: It has a large garden, and the staff plan two hours of outdoor play every day, which helps the children stay healthy, sleep better at night, and make new friends.","t":"A：市中心的新托兒所收費比車站附近那家貴，為什麼還有這麼多上班族父母選擇它？ B：它有一個大花園，而且工作人員每天安排兩小時的【戶外遊戲】，能幫助孩子保持健康、晚上睡得更好，還能交到新朋友。"},{"w":"imagination","p":"n.","d":"the ability to form new pictures and ideas in your mind","c":"想像力","s":"A: The toy company's new advertisement shows only a cardboard box and a little girl, so why did the marketing team choose such a simple idea? B: They wanted to show that a child's imagination can turn an empty box into a spaceship or a castle, and parents responded very positively to that message online.","t":"A：玩具公司的新廣告只有一個紙箱和一個小女孩，行銷團隊為什麼選這麼簡單的點子？ B：他們想表達孩子的【想像力】可以把空箱子變成太空船或城堡，而家長們在網路上對這個訊息的反應非常正面。"},{"w":"imaginative","p":"adj.","d":"having or showing new and creative ideas","c":"富有想像力的","s":"A: The publisher received over two hundred stories for its children's writing contest this year, so how did the judges choose the winner? B: They picked a ten-year-old boy's very imaginative story about a talking bicycle that travels around Taiwan, because it was original, funny, and full of surprising ideas.","t":"A：出版社今年的兒童寫作比賽收到超過兩百篇故事，評審是怎麼選出優勝者的？ B：他們選了一個十歲男孩非常【富有想像力】的故事，講一輛會說話的腳踏車環遊台灣，因為它很有原創性、很有趣，而且充滿令人驚喜的點子。"},{"w":"pretend","p":"v.","d":"to act as if something is true when it is not, often in play","c":"假裝","s":"A: Your daughter was talking to her stuffed animals in the waiting room for twenty minutes, so was she bored while you were seeing the bank manager? B: Not at all, she loves to pretend that she owns a small restaurant, so she was taking their orders and serving them imaginary noodles.","t":"A：你女兒在等候室跟她的絨毛玩具說了二十分鐘的話，你和銀行經理談事情時她覺得無聊嗎？ B：一點也不，她很喜歡【假裝】自己開了一家小餐廳，所以她在幫它們點餐，還端上想像出來的麵。"},{"w":"role-play","p":"n.","d":"an activity in which people act as different characters","c":"角色扮演","s":"A: How did the English teacher help the young students feel less nervous about speaking at the school's international day? B: She set up a short role-play in which the children acted as shop owners and customers, so they practiced asking prices and saying thank you before they met the foreign visitors.","t":"A：英文老師是怎麼幫助年幼的學生在學校國際日時說話不那麼緊張的？ B：她安排了一段簡短的【角色扮演】，讓孩子們扮成店主和顧客，所以他們在見到外國訪客之前就練習了問價錢和說謝謝。"},{"w":"drawing","p":"n.","d":"a picture made with a pencil, pen, or crayon","c":"圖畫；素描","s":"A: I noticed a colorful picture of a house and a big sun on your office wall, so did you buy it at the art fair last weekend? B: No, it is a drawing my five-year-old son made with crayons for my birthday, and I put it there because it makes me smile during long meetings.","t":"A：我注意到你辦公室牆上有一幅色彩鮮豔、畫著房子和大太陽的畫，是你上週末在藝術市集買的嗎？ B：不是，那是我五歲兒子用蠟筆為我生日畫的【圖畫】，我把它掛在那裡，因為在冗長的會議中它會讓我微笑。"},{"w":"coloring","p":"n.","d":"the activity of adding color to pictures, often with crayons","c":"著色；塗色","s":"A: The family restaurant on the corner gets very busy on Sunday afternoons, so how do the waiters keep the young customers quiet while they wait for food? B: They give every child a box of crayons and some coloring pages with animals and cartoon cars, so the kids stay at the table and the parents can relax.","t":"A：轉角那家家庭餐廳週日下午很忙，服務生是怎麼讓小客人在等餐時保持安靜的？ B：他們給每個孩子一盒蠟筆和幾張畫有動物和卡通汽車的【著色】頁，這樣孩子就會待在餐桌旁，父母也能放鬆。"},{"w":"painting","p":"n.","d":"the activity of making pictures with paint","c":"繪畫","s":"A: The community center is offering several weekend classes for kids this spring, so which one do you think your daughter will choose? B: She will probably sign up for painting, because she loves mixing bright colors with a brush and wants to make a picture of our cat for her grandmother.","t":"A：社區中心今年春天開了幾堂週末兒童課程，你覺得你女兒會選哪一堂？ B：她大概會報名【繪畫】課，因為她喜歡用畫筆調出鮮豔的顏色，還想畫一張我們家貓咪的畫送給奶奶。"},{"w":"craft","p":"n.","d":"something made by hand with skill, or the activity of making it","c":"手工藝","s":"A: What will the children do during the holiday workshop at the department store while their parents are shopping on the upper floors? B: The staff will help them make a simple paper craft, such as a lantern or a card, using glue, scissors, and colored paper that the store provides for free.","t":"A：家長在百貨公司樓上購物時，孩子們在假日工作坊裡會做什麼？ B：工作人員會幫他們做一個簡單的紙【手工藝品】，例如燈籠或卡片，用的是百貨公司免費提供的膠水、剪刀和色紙。"},{"w":"sing","p":"v.","d":"to make music with your voice","c":"唱歌","s":"A: The kindergarten is holding a small concert for parents at the end of the term, so what will your son's class perform on stage? B: The children will sing three short songs in English while their teacher plays the piano, and they have been practicing every morning after breakfast for two weeks.","t":"A：幼兒園學期末要為家長辦一場小型音樂會，你兒子的班上要表演什麼？ B：孩子們會在老師彈鋼琴時用英文【唱】三首短歌，他們已經每天早餐後練習兩個星期了。"},{"w":"dance","p":"v.","d":"to move your body to music","c":"跳舞","s":"A: Why was the hotel ballroom so noisy during the wedding reception last night, even though the band had already finished? B: The DJ played some popular children's songs, and all the little guests hurried to the middle of the room to dance and spin around until almost eleven o'clock.","t":"A：昨晚的婚宴上樂團已經演奏完了，為什麼飯店宴會廳還這麼吵？ B：DJ放了一些熱門兒歌，所有的小賓客都趕到廳中央【跳舞】、轉圈圈，一直到快十一點。"},{"w":"nursery rhyme","p":"n.phr.","d":"a short traditional poem or song for young children","c":"童謠","s":"A: The children's bookstore wants to attract more young families on weekday mornings, so what new event are the managers planning? B: They will hold a free music hour where a teacher leads parents and babies in singing a classic nursery rhyme like 'Twinkle, Twinkle, Little Star' with simple hand movements.","t":"A：童書店想在平日早上吸引更多年輕家庭，經理們在規劃什麼新活動？ B：他們會辦一個免費的音樂時段，由一位老師帶領家長和寶寶一起唱經典【童謠】，例如〈一閃一閃亮晶晶〉，並搭配簡單的手部動作。"},{"w":"storytelling","p":"n.","d":"the activity of telling or reading stories to people","c":"說故事","s":"A: The public library has many visitors on Saturday afternoons, so which event do the young children enjoy most there? B: They love the storytelling hour, when a volunteer reads a picture book aloud with funny voices and asks the kids questions about what might happen next in the plot.","t":"A：公共圖書館週六下午有很多訪客，小朋友在那裡最喜歡哪個活動？ B：他們最喜歡【說故事】時間，一位志工會用逗趣的聲音朗讀繪本，還會問孩子接下來的情節可能會怎麼發展。"},{"w":"reading","p":"n.","d":"the activity of looking at and understanding written words","c":"閱讀","s":"A: The school asked parents to limit screen time at home, so how are you keeping your kids busy in the evenings now? B: We have made thirty minutes of reading part of their bedtime routine, and every Friday we visit the library so they can choose new books about animals and space.","t":"A：學校請家長在家限制孩子使用螢幕的時間，你現在晚上都怎麼讓孩子有事做？ B：我們把三十分鐘的【閱讀】變成他們睡前的固定習慣，而且每週五都去圖書館，讓他們挑選關於動物和太空的新書。"},{"w":"listen","p":"v.","d":"to pay attention to sounds or to what someone says","c":"聆聽","s":"A: The training company is running a weekend program that teaches young children how to behave well during group activities, so what is the first skill they practice? B: The coaches first teach them to listen carefully when someone else is speaking, so they wait for their turn instead of shouting out answers.","t":"A：那家培訓公司正在辦一個週末課程，教小朋友在團體活動中守規矩，他們第一個練習的技能是什麼？ B：教練們會先教他們在別人說話時仔細【聆聽】，讓他們等輪到自己再說，而不是大聲喊出答案。"},{"w":"explore","p":"v.","d":"to travel around a place to learn about it","c":"探索","s":"A: Our family is staying at a farm resort in Yilan next month, so what activities does the resort offer for young guests? B: The kids can explore the forest trail with a guide, look for insects under the leaves, and visit a small river where they can see fish and frogs.","t":"A：我們家下個月要住宜蘭的一間農場度假村，那裡有什麼給小房客的活動？ B：孩子們可以跟著導覽員【探索】森林步道、在樹葉底下找昆蟲，還可以去一條小河看魚和青蛙。"},{"w":"exploration","p":"n.","d":"the act of looking around a place or thing to discover more","c":"探索","s":"A: Why does the new science museum let children touch almost everything instead of keeping the exhibits behind glass? B: The designers believe that hands-on exploration helps kids remember what they learn, so visitors can build bridges, test magnets, and dig for model dinosaur bones in a large sand pit.","t":"A：新的科學博物館為什麼讓孩子幾乎什麼都能摸，而不是把展品放在玻璃後面？ B：設計師相信親自動手的【探索】能幫助孩子記住所學，所以參觀者可以搭橋、測試磁鐵，還能在大沙坑裡挖恐龍骨頭模型。"},{"w":"climb","p":"v.","d":"to go up something using your hands and feet","c":"爬；攀爬","s":"A: The building manager asked us to check the new play area in the lobby before it opens on Monday, so is everything safe for the children? B: Mostly, but the rope wall is too high, and kids could climb over the top and fall onto the hard floor, so we need thicker mats.","t":"A：大樓管理員請我們在週一開放前檢查大廳新的遊戲區，對孩子來說一切都安全嗎？ B：大致上是，但繩網牆太高了，孩子可能會【爬】過頂端掉到堅硬的地板上，所以我們需要更厚的墊子。"},{"w":"run","p":"v.","d":"to move quickly on your feet","c":"跑","s":"A: Why did the school decide to remove some of the old benches from the sports field during the summer holiday? B: The children needed more open space to run around safely at lunchtime, and the teachers were worried that someone would trip over the benches and get hurt.","t":"A：學校為什麼決定在暑假期間移走運動場上一些舊長椅？ B：孩子們午餐時間需要更多空地可以安全地【跑】來跑去，而且老師們擔心有人會被長椅絆倒受傷。"},{"w":"jump","p":"v.","d":"to push yourself off the ground into the air with your legs","c":"跳","s":"A: The trampoline park near the shopping mall is offering a discount for company groups, so should we take our team's children there next month? B: Good idea, the kids can jump as high as they want on the soft surfaces, and there is a café where the parents can sit and chat.","t":"A：購物中心附近的彈跳床樂園有公司團體優惠，我們下個月要不要帶團隊同事的孩子去？ B：好主意，孩子們可以在柔軟的彈跳床上盡情地【跳】，那裡還有一間咖啡館讓家長坐著聊天。"},{"w":"ride","p":"v.","d":"to sit on and control a bicycle, horse, etc.","c":"騎","s":"A: The city just finished building a new riverside park with wide paths, so what will families be able to do there on weekends? B: Children can ride their bicycles along the river without worrying about cars, and there is a rental shop near the entrance for families who don't have their own.","t":"A：市政府剛蓋好一座有寬敞步道的河濱公園，週末家庭可以在那裡做什麼？ B：孩子們可以沿著河邊【騎】腳踏車，不用擔心汽車，而且入口附近有一家出租店，給沒有自己車子的家庭使用。"},{"w":"bike riding","p":"n.phr.","d":"the activity of riding a bicycle for fun or exercise","c":"騎腳踏車","s":"A: Your son seems much more confident and active than he was last year, so has he joined any new after-school clubs recently? B: Yes, he has taken up bike riding with his father every weekend, and they usually travel about ten kilometers along the coast before stopping for breakfast at a small café.","t":"A：你兒子看起來比去年更有自信、更活潑了，他最近有參加什麼新的課後社團嗎？ B：有，他每個週末都跟爸爸去【騎腳踏車】，他們通常沿著海岸騎大約十公里，再停在一家小咖啡館吃早餐。"},{"w":"sports","p":"n.","d":"games or activities in which people use their bodies and often compete","c":"運動","s":"A: The company is planning a family fun day at the stadium in October, so what kind of activities should we include for employees' children? B: We should offer several team sports like soccer and relay races, because they are easy to organize, and the kids will learn to cooperate with new friends.","t":"A：公司打算十月在體育場辦家庭同樂日，我們應該為員工的孩子安排哪些活動？ B：我們應該提供幾項團隊【運動】，例如足球和接力賽，因為它們容易安排，孩子們也能學著和新朋友合作。"},{"w":"swimming","p":"n.","d":"the activity of moving through water using your arms and legs","c":"游泳","s":"A: The hotel we booked for our business trip to Kenting has a large pool, so do you think your kids will enjoy staying there? B: Absolutely, they love swimming more than any other summer activity, and they took lessons at the sports center for three months, so they can now float and kick without help.","t":"A：我們出差去墾丁訂的飯店有一個大泳池，你覺得你的孩子會喜歡住那裡嗎？ B：當然，他們最愛【游泳】，勝過任何其他夏日活動，而且他們在運動中心上了三個月的課，現在不用別人幫忙就能漂浮和踢水了。"},{"w":"playground","p":"n.","d":"an outdoor area with equipment for children to play on","c":"遊樂場","s":"A: The property developer says the new housing project will attract young families, so what facilities are they adding to the site? B: They are building a large playground with slides, swings, and a sandbox in the center of the complex, so parents can watch their children from the windows of their apartments.","t":"A：建商說新的住宅案會吸引年輕家庭，他們在基地上增加了哪些設施？ B：他們正在社區中央蓋一座有溜滑梯、鞦韆和沙坑的大型【遊樂場】，讓父母可以從公寓窗戶看著孩子。"},{"w":"picnic","p":"n.","d":"a meal eaten outdoors, often in a park","c":"野餐","s":"A: The weather forecast says it will be sunny and warm on Sunday, so do you have any plans with your family this weekend? B: We are going to have a picnic by the lake in Daan Park, and the kids will help me make sandwiches and pack fruit and cold drinks in the morning.","t":"A：天氣預報說週日會晴朗溫暖，這個週末你和家人有什麼計畫嗎？ B：我們要去大安公園的湖邊【野餐】，孩子們早上會幫我做三明治，並把水果和冷飲打包好。"},{"w":"collect","p":"v.","d":"to get and keep things of the same type as a hobby","c":"收集","s":"A: Why is your son so excited about the new convenience store promotion that started at the beginning of this month? B: He likes to collect the small cartoon stickers that come with each purchase, and he wants to fill the whole album before the event ends in December.","t":"A：你兒子為什麼對這個月初開始的便利商店新促銷活動這麼興奮？ B：他喜歡【收集】每次購物附贈的小卡通貼紙，而且想在活動十二月結束前把整本集點冊貼滿。"},{"w":"collection","p":"n.","d":"a group of similar things that someone has gathered","c":"收藏品","s":"A: The toy museum is asking local residents to lend items for its new exhibition about childhood in the 1980s, so are you going to help? B: Yes, my father still has his collection of old metal cars from his school days, and he is happy to let the museum display them for three months.","t":"A：玩具博物館正在請當地居民出借物品，舉辦一個關於1980年代童年的新展覽，你會幫忙嗎？ B：會，我父親還留著他學生時代的舊金屬小汽車【收藏】，他很樂意讓博物館展出三個月。"},{"w":"help out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to help someone, especially by doing a share of the work","c":"幫忙","s":"A: The children at your neighbor's house seem very busy in the garden every Saturday morning, so what are they doing out there? B: Their grandparents grow vegetables, and the kids help out by watering the plants and picking tomatoes, which teaches them responsibility and earns them a little pocket money.","t":"A：你鄰居家的孩子每週六早上在花園裡看起來都很忙，他們在那裡做什麼？ B：他們的祖父母種菜，孩子們會【幫忙】澆水和摘番茄，這能培養他們的責任感，還能賺一點零用錢。"},{"w":"chores","p":"n.","d":"small regular jobs at home, like cleaning or washing dishes","c":"家務；雜事","s":"A: How do you get your kids to stop watching cartoons and do something useful on weekend mornings at home? B: We made a simple chart of household chores, such as feeding the dog and folding laundry, and they earn a sticker for each task they finish before lunch.","t":"A：週末早上在家，你是怎麼讓孩子不再看卡通、做點有用的事？ B：我們做了一張簡單的【家務】表，例如餵狗和摺衣服，他們每在午餐前完成一項就能得到一張貼紙。"},{"w":"hobby","p":"n.","d":"an activity you do for fun in your free time","c":"嗜好","s":"A: The manager asked about your childhood during the job interview this morning, so what did you tell her? B: I said that my favorite hobby was building model airplanes, because it taught me patience and attention to detail, which are useful skills for an engineering position like this one.","t":"A：今天早上面試時經理問了你的童年，你怎麼回答她？ B：我說我最喜歡的【嗜好】是做模型飛機，因為它教會我耐心和注重細節，這些對像這樣的工程職位都是很有用的技能。"}]},{"unit":56,"theme":"Children's Education 兒童教育","cards":[{"w":"education","p":"n.","d":"the process of teaching and learning, especially at school","c":"教育","s":"A: Our company is thinking about opening a training center for the children of our factory workers, so what do you think parents care about most? B: Most of them want their kids to get a good education, because they believe that strong schooling will help their children find better jobs than they had.","t":"A：我們公司正考慮為工廠員工的孩子開設一個培訓中心，你覺得家長最在乎的是什麼？ B：他們大多數希望孩子能受到良好的【教育】，因為他們相信紮實的學校教育能幫助孩子找到比自己更好的工作。"},{"w":"schooling","p":"n.","d":"the education a child receives at school","c":"學校教育","s":"A: The new manager from Singapore said she moved here with her two sons last month, so where are the boys studying now? B: They are attending an international school near the station, and she told me that their schooling costs a lot but the small classes are worth the money.","t":"A：新來的新加坡經理說她上個月帶著兩個兒子搬來這裡，那兩個男孩現在在哪裡讀書？ B：他們在車站附近的一所國際學校上學，她告訴我他們的【學校教育】花費很高，但小班制是值得的。"},{"w":"learning","p":"n.","d":"the process of gaining knowledge or skills","c":"學習","s":"A: Why did the library decide to buy so many tablets and educational games for the children's corner this year? B: The director believes that learning should be fun, so she wants young visitors to explore science and language through games instead of just sitting quietly with heavy books.","t":"A：圖書館今年為什麼決定為兒童區購買這麼多平板電腦和教育遊戲？ B：館長認為【學習】應該是有趣的，所以她希望年幼的訪客能透過遊戲探索科學和語言，而不只是安靜地坐著看厚重的書。"},{"w":"teach","p":"v.","d":"to show or explain to someone how to do something","c":"教；教導","s":"A: I heard you are volunteering at the community center on Saturday mornings, so what exactly do you do there with the kids? B: I teach a group of ten-year-olds how to use simple computer programs, and afterward we usually play board games together until their parents arrive.","t":"A：我聽說你週六早上在社區中心當志工，你在那裡和孩子們具體做些什麼？ B：我【教】一群十歲的孩子如何使用簡單的電腦程式，之後我們通常會一起玩桌遊，直到他們的父母來接。"},{"w":"teacher","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to help students learn","c":"老師","s":"A: Your daughter seems much more confident about speaking English than she was last year, so what made the biggest difference for her? B: Her new teacher at the language school is very patient, and she always gives every child a chance to speak in front of the class without feeling nervous.","t":"A：你女兒說英文似乎比去年有自信多了，對她來說最大的改變是什麼？ B：她在語言學校的新【老師】非常有耐心，總是給每個孩子在全班面前說話的機會，而不會讓他們感到緊張。"},{"w":"student","p":"n.","d":"a person who is studying at a school or university","c":"學生","s":"A: The science museum is offering free tickets next month, but does the offer include everyone or only certain groups of visitors? B: Any student under eighteen can get in for free if they show a school ID card at the front desk, so it is a great chance for families.","t":"A：科學博物館下個月提供免費門票，但這個優惠是適用所有人還是只限特定族群的訪客？ B：任何未滿十八歲的【學生】只要在櫃台出示學生證就能免費入場，所以這對家庭來說是個很好的機會。"},{"w":"curriculum","p":"n.","d":"all the subjects that are taught in a school","c":"課程","s":"A: The board of education announced some major changes for elementary schools starting next September, so what will be different for the kids? B: The new curriculum will include coding classes and more outdoor science projects, and schools will reduce the number of tests that students take each term.","t":"A：教育局宣布從明年九月起國小將有一些重大改變，對孩子來說會有什麼不同？ B：新的【課程】將包含程式設計課和更多戶外科學專題，而且學校會減少學生每學期的考試次數。"},{"w":"lesson","p":"n.","d":"a period of time in which someone is taught something","c":"一堂課；課程","s":"A: Is your son still taking swimming classes at the sports center near your apartment, or did he stop after the summer vacation? B: He still goes every Wednesday, and each lesson lasts about forty-five minutes, so I can finish my shopping at the supermarket before I pick him up.","t":"A：你兒子還在你公寓附近的運動中心上游泳課嗎？還是暑假後就停了？ B：他還是每週三去，每一【堂課】大約四十五分鐘，所以我可以在接他之前先在超市買完東西。"},{"w":"classroom","p":"n.","d":"a room where students have lessons","c":"教室","s":"A: The parents' association raised a lot of money at the spring fair, so how is the school planning to spend it? B: They will repaint every classroom on the second floor and buy new desks and chairs, because the old furniture is broken and too small for the older children.","t":"A：家長會在春季園遊會上募得了不少錢，學校打算怎麼使用這筆錢？ B：他們會重新粉刷二樓的每一間【教室】，並購買新的桌椅，因為舊家具已經壞了，對年紀較大的孩子來說也太小了。"},{"w":"homework","p":"n.","d":"school work that students do at home","c":"回家作業","s":"A: You usually leave the office right at five o'clock these days, so do you have a new class or appointment in the evening? B: Not really, but my twins have a lot of homework now that they are in third grade, and I like to sit with them while they do it after dinner.","t":"A：你最近通常五點一到就下班，晚上是有新的課程還是約會嗎？ B：其實沒有，只是我的雙胞胎升上三年級後有很多【回家作業】，我喜歡晚餐後坐在旁邊陪他們寫。"},{"w":"literacy","p":"n.","d":"the ability to read and write","c":"讀寫能力","s":"A: Why is the publishing company donating thousands of picture books to schools in the mountain areas this year? B: The company wants to improve literacy among young children there, because many of them do not have libraries nearby and some still cannot read simple sentences by the age of eight.","t":"A：出版社今年為什麼要捐贈數千本繪本給山區的學校？ B：公司希望提升當地幼童的【讀寫能力】，因為許多孩子附近沒有圖書館，有些到了八歲還看不懂簡單的句子。"},{"w":"numeracy","p":"n.","d":"the ability to understand and work with numbers","c":"算術能力","s":"A: The after-school program uses a lot of cooking activities, but how does making cookies actually help the kids with their studies? B: Measuring flour, counting eggs, and dividing the cookies equally all build numeracy, so children practice basic math skills without even noticing that they are learning something.","t":"A：課後輔導班使用很多烹飪活動，但做餅乾到底對孩子的課業有什麼幫助？ B：量麵粉、數雞蛋和平均分配餅乾都能培養【算術能力】，所以孩子們在不知不覺中就練習了基本的數學技巧。"},{"w":"reading","p":"n.","d":"the activity of looking at and understanding written words","c":"閱讀","s":"A: My nephew spends almost every evening playing games on his phone, so how can his parents get him interested in books? B: They could make reading part of the family routine, for example by spending twenty minutes together with stories before bed and visiting the library every weekend.","t":"A：我姪子幾乎每天晚上都在手機上玩遊戲，他父母要怎麼讓他對書產生興趣？ B：他們可以把【閱讀】變成家庭作息的一部分，例如睡前一起花二十分鐘看故事，並且每個週末去圖書館。"},{"w":"writing","p":"n.","d":"the activity or skill of putting words on paper or a screen","c":"寫作","s":"A: The judges for the children's story competition have finished reading all the entries, so did any of them stand out? B: One girl's writing was especially impressive, because she described her grandmother's farm with such clear details that we could almost smell the fresh rice fields.","t":"A：兒童故事比賽的評審已經看完所有參賽作品了，有沒有哪一篇特別突出？ B：有一個女孩的【寫作】特別令人印象深刻，因為她把祖母的農場描寫得非常細膩，我們幾乎能聞到新鮮稻田的味道。"},{"w":"assessment","p":"n.","d":"a way of judging how much someone has learned","c":"評量；評估","s":"A: Before the kids join the advanced English class, does the school check their level, or can parents just sign them up? B: Every child takes a short assessment with a teacher first, which includes a few listening questions and a simple conversation, so the school can place them in the right group.","t":"A：孩子加入英文進階班之前，學校會檢查他們的程度嗎？還是家長直接報名就可以？ B：每個孩子都會先和老師進行一個簡短的【評量】，包括幾題聽力和簡單的對話，這樣學校才能把他們分到合適的組別。"},{"w":"exam","p":"n.","d":"an official test of knowledge or skill","c":"考試","s":"A: Your son looked really tired when I saw him at the bus stop this morning, so is something wrong at school? B: He has been studying late every night because he has an important exam next Monday, and the results will decide whether he can enter the senior high school he wants.","t":"A：我今天早上在公車站看到你兒子，他看起來真的很累，學校發生什麼事了嗎？ B：他每天晚上都讀書到很晚，因為下週一有一場重要的【考試】，結果將決定他能不能進入想讀的高中。"},{"w":"discipline","p":"n.","d":"training people to obey rules and control their behavior","c":"紀律","s":"A: The new kindergarten seems very popular with parents in our neighborhood, so what makes it different from the others? B: The teachers there believe that gentle but firm discipline is important, so they set clear rules about sharing toys and cleaning up, and the children learn to follow them happily.","t":"A：新開的幼兒園似乎很受我們社區家長歡迎，它和其他幼兒園有什麼不同？ B：那裡的老師認為溫和但堅定的【紀律】很重要，所以他們訂下分享玩具和收拾整理的明確規則，孩子們也學會開心地遵守。"},{"w":"guidance","p":"n.","d":"help and advice about how to do something","c":"指導；輔導","s":"A: My daughter cannot decide whether she should study art or engineering in college, and she is getting really stressed about it. B: Maybe she should ask the school counselor for some guidance, because counselors know a lot about different careers and can help students think about their strengths and interests.","t":"A：我女兒無法決定大學要讀藝術還是工程，她為此感到壓力很大。 B：也許她應該向學校的輔導老師尋求一些【指導】，因為輔導老師很了解各種職業，也能幫助學生思考自己的長處和興趣。"},{"w":"support","p":"v.","d":"to help someone or something, especially when help is needed","c":"支持；幫助","s":"A: Our firm wants to do something useful for the local community this year, so do you have any ideas for a project? B: We could support the reading program at the public library by giving books and sending volunteers twice a month to help children who are falling behind at school.","t":"A：我們公司今年想為當地社區做些有意義的事，你對專案有什麼想法嗎？ B：我們可以透過捐書和每個月派兩次志工，幫助課業落後的孩子，來【支持】公立圖書館的閱讀計畫。"},{"w":"encourage","p":"v.","d":"to give someone confidence or hope to do something","c":"鼓勵","s":"A: Your son used to be so shy, but yesterday he sang a song in front of the whole school at the concert, didn't he? B: Yes, his music teacher worked hard to encourage him, and she kept telling him that his voice was beautiful until he finally believed it himself.","t":"A：你兒子以前很害羞，但他昨天在音樂會上當著全校的面唱了一首歌，對吧？ B：是啊，他的音樂老師很努力地【鼓勵】他，一直告訴他他的聲音很好聽，直到他自己終於相信了。"},{"w":"motivate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone want to do something","c":"激勵；激發動機","s":"A: The kids in the after-school club used to complain about doing math, but now they seem excited about it, so what changed? B: The coordinator found a smart way to motivate them by giving small prizes and points for every finished worksheet, and the class with the most points wins a pizza party.","t":"A：課後社團的孩子們以前抱怨做數學，現在卻似乎很興奮，是什麼改變了？ B：協調員找到一個聰明的方法來【激勵】他們，每完成一張學習單就給小獎品和積分，積分最多的班級可以贏得披薩派對。"},{"w":"educate","p":"v.","d":"to teach someone, especially over a period of time","c":"教育","s":"A: Why is the city hospital sending nurses to visit elementary schools all through the month of October? B: They want to educate children about healthy eating and washing their hands properly, because doctors have seen more kids getting sick from poor habits during the cold season.","t":"A：市立醫院為什麼整個十月都派護理師去拜訪國小？ B：他們想【教育】孩子有關健康飲食和正確洗手的知識，因為醫生發現在寒冷的季節有越來越多孩子因為不良習慣而生病。"},{"w":"develop","p":"v.","d":"to grow or make something grow stronger or better","c":"培養；發展","s":"A: Do you really think the weekend robot club is worth the high fee that the center charges for each term? B: I think so, because it helps kids develop problem-solving skills and teamwork, and my daughter now plans her projects carefully and explains her ideas clearly to her teammates.","t":"A：你真的認為週末機器人社團值得中心每學期收的高額費用嗎？ B：我認為值得，因為它能幫助孩子【培養】解決問題的能力和團隊合作，我女兒現在會仔細規劃她的專案，並清楚地向隊友解釋自己的想法。"},{"w":"practice","p":"v.","d":"to do something again and again to get better at it","c":"練習","s":"A: Your daughter played the violin so beautifully at the company's year-end party, so how long has she been learning? B: Only about two years, but she has to practice for at least an hour every day after school, even on weekends when her friends invite her to go out and play.","t":"A：你女兒在公司尾牙上小提琴拉得真好聽，她學多久了？ B：只有大約兩年，但她每天放學後至少要【練習】一個小時，即使週末朋友找她出去玩也一樣。"},{"w":"focus","p":"v.","d":"to give all your attention to something","c":"專注","s":"A: The noise from the construction site next to the school has been terrible this month, so how are the students managing in class? B: Many of them find it hard to focus on their lessons, so the principal has asked the builders to do the loudest work only after three o'clock.","t":"A：學校隔壁工地的噪音這個月非常嚴重，學生們上課時怎麼應付？ B：很多學生覺得很難【專注】在課業上，所以校長已經要求建商只在三點以後才進行最吵的工程。"},{"w":"inclusive","p":"adj.","d":"welcoming and including all kinds of people","c":"包容的；融合的","s":"A: The father of a boy who uses a wheelchair asked whether the new private school would accept his son, so what did the school say? B: The principal told him that they run an inclusive program, so the building has ramps and elevators, and every class welcomes children with different needs.","t":"A：一位坐輪椅男孩的父親詢問新的私立學校是否會接受他的兒子，學校怎麼說？ B：校長告訴他學校實施【融合】課程，所以建築物有斜坡和電梯，每個班級都歡迎有不同需求的孩子。"},{"w":"effective","p":"adj.","d":"working well and producing the result you want","c":"有效的","s":"A: We tried several ways to help the new staff's children with their summer homework, so which one worked the best? B: Small study groups were the most effective, because older kids helped younger ones and everyone finished their tasks faster than when they studied alone at home.","t":"A：我們試了幾種方法幫助新進員工的孩子完成暑假作業，哪一種效果最好？ B：小型讀書會最【有效】，因為大孩子會幫助小孩子，每個人都比獨自在家讀書時更快完成任務。"},{"w":"creative","p":"adj.","d":"good at making new and interesting things or ideas","c":"有創意的","s":"A: The marketing team was really impressed by the drawings the employees' kids made for our calendar, weren't they? B: Yes, the children were so creative that one boy turned our company logo into a flying dragon, and the design team now wants to use his idea in our next advertisement.","t":"A：行銷團隊對員工的孩子為我們月曆畫的圖真的印象深刻，對吧？ B：是啊，孩子們非常【有創意】，有一個男孩把我們公司的標誌變成了一條飛龍，設計團隊現在想在下一支廣告中使用他的點子。"},{"w":"academic","p":"adj.","d":"related to school, study, and learning","c":"學業的；學術的","s":"A: Why did the private high school offer that girl from the countryside a full scholarship for all three years? B: Her academic results were excellent in every subject, especially science and mathematics, and she also volunteered at the local clinic every weekend to help elderly patients.","t":"A：那所私立高中為什麼提供那位鄉下女孩三年的全額獎學金？ B：她每一科的【學業】成績都很優秀，尤其是自然科學和數學，而且她每個週末還在當地診所當志工幫助年長的病患。"},{"w":"basic","p":"adj.","d":"simple and necessary as a first step","c":"基本的","s":"A: The summer camp is only two weeks long, so can the kids really learn anything useful about computers in such a short time? B: They will not become experts, of course, but they will learn basic skills like typing, saving files, and searching online safely, which will help them a lot at school.","t":"A：夏令營只有兩週，孩子們真的能在這麼短的時間內學到有用的電腦知識嗎？ B：當然他們不會成為專家，但他們會學到【基本】技能，像是打字、儲存檔案和安全地上網搜尋，這對他們在學校會有很大的幫助。"},{"w":"formal","p":"adj.","d":"official, and following the usual system of schools or training","c":"正規的；正式的","s":"A: The new receptionist speaks four languages very well, so did she study them at a university abroad? B: Actually, she had very little formal schooling as a child because her family traveled a lot, but she picked up languages by talking with people in every country they lived in.","t":"A：新來的接待員能說流利的四種語言，她是在國外大學學的嗎？ B：其實她小時候因為家人經常旅行，很少接受【正規】學校教育，但她在他們住過的每個國家透過和當地人交談學會了語言。"},{"w":"early","p":"adj.","d":"happening near the beginning of a period of time","c":"早期的；幼年的","s":"A: Why is the government spending so much money on preschools and training for kindergarten teachers this year? B: Studies show that the early years of a child's life are very important for the brain, so good care before age six can help children do better later at school.","t":"A：政府今年為什麼要花這麼多錢在幼兒園和幼教老師的培訓上？ B：研究顯示孩子生命中的【早期】幾年對大腦非常重要，所以六歲前的良好照顧能幫助孩子日後在學校表現更好。"},{"w":"lifelong","p":"adj.","d":"lasting for the whole of a person's life","c":"終身的","s":"A: Your father retired from the bank last year, but I heard he is taking Japanese and painting classes now, isn't he? B: Yes, he believes in lifelong learning, and he says that studying new things keeps his mind sharp and gives him a reason to meet new friends every week.","t":"A：你父親去年從銀行退休了，但我聽說他現在在上日文課和繪畫課，對嗎？ B：是的，他相信【終身】學習，他說學習新事物能讓頭腦保持敏銳，也讓他每週都有理由認識新朋友。"},{"w":"quality","p":"adj.","d":"of a high standard; very good","c":"優質的","s":"A: Many young families are moving to the new town near the science park, so what is attracting them there? B: Besides the cheaper apartments, the town offers quality education, with modern schools, well-trained teachers, and free after-school activities for every child who lives in the area.","t":"A：很多年輕家庭搬到科學園區附近的新市鎮，是什麼吸引他們去那裡？ B：除了比較便宜的公寓之外，那個市鎮還提供【優質】教育，有現代化的學校、訓練有素的老師，以及給區內每個孩子的免費課後活動。"},{"w":"well-rounded","p":"adj.","d":"having many different skills and interests","c":"全面發展的","s":"A: Why do so many parents in this neighborhood send their children to music, sports, and art classes on weekends? B: They want their kids to become well-rounded people who are good at many things, not just test scores, because companies today look for people with a wide range of skills.","t":"A：為什麼這個社區有這麼多家長在週末送孩子去上音樂、運動和美術課？ B：他們希望孩子成為【全面發展】的人，擅長很多事情，而不只是考試成績，因為現在的公司都在尋找具備多種技能的人。"}]},{"unit":57,"theme":"Chocolate 巧克力","cards":[{"w":"cocoa","p":"n.","d":"powder made from roasted cacao beans, used in drinks and baking","c":"可可（粉）","s":"A: The café wants to add a warm winter drink to the menu before the holiday season, so what ingredients should we order from the supplier this week? B: Let's order a large bag of good-quality cocoa powder, because customers love hot chocolate on cold evenings and we can also use it in our brownies.","t":"A：咖啡館想在節慶季節前在菜單上新增一款冬季熱飲，我們這週該向供應商訂哪些材料？ B：我們訂一大袋優質的【可可】粉吧，因為顧客在寒冷的晚上很喜歡熱巧克力，我們也可以把它用在布朗尼裡。"},{"w":"cacao","p":"n.","d":"the tree or raw beans that chocolate is made from","c":"可可樹；可可豆","s":"A: Our marketing team wants to explain where our chocolate comes from on the new website, so do you have any photos from the farm visit last spring? B: Yes, I took dozens of pictures of the farmers in Ghana picking cacao pods and drying the beans in the sun before shipping them to our factory.","t":"A：我們的行銷團隊想在新網站上說明我們的巧克力來自哪裡，你有去年春天參訪農場的照片嗎？ B：有，我拍了幾十張迦納農民採摘【可可】果莢、並在運往我們工廠前把豆子放在陽光下曬乾的照片。"},{"w":"bar","p":"n.","d":"a small flat block of chocolate or other food","c":"條；塊","s":"A: I want to buy something small for each member of my team to thank them for working late during the busy season, but I don't have much money left. What do you suggest? B: You could give everyone a bar of dark chocolate from the shop downstairs, because it is cheap, nicely wrapped, and easy to leave on their desks.","t":"A：我想買點小東西送給團隊的每位成員，感謝他們在旺季加班，但我剩的錢不多了。你有什麼建議？ B：你可以從樓下的店買一【條】黑巧克力送給每個人，因為它便宜、包裝漂亮，又方便放在他們的桌上。"},{"w":"truffle","p":"n.","d":"a soft, round chocolate candy, often with a creamy center","c":"松露巧克力","s":"A: The hotel manager asked us to choose a small sweet to leave on each guest's pillow at night, so which option did the kitchen staff recommend? B: They suggested a handmade chocolate truffle rolled in cocoa powder, because it looks elegant, tastes wonderful, and guests often mention it in their online reviews.","t":"A：飯店經理請我們選一款晚上放在每位客人枕頭上的小甜點，廚房員工推薦哪一種？ B：他們建議裹上可可粉的手工【松露巧克力】，因為它看起來高雅、味道很棒，而且客人常在網路評論中提到它。"},{"w":"bonbon","p":"n.","d":"a small sweet candy, often covered in chocolate","c":"夾心糖；糖果","s":"A: The front desk wants to put a bowl of candy in the lobby for visitors who wait for their appointments, so what kind should we order? B: Let's order a large box from the local chocolate maker, because each bonbon is wrapped in colorful paper, easy to share, and won't melt in the air-conditioned waiting area.","t":"A：櫃檯想在大廳放一碗糖果給等候預約的訪客，我們該訂哪一種？ B：我們向本地巧克力商訂一大盒吧，因為每顆【夾心糖】都包著彩色糖紙，方便分享，而且在有空調的等候區也不會融化。"},{"w":"filling","p":"n.","d":"the soft food inside a cake, candy, or pastry","c":"餡料；內餡","s":"A: Several customers said our new chocolate pastries were too dry last week, so has the bakery team found a way to improve the recipe before the weekend? B: Yes, they added a soft orange filling inside each pastry, and the testers in the office said it tastes fresher and much more interesting now.","t":"A：上週有幾位顧客說我們新的巧克力酥皮點心太乾，烘焙團隊在週末前找到改良食譜的方法了嗎？ B：有，他們在每個點心裡加了柔軟的柳橙【內餡】，辦公室的試吃人員說現在吃起來更清爽，也有趣多了。"},{"w":"cocoa butter","p":"n.phr.","d":"the natural fat from cacao beans, used in chocolate and skin creams","c":"可可脂","s":"A: Why does the expensive chocolate from the Swiss supplier feel so much smoother than the cheaper brand we sold last year? B: The Swiss company uses pure cocoa butter instead of vegetable oil, so the chocolate melts slowly on your tongue, and that is why many customers are happy to pay a higher price.","t":"A：為什麼瑞士供應商的高價巧克力吃起來比我們去年賣的便宜品牌滑順這麼多？ B：那家瑞士公司使用純【可可脂】而不是植物油，所以巧克力會在舌頭上慢慢融化，這就是很多顧客樂意付更高價格的原因。"},{"w":"sweet","p":"adj.","d":"tasting of sugar","c":"甜的","s":"A: The new energy bar we are testing is popular with the younger staff, but why did the older managers give it such low scores in the survey? B: Most of them said it was far too sweet for their taste, so the product team plans to reduce the sugar and add more nuts before the official launch in March.","t":"A：我們正在測試的新能量棒很受年輕員工歡迎，但為什麼年長的主管在調查中給它這麼低的分數？ B：他們大多說它對他們來說太【甜】了，所以產品團隊打算在三月正式上市前減少糖分，並加入更多堅果。"},{"w":"bitter","p":"adj.","d":"having a strong, sharp taste that is not sweet","c":"苦的","s":"A: I tried the ninety-percent chocolate that the sales representative left in the meeting room this morning, but I could only finish one small piece. Did you like it? B: Not really, because it was much too bitter for me, although our director said it tastes perfect with a strong cup of black coffee after lunch.","t":"A：我試了業務代表今天早上留在會議室的百分之九十巧克力，但我只吃得完一小塊。你喜歡嗎？ B：不太喜歡，因為對我來說太【苦】了，不過我們主任說它午餐後配一杯濃黑咖啡吃剛剛好。"},{"w":"rich","p":"adj.","d":"having a strong, full flavor, often with a lot of butter, cream, or chocolate","c":"濃郁的","s":"A: We need a dessert for the client dinner on Thursday night, but some guests may feel full after the main course, so should we serve the chocolate cake? B: I'd choose something lighter, because that cake is very rich and heavy, and people usually prefer fresh fruit or sorbet after a big meal.","t":"A：週四晚上的客戶晚宴我們需要一道甜點，但有些客人吃完主菜可能會很飽，我們該上巧克力蛋糕嗎？ B：我會選清淡一點的，因為那個蛋糕非常【濃郁】又厚重，大家大餐後通常比較喜歡新鮮水果或雪酪。"},{"w":"smooth","p":"adj.","d":"having an even texture without lumps","c":"滑順的","s":"A: The chocolate sauce in our new dessert looked lumpy in the photos for the menu, so did the kitchen staff find out what went wrong yesterday? B: They heated it too quickly, so today the chef stirred it slowly over low heat until it became completely smooth and shiny, and the new photos look excellent.","t":"A：菜單照片中我們新甜點的巧克力醬看起來結塊了，廚房員工昨天找出問題出在哪裡了嗎？ B：他們加熱得太快了，所以今天主廚用小火慢慢攪拌，直到它變得完全【滑順】又有光澤，新照片看起來很棒。"},{"w":"creamy","p":"adj.","d":"soft and thick like cream","c":"綿密的；含奶油的","s":"A: Our café is planning a new cold drink for the summer months, and the owner wants something that feels special, so what did the test group prefer? B: Most people chose the chocolate milkshake made with fresh ice cream, because it was thick and creamy, and it reminded them of the drinks they had as children.","t":"A：我們咖啡館正在規劃夏季的新冷飲，老闆想要一款感覺特別的，試飲小組比較喜歡哪一款？ B：大多數人選了用新鮮冰淇淋做的巧克力奶昔，因為它濃稠又【綿密】，讓他們想起小時候喝的飲料。"},{"w":"dark","p":"adj.","d":"(of chocolate) containing a lot of cocoa and little or no milk","c":"黑的；深色的","s":"A: The health company wants to give its members a small chocolate gift, but it should match its healthy image, so which type do you think fits best? B: I'd recommend dark chocolate with at least seventy percent cocoa, because it has less sugar than other kinds, and many people believe it is better for the heart.","t":"A：那家健康公司想送會員一份小巧克力禮物，但要符合它健康的形象，你覺得哪一種最合適？ B：我會推薦可可含量至少百分之七十的【黑】巧克力，因為它的糖比其他種類少，而且很多人認為它對心臟比較好。"},{"w":"milk","p":"n.","d":"the white liquid from cows; \"milk chocolate\" is chocolate made with milk","c":"牛奶","s":"A: The children's hospital asked us to donate chocolate for its holiday party next Saturday, so which kind should we send to make the kids happy? B: Most young children find dark chocolate too strong, so let's send milk chocolate in small fun shapes, because it is softer, sweeter, and much more popular with kids.","t":"A：兒童醫院請我們為下週六的節日派對捐贈巧克力，我們該送哪一種才能讓孩子們開心？ B：大多數小孩覺得黑巧克力太濃烈，所以我們送造型有趣的小塊【牛奶】巧克力吧，因為它更軟、更甜，也更受孩子歡迎。"},{"w":"white","p":"adj.","d":"(of chocolate) made from cocoa butter, sugar, and milk, without dark cocoa solids","c":"白的","s":"A: The bakery wants to decorate the wedding cookies for Saturday's big order with a different color, because the brown chocolate looks too plain. Any ideas? B: We could melt some white chocolate and draw thin lines on top, because it stands out nicely against the brown, and the bride said she wants an elegant look.","t":"A：麵包店想用不同的顏色裝飾週六那筆大訂單的婚禮餅乾，因為咖啡色巧克力看起來太單調了。有什麼點子嗎？ B：我們可以融化一些【白】巧克力在上面畫細線，因為它在咖啡色上很顯眼，而且新娘說她想要高雅的感覺。"},{"w":"melt","p":"v.","d":"to change from solid to liquid because of heat","c":"融化","s":"A: We are shipping two hundred boxes of chocolate to our client in Kaohsiung next week, but the weather forecast says it will be very hot. How can we protect them? B: We should use the refrigerated delivery service, because the chocolates will quickly melt in a normal truck, and the client would definitely ask for a refund.","t":"A：我們下週要運兩百盒巧克力給高雄的客戶，但氣象預報說天氣會很熱。我們要怎麼保護它們？ B：我們應該用冷藏配送服務，因為巧克力在一般貨車裡很快就會【融化】，客戶一定會要求退款。"},{"w":"temper","p":"v.","d":"to heat and cool chocolate carefully so it becomes shiny and firm","c":"為（巧克力）調溫","s":"A: The chocolates from the new trainee look dull and gray instead of shiny, and some of them break too easily. What do you think the problem is? B: He probably didn't temper the chocolate correctly, so I will show him how to heat and cool it to the right temperatures during tomorrow's training session.","t":"A：新實習生做的巧克力看起來暗沉灰白而不是有光澤，有些還很容易斷裂。你覺得問題出在哪裡？ B：他可能沒有正確地為巧克力【調溫】，所以我明天培訓時會教他如何把它加熱和冷卻到正確的溫度。"},{"w":"coat","p":"v.","d":"to cover something with a thin layer","c":"裹上；覆蓋","s":"A: The strawberries we bought for the company's anniversary party look fresh, but they seem a little plain for such a special event. Any suggestions? B: We could coat them in melted dark chocolate and add some nuts on top, because guests usually love dipped fruit, and it looks very attractive on the dessert table.","t":"A：我們為公司週年派對買的草莓看起來很新鮮，但對這麼特別的活動來說似乎有點單調。有什麼建議嗎？ B：我們可以把它們【裹上】融化的黑巧克力，再在上面撒些堅果，因為客人通常很喜歡沾醬水果，而且放在甜點桌上看起來很吸引人。"},{"w":"bake","p":"v.","d":"to cook food such as bread or cake in an oven","c":"烘烤","s":"A: Our team wants to raise money for the local animal shelter next Friday, but we have a very small budget for the event. Do you have any ideas? B: Several of us could bake chocolate brownies at home on Thursday night and sell them in the lobby, because people always buy homemade treats for a good cause.","t":"A：我們團隊想在下週五為本地動物收容所募款，但活動預算非常少。你有什麼點子嗎？ B：我們幾個人可以週四晚上在家【烤】巧克力布朗尼，然後在大廳販售，因為大家總是會為了好的目的買自製點心。"},{"w":"flavor","p":"n.","d":"the particular taste of a food or drink","c":"口味；風味","s":"A: The marketing department wants to launch a limited chocolate product for the summer, so what did customers ask for in last month's online survey? B: Many of them asked for a new flavor like mango or passion fruit, because they think tropical tastes feel more refreshing during the hot months in Taiwan.","t":"A：行銷部想在夏天推出一款限定巧克力產品，顧客在上個月的線上調查中提出了什麼要求？ B：很多人希望有像芒果或百香果這樣的新【口味】，因為他們覺得熱帶風味在台灣炎熱的月份裡感覺更清爽。"},{"w":"aroma","p":"n.","d":"a strong, pleasant smell","c":"香氣","s":"A: Why do so many people walk into the chocolate shop near the train station, even when they are in a hurry to catch the morning train? B: The owner makes hot chocolate near the front door every morning, so the sweet aroma fills the whole street, and commuters find it hard to walk past without buying something.","t":"A：為什麼這麼多人走進火車站附近的巧克力店，即使他們正趕著搭早班火車？ B：老闆每天早上都在門口附近做熱巧克力，所以甜甜的【香氣】瀰漫整條街，通勤族很難不買點東西就走過去。"},{"w":"dessert","p":"n.","d":"sweet food eaten at the end of a meal","c":"甜點","s":"A: The restaurant is preparing the set menu for the company's year-end banquet, and the manager wants to know what we would like to serve after the main course. B: Let's choose a warm chocolate cake with vanilla ice cream for dessert, because almost everyone likes it, and it is the chef's most famous dish.","t":"A：餐廳正在準備公司尾牙的套餐菜單，經理想知道主菜之後我們想上什麼。 B：我們選溫熱的巧克力蛋糕配香草冰淇淋當【甜點】吧，因為幾乎每個人都喜歡，而且這是主廚最有名的料理。"},{"w":"treat","p":"n.","d":"something special and pleasant, such as food, that you give or enjoy","c":"犒賞；點心","s":"A: Our sales team finally reached its yearly target this afternoon after months of hard work, so how should the manager thank everyone before the weekend? B: She is planning to bring a box of fancy Belgian chocolates as a special treat for the team, and she will also let everyone leave an hour early on Friday.","t":"A：我們業務團隊經過幾個月的努力，今天下午終於達成年度目標，經理在週末前該怎麼感謝大家？ B：她打算帶一盒精緻的比利時巧克力作為團隊的特別【犒賞】，而且週五還會讓大家提早一小時下班。"},{"w":"indulgence","p":"n.","d":"something you enjoy that is not really necessary, often a little unhealthy","c":"放縱；享受","s":"A: You usually eat a very healthy lunch every day, so why did you buy that expensive chocolate cake at the café downstairs this afternoon? B: I finished a difficult project report after working late all week, so this cake is my small indulgence, and I will go back to salads and fruit on Monday.","t":"A：你平常每天午餐都吃得很健康，那為什麼今天下午在樓下咖啡館買了那個昂貴的巧克力蛋糕？ B：我整週加班，終於完成了一份困難的專案報告，所以這塊蛋糕是我的小小【放縱】，週一我就會回去吃沙拉和水果。"},{"w":"craving","p":"n.","d":"a very strong wish to eat or have something","c":"渴望；嘴饞","s":"A: Why do you always keep a few pieces of chocolate in your desk drawer, even though you say you are trying to eat less sugar this year? B: I often get a strong craving for something sweet around three o'clock, so one small piece helps me stay focused until the end of the working day.","t":"A：你說今年想少吃糖，為什麼總是在桌子抽屜裡放幾塊巧克力？ B：我常在三點左右非常【渴望】吃點甜的，所以吃一小塊能幫我保持專注到下班。"},{"w":"snack","p":"n.","d":"a small amount of food eaten between meals","c":"點心；零食","s":"A: The training session on Wednesday will last from nine to five, and the trainer is worried that people will get tired after lunch. What should we prepare? B: Let's put a basket of chocolate cookies and fruit at the back of the room, so everyone can grab a quick snack during the short afternoon break.","t":"A：週三的培訓從九點持續到五點，講師擔心大家午餐後會累。我們該準備什麼？ B：我們在教室後面放一籃巧克力餅乾和水果吧，這樣大家在下午短暫休息時可以快速拿點【點心】吃。"},{"w":"luxury","p":"n.","d":"something expensive and enjoyable that you do not really need","c":"奢侈品；奢華","s":"A: Why does the department store charge almost two thousand dollars for that small box of chocolates, when the supermarket sells similar ones for much less? B: That brand sells itself as a luxury, so every piece is handmade in France, wrapped in gold paper, and packed in a beautiful wooden box.","t":"A：為什麼百貨公司那一小盒巧克力要價將近兩千元，超市類似的卻便宜得多？ B：那個品牌把自己定位為【奢侈品】，所以每一顆都是在法國手工製作，用金色紙包裝，再裝進漂亮的木盒裡。"},{"w":"handmade","p":"adj.","d":"made by hand, not by machine","c":"手工製的","s":"A: The small shop on Lin Street sells chocolates at twice the price of the big brands, but it always has a long line on weekends. Why is that? B: Everything there is handmade by the owner and two assistants in the kitchen behind the shop, so customers know each piece is fresh and made with care.","t":"A：林街那家小店的巧克力價格是大品牌的兩倍，但週末總是大排長龍。為什麼會這樣？ B：那裡的每樣東西都是老闆和兩位助手在店後面的廚房【手工製作】的，所以顧客知道每一顆都新鮮又用心。"},{"w":"organic","p":"adj.","d":"grown without chemical fertilizers or pesticides","c":"有機的","s":"A: Our supermarket chain wants to attract more health-conscious shoppers this year, so which new chocolate products should we put on the shelves first? B: Let's start with bars made from organic cocoa grown without chemicals, because younger customers check labels carefully, and they are willing to pay more for natural products.","t":"A：我們的連鎖超市今年想吸引更多注重健康的顧客，我們該先把哪些新的巧克力產品上架？ B：我們先從用不含化學物質種植的【有機】可可做成的巧克力條開始吧，因為年輕顧客會仔細看標籤，而且願意為天然產品多付錢。"},{"w":"packaging","p":"n.","d":"the boxes, paper, or plastic used to wrap and sell a product","c":"包裝","s":"A: Sales of our chocolate gift boxes dropped last quarter, even though customers still say the taste is excellent. What do you think went wrong? B: The design team believes the packaging looks old-fashioned compared with our competitors' products, so they are creating a brighter box with a modern logo for the holiday season.","t":"A：雖然顧客仍然說味道很棒，但我們巧克力禮盒上一季的銷量下滑了。你覺得哪裡出了問題？ B：設計團隊認為和競爭對手的產品相比，我們的【包裝】看起來很過時，所以他們正在為節慶季節設計一款有現代標誌、更明亮的盒子。"},{"w":"gift","p":"n.","d":"something you give to someone, often on a special occasion","c":"禮物","s":"A: Our most important client in Tokyo is retiring at the end of this month after thirty years, so what should we send to thank her for her support? B: Let's send a beautiful box of local chocolates with a handwritten card as a farewell gift, because she always enjoyed tasting Taiwanese sweets during her visits.","t":"A：我們在東京最重要的客戶做了三十年，這個月底就要退休了，我們該送什麼感謝她的支持？ B：我們送一盒漂亮的在地巧克力配上手寫卡片作為臨別【禮物】吧，因為她每次來訪時都很喜歡品嚐台灣甜點。"},{"w":"satisfying","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel pleased because it gives you what you need or want","c":"令人滿足的","s":"A: I usually feel hungry again an hour after eating a regular candy bar, so why do you choose the chocolate with nuts for your afternoon break? B: The nuts give it more protein and fiber, so it is much more satisfying and keeps me full until dinner, especially on days when I have long meetings.","t":"A：我平常吃完一般的糖果棒一小時後又會餓，為什麼你下午休息時都選有堅果的巧克力？ B：堅果讓它有更多蛋白質和纖維，所以更【令人滿足】，能讓我一直飽到晚餐，尤其是在我有長時間會議的日子。"},{"w":"decadent","p":"adj.","d":"very rich and enjoyable, in a way that feels like a bit too much","c":"極致奢華的；濃郁享受的","s":"A: The hotel's new chocolate dessert costs almost five hundred dollars, so why are so many guests posting photos of it on social media this month? B: It is a truly decadent creation with three layers of chocolate, gold leaf, and a warm sauce poured at the table, so people feel it is worth the price.","t":"A：飯店新推出的巧克力甜點要價將近五百元，為什麼這個月有這麼多客人在社群媒體上貼它的照片？ B：它是一道真正【極致奢華】的作品，有三層巧克力、金箔，還有在桌邊淋上的熱醬汁，所以大家覺得物有所值。"}]},{"unit":58,"theme":"City 城市","cards":[{"w":"urban","p":"adj.","d":"relating to a city or town","c":"城市的；都市的","s":"A: Our company is planning to open three new fitness centers next year, so should we choose locations in small towns or in big cities? B: I think we should focus on urban areas first, because young office workers who live near the city center have more money and less free time to drive far away for exercise.","t":"A：我們公司計畫明年開三家新的健身中心，我們應該選在小鎮還是大城市？ B：我認為我們應該先把重點放在【都市】地區，因為住在市中心附近的年輕上班族比較有錢，也比較沒有空閒時間開車到遠處運動。"},{"w":"downtown","p":"n.","d":"the main business area in the center of a city","c":"市中心；商業區","s":"A: The client from Singapore wants to meet us on Thursday afternoon, but she is staying at a hotel near the airport, so where should we hold the meeting? B: Let's book a quiet meeting room near downtown, because it is only twenty minutes away by train and there are many good restaurants nearby for lunch afterward.","t":"A：新加坡的客戶想在星期四下午和我們見面，但她住在機場附近的飯店，我們應該在哪裡開會？ B：我們在【市中心】附近訂一間安靜的會議室吧，因為搭火車只要二十分鐘，而且附近有很多不錯的餐廳可以在會後吃午餐。"},{"w":"suburb","p":"n.","d":"an area where people live outside the center of a city","c":"郊區","s":"A: You used to live in a small apartment right next to the office, so why did you decide to move so far away last spring? B: After our second child was born, we bought a house with a garden in a quiet suburb, and although my trip to work is longer now, my kids have much more space to play outside.","t":"A：你以前住在辦公室旁邊的小公寓，為什麼去年春天決定搬到那麼遠的地方？ B：我們第二個孩子出生後，在一個安靜的【郊區】買了一間有花園的房子，雖然我現在上班的路程比較長，但孩子們有更多空間可以在戶外玩。"},{"w":"neighborhood","p":"n.","d":"a small area of a town and the people who live there","c":"社區；街坊","s":"A: The real estate agent showed me two apartments today, and they are almost the same price, so how should I decide between them? B: You should walk around each neighborhood in the evening, because it will help you see whether the area feels safe, whether there are shops nearby, and how noisy it becomes at night.","t":"A：房仲今天帶我看了兩間公寓，價格幾乎一樣，我該怎麼在兩者之間做決定？ B：你應該在傍晚到每個【社區】附近走走，因為這能幫你看出那一帶是否讓人覺得安全、附近有沒有商店，以及晚上會變得多吵。"},{"w":"street","p":"n.","d":"a public road in a city or town with buildings along it","c":"街道","s":"A: I am driving to the new client's office for the first time this afternoon, but my GPS keeps showing two different addresses, so can you help me? B: Their building is on Elm street, right across from the big department store, and you can park in the public lot behind the post office.","t":"A：我今天下午要第一次開車去新客戶的辦公室，但我的導航一直顯示兩個不同的地址，你可以幫我嗎？ B：他們的大樓在榆樹【街】上，就在那家大百貨公司正對面，你可以把車停在郵局後面的公共停車場。"},{"w":"avenue","p":"n.","d":"a wide street in a city, often with trees","c":"大街；大道","s":"A: The marketing team wants our new store to be seen by as many shoppers as possible, so which location do you prefer? B: I prefer the empty shop on Fifth avenue, because the wide road is lined with famous brand stores and thousands of tourists walk past it every weekend, even though the rent is quite high.","t":"A：行銷團隊希望我們的新店能被越多購物者看到越好，你比較喜歡哪個地點？ B：我比較喜歡第五【大道】上那間空店面，因為那條寬闊的路兩旁都是知名品牌商店，每個週末有數千名觀光客經過，雖然租金相當高。"},{"w":"boulevard","p":"n.","d":"a wide city road, often with trees on both sides","c":"林蔭大道","s":"A: The city government plans to hold the international marathon next month, so which roads will be closed on the morning of the race? B: The main boulevard that runs from the train station to the river will be closed from five to eleven, so employees who drive to work should leave home early or take the subway.","t":"A：市政府計畫下個月舉辦國際馬拉松，比賽當天早上哪些道路會封閉？ B：從火車站延伸到河邊的那條主要【林蔭大道】會從五點封到十一點，所以開車上班的員工應該提早出門或改搭捷運。"},{"w":"district","p":"n.","d":"a particular area of a city or country","c":"區；地區","s":"A: Our bank is looking for a place to open a new branch for small business owners, so do you have any recommendations in the city? B: The financial district near City Hall would be ideal, because many companies have their offices there and the area is easy to reach by both bus and train.","t":"A：我們銀行正在找地點，要為小型企業主開一家新分行，你對市區有什麼建議嗎？ B：市政府附近的金融【區】會很理想，因為很多公司的辦公室都在那裡，而且搭公車和火車都很容易到達。"},{"w":"skyscraper","p":"n.","d":"a very tall modern building in a city","c":"摩天大樓","s":"A: The architecture firm has invited us to visit their newest project downtown, so what exactly have they been building for the past three years? B: They have just finished a sixty-floor skyscraper with offices, a hotel, and a shopping center inside, and visitors can enjoy an amazing view of the whole city from the top floor.","t":"A：那家建築事務所邀請我們去參觀他們在市中心的最新案子，他們過去三年到底在蓋什麼？ B：他們剛完成一棟六十層樓的【摩天大樓】，裡面有辦公室、飯店和購物中心，訪客可以從頂樓欣賞整座城市的壯觀景色。"},{"w":"landmark","p":"n.","d":"a famous building or place that is easy to recognize","c":"地標","s":"A: Our overseas guests will arrive on Saturday, and they only have one free afternoon before the conference starts, so where should we take them? B: We should take them to Taipei 101, because it is the city's most famous landmark, and they can also visit the shopping mall and the food court on the lower floors.","t":"A：我們的海外貴賓星期六抵達，會議開始前他們只有一個空閒的下午，我們應該帶他們去哪裡？ B：我們應該帶他們去台北101，因為那是這座城市最有名的【地標】，他們還可以逛逛低樓層的購物中心和美食街。"},{"w":"square","p":"n.","d":"an open public area in a city with buildings around it","c":"廣場","s":"A: The company wants to hold a free outdoor concert to celebrate its twentieth anniversary, so where can thousands of people gather at once? B: The main square in front of the old city hall is large enough, and the city government usually gives permission for public events there as long as we apply two months early.","t":"A：公司想舉辦一場免費戶外音樂會慶祝二十週年，哪裡可以一次容納數千人聚集？ B：舊市政廳前的主【廣場】夠大，而且只要我們提早兩個月申請，市政府通常會核准在那裡舉辦公開活動。"},{"w":"plaza","p":"n.","d":"an open public space, often with shops around it","c":"廣場；購物廣場","s":"A: The new office building has a large open space on the ground floor, so how is the management company planning to use it? B: They are turning it into a shopping plaza with cafés, a bookstore, and benches under the trees, so that employees and local residents can relax there during lunch breaks and on weekends.","t":"A：新辦公大樓的一樓有一大片開放空間，管理公司打算怎麼使用它？ B：他們要把它改成一個購物【廣場】，裡面有咖啡館、書店和樹下的長椅，讓員工和當地居民可以在午休時間和週末在那裡放鬆。"},{"w":"park","p":"n.","d":"a large public area with grass and trees","c":"公園","s":"A: Many of our employees have said that they feel stressed and tired after sitting in front of their computers all day, so what can we do? B: We could organize a short walking group at lunchtime, because there is a beautiful park with a lake and shady trees only five minutes from our office building.","t":"A：很多員工反映整天坐在電腦前讓他們覺得壓力大又疲累，我們能做些什麼？ B：我們可以在午餐時間組織一個簡短的健走小組，因為離我們辦公大樓只要五分鐘就有一座有湖和樹蔭的漂亮【公園】。"},{"w":"traffic","p":"n.","d":"the cars and other vehicles moving on roads","c":"交通；車流","s":"A: You are usually the first person in the office every morning, so why did you arrive almost an hour late today? B: There was a serious accident on the highway near the bridge, and the traffic was so heavy that my car barely moved for forty minutes, so next time I will probably take the train instead.","t":"A：你通常每天早上都是第一個到辦公室的人，今天為什麼遲到將近一個小時？ B：橋附近的高速公路發生嚴重車禍，【交通】非常壅塞，我的車有四十分鐘幾乎動不了，所以下次我可能會改搭火車。"},{"w":"commute","p":"v.","d":"to travel regularly between home and work","c":"通勤","s":"A: Since you moved to Taoyuan last year, how long does it take you to get to our Taipei office every morning? B: I commute by high-speed rail and then take the subway for two stops, so the whole trip takes about fifty minutes, which gives me enough time to read the news and answer emails.","t":"A：你去年搬到桃園之後，每天早上到我們台北辦公室要花多久時間？ B：我搭高鐵【通勤】，然後再坐兩站捷運，所以整趟路程大約五十分鐘，讓我有足夠的時間看新聞和回覆電子郵件。"},{"w":"crowded","p":"adj.","d":"full of too many people","c":"擁擠的","s":"A: I need to buy a birthday present for my manager after work today, so do you think I should go to the night market or the department store? B: I would avoid the night market tonight, because it is always extremely crowded on Friday evenings, and you will spend more time waiting in lines than actually shopping.","t":"A：我今天下班後需要幫經理買生日禮物，你覺得我該去夜市還是百貨公司？ B：我今晚會避開夜市，因為星期五晚上那裡總是非常【擁擠】，你排隊等候的時間會比真正逛街的時間還多。"},{"w":"busy","p":"adj.","d":"full of people, vehicles or activity","c":"繁忙的；熱鬧的","s":"A: The owner wants to move our small bakery to a new location next year, so what kind of place is she looking for? B: She wants a shop on a busy corner near the train station, because thousands of commuters walk past there every morning and many of them would happily buy fresh bread on the way to work.","t":"A：老闆想在明年把我們的小麵包店搬到新地點，她在找什麼樣的地方？ B：她想要一間在火車站附近【熱鬧】街角的店面，因為每天早上有數千名通勤族從那裡經過，很多人會很樂意在上班途中買新鮮麵包。"},{"w":"vibrant","p":"adj.","d":"full of energy, life and excitement","c":"充滿活力的","s":"A: Our travel agency is creating a new tour package for young travelers, so what kind of city do you think they would enjoy most? B: Young people usually love a vibrant city with colorful street art, live music, and lively night markets, so I suggest that we include Kaohsiung and Tainan in the trip.","t":"A：我們旅行社正在為年輕旅客設計新的套裝行程，你覺得他們最喜歡哪一種城市？ B：年輕人通常喜愛有繽紛街頭藝術、現場音樂和熱鬧夜市、【充滿活力】的城市，所以我建議把高雄和台南排進行程。"},{"w":"modern","p":"adj.","d":"new and using the latest ideas or designs","c":"現代的","s":"A: The old train station looks very different from the photos I saw last year, so did the city government rebuild it? B: Yes, they kept the historic front wall but replaced the inside with a bright and modern hall that has glass roofs, digital signs, and comfortable waiting areas for passengers.","t":"A：舊火車站看起來和我去年看到的照片很不一樣，市政府重建了它嗎？ B：是的，他們保留了具歷史意義的正面牆，但把內部換成一個明亮又【現代】的大廳，有玻璃屋頂、數位看板和舒適的旅客候車區。"},{"w":"historic","p":"adj.","d":"important in history","c":"有歷史意義的；歷史悠久的","s":"A: The developer wants to tear down the old tea factory near the river and build apartments, so why are so many residents against the plan? B: The building is more than a hundred years old and is considered a historic site, so local people believe it should be protected and turned into a museum instead.","t":"A：開發商想拆除河邊的老茶廠蓋公寓，為什麼這麼多居民反對這項計畫？ B：那棟建築已經超過一百年，被視為【具歷史意義的】古蹟，所以當地人認為應該保護它，改建成博物館。"},{"w":"population","p":"n.","d":"the number of people living in a place","c":"人口","s":"A: The supermarket chain is thinking about opening a store in Hsinchu, so what information does the planning team need before making a final decision? B: They need to know how quickly the population of the city is growing, because more people moving there for technology jobs means more families who will shop for groceries every week.","t":"A：那家連鎖超市正在考慮在新竹開店，規劃團隊在做最後決定之前需要哪些資訊？ B：他們需要知道這座城市的【人口】成長得有多快，因為越多人為了科技業工作搬到那裡，就代表每週會有越多家庭來採買食品雜貨。"},{"w":"resident","p":"n.","d":"a person who lives in a particular place","c":"居民","s":"A: The building manager sent an email saying that the elevator will be repaired next week, so what should people living on the top floors do? B: Every resident who has difficulty using the stairs can contact the front desk, and the staff will help carry their shopping bags and heavy packages up to their apartments.","t":"A：大樓管理員寄電子郵件說下週要修電梯，住在頂樓的人該怎麼辦？ B：每位爬樓梯有困難的【居民】都可以聯絡櫃檯，工作人員會幫忙把購物袋和重的包裹搬到他們的公寓。"},{"w":"tourist","p":"n.","d":"a person who travels to a place for fun","c":"觀光客","s":"A: Sales at our gift shop have increased by thirty percent this summer, so what do you think is the main reason for this success? B: Since the new airline started direct flights from Japan, many more tourist groups visit the old street every day, and they love buying our handmade tea cups as souvenirs.","t":"A：我們禮品店今年夏天的業績成長了百分之三十，你覺得成功的主要原因是什麼？ B：自從新的航空公司開了從日本出發的直飛航班，每天有更多【觀光客】團體來逛老街，他們很喜歡買我們手工做的茶杯當紀念品。"},{"w":"transport","p":"n.","d":"a system for carrying people or goods from place to place","c":"交通運輸","s":"A: Many new employees have asked whether they really need to buy a car after moving to the city for this job, so what should we tell them? B: Tell them that public transport here is cheap and reliable, because buses and trains run every few minutes and can take them almost anywhere in the city.","t":"A：很多新員工問，為了這份工作搬到這座城市後，他們是否真的需要買車，我們該怎麼告訴他們？ B：告訴他們這裡的大眾【運輸】既便宜又可靠，因為公車和火車每幾分鐘就有一班，幾乎可以載他們到市區任何地方。"},{"w":"subway","p":"n.","d":"an underground train system in a city","c":"地鐵；捷運","s":"A: The conference center is on the other side of the city, and the taxi drivers say the roads will be very busy tomorrow morning, so how should we get there? B: Let's take the subway, because the underground trains are not affected by road traffic, and the station is right next to the main entrance of the center.","t":"A：會議中心在城市的另一邊，計程車司機說明天早上路上會很塞，我們該怎麼去？ B：我們搭【捷運】吧，因為地下列車不受道路交通影響，而且車站就在會議中心主要入口旁邊。"},{"w":"bus","p":"n.","d":"a large vehicle that carries many passengers on a fixed route","c":"公車","s":"A: The company is moving to a new office in the science park next month, and many employees are worried about how they will get there without a car, so what is the plan? B: Management has arranged a free shuttle bus that will leave the main train station every fifteen minutes during rush hour in the morning and evening.","t":"A：公司下個月要搬到科學園區的新辦公室，很多員工擔心沒有車要怎麼去，計畫是什麼？ B：管理階層安排了免費接駁【公車】，早晚尖峰時段每十五分鐘從火車總站發車一次。"},{"w":"intersection","p":"n.","d":"a place where two or more roads cross","c":"十字路口","s":"A: The delivery driver called again and said he cannot find our warehouse, even though he is very close, so how should I explain the way? B: Tell him to turn left at the next intersection with the big traffic lights and the gas station, and our gray building will be the third one on the right side.","t":"A：送貨司機又打電話來說他找不到我們的倉庫，雖然他已經很近了，我該怎麼跟他說明路線？ B：告訴他在下一個有大紅綠燈和加油站的【十字路口】左轉，我們的灰色建築就是右手邊的第三棟。"},{"w":"crosswalk","p":"n.","d":"a marked place where people can walk across a road","c":"斑馬線；行人穿越道","s":"A: Parents at the school next to our office are worried about their children's safety in the morning, so what has the city decided to do? B: The city is painting a new crosswalk in front of the school gate and adding a traffic light, so that students can cross the road safely when cars are coming.","t":"A：我們辦公室隔壁學校的家長擔心孩子早上的安全，市政府決定怎麼做？ B：市政府要在校門前漆一條新的【斑馬線】並增設紅綠燈，讓學生在有車來的時候也能安全過馬路。"},{"w":"sidewalk","p":"n.","d":"a path at the side of a road for people to walk on","c":"人行道","s":"A: The restaurant manager wants to put a few tables outside so that customers can enjoy the warm spring weather, so is that allowed in this area? B: Yes, but we must apply for a permit first, and we have to leave enough space on the sidewalk so that people with strollers and wheelchairs can still pass by easily.","t":"A：餐廳經理想在外面擺幾張桌子，讓客人享受溫暖的春天天氣，這一區允許這樣做嗎？ B：可以，但我們必須先申請許可，而且要在【人行道】上留下足夠的空間，讓推嬰兒車和坐輪椅的人仍然可以輕鬆通過。"},{"w":"market","p":"n.","d":"a place where people buy and sell food and goods","c":"市場","s":"A: The chef at our hotel restaurant always says that his vegetables taste much fresher than the ones in supermarkets, so where does he buy them? B: He goes to the traditional market near the river at six o'clock every morning, where local farmers sell fruit, vegetables, and fish that were picked or caught only a few hours earlier.","t":"A：我們飯店餐廳的主廚總是說他的蔬菜比超市的新鮮多了，他都在哪裡買？ B：他每天早上六點去河邊的傳統【市場】，當地農民在那裡賣幾個小時前才摘下或捕到的水果、蔬菜和魚。"},{"w":"mall","p":"n.","d":"a large building with many shops inside","c":"購物中心","s":"A: The weather forecast says it will rain all weekend, so where can we take the visiting sales team to relax after the training sessions finish? B: We could take them to the new shopping mall next to the station, because it has hundreds of stores, a cinema, and a large food court, so nobody will get wet.","t":"A：天氣預報說整個週末都會下雨，訓練課程結束後，我們可以帶來訪的業務團隊去哪裡放鬆？ B：我們可以帶他們去車站旁邊新開的【購物中心】，因為那裡有數百家店、一間電影院和一個大型美食街，沒有人會淋濕。"},{"w":"restaurant","p":"n.","d":"a place where people pay to sit and eat meals","c":"餐廳","s":"A: We need to take the visiting directors out for dinner after the board meeting on Wednesday, so have you made a reservation anywhere yet? B: I booked a private room at a seafood restaurant on the twentieth floor, because the food there is excellent and the guests can enjoy a wonderful night view of the river.","t":"A：星期三董事會開完後，我們需要帶來訪的董事們去吃晚餐，你已經在哪裡訂位了嗎？ B：我在二十樓的一家海鮮【餐廳】訂了包廂，因為那裡的菜很棒，客人還能欣賞美麗的河岸夜景。"},{"w":"cafe","p":"n.","d":"a small place that sells coffee, drinks and light meals","c":"咖啡館","s":"A: I have an online job interview at ten tomorrow morning, but the internet at my apartment has been very slow this week, so where can I go? B: There is a quiet cafe around the corner with fast WiFi and private booths, so you can order a coffee and do the interview there without any noise.","t":"A：我明天早上十點有一場線上工作面試，但這週我公寓的網路一直很慢，我可以去哪裡？ B：轉角有一家安靜的【咖啡館】，有快速的無線網路和私人座位區，你可以點杯咖啡，在那裡安靜地面試。"},{"w":"nightlife","p":"n.","d":"entertainment such as bars, music and clubs at night","c":"夜生活","s":"A: Our company is sending three young engineers to work in Bangkok for six months, so what do you think they will enjoy most about living there? B: They will probably love the nightlife, because the city has rooftop bars, live music, and night markets that stay open until very late, even after a long day at work.","t":"A：我們公司要派三位年輕工程師到曼谷工作六個月，你覺得他們最喜歡那裡生活的哪一點？ B：他們大概會很愛那裡的【夜生活】，因為那座城市有屋頂酒吧、現場音樂和營業到很晚的夜市，即使上班一整天後也能去玩。"},{"w":"skyline","p":"n.","d":"the shape of buildings against the sky","c":"天際線","s":"A: The photographer for our company's annual report wants to take a picture that shows how much the city has grown, so where should he stand? B: He should go to the top of the hill behind the university at sunset, because from there he can capture the whole skyline with all the tall office towers lit up.","t":"A：為公司年報拍照的攝影師想拍一張能呈現這座城市成長多少的照片，他應該站在哪裡？ B：他應該在日落時到大學後面的山頂，因為從那裡他可以拍到所有高聳辦公大樓都亮燈的整片【天際線】。"}]},{"unit":59,"theme":"Classmates 同學","cards":[{"w":"peer","p":"n.","d":"a person of the same age, class or level as you","c":"同儕；同輩","s":"A: The new interns seem nervous about giving feedback to the senior designers, so how can we help them feel more confident during their first month? B: Let's pair each intern with a peer from last year's program, because people usually ask questions more freely when the person helping them is at the same level.","t":"A：新來的實習生似乎不太敢給資深設計師意見，我們要怎麼幫助他們在第一個月更有自信？ B：我們讓每位實習生搭配一位去年計畫的【同儕】吧，因為當幫忙的人和自己程度相同時，大家通常會更放心地發問。"},{"w":"schoolmate","p":"n.","d":"a person who goes or went to the same school as you","c":"同校同學；校友","s":"A: I heard you already knew the new marketing manager before she joined our company last week, so where did you two first meet? B: She was my schoolmate at a high school in Tainan, and although we were in different classes, we often took the same bus home every afternoon.","t":"A：聽說新來的行銷經理上週加入公司前你就認識她了，你們兩個最初是在哪裡認識的？ B：她是我在台南念高中時的【同校同學】，雖然我們不同班，但每天下午常搭同一班公車回家。"},{"w":"friend","p":"n.","d":"a person you know well and like","c":"朋友","s":"A: You look really happy today, and you keep smiling at your phone, so did you get some good news from the head office this morning? B: Not exactly, but my closest friend from university just told me she is moving to Taipei next month and will work in the building across the street.","t":"A：你今天看起來好開心，一直對著手機微笑，是今天早上收到總公司的好消息嗎？ B：不完全是，是我大學時最要好的【朋友】剛告訴我，她下個月要搬到台北，而且會在對街的大樓上班。"},{"w":"teammate","p":"n.","d":"a person who is on the same team as you","c":"隊友","s":"A: Our department won the company basketball tournament on Saturday, so who scored the winning points in the last few seconds of the game? B: Kevin from accounting threw the final shot, but he said he could not have done it without his teammate, who passed him the ball at exactly the right moment.","t":"A：我們部門星期六贏得了公司籃球賽，最後幾秒是誰得到致勝分的？ B：會計部的 Kevin 投進最後一球，但他說如果沒有他的【隊友】在最恰當的時刻把球傳給他，他不可能做到。"},{"w":"partner","p":"n.","d":"a person you work or do an activity with","c":"夥伴；搭檔","s":"A: The training course next week includes several role-play exercises about handling customer complaints, so do we need to prepare anything before the first session? B: Yes, the trainer asked everyone to choose a partner from another department and practice a short conversation together, so you should contact someone by Thursday.","t":"A：下週的培訓課程有好幾個處理客訴的角色扮演練習，第一堂課前我們需要準備什麼嗎？ B：需要，講師要求每個人從其他部門選一位【搭檔】，一起練習一段簡短的對話，所以你應該在星期四前聯絡好人選。"},{"w":"group","p":"n.","d":"a number of people who do something together","c":"小組；群體","s":"A: There are almost forty new employees at the orientation today, so how will the trainers manage such a large number of people in one room? B: They plan to divide everyone into a small group of five or six people, and each one will have its own table, leader, and set of tasks.","t":"A：今天的新人訓練有將近四十位新員工，訓練師要怎麼在一個房間裡帶這麼多人？ B：他們打算把大家分成五、六人一組的【小組】，每組都有自己的桌子、組長和一套任務。"},{"w":"class","p":"n.","d":"a group of students taught together; a course of lessons","c":"班級；課程","s":"A: You have been leaving the office early every Tuesday and Thursday this month, so are you taking care of something important for your family? B: No, I signed up for an evening Japanese class near the train station, because our company is going to open a new branch in Osaka next spring.","t":"A：你這個月每週二和週四都提早下班，是在處理家裡重要的事嗎？ B：不是，我報名了火車站附近的晚間日文【課程】，因為我們公司明年春天要在大阪開新分公司。"},{"w":"cooperate","p":"v.","d":"to work together with others to reach the same goal","c":"合作；配合","s":"A: The building manager says the fire drill will take about thirty minutes on Friday afternoon, so what does he expect from all the tenants? B: He hopes every company will cooperate with the safety team by leaving quickly through the stairs, because last year many workers ignored the alarm and stayed at their desks.","t":"A：大樓管理員說星期五下午的消防演習大約要三十分鐘，他希望所有租戶怎麼做？ B：他希望每家公司都能【配合】安全小組，迅速從樓梯離開，因為去年很多員工不理會警報，一直待在座位上。"},{"w":"collaborate","p":"v.","d":"to work together with someone to create or achieve something","c":"協作；共同合作","s":"A: The new advertising campaign for the sports drink looks amazing, so did our design team create all the videos and posters by themselves? B: No, they decided to collaborate with a young film studio from Kaohsiung, and the two teams spent three months sharing ideas, writing scripts, and filming together.","t":"A：那款運動飲料的新廣告看起來好棒，所有影片和海報都是我們設計團隊自己做的嗎？ B：不是，他們決定和一家來自高雄的年輕影像工作室【共同合作】，兩個團隊花了三個月一起交流想法、寫腳本和拍攝。"},{"w":"share","p":"v.","d":"to have or use something together with others","c":"分享；共用","s":"A: The office is getting very crowded since the sales team moved to our floor, so where will the two new assistants sit next week? B: Until the renovation upstairs is finished, they will have to share the long desk by the window, and they can keep their files in the cabinet behind it.","t":"A：自從業務團隊搬到我們這層後辦公室變得好擠，下週兩位新助理要坐哪裡？ B：在樓上整修完成之前，他們得【共用】窗邊那張長桌，文件可以放在後面的櫃子裡。"},{"w":"support","p":"v.","d":"to help and encourage someone","c":"支持；支援","s":"A: Linda seems worried about leading her first big project while the director is away on a business trip, so is there anything we can do? B: Let's support her by answering her questions quickly and offering to check her reports, because she will feel much calmer if she knows the team is behind her.","t":"A：主任出差期間，Linda 要帶她的第一個大型專案，她似乎很擔心，我們能做些什麼嗎？ B：我們就盡快回答她的問題、主動幫她檢查報告來【支持】她，因為只要知道團隊站在她這邊，她會安心很多。"},{"w":"discuss","p":"v.","d":"to talk about something with other people","c":"討論","s":"A: The customer survey shows that many people are unhappy with our delivery times, so when will the managers decide how to solve this problem? B: They are meeting on Monday morning to discuss several possible plans, including hiring more drivers and opening a small warehouse in the southern part of the city.","t":"A：顧客調查顯示很多人不滿意我們的送貨時間，經理們什麼時候會決定怎麼解決這個問題？ B：他們星期一早上會開會【討論】幾個可能的方案，包括多雇幾位司機和在市區南邊開一個小倉庫。"},{"w":"interact","p":"v.","d":"to talk and do things with other people","c":"互動","s":"A: Why did the hotel ask its front desk staff to stand beside the counter instead of sitting behind the computer screens all day? B: The manager believes that guests feel more welcome when employees interact with them face to face, smile often, and offer useful advice about restaurants and places to visit nearby.","t":"A：為什麼飯店要求櫃檯人員站在櫃檯旁邊，而不是整天坐在電腦螢幕後面？ B：經理認為當員工面對面和客人【互動】、常常微笑，並提供附近餐廳和景點的實用建議時，客人會覺得更受歡迎。"},{"w":"respect","p":"v.","d":"to treat someone or something with care because you think they are important","c":"尊重","s":"A: Our new team includes people from five different countries, so how can we avoid misunderstandings when we plan meetings and company events? B: We should respect everyone's holidays and customs, ask politely when we are not sure about something, and choose times and foods that work for the whole team.","t":"A：我們的新團隊有來自五個不同國家的人，規劃會議和公司活動時要怎麼避免誤會？ B：我們應該【尊重】每個人的節日和習俗，不確定時禮貌地詢問，並選擇適合整個團隊的時間和食物。"},{"w":"helpful","p":"adj.","d":"useful; willing to help","c":"有幫助的；樂於助人的","s":"A: How was your first week at the new branch, and did you have any trouble learning the computer system the company uses for orders? B: It was great, because the staff there were very helpful and showed me every step slowly, so I could process orders by myself by Wednesday afternoon.","t":"A：你在新分店的第一週怎麼樣？學公司的訂單電腦系統有遇到困難嗎？ B：很棒，因為那裡的員工都非常【樂於助人】，慢慢地教我每個步驟，所以到星期三下午我就能自己處理訂單了。"},{"w":"friendly","p":"adj.","d":"kind and pleasant to other people","c":"友善的","s":"A: We are looking for a café where we can hold a relaxed meeting with our new clients from Singapore next Friday, so do you know a good place? B: There is a quiet café on Fifth Street where the owner is very friendly, remembers every guest's name, and often brings free cookies to the table.","t":"A：我們在找一家咖啡館，下週五要和新加坡的新客戶輕鬆開個會，你知道哪裡不錯嗎？ B：第五街有一家安靜的咖啡館，老闆非常【友善】，記得每位客人的名字，還常常送免費餅乾到桌上。"},{"w":"competitive","p":"adj.","d":"wanting very much to win or be better than others","c":"好勝的；競爭激烈的","s":"A: The sales contest only started on Monday, but Jason has already called over a hundred customers, so why is he working so hard this week? B: He is a very competitive person who always wants to finish first, and the winner of this contest will also get a free trip to Japan.","t":"A：業績競賽星期一才開始，Jason 已經打給超過一百位客戶了，他這週為什麼這麼拚？ B：他是個非常【好勝】的人，總是想拿第一，而且這次比賽的優勝者還能免費去日本旅行。"},{"w":"supportive","p":"adj.","d":"giving help and encouragement","c":"支持的；給予鼓勵的","s":"A: You decided to take evening classes for your master's degree while working full-time, so how does your manager feel about your busy schedule? B: She has been very supportive about it, and she even lets me leave thirty minutes early on exam days so that I can get to campus on time.","t":"A：你決定一邊全職工作一邊上夜間碩士課程，你的主管對你這麼忙的行程有什麼看法？ B：她一直非常【支持】，甚至讓我在考試那天提早三十分鐘下班，好讓我準時到學校。"},{"w":"cooperative","p":"adj.","d":"willing to work with others and help them","c":"合作的；配合的","s":"A: The software company in Hsinchu finally agreed to fix the problems with our new booking system, so how was the meeting with their engineers yesterday? B: It went smoothly, because their team was very cooperative, answered all our questions, and promised to send us an updated version before the end of the month.","t":"A：新竹那家軟體公司終於同意修正我們新訂位系統的問題，昨天和他們工程師的會議怎麼樣？ B：很順利，因為他們的團隊非常【配合】，回答了我們所有的問題，還答應在月底前寄給我們更新版本。"},{"w":"active","p":"adj.","d":"doing a lot of things; taking part","c":"積極的；活躍的","s":"A: The company wants to choose one employee to represent our office at the regional leadership program next spring, so who do you think should go? B: I would recommend Grace, because she is very active in team meetings, often shares new ideas, and volunteers to organize events for the whole department.","t":"A：公司想選一位員工代表我們辦公室參加明年春天的區域領導力課程，你覺得誰該去？ B：我推薦 Grace，因為她在團隊會議中非常【積極】，常常提出新點子，還自願幫整個部門籌辦活動。"},{"w":"quiet","p":"adj.","d":"making little noise; not talking much","c":"安靜的；文靜的","s":"A: The new accountant does not say much during our weekly meetings, so do you think she is unhappy with her job or with the team? B: I don't think so, because she is just a quiet person who prefers listening, and her reports are always the most careful and detailed ones in the office.","t":"A：新來的會計在每週會議中話不多，你覺得她是對工作或團隊不滿意嗎？ B：我不這麼認為，她只是個【文靜】的人，比較喜歡傾聽，而且她的報告一直是辦公室裡最仔細、最詳盡的。"},{"w":"popular","p":"adj.","d":"liked by many people","c":"受歡迎的","s":"A: Why is there always such a long line at the small noodle shop next to our office building every day around twelve o'clock? B: It is very popular with office workers in this area because the prices are low, the portions are big, and the owner can prepare an order in less than five minutes.","t":"A：為什麼我們辦公大樓旁邊那家小麵店每天中午十二點左右都大排長龍？ B：它在這一帶的上班族之間非常【受歡迎】，因為價格便宜、份量大，而且老闆不到五分鐘就能做好一份餐點。"},{"w":"familiar","p":"adj.","d":"known to you because you have seen or used it before","c":"熟悉的","s":"A: We need someone to help the visitors from our German partner find their way around the factory tomorrow, so who should we ask to guide them? B: Let's ask Peter, because he has worked in every section of the factory for ten years and is familiar with all the machines and safety rules.","t":"A：明天需要有人幫德國合作夥伴的訪客認識工廠環境，我們該請誰帶他們？ B：請 Peter 吧，因為他在工廠每個部門都待過，做了十年，對所有機器和安全規定都很【熟悉】。"},{"w":"diverse","p":"adj.","d":"very different from each other; including many types","c":"多元的；多樣的","s":"A: The new international school near the science park has been hiring a lot of teachers this year, so what kind of students do they have? B: Their student body is very diverse, with children from more than twenty countries, so the school also offers language support classes and cultural events every month.","t":"A：科學園區附近那所新的國際學校今年聘了很多老師，他們的學生是什麼樣的？ B：他們的學生非常【多元】，有來自二十多個國家的孩子，所以學校每個月也會提供語言輔導課和文化活動。"},{"w":"attentive","p":"adj.","d":"listening or watching carefully; noticing what others need","c":"專心的；體貼周到的","s":"A: The hotel received excellent reviews on the travel website last month, so what did the guests like most about their stay there? B: Many of them said the staff were very attentive, because they noticed small things like extra pillows or birthday plans and took care of them before guests even asked.","t":"A：那家飯店上個月在旅遊網站上得到很好的評價，客人最喜歡住宿的哪一點？ B：很多人說員工非常【體貼周到】，因為他們會注意到額外枕頭或生日安排這類小事，甚至在客人開口之前就處理好了。"},{"w":"respectful","p":"adj.","d":"showing politeness and care for others","c":"尊重人的；有禮貌的","s":"A: Some customers become very angry on the phone when their packages arrive late, so how should new call center staff deal with them? B: They should stay calm and respectful, listen without interrupting, apologize for the delay, and explain clearly when the customer can expect to receive the package.","t":"A：包裹延遲送達時，有些客人在電話裡會非常生氣，新來的客服人員該怎麼應對？ B：他們應該保持冷靜和【有禮貌】，不打斷對方地傾聽，為延誤道歉，並清楚說明客人預計何時能收到包裹。"},{"w":"discussion","p":"n.","d":"a talk about something between people","c":"討論","s":"A: The meeting about the new holiday schedule lasted almost three hours yesterday afternoon, so why did it take so long to make a decision? B: There was a long discussion about whether the factory should close for a whole week in February or only for three days, because both choices have problems.","t":"A：昨天下午關於新假期安排的會議開了將近三個小時，為什麼這麼久才做出決定？ B：大家針對工廠二月該停工整整一週還是只停三天進行了很長的【討論】，因為兩種選擇都有問題。"},{"w":"activity","p":"n.","d":"something people do for fun or to reach a goal","c":"活動","s":"A: The human resources department wants to plan something special for the staff before the busy season starts in October, so do you have any ideas? B: A team-building activity like a cooking contest or a mountain hike would be fun, because people from different departments could get to know each other better.","t":"A：人資部想在十月旺季開始前為員工安排一些特別的事，你有什麼想法嗎？ B：像烹飪比賽或爬山這類團隊建立【活動】會很有趣，因為不同部門的人可以更了解彼此。"},{"w":"assignment","p":"n.","d":"a piece of work given to someone as part of a job or course","c":"任務；作業","s":"A: You look very busy this week, and I saw you stay at the office until nine last night, so what are you working on now? B: My manager gave me a special assignment to compare the prices of five suppliers, and she needs my report before the budget meeting on Friday morning.","t":"A：你這週看起來好忙，我看到你昨晚待在辦公室到九點，你現在在忙什麼？ B：主管交給我一項特別【任務】，要比較五家供應商的價格，她需要在星期五早上預算會議前拿到我的報告。"},{"w":"presentation","p":"n.","d":"a talk that gives information to a group of people","c":"簡報；發表","s":"A: The clients from Tokyo are arriving at ten tomorrow morning, so is everything ready for the meeting in the large conference room? B: Almost, but I still need to check the projector and practice my presentation about our new products one more time, because I want to finish it in twenty minutes.","t":"A：東京的客戶明天早上十點到，大會議室的會議都準備好了嗎？ B：差不多了，但我還要檢查投影機，並再練習一次介紹新產品的【簡報】，因為我想在二十分鐘內講完。"},{"w":"study","p":"v.","d":"to spend time learning about a subject","c":"研讀；學習","s":"A: You told me you are planning to apply for the position at our London office next year, so how are you preparing for the interview? B: I study business English for an hour every night after dinner, and on weekends I join an online group where we practice speaking about our jobs.","t":"A：你跟我說你打算明年申請倫敦辦公室的職位，你怎麼準備面試？ B：我每天晚餐後花一小時【研讀】商用英文，週末則參加一個線上社團，一起練習談論我們的工作。"},{"w":"review","p":"v.","d":"to look at or check something again carefully","c":"審閱；複習","s":"A: The contract with the new cleaning company is almost ready, so can we sign it this afternoon and let them start working next Monday? B: Not yet, because our lawyer wants to review every page carefully first, especially the part about the price increases and what happens if they miss a cleaning day.","t":"A：和新清潔公司的合約快好了，我們今天下午可以簽約，讓他們下週一開始工作嗎？ B：還不行，因為我們的律師想先仔細【審閱】每一頁，尤其是漲價的部分，以及如果他們漏掉一天清潔會怎樣。"},{"w":"get along","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have a friendly relationship with someone","c":"相處融洽","s":"A: The two new engineers will share an office and travel together to the factory in Vietnam every month, so do you think that will cause any problems? B: I don't think so, because they already get along very well, often eat lunch together, and even went hiking with their families last weekend.","t":"A：兩位新工程師要共用一間辦公室，每個月還要一起去越南的工廠，你覺得會有問題嗎？ B：我不這麼認為，因為他們已經【相處融洽】，常一起吃午餐，上週末甚至帶著家人一起去爬山。"}]},{"unit":60,"theme":"Climate 氣候","cards":[{"w":"climate","p":"n.","d":"the usual weather conditions in a place over a long time","c":"氣候","s":"A: Our company is thinking about opening a new factory in the south of the country next year, so what do managers need to consider before they choose the location? B: They should study the local climate carefully, because hot and wet conditions all year round can damage machines and raise cooling costs.","t":"A：我們公司正考慮明年在國家南部開設一間新工廠，經理們在選擇地點前需要考慮什麼？ B：他們應該仔細研究當地的【氣候】，因為全年炎熱潮濕的環境會損壞機器並提高冷卻成本。"},{"w":"weather","p":"n.","d":"the conditions in the air at a particular time, such as rain, sun or wind","c":"天氣","s":"A: The outdoor product launch is planned for Saturday afternoon in the park, but I heard it might rain, so should we prepare a backup plan just in case? B: Yes, let's check the weather report again on Thursday, and if it looks bad, we can move the event into the hotel ballroom.","t":"A：戶外產品發表會預定在週六下午於公園舉行，但我聽說可能會下雨，我們要不要準備一個備案以防萬一？ B：要，我們週四再查一次【天氣】預報，如果看起來不好，就把活動移到飯店宴會廳。"},{"w":"temperature","p":"n.","d":"how hot or cold something is","c":"溫度；氣溫","s":"A: Several employees on the third floor have complained that the office feels too cold in the afternoons, so is there anything the building manager can do? B: He said he will raise the temperature on the air conditioner by two degrees and also check whether any windows near the meeting rooms are leaking.","t":"A：三樓有好幾位員工抱怨下午辦公室太冷，大樓管理員能做些什麼嗎？ B：他說會把冷氣的【溫度】調高兩度，也會檢查會議室附近是否有窗戶漏風。"},{"w":"rainfall","p":"n.","d":"the amount of rain that falls in an area","c":"降雨量","s":"A: The farmers who supply vegetables to our restaurant chain say prices may go up this autumn, so do you know why that is happening? B: The total rainfall this summer was much lower than usual, so many fields were too dry and the harvest will be smaller than last year's.","t":"A：供應我們連鎖餐廳蔬菜的農民說今年秋天價格可能會上漲，你知道為什麼嗎？ B：今年夏天的總【降雨量】比平常少很多，所以許多田地太乾，收成會比去年少。"},{"w":"humidity","p":"n.","d":"the amount of water in the air","c":"濕度","s":"A: The paper in our storage room keeps getting soft and wavy before we can use it in the printers, so what do you think the problem is? B: The humidity in that room is very high during the rainy season, so we should buy a dehumidifier and keep the door closed.","t":"A：我們儲藏室裡的紙在放進印表機前總是變軟變皺，你覺得問題出在哪裡？ B：那個房間在雨季時【濕度】很高，所以我們應該買一台除濕機，並且把門關好。"},{"w":"atmosphere","p":"n.","d":"the mixture of gases around the earth","c":"大氣（層）","s":"A: I'm preparing a short presentation for our environmental training next week, so could you help me explain why factory smoke is such a serious problem? B: Sure, you can say that the smoke releases harmful gases into the atmosphere, where they trap heat and make the air dirtier for everyone who lives nearby.","t":"A：我正在為下週的環保訓練準備一個簡短報告，你能幫我解釋為什麼工廠排煙是這麼嚴重的問題嗎？ B：當然，你可以說煙會把有害氣體排放到【大氣】中，這些氣體會留住熱量，並讓附近居民呼吸的空氣更髒。"},{"w":"season","p":"n.","d":"one of the four periods of the year, such as spring or winter","c":"季節","s":"A: Our travel agency is planning special tour packages to Japan, so which time of year do you think will attract the most customers from Taiwan? B: I think spring is the best season because the cherry blossoms are beautiful, the temperature is comfortable, and many families take vacations in early April.","t":"A：我們旅行社正在規劃前往日本的特別旅遊行程，你認為一年中哪個時候最能吸引台灣客人？ B：我認為春天是最好的【季節】，因為櫻花很美、氣溫舒適，而且許多家庭在四月初會去度假。"},{"w":"seasonal","p":"adj.","d":"happening or needed only at a certain time of year","c":"季節性的","s":"A: Our ice cream shop always gets very busy from June to August, but we don't need as many workers in winter, so how should we handle staffing? B: We could hire seasonal workers, such as university students on summer break, who are happy to work for three months and then return to school.","t":"A：我們的冰淇淋店每年六月到八月都很忙，但冬天不需要那麼多員工，我們該如何安排人力？ B：我們可以雇用【季節性的】工作人員，例如放暑假的大學生，他們很樂意工作三個月然後回學校。"},{"w":"tropical","p":"adj.","d":"from or like the hot, wet areas near the equator","c":"熱帶的","s":"A: The marketing team wants to hold next year's sales conference somewhere warm and relaxing, so do you have any ideas for a good place? B: How about a tropical island in Southeast Asia, where the weather is hot, the beaches are beautiful, and the resort hotels have large meeting rooms?","t":"A：行銷團隊希望明年的業務會議在溫暖又放鬆的地方舉行，你有什麼好地點的建議嗎？ B：東南亞的【熱帶】島嶼怎麼樣？那裡天氣炎熱、海灘漂亮，而且度假飯店有大型會議室。"},{"w":"temperate","p":"adj.","d":"not very hot and not very cold","c":"溫帶的；溫和的","s":"A: Our company is choosing between two cities for its new European office, so why did the director say that the weather was an important factor? B: She prefers the city with a temperate climate, because staff will not suffer from extreme heat in summer or heavy snow that stops trains in winter.","t":"A：公司正在兩個城市中為新的歐洲辦公室做選擇，為什麼主管說天氣是重要因素？ B：她偏好【溫帶】氣候的城市，因為員工夏天不會受酷熱之苦，冬天也不會遇到讓火車停駛的大雪。"},{"w":"arid","p":"adj.","d":"very dry, with little or no rain","c":"乾旱的","s":"A: The engineers are designing a new water system for the factory we are building in the desert region, so why does it cost so much more than usual? B: The land there is extremely arid, with almost no rain for most of the year, so they must pipe water in from a river eighty kilometers away.","t":"A：工程師正在為我們在沙漠地區興建的工廠設計新的供水系統，為什麼費用比平常高這麼多？ B：那裡的土地極度【乾旱】，一年中大部分時間幾乎不下雨，所以他們必須從八十公里外的河流引水過來。"},{"w":"polar","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the very cold areas around the North or South Pole","c":"極地的","s":"A: I saw that the science museum downtown has a new exhibition this month, so do you think it would be a good trip for our staff family day? B: Yes, the polar exhibition is perfect for kids, because they can learn about penguins, ice, and how animals survive in the coldest places on earth.","t":"A：我看到市中心的科學博物館這個月有新展覽，你覺得那適合當作我們員工家庭日的行程嗎？ B：適合，那個【極地】展覽很適合小孩，因為他們可以認識企鵝、冰，以及動物如何在地球上最冷的地方生存。"},{"w":"forecast","p":"n.","d":"a statement about what will probably happen, especially with the weather","c":"預報；預測","s":"A: We are supposed to fly to Okinawa for the client meeting on Monday morning, but I'm worried about the typhoon, so what did the news say? B: The latest forecast says the storm will arrive on Sunday night, so the airline may cancel our flight and we should call the client today.","t":"A：我們預定週一早上飛到沖繩和客戶開會，但我擔心颱風，新聞怎麼說？ B：最新的【預報】說暴風會在週日晚上抵達，所以航空公司可能會取消我們的航班，我們今天應該打電話給客戶。"},{"w":"drought","p":"n.","d":"a long period with little or no rain","c":"乾旱","s":"A: The coffee supplier just told us that bean prices will rise by twenty percent next quarter, so did they explain the reason for such a big increase? B: Yes, a long drought in Brazil lasted for almost six months, and many coffee farms lost a large part of their crop because there was no water.","t":"A：咖啡供應商剛告訴我們下一季咖啡豆價格會上漲百分之二十，他們有解釋漲這麼多的原因嗎？ B：有，巴西一場長期【乾旱】持續了將近六個月，許多咖啡農場因為缺水損失了大部分作物。"},{"w":"flood","p":"n.","d":"a large amount of water covering land that is usually dry","c":"洪水；水災","s":"A: Why is the warehouse team moving all the boxes from the ground floor up to the second floor this afternoon? B: The river next to the building rose quickly after three days of heavy rain, and the city warned that a flood could reach our area tonight, so we want to protect the products.","t":"A：倉庫團隊今天下午為什麼要把一樓的箱子全部搬到二樓？ B：連續下了三天大雨後，大樓旁邊的河水迅速上漲，市政府警告今晚【洪水】可能淹到我們這一區，所以我們想保護產品。"},{"w":"storm","p":"n.","d":"very bad weather with strong winds and heavy rain","c":"暴風雨","s":"A: The power went off in the whole office building around two o'clock, and my computer shut down before I saved my report, so what happened? B: A strong storm with heavy rain and lightning passed over the city, and it damaged some power lines near the train station.","t":"A：兩點左右整棟辦公大樓停電了，我的電腦在我存檔報告前就關機了，發生了什麼事？ B：一場夾帶大雨和閃電的強烈【暴風雨】經過市區，損壞了火車站附近的一些電線。"},{"w":"heatwave","p":"n.","d":"a period of unusually hot weather","c":"熱浪","s":"A: Sales of fans and air conditioners at our electronics stores have doubled this week, so did the marketing team start a special promotion? B: No, the main reason is the heatwave, because temperatures have stayed above thirty-seven degrees for six days and many people cannot sleep at night.","t":"A：我們電器行的電風扇和冷氣銷量這週翻倍了，是行銷團隊開始了特別促銷嗎？ B：不是，主要原因是【熱浪】，因為氣溫已經連續六天超過三十七度，很多人晚上都睡不著。"},{"w":"cold spell","p":"n.phr.","d":"a short period of very cold weather","c":"寒流；一段寒冷期","s":"A: The vegetable prices at the market went up suddenly this week, and our restaurant's food costs are much higher, so what caused the change? B: A sudden cold spell last weekend brought freezing temperatures to the farms in central Taiwan, and many leafy vegetables were damaged by the frost.","t":"A：這週市場的菜價突然上漲，我們餐廳的食材成本高了很多，是什麼造成的？ B：上週末一波突如其來的【寒流】讓中台灣的農場出現低溫，許多葉菜都被霜凍壞了。"},{"w":"wind","p":"n.","d":"air that moves quickly across the land","c":"風","s":"A: Why did the construction company stop using the tall crane on the new office tower this afternoon? B: The wind became too strong after lunch, and the safety manager decided it was dangerous to lift heavy steel beams that high, so the workers will continue tomorrow morning if it is calmer.","t":"A：建設公司今天下午為什麼停止使用新辦公大樓上的高塔吊車？ B：午餐後【風】變得太強，安全經理認為把沉重的鋼樑吊到那麼高很危險，所以如果明天早上比較平靜，工人會繼續施工。"},{"w":"cloud cover","p":"n.phr.","d":"the amount of the sky that is covered by clouds","c":"雲層覆蓋；雲量","s":"A: The photography team wants to take pictures of the new hotel from the air using a drone, so is tomorrow a good day to do it? B: Probably not, because thick cloud cover is expected all morning, so the sky will look gray and the building will not stand out in the photos.","t":"A：攝影團隊想用無人機從空中拍新飯店的照片，明天是適合拍攝的日子嗎？ B：可能不是，因為預計整個早上都會有厚厚的【雲層覆蓋】，天空看起來會灰灰的，建築物在照片中不會突出。"},{"w":"sunlight","p":"n.","d":"the light that comes from the sun","c":"陽光","s":"A: The interior designer is planning the layout of our new office, so where does she suggest we put the main work area for the staff? B: She wants it next to the large windows on the east side, because the room gets plenty of natural sunlight in the morning and people will feel more awake.","t":"A：室內設計師正在規劃我們新辦公室的配置，她建議把員工的主要工作區放在哪裡？ B：她想把它放在東側的大窗戶旁邊，因為那個房間早上有充足的自然【陽光】，大家會覺得比較有精神。"},{"w":"greenhouse effect","p":"n.phr.","d":"the warming of the earth because gases in the air trap the sun's heat","c":"溫室效應","s":"A: Our company is making a short environmental video for customers, and I need to explain why the earth is getting warmer, so can you help me with the script? B: You could start with the greenhouse effect, which happens when gases like carbon dioxide trap heat from the sun and stop it from escaping into space.","t":"A：我們公司正在為客戶製作一支簡短的環保影片，我需要解釋地球為什麼越來越暖，你可以幫我寫腳本嗎？ B：你可以從【溫室效應】開始講，它是指像二氧化碳這類氣體留住太陽的熱，使熱無法散逸到太空中。"},{"w":"global warming","p":"n.phr.","d":"the slow rise in the earth's average temperature","c":"全球暖化","s":"A: The insurance company sent us a letter saying our business insurance will cost more next year, so did they explain why the price is going up? B: They said global warming is causing more typhoons and floods every year, so they must pay for more damage and are raising prices for all customers.","t":"A：保險公司寄信給我們說明年的商業保險費會變貴，他們有解釋為什麼漲價嗎？ B：他們說【全球暖化】每年造成更多颱風和水災，所以他們必須支付更多損失，因此對所有客戶調漲價格。"},{"w":"climate change","p":"n.phr.","d":"long-term changes in the earth's weather patterns, mainly caused by people","c":"氣候變遷","s":"A: Our board of directors asked every department to suggest ways to cut energy use this year, so why are they suddenly so interested in this issue? B: Many investors now worry about climate change, and they want companies to show clear plans for reducing pollution and protecting the environment in the future.","t":"A：董事會要求每個部門今年提出減少能源使用的方法，他們為什麼突然這麼關心這個議題？ B：現在許多投資人擔心【氣候變遷】，他們希望公司提出明確的計畫來減少污染並保護未來的環境。"},{"w":"emissions","p":"n.","d":"gases or other substances sent out into the air","c":"排放物；排放量","s":"A: The government announced new environmental rules for factories last month, so what does our plant need to change before the deadline in December? B: We must reduce our carbon emissions by fifteen percent, so the engineers are replacing the old boilers and adding filters to the chimneys.","t":"A：政府上個月公布了新的工廠環保規定，我們工廠在十二月截止日前需要做哪些改變？ B：我們必須把碳【排放量】減少百分之十五，所以工程師正在更換舊鍋爐，並在煙囪加裝濾網。"},{"w":"carbon","p":"n.","d":"a chemical element; often used to mean the carbon dioxide released into the air","c":"碳","s":"A: Our customers keep asking whether our delivery service is environmentally friendly, so what should I tell them when they call the hotline? B: Tell them we switched to electric vans last year, which cut the amount of carbon our trucks release by almost half, and we plan to replace the rest by 2028.","t":"A：客戶一直問我們的配送服務是否環保，他們打客服專線時我該怎麼回答？ B：告訴他們我們去年改用電動貨車，讓車隊排放的【碳】減少了將近一半，而且我們計畫在2028年前汰換其餘車輛。"},{"w":"sustainable","p":"adj.","d":"able to continue for a long time without harming the environment","c":"永續的；可持續的","s":"A: The new hotel owner wants to attract younger travelers who care about the environment, so what changes is she planning for the building? B: She wants to make the hotel more sustainable by installing solar panels, collecting rainwater for the gardens, and serving food from local farms instead of imported products.","t":"A：新的飯店老闆想吸引重視環保的年輕旅客，她打算對建築物做哪些改變？ B：她想透過安裝太陽能板、收集雨水澆花園，以及供應當地農場的食物而非進口產品，讓飯店更加【永續】。"},{"w":"extreme","p":"adj.","d":"very great or severe; much more than usual","c":"極端的","s":"A: Why did the airport cancel so many flights yesterday, even though the sky looked clear here in the city? B: The problem was at the other end, because extreme weather in northern Japan, including heavy snow and freezing winds, closed three airports there for most of the day.","t":"A：昨天這裡市區的天空看起來很晴朗，機場為什麼還取消了這麼多航班？ B：問題出在另一端，因為日本北部的【極端】天氣，包括大雪和冰冷的強風，讓那裡三座機場大半天都關閉了。"},{"w":"variable","p":"adj.","d":"likely to change often","c":"多變的；易變的","s":"A: I'm going to London for a week of meetings with our British partners next month, so what kind of clothes do you think I should pack? B: The weather there is very variable in spring, so it might be sunny in the morning and rainy in the afternoon, and you should bring a light jacket and an umbrella.","t":"A：我下個月要去倫敦和英國夥伴開一週的會，你覺得我該帶什麼樣的衣服？ B：那裡春天的天氣非常【多變】，可能早上晴天、下午下雨，你應該帶一件薄外套和一把雨傘。"},{"w":"mild","p":"adj.","d":"not too hot and not too cold; pleasant","c":"溫和的；暖和的","s":"A: Our company is choosing a place for the annual staff trip in January, so why did the planning committee choose southern Taiwan instead of the mountains? B: The winter weather in the south is usually mild, around twenty-three degrees, so people can enjoy outdoor activities without thick coats or the risk of icy roads.","t":"A：公司正在為一月的年度員工旅遊選地點，為什麼籌備委員會選擇南台灣而不是山區？ B：南部冬天的天氣通常很【溫和】，大約二十三度，大家不用穿厚外套，也不必擔心路面結冰，就能享受戶外活動。"},{"w":"predictable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be known or expected before it happens","c":"可預測的","s":"A: Why do the managers at the beach resort plan their busy summer schedule so early, even in February? B: The weather there is quite predictable, with sunny days from June to September almost every year, so they can confidently hire extra staff and book tour groups many months ahead.","t":"A：海灘度假村的經理們為什麼這麼早，甚至在二月就規劃夏季旺季的排班？ B：那裡的天氣相當【可預測】，幾乎每年六月到九月都是晴天，所以他們可以放心地提前好幾個月加聘人手和預訂旅行團。"},{"w":"unstable","p":"adj.","d":"likely to change suddenly; not steady","c":"不穩定的","s":"A: The hiking club from our company planned to climb Jade Mountain this weekend, so why did the leader suddenly postpone the trip? B: The weather in the mountains has been very unstable this week, with sudden thunderstorms in the afternoons, so she thought it was too risky for the group.","t":"A：公司的登山社原本計畫這週末去爬玉山，為什麼領隊突然延期了？ B：這週山上的天氣非常【不穩定】，下午常有突如其來的雷陣雨，所以她認為對團體來說太危險了。"},{"w":"long-term","p":"adj.","d":"continuing for a long time into the future","c":"長期的","s":"A: Why did the city council decide to build a new seawall along the harbor, when it will take ten years to finish? B: They are thinking about the long-term risk of rising sea levels, because experts say that many shops and homes near the port could be under water in fifty years.","t":"A：市議會為什麼決定沿著港口興建新的海堤，明明要花十年才能完工？ B：他們考量的是海平面上升的【長期】風險，因為專家說港口附近的許多商店和住家五十年後可能會被淹沒。"},{"w":"average","p":"adj.","d":"usual or typical; found by adding amounts and dividing by the number of them","c":"平均的","s":"A: The new branch manager is moving from Taipei to Hualien next month, so is she worried about how the weather there will be different? B: Not really, because the average temperature in Hualien is only about one degree lower than in Taipei, although she says it rains more in the winter months.","t":"A：新的分店經理下個月要從台北搬到花蓮，她會擔心那裡的天氣不一樣嗎？ B：不太會，因為花蓮的【平均】氣溫只比台北低大約一度，不過她說冬季月份那裡比較常下雨。"}]},{"unit":61,"theme":"Clothes 服裝","cards":[{"w":"fashionable","p":"adj.","d":"following the latest style; popular now","c":"時髦的；流行的","s":"A: I'm meeting an important client from Milan for lunch tomorrow, and I'm worried my old gray jacket looks a bit boring, so what do you think I should wear? B: You could try that navy blazer you bought last month, because it looks very fashionable but still professional enough for a business meal.","t":"A：我明天要和一位來自米蘭的重要客戶吃午餐，我擔心我那件舊灰色外套看起來有點無聊，你覺得我該穿什麼？ B：你可以試試上個月買的那件海軍藍西裝外套，因為它看起來很【時髦】，但對商務餐敘來說也夠正式。"},{"w":"fashion house","p":"n.phr.","d":"a company that designs and sells expensive clothes","c":"時裝公司；服裝品牌","s":"A: Our marketing team has been asked to design the online campaign for a luxury brand next season, but do you know much about the company? B: Yes, it is a famous French fashion house that has made elegant dresses and handbags since 1920, so we should keep the style simple and classic.","t":"A：我們行銷團隊被要求為一個奢侈品牌設計下一季的線上活動，你對這家公司了解多少？ B：知道，它是一家有名的法國【時裝公司】，從1920年起就製作優雅的洋裝和手提包，所以我們應該讓風格保持簡單經典。"},{"w":"fashion icon","p":"n.phr.","d":"a famous person whose style many people copy","c":"時尚偶像；時尚指標人物","s":"A: Why did the department store decide to put a large photo of that famous actress at the main entrance of the new shop? B: She is a real fashion icon whom many young shoppers admire, so the managers believe her picture will attract more customers to the new clothing section this winter.","t":"A：為什麼百貨公司決定在新店的正門口放那位知名女演員的大照片？ B：她是許多年輕購物者崇拜的真正【時尚偶像】，所以經理們相信她的照片會在今年冬天吸引更多顧客到新的服飾區。"},{"w":"fashion show","p":"n.phr.","d":"an event where models wear new clothes for an audience","c":"時裝秀","s":"A: The hotel ballroom looks very busy this afternoon, with workers carrying lights and a long stage, so what event is happening tonight? B: A local designer is holding a fashion show to present her spring collection, and about three hundred buyers and reporters have already registered to attend.","t":"A：今天下午飯店宴會廳看起來很忙，工人們搬著燈光和一座長舞台，今晚有什麼活動？ B：一位本地設計師要舉辦一場【時裝秀】來發表她的春季系列，已經有大約三百位買家和記者報名參加。"},{"w":"old fashioned","p":"adj.phr.","d":"no longer modern or popular","c":"過時的；老式的","s":"A: Should we keep using the brown uniforms for the front desk staff, or is it time to order new ones before the hotel reopens in March? B: I think we should replace them, because several guests said the design looks old fashioned and does not match our modern lobby.","t":"A：我們應該繼續讓櫃檯人員穿那套咖啡色制服，還是該在飯店三月重新開幕前訂新的？ B：我覺得應該換掉，因為好幾位客人說那個設計看起來很【過時】，和我們現代化的大廳不搭。"},{"w":"tie","p":"n.","d":"a long narrow piece of cloth worn around the neck with a shirt","c":"領帶","s":"A: I have a job interview at the bank tomorrow morning, and I already ironed my white shirt, but do you think I need anything else? B: Yes, you should wear a dark blue tie with that shirt, because most managers at the bank dress formally and will notice small details.","t":"A：我明天早上在銀行有工作面試，我已經燙好白襯衫了，你覺得我還需要什麼嗎？ B：需要，你應該搭配一條深藍色【領帶】，因為銀行大部分主管都穿著正式，會注意到小細節。"},{"w":"suit","p":"n.","d":"a jacket and trousers or skirt made of the same cloth","c":"西裝；套裝","s":"A: The sales director is flying to Singapore next week to sign a large contract with a new partner, so has he prepared everything? B: Almost, but he still needs to pick up his gray suit from the dry cleaner, since he wants to look professional at the signing ceremony.","t":"A：業務總監下週要飛去新加坡和新合作夥伴簽一份大合約，他都準備好了嗎？ B：差不多了，但他還要去乾洗店拿他的灰色【西裝】，因為他想在簽約儀式上看起來很專業。"},{"w":"shorts","p":"n.","d":"short trousers that end above the knee","c":"短褲","s":"A: The company picnic is at the beach on Saturday, and the weather report says it will be very hot, so what should employees wear? B: The organizers said comfortable shorts and sandals are fine, but everyone should bring a hat and sunscreen because we will be outdoors all afternoon.","t":"A：公司野餐週六在海邊，氣象預報說會很熱，員工應該穿什麼？ B：主辦人說穿舒適的【短褲】和涼鞋就可以，但大家都應該帶帽子和防曬乳，因為我們整個下午都會在戶外。"},{"w":"T-shirt","p":"n.","d":"a simple cotton shirt with short sleeves and no collar","c":"T恤","s":"A: We are planning a charity run for our staff next month, and many people want something to remember the event, so do you have any ideas? B: We could print our company logo on a bright orange T-shirt for every runner, because it is cheap, useful, and easy to see in photos.","t":"A：我們正在計畫下個月為員工舉辦慈善路跑，很多人想要紀念這次活動的東西，你有什麼點子嗎？ B：我們可以在每位跑者的亮橘色【T恤】上印公司標誌，因為它便宜、實用，在照片裡也很顯眼。"},{"w":"trousers","p":"n.","d":"a piece of clothing that covers each leg separately","c":"長褲","s":"A: You ordered a new uniform from the online store last week, but you looked unhappy when the package arrived this morning, so was something wrong with it? B: Yes, the jacket fits perfectly, but the trousers are about five centimeters too long, so I need to send them back and ask for a shorter pair.","t":"A：你上週在網路商店訂了一套新制服，但今天早上包裹到的時候你看起來不太高興，是有什麼問題嗎？ B：對，外套非常合身，但【長褲】長了大約五公分，所以我得退回去，請他們換一條短一點的。"},{"w":"suitcase","p":"n.","d":"a large case with a handle for carrying clothes when traveling","c":"行李箱","s":"A: You are leaving for the trade fair in Frankfurt early tomorrow morning, so have you finished packing all your clothes and product samples yet? B: Not yet, because my old suitcase broke last month, so I need to buy a new one with strong wheels at the mall after work today.","t":"A：你明天一早要出發去法蘭克福參加商展，你的衣服和產品樣品都打包好了嗎？ B：還沒，因為我那個舊【行李箱】上個月壞了，所以我今天下班後得去購物中心買一個輪子堅固的新的。"},{"w":"dress","p":"n.","d":"a piece of women's clothing that covers the body and legs","c":"洋裝；連身裙","s":"A: My sister is getting married in a garden in May, and I want to look nice without spending too much money, so where should I shop? B: The new boutique near our office is having a sale this week, and I saw a lovely light blue dress there for only half the usual price.","t":"A：我姊姊五月要在花園裡結婚，我想穿得好看但又不想花太多錢，我該去哪裡買？ B：我們辦公室附近那家新精品店這週在特價，我在那裡看到一件很漂亮的淺藍色【洋裝】，只要平常價格的一半。"},{"w":"flip flop","p":"n.","d":"a light open sandal held on by a strap between the toes","c":"夾腳拖鞋","s":"A: Why are you walking with only one shoe on after the team-building trip to the beach this afternoon? B: A big wave took my left flip flop away while we were playing volleyball near the water, so I have to buy a new pair at the hotel shop before dinner.","t":"A：今天下午去海邊參加團隊建立活動後，你為什麼只穿一隻鞋走路？ B：我們在水邊打排球的時候，一個大浪把我左腳的【夾腳拖】捲走了，所以我晚餐前得去飯店商店買一雙新的。"},{"w":"waistcoat","p":"n.","d":"a sleeveless jacket with buttons worn over a shirt","c":"背心（西裝背心）","s":"A: The restaurant manager wants all the waiters to look more elegant at the wedding dinner on Sunday, so what will they wear? B: Each waiter will wear a white shirt, black trousers, and a dark red waistcoat over the shirt, which matches the colors of the wedding decorations.","t":"A：餐廳經理希望週日婚宴上所有服務生看起來更優雅，他們會穿什麼？ B：每位服務生都會穿白襯衫、黑長褲，再在襯衫外加一件深紅色【西裝背心】，和婚禮佈置的顏色相配。"},{"w":"backpack","p":"n.","d":"a bag carried on your back with two straps","c":"背包","s":"A: You ride your bicycle to the office every day, so how do you carry your laptop, lunch box, and documents without dropping anything? B: I put everything in a large waterproof backpack, which keeps my hands free and protects my computer when it suddenly starts raining on the way.","t":"A：你每天騎腳踏車上班，你是怎麼帶筆電、便當和文件而不掉東西的？ B：我把所有東西都放進一個大的防水【背包】，這樣雙手可以空出來，在路上突然下雨時也能保護我的電腦。"},{"w":"briefcase","p":"n.","d":"a flat case for carrying papers to work","c":"公事包","s":"A: The new lawyer seems very organized, and she always arrives at meetings with every contract ready, so how does she keep her papers so neat? B: She carries a brown leather briefcase with several sections inside, so each client's documents stay separate and she can find them quickly.","t":"A：新來的律師看起來很有條理，每次開會都把所有合約準備好，她是怎麼讓文件保持這麼整齊的？ B：她帶著一個裡面分好幾格的咖啡色皮革【公事包】，所以每位客戶的文件都分開放，她能很快找到。"},{"w":"casual clothes","p":"n.phr.","d":"comfortable, informal clothes such as jeans","c":"便服；休閒服","s":"A: The company has announced a new rule about what we can wear on Fridays, but I missed the meeting this morning, so what did they say? B: From next week, employees may wear casual clothes such as jeans and polo shirts on Fridays, unless they have meetings with important customers.","t":"A：公司宣布了一項關於星期五可以穿什麼的新規定，但我錯過了今天早上的會議，他們說了什麼？ B：從下週開始，員工星期五可以穿牛仔褲和Polo衫之類的【便服】，除非他們要和重要客戶開會。"},{"w":"vintage clothes","p":"n.phr.","d":"good-quality old clothes from an earlier time","c":"復古服裝；古著","s":"A: That small shop on Second Avenue always has a long line of young people outside on weekends, so what does it sell? B: It sells vintage clothes from the 1970s and 1980s, such as old leather jackets and colorful shirts, which have become very popular with university students recently.","t":"A：第二大道上那家小店週末外面總是排著一長串年輕人，它賣什麼？ B：它賣1970和1980年代的【復古服裝】，像是舊皮夾克和色彩鮮豔的襯衫，最近在大學生之間變得非常受歡迎。"},{"w":"smart clothes","p":"n.phr.","d":"neat, formal clothes for special or business events","c":"體面的服裝；正式服裝","s":"A: I've been invited to the annual awards dinner at the Grand Hotel next Friday, but the invitation does not mention a dress code, so what should I do? B: You should wear smart clothes, like a jacket and nice shoes, because the CEO and many important guests will give speeches there.","t":"A：我受邀參加下週五在大飯店舉辦的年度頒獎晚宴，但邀請函沒提到服裝規定，我該怎麼辦？ B：你應該穿【體面的服裝】，像是西裝外套和好看的鞋子，因為執行長和許多重要來賓都會在那裡致詞。"},{"w":"second-hand","p":"adj.","d":"already used or owned by someone else","c":"二手的","s":"A: Our small startup needs desks and chairs for the five new employees, but the budget is very limited this year, so how can we save money? B: We could buy second-hand furniture from the office that is closing downstairs, because the owner is selling everything in good condition at low prices.","t":"A：我們小新創公司需要為五位新員工準備桌椅，但今年預算很有限，我們要怎麼省錢？ B：我們可以向樓下要歇業的辦公室買【二手】家具，因為老闆正以低價出售所有狀況良好的東西。"},{"w":"keen on","p":"adj.phr.","d":"very interested in something or liking it a lot","c":"熱衷於；很喜歡","s":"A: We need someone to help choose the new uniforms for our hotel staff, and the deadline is next Monday, so who should we ask? B: Lisa from reception is very keen on fashion and often reads design magazines, so I'm sure she would be happy to join the project.","t":"A：我們需要有人幫忙挑選飯店員工的新制服，截止日是下週一，我們該問誰？ B：櫃檯的Lisa非常【熱衷於】時尚，常常看設計雜誌，所以我相信她會很樂意加入這個專案。"},{"w":"stylish","p":"adj.","d":"attractive and fashionable in appearance","c":"有型的；時尚的","s":"A: The interior designer showed us three ideas for the new reception area yesterday, so which one do you think the visitors will like best? B: I prefer the second design, because the gray sofas and gold lamps look modern and stylish, and they will give clients a good first impression.","t":"A：室內設計師昨天給我們看了新接待區的三個構想，你覺得訪客會最喜歡哪一個？ B：我比較喜歡第二個設計，因為灰色沙發和金色燈具看起來既現代又【有型】，會給客戶好的第一印象。"},{"w":"abandon","p":"v.","d":"to stop doing or planning something before it is finished","c":"放棄；中止","s":"A: The clothing company spent two years developing a line of paper jackets, so why did they stop selling them so suddenly last month? B: Customers complained that the jackets tore easily in the rain, so the managers decided to abandon the project and focus on cotton products instead.","t":"A：那家服飾公司花了兩年開發一系列紙製外套，為什麼上個月突然停止販售？ B：顧客抱怨外套在雨中很容易破，所以經理們決定【放棄】這個計畫，改為專注於棉製產品。"},{"w":"fancy","p":"adj.","d":"expensive and of high quality, often with decoration","c":"高級的；花俏的","s":"A: The sales team reached its yearly target in only ten months, so how is the manager planning to thank everyone for their hard work? B: She has booked a fancy restaurant on the top floor of a hotel downtown, where we will enjoy a seven-course dinner and a view of the city.","t":"A：業務團隊只用了十個月就達成年度目標，經理打算怎麼感謝大家的辛勞？ B：她在市中心一家飯店頂樓訂了一間【高級】餐廳，我們會在那裡享用七道菜的晚餐，還能欣賞城市景色。"},{"w":"mix and match","p":"v.phr.","d":"to combine different pieces of clothing in different ways","c":"混搭","s":"A: I'm going on a ten-day business trip to three countries, but my suitcase is small, so how can I bring enough outfits for every meeting? B: Pack a few pieces in simple colors like black, white, and navy, so you can mix and match them easily and create a different look each day.","t":"A：我要去三個國家出差十天，但我的行李箱很小，要怎麼帶足夠每場會議穿的衣服？ B：帶幾件黑色、白色和海軍藍等簡單顏色的單品，這樣你就能輕鬆【混搭】它們，每天打造不同的造型。"},{"w":"heap","p":"n.","d":"an untidy pile of things","c":"一堆","s":"A: The storeroom behind the clothing shop is such a mess, and the new manager is visiting tomorrow, so what happened in there? B: The delivery company dropped all the winter coats in a big heap on the floor this morning, and nobody has had time to hang them up yet.","t":"A：服飾店後面的倉庫好亂，新經理明天就要來了，裡面發生什麼事了？ B：貨運公司今天早上把所有冬季大衣在地上丟成一大【堆】，到現在還沒有人有時間把它們掛起來。"},{"w":"ridiculous","p":"adj.","d":"very silly or unreasonable","c":"荒謬的；離譜的","s":"A: Did you see the price of the plain white T-shirt in the new designer shop at the airport while we were waiting for our flight? B: Yes, it cost almost two hundred dollars, which is a ridiculous amount for a simple cotton shirt that you can buy anywhere for much less.","t":"A：我們等班機的時候，你有看到機場那家新設計師商店裡素白T恤的價格嗎？ B：有，要價將近兩百美元，對一件到處都能用便宜得多的價格買到的簡單棉衫來說，真是【離譜的】金額。"},{"w":"denim","p":"n.","d":"a strong cotton cloth, usually blue, used to make jeans","c":"丹寧布；牛仔布","s":"A: Our factory received a large order from a jeans company in Europe, so what kind of material do we need to buy in the next few weeks? B: We need about five thousand meters of strong blue denim, and the supplier promised to deliver it before the end of the month.","t":"A：我們工廠接到歐洲一家牛仔褲公司的大訂單，接下來幾週我們需要買什麼布料？ B：我們需要大約五千公尺耐用的藍色【丹寧布】，供應商答應會在月底前送到。"},{"w":"trendy","p":"adj.","d":"very fashionable and modern at the moment","c":"新潮的；流行的","s":"A: The café on the corner has completely changed its look since it reopened last week, so why is it suddenly so crowded with young customers? B: The new owner turned it into a trendy place with bright lights, colorful chairs, and pretty desserts that people love to share online.","t":"A：轉角那家咖啡館上週重新開幕後外觀完全變了，為什麼突然擠滿了年輕顧客？ B：新老闆把它改造成一個【新潮的】地方，有明亮的燈光、彩色椅子和漂亮的甜點，大家都很喜歡在網路上分享。"}]}];
